window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["people-ayanokouji-kiyotaka"]=[{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p14-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka opening monologue  equality is a lie  ch 1  direct address to the reader before the story opens  not a character scene  i know this is kind of sudden  but  please  it will only take a moment  i want your honest opinion   are people equal or not   a proper society will constantly strive for equality  there are those who clamor for men and women to always be considered equal  as a result  we raised the employment rate for women  we made specialized subway cars only for women  sometimes  women will even argue over the order of names in a family register  the public opinion of people with disabilities has also changed  we re now told that we should not use the term  disabled people  when referring to them  so as not to discriminate  nowadays  children are taught that all people are created equal   but is that true  i have my doubts  if men and women have different abilities  then their roles should also differ  people with disabilities are still disabled  no matter what polite euphemisms you use  no matter how you try to avert your eyes  the meaning of the word does not change   so  my answer would be   no  we are not equal  to be human is to be unequal  equality does not exist   long ago  in a bygone era  a great man said that heaven does not set one man above or below any other  however  he did not necessarily adhere to the idea that everyone is equal  did you know that there is more to that famous passage  the rest goes like this  everyone is equal when they are born  so i ask  why do we see differences in position and status  and it continues  do you or do you not encourage learning to create a difference   so then  education creates an imbalance  the point s spelled out there  in the incredibly famous work gakumon no sume  even though this is the year 2015  the modern era  nothing about these teachings has changed  the situation has only grown more complex and fraught   in any case  we are human beings  we are living  thinking creatures   i don t think it right to simply say that we are unequal and then live our lives based on pure instinct  in other words  though  equality  is a complete lie  we cannot accept inequality  either  right now  i m trying to come up with a new answer for humanity s eternal question   hey  you there  you  the one reading this book right now  have you ever given serious thought to the future   have you ever considered the purpose of going to high school or to college  though the future may seem hazy right now  do you think you ll find a job someday  that s what i used to think  back when i finished my compulsory education and became a high school student  i hadn t really considered the future  i d only felt joy at being nearly free of obligation  i didn t consider the incredible influence that school would continue to have in my life  on my future  i didn t even understand the purpose behind studying language or numbers  philosophical  contrarian on equality  frames the self as a detached analyst","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Opening monologue: equality is a lie (Ch.1)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.14-15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">direct address to the reader before the story opens; not a character scene<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I know this is kind of sudden, but, please, it will only take a moment. I want your honest opinion.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Are people equal or not?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;A proper society will constantly strive for equality. There are those who clamor for men and women to always be considered equal. As a result, we raised the employment rate for women, we made specialized subway cars only for…<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;A proper society will constantly strive for equality. There are those who clamor for men and women to always be considered equal. As a result, we raised the employment rate for women, we made specialized subway cars only for women. Sometimes, women will even argue over the order of names in a family register. The public opinion of people with disabilities has also changed. We’re now told that we should not use the term “disabled people” when referring to them, so as not to discriminate. Nowadays, children are taught that all people are created equal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;But is that true? I have my doubts. If men and women have different abilities, then their roles should also differ. People with disabilities are still disabled, no matter what polite euphemisms you use. No matter how you try to avert your eyes, the meaning of the word does not change.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;So, my answer would be, “No, we are not equal.” To be human is to be unequal. Equality does not exist.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Long ago, in a bygone era, a great man said that heaven does not set one man above or below any other. However, he did not necessarily adhere to the idea that everyone is equal. Did you know that there is more to that famous passage? The rest goes like this: Everyone is equal when they are born, so I ask, why do we see differences in position and status? And it continues: Do you or do you not encourage learning to create a difference?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;So then, education creates an imbalance. The point’s spelled out there, in the incredibly famous work Gakumon no Sume. Even though this is the year 2015, the modern era, nothing about these teachings has changed. The situation has only grown more complex and fraught.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;In any case, we are human beings. We are living, thinking creatures.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I don’t think it right to simply say that we are unequal and then live our lives based on pure instinct. In other words, though “equality” is a complete lie, we cannot accept inequality, either. Right now, I’m trying to come up with a new answer for humanity’s eternal question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Hey, you there. You, the one reading this book right now. Have you ever given serious thought to the future?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Have you ever considered the purpose of going to high school or to college? Though the future may seem hazy right now, do you think you’ll find a job someday? That’s what I used to think. Back when I finished my compulsory education and became a high school student, I hadn’t really considered the future. I’d only felt joy at being nearly free of obligation. I didn’t consider the incredible influence that school would continue to have in my life, on my future. I didn’t even understand the purpose behind studying language or numbers.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> philosophical, contrarian on equality; frames the self as a detached analyst<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p16-1\">→ After: Horikita&#x27;s coercion in class (Ch.2 open, present)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p16-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka horikita s coercion in class  ch 2 open  present  class d classroom after class  horikita wakes feigning sleep ak  ayanokouji kun  do you have a moment   if you do not awaken within three seconds  i will bestow additional punishment upon you   what do you mean   punishment   that s nothing but harassment  or rather  bullying  and besides  that last one sounds strangely familiar  because you ve already stabbed me before   she came  she was here  it was terrifying    devil shostakovich symphony no 11 imagery  she is  the devil  seeking  her slave   sleeping strategy  pretend not to hear  abandoned instantly under threat  would you prefer to regret while you suffer or regret while you despair   all right  then  what am i supposed to do  conflict avoidant surface  compliance when pressure is concrete  dry self aware humor  computer like brain  self metaphor  runs cost benefit on social encounters coerced helper dynamic  she stabbed him with compass earlier  scar on right forearm shown as  evidence  she demands evidence  he concedes none  reluctantly accepts helping horikita  frames deal as mistake inner monologue sarcastic  mocks his own compliance  filled with trepidation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Horikita&#x27;s coercion in class (Ch.2 open, present)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.16-18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D classroom after class; Horikita wakes feigning-sleep AK<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, do you have a moment?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;If you do not awaken within three seconds, I will bestow additional punishment upon you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What do you mean, &#x27;punishment&#x27;?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s nothing but harassment, or rather, bullying! And besides, that last one sounds strangely familiar, because you&#x27;ve already stabbed me before!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;She came. She was here. It was terrifying.&quot; — devil/Shostakovich Symphony No.11 imagery; she is &quot;the devil&quot; seeking &quot;her slave&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Sleeping Strategy&quot;: pretend not to hear; abandoned instantly under threat<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Would you prefer to regret while you suffer or regret while you despair?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;All right, then. What am I supposed to do?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> conflict-avoidant surface; compliance when pressure is concrete; dry self-aware humor<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;computer-like brain&quot; self-metaphor; runs cost-benefit on social encounters<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> coerced helper dynamic; she stabbed him with compass earlier (scar on right forearm shown as &quot;evidence&quot;; she demands evidence, he concedes none)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> reluctantly accepts helping Horikita; frames deal as mistake<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> inner monologue sarcastic, mocks his own compliance (&quot;filled with trepidation&quot;)<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p14-1\">← Before: Opening monologue: equality is a lie (Ch.1)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p19-1\">→ After: Flashback 2.1: entrance-ceremony bus (April)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p19-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka flashback 2 1  entrance ceremony bus  april  bus to school  entrance ceremony day  flashback opens chapter 2 1 flashback structure  present past cut at p 18  two months ago  mind  clear as a passing stream  seat finder s luck  forgot the wobbling elderly woman until commotion  scene others  blond high school boy takes priority seat  office lady scolds  boy refuses  argues  no legal obligation  elderly woman tries to stop the commotion ak passive observer  does not intervene  watches crowd dynamics  unnamed yet blond boy   koenji  confirmed later  first observed by ak  registers his anti social honesty page ends mid scene  bus conflict continues p 21","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Flashback 2.1: entrance-ceremony bus (April)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.19-20<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">bus to school, entrance ceremony day; flashback opens<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">mind &quot;clear as a passing stream&quot;; seat-finder&#x27;s luck; forgot the wobbling elderly woman until commotion [scene-others] blond high-school boy takes priority seat; office lady scolds; boy refuses, argues &quot;no legal obligation&quot;…<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> chapter 2.1 flashback structure; present→past cut at p.18 (&quot;two months ago&quot;)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> mind &quot;clear as a passing stream&quot;; seat-finder&#x27;s luck; forgot the wobbling elderly woman until commotion [scene-others] blond high-school boy takes priority seat; office lady scolds; boy refuses, argues &quot;no legal obligation&quot;; elderly woman tries to stop the commotion<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK passive observer; does not intervene; watches crowd dynamics<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> (unnamed-yet blond boy = Koenji, confirmed later) first observed by AK; registers his anti-social honesty<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> page ends mid-scene; bus conflict continues p.21+<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p16-1\">← Before: Horikita&#x27;s coercion in class (Ch.2 open, present)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p21-1\">→ After: Bus: the uniformed girl intervenes (unnamed Kushida)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p21-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka bus  the uniformed girl intervenes  unnamed kushida  same bus  schoolgirl in our uniform argues with koenji on society s sake  i have no interest in contributing to society  i care only for my own satisfaction  analyzed the bus  two kinds   pretended not to hear   hesitant  none would move  himself included  like everyone else  i didn t move  elderly vs youth value argument   cold utilitarian framing  still didn t act passivity is principled  not shy  he judges intervention pointless for himself seated beside him  expressionless  eyes meet    even without speaking a word  i could tell that we shared the same opinion  neither of us considered it necessary to give up our seat   unnamed yet  the intervening girl  registers her courage  impressed  how could someone pour so much courage  into so few words  working woman ultimately yields seat after the girl s public appeal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Bus: the uniformed girl intervenes (unnamed Kushida)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.21-24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">same bus; schoolgirl in our uniform argues with Koenji on society&#x27;s sake<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;I have no interest in contributing to society. I care only for my own satisfaction.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">analyzed the bus: two kinds — pretended not to hear / hesitant; none would move; himself included (&quot;like everyone else, I didn&#x27;t move&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">elderly vs youth value argument — cold utilitarian framing; still didn&#x27;t act<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> passivity is principled, not shy: he judges intervention pointless for himself<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> seated beside him, expressionless; eyes meet — &quot;Even without speaking a word, I could tell that we shared the same opinion. Neither of us considered it necessary to give up our seat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> (unnamed yet, the intervening girl) registers her courage; impressed (&quot;How could someone pour so much courage... into so few words?&quot;)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> working woman ultimately yields seat after the girl&#x27;s public appeal<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p19-1\">← Before: Flashback 2.1: entrance-ceremony bus (April)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p25-1\">→ After: Gate confrontation: first AK↔Horikita exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p25-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka gate confrontation  first ak horikita exchange school gate after disembarking  horikita confronts him  you were looking at me  why   i didn t give up my seat because i thought it would be pointless  that s all   i don t want to spend any time around people like you   i feel the same way   his reply  muttered  dislikes trouble as philosophy  letting sleeping dogs lie  honest about it when asked mutual wariness established on day one  parallel non interventionists  different reasons  his convenience vs her pointlessness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Gate confrontation: first AK↔Horikita exchange<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">school gate after disembarking; Horikita confronts him<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You were looking at me. Why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I didn&#x27;t give up my seat because I thought it would be pointless. That&#x27;s all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t want to spend any time around people like you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I feel the same way,&quot; (his reply, muttered)<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> dislikes trouble as philosophy (&quot;letting sleeping dogs lie&quot;); honest about it when asked<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> mutual wariness established on day one; parallel non-interventionists, different reasons (his convenience vs her pointlessness)<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p21-1\">← Before: Bus: the uniformed girl intervenes (unnamed Kushida)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p26-1\">→ After: Classroom day one: friendship anxiety + name exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p26-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka classroom day one  friendship anxiety   name exchange first year class d classroom before ceremony rehearsed friend making scenarios the day before   completely isolated  ventured alone into a battlefield  do or die    social inexperience from upbringing paralyzed analyzing approaches  rotund boy beaten to the punch by glasses boy   what on earth are  friends  anyway   that s quite a heavy sigh  considering the school year has only begun  meeting you again makes me want to sigh   nice to meet you  i m ayanokouji kiyotaka   i m horikita suzune   wow  she was cute  or rather  she was beautiful  such a calm  cool beauty  self description   i have no particular hobbies  but i m interested in just about anything  i don t need many friends  but i think it would be nice to have at least a few   spoken just like someone who avoids trouble  i don t think i could ever like such a person   jeez  i feel like you trashed my entire existence in one second  wants ordinary connections but lacks the practiced social scripts  self aware of the gap names exchanged  she reads crime and punishment   he files her taste as reflective of personality","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Classroom day one: friendship anxiety + name exchange<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.26-28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">first-year Class D classroom before ceremony<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;That&#x27;s quite a heavy sigh, considering the school year has only begun. Meeting you again makes me want to sigh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nice to meet you. I&#x27;m Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m Horikita Suzune.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> rehearsed friend-making scenarios the day before; &quot;completely isolated... ventured alone into a battlefield... do or die&quot; — social inexperience from upbringing<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> paralyzed analyzing approaches (rotund boy beaten to the punch by glasses boy); &quot;What on earth are &#x27;friends,&#x27; anyway?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26-27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Wow. She was cute. Or rather, she was beautiful... Such a calm, cool beauty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> self-description: &quot;I have no particular hobbies, but I&#x27;m interested in just about anything. I don&#x27;t need many friends, but I think it would be nice to have at least a few.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Spoken just like someone who avoids trouble. I don&#x27;t think I could ever like such a person.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Jeez, I feel like you trashed my entire existence in one second,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> wants ordinary connections but lacks the practiced social scripts; self-aware of the gap<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> names exchanged; she reads Crime and Punishment — he files her taste as reflective of personality<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p25-1\">← Before: Gate confrontation: first AK↔Horikita exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p29-1\">→ After: Chiyabashira + school rules + S System (orientation)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p29-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka chiyabashira   school rules   s system  orientation  homeroom teacher s first lecture chiyabashira sae   japanese history  class d homeroom for 3 years  dorms mandatory  outside contact forbidden  even family w o authorization  leaving campus forbidden s system  student id   credit card   facility access  100 000 points deposited on admission   monthly  1 point   1 yen  no cash out after graduation  no saving advantage  transfers allowed  extortion bullying monitored  this school doesn t seem as strict as i thought    aloud  then agrees with horikita s  almost too much preferential treatment  it s frightening    veil of mystery  expects hidden risk campus  600 000 m  karaoke theater cafe boutique  government run   100  placement rate advertised","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chiyabashira + school rules + S System (orientation)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.29-32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">homeroom teacher&#x27;s first lecture<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;This school doesn&#x27;t seem as strict as I thought&quot; — aloud; then agrees with Horikita&#x27;s &quot;almost too much preferential treatment. It&#x27;s frightening&quot; — veil of mystery; expects hidden risk<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Chiyabashira Sae — Japanese history, Class D homeroom for 3 years; dorms mandatory; outside contact forbidden (even family w/o authorization); leaving campus forbidden<span class=\"pg\">p.30-31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> S System: student ID = credit card + facility access; 100,000 points deposited on admission &amp; monthly; 1 point = 1 yen; no cash-out after graduation (no saving advantage); transfers allowed; extortion/bullying monitored<span class=\"pg\">p.30-31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> campus &gt;600,000 m², karaoke/theater/café/boutique; government-run; ~100% placement rate advertised<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p26-1\">← Before: Classroom day one: friendship anxiety + name exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p32-1\">→ After: Class introductions (cast assembly)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p32-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka class introductions  cast assembly  voluntary intros led by hirata after chiyabashira leaves  starting today  we re all going to be classmates  introduce ourselves and become friends as soon as possible  analysis of inogashira freezing   do your best  pressures   just take things slowly  don t rush  actually helps   reads social mechanics precisely  my first goal is to become friends with everyone  share your contact information with me  kushida is genuine type  then  p 37   she said it as though she knew i d been critiquing everyone s introductions  i felt strangely uncomfortable    first unease re kushida  scene others  red haired delinquent refuses intros  later  ryuuen kakeru  leaves with crew  yamauchi baseball claims  ike comic self intro  koenji claims conglomerate heir   threatens to  punish  ugly things own intro   um  well  my name is ayanokouji kiyotaka  and  uh  i don t really have any special skills or anything  i ll do my best to get along with all of you   i d failed    worst intro  attracts no attention by design instinct  applause  felt somewhat like pity  which strangely pained me  despite that  i felt kind of glad  deliberately unmemorable self presentation  mixed relief pain at invisibility   wants ordinary  flinches from it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Class introductions (cast assembly)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.32-40<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">voluntary intros led by Hirata after Chiyabashira leaves<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;Starting today, we&#x27;re all going to be classmates... introduce ourselves and become friends as soon as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;My first goal is to become friends with everyone... share your contact information with me!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">own intro: &quot;Um. Well, my name is Ayanokouji Kiyotaka. And, uh, I don&#x27;t really have any special skills or anything. I&#x27;ll do my best to get along with all of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> analysis of Inogashira freezing: &quot;Do your best!&quot; pressures; &quot;Just take things slowly. Don&#x27;t rush&quot; actually helps — reads social mechanics precisely<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Kushida is genuine type; then (p.37) &quot;She said it as though she knew I&#x27;d been critiquing everyone&#x27;s introductions. I felt strangely uncomfortable&quot; — first unease re Kushida [scene-others] red-haired delinquent refuses intros (later: Ryuuen Kakeru), leaves with crew; Yamauchi baseball claims; Ike comic self-intro; Koenji claims conglomerate heir + threatens to &quot;punish&quot; ugly things<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;d failed!&quot; — worst intro, attracts no attention by design instinct; applause &quot;felt somewhat like pity, which strangely pained me. Despite that... I felt kind of glad.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> deliberately unmemorable self-presentation; mixed relief/pain at invisibility — wants ordinary, flinches from it<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p29-1\">← Before: Chiyabashira + school rules + S System (orientation)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p41-1\">→ After: Convenience store with Horikita (post-ceremony)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p41-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka convenience store with horikita  post ceremony  campus store  horikita buying cheapest toiletries  i m the sort who doesn t know when you might need money  surprised she stayed for intros  registers her price choices as revealing debate  her logic  no evidence self intros lead to friendship  wins  he averts eyes  admits intro disaster  might have been a miracle i d managed to get her name  razor joke  five blades    fails colossally  i don t have anything to shave  not on my chin  not under my armpits  and not down there   you don t seem adept at socializing  you re terrible at conversation  tries jokes to close social distance  reads own failure in real time  jokes failed colossally with women  store free bin  emergency relief for point broke students  3 items month noticed  horikita really was cute    attraction registering despite wariness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Convenience store with Horikita (post-ceremony)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.41-45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">campus store; Horikita buying cheapest toiletries<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m the sort who doesn&#x27;t know when you might need money,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">razor joke (five blades) — fails colossally<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t have anything to shave. Not on my chin, not under my armpits, and not down there.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> surprised she stayed for intros; registers her price choices as revealing<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> debate: her logic &quot;no evidence self-intros lead to friendship&quot; wins; he averts eyes; admits intro disaster &quot;might have been a miracle I&#x27;d managed to get her name&quot;<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You don&#x27;t seem adept at socializing. You&#x27;re terrible at conversation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> tries jokes to close social distance; reads own failure in real time (&quot;jokes failed colossally with women&quot;)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> store free-bin: emergency relief for point-broke students, 3 items/month<span class=\"pg\">p.45-46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> noticed &quot;Horikita really was cute&quot; — attraction registering despite wariness<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p32-1\">← Before: Class introductions (cast assembly)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p46-1\">→ After: Sudou incident: Class D stigma + cameras<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p46-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune second-years ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudou incident  class d stigma   cameras store register dispute  red haired classmate    sudou   corrects unnamed  delinquent  from intros   my name s ayanokouji  i m from your class  i just asked because it sounded like there was trouble   i can pay for you  i mean  it d be annoying if you had to head all the way back to the dorms  i don t mind   my name s sudou   he said   thanks for helping me out  i owe you   you re acting like a pushover right from the start  do you intend to become his servant   i didn t care about making friends  i just wanted to help  no big deal   it s mostly defenseless people who stay away from those types  if he acted violently  i could rebuff him   hey  get over here  i ll smack that smug look off your face   at horikita  ak holds him back   you re in class d  aren t you     since you re  defective  we ll let you off the hook     you guys ll be in hell soon enough  upperclassmen treat class d as known trash tier  can t explain how they knew spots surveillance cameras  cleans sudou s spilled noodles himself  reluctantly  i bent down    quiet maintenance of order  no credit convenience store exterior   two cameras noted  school watches  first concrete class d stigma data point  defective  hell awaiting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sudou incident: Class D stigma + cameras<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.46-51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">store register dispute; red-haired classmate = **Sudou** (corrects unnamed &quot;delinquent&quot; from intros)<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My name&#x27;s Ayanokouji. I&#x27;m from your class. I just asked because it sounded like there was trouble.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can pay for you. I mean, it&#x27;d be annoying if you had to head all the way back to the dorms. I don&#x27;t mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;My name&#x27;s Sudou,&quot; (he said)<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thanks for helping me out. I owe you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re acting like a pushover right from the start. Do you intend to become his servant?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I didn&#x27;t care about making friends. I just wanted to help. No big deal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s mostly defenseless people who stay away from those types. If he acted violently, I could rebuff him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey, get over here! I&#x27;ll smack that smug look off your face!&quot; (at Horikita; AK holds him back)<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re in Class D, aren&#x27;t you?&quot; ... &quot;Since you&#x27;re &#x27;defective,&#x27; we&#x27;ll let you off the hook&quot; / &quot;You guys&#x27;ll be in hell soon enough&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> upperclassmen treat Class D as known trash tier; can&#x27;t explain how they knew<span class=\"pg\">p.50-51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> spots surveillance cameras; cleans Sudou&#x27;s spilled noodles himself (&quot;Reluctantly, I bent down...&quot;) — quiet maintenance of order, no credit<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> convenience store exterior — two cameras noted (school watches)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> first concrete Class D stigma data point (defective, hell awaiting)<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p41-1\">← Before: Convenience store with Horikita (post-ceremony)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p52-1\">→ After: Dorm 401: freedom monologue (CORE BACKSTORY ANCHOR)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p52-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka dorm 401  freedom monologue  core backstory anchor  alone in dorm room after move in  i d chosen this school for one fundamental reason  at this high school  people were not allowed to contact students without permission  i greatly appreciated that  i was free   no one else s eyes or words would ever reach me  i could start ag no  i could begin anew entirely  a new life   he cuts the word off at  start ag  and restarts  admitted before   thought i would be been fine either way  that the difference between passing and failing would have been trivial  but my true feelings finally welled up  i was glad to have been admitted here   corpus reads  would be been    kept verbatim  resolves  enjoy fullest life  without drawing attention to myself   his narration  excited sleeplessness   first taste of unwatched life co ed dorms  romantic relations  frowned upon  room  8 tatami  no utility costs deducted  freedom   liberte  wordplay  he almost doesn t want to graduate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Dorm 401: freedom monologue (CORE BACKSTORY ANCHOR)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.52-53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">alone in dorm room after move-in<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;d chosen this school for one fundamental reason... At this high school, people were not allowed to contact students without permission... I greatly appreciated that. I was free.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> &quot;No one else&#x27;s eyes or words would ever reach me. I could start ag—no. I could begin anew entirely. A new life.&quot; (he cuts the word off at &quot;start ag—&quot; and restarts)<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> admitted before, &quot;thought I would be been fine either way, that the difference between passing and failing would have been trivial. But my true feelings finally welled up. I was glad to have been admitted here.&quot; (corpus reads &quot;would be been&quot; — kept verbatim)<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> resolves: enjoy fullest life &quot;without drawing attention to myself&quot; (his narration); excited sleeplessness — first taste of unwatched life<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> co-ed dorms; romantic relations &quot;frowned upon&quot;; room ~8 tatami; no utility costs deducted<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> &quot;freedom / liberté&quot; wordplay; he almost doesn&#x27;t want to graduate<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p46-1\">← Before: Sudou incident: Class D stigma + cameras<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p54-1\">→ After: Lunchtime envy + Kushida&#x27;s approach<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p54-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka lunchtime envy   kushida s approach day 1 class ends  ak watches half the room leave for lunch envious of others  groups   still hadn t managed to befriend a single one  worries loneliness will make him stand out bullying target  how pathetic     your thoughts are like an open book   scene others  hirata s lunch invite  girls swarm  his hand dies mid raise  comedy beat  social failure   you re ayanokouji kun  right   ayanokouji kun  are you on good terms with horikita san   horikita turned me down   contact info   i don t think she s very good at interacting with others  why are you asking about horikita  anyway  she remembered his lame intro    somehow  that made me really happy  handshake   today was probably my lucky day  first private exchange  she is warm   probing about horikita  he files happiness  not suspicion  yet  she sits back beside him p 59 with  don t talk to me  aura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Lunchtime envy + Kushida&#x27;s approach<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.54-58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">day-1 class ends; AK watches half the room leave for lunch<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;How pathetic.&quot; / &quot;Your thoughts are like an open book.&quot; [scene-others] Hirata&#x27;s lunch invite: girls swarm; his hand dies mid-raise (comedy beat, social failure)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re Ayanokouji-kun, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, are you on good terms with Horikita-san?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> envious of others&#x27; groups; &quot;still hadn&#x27;t managed to befriend a single one&quot;; worries loneliness will make him stand out/bullying target<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horikita turned me down.&quot; (contact info)<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t think she&#x27;s very good at interacting with others. Why are you asking about Horikita, anyway?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> she remembered his lame intro — &quot;Somehow, that made me really happy&quot;; handshake; &quot;Today was probably my lucky day&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> first private exchange; she is warm + probing about Horikita; he files happiness, not suspicion (yet)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> she sits back beside him p.59 with &quot;don&#x27;t talk to me&quot; aura<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p52-1\">← Before: Dorm 401: freedom monologue (CORE BACKSTORY ANCHOR)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p59-1\">→ After: Club fair talk with Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p59-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka club fair talk with horikita classroom lunch  club fair pa announcement  5pm gym no 1   i m not interested in joining a club   listen  don t count me as one of your friends   if you seriously want to make a friend  you should be more insistent   i can t  though  i ve devoted myself to walking a lonely road   i have trouble comprehending your contradictory way of thinking  friendship desire vs passivity contradiction  self diagnosed and hers too  clubs    last chance  social engineering attempt she denies friendship but keeps returning to sit with him  mutual orbit forming","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Club fair talk with Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.59-60<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">classroom lunch; club-fair PA announcement (5pm Gym No.1)<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m not interested in joining a club.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Listen, don&#x27;t count me as one of your friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;If you seriously want to make a friend, you should be more insistent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t, though. I&#x27;ve devoted myself to walking a lonely road.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have trouble comprehending your contradictory way of thinking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> friendship desire vs passivity contradiction, self-diagnosed and hers too; clubs = &quot;last chance&quot; social engineering attempt<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> she denies friendship but keeps returning to sit with him; mutual orbit forming<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p54-1\">← Before: Lunchtime envy + Kushida&#x27;s approach<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p61-1\">→ After: Violence debate; she joins the club fair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p61-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka violence debate  she joins the club fair classroom lunch continues karate chop retaliation  then   violence has existed since the dawn of time  the most effective means of achieving resolution   on the inside  she was a cruel beast  despite honors student civility  gives up arguing  well  if it s only for a little while after school  i ll go with you    joins the club fair  watching you flail about as you fail to make friends sounds somewhat interesting  learns the hard way her cruelty is principled  still chooses her company pact to attend fair together   first voluntary joint activity","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p61-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Violence debate; she joins the club fair<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.61-62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">classroom lunch continues<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> karate-chop retaliation; then: &quot;Violence has existed since the dawn of time... the most effective means of achieving resolution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Well, if it&#x27;s only for a little while after school, I&#x27;ll go with you,&quot; — joins the club fair<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Watching you flail about as you fail to make friends sounds somewhat interesting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;on the inside, she was a cruel beast&quot; despite honors-student civility; gives up arguing<span class=\"pg\">p.61-62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> learns the hard way her cruelty is principled; still chooses her company<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> pact to attend fair together — first voluntary joint activity<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p59-1\">← Before: Club fair talk with Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p63-1\">→ After: Club fair: Horikita Manabu&#x27;s speech<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p63-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka club fair  horikita manabu s speech gym no 1   100 first years  tachibana  student council secretary  hosts clubs professional tier  o2 chambers etc  min 3 people to found a club  club budget tied to member count on athletic clubs   gatherings of people with nothing better to do  would quit  in the blink of an eye   scene others  horikita freezes when baseball rep on stage  real trigger  last man standing    horikita manabu  student council president  3rd year   170cm  glasses  calculating gaze   i m the student council president  my name is horikita manabu    silences 100  students with presence alone  recruitment speech  no other club involvement  rejects naive outlook   council s right and duty to enforce and amend the rules  but the school expects more  sensed his power is personal  not positional  noticed sibling surname coincidence with horikita suzune    perhaps they just happened to have the same surname  or  maybe  she remains  still as a statue    unexplained freeze  ak files the reaction first sighting of the school s dominant authority figure  suzune s private stake in him planted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Club fair: Horikita Manabu&#x27;s speech<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.63-68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gym No.1, ~100 first-years; Tachibana (student council secretary) hosts<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> on athletic clubs: &quot;gatherings of people with nothing better to do&quot;; would quit &quot;in the blink of an eye&quot; [scene-others] Horikita freezes when baseball rep on stage; real trigger: last man standing = **Horikita Manabu**, student…<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m the student council president. My name is Horikita Manabu,&quot; — silences 100+ students with presence alone; recruitment speech: no other-club involvement; rejects naive outlook; &quot;council&#x27;s right and duty to enforce and amend…<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">sensed his power is personal, not positional; noticed sibling surname coincidence with Horikita Suzune — &quot;perhaps they just happened to have the same surname. Or, maybe…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> clubs professional-tier (O2 chambers etc.); min 3 people to found a club; club budget tied to member count<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> on athletic clubs: &quot;gatherings of people with nothing better to do&quot;; would quit &quot;in the blink of an eye&quot; [scene-others] Horikita freezes when baseball rep on stage; real trigger: last man standing = **Horikita Manabu**, student council president (3rd year, ~170cm, glasses, calculating gaze)<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m the student council president. My name is Horikita Manabu,&quot; — silences 100+ students with presence alone; recruitment speech: no other-club involvement; rejects naive outlook; &quot;council&#x27;s right and duty to enforce and amend the rules, but the school expects more&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> she remains &quot;still as a statue&quot; — unexplained freeze; AK files the reaction<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> first sighting of the school&#x27;s dominant authority figure; Suzune&#x27;s private stake in him planted<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p61-1\">← Before: Violence debate; she joins the club fair<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p68-1\">→ After: Group chat: first male-group contact exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p68-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"sudou-ken ike-kanji horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka group chat  first male group contact exchange fair ends  sudou   ike   yamauchi approach ak basketball since elementary  joining team here  i want to get my first girlfriend in class d  that s my goal   yeah  oh  by the way  i made a group chat for the guys yesterday   takes out his phone   do you want to join in  too  it s pretty handy  happy to be invited    finally  i d found the perfect chance to make friends  then horikita vanishes into crowd  he pauses  worried  but exchanges contacts and stays social hunger  grabs any thread  guiltless about taking it almost follows her  decides not to   boundary instinct vs curiosity","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Group chat: first male-group contact exchange<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.68-71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">fair ends; Sudou + Ike + Yamauchi approach AK<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> basketball since elementary; joining team here<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> &quot;I want to get my first girlfriend in Class D. That&#x27;s my goal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> &quot;Yeah. Oh, by the way, I made a group chat for the guys yesterday.&quot; (takes out his phone)<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you want to join in, too? It&#x27;s pretty handy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> happy to be invited — &quot;Finally, I&#x27;d found the perfect chance to make friends!&quot;; then Horikita vanishes into crowd; he pauses (worried?) but exchanges contacts and stays<span class=\"pg\">p.69-71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> social hunger: grabs any thread; guiltless about taking it<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> almost follows her; decides not to — boundary instinct vs curiosity<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p63-1\">← Before: Club fair: Horikita Manabu&#x27;s speech<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p72-1\">→ After: Swim-class day: betting ring + social foothold<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p72-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka swim class day  betting ring   social foothold one week after entrance ceremony  professor  sotomura  runs breast size odds  1000 point bets  scene others  yamauchi claims he confessed to sakura  she was huge  man  ak doubts the claim jealous of their easy banter   i couldn t let this opportunity go to waste    joins betting not for gambling but belonging  doesn t know half the class s names  umm  so  is it okay if i join you  willing to play along with crude rituals as social entry fee  keeps private assessment  men have only two things constantly on their minds  he files  doesn t endorse","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Swim-class day: betting ring + social foothold<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.72-75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">one week after entrance ceremony; Professor (Sotomura) runs breast-size odds, 1000-point bets [scene-others] Yamauchi claims he confessed to Sakura (&quot;She was huge, man&quot;); AK doubts the claim<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">jealous of their easy banter; &quot;I couldn&#x27;t let this opportunity go to waste&quot; — joins betting not for gambling but belonging; doesn&#x27;t know half the class&#x27;s names<span class=\"pg\">p.73-74<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Umm. So, is it okay if I join you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> willing to play along with crude rituals as social entry fee; keeps private assessment (&quot;men have only two things constantly on their minds&quot; he files, doesn&#x27;t endorse)<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p68-1\">← Before: Group chat: first male-group contact exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p76-1\">→ After: Pool: girls counter-surveil; Kushida &amp; Horikita bodies noticed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p76-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka pool  girls counter surveil  kushida   horikita bodies noticed 50m indoor pool  boys plan to ogle  girls route around them via 2f observation deck real time social calibration   had i started talking naturally to ike and the others  this was the moment for a new friendship to be born  kushida voluptuous  d e estimate  then horikita in swimsuit   she looked good  not bad at all  but if i stared  something bad would result  internal battle to stay normal attraction acknowledged instantly then suppressed for stability   pattern of denying self impulses to stay unremarkable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Pool: girls counter-surveil; Kushida &amp; Horikita bodies noticed<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.76-79<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">50m indoor pool; boys plan to ogle; girls route around them via 2F observation deck<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">real-time social calibration: &quot;Had I started talking naturally to Ike and the others?... This was the moment for a new friendship to be born.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77-78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Kushida voluptuous (D/E estimate); then Horikita in swimsuit: &quot;She looked good. Not bad at all. But if I stared... something bad would result.&quot; internal battle to stay normal<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> attraction acknowledged instantly then suppressed for stability — pattern of denying self impulses to stay unremarkable<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p72-1\">← Before: Swim-class day: betting ring + social foothold<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p81-1\">→ After: First physical tell: &quot;above average&quot; forearms/back<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p81-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka first physical tell   above average  forearms back poolside  before class starts  horikita scrutinizes ak s body  judging from the development of your forearms and your back muscles  you seem above average   i guess my parents blessed me with good genes   deflection   i don t think that s the only reason  first canon evidence of hidden training   muscle development visible despite clubless  unathletic cover  observer   horikita s sharp eye only lies smooth when cornered  good genes  registers her dissatisfaction  keeps cover","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p81-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">First physical tell: &quot;above average&quot; forearms/back<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.81<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">poolside, before class starts; Horikita scrutinizes AK&#x27;s body<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;judging from the development of your forearms and your back muscles, you seem above average.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I guess my parents blessed me with good genes?&quot; (deflection)<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t think that&#x27;s the only reason.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> first canon evidence of hidden training — muscle development visible despite clubless, unathletic cover; observer = Horikita&#x27;s sharp eye only<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> lies smooth when cornered (&quot;good genes&quot;); registers her dissatisfaction, keeps cover<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p76-1\">← Before: Pool: girls counter-surveil; Kushida &amp; Horikita bodies noticed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p82-1\">→ After: Swim races: hierarchy data + Koenji 23.22s<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p82-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka swim races  hierarchy data   koenji 23 22s 50m indoor pool  pe teacher  1st place   5000 points  last   supplementary lessons class rewards points for athletic wins   micro economy of effort horikita swims  28s  wins her heat comfortably  onodera  ex team   26s wins girls overall  kushida  31s 4th  i just can t come in last     i don t like competing against people  i just like avoiding trouble  ak finishes 36s  10th of 16   calibrated to dodge last place only  sandbagging by design sudou 25s  hirata 26 13 first  girls adore  sudou vows revenge  koenji 23 22s    beats sudou by  5m in final  textbook dive   wasn t short of breath at all  beats both sudou and implied elite times  my abdominal muscles  back muscles  and psoas major muscle seem to be in good shape  as usual  she examines ak s build   even better built than sudou    his cover under casual scrutiny  nervous  state of emergency   i m aiming for kushida chan  don t get in the way    ak privately dismisses odds  and his own","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p82-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Swim races: hierarchy data + Koenji 23.22s<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.82-88<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">50m indoor pool; PE teacher; 1st place = 5000 points, last = supplementary lessons<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I just can&#x27;t come in last.&quot; / &quot;I don&#x27;t like competing against people. I just like avoiding trouble&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84-85<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;My abdominal muscles, back muscles, and psoas major muscle seem to be in good shape, as usual.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m aiming for Kushida-chan. Don&#x27;t get in the way!&quot; — AK privately dismisses odds (and his own)<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> class rewards points for athletic wins — micro-economy of effort<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Horikita swims ~28s, wins her heat comfortably; Onodera (ex-team) ~26s wins girls overall; Kushida ~31s 4th<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK finishes 36s, 10th of 16 — calibrated to dodge last place only; sandbagging by design<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Sudou 25s; Hirata 26.13 first (girls adore); Sudou vows revenge<span class=\"pg\">p.85-86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> **Koenji 23.22s** — beats Sudou by ~5m in final; textbook dive; &quot;wasn&#x27;t short of breath at all&quot;; beats both Sudou and implied elite times<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> she examines AK&#x27;s build: &quot;even better built than Sudou&quot; — his cover under casual scrutiny; nervous &quot;state of emergency&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p81-1\">← Before: First physical tell: &quot;above average&quot; forearms/back<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p89-1\">→ After: Ch.5 &quot;Friends&quot;: café refusals + Hirata&#x27;s concern<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p89-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  friends  cafe refusals   hirata s concern classroom after class  kushida s repeated invitations bounced  don t invite me again  it s a bother   i ll invite you again   smiling  unbowed  he asks ak to nudge horikita toward people  bullying prevention worry  i absolutely do not want any bullying in our class   well  that s up to the individual  isn t it    declines to intervene directly predicts within a month she d be  like a tumor in our class  chooses non involvement   then immediately violates it  p 91","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p89-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 &quot;Friends&quot;: café refusals + Hirata&#x27;s concern<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.89-90<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">classroom after class; Kushida&#x27;s repeated invitations bounced<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Don&#x27;t invite me again. It&#x27;s a bother,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ll invite you again.&quot; (smiling, unbowed)<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, that&#x27;s up to the individual, isn&#x27;t it?&quot; — declines to intervene directly<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> he asks AK to nudge Horikita toward people; bullying-prevention worry (&quot;I absolutely do not want any bullying in our class&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> predicts within a month she&#x27;d be &quot;like a tumor in our class&quot;; chooses non-involvement — then immediately violates it (p.91+)<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p82-1\">← Before: Swim races: hierarchy data + Koenji 23.22s<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p91-1\">→ After: Kushida&#x27;s recruitment of AK (dorm wall → plan)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p91-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kushida s recruitment of ak  dorm wall   plan  dorm corridor  kushida waited for him  takes his hand  have you seen horikita san smile even once  class social map   4 influential girls  facades  kushida exception   loved by every group   plus  she was really cute  cuteness makes everything better   won t you help me   cute   pleading   upturned eyes   lethal   his internal formula   well  i guess i don t have a choice  just this once  okay  folds for warmth despite trouble aversion   just this once    his standard self permission plan  ak invites horikita to palate first  kushida s friends stage seat churn   staged  coincidence  kushida   i think that horikita san trusts you  ayanokouji kun     she seems to trust you more than anyone else in the class  at the very least  attributes her trust to bus seat coincidence only  files possibility that chance meetings create any bond    might eventually become lovers  fantasy re kushida  one percent chance he admits","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p91-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kushida&#x27;s recruitment of AK (dorm wall → plan)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.91-94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">dorm corridor; Kushida waited for him; takes his hand<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;have you seen Horikita-san smile even once?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Won&#x27;t you…help me?&quot; (Cute + Pleading + Upturned Eyes = Lethal — his internal formula)<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, I guess I don&#x27;t have a choice. Just this once, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> class social map: ~4 influential girls, façades; Kushida exception — loved by every group; &quot;Plus, she was really cute. Cuteness makes everything better.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> folds for warmth despite trouble-aversion; &quot;just this once&quot; = his standard self-permission<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> plan: AK invites Horikita to Palate first; Kushida&#x27;s friends stage seat churn → staged &quot;coincidence&quot;; Kushida: &quot;I think that Horikita-san trusts you, Ayanokouji-kun&quot; — &quot;She seems to trust you more than anyone else in the class, at the very least.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93-94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> attributes her trust to bus-seat coincidence only; files possibility that chance meetings create any bond — &quot;might eventually become lovers&quot; fantasy re Kushida, one percent chance he admits<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p89-1\">← Before: Ch.5 &quot;Friends&quot;: café refusals + Hirata&#x27;s concern<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p95-1\">→ After: Palate café: setup exposed; Horikita&#x27;s aloneness bombshell<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p95-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka palate cafe  setup exposed  horikita s aloneness bombshell campus cafe palate  staged meeting executed then burned ak s cover reason  male alone cafe taboo  pancakes pretext  i don t like this  what are you plotting    saw through it  class d faces  impossible seat turnover timing  sorry  horikita  we planned this   confesses when further lies would sink them   horikita san  please be my friend   do you think that feelings of trust would arise out of something forced  ak intercedes   i kind of understand your thoughts on the matter  horikita  in junior high  i never knew anyone s contact information or hung out with anyone after class  i was always alone   you wanted friends but couldn t get them  i considered friends unnecessary  so i didn t make any  saying we are similar would be incorrect   it will be my ninth year in a row of being alone  if you include kindergarten  it would actually be slightly longer    lifelong isolation  stated flatly kushida s odd line   when i saw you  i felt like it wasn t the first time we d met   planted  unexplained  recovers smile instantly after collapse  thanks ak   i feel like horikita san might hate you now  ak wanted horikita to  consider the benefits of friendship    genuine altruism surfacing under kushida s influence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Palate café: setup exposed; Horikita&#x27;s aloneness bombshell<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.95-100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">campus café Palate; staged meeting executed then burned<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t like this. What are you plotting?&quot; — saw through it: Class D faces, impossible seat-turnover timing<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sorry, Horikita. We planned this.&quot; (confesses when further lies would sink them)<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Horikita-san. Please be my friend!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> AK&#x27;s cover reason: male-alone café taboo; pancakes pretext<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;do you think that feelings of trust would arise out of something forced?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> AK intercedes: &quot;I kind of understand your thoughts on the matter, Horikita... In junior high, I never knew anyone&#x27;s contact information or hung out with anyone after class. I was always alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You wanted friends but couldn&#x27;t get them. I considered friends unnecessary, so I didn&#x27;t make any. Saying we are similar would be incorrect.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99-100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> &quot;It will be my ninth year in a row of being alone... if you include kindergarten, it would actually be slightly longer.&quot; — lifelong isolation, stated flatly<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida&#x27;s odd line: &quot;When I saw you, I felt like it wasn&#x27;t the first time we&#x27;d met.&quot; (planted; unexplained)<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> recovers smile instantly after collapse; thanks AK; &quot;I feel like Horikita-san might hate you now&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK wanted Horikita to &quot;consider the benefits of friendship&quot; — genuine altruism surfacing under Kushida&#x27;s influence<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p91-1\">← Before: Kushida&#x27;s recruitment of AK (dorm wall → plan)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p101-1\">→ After: Aftermath advice: wait for coincidence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p101-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka aftermath advice  wait for coincidence cafe continues after horikita leaves  just think of horikita as a special case  your only option is to wait for a real coincidence to come along  her goal restated  friends with everyone in d  and  other classes  one failure   unacceptable  if i can t become friends with one girl in my class  then that means i ll never achieve my goal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Aftermath advice: wait for coincidence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.101<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">café continues after Horikita leaves<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just think of Horikita as a special case. Your only option is to wait for a real coincidence to come along.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;if I can&#x27;t become friends with one girl in my class, then that means I&#x27;ll never achieve my goal…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> her goal restated: friends with everyone in D *and* other classes; one failure = unacceptable<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p95-1\">← Before: Palate café: setup exposed; Horikita&#x27;s aloneness bombshell<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p102-1\">→ After: Three weeks in: friends acquired + May pop quiz<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p102-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka three weeks in  friends acquired   may pop quiz math class   idiot trio   ike yamauchi sudou  formed ak now has casual friends  store pool group chat path   human relationships are rather mysterious    no exact friendship birth moment rumor  dating hirata  ak s inner read  cute   girly  type  would ve pounced on pretty boys in jh   apologizes to her in his head  notes his type   kinder  more ladylike girl   i hate that look on your face    catches his sleazy thoughts live  may pop quiz    5 subjects   4 qs  100 pts  first 17 easy  final 3  order of magnitude  harder  math needs complex formulae  chiyabashira   it won t be reflected in your report cards    odd phrasing  ak senses another evaluation channel  i guess i ll just solve these problems the same way i did on the entrance exam    states he can match entrance exam difficulty casually  watching horikita ace it assumes hidden tests are for evaluation of something else  suspicious of school s true metrics from day one","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p102-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Three weeks in: friends acquired + May pop quiz<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.102-105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">math class; &quot;Idiot Trio&quot; (Ike/Yamauchi/Sudou) formed **May pop quiz** — 5 subjects × 4 Qs, 100 pts; first 17 easy, final 3 &quot;order of magnitude&quot; harder (math needs complex formulae)<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I hate that look on your face.&quot; — catches his sleazy thoughts live<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> AK now has casual friends (store→pool→group chat path); &quot;Human relationships are rather mysterious&quot; — no exact friendship-birth moment<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> rumor: dating Hirata; AK&#x27;s inner read: cute, &quot;girly&quot; type, would&#x27;ve pounced on pretty boys in JH — apologizes to her in his head; notes his type: &quot;kinder, more ladylike girl&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Chiyabashira: &quot;It won&#x27;t be reflected in your report cards&quot; — odd phrasing; AK senses another evaluation channel<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;I guess I&#x27;ll just solve these problems the same way I did on the entrance exam&quot; — states he can match entrance-exam difficulty casually; watching Horikita ace it<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> assumes hidden tests are for evaluation of something else; suspicious of school&#x27;s true metrics from day one<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p101-1\">← Before: Aftermath advice: wait for coincidence<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p106-1\">→ After: Dating rumors + point-burn culture<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p106-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka dating rumors   point burn culture vending machine hangout with idiot trio boys assume he s dating her  he denies flatly  yamauchi   she disappears into the background  like a shadow    class barely knows her name without kushida admits remembering  about half of their names    his own class knowledge is thin confirmed dating karuizawa  hondou saw hand holding  yamauchi burned  90k pts in 3 weeks  ps viva  25k  free mineral water   vegetable set   survival tier  ak buys cocoa milk  small point spends  to avoid social friction uses minor spending as hassle insurance  observes others  financial self destruction without comment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Dating rumors + point-burn culture<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.106-110<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">vending machine hangout with Idiot Trio<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">admits remembering &quot;about half of their names&quot; — his own class knowledge is thin<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> boys assume he&#x27;s dating her; he denies flatly; Yamauchi: &quot;She disappears into the background, like a shadow&quot; — class barely knows her name without Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> confirmed dating Karuizawa (Hondou saw hand-holding)<span class=\"pg\">p.107-108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Yamauchi burned &gt;90k pts in 3 weeks (PS Viva ~25k); free mineral water + vegetable set = survival tier; AK buys cocoa/milk (small point spends) to avoid social friction<span class=\"pg\">p.108-110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> uses minor spending as hassle-insurance; observes others&#x27; financial self-destruction without comment<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p102-1\">← Before: Three weeks in: friends acquired + May pop quiz<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p112-1\">→ After: Mixed hangout: boutique + points philosophy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p112-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka mixed hangout  boutique   points philosophy after class group  ike  yamauchi  kushida   ak  kushida adds hirata  karuizawa  matsushita  mori organizes three subgroups by reading the room  occasionally smiles sweetly at ak   he notices the management  not just the warmth karuizawa spends 30k on clothes  hirata carries bags  ike wants 200 300k month  hirata kushida fear luxury corrupts money sense post graduation  hmm  well  i don t really fully understand it yet  i m not sure    refuses to perform a position on the point economy school doesn t select on standardized tests  ike yamauchi dumb   smart mix admitted  curiosity seed   how in the world did it select potential students  withholds opinions he hasn t finished computing  public ignorance as default","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mixed hangout: boutique + points philosophy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.112-119<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">after-class group: Ike, Yamauchi, Kushida + AK; Kushida adds Hirata, Karuizawa, Matsushita, Mori<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hmm, well, I don&#x27;t really fully understand it yet. I&#x27;m not sure.&quot; — refuses to perform a position on the point economy<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">school doesn&#x27;t select on standardized tests (Ike/Yamauchi dumb + smart mix admitted); curiosity seed: &quot;how in the world did it select potential students?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118-119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> organizes three subgroups by reading the room; occasionally smiles sweetly at AK — he notices the management, not just the warmth<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Karuizawa spends 30k on clothes (Hirata carries bags); Ike wants 200-300k/month; Hirata+Kushida fear luxury corrupts money sense post-graduation<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> withholds opinions he hasn&#x27;t finished computing; public ignorance as default<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p106-1\">← Before: Dating rumors + point-burn culture<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p120-1\">→ After: May 1: points don&#x27;t arrive (crisis trigger)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p120-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka may 1  points don t arrive  crisis trigger  first morning of may  hondou yamauchi ike report no deposit  ak s balance unchanged too points were wired  without any issues    class d received nothing   are you kids really that dumb  ominous first concrete point loss event  ak registered early  checked that morning  assumed wires would come later  calm under systemic shock  watches rather than reacts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">May 1: points don&#x27;t arrive (crisis trigger)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.120<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">first morning of May; Hondou/Yamauchi/Ike report no deposit; AK&#x27;s balance unchanged too<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> points were wired &quot;without any issues&quot; — class D received nothing; &quot;Are you kids really that dumb?&quot; ominous<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> first concrete point-loss event; AK registered early (checked that morning, assumed wires would come later)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> calm under systemic shock; watches rather than reacts<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p112-1\">← Before: Mixed hangout: boutique + points philosophy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p121-1\">→ After: Point crisis explained: Class D = defective<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p121-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka point crisis explained  class d   defective may 1 homeroom  chiyabashira reveals zero points  we re in class d  so we didn t receive a single point    solves it first  casually 98 absences late   391 talking phone infractions in 1 month   100k wasted   your class s results are reflected in the points  evaluation methods undisclosed even perfect behavior won t raise points from zero baseline this month   cruel hint  fix behavior for next month s eval  not retroactive standings poster  a 940  b 650  c 490  d 0  1000 pts   100 000 yen  points   class rank   500 promotes to c he   horikita both flag numbers  too even    suspected engineered crisis sorting    students are sorted by their level of excellence  class d    the last bastion for failures  you are the worst of the worst  you re defective   i  on the other hand  was glad  this meant i couldn t go any lower    bottom is safety  anonymity secured by placement reads systemic humiliation as personal opportunity  joy in having no reputation to lose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Point crisis explained: Class D = defective<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.121-127<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">May 1 homeroom; Chiyabashira reveals zero points<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;We&#x27;re in Class D, so we didn&#x27;t receive a single point.&quot; — solves it first, casually<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">he + Horikita both flag numbers &quot;too even&quot; — suspected engineered crisis<span class=\"pg\">p.125-126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">**&quot;I, on the other hand, was glad. This meant I couldn&#x27;t go any lower.&quot;** — bottom is safety; anonymity secured by placement<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> 98 absences/late + 391 talking/phone infractions in 1 month → 100k wasted; &quot;your class&#x27;s results are reflected in the points&quot;; evaluation methods undisclosed<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> even perfect behavior won&#x27;t raise points from zero baseline this month — cruel hint: fix behavior for NEXT month&#x27;s eval, not retroactive<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> standings poster: A=940, B=650, C=490, D=0; 1000 pts = 100,000 yen; points = class rank; ≥500 promotes to C<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> sorting = &quot;students are sorted by their level of excellence&quot;; Class D = &quot;the last bastion for failures. You are the worst of the worst. You&#x27;re defective.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> reads systemic humiliation as personal opportunity; joy in having no reputation to lose<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p120-1\">← Before: May 1: points don&#x27;t arrive (crisis trigger)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p127-1\">→ After: Quiz results + the Class A ultimatum<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p127-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka quiz results   the class a ultimatum same homeroom  pop quiz scores posted with red line at 32 sudou 14  ike 24  avg 65  below 32 under midterm rules   dropout  7 students at risk  koenji 90   tied yukimura  solved one super hard problem  dramatic proof intellect exists in d  your only option is to overtake class a  this school guarantees nothing for any other students    graduation futures gate on class a rejects resentment   the school simply hasn t seen my potential yet  the school would come crying to take me back  future secured by conglomerate  class rank  a trivial matter  ak watches the reveal without visible reaction  files school s true leverage structure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Quiz results + the Class A ultimatum<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.127-130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">same homeroom; pop-quiz scores posted with red line at 32<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> rejects resentment: &quot;The school simply hasn&#x27;t seen my potential yet... the school would come crying to take me back.&quot; Future secured by conglomerate; class rank &quot;a trivial matter&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Sudou 14, Ike 24, avg 65; below-32 under midterm rules = dropout (7 students at risk)<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Koenji 90 — tied Yukimura, solved one super-hard problem; dramatic proof intellect exists in D<span class=\"pg\">p.128-129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> **&quot;your only option is to overtake Class A. This school guarantees nothing for any other students.&quot;** — graduation futures gate on Class A<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK watches the reveal without visible reaction; files school&#x27;s true leverage structure<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p121-1\">← Before: Point crisis explained: Class D = defective<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p131-1\">→ After: Chaos, Kushida&#x27;s de-escalation, strategy-meeting refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p131-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka chaos  kushida s de escalation  strategy meeting refusal break  yukimura spirals  grabs hirata s collar  kushida separates them yukimura  reflexively took half a step back  from her   her presence alone disarms aggression  class unifying aura noted ak photographs class point poster   calculating deduction rates in real time  wants countermeasure math unusually impatient  her frame  points are byproduct  free options exist  ak spent  20k only  they baited us into spending all our points over the course of this one month  and we fell for it   scene others  hirata podium call for cooperation  sudou rebels  just don t involve me  and walks  class immediately resents sudou  top latecomer  recruits ak   horikita to small strategy discussion  i refuse  i won t participate   twice  ak declines too    ah i ll pass  i m sorry    motive  if only horikita absent  she d be treated like sudou explains own refusal as protecting her from scapegoating  hirata  probably understood what i was thinking  her cryptic   if an unintelligent student tries to lead the discussion  the group will fall further into chaos  i can t meekly accept my current situation    seeds her s system   individual action strategy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chaos, Kushida&#x27;s de-escalation, strategy-meeting refusal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.131-136<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">break; Yukimura spirals, grabs Hirata&#x27;s collar; Kushida separates them<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;They baited us into spending all our points over the course of this one month, and we fell for it.&quot; [scene-others] Hirata podium call for cooperation; Sudou rebels &quot;Just don&#x27;t involve me&quot; and walks; class immediately resents…<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I refuse. I won&#x27;t participate.&quot; (twice)<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">AK declines too — &quot;Ah…I&#x27;ll pass. I&#x27;m sorry.&quot; — motive: if only Horikita absent, she&#x27;d be treated like Sudou<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Yukimura &quot;reflexively took half a step back&quot; from her — her presence alone disarms aggression; class-unifying aura noted<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK photographs class-point poster — calculating deduction rates in real time; wants countermeasure math<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> unusually impatient; her frame: points are byproduct, free options exist; AK spent ~20k only<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;They baited us into spending all our points over the course of this one month, and we fell for it.&quot; [scene-others] Hirata podium call for cooperation; Sudou rebels &quot;Just don&#x27;t involve me&quot; and walks; class immediately resents Sudou (top latecomer)<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> recruits AK + Horikita to small strategy discussion<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> explains own refusal as protecting her from scapegoating; Hirata &quot;probably understood what I was thinking&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> her cryptic: &quot;if an unintelligent student tries to lead the discussion, the group will fall further into chaos... I can&#x27;t meekly accept my current situation&quot; — seeds her S-System / individual-action strategy<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p127-1\">← Before: Quiz results + the Class A ultimatum<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p137-1\">→ After: Resale desperation + summons to Chiyabashira<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p137-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou hoshinomiya-chie ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka resale desperation   summons to chiyabashira the pa summons names him   ayanokouji kun  from first year class d  after school  yamauchi tries to flip ps viva to ak  1k bid  then professor  22k  kushida lends 2k to karuizawa freely borrows points from multiple girls serially  ak flags lending as  a recipe for disaster   i can t just ignore a friend in need    generosity uncalculating  or masked  ak spent  barely any  points himself pa summons   ayanokouji kun  from first year class d  please come see chiyabashira sensei in the faculty office  introduces self  class b teacher  bff of chiyabashira since hs  flirts openly  caresses his cheek  ak freezes  considers then rejects licking her fingers escape  had a feeling that d get me expelled  physical comedy survival instinct  absurd options evaluated seriously","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Resale desperation + summons to Chiyabashira<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.137-140<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">after school; Yamauchi tries to flip PS Viva to AK (1k bid) then Professor (22k); Kushida lends 2k to Karuizawa freely PA summons: &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, from first-year Class D. Please come see Chiyabashira-sensei in the faculty office.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> introduces self: Class B teacher, BFF of Chiyabashira since HS; flirts openly (caresses his cheek); AK freezes, considers then rejects licking-her-fingers escape &quot;had a feeling that&#x27;d get me expelled&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139-140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> The PA summons names him: “Ayanokouji-kun, from first-year Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> borrows points from multiple girls serially; AK flags lending as &quot;a recipe for disaster&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;I can&#x27;t just ignore a friend in need&quot; — generosity uncalculating (or masked); AK spent &quot;barely any&quot; points himself<span class=\"pg\">p.138-139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> physical-comedy survival instinct; absurd options evaluated seriously<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p131-1\">← Before: Chaos, Kushida&#x27;s de-escalation, strategy-meeting refusal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p141-1\">→ After: Guidance room: Horikita&#x27;s protest (AK hidden in kitchenette)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p141-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka guidance room  horikita s protest  ak hidden in kitchenette  guidance office  chiyabashira hides ak in kitchenette  horikita demands sorting explanation  scene others   p 141 142   ichinose honami  first appearance  light pink hair    lures hoshinomiya away via  student council wishes to discuss   i solved nearly every problem on the entrance examination  at the very least  i shouldn t have been sorted into class d  horikita    3rd highest entrance test score  among first years  interview  evaluated you quite highly  academic superiority   school s metric  hereditary succession society speech    back  ak groans  chest hurts   white room trigger residue  sudou admitted   non academic criteria exist  class a under crushing pressure   strange students who would happily be  set at a low level    aimed at ak  i will ask the school again  at another time    won t drop it she almost says  bro   brother  when told someone relevant is waiting   sibling secret on a knife edge  ak identifies himself instead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p141-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Guidance room: Horikita&#x27;s protest (AK hidden in kitchenette)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.141-145<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">guidance office; Chiyabashira hides AK in kitchenette; Horikita demands sorting explanation [scene-others] (p.141-142) **Ichinose Honami** first appearance (light-pink hair) — lures Hoshinomiya away via &quot;student council wishes to discuss&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I solved nearly every problem on the entrance examination... At the very least, I shouldn&#x27;t have been sorted into Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142-143<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> academic superiority ≠ school&#x27;s metric; hereditary-succession society speech — **[back] AK groans, chest hurts** (White Room trigger residue)<span class=\"pg\">p.143-144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I will ask the school again, at another time.&quot; — won&#x27;t drop it<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Horikita = **3rd-highest entrance test score** among first-years; interview &quot;evaluated you quite highly&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Sudou admitted → non-academic criteria exist; Class A under crushing pressure; &quot;Strange students who would happily be... set at a low level&quot; — aimed at AK<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> she almost says &quot;bro—&quot; (brother) when told someone relevant is waiting — sibling secret on a knife-edge; AK identifies himself instead<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p137-1\">← Before: Resale desperation + summons to Chiyabashira<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p145-1\">→ After: The all-50s reveal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p145-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the all 50s reveal chiyabashira shows horikita ak s entrance sheet   short test paper entrance   50 50 50 50 50  across five subjects  short test also 50  3  solved 5th math problem   complex formula  perfect  vs 10th problem 76  completion   he failed an easy one  chiyabashira   he did it intentionally   it s a coincidence  there s no evidence that it s not  besides  what would i gain by manipulating my scores  if i were intelligent enough to achieve high marks  i would ve tried to get perfect scores    deliberate low score camouflage strategy  first explicit  he may be even more intelligent than you  horikita    she flinches  ak prays her to stop maintains the coincidence lie under direct teacher pressure   odious student  self branding  jokes about destroying furniture   e class   expelled  punchline filed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p145-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The all-50s reveal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.145-148<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chiyabashira shows Horikita AK&#x27;s entrance sheet + short-test paper<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s a coincidence. There&#x27;s no evidence that it&#x27;s not. Besides, what would I gain by manipulating my scores... If I were intelligent enough to achieve high marks, I would&#x27;ve tried to get perfect scores.&quot; — deliberate low-score…<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;He may be even more intelligent than you, Horikita.&quot; — she flinches; AK prays her to stop<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> entrance: **50/50/50/50/50** across five subjects; short test also 50<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> **3% solved 5th math problem** (complex formula, perfect) vs 10th problem 76% completion — he failed an easy one; Chiyabashira: &quot;He did it intentionally.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s a coincidence. There&#x27;s no evidence that it&#x27;s not. Besides, what would I gain by manipulating my scores... If I were intelligent enough to achieve high marks, I would&#x27;ve tried to get perfect scores.&quot; — deliberate low-score camouflage strategy, first explicit<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> maintains the coincidence lie under direct teacher pressure; &quot;odious student&quot; self-branding; jokes about destroying furniture; &quot;E Class = expelled&quot; punchline filed<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p141-1\">← Before: Guidance room: Horikita&#x27;s protest (AK hidden in kitchenette)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p148-1\">→ After: Hallway: her motive + the pawn offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p148-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hallway  her motive   the pawn offer post guidance walk  horikita presses on the scores  first  i want to ascertain this school s true motives  why was i put into class d  when i discover the answer  i ll aim for a  no  i will definitely make it to a  her anxiety replaced overflowing confidence  his read  individual heroics can t fix class  class drags individuals down  i need your help  ayanokouji kun   i refuse    she overrides   i always knew you d help  i heard the voice inside your head   shogi analogy   right now  i don t need a gold or silver general  i want a pawn   hirata   gold silver  ak   pawn   haven t you been thinking   i ve always been a pawn  i don t want to advance  all along    nails his core self image first explicit alliance attempt  rejected for now  she leaves door open  contact me once you ve given it some thought","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hallway: her motive + the pawn offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.148-151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">post-guidance walk; Horikita presses on the scores<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> **&quot;First, I want to ascertain this school&#x27;s true motives. Why was I put into Class D?... When I discover the answer, I&#x27;ll aim for A. No, I will definitely make it to A.&quot;**<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I need your help, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I refuse,&quot; — she overrides: &quot;I always knew you&#x27;d help... I heard the voice inside your head.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> her anxiety replaced overflowing confidence; his read: individual heroics can&#x27;t fix class; class drags individuals down<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> **shogi analogy: &quot;Right now, I don&#x27;t need a gold or silver general. I want a pawn.&quot;** (Hirata = gold/silver, AK = pawn)<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;haven&#x27;t you been thinking, &#x27;I&#x27;ve always been a pawn, I don&#x27;t want to advance,&#x27; all along?&quot; — nails his core self-image<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> first explicit alliance attempt; rejected for now; she leaves door open (&quot;contact me once you&#x27;ve given it some thought&quot;)<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p145-1\">← Before: The all-50s reveal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p152-1\">→ After: Compass stab #2 + Hirata&#x27;s study group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p152-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka compass stab  2   hirata s study group class  ak dozes  horikita stabs arm with compass denial comedy  when did i stab with you a compass needle  ayanokouji kun    emtl phrasing kept  then purpose   if you get caught sleeping  that would undoubtedly lead to a loss in points    she polices his  class s  point relevant behavior with violence announces study group  classroom 5 7pm daily until midterms  high scorers coach  sudou ike yamauchi abstain  rocky with hirata since intro game fight","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Compass stab #2 + Hirata&#x27;s study group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.152-153<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">class; AK dozes; Horikita stabs arm with compass<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> denial comedy (&quot;When did I stab with you a compass needle, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot; — EMTL phrasing kept); then purpose: &quot;If you get caught sleeping, that would undoubtedly lead to a loss in points&quot; — she polices his (class&#x27;s) point-relevant behavior with violence<span class=\"pg\">p.152-153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> announces study group: classroom 5-7pm daily until midterms, high-scorers coach; Sudou/Ike/Yamauchi abstain; rocky with Hirata since intro-game fight<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p148-1\">← Before: Hallway: her motive + the pawn offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p154-1\">→ After: Lunch bribery: tutoring deal + first contact info<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p154-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka lunch bribery  tutoring deal   first contact info cafeteria  horikita treats ak  special set  grabs his hand mid meal strategy  lateness talking fixed  half reasons gone  midterms next lever  hirata s group won t reach the three at risk   bring them to the library  and i ll tutor them   this is insane  do you honestly think someone who does his best to lead an utterly harmless and inoffensive life   it s not a matter of can or can t  just do it  she invokes cafe betrayal debt   i said that to kushida san  i don t remember saying that to you    dirty play acknowledged   cooperate  or make me your enemy   i can t guarantee anything  are you okay with that   receives horikita s phone   email   first girl s contact info of his high school life   wasn t particularly happy  about it being hers  coerced cooperation  keeps exit language  accepts under blackmail framing because friendship safety nets  sudou ike  at risk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p154-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Lunch bribery: tutoring deal + first contact info<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.154-157<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">cafeteria; Horikita treats AK (special set), grabs his hand mid-meal<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> strategy: lateness/talking fixed (&gt;half reasons gone); midterms next lever; Hirata&#x27;s group won&#x27;t reach the three at-risk; &quot;Bring them to the library, and I&#x27;ll tutor them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This is insane. Do you honestly think someone who does his best to lead an utterly harmless and inoffensive life...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s not a matter of can or can&#x27;t. Just do it,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> she invokes café-betrayal debt: &quot;I said that to Kushida-san. I don&#x27;t remember saying that to you&quot; — dirty play acknowledged; &quot;Cooperate? Or make me your enemy?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t guarantee anything. Are you okay with that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> **receives Horikita&#x27;s phone + email — first girl&#x27;s contact info of his high school life** (&quot;wasn&#x27;t particularly happy&quot; about it being hers)<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> coerced cooperation; keeps exit language; accepts under blackmail-framing because friendship-safety nets (Sudou/Ike) at risk<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p152-1\">← Before: Compass stab #2 + Hirata&#x27;s study group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p158-1\">→ After: Recruitment fails; incentive brainstorm; Kushida pivot<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p158-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ike-kanji kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka recruitment fails  incentive brainstorm  kushida pivot classroom  ak tries direct invites  horikita  i don t really know anything about her  sounds fishy  i ll pass  i ll be fine cramming for the test the night before   pass  a high school student s free time is precious   i still have 425 plans remaining    sarcasm  then incentive logic  needs concrete juicy bonus for studying proposes horikita as girlfriend   kiss incentives   met with death threats  compass at neck   horikita clearly didn t understand men  identifies her as perfect recruiter  sociable  ike s love  high scores    then freezes  horikita s anti kushida stance  self censors mid call","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p158-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Recruitment fails; incentive brainstorm; Kushida pivot<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.158-160<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">classroom; AK tries direct invites<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Horikita? I don&#x27;t really know anything about her. Sounds fishy; I&#x27;ll pass. I&#x27;ll be fine cramming for the test the night before.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> &quot;Pass!... A high school student&#x27;s free time is precious&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I still have 425 plans remaining,&quot; — sarcasm; then incentive logic: needs concrete juicy bonus for studying<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> proposes Horikita-as-girlfriend / kiss incentives — met with death threats (compass at neck); &quot;Horikita clearly didn&#x27;t understand men&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159-160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> identifies her as perfect recruiter (sociable, Ike&#x27;s love, high scores) — then freezes: Horikita&#x27;s anti-Kushida stance; self-censors mid-call<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p154-1\">← Before: Lunch bribery: tutoring deal + first contact info<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p162-1\">→ After: Kushida recruited (ambassador of goodwill)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p162-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kushida recruited  ambassador of goodwill  hallway after class  ak pitches study group rescue via kushida  rejoice  kushida  you ve been selected as an ambassador of goodwill   it s cruel to expel someone for getting a bad grade  i ll do anything i can to be useful    frames horikita as  starting to think of her classmates as friends  already has sudou ike yamauchi numbers  only ak   horikita missing  asks if ak horikita dating  class girl rumor  gets ak s number    another girl s number  logged deploys theatrical framing  ambassador  to make recruitment feel like honor not labor","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p162-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kushida recruited (ambassador of goodwill)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.162-166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">hallway after class; AK pitches study-group rescue via Kushida<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Rejoice, Kushida. You&#x27;ve been selected as an ambassador of goodwill.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s cruel to expel someone for getting a bad grade... I&#x27;ll do anything I can to be useful!&quot; — frames Horikita as &quot;starting to think of her classmates as friends&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> already has Sudou/Ike/Yamauchi numbers; only AK + Horikita missing; asks if AK-Horikita dating (class-girl rumor); gets AK&#x27;s number — &quot;another girl&#x27;s number&quot; logged<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> deploys theatrical framing (&quot;ambassador&quot;) to make recruitment feel like honor not labor<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p158-1\">← Before: Recruitment fails; incentive brainstorm; Kushida pivot<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p167-1\">→ After: Night negotiations: Horikita&#x27;s veto + Kushida&#x27;s takeover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p167-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka night negotiations  horikita s veto   kushida s takeover dorm  texts then phone call with horikita  then call with kushida  i don t remember giving you permission   re kushida    objects to unsanctioned networking deal  kushida may gather  may not join   i will not allow her into our study group  i refuse to budge on this   don t you feel uncomfortable sitting next to someone you hate    explicit hatred stated ruminates  defective product   second year words   even horikita  who appeared flawless  probably had some defects of her own  ak tries to withdraw request  she instantly parses split  was she against me gathering people  or did she not want me to join  takes control   could you leave things to me this time  i ll bring everyone over tomorrow  of course  i ll be coming along  too    comes regardless of veto  i ll leave it to you  then    hands agency away  predicts disaster  proceeds anyway  trouble aversion override for friends  safety","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p167-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Night negotiations: Horikita&#x27;s veto + Kushida&#x27;s takeover<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.167-171<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">dorm; texts then phone call with Horikita; then call with Kushida<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t remember giving you permission&quot; (re Kushida) — objects to unsanctioned networking<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">ruminates &quot;Defective product&quot; (second-year words); &quot;Even Horikita, who appeared flawless, probably had some defects of her own&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll leave it to you, then.&quot; — hands agency away; predicts disaster, proceeds anyway (trouble-aversion override for friends&#x27; safety)<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> deal: Kushida may gather, may NOT join; &quot;I will not allow her into our study group. I refuse to budge on this.&quot;; &quot;Don&#x27;t you feel uncomfortable sitting next to someone you hate?&quot; — explicit hatred stated<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> AK tries to withdraw request; she instantly parses split (&quot;Was she against me gathering people, or did she not want me to join?&quot;); takes control: &quot;Could you leave things to me this time?... I&#x27;ll bring everyone over tomorrow. Of course, I&#x27;ll be coming along, too.&quot; — comes regardless of veto<span class=\"pg\">p.169-170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p162-1\">← Before: Kushida recruited (ambassador of goodwill)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p172-1\">→ After: Study group day 1: collapse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p172-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka study group day 1  collapse library  kushida delivers ike yamauchi sudou   okitani  trojan  okitani  39 pts  blue bob  as entry wedge  confirms he s allowed  then claims own weak scores to force re admission  horikita growls  fine  pass mark   32  horikita target   50 for all  aiming to just skate by is dangerous   i m sorry  you re far too ignorant and incompetent  i seriously shiver at the thought of what the future will bring    teaching style  contempt basketball pro dream mocked by horikita  a simpleton like you  could never hope to go pro  pro income insufficient  collar grab   kushida intercepts his arm faster than ak can move  sudou quits   i took a day off from my club activities for this  her grip speed intervention registered  ak s readiness to grapple noted as too slow   social observer  not physical intervener  this time   scene others  ike quits  i don t care if you get expelled  yamauchi   okitani follow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p172-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Study group day 1: collapse<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.172-177<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">library; Kushida delivers Ike/Yamauchi/Sudou + Okitani (Trojan)<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m sorry, you&#x27;re far too ignorant and incompetent... I seriously shiver at the thought of what the future will bring.&quot; — teaching style: contempt<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Okitani (39 pts, blue bob) as entry wedge: confirms he&#x27;s allowed, then claims own weak scores to force re-admission; Horikita growls &quot;Fine,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172-173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> pass mark = 32; Horikita target = 50 for all (&quot;Aiming to just skate by is dangerous&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> basketball-pro dream mocked by Horikita (&quot;a simpleton like you... could never hope to go pro&quot;; pro income insufficient); collar grab; **Kushida intercepts his arm faster than AK can move**; Sudou quits: &quot;I took a day off from my club activities for this&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176-177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> her grip-speed intervention registered; AK&#x27;s readiness-to-grapple noted as too slow — social observer, not physical intervener (this time) [scene-others] Ike quits (&quot;I don&#x27;t care if you get expelled&quot;); Yamauchi + Okitani follow<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p167-1\">← Before: Night negotiations: Horikita&#x27;s veto + Kushida&#x27;s takeover<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p178-1\">→ After: &quot;Get rid of the dead weight&quot; + divergence<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p178-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka  get rid of the dead weight    divergence library  only ak   horikita   kushida remain  then two  it s better to get rid of the dead weight    expelling failures raises class average  study group   unproductive irritation ak aligns   if that s horikita s answer  then isn t it fine  stands to leave   i definitely don t want everything to fall apart so quickly  horikita s accusation   i don t think that you actually want to save them  kushida   why do you try to antagonize people  that s very sad    exits  you re at least somewhat better than those worthless idiots  if there s some subject you re struggling with  i could teach you   offer  he declines   i just want to talk to my friends  do you have a problem with that   you call them your friends  yet you simply stand by and watch as they re expelled  from my point of view  you re cruel  counter   shouldn t you try to understand sudou s situation  don t you think you d understand him better if you considered his reasons for enrolling   not interested    returns to textbook  alone first real moral pushback against her utilitarian frame  understands her logic  refuses to adopt it fully  keeps friendship tether even at failure risk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p178-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">&quot;Get rid of the dead weight&quot; + divergence<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.178-180<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">library, only AK + Horikita + Kushida remain; then two<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;it&#x27;s better to get rid of the dead weight&quot; — expelling failures raises class average; study group = unproductive irritation<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">AK aligns: &quot;If that&#x27;s Horikita&#x27;s answer, then isn&#x27;t it fine?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re at least somewhat better than those worthless idiots. If there&#x27;s some subject you&#x27;re struggling with, I could teach you.&quot; (offer; he declines)<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> stands to leave: &quot;I definitely don&#x27;t want everything to fall apart so quickly&quot;; Horikita&#x27;s accusation: &quot;I don&#x27;t think that you actually want to save them&quot;; Kushida: &quot;Why do you try to antagonize people? That&#x27;s…very sad&quot; — exits<span class=\"pg\">p.178-179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I just want to talk to my friends. Do you have a problem with that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You call them your friends, yet you simply stand by and watch as they&#x27;re expelled. From my point of view, you&#x27;re cruel.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> counter: &quot;shouldn&#x27;t you try to understand Sudou&#x27;s situation?... Don&#x27;t you think you&#x27;d understand him better if you considered his reasons for enrolling?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Not interested.&quot; — returns to textbook, alone<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> first real moral pushback against her utilitarian frame; understands her logic, refuses to adopt it fully; keeps friendship tether even at failure risk<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p172-1\">← Before: Study group day 1: collapse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p181-1\">→ After: ROOFTOP: Kushida unmasked (MAJOR)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p181-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka rooftop  kushida unmasked  major  school building roof after hours  ak follows kushida  overhears private vent vent   ahhh  so annoying  it d be better if she just died  horikita  you re so annoying    voice  so low that it didn t sound at all like kushida  can t reconcile hate with her forcing proximity  first hypothesis   kushida and horikita were   prior connection  caught when door kicks  confrontation  if you tell anyone what you just heard  i won t forgive you  then rape threat   breast print  evidence  setup  presses his palm to her breast   your fingerprints are on my clothes  evidence of my claim    unhinged cool threat performance  hey  kushida  which is the real you     that s none of your business   is it bad to want everyone to like you  my existence has meaning    core motive  universal likability   existence proof  i absolutely despise gloomy  ordinary guys like you   ak deduction  she knew horikita s name before intros   the only person who knew was sudou  you got close to me so you could spy on her  right    she shudders  prior school connection implied  not confirmed pact of secrecy  even if i did  it s not like anyone would believe me  her read of ak   fundamentally indifferent to other people    bus seat observation as proof  horikita trust analysis   she seems to trust you more than anyone else   jekyll switch  furious   kicks his thigh   grabs bag   returns beaming  let s head back together     i couldn t tell which kushida was the real one  ak unshattered  most people possessed both a public face and a private  inner self","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p181-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">ROOFTOP: Kushida unmasked (MAJOR)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.181-188<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">school building roof after hours; AK follows Kushida; overhears private vent caught when door kicks; confrontation<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> vent: &quot;Ahhh, so annoying!... It&#x27;d be better if she just died…... Horikita, you&#x27;re so annoying!&quot; — voice &quot;so low that it didn&#x27;t sound at all like Kushida&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> **&quot;If you tell anyone what you just heard, I won&#x27;t forgive you.&quot;** then rape-threat + breast-print &quot;evidence&quot; setup: presses his palm to her breast, &quot;Your fingerprints are on my clothes. Evidence of my claim.&quot; — unhinged-cool…<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hey, Kushida. Which is the real you?&quot; — &quot;That&#x27;s none of your business.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> can&#x27;t reconcile hate with her forcing proximity; first hypothesis: &quot;Kushida and Horikita were…&quot; (prior connection)<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> **&quot;If you tell anyone what you just heard, I won&#x27;t forgive you.&quot;** then rape-threat + breast-print &quot;evidence&quot; setup: presses his palm to her breast, &quot;Your fingerprints are on my clothes. Evidence of my claim.&quot; — unhinged-cool threat performance<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is it bad to want everyone to like you?... my existence has meaning.&quot; — core motive: universal likability = existence proof<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I absolutely despise gloomy, ordinary guys like you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> **AK deduction: she knew Horikita&#x27;s name before intros** (&quot;The only person who knew was Sudou... You got close to me so you could spy on her, right?&quot;) — she shudders; prior-school connection implied, not confirmed<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> pact of secrecy (&quot;even if I did, it&#x27;s not like anyone would believe me&quot;); her read of AK: &quot;fundamentally indifferent to other people&quot; — bus-seat observation as proof; Horikita trust analysis: &quot;she seems to trust you more than anyone else&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186-187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> **Jekyll switch**: furious → kicks his thigh → grabs bag → returns beaming &quot;Let&#x27;s head back together&quot; — &quot;I couldn&#x27;t tell which Kushida was the real one&quot;; AK unshattered (&quot;Most people possessed both a public face and a private, inner self&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p178-1\">← Before: &quot;Get rid of the dead weight&quot; + divergence<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p189-1\">→ After: Group-chat bullying plot + apathy crisis<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p189-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka group chat bullying plot   apathy crisis dorm room  group chat  satou joins  boys rage at horikita  hit ignore hide shoes ideas  chat stance   i m on no one s side  if you guys want to bully her  i won t stop you  then warns school punishes bullying  ends with  if kushida heard about this  she d probably hate you    deploys her popularity as deterrent neutral surface  protective act underneath  understands online vs faceto face courage gap  apathy crisis   i should ve been at the center of this situation  and yet i felt like i was drifting past it  doesn t feel expulsion urgency because  this was everyone else s problem  not mine  haunted by  only a fool wouldn t use his innate abilities     i wonder if that s what i am  after all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p189-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Group-chat bullying plot + apathy crisis<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.189-191<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">dorm room; group chat: Satou joins; boys rage at Horikita (hit/ignore/hide-shoes ideas)<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">chat stance: &quot;I&#x27;m on no one&#x27;s side. If you guys want to bully her, I won&#x27;t stop you.&quot; then warns school punishes bullying; ends with &quot;If Kushida heard about this, she&#x27;d probably hate you&quot; — deploys her popularity as deterrent<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">**apathy crisis**: &quot;I should&#x27;ve been at the center of this situation, and yet I felt like I was drifting past it&quot;; doesn&#x27;t feel expulsion urgency because &quot;This was everyone else&#x27;s problem, not mine&quot;; haunted by &quot;Only a fool…<span class=\"pg\">p.190-191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> neutral surface, protective act underneath; understands online-vs-faceto-face courage gap<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> **apathy crisis**: &quot;I should&#x27;ve been at the center of this situation, and yet I felt like I was drifting past it&quot;; doesn&#x27;t feel expulsion urgency because &quot;This was everyone else&#x27;s problem, not mine&quot;; haunted by &quot;Only a fool wouldn&#x27;t use his innate abilities&quot; — &quot;I wonder if that&#x27;s what I am, after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190-191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p181-1\">← Before: ROOFTOP: Kushida unmasked (MAJOR)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p192-1\">→ After: NIGHT FIGHT: Horikita Manabu vs AK (MAJOR)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p192-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka night fight  horikita manabu vs ak  major  dorm exterior night  ak follows suzune  witnesses brother sister explicit  manabu    niisan   i m far different from the useless girl you once knew  he   you re my little sister  if people around here learned the truth  i would be humiliated  leave this school immediately   do you want to relive the pain of the past   shared trauma hinted   you possess neither the abilities nor the qualities needed to reach class a   physical intervention  grabs manabu s pinning arm  then combat exchange   evades backhand  step back  evades sharp kick  slaps away probing hand  manabu   good reflexes  have you been taught     first explicit combat feat  horikita manabu 5th dan karate   4th dan aikido  her info  p 196  cover story   yes  i was taught piano and calligraphy  national music competition    comedy deflection under martial probing  slips again  tea ceremony  vs  calligraphy  when she probes dan rank  she   you purposefully get lower test scores  and you say that you studied piano and calligraphy  i really don t understand you  her voice  strained  i d never heard her voice like that    orders him to stop  after   he s not my friend  just my classmate   to brother  parting   with you around  things might get interesting    ak flagged as variable by top authority breaks cover for the first time to protect someone  immediately re weaves cover stories  inconsistent on purpose  registers manabu s danger level honestly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">NIGHT FIGHT: Horikita Manabu vs AK (MAJOR)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.192-197<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">dorm exterior night; AK follows Suzune; witnesses brother-sister<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;You possess neither the abilities nor the qualities needed to reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">cover story: &quot;Yes, I was taught piano and calligraphy... national music competition&quot; — comedy deflection under martial probing; slips again (&quot;tea ceremony&quot; vs &quot;calligraphy&quot;) when she probes dan rank; she: &quot;You purposefully get…<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> parting: &quot;With you around, things might get interesting.&quot; — AK flagged as variable by top authority<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> explicit: Manabu = &quot;niisan&quot;; &quot;I&#x27;m far different from the useless girl you once knew&quot;; he: &quot;you&#x27;re my little sister. If people around here learned the truth, I would be humiliated. Leave this school immediately.&quot;; &quot;Do you want to relive the pain of the past?&quot; (shared trauma hinted)<span class=\"pg\">p.192-193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> **physical intervention: grabs Manabu&#x27;s pinning arm**; then combat exchange — evades backhand (step back), evades sharp kick, slaps away probing hand; Manabu: &quot;Good reflexes... Have you been taught?&quot; — **first explicit combat feat**; Horikita Manabu 5th dan karate + 4th dan aikido (her info, p.196)<span class=\"pg\">p.193-194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> cover story: &quot;Yes, I was taught piano and calligraphy... national music competition&quot; — comedy deflection under martial probing; slips again (&quot;tea ceremony&quot; vs &quot;calligraphy&quot;) when she probes dan rank; she: &quot;You purposefully get lower test scores, and you say that you studied piano and calligraphy. I really don&#x27;t understand you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> her voice &quot;strained... I&#x27;d never heard her voice like that&quot; — orders him to stop; after: &quot;He&#x27;s…not my friend. Just my classmate.&quot; (to brother)<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> breaks cover for the first time to protect someone; immediately re-weaves cover stories (inconsistent on purpose?); registers Manabu&#x27;s danger level honestly<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p189-1\">← Before: Group-chat bullying plot + apathy crisis<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p197-1\">→ After: Night walk back: demerit-risk argument + her flaw<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p197-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka night walk back  demerit risk argument   her flaw dorm return walk  unusually long horikita conversation her cold frame restated  hirata will save failers anyway   if we dump the failures  attaining a higher rank will be simple  my goal is to have class d reach class a status  however  that s for my own sake and no one else s  his counter  unseen expulsion penalties possible  100 100 000 pts   you would ve just abandoned the failures from the very beginning     catches her inconsistency  she proposed the study group   i was starting to sound worked up  because i d started to  rather selfishly  consider her a friend  i didn t want horikita to come to regret her decision  grabbed wrist at elevator   she doesn t strike back  her refusal to hit me indicated that horikita felt the way i did  of course  she probably didn t even realize it herself  bus seat revisit  both agree merit gain loss frame  then the diagnosis   your flaw is that you think of everyone else as a burden  and so you detach yourself and never let anyone come close  isn t it possible they placed you in class d because you consider yourself superior to everyone   continues","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p197-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Night walk back: demerit-risk argument + her flaw<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.197-200<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">dorm return walk; unusually long Horikita conversation<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">his counter: unseen expulsion penalties possible (100→100,000 pts); &quot;You would&#x27;ve just abandoned the failures from the very beginning&quot; — **catches her inconsistency: she proposed the study group**<span class=\"pg\">p.197-198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">bus-seat revisit: both agree merit/gain-loss frame; then the diagnosis:<span class=\"pg\">p.199-200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">**&quot;Your flaw is that you think of everyone else as a burden, and so you detach yourself and never let anyone come close. Isn&#x27;t it possible they placed you in Class D because you consider yourself superior to everyone?&quot;**…<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> her cold frame restated: Hirata will save failers anyway; &quot;if we dump the failures... attaining a higher rank will be simple... my goal is to have Class D reach Class A status. However, that&#x27;s for my own sake and no one else&#x27;s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;I was starting to sound worked up... because I&#x27;d started to, rather selfishly, consider her a friend. I didn&#x27;t want Horikita to come to regret her decision.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> grabbed wrist at elevator — she doesn&#x27;t strike back (&quot;her refusal to hit me indicated that Horikita felt the way I did. Of course, she probably didn&#x27;t even realize it herself&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> **&quot;Your flaw is that you think of everyone else as a burden, and so you detach yourself and never let anyone come close. Isn&#x27;t it possible they placed you in Class D because you consider yourself superior to everyone?&quot;** (continues)<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p192-1\">← Before: NIGHT FIGHT: Horikita Manabu vs AK (MAJOR)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p201-1\">→ After: Mission statement slips + devil&#x27;s handshake<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p201-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka mission statement slips   devil s handshake night walk continues  every individual has his or her own strengths and weaknesses  that s what it means to be human    sudou physical   her  ike communication   her   you d most likely bring the class average down  so  does that make you incompetent  no   it s frustrating  but what you said was basically correct  you ve persuaded me  i have to concede that point  demands truth   cut the crap  i want to know the real reason  is it for points  to rise up  or is it to save your friends   because i want to know what a person with true merit looks like  what is equality  i came to this school to find answers to those questions    words  freely spilled out  before i could collect my thoughts  first stated life mission since ch 1  there s no way that you could fool me into believing you  ayanokouji kun  alliance formalized  she ll protect sudou ike  for my own sake  strategic means  handshake  narrator note   i would soon realize that i d just made a deal with the devil","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p201-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mission statement slips + devil&#x27;s handshake<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.201-202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">night walk continues<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">**&quot;Every individual has his or her own strengths and weaknesses. That&#x27;s what it means to be human.&quot;** — Sudou physical &gt; her; Ike communication &gt; her; &quot;you&#x27;d most likely bring the class average down. So, does that make you…<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s frustrating, but what you said was basically correct. You&#x27;ve persuaded me; I have to concede that point.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> demands truth: &quot;Cut the crap. I want to know the real reason. Is it for points? To rise up... Or is it to save your friends?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> **&quot;Every individual has his or her own strengths and weaknesses. That&#x27;s what it means to be human.&quot;** — Sudou physical &gt; her; Ike communication &gt; her; &quot;you&#x27;d most likely bring the class average down. So, does that make you incompetent? No.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> **&quot;Because I want to know what a person with true merit looks like. What is equality?... I came to this school to find answers to those questions.&quot;** — words &quot;freely spilled out... before I could collect my thoughts&quot;; first stated life-mission since Ch.1<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no way that you could fool me into believing you, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> alliance formalized: she&#x27;ll protect Sudou/Ike &quot;for my own sake... strategic means&quot;; handshake; narrator note: **&quot;I would soon realize that I&#x27;d just made a deal with the devil.&quot;**<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p197-1\">← Before: Night walk back: demerit-risk argument + her flaw<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p203-1\">→ After: Second recruitment: honest selfishness wins Kushida<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p203-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka second recruitment  honest selfishness wins kushida classroom   palate cafe  scene of prior crime  deliberately reused  horikita s forged  written contract  with his seal   comedy  torn up to kushida   no  this is for me    honest selfish motive respects the honesty  i just didn t want you to try to lie to me  i m glad you were honest  okay  i ll help  then  asks full partnership   i want to work on getting into class a with you  i want to help with everything else you ll be doing    horikita conditions  study group must go well first  triple handshake ak s title assigned without consent   he s working as my assistant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Second recruitment: honest selfishness wins Kushida<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.203-206<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">classroom + Palate café (scene of prior crime, deliberately reused)<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> to Kushida: &quot;No. This is for me.&quot; — honest selfish motive<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s forged &quot;written contract&quot; with his seal — comedy; torn up<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> respects the honesty (&quot;I just didn&#x27;t want you to try to lie to me. I&#x27;m glad you were honest. Okay, I&#x27;ll help.&quot;) then **asks full partnership**: &quot;I want to work on getting into Class A with you. I want to help with everything else you&#x27;ll be doing.&quot; — Horikita conditions: study group must go well first; triple handshake<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s title assigned without consent: &quot;He&#x27;s working as my assistant.&quot;<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p201-1\">← Before: Mission statement slips + devil&#x27;s handshake<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p207-1\">→ After: Sudou&#x27;s pride + the date-incentive play<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p207-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudou s pride   the date incentive play classroom  group reconvened via kushida s  honey trap   i hate you  sudou kun     however  our mutual abhorrence is trivial right now  i will teach you for my own sake  you will do your best for your own sake   you really want to get up to class a  then  even if that means inviting someone you hate  like me   rule plan   p 208 209  horikita s method v2  study during class  6 wasted hrs  10 min break tutoring by horikita ak kushida individually  no note taking  trying to memorize things is surprisingly difficult when you re writing down notes  target comprehension of half page essentials basketball analogy   you only improve by practicing  all the time    sudou  inhaled sharply  surprised by his own words  still refuses  pride   ak s pivot   hey  kushida  do you have a boyfriend  if i can get fifty points on the test  will you go out with me    staged  ike yamauchi escalate 51 52  kushida improvises  date with highest scorer  a date  huh  that doesn t sound too bad  jeez  guess i don t have a choice  all right  i ll join   remember  boys are the simplest creatures on earth    social engineering as class weapon","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sudou&#x27;s pride + the date-incentive play<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.207-211<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">classroom; group reconvened via Kushida&#x27;s &quot;honey trap&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> **&quot;I hate you, Sudou-kun.&quot;** / &quot;However, our mutual abhorrence is trivial right now. I will teach you for my own sake. You will do your best for your own sake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;You really want to get up to Class A, then? Even if that means inviting someone you hate, like me?&quot; [rule/plan] (p.208-209) Horikita&#x27;s method v2: study during class (6 wasted hrs), 10-min break tutoring by Horikita/AK/Kushida…<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> basketball analogy: &quot;You only improve by practicing, all the time.&quot; — Sudou &quot;inhaled sharply, surprised by his own words&quot;; still refuses (pride)<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You really want to get up to Class A, then? Even if that means inviting someone you hate, like me?&quot; [rule/plan] (p.208-209) Horikita&#x27;s method v2: study during class (6 wasted hrs), 10-min break tutoring by Horikita/AK/Kushida individually; NO note-taking (&quot;Trying to memorize things is surprisingly difficult when you&#x27;re writing down notes&quot;); target comprehension of half-page essentials<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> **AK&#x27;s pivot: &quot;Hey, Kushida. Do you have a boyfriend?... If I can get fifty points on the test, will you go out with me?&quot;** — staged; Ike/Yamauchi escalate 51/52; Kushida improvises: date with highest scorer<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A date, huh? That doesn&#x27;t sound too bad. Jeez, guess I don&#x27;t have a choice. All right, I&#x27;ll join,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Remember, boys are the simplest creatures on earth.&quot; — social engineering as class weapon<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p203-1\">← Before: Second recruitment: honest selfishness wins Kushida<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p212-1\">→ After: Study week + rankings lore + Kushida&#x27;s alliance probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p212-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka study week   rankings lore   kushida s alliance probe class time studying works  lunch library sessions  cafe interlude  respect for sudou   many of the first year students  didn t have a  dream  yet  at least sudou was already working hard in pursuit of his dream  that was worthy of praise  questions school s design  talent beyond academics enrolled  yet single failing grade expels    unless the system itself was a lie  lunch sabotage  jumps out to invite ak  horikita exits cold   after i d discovered kushida s secret  she d been rather blatant about keeping tabs on me   scene others   p 214  koenji daily at palate with third year girls  more mature girls are the best  first year ranking charts exist  hot guy  satonaka a  1  hirata  2  ak  5  also gloominess   boys who should die  kushida blunt   there s something missing  some element of attractiveness  about ak  ally ultimatum   if you had to choose either horikita san or me as your ally  whom would you choose  if horikita and i happen to clash  i hope that you ll cooperate with me  ayanokouji kun   i m no one s ally or enemy  i m neutral    then   there are some situations where you can t avoid trouble by staying neutral   her warning  smiling hate   didn t you say that you hated me  though   ha ha ha  yes  i did  sorry  but that s how i really feel   first  we d need to build a relationship of mutual trust    mutual un readability locked in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p212-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Study week + rankings lore + Kushida&#x27;s alliance probe<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.212-217<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">class-time studying works; lunch library sessions; café interlude<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">**respect for Sudou**: &quot;Many of the first-year students... didn&#x27;t have a &#x27;dream&#x27; yet... At least Sudou was already working hard in pursuit of his dream. That was worthy of praise.&quot;; questions school&#x27;s design: talent beyond…<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m no one&#x27;s ally or enemy. I&#x27;m neutral.&quot; — then: &quot;There are some situations where you can&#x27;t avoid trouble by staying neutral&quot; (her warning)<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> **respect for Sudou**: &quot;Many of the first-year students... didn&#x27;t have a &#x27;dream&#x27; yet... At least Sudou was already working hard in pursuit of his dream. That was worthy of praise.&quot;; questions school&#x27;s design: talent beyond academics enrolled, yet single failing grade expels — &quot;Unless the system itself was a lie&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> lunch sabotage: jumps out to invite AK; Horikita exits cold; &quot;after I&#x27;d discovered Kushida&#x27;s secret, she&#x27;d been rather blatant about keeping tabs on me&quot; [scene-others] (p.214) Koenji daily at Palate with third-year girls (&quot;more mature girls are the best&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> first-year ranking charts exist (hot-guy: Satonaka-A #1, Hirata #2, AK #5; also gloominess, &quot;Boys Who Should Die&quot;); Kushida blunt: &quot;There&#x27;s something missing, some element of attractiveness&quot; about AK<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> **ally ultimatum**: &quot;if you had to choose either Horikita-san or me as your ally, whom would you choose?... If Horikita and I happen to clash, I hope that you&#x27;ll cooperate with me, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> smiling-hate: &quot;Didn&#x27;t you say that you hated me, though?&quot; &quot;Ha ha ha, yes, I did. Sorry, but that&#x27;s how I really feel.&quot;; &quot;First, we&#x27;d need to build a relationship of mutual trust.&quot; — mutual un-readability locked in<span class=\"pg\">p.216-217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p207-1\">← Before: Sudou&#x27;s pride + the date-incentive play<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p218-1\">→ After: Library grind + Class C Yamawaki taunt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p218-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou yamawaki horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka library grind   class c yamawaki taunt library sessions  ike sudou progress  francis bacon correct  then class c boys approach openly admits shared lunch to ike   fans jealousy  ak notes worse cover maintained class c   i m glad that they separate the classes  that way i don t have to study with losers like you     if we happened to fight  how many points would you lose  oh wait  you guys don t even have any points  counters  ruckus   expulsion risk for them too   clearly there were errors of calculation in placing class c and a    first public class d defiance frame","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Library grind + Class C Yamawaki taunt<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.218-220<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">library sessions; Ike/Sudou progress (Francis Bacon correct); then Class C boys approach<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#yamawaki\">Yamawaki<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamawaki<\/b> Class C: &quot;I&#x27;m glad that they separate the classes... That way I don&#x27;t have to study with losers like you.&quot; / &quot;If we happened to fight, how many points would you lose? Oh wait, you guys don&#x27;t even have any points&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> counters: ruckus = expulsion risk for them too; &quot;Clearly there were errors of calculation in placing Class C and A&quot; — first public Class-D defiance frame<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> openly admits shared lunch to Ike — fans jealousy; AK notes worse cover maintained<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p212-1\">← Before: Study week + rankings lore + Kushida&#x27;s alliance probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p221-1\">→ After: Test-scope sabotage revealed + Sudou&#x27;s turn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p221-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka test scope sabotage revealed   sudou s turn library confrontation ends  then faculty room second appearance  blonde light pink haired class b beauty de escalates sudou with pure logic  yamawaki group apologizes to her  ak   unlike horikita  she managed to keep everyone in line    first filed impression  yamawaki leak  class c knew test material changed  chiyabashira confirms   the test s topics changed last friday  sorry  i must ve forgotten to inform you    no remorse  other teachers indifferent  hoshinomiya waves ak refuses accident theory  i didn t think that our teacher had simply forgotten    sabotage pattern suspected ak assigns her to brief whole class    you re the best candidate we have  she accepts  bows to horikita   starting tomorrow i ll take a break from club activities  will that work    club time sacrifice   sincere commitment signal  ike yamauchi follow   we re definitely gonna do this  removes his hand from her shoulder   please do not touch me  if you do so again  i won t show you any mercy    accepts alliance  keeps physical boundary absolute","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Test-scope sabotage revealed + Sudou&#x27;s turn<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.221-228<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">library confrontation ends; then faculty room **Yamawaki leak: Class C knew test material changed**; Chiyabashira confirms: &quot;The test&#x27;s topics changed last Friday. Sorry, I must&#x27;ve forgotten to inform you.&quot; — no remorse; other teachers indifferent; Hoshinomiya waves<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">AK refuses accident theory (&quot;I didn&#x27;t think that our teacher had simply forgotten&quot;) — sabotage pattern suspected<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> **bows to Horikita**: &quot;Starting tomorrow…I&#x27;ll take a break from club activities. Will that work?&quot; — club-time sacrifice = sincere commitment signal; Ike/Yamauchi follow: &quot;We&#x27;re definitely gonna do this!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> second appearance: blonde/light-pink-haired Class B beauty de-escalates Sudou with pure logic; Yamawaki group apologizes to HER; AK: &quot;Unlike Horikita, she managed to keep everyone in line.&quot; — first filed impression<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> AK assigns her to brief whole class — &quot;You&#x27;re the best candidate we have&quot;; she accepts<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> removes his hand from her shoulder: &quot;Please do not touch me. If you do so again, I won&#x27;t show you any mercy.&quot; — accepts alliance, keeps physical boundary absolute<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p218-1\">← Before: Library grind + Class C Yamawaki taunt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p229-1\">→ After: Past-paper heist (MAJOR STRATEGY)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p229-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka past paper heist  major strategy  cafeteria stakeout   third year class d buyer   kushida debrief identifies target via free vegetable set eating  poverty heuristic    social engineering read of cafeteria economics  approaches  third year  also in class d  aren t you  negotiated 10k    15k points  for old midterms   first year mock answers  threat backstop   even if you re an upperclassman  i ll do anything  to make sure you re expelled  transfer records leverage noted by seller verification  mock hard problems  word identical  to prior year  they re the same  every single word is identical  deduction chain  chiyabashira s odd confidence   past paper route is the intended safety valve for athletic admissions plan  withhold papers until day before test  release via kushida   mass overnight cram   everyone above 32   overconfidence  might end up digging our own graves  credit laundering  she announces papers as hers  a third year student you re close to  ak   i like to avoid trouble  i don t want to stand out  her line   don t you feel that a strange bond of mutual trust forms between people who share a secret  operates full covert op under class savior framing while keeping fingerprints off  reads system design  expulsion proofing exists  better than any classmate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Past-paper heist (MAJOR STRATEGY)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.229-235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">cafeteria stakeout → third-year Class D buyer → Kushida debrief<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">plan: withhold papers until day-before test; release via Kushida → mass overnight cram = everyone above 32; &quot;overconfidence... might end up digging our own graves&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233-234<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> identifies target via free-vegetable-set eating (poverty heuristic) — social engineering read of cafeteria economics; approaches &quot;third-year... also in Class D, aren&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.229-230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> negotiated 10k → **15k points** for old midterms + first-year mock answers; threat-backstop: &quot;Even if you&#x27;re an upperclassman, I&#x27;ll do anything... to make sure you&#x27;re expelled&quot;; transfer-records leverage noted by seller<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> verification: mock hard-problems **word-identical** to prior year (&quot;They&#x27;re the same. Every single word is identical.&quot;); deduction chain: Chiyabashira&#x27;s odd confidence → past-paper route is the intended safety valve for athletic admissions<span class=\"pg\">p.232-233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> credit laundering: she announces papers as hers (&quot;a third-year student you&#x27;re close to&quot;); AK: &quot;I like to avoid trouble. I don&#x27;t want to stand out.&quot;; her line: &quot;Don&#x27;t you feel that a strange bond of mutual trust forms between people who share a secret?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> operates full covert op under class-savior framing while keeping fingerprints off; reads system design (expulsion-proofing exists) better than any classmate<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p221-1\">← Before: Test-scope sabotage revealed + Sudou&#x27;s turn<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p236-1\">→ After: Release + the hate confession<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p236-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka release   the hate confession classroom  day before midterm  kushida distributes unique deployment  only she could deliver without faction backlash  class elation  an easy victory  genuine praise   if you weren t here  the study group would not have succeeded  then the check   you hate me  don t you  smile drops  answers flat   that s right  i really hate you    no reason offered  horikita   knowing that is good enough  i can continue working with you without hesitation  partnership now explicitly built on mutual hatred   shared class goals   no illusion of friendship required","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Release + the hate confession<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.236-239<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">classroom, day before midterm; Kushida distributes<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> smile drops, answers flat: **&quot;That&#x27;s right. I really hate you.&quot;** — no reason offered; Horikita: &quot;Knowing that is good enough. I can continue working with you without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> unique deployment: only she could deliver without faction backlash; class elation (&quot;An easy victory!&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> genuine praise: &quot;If you weren&#x27;t here, the study group would not have succeeded.&quot;; then the check: **&quot;You hate me, don&#x27;t you?&quot;**<span class=\"pg\">p.237-238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> partnership now explicitly built on mutual hatred + shared class goals — no illusion of friendship required<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p229-1\">← Before: Past-paper heist (MAJOR STRATEGY)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p240-1\">→ After: Midterm week + Sudou&#x27;s English scare + apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p240-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka midterm week   sudou s english scare   apology exam days  vacation reward if no failures  island seed  old paper theory confirmed live  tests match  horikita s lesson predictions accurate    the silent girl beside me was even more impressive than i d imagined   slept through english review of old papers    10 min cram only  horikita tactical coaching   memorize the problems that are worth a lot of points and those with the shortest answers   the apology  acknowledges fault  you didn t cut any corners or give up  hold your head high  then amends basketball insult   researched the pro path  incredibly rocky  regret stated   someone who doesn t understand how difficult  basketball is has no right to dismiss that dream as foolish  if you do  you might be able to go pro  bow  class stunned  i  i think i might be in love with horikita    crush born from respect apology","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Midterm week + Sudou&#x27;s English scare + apology<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.240-245<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">exam days; vacation reward if no failures (island seed)<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> **slept through English review of old papers** — 10-min cram only; Horikita tactical coaching: &quot;memorize the problems that are worth a lot of points and those with the shortest answers&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241-242<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> **&quot;I… I think I might be in love with Horikita…&quot;** — crush born from respect-apology<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> old-paper theory confirmed live: tests match; Horikita&#x27;s lesson-predictions accurate — &quot;The silent girl beside me was even more impressive than I&#x27;d imagined.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> **the apology**: acknowledges fault (&quot;You didn&#x27;t cut any corners or give up... hold your head high&quot;), then amends basketball insult — researched the pro path (&quot;incredibly rocky&quot;), regret stated: &quot;Someone who doesn&#x27;t understand how difficult... basketball is has no right to dismiss that dream as foolish... If you do, you might be able to go pro.&quot;; bow; class stunned<span class=\"pg\">p.244-245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p236-1\">← Before: Release + the hate confession<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p246-1\">→ After: Sudou&#x27;s fake expulsion + the point purchase (CLIMAX)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p246-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudou s fake expulsion   the point purchase  climax  results day  then faculty office corridor  midterm pass line   class average   2   79 6 2   39 8   sudou english 39 fails by 0 8  previous test s 32 line from same formula  chiyabashira   when did anyone say that thirty two points was a passing grade    moving goalposts  her sacrifice  deliberately scored 51 in english  vs  100 elsewhere  to drag class average down so 39 would clear   then exposed  rounding policy differs  down then  up now   i should have tried to lower my score just a little more   why  you said that you hated me     don t misunderstand  i did this for my own sake   kindness laundered as self interest  ak to chiyabashira   do you think that today s japanese society is fair     i think that equality is a fiction    reprises ch 1 thesis as challenge   we should strive for equality  at least a little  teacher confirms she knows his past paper op  i already know that you contacted a third year student  praises it as  one correct solution  you did very well   the gambit   please sell me one point that i can apply to sudou s english test    reframes tests as purchasable school  goods  per orientation rules chiyabashira prices one test point at 100 000  horikita joins  i ll pay  too  combined payment accepted   sudou s expulsion voided  ak    disagreeable  purposeful low scores  credit laundering to kushida  buying test points    i don t think that you re special  i think you re disagreeable   honestly  maybe the students in class d are defective  however  that doesn t mean they re trash     the difference is paper thin  however  with repairs  a defective product may become a superior article  ak notes her  major transformation  barely glimpsed from outside  chiyabashira s faint smile   shared recognition  ending chop  for whatever    his almost slip  bothersome classm  corrected to  bothersome person  then he chases after her  arc beat  almost classmate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sudou&#x27;s fake expulsion + the point purchase (CLIMAX)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.246-255<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">results day; then faculty-office corridor<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">AK to Chiyabashira: &quot;Do you think that today&#x27;s Japanese society is fair?&quot; ... &quot;I think that equality is a fiction.&quot; — reprises Ch.1 thesis as challenge; &quot;we should strive for equality. At least a little.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">**the gambit: &quot;Please sell me one point that I can apply to Sudou&#x27;s English test.&quot;** — reframes tests as purchasable school &quot;goods&quot; per orientation rules<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> AK = &quot;disagreeable&quot;: purposeful low scores, credit laundering to Kushida, buying test points — &quot;I don&#x27;t think that you&#x27;re special... I think you&#x27;re disagreeable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> **midterm pass line = class average ÷ 2** (79.6/2 = 39.8 → Sudou English 39 fails by 0.8); previous test&#x27;s 32-line from same formula; Chiyabashira: &quot;When did anyone say that thirty-two points was a passing grade?&quot; — moving goalposts<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> **her sacrifice**: deliberately scored 51 in English (vs ~100 elsewhere) to drag class average down so 39 would clear — then exposed: rounding policy differs (down then, up now); &quot;I should have tried to lower my score just a little more&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Why? You said that you hated me&quot; — &quot;Don&#x27;t misunderstand. I did this for my own sake.&quot; (kindness laundered as self-interest)<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> teacher confirms she knows his past-paper op (&quot;I already know that you contacted a third-year student&quot;); praises it as &quot;one correct solution... you did very well&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Chiyabashira prices one test point at 100,000; Horikita joins (&quot;I&#x27;ll pay, too&quot;); combined payment accepted; **Sudou&#x27;s expulsion voided**<span class=\"pg\">p.253-254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> **&quot;Honestly, maybe the students in Class D are defective. However, that doesn&#x27;t mean they&#x27;re trash.&quot;** / &quot;The difference is paper thin. However, with repairs, a defective product may become a superior article.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK notes her &quot;major transformation&quot; barely glimpsed from outside; Chiyabashira&#x27;s faint smile = shared recognition; ending chop &quot;For whatever.&quot; — his almost-slip &quot;bothersome classm—&quot; corrected to &quot;bothersome person,&quot; then he chases after her (arc beat: almost-classmate)<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p240-1\">← Before: Midterm week + Sudou&#x27;s English scare + apology<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p256-1\">→ After: Victory celebration: team solidifies<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p256-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka victory celebration  team solidifies evening  ak s plain dorm room  chosen for emptiness  former  association of failures    horikita   kushida  attends the party     simply participating in this gathering was a sign of her progress  the old horikita most definitely would not have come  sudou fully thawed  you re a surprisingly good person  horikita  formalizes the trio   horikita san  ayanokouji kun  and i are all working together to get into class a  i want you three to help us    idiot trio recruited to the cause conditional join   well  if horikita asked me to help  i would  i guess    crush driven loyalty  horikita returns banter rhythm established  in this school  ability is paramount  you can t do so half heartedly  otherwise you ll be a burden   ability was paramount  huh  i felt my chest tighten    white room resonance  closing wish   i wouldn t mind seeing horikita smile","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p256-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Victory celebration: team solidifies<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.256-262<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">evening, AK&#x27;s plain dorm room (chosen for emptiness); former &quot;association of failures&quot; + Horikita + Kushida<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;In this school, ability is paramount... you can&#x27;t do so half-heartedly. Otherwise you&#x27;ll be a burden.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">**&quot;Ability was paramount, huh? I felt my chest tighten.&quot;** — White Room resonance; closing wish: **&quot;I wouldn&#x27;t mind seeing Horikita smile.&quot;**<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> **attends the party** — &quot;simply participating in this gathering was a sign of her progress. The old Horikita most definitely would not have come.&quot;; Sudou fully thawed (&quot;you&#x27;re a surprisingly good person, Horikita&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.256-257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> formalizes the trio: &quot;Horikita-san, Ayanokouji-kun, and I are all working together to get into Class A... I want you three to help us.&quot; — Idiot Trio recruited to the cause<span class=\"pg\">p.258-259<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> conditional join: &quot;Well, if Horikita asked me to help, I would. I guess.&quot; — crush-driven loyalty; Horikita-returns-banter rhythm established<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p246-1\">← Before: Sudou&#x27;s fake expulsion + the point purchase (CLIMAX)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p263-1\">→ After: Postscript (meta)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p263-1","v":"y1v1","y":1,"o":1,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka postscript  meta  author kinugasa syougo  theme stated   academics aren t everything  in story year 2015  illustrator tomose shunsaku  author insomnia noted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p263-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Postscript (meta)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V1 · p.263-264<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> author Kinugasa Syougo; theme stated: &quot;academics aren&#x27;t everything&quot;; in-story year 2015; illustrator Tomose Shunsaku; author insomnia noted<\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v1-p256-1\">← Before: Victory celebration: team solidifies<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p15-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  july 1  first class points  delayed deposit july 1  class d homeroom  abnormally raucous  the first monthly point deposit since enrollment is expected  system recap for the reader   we used these private points to purchase daily necessities  meals  even electrical appliances  at this school  points are currency  they are very important   if you didn t have any private points  you were forced to live day today without spending money  you couldn t use real currency anywhere on campus  class d sat at zero class points since june  every class started with 1000 class points  deposit   class points   100 paid into each private account on day 1   however  my perspective changed when i bought a point for the midterm test    private points can change your situation  you  could likely purchase more than just test points   are you disappointed because the gap between the classes has widened  horikita   the sharp witted hirata hadn t missed a beat  splendid   hirata decoding horikita s  get something  reads chabashira s hedged closing  if there are still points left  that is  as deliberate   there was deeper meaning behind chabashira sensei s words","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): first class points, delayed deposit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.15–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">July 1, Class D homeroom, abnormally raucous: the first monthly point deposit since enrollment is expected.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">System recap for the reader: &quot;We used these private points to purchase daily necessities, meals, even electrical appliances. At this school, points are currency. They are very important.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;If you didn’t have any private points, you were forced to live day-today without spending money. You couldn’t use real currency anywhere on campus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you disappointed because the gap between the classes has widened, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class D sat at zero class points since June; every class started with 1000 class points; deposit = class points × 100 paid into each private account on day 1.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;However, my perspective changed when I bought a point for the midterm test.&quot; — private points can change your situation; you &quot;could likely purchase more than just test points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The sharp-witted Hirata hadn’t missed a beat. Splendid.&quot; (Hirata decoding Horikita&#x27;s &quot;get something&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Chabashira&#x27;s hedged closing (&quot;If there are still points left, that is.&quot;) as deliberate: &quot;There was deeper meaning behind Chabashira-sensei’s words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16–19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): having friends and still eating alone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2  lunch  having friends and still eating alone  meanwhile  i don t really belong anywhere   however  now i was experiencing a strange phenomenon  i had friends  yet i was still on my own   i m over here  guys  it s okay for you to invite me  my glances were filled with selfishness and anticipation  i was flooded by feelings of self loathing  fear of the low tier friend question   did they all consider me a low tier friend  or was our friendship all in my head   you seem completely used to solitude   to horikita  meant as sarcasm  taken by her as sincere   doesn t it cost quite a bit and take a lot of effort to make your own lunch   don t tell me  not only are you a bright scholar  you re an accomplished cook as well  that doesn t seem to fit your personality   but why did you decide to go through the trouble of making your own lunch   do i already miss riding the big cafeteria bound wave of students  koenji assessment   he didn t love solitude  but rather  loved himself and cared little for others  i respected that he didn t seem bothered at all by being alone  notes the quiet bespectacled classmate  sakura  making her own bento   she was always alone  and i d never seen her talk to anyone  sticks to horikita despite constant insults   i wished i had a comeback for that  but i couldn t argue  i just wanted her to cut me a break","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): having friends and still eating alone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19–21<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You seem completely used to solitude,&quot; (to Horikita; meant as sarcasm, taken by her as sincere)<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Doesn’t it cost quite a bit and take a lot of effort to make your own lunch?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t tell me. Not only are you a bright scholar, you’re an accomplished cook as well? That doesn’t seem to fit your personality.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Meanwhile, I don’t really belong anywhere.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;However, now I was experiencing a strange phenomenon: I had friends, yet I was still on my own.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’m over here, guys. It’s okay for you to invite me. My glances were filled with selfishness and anticipation. I was flooded by feelings of self-loathing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Fear of the low-tier-friend question: &quot;Did they all consider me a low-tier friend? Or was our friendship all in my head?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But why did you decide to go through the trouble of making your own lunch?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do I already miss riding the big cafeteria-bound wave of students?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Kōenji assessment: &quot;He didn’t love solitude, but rather, loved himself and cared little for others. I respected that he didn’t seem bothered at all by being alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Notes the quiet bespectacled classmate (Sakura) making her own bento: &quot;She was always alone, and I’d never seen her talk to anyone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sticks to Horikita despite constant insults: &quot;I wished I had a comeback for that, but I couldn’t argue. I just wanted her to cut me a break.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p15-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): first class points, delayed deposit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): Horikita, Kushida, and the &quot;hate&quot; chat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  after school  horikita  kushida  and the  hate  chat  there was some value in being able to vanish like a ninja into a crowd  if i hung toward the back of some group of friends  i could pretend i was one of them   i don t really think so  what about you  horikita  you were the only person who gave sudou a helping hand  on walking home with horikita   since we didn t have lunch together or just casually hang out  i found it odd  then again  we had the same path back to the dormitory   that reminds me  you should join in the chat now and again  you re the only one who hasn t caught up in a long time   telling horikita to catch up on the class group chat  she keeps notifications off and is  not interested   i wonder  well  if i had to think of a reason  i guess i got used to attending school  and then i made some friends  also  kushida was probably a big influence   i admit i found it shocking when she said that she hated you  horikita  but i think it s only natural that everyone has people they like and people they hate  there s no point being concerned about it  i mean  you still pretend to get along well with kushida san even though she said she hates you  right   hey    followed by   what the heck  it really hurt when she said it straight out like that   were you testing me   no need  i m fine with the kushida we have now     even though i d spoken the words  i did feel disgusted with myself  routine walking and talking pair now  she notices he is  quite talkative lately  he admits he only relaxes around a few specific people  if she were another girl  i probably wouldn t have been able to converse normally","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): Horikita, Kushida, and the &quot;hate&quot; chat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t really think so. What about you, Horikita? You were the only person who gave Sudou a helping hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That reminds me. You should join in the chat now and again. You’re the only one who hasn’t caught up in a long time.&quot; (telling Horikita to catch up on the class group chat; she keeps notifications off and is &quot;not interested&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I wonder. Well, if I had to think of a reason, I guess I got used to attending school, and then I made some friends. Also, Kushida was probably a big influence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;There was some value in being able to vanish like a ninja into a crowd. If I hung toward the back of some group of friends, I could pretend I was one of them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On walking home with Horikita: &quot;Since we didn’t have lunch together or just casually hang out, I found it odd. Then again, we had the same path back to the dormitory.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I admit I found it shocking when she said that she hated you, Horikita. But I think it’s only natural that everyone has people they like and people they hate. There’s no point being concerned about it. I mean, you still pretend to get along well with Kushida-san even though she said she hates you, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey…&quot; — followed by: &quot;What the heck? It really hurt when she said it straight out like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Were you testing me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No need. I’m fine with the Kushida we have now,&quot; — &quot;Even though I’d spoken the words, I did feel disgusted with myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Routine walking-and-talking pair now; she notices he is &quot;quite talkative lately&quot;; he admits he only relaxes around a few specific people (&quot;If she were another girl, I probably wouldn’t have been able to converse normally.&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.19–26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): having friends and still eating alone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4 (night): Sudou&#x27;s brawl, duplicate keys, Kushida&#x27;s pressure<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"sudou-ken kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 4  night  sudou s brawl  duplicate keys  kushida s pressure private balance after the midterm point purchase   i saw that i had 8 320 private points     i had nearly bankrupted myself just to buy the point sudou needed to pass   converted  the points came to roughly 8700 yen  although that wasn t a giant improvement  it was still big bucks   87 class points expected payout   why re you here  actually  forget that   how did you even get in   i learned this extremely important fact just now   learning the group cloned his room key   no  i can t forget about it  hand over the key   what an illogical argument  even if you re ignorant of committing a crime  it s still a crime  friendship doesn t mean automatically allowing people to do whatever they want   if you need advice or you re worried about something  why not ask ike or yamauchi   did you insult chabashira sensei  by any chance   then what  did you grab her by the collar and threaten to kill her or something   you beat them up  so  uh  why did you do that   well  i wonder about that  i don t think it s quite that simple   well  the school doesn t trust you  right  it wouldn t be that odd for someone in your class  like kushida  for instance  to support you even if you re lying  after all  they don t want their points to go down   even if the other party is at fault  it s still highly likely that sudou will take some of the blame  legal literacy play   sudou hit them  but they didn t hit sudou  i think that s a big part of it  in such a case  claiming it as legitimate self defense is difficult  had they come at you with a knife or a metal bat  i think things would have been quite different  self defense means that you have the right to defend yourself against sudden  dangerous attacks made against your person  so  i don t think we can really claim that this was self defense   i think the school might have offered an extension because they found it difficult to make a judgment at this time   whoever reported it first has the advantage  the victim s testimony can work as evidence  his read on class c s plan  flagged as imagination   that was what i imagined their plan to be  anyway   they let themselves be beaten to destroy sudou s regular spot   if trying to explain the situation won t work  then we ll need to find ironclad proof   so there might be an eyewitness   no  at this stage it s probably only being discussed by the school and the people involved   if those guys in class c had intended to spread rumors  we probably would ve heard about it already   yeah  it wouldn t be good if the accused tried anything   there s just not much i can do  i mean  i can only really respond to sudou s story  if it were horikita or hirata here  they d probably be able to give expert advice  toward kushida   as kushida looked up at me with uneasy eyes  i had the sudden urge to embrace her  i stretched my back out and tried to shake those thoughts  on the duplicate keys   wasn t it fine for kushida to have a key  anyway  i suppose that in the delusional part of my brain  giving her a key made it feel like she was my girlfriend  men certainly are devious creatures   i don t know if i should be happy about that or not   i m trying  more or less  i just haven t been able to  like right now  i didn t have the guts to promise that i d help   kushida  you re going to help  aren t you   remember when i said it d be better to talk with horikita or hirata  well  sudou hates hirata  so that makes horikita the obvious choice   don t know  we ll have to ask and find out  i don t think she ll just quietly stand by and watch as class d collapses  probably   is it okay if i m useless   it s risky  aside from the question of who started the fight  those three reported it to the school  that means they have the upper hand  also  i just don t think it would work  since they started it  chapter close   no matter how much i thought about it  i couldn t come up with any solutions  sudou came to him first for help   kushida   he came to you before horikita san  hirata kun  or even ike kun  keeps her double nature in view while cooperating   i remembered that kushida once directly told me that she hated me  but i might get burned if i forgot about it entirely  under pressure he interrogates facts  then produces a dispassionate procedural analysis  evidence  reporting order  self defense definition  rather than emotional reassurance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4 (night): Sudou&#x27;s brawl, duplicate keys, Kushida&#x27;s pressure<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.27–38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why’re you here? Actually, forget that – how did you even get in?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I learned this extremely important fact just now,&quot; (learning the group cloned his room key)<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No, I can’t forget about it. Hand over the key.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Private balance after the midterm point purchase: &quot;I saw that I had 8,320 private points.&quot; — &quot;I had nearly bankrupted myself just to buy the point Sudou needed to pass.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Converted, the points came to roughly 8700 yen. Although that wasn’t a giant improvement, it was still big bucks.&quot; (87 class points expected payout)<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;What an illogical argument. Even if you’re ignorant of committing a crime, it’s still a crime. Friendship doesn’t mean automatically allowing people to do whatever they want.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you need advice or you’re worried about something, why not ask Ike or Yamauchi?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did you insult Chabashira-sensei, by any chance?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then what? Did you grab her by the collar and threaten to kill her or something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You beat them up? So, uh, why did you do that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I wonder about that. I don’t think it’s quite that simple.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, the school doesn’t trust you, right? It wouldn’t be that odd for someone in your class, like Kushida, for instance, to support you even if you’re lying. After all, they don’t want their points to go down.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even if the other party is at fault, it’s still highly likely that Sudou will take some of the blame.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Legal-literacy play: &quot;Sudou hit them, but they didn’t hit Sudou. I think that’s a big part of it. In such a case, claiming it as legitimate self-defense is difficult. Had they come at you with a knife or a metal bat, I think things would have been quite different. Self-defense means that you have the right to defend yourself against sudden, dangerous attacks made against your person. So, I don’t think we can really claim that this was self-defense.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think the school might have offered an extension because they found it difficult to make a judgment at this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Whoever reported it first has the advantage. The victim’s testimony can work as evidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His read on Class C&#x27;s plan, flagged as imagination: &quot;That was what I imagined their plan to be, anyway.&quot; (they let themselves be beaten to destroy Sudou&#x27;s regular spot)<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If trying to explain the situation won’t work, then we’ll need to find ironclad proof,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So there might be an eyewitness?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, at this stage it’s probably only being discussed by the school and the people involved.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If those guys in Class C had intended to spread rumors, we probably would’ve heard about it already.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. It wouldn’t be good if the accused tried anything,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s just not much I can do. I mean, I can only really respond to Sudou’s story. If it were Horikita or Hirata here, they’d probably be able to give expert advice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Toward Kushida: &quot;As Kushida looked up at me with uneasy eyes, I had the sudden urge to embrace her. I stretched my back out and tried to shake those thoughts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the duplicate keys: &quot;Wasn’t it fine for Kushida to have a key, anyway? I suppose that in the delusional part of my brain, giving her a key made it feel like she was my girlfriend. Men certainly are devious creatures.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t know if I should be happy about that or not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m trying, more or less. I just haven’t been able to. Like right now, I didn’t have the guts to promise that I’d help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Kushida, you’re going to help, aren’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Remember when I said it’d be better to talk with Horikita or Hirata? Well, Sudou hates Hirata, so that makes Horikita the obvious choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don’t know. We’ll have to ask and find out. I don’t think she’ll just quietly stand by and watch as Class D collapses. Probably.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is it okay if I’m useless?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s risky. Aside from the question of who started the fight, those three reported it to the school. That means they have the upper hand. Also, I just don’t think it would work, since they started it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Chapter close: &quot;No matter how much I thought about it, I couldn’t come up with any solutions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou came to him first for help — Kushida: &quot;He came to you before Horikita-san, Hirata-kun, or even Ike-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Keeps her double-nature in view while cooperating: &quot;I remembered that Kushida once directly told me that she hated me... But I might get burned if I forgot about it entirely.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Under pressure he interrogates facts, then produces a dispassionate procedural analysis (evidence, reporting order, self-defense definition) rather than emotional reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): Horikita, Kushida, and the &quot;hate&quot; chat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): the fight goes public<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 open  july 2 homeroom  the fight goes public chabashira briefs class d on the sudou class c incident  the classroom erupts  ak watches her  serene beauty  of total neutrality   i planned to fade out  but   his protest to himself at being swept into lunch with the group   this was typical of japanese people  they would follow suit when someone took the lead  though they probably mocked him in their hearts  they would help sudou a little bit   well  i guessed i didn t have to take a turn  i wouldn t be any good at this  anyway  better to just leave it to them and fade out quietly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): the fight goes public<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira briefs Class D on the Sudou–Class C incident; the classroom erupts; AK watches her &quot;serene beauty&quot; of total neutrality.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I planned to fade out… But…&quot; (his protest to himself at being swept into lunch with the group)<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;This was typical of Japanese people. They would follow suit when someone took the lead. Though they probably mocked him in their hearts, they would help Sudou a little bit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;Well, I guessed I didn’t have to take a turn. I wouldn’t be any good at this, anyway. Better to just leave it to them and fade out quietly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4 (night): Sudou&#x27;s brawl, duplicate keys, Kushida&#x27;s pressure<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): Horikita&#x27;s refusal dissected, the boys&#x27; romance council<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  cafeteria  horikita s refusal dissected  the boys  romance council on being ranked   apparently i was second to yamauchi  judging by the  too   sudou s  i m really counting on you too  ayanokouji   even if you ask me to help  you do know that there s not much i can do  right   just as expected  ike couldn t come up with how i d be useful  i looked over at kushida smugly  it was like i was showing off a talentless person s power   i had no idea how to answer  did they think i was her user manual  i took a huge mouthful of rice to avoid the question  his private read of horikita  she saw  the ending  when the teachers announced the incident    the possibility of a happy ending was almost nonexistent  she d probably been cold towards sudou on purpose  however  if i told them that now  they d probably become discouraged   ah  well  this might not be relevant  but i d like to say something  i think that horikita usually speaks in a rather brusque manner  but i think  that you guys misunderstand her   i think that she wouldn t help without any reason to do so   well  yeah  i m just guessing like you said  sudou   horikita is smart  right  so i think she probably had some idea   well  it d be great if a witness stepped forward  the teachers are going around and talking to each class about the incident  when they do find someone  things should get settled quickly   it wasn t unreasonable for horikita to throw in the towel  besides  even if there had been a witness  it d be checkmate for us if that witness happened to come from class c  this school was a hierarchy  after all   why would you say that  you know such a statement will alienate about half of the students here  right    his answer to ike s  i think people who participate in clubs are stupid  which is ike s line  on ike s page   nope   nothing between him and horikita   anyone     nope  no one    internally   if i had to choose someone  i probably would have picked  kushida  she was the person i talked to the most  so that was only natural  but knowing that she didn t like me  i couldn t really imagine things progressing   unlike you guys  i don t really know any girls apart from horikita and kushida   isn t it kind of pathetic that you re trying to introduce me to girls when you don t have a girlfriend yourself   i wondered if participating in such a shameless competition would actually make me their friend  it sounded difficult   although it was fine for them to get all excited  sudou s problem still hadn t been resolved  his verdict on ike s location tracking of kushida   he crossed his arms and wore a confident smile  what he was doing sounded just like stalking  another step forward and it would be appropriate to involve the police    he names the behaviour and does nothing about it  on the boys  fantasies aloud at the lunch table   in some ways  i felt a little sorry for kushida  she was most likely the subject of their nightly fantasies  in group defense he self deprecates on purpose  deflects horikita analysis into  just guessing  to protect morale  keeps score of his own low usefulness claims while privately holding the sharpest read in the room  ike s grudging  at least him being there is better than not  i guess  probably    ak s utility officially unexplained even to his defenders  publicly defends her reasoning to the boys  ike reads it as romance leaning  she s important to him  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): Horikita&#x27;s refusal dissected, the boys&#x27; romance council<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Even if you ask me to help, you do know that there’s not much I can do, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ah. Well, this might not be relevant, but I’d like to say something. I think that Horikita usually speaks in a rather brusque manner. But I think… that you guys misunderstand her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think that she wouldn’t help without any reason to do so.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On being ranked: &quot;Apparently I was second to Yamauchi, judging by the &#x27;too.&#x27;&quot; (Sudou&#x27;s &quot;I&#x27;m really counting on you too, Ayanokouji.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Just as expected, Ike couldn’t come up with how I’d be useful. I looked over at Kushida smugly. It was like I was showing off a talentless person’s power.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I had no idea how to answer. Did they think I was her user manual? I took a huge mouthful of rice to avoid the question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His private read of Horikita: she saw &quot;the ending&quot; when the teachers announced the incident — &quot;the possibility of a happy ending was almost nonexistent... she’d probably been cold towards Sudou on purpose. However, if I told them that now, they’d probably become discouraged.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well… Yeah, I’m just guessing like you said, Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horikita is smart, right? So I think she probably had some idea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, it’d be great if a witness stepped forward. The teachers are going around and talking to each class about the incident. When they do find someone, things should get settled quickly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;It wasn’t unreasonable for Horikita to throw in the towel. Besides, even if there had been a witness, it’d be checkmate for us if that witness happened to come from Class C... This school was a hierarchy, after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Why would you say that? You know such a statement will alienate about half of the students here, right?&quot; — his answer to Ike&#x27;s &quot;I think people who participate in clubs are stupid&quot;, which is Ike&#x27;s line, on Ike&#x27;s page.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nope.&quot; (nothing between him and Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Anyone…&quot; → &quot;Nope, no one,&quot; — internally: &quot;If I had to choose someone, I probably would have picked… Kushida? She was the person I talked to the most, so that was only natural. But knowing that she didn’t like me, I couldn’t really imagine things progressing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Unlike you guys, I don’t really know any girls apart from Horikita and Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn’t it kind of pathetic that you’re trying to introduce me to girls when you don’t have a girlfriend yourself?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I wondered if participating in such a shameless competition would actually make me their friend. It sounded difficult.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Although it was fine for them to get all excited, Sudou’s problem still hadn’t been resolved.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His verdict on Ike&#x27;s location-tracking of Kushida: &quot;He crossed his arms and wore a confident smile. What he was doing sounded just like stalking. Another step forward and it would be appropriate to involve the police.&quot; — he names the behaviour and does nothing about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the boys&#x27; fantasies aloud at the lunch table: &quot;In some ways, I felt a little sorry for Kushida. She was most likely the subject of their nightly fantasies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> In group defense he self-deprecates on purpose; deflects Horikita-analysis into &quot;just guessing&quot; to protect morale; keeps score of his own low usefulness claims while privately holding the sharpest read in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike&#x27;s grudging &quot;At least him being there is better than not, I guess? Probably?&quot; — AK&#x27;s utility officially unexplained even to his defenders.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Publicly defends her reasoning to the boys; Ike reads it as romance-leaning (&quot;She’s important to him, right?&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.46–47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): the fight goes public<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: roped in by Kushida; the Class B strategy session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 2 3 3  roped in by kushida  the class b strategy session team map  hirata   karuizawa lead the  hero   gal team  kushida the  beautiful girl   entourage team  ak tries to slip out   what  do you need something   i m sorry  kushida  i m going to steel my heart and refuse your invitation     thinks   p 55   i couldn t refuse  slightly upturned eyes   pleading   lethal  with the willpower breakdown analogy  everyone has their breaking point  it s a human mechanism   well  i can t argue with you there   kushida s chase horikita plan   busy  but everyone else is busy with sudou s case right now   blurted  earns horikita s glare   please stop saying that i understand you   after horikita tells kushida to ask him  the perpetrator lecture to kushida   i understand a little of what horikita meant  at the very least  sudou does share some fault in this case  he s the type who gets angry easily  right  whenever he s faced with someone he doesn t like  he lashes out  and speaks and acts in an aggressive  domineering way  when i heard he was being considered for a regular spot on the basketball team  i was both surprised and impressed  no one disagrees that he s an incredible player  but if he acts so arrogant and prideful  some people will come to hate him  those who work incredibly hard for their spot would probably see sudou as a rather disagreeable person  then there are the rumors  right  people say that sudou s been fighting people since junior high  i haven t met anyone who knew sudou at his previous school  but considering how many people are talking about it  there might be something to the rumor   this was bound to happen eventually  that s why horikita said sudou was a perpetrator   yeah  as long as he continues to antagonize those around him  trouble will inevitably follow  also  if there s no proof  then people will use his image against him  in other words  they ll judge him based on their impressions  for example  let s say there was a murder case  there are two suspects  one of them has committed murder in the past  while the other is a good  upstanding citizen  based on that information  who would you believe   the truth might be different  however  the less information you have upon which to base your judgment  the more you have to rely on whatever meager information you have at hand  that s what s happening here  horikita cannot overlook the fact that sudou doesn t recognize his flaws   i didn t think this was exactly a  you reap what you sow  situation  though   i guess so  yeah  by punishing him  she wants him to understand himself better   you should act according to your own principles  kushida  i don t think it s wrong to want to help sudou   however  i think it would be better if we carefully considered whether or not to directly point out sudou s problems  if he doesn t actually take the time to reflect  there s no point  there are certain realizations you can only come to on your own   kushida arched her back and stretched  i d changed her thinking    influence over the class s social engine  exercised quietly and without credit   if no one has any objections  how about we start by asking around class b   because that s the class that would most want a witness   between d and c  which class most threatens class b  or to put it another way  which class is more likely to threaten b s place in the ranking   we know too little about class a  i don t think they d want to get involved in a troublesome affair that might negatively impact their points  it s also possible that class a students don t care  as they feel no connection to what goes on between c and d  caution about b   if they had a particularly cunning person  he or she might have devised a plan to defeat not only c  but class d as well   stop   reflexively grabbing kushida s collar to halt her charge   it is certainly true that your excellent communication skills are indispensable  however  this isn t the same as casually strolling into another class and trying to make friends   do you know anyone in class b     well then  let s talk to those people first then   i see  you might be right about that  we should do what you think is best  kushida   concedes the one by one vs group ask debate   suddenly  i felt a sensation  like someone was watching me  i turned around    watched sense in a one third empty classroom  unresolved in chapter   so cuuute  reaction   she was probably being adorable on purpose  despite thinking that  my heart pounded like crazy   i wanna go home   grumbling at the window during the class b visit   you re probably right   to ike s anti club rant   agreeing while internally cataloguing club benefits   you gained the skills necessary to build relationships with other people  and you also got to experience victory and defeat   i waited for a few minutes until i received kushida s report  i certainly didn t expect what she told me    chapter ending hook into ch 4  she commands his schedule by asking nicely  he concedes plans to her judgment while supplying the strategy  collar grab intimacy registers as both protectiveness and fluster","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: roped in by Kushida; the Class B strategy session<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Team map: Hirata &amp; Karuizawa lead the &quot;Hero &amp; Gal Team,&quot; Kushida the &quot;Beautiful Girl &amp; Entourage Team&quot;; AK tries to slip out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What? Do you need something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, I can’t argue with you there.&quot; (Kushida&#x27;s chase-Horikita plan)<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Busy? But everyone else is busy with Sudou’s case right now,&quot; (blurted; earns Horikita&#x27;s glare)<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry, Kushida. I’m going to steel my heart and refuse your invitation.&quot; → [thinks] (p.55) &quot;I couldn’t refuse. Slightly upturned eyes + pleading = lethal.&quot; with the willpower-breakdown analogy (&quot;everyone has their breaking point. It’s a human mechanism.&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Please stop saying that I understand you.&quot; (after Horikita tells Kushida to ask him)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The perpetrator lecture to Kushida: &quot;I understand a little of what Horikita meant. At the very least, Sudou does share some fault in this case. He’s the type who gets angry easily, right? Whenever he’s faced with someone he doesn’t like, he lashes out, and speaks and acts in an aggressive, domineering way. When I heard he was being considered for a regular spot on the basketball team, I was both surprised and impressed. No one disagrees that he’s an incredible player, but if he acts so arrogant and prideful, some people will come to hate him. Those who work incredibly hard for their spot would probably see Sudou as a rather disagreeable person. Then there are the rumors, right? People say that Sudou’s been fighting people since junior high. I haven’t met anyone who knew Sudou at his previous school, but considering how many people are talking about it, there might be something to the rumor.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This was bound to happen eventually. That’s why Horikita said Sudou was a perpetrator.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. As long as he continues to antagonize those around him, trouble will inevitably follow. Also, if there’s no proof, then people will use his image against him. In other words, they’ll judge him based on their impressions. For example, let’s say there was a murder case. There are two suspects. One of them has committed murder in the past, while the other is a good, upstanding citizen. Based on that information, who would you believe?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The truth might be different. However, the less information you have upon which to base your judgment, the more you have to rely on whatever meager information you have at hand. That’s what’s happening here. Horikita cannot overlook the fact that Sudou doesn’t recognize his flaws.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I didn’t think this was exactly a &#x27;you reap what you sow&#x27; situation, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess so, yeah. By punishing him, she wants him to understand himself better.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should act according to your own principles, Kushida. I don’t think it’s wrong to want to help Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, I think it would be better if we carefully considered whether or not to directly point out Sudou’s problems. If he doesn’t actually take the time to reflect, there’s no point. There are certain realizations you can only come to on your own.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;Kushida arched her back and stretched; I’d changed her thinking.&quot; — influence over the class&#x27;s social engine, exercised quietly and without credit.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If no one has any objections, how about we start by asking around Class B?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Because that’s the class that would most want a witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Between D and C, which class most threatens Class B? Or to put it another way, which class is more likely to threaten B’s place in the ranking?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We know too little about Class A. I don’t think they’d want to get involved in a troublesome affair that might negatively impact their points. It&#x27;s also possible that Class A students don’t care, as they feel no connection to what goes on between C and D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Caution about B: &quot;If they had a particularly cunning person, he or she might have devised a plan to defeat not only C, but Class D as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Stop.&quot; (reflexively grabbing Kushida&#x27;s collar to halt her charge)<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It is certainly true that your excellent communication skills are indispensable. However, this isn’t the same as casually strolling into another class and trying to make friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you know anyone in Class B?&quot; → &quot;Well then, let’s talk to those people first then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. You might be right about that. We should do what you think is best, Kushida.&quot; (concedes the one-by-one vs group-ask debate)<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;Suddenly, I felt a sensation, like someone was watching me. I turned around.&quot; — watched-sense in a one-third-empty classroom; unresolved in-chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;So cuuute!&quot; reaction: &quot;She was probably being adorable on purpose… Despite thinking that, my heart pounded like crazy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wanna go home.&quot; (grumbling at the window during the Class B visit)<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re probably right,&quot; (to Ike&#x27;s anti-club rant — agreeing while internally cataloguing club benefits: &quot;You gained the skills necessary to build relationships with other people, and you also got to experience victory and defeat.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I waited for a few minutes until I received Kushida’s report. I certainly didn’t expect what she told me.&quot; — chapter-ending hook into Ch.4.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She commands his schedule by asking nicely; he concedes plans to her judgment while supplying the strategy; collar-grab intimacy registers as both protectiveness and fluster.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): Horikita&#x27;s refusal dissected, the boys&#x27; romance council<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: the class-change rule, and the mean-teacher read<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 0 4 1  the class change rule  and the mean teacher read on the search s division of labour   meanwhile  i was alone  like always  i could talk to kushida  but felt disadvantaged when it came to a big group  i couldn t really talk  so i asked kushida to fill in me later  the only witness to horikita s contempt for the grievance session   as her neighbor  i was the only one who noticed    and on her book   at a glance  i saw she was reading dostoevsky s demons  a good choice  he is one of two who can authenticate the class change claim  and he reads the teacher s glance   chabashira sensei shot a quick glance over at horikita and me  we had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school  his prior on the teacher  stated as a rule of the school   chabashira sensei sometimes withheld information  but she didn t lie  his verdict on the club points reveal   at any rate  i deduced that our homeroom teacher was being extremely and deliberately mean    followed by an even handed note on ike s side   if someone were to join a club simply for the sake of earning points  he or she probably wouldn t see great results  on the other hand  someone who joined the club for the sake of points might discover that they possessed a talent for it   horikita  doesn t this mean there s some value in saving sudou    the argument he chooses to make when he decides to move her  points  not feeling   it s better to have a lot of private points  right  he can supplement his own grade if he fails  and he can save others   whether class points or private points  it was better to have a lot of them  there were absolutely no negatives to that  also  we knew very little about how else to earn points at this stage  if our chances improved with sudou in the class  then that was reason enough to make an effort  he stops the moment she concedes   i considered it unnecessary to say more  so i stopped talking  horikita pondered the issue in silence  his self assessment on the canvassing   i hung behind kushida  ike  and the others  trailing them like a ghost  i was impressed  surprised  and in awe of their natural conversation skills  how could they talk with people they d never met before and behave like old friends  monsters  on horikita s refusal of kushida s invitations  which he watches daily   my neighbor who continued to reject kushida s invitations  no matter what sat with a nonchalant expression as she prepared for class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: the class-change rule, and the mean-teacher read<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He stops the moment she concedes: &quot;I considered it unnecessary to say more, so I stopped talking. Horikita pondered the issue in silence.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">On the search&#x27;s division of labour: &quot;Meanwhile, I was alone, like always. I could talk to Kushida, but felt disadvantaged when it came to a big group. I couldn’t really talk, so I asked Kushida to fill in me later.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Horikita. Doesn’t this mean there’s some value in saving Sudou?&quot; — the argument he chooses to make when he decides to move her: points, not feeling.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It’s better to have a lot of private points, right? He can supplement his own grade if he fails, and he can save others.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The only witness to Horikita&#x27;s contempt for the grievance session: &quot;As her neighbor, I was the only one who noticed.&quot; — and on her book: &quot;At a glance, I saw she was reading Dostoevsky’s Demons. A good choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> He is one of two who can authenticate the class-change claim, and he reads the teacher&#x27;s glance: &quot;Chabashira-sensei shot a quick glance over at Horikita and me. We had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His prior on the teacher, stated as a rule of the school: &quot;Chabashira-sensei sometimes withheld information, but she didn’t lie.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His verdict on the club-points reveal: &quot;At any rate, I deduced that our homeroom teacher was being extremely and deliberately mean.&quot; — followed by an even-handed note on Ike&#x27;s side: &quot;If someone were to join a club simply for the sake of earning points, he or she probably wouldn’t see great results... On the other hand, someone who joined the club for the sake of points might discover that they possessed a talent for it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Whether class points or private points, it was better to have a lot of them. There were absolutely no negatives to that. Also, we knew very little about how else to earn points at this stage. If our chances improved with Sudou in the class, then that was reason enough to make an effort.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His self-assessment on the canvassing: &quot;I hung behind Kushida, Ike, and the others, trailing them like a ghost. I was impressed, surprised, and in awe of their natural conversation skills... How could they talk with people they’d never met before and behave like old friends? Monsters.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On Horikita&#x27;s refusal of Kushida&#x27;s invitations, which he watches daily: &quot;my neighbor—who continued to reject Kushida’s invitations, no matter what—sat with a nonchalant expression as she prepared for class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: roped in by Kushida; the Class B strategy session<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: Horikita names the witness, and he cannot place her either<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 1  horikita names the witness  and he cannot place her either he notices the game sudou is playing while the meeting works   the person of interest  sudou  was completely engrossed in some kind of digital basketball game on his phone  i think the game was called generation of miracles or something  but i still didn t quite understand   she spoke as if she had already found the hypothetical witness    and the room s verdict on it   no one  myself included  really believed her until we heard her next words  horikita s observation beats his own  and he says so plainly   i hadn t noticed that at all  i was genuinely impressed by horikita s observational prowess  horikita s jab at him lands by name   since you were one of the people who also stares at kushida san  it s not surprising you didn t notice  his own contribution to identifying sakura is a memory of a name only   i probably know her  i feel like i ve heard her name somewhere before     i felt like i almost had something  but not quite  on being lumped in with the boys  appraisal of sakura s body without having said anything   even though i hadn t said anything  i felt like i was being lumped into the same category as ike and yamauchi  kushida s bitter smile seemed to say  you re also fixated on boobs  aren t you  you disgusting pervert  granted  that was my persecution complex speaking   i could barely match sakura s name to a face  i recalled seeing her back when we were making bets  the bet had been about boobs  though  i guess we were birds of a feather after all  his taxonomy of the class s four kinds of solitude  with himself as a category   kushida and hirata were proactive and able to open up to just about anyone  horikita didn t feel the agony of solitude  so what about sakura  did she like being alone  like horikita  or was she suffering because she didn t know how to connect with people  like me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: Horikita names the witness, and he cannot place her either<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.75–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He notices the game Sudou is playing while the meeting works: &quot;the person of interest, Sudou, was completely engrossed in some kind of digital basketball game on his phone... I think the game was called Generation of Miracles or something, but I still didn’t quite understand.&quot; His taxonomy of the class&#x27;s four kinds of solitude, with himself as a category: &quot;Kushida and Hirata were proactive and able to open up to just about anyone. Horikita didn’t feel the agony of solitude. So what about Sakura? Did she like being alone, like Horikita? Or was she suffering because she didn’t know how to connect with people, like me?&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">&quot;She spoke as if she had already found the hypothetical witness.&quot; — and the room&#x27;s verdict on it: &quot;No one, myself included, really believed her…until we heard her next words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Horikita&#x27;s jab at him lands by name: &quot;Since you were one of the people who also stares at Kushida-san, it’s not surprising you didn’t notice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">His own contribution to identifying Sakura is a memory of a name only: &quot;I probably know her. I feel like I’ve heard her name somewhere before,&quot; — &quot;I felt like I almost had something, but not quite.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s observation beats his own, and he says so plainly: &quot;I hadn’t noticed that at all. I was genuinely impressed by Horikita’s observational prowess.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On being lumped in with the boys&#x27; appraisal of Sakura&#x27;s body without having said anything: &quot;Even though I hadn’t said anything, I felt like I was being lumped into the same category as Ike and Yamauchi. Kushida’s bitter smile seemed to say, You’re also fixated on boobs, aren’t you? You disgusting pervert. Granted, that was my persecution complex speaking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I could barely match Sakura’s name to a face. I recalled seeing her back when we were making bets. The bet had been about boobs, though. I guess we were birds of a feather after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: the class-change rule, and the mean-teacher read<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the theory of personal space, and the cameras he had already found<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 2 4 3  the theory of personal space  and the cameras he had already found he diagnoses kushida s failure analytically  in the middle of an awkward conversation  by citing a discipline   cultural anthropologist edward hall further divided the idea of personal space into four parts  one such zone is the so called  intimate space    and applies it   however  sakura had clearly rejected kushida  no rather  it looked like she was running away  what he notices about sakura s body that nobody else in the room reports   sakura concealed her dominant hand while also avoiding eye contact  even if she weren t comfortable meeting someone s eyes  people generally looked in the direction of those to whom they were speaking  his own reading of kushida s one to one manner  held alongside the class s   though it was mostly out of formal obligation  sakura had exchanged numbers with kushida  kushida s behavior in a one on one conversation was different  though  i don t think horikita was wrong to feel some discomfort when speaking with kushida  i d found something a bit off putting about it myself   i don t think self defense is all that helpful in this case    ak   ah  i d accidentally said that aloud  the slip is the same conclusion he gave sudou privately in ch 2  p 33  said now without choosing to  kushida invades his space to ask for his loyalty and he catalogues his own reaction instead   man  kushida looked super cute up close  rather than feeling uncomfortable about this invasion of my personal space  i wanted her to come even closer   well  yeah  i am  why are you asking me that again  though   that he is sudou s ally  asserted without qualification   if even sakura  the key witness  denied sudou her help  then we d made no progress   there s a popular expression in this world  great talents mature late  sudou could probably become a professional player in the nba  right  i think there s a possibility that he ll make a great contribution to society  the power of youth is infinite    his own verdict on the performance   i uttered a catchphrase that sounded about as original as a television commercial  his discovery of the classroom cameras and the reason no one else saw them   well  ordinary people don t typically concern themselves with hidden cameras  or they might have accidentally spotted them  horikita asks him to walk back and he touches her forehead first   after hearing that invitation  i reflexively placed my hand against her forehead  it felt nice and cool  but i noticed the softness of her skin     it was rare for horikita to invite me anywhere  with the world going so topsy turvy  i wondered if it would rain tomorrow  hirata briefs him on the witness for horikita relay reasons  and invites him to hang out with the couple  ak s interior reaction is the volume s most explicit record of wanting to be included   hirata smiled  agreeably  if i were a girl  i would have gone from zero to 100 right there  and  ahh  i said the exact opposite of what i d been thinking  damn  curse my terrible mouth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the theory of personal space, and the cameras he had already found<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.86–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida invades his space to ask for his loyalty and he catalogues his own reaction instead: &quot;Man, Kushida looked super cute up close. Rather than feeling uncomfortable about this invasion of my personal space, I wanted her to come even closer.&quot; Horikita asks him to walk back and he touches her forehead first: &quot;After hearing that invitation, I reflexively placed my hand against her forehead. It felt nice and cool, but I noticed the softness of her skin.&quot; — &quot;It was rare for Horikita to invite me anywhere. With the world going so topsy-turvy, I wondered if it would rain tomorrow.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t think self-defense is all that helpful in this case.&quot; — AK: &quot;Ah, I’d accidentally said that aloud.&quot; The slip is the same conclusion he gave Sudou privately in Ch.2 (p.33), said now without choosing to.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well… Yeah, I am. Why are you asking me that again, though?&quot; (that he is Sudou&#x27;s ally, asserted without qualification)<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There’s a popular expression in this world: Great talents mature late. Sudou could probably become a professional player in the NBA, right? I think there’s a possibility that he’ll make a great contribution to society. The power…<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He diagnoses Kushida&#x27;s failure analytically, in the middle of an awkward conversation, by citing a discipline: &quot;Cultural anthropologist Edward Hall further divided the idea of personal space into four parts. One such zone is the so-called “intimate space.”&quot; — and applies it: &quot;However, Sakura had clearly rejected Kushida. No…rather, it looked like she was running away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he notices about Sakura&#x27;s body that nobody else in the room reports: &quot;Sakura concealed her dominant hand while also avoiding eye contact. Even if she weren’t comfortable meeting someone’s eyes, people generally looked in the direction of those to whom they were speaking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His own reading of Kushida&#x27;s one-to-one manner, held alongside the class&#x27;s: &quot;Though it was mostly out of formal obligation, Sakura had exchanged numbers with Kushida. Kushida’s behavior in a one on one conversation was different, though. I don’t think Horikita was wrong to feel some discomfort when speaking with Kushida. I’d found something a bit off-putting about it myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;If even Sakura, the key witness, denied Sudou her help, then we’d made no progress.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s a popular expression in this world: Great talents mature late. Sudou could probably become a professional player in the NBA, right? I think there’s a possibility that he’ll make a great contribution to society. The power of youth is infinite.&quot; — his own verdict on the performance: &quot;I uttered a catchphrase that sounded about as original as a television commercial.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His discovery of the classroom cameras and the reason no one else saw them: &quot;Well, ordinary people don’t typically concern themselves with hidden cameras... Or they might have accidentally spotted them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata briefs him on the witness for Horikita-relay reasons, and invites him to hang out with the couple; AK&#x27;s interior reaction is the volume&#x27;s most explicit record of wanting to be included: &quot;Hirata smiled, agreeably. If I were a girl, I would have gone from zero to 100 right there&quot; and &quot;Ahh, I said the exact opposite of what I’d been thinking. Damn, curse my terrible mouth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: Horikita names the witness, and he cannot place her either<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the special building, and the friend line he chooses to say<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 4  the special building  and the friend line he chooses to say  sudou was the first friend that i made here  i want to help him    said to horikita at the scene of the fight  nothing in his narration supports it  and she answers it as a contradiction   you re as contradictory as ever  since you re helping out a friend   i decided to take some initiative by myself  since i m not very good at interacting with hirata  kushida  or large groups of people  being social s definitely not my forte  i thought everyone would make me run around the school or the classroom today  so i decided to bolt instead  i like to avoid trouble  remember    the cover persona  offered as his own explanation for being at the building   of course i haven t  it s your job to come up with plans  horikita  i won t ask you to save sudou  but it d be nice for you to point class d in the right direction  his read of horikita s candor  and of everyone else s   most people aren t suited for loneliness  therefore  they sometimes behave hypocritically  like saving someone out of feigned altruism in order to make other people adore them  that didn t seem to be horikita s style  though  the case in one line  as he states it to himself at the scene   one party  either sudou or the class c students  had summoned the other to the special building  after that  as if by destiny  the two enemies started brawling  that was the whole case     our only proof was sudou s word  we were completely in the dark   you shouldn t feel obligated to appear as the witness  sakura  it d be pointless to force you to testify  but if someone scary is trying to intimidate you or something  please talk to us  i have no idea how much i can help  but i ll try    and his note on the recipient   sakura stopped  but didn t turn around   are you talking about me  horikita muttered    ignoring the existence of such a scary monster  i decided to let sakura go   then that s fine  however  if someone else tries to hound you about it  please tell me  how much horikita s certainty is worth   so far  we d been operating based purely on horikita s dogmatism and prejudices  it was quite possible that sakura wasn t the witness  like she said  he volunteers the whole case to a class b stranger   i told her that three people from class c had called sudou over  and there was a fistfight    his stated reason   since there wasn t much information to be gained anyway  it may not have been worth keeping quiet  his running account of ichinose s offer   obviously  i couldn t trust ichinose yet  she was a student from class b  and she gained nothing by involving herself  if helping others out of sheer goodwill was reflected in class or private points  then i could understand her motivation  on who decides   i glanced over to see what horikita thought  i didn t really have the power to decide in the first place  that was horikita s job  the information gap is now his explicit grievance against the school   this was yet another oversight  another instance where chabashira sensei had failed to disclose something important  a usual  our teacher didn t even pretend to give us equal treatment  i felt discriminated against","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the special building, and the friend line he chooses to say<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.97–107<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sudou was the first friend that I made here. I want to help him.&quot; — said to Horikita at the scene of the fight; nothing in his narration supports it, and she answers it as a contradiction: &quot;you’re as contradictory as ever, since…<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I decided to take some initiative by myself, since I’m not very good at interacting with Hirata, Kushida, or large groups of people. Being social’s definitely not my forte. I thought everyone would make me run around the school…<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Of course I haven’t. It’s your job to come up with plans, Horikita. I won’t ask you to save Sudou, but it’d be nice for you to point Class D in the right direction.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou was the first friend that I made here. I want to help him.&quot; — said to Horikita at the scene of the fight; nothing in his narration supports it, and she answers it as a contradiction: &quot;you’re as contradictory as ever, since you’re helping out a friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I decided to take some initiative by myself, since I’m not very good at interacting with Hirata, Kushida, or large groups of people. Being social’s definitely not my forte. I thought everyone would make me run around the school or the classroom today, so I decided to bolt instead. I like to avoid trouble, remember?&quot; — the cover persona, offered as his own explanation for being at the building.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His read of Horikita&#x27;s candor, and of everyone else&#x27;s: &quot;most people aren’t suited for loneliness. Therefore, they sometimes behave hypocritically, like saving someone out of feigned altruism in order to make other people adore them. That didn’t seem to be Horikita’s style, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The case in one line, as he states it to himself at the scene: &quot;One party, either Sudou or the Class C students, had summoned the other to the special building. After that, as if by destiny, the two enemies started brawling... That was the whole case.&quot; — &quot;Our only proof was Sudou’s word. We were completely in the dark.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You shouldn’t feel obligated to appear as the witness, Sakura. It’d be pointless to force you to testify. But if someone scary is trying to intimidate you or something, please talk to us. I have no idea how much I can help, but I’ll try.&quot; — and his note on the recipient: &quot;Sakura stopped, but didn’t turn around.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Are you talking about me?&quot; Horikita muttered — &quot;Ignoring the existence of such a scary monster, I decided to let Sakura go.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then that’s fine. However, if someone else tries to hound you about it, please tell me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> How much Horikita&#x27;s certainty is worth: &quot;So far, we’d been operating based purely on Horikita’s dogmatism and prejudices. It was quite possible that Sakura wasn’t the witness, like she said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> He volunteers the whole case to a Class B stranger: &quot;I told her that three people from Class C had called Sudou over, and there was a fistfight...&quot; — his stated reason: &quot;since there wasn’t much information to be gained anyway, it may not have been worth keeping quiet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His running account of Ichinose&#x27;s offer: &quot;Obviously, I couldn’t trust Ichinose yet. She was a student from Class B, and she gained nothing by involving herself. If helping others out of sheer goodwill was reflected in class or private points, then I could understand her motivation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On who decides: &quot;I glanced over to see what Horikita thought... I didn’t really have the power to decide in the first place; that was Horikita’s job.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The information gap is now his explicit grievance against the school: &quot;This was yet another oversight, another instance where Chabashira-sensei had failed to disclose something important... A usual, our teacher didn’t even pretend to give us equal treatment. I felt discriminated against.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the theory of personal space, and the cameras he had already found<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school with Class B&#x27;s representative<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 6  walking to school with class b s representative  it seemed i could have normal  relationship building conversations after all   i don t have to leave so early  i usually hang around my room for about 20 minutes    his answer to her question   aren t you usually a little late   was this the so called popularity phase i was told would occur three times in my life  i hadn t experienced it yet  it was about time that i entered my first phase  his default reading of any gift the school gives   it was all incredibly suspicious  i really didn t think our school was going to be so good to be true  they had to be keeping something from us  his own price for the coming summer event   it would probably be worth more than 10 or 20 points  however  it was difficult to imagine that it would change things by 500 or even 1 000 points   only people who have meaningful friendships can enjoy a vacation to its fullest  there s nothing quite as uncomfortable as traveling without close friends  especially when you re traveling with a group  just imagining it made me feel like throwing up   i don t hate it  i don t think i do  anyway    to  do you hate traveling   just recalled something a little bit traumatic    his own staging of the line   my dry laugher echoed through the hot hallway   translation typo kept as printed  the only trip he owns   i d never traveled with a friend before  i had gone to new york with my parents a long  long time ago  not a single millisecond of it had been fun  his private sorting of class d s misplacement  and the first naming of yukimura   horikita  kouenji  and yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone   isn t that how societal competition works  though  i don t think there s anything particularly strange about that   wouldn t it be wiser not to talk to someone from another class about this     i asked ichinose  feeling slightly worried  what he is actually checking for   after all  it was possible she could ve given me a valuable hint  and i d do something with it   i m not smart enough to engage in an exchange of ideas  all i can say is   i m sorry   that wasn t in the any of the hundred million books i d read    his reaction to her question about confessions  the grammar is the translation s  kept as printed  his unspoken defence  written as a line of dialogue inside his own head   was she going to call me disgusting  or a virgin  or a shitty moron   did someone confess to you   i don t think there s much point in looking for evidence or another witness  doing that would be a waste of time and a headache    his own dismissal of the case he is still working  speaker fixed by her answer   but you went to the scene of the crime the other day to investigate  right   even though i knew absolutely nothing was going to happen  i was pretty excited  that was what being a man was all about","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school with Class B&#x27;s representative<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.116–122<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t have to leave so early. I usually hang around my room for about 20 minutes.&quot; — his answer to her question, &quot;Aren’t you usually a little late?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t hate it. I don’t think I do, anyway…&quot; — to &quot;Do you hate traveling?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just recalled something a little bit traumatic.&quot; — his own staging of the line: &quot;My dry laugher echoed through the hot hallway.&quot; (translation typo kept as printed).<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;It seemed I could have normal, relationship-building conversations after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Was this the so-called popularity phase I was told would occur three times in my life? I hadn’t experienced it yet; it was about time that I entered my first phase.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His default reading of any gift the school gives: &quot;It was all incredibly suspicious. I really didn’t think our school was going to be so good to be true. They had to be keeping something from us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His own price for the coming summer event: &quot;It would probably be worth more than 10 or 20 points. However, it was difficult to imagine that it would change things by 500 or even 1,000 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Only people who have meaningful friendships can enjoy a vacation to its fullest. There’s nothing quite as uncomfortable as traveling without close friends, especially when you’re traveling with a group. Just imagining it made me feel like throwing up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The only trip he owns: &quot;I’d never traveled with a friend before. I had gone to New York with my parents a long, long time ago. Not a single millisecond of it had been fun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His private sorting of Class D&#x27;s misplacement, and the first naming of Yukimura: &quot;Horikita, Kouenji, and Yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn’t that how societal competition works, though? I don’t think there’s anything particularly strange about that,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wouldn’t it be wiser not to talk to someone from another class about this?&quot; — &quot;I asked Ichinose, feeling slightly worried.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he is actually checking for: &quot;After all, it was possible she could’ve given me a valuable hint, and I’d do something with it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m not smart enough to engage in an exchange of ideas. All I can say is, ‘I’m sorry.’&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;That…wasn’t in the any of the hundred million books I’d read.&quot; — his reaction to her question about confessions; the grammar is the translation&#x27;s, kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His unspoken defence, written as a line of dialogue inside his own head: &quot;Was she going to call me disgusting, or a virgin, or a shitty moron?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did someone confess to you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t think there’s much point in looking for evidence or another witness. Doing that would be a waste of time and a headache.&quot; — his own dismissal of the case he is still working; speaker fixed by her answer, &quot;But you went to the scene of the crime the other day to investigate, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Even though I knew absolutely nothing was going to happen, I was pretty excited. That was what being a man was all about.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the special building, and the friend line he chooses to say<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.7: he refuses to be the lie in someone else&#x27;s confession<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 7  he refuses to be the lie in someone else s confession  so  what should i do next   no way  did ichinose plan to confess to me    the misread the section is built on  corrected in the next line by her  i think someone will confess their feelings to me here   wouldn t it be better if i weren t here   i don t really think i m the person to ask for this  i don t have any experience with romantic confessions  there are probably other people in class b who could help   but ichinose  aren t you used to people confessing their feelings to you   i understand that you don t want to hurt anyone  but won t it be worse if they find out you lied   honestly  i think it would be much better for you to talk with this person one on one  truthfully   i m just a friend     i cut ichinose off before she could finish   ichinose  i didn t think this was something i should say  considering no one s ever confessed to me before  but i think it was a mistake for you to call me here     i spoke honestly  for both their sakes  the lecture on confession   it s true that confessing your feelings isn t easy to do  you spend every day in complete anguish  as you create the experience in your head over and over  and yet  you still can t confess your feelings  even when you think the time has come to actually do it  you can t say the words  i like you  they get stuck in your throat  that s what i think  don t you think you should answer someone when they desperately long to express their feelings  if you make the situation unclear  both of you may regret it later   trying to prevent someone s pain was useless  if you turned someone down  their feelings would inevitably be hurt  and then  even more hurt if the excuse were built on a lie   i left without waiting for ichinose s reply   that depends on you both   i m sorry for acting so full of myself back there     i said   i wondered how class b s ichinose honami planned to resolve this difficult situation  i had to admit  i was looking forward to seeing it  the one extended piece of sincere moral advice he gives all volume is about someone else s confession  delivered to a girl who did not ask for it  and followed by walking away before the answer arrives","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.7: he refuses to be the lie in someone else&#x27;s confession<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.123–127<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So, what should I do next?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Wouldn’t it be better if I weren’t here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t really think I’m the person to ask for this. I don’t have any experience with romantic confessions. There are probably other people in Class B who could help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;No way… Did Ichinose plan to confess to me?!&quot; — the misread the section is built on, corrected in the next line by her &quot;I think someone will confess their feelings to me here&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But Ichinose, aren’t you used to people confessing their feelings to you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand that you don’t want to hurt anyone, but won’t it be worse if they find out you lied?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Honestly, I think it would be much better for you to talk with this person one-on-one. Truthfully.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m just a friend.&quot; — &quot;I cut Ichinose off before she could finish.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ichinose. I didn’t think this was something I should say, considering no one’s ever confessed to me before. But I think it was a mistake for you to call me here.&quot; — &quot;I spoke honestly, for both their sakes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The lecture on confession: &quot;It’s true that confessing your feelings isn’t easy to do. You spend every day in complete anguish, as you create the experience in your head over and over. And yet, you still can’t confess your feelings. Even when you think the time has come to actually do it, you can’t say the words ‘I like you’. They get stuck in your throat. That’s what I think. Don’t you think you should answer someone when they desperately long to express their feelings? If you make the situation unclear, both of you may regret it later.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Trying to prevent someone’s pain was useless. If you turned someone down, their feelings would inevitably be hurt.&quot; and then &quot;Even more hurt if the excuse were built on a lie.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I left without waiting for Ichinose’s reply.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That depends on you both.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry for acting so full of myself back there,&quot; — &quot;I said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I wondered how Class B’s Ichinose Honami planned to resolve this difficult situation. I had to admit, I was looking forward to seeing it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The one extended piece of sincere moral advice he gives all volume is about someone else&#x27;s confession, delivered to a girl who did not ask for it, and followed by walking away before the answer arrives.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school with Class B&#x27;s representative<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.8: the first call she makes to him, and the silence she cannot finish<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 8  the first call she makes to him  and the silence she cannot finish  caller id displayed the name  kushida kikyou  i did a double take to make sure of what i saw  knowing i wouldn t have the guts to call her back  i rolled my chair across the room  snatched my phone off the stand  and dove onto the bed   i don t think you should feel responsible  kushida  not in the least  besides  she s going to get it fixed  right  since it s so important to her  wouldn t she get it repaired no matter what  he corrects his own answer mid call   however  as i spoke i realized it probably wasn t that simple  and  it was probably similar to how someone might feel about dining alone in a restaurant   do you want me to ask if she knows anything about sudou s incident   kushida had probably chosen me through the process of elimination  as i was the least harmful candidate  if she d invited ike or yamauchi along  they would have had eyes only for kushida   okay  i understand  let s go     my voice cracked with a little too much excitement   it was proof that she could invade my personal space without causing discomfort  in my mind  i d firmly recognized her as my friend  his real opinion of horikita s singularity  withheld   horikita wasn t special  she belonged to a unique class of people  i kept quiet  though  afraid that if i badmouthed her she d find out about it   when i think of my relationship with horikita  it s like there s a wall between us  or perhaps i should say that s the extent of our relationship  if you understand what i m getting at   ah  that reminds me  i wanted to ask you something  your room is on the ninth floor  right  kushida   oh  no reason  just curious   ah  if only i were a pretty boy with excellent communication skills  i couldn t help but wish for that   it s getting late  should i hang up now     i asked  unable to bear the silence  his self assessment on the edge of her almost sentence   sorry  kushida  if i were on the battlefield  i d be the sniper  the chicken who would stay far away from the fighting  forgive me  one modest reply in this call carries no speaker tag in the translation and is not assigned here  after kushida credits  you and hirata  for class d coming together  an unattributed voice disowns any specialness and is answered   i think hirata would definitely say the same thing  she calls him first  late  to ask a favour  he reports her near confession and does not ask her to finish it   i lacked the courage to say  and  to her  so i let it go","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.8: the first call she makes to him, and the silence she cannot finish<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.128–131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;Caller ID displayed the name: Kushida Kikyou. I did a double take to make sure of what I saw. Knowing I wouldn’t have the guts to call her back, I rolled my chair across the room, snatched my phone off the stand, and dove onto the bed.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don’t think you should feel responsible, Kushida. Not in the least. Besides, she’s going to get it fixed, right? Since it’s so important to her, wouldn’t she get it repaired no matter what?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you want me to ask if she knows anything about Sudou’s incident?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Okay, I understand. Let’s go.&quot; — &quot;My voice cracked with a little too much excitement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He corrects his own answer mid-call: &quot;However, as I spoke I realized it probably wasn’t that simple.&quot; and &quot;It was probably similar to how someone might feel about dining alone in a restaurant.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Kushida had probably chosen me through the process of elimination, as I was the least harmful candidate. If she’d invited Ike or Yamauchi along, they would have had eyes only for Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;It was proof that she could invade my personal space without causing discomfort. In my mind, I’d firmly recognized her as my friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His real opinion of Horikita&#x27;s singularity, withheld: &quot;Horikita wasn’t special. She belonged to a unique class of people. I kept quiet, though, afraid that if I badmouthed her she’d find out about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When I think of my relationship with Horikita, it’s like there’s a wall between us. Or perhaps I should say that’s the extent of our relationship, if you understand what I’m getting at.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, that reminds me. I wanted to ask you something. Your room is on the ninth floor, right, Kushida?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no reason. Just curious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Ah, if only I were a pretty boy with excellent communication skills. I couldn’t help but wish for that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s getting late. Should I hang up now?&quot; — &quot;I asked, unable to bear the silence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His self-assessment on the edge of her almost-sentence: &quot;Sorry, Kushida. If I were on the battlefield, I’d be the sniper, the chicken who would stay far away from the fighting. Forgive me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> One modest reply in this call carries no speaker tag in the translation and is not assigned here: after Kushida credits &quot;you and Hirata&quot; for Class D coming together, an unattributed voice disowns any specialness and is answered, &quot;I think Hirata would definitely say the same thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She calls him first, late, to ask a favour; he reports her near-confession and does not ask her to finish it: &quot;I lacked the courage to say&quot; and &quot;to her, so I let it go.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128–131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.7: he refuses to be the lie in someone else&#x27;s confession<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: the mall, and the form he fills in himself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 9 4 10  the mall  and the form he fills in himself  our back and forth felt like the template for a date   seeing kushida in casual attire for the first time was so overwhelming  i couldn t look away  the gathering he was not told about   last week  really glad i came despite that  what the heck was she talking about  and  this was the first i d heard about it  i didn t recall any previous  hidden event   i looked up to the heavens and lamented my worthlessness  it s not like ike and the others were bad for not inviting me  i was the bad guy  the one who hadn t been invited   don t worry about it  really  i don t care  was it fun   i think we ve had really nice weather lately     worried that we were heading into cliched territory  i steered the conversation in another direction   ah  sorry  i think i might look a little out of place next to you   so  you re saying someone simple like me is a good match for you  i should accept an insult like that   i felt the quick thrust of a knife  maybe i d dug my own grave by setting myself up like that  but it was still a shock   perhaps it was love at first sight   no  i don t think you blend in too much  i definitely felt your presence   had sakura really been sitting there the entire time  amazing that we hadn t noticed her at all  not a sign of her presence or aura   because kushida didn t show any signs of disliking the conversation  he probably thought he could successfully ask her out  however  i believed she would try her hardest to sidestep the invitation  what he sees and neither girl does   both sakura and kushida were looking down at the form  so they didn t notice  but the clerk had unsettling eyes  even men would find it a little creepy   can i see that for a second   when the repairs are finished  please contact me   the manufacturer warranty explicitly shows where the item was sold and the date of purchase  also  i doubt there d be any legal problems with me putting my information down  it should be perfectly fine if the user s name is different than the purchaser s   or  is there a reason why she specifically has to enter her information   if that s all it takes to please you  then it actually makes me sorry for you   well  you re making it out to be bigger than it was  honestly  i was only watching out for that rather weird clerk  i guess he gave the impression that he really  really loved girls   although my imagination ran wild  i couldn t let it show on my face  i had to remain neutral  the question about whether sakura photographs people carries no speaker tag and is not assigned  only her refusal and his report of it are recorded   it sounded like she didn t want to go into the details with me   hey professor  do you have a minute   professor  did you buy your laptop computer from the school  with your points   i m looking for something     i explained the gist of what i wanted  although many similar products sat on the displays in front of me  i didn t know which one to choose  why he phones a classmate instead of the clerk   it probably would ve been faster to just ask the store clerk  but i didn t want to for various reasons   sotomura s nickname was professor  which undoubtedly made it sound like he was rather intelligent  in reality  he was just a huge otaku  he gathered information daily  comprehensively spanning a wide variety of topics  from dating sims to anime and manga   today was just a preliminary inspection  i don t have enough points to buy anything   when entering a subject that i didn t understand  it was important to find an expert  the object he is shopping for is not named in chapter 4  it is described only as something with  many similar products  on the display  the visit is booked as a  preliminary inspection  and the purchase is deferred for lack of points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: the mall, and the form he fills in himself<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.132–144<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;Our back and forth felt like the template for a date.&quot; The question about whether Sakura photographs people carries no speaker tag and is not assigned; only her refusal and his report of it are recorded: &quot;It sounded like she didn’t want to go into the details with me.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t worry about it. Really, I don’t care. Was it fun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think we’ve had really nice weather lately.&quot; — &quot;Worried that we were heading into clichéd territory, I steered the conversation in another direction.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ah. Sorry. I think I might look a little out of place next to you,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Seeing Kushida in casual attire for the first time was so overwhelming, I couldn’t look away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The gathering he was not told about: &quot;Last week? Really glad I came despite that? What the heck was she talking about?&quot; and &quot;This was the first I’d heard about it. I didn’t recall any previous, hidden event.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I looked up to the heavens and lamented my worthlessness. It’s not like Ike and the others were bad for not inviting me. I was the bad guy, the one who hadn’t been invited.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, you’re saying someone simple like me is a good match for you? I should accept an insult like that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I felt the quick thrust of a knife. Maybe I’d dug my own grave by setting myself up like that, but it was still a shock.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps it was love at first sight?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, I don’t think you blend in too much. I definitely felt your presence,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;Had Sakura really been sitting there the entire time? Amazing that we hadn’t noticed her at all. Not a sign of her presence or aura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Because Kushida didn’t show any signs of disliking the conversation, he probably thought he could successfully ask her out. However, I believed she would try her hardest to sidestep the invitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he sees and neither girl does: &quot;Both Sakura and Kushida were looking down at the form, so they didn’t notice. But the clerk had unsettling eyes. Even men would find it a little creepy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can I see that for a second?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When the repairs are finished, please contact me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The manufacturer warranty explicitly shows where the item was sold and the date of purchase. Also, I doubt there’d be any legal problems with me putting my information down. It should be perfectly fine if the user’s name is different than the purchaser’s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Or, is there a reason why she specifically has to enter her information?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;If that’s all it takes to please you, then it actually makes me sorry for you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, you’re making it out to be bigger than it was. Honestly, I was only watching out for that rather weird clerk. I guess he gave the impression that he really, really loved girls.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Although my imagination ran wild, I couldn’t let it show on my face. I had to remain neutral.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey Professor, do you have a minute?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Professor, did you buy your laptop computer from the school, with your points?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m looking for something.&quot; — &quot;I explained the gist of what I wanted. Although many similar products sat on the displays in front of me, I didn’t know which one to choose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Why he phones a classmate instead of the clerk: &quot;It probably would’ve been faster to just ask the store clerk, but I didn’t want to for various reasons.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Sotomura’s nickname was Professor, which undoubtedly made it sound like he was rather intelligent. In reality, he was just a huge otaku. He gathered information daily, comprehensively spanning a wide variety of topics, from dating sims to anime and manga.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Today was just a preliminary inspection. I don’t have enough points to buy anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;When entering a subject that I didn’t understand, it was important to find an expert.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The object he is shopping for is not named in Chapter 4: it is described only as something with &quot;many similar products&quot; on the display, the visit is booked as a &quot;preliminary inspection&quot;, and the purchase is deferred for lack of points.<span class=\"pg\">p.143–144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.8: the first call she makes to him, and the silence she cannot finish<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.10–4.11: the wall around Sakura, and the call that goes nowhere<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 10 4 11  the wall around sakura  and the call that goes nowhere  perhaps this was how people became friends  little by little  even sakura  who seemed to have hardly interacted with another person ever  was steadily growing closer to kushida  his stated theory of how to reach an unsociable person  in the same breath as kushida s practice of it   if you tried to strong arm people who weren t good at socializing  it could backfire  rather than be grateful  they d probably find it off putting  rather than draw them nearer  being overbearing would probably end up pushing them further away   the fact that sakura had waited until now to talk proved that she was more concerned about sudou s case than anything else  i wondered if getting a foothold on friendship made her want to cooperate   i wondered if a new friendship had been born right here  right now  at any rate  we had sudou s witness   that reminds me  why did you try to get sakura to take off her glasses     i asked kushida   back when her camera fell and sakura had bent down to pick it up  i d seen her glasses from the side  something about them had struck me as being out of place   i felt like there s something a little off  like she s wearing fake glasses   although real glasses and fake ones appear similar at first glance  there is definitely a difference between them  real glasses show some distortion on the lenses  there wasn t any distortion on sakura s glasses   or maybe it s to cover up some kind of complex  like how someone thinks they ll appear intelligent by putting on glasses   in sakura s case  though  she probably wears them because she doesn t want others to see her true self  she s always slouching and won t look people in the eye  i doubt it s simply because she dislikes other people   i felt like there was some hidden way to get over that wall  something  his caller priority rule  stated in full   if it were ike or yamauchi  i d call them back later  but if it were horikita i d have to think about it   i answered sakura s call before it cut out   even when i formally exchanged contact information with someone  nine times out of ten i wouldn t get a call   what should i do  please  hirata  teach me   something about the emotion behind her words made me uneasy  so i cast a verbal line to see if i could reel in anything else  however  the line tautened and snapped as soon as it touched water   did something happen  he remembers kushida s morning wording  and remembers it wrongly   i was asked to invite you as well  ayanokouji kun  did you talk to sakura san    what she actually said at the mall was  she asked me to invite you  ayanokouji kun  the only thing he contributed that day  by his own inventory   sakura and kushida struck up most of the conversations  but i d broached a topic  namely  the clerk at the store who d helped with the repair order  i hadn t brought up anything else   all of the puzzle pieces i d collected were too small  and too few  i was able to conjure up several scenarios and speculations  but they all lacked credibility  i didn t have enough information to come to a definitive decision  why he will not simply go and ask her   if i just went up and started talking to sakura  who normally didn t talk to anyone  it would make her stand out  she wouldn t like that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.10–4.11: the wall around Sakura, and the call that goes nowhere<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.145–151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;I answered Sakura’s call before it cut out.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That reminds me, why did you try to get Sakura to take off her glasses?&quot; — &quot;I asked Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I felt like there’s something a little off, like she’s wearing fake glasses.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Although real glasses and fake ones appear similar at first glance, there is definitely a difference between them. Real glasses show some distortion on the lenses. There wasn’t any distortion on Sakura’s glasses.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Perhaps this was how people became friends, little by little. Even Sakura, who seemed to have hardly interacted with another person ever, was steadily growing closer to Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His stated theory of how to reach an unsociable person, in the same breath as Kushida&#x27;s practice of it: &quot;If you tried to strong-arm people who weren’t good at socializing, it could backfire. Rather than be grateful, they’d probably find it off-putting. Rather than draw them nearer, being overbearing would probably end up pushing them further away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The fact that Sakura had waited until now to talk proved that she was more concerned about Sudou’s case than anything else. I wondered if getting a foothold on friendship made her want to cooperate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I wondered if a new friendship had been born right here, right now. At any rate, we had Sudou’s witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Back when her camera fell and Sakura had bent down to pick it up, I’d seen her glasses from the side. Something about them had struck me as being out of place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Or maybe it’s to cover up some kind of complex? Like how someone thinks they’ll appear intelligent by putting on glasses?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In Sakura’s case, though, she probably wears them because she doesn’t want others to see her true self. She’s always slouching and won’t look people in the eye. I doubt it’s simply because she dislikes other people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I felt like there was some hidden way to get over that wall. Something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His caller-priority rule, stated in full: &quot;If it were Ike or Yamauchi, I’d call them back later. But if it were Horikita…I’d have to think about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Even when I formally exchanged contact information with someone, nine times out of ten I wouldn’t get a call.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;What should I do? Please, Hirata. Teach me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Something about the emotion behind her words made me uneasy, so I cast a verbal line to see if I could reel in anything else. However, the line tautened and snapped as soon as it touched water.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did something happen?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He remembers Kushida&#x27;s morning wording, and remembers it wrongly: &quot;I was asked to invite you as well, Ayanokouji-kun. Did you talk to Sakura-san?&quot; — what she actually said at the mall was &quot;She asked me to invite you, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The only thing he contributed that day, by his own inventory: &quot;Sakura and Kushida struck up most of the conversations, but I’d broached a topic. Namely, the clerk at the store who’d helped with the repair order. I hadn’t brought up anything else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;All of the puzzle pieces I’d collected were too small, and too few. I was able to conjure up several scenarios and speculations, but they all lacked credibility. I didn’t have enough information to come to a definitive decision.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Why he will not simply go and ask her: &quot;If I just went up and started talking to Sakura, who normally didn’t talk to anyone, it would make her stand out. She wouldn’t like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: the mall, and the form he fills in himself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: the last day, and a screen he should not have seen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 0  the last day  and a screen he should not have seen one day before the meeting  the class is united but  it was obvious that we lacked firm  irrefutable evidence  a flyer on the bulletin board by the stairway offers points to anyone with information on sudou and class c  kanzaki of class b posted it on friday   i saw the paper on the bulletin board  did you post it  ichinose   huh  this wasn t you  introduced to kanzaki   he was tall and slender  a pretty boy  but in a different way from hirata   nice to meet you  kanzaki  the leaked account of ishizaki changes his picture of the fight   yet sudou had turned the tables  and beat them all without once being hit himself  then  i couldn t help but feel there was something unnatural about that  his private odds  said to no one   if we got testimony from class d  though  our chances would probably be 6 to 4  or maybe 7 to 3   no  we can t say anything yet    and he keeps her out of it   i concealed sakura s name since we were still negotiating  the payment mechanism  taught at the counter   from your id number  you can issue a temporary token key  if you open that  and send the key  you should get a request for payment  he walks ichinose through the points screen  being close enough to notice her scent makes his heart rate climb  what he sees on her phone is never described  only its effect   the fragment of screen i d noticed had burned itself into my mind and wouldn t go away  then  ichinose might prove a huge obstacle for horikita in her quest to reach class a  the chapter does not name what was on the screen  it stays open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.0: the last day, and a screen he should not have seen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.152–158<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One day before the meeting; the class is united but &quot;it was obvious that we lacked firm, irrefutable evidence&quot;. A flyer on the bulletin board by the stairway offers points to anyone with information on Sudou and Class C; Kanzaki of Class B posted it on Friday. Introduced to Kanzaki: &quot;He was tall and slender. A pretty boy, but in a different way from Hirata.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I saw the paper on the bulletin board. Did you post it, Ichinose?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Huh? This wasn’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nice to meet you, Kanzaki.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The leaked account of Ishizaki changes his picture of the fight: &quot;Yet Sudou had turned the tables, and beat them all without once being hit himself.&quot; then &quot;I couldn’t help but feel there was something unnatural about that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His private odds, said to no one: &quot;If we got testimony from Class D, though, our chances would probably be 6 to 4, or maybe 7 to 3.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, we can’t say anything yet.&quot; — and he keeps her out of it: &quot;I concealed Sakura’s name since we were still negotiating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The payment mechanism, taught at the counter: &quot;From your ID number, you can issue a temporary token key. If you open that, and send the key, you should get a request for payment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He walks Ichinose through the points screen; being close enough to notice her scent makes his heart rate climb.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he sees on her phone is never described, only its effect: &quot;The fragment of screen I’d noticed had burned itself into my mind and wouldn’t go away.&quot; then &quot;Ichinose might prove a huge obstacle for Horikita in her quest to reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The chapter does not name what was on the screen; it stays open.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.10–4.11: the wall around Sakura, and the call that goes nowhere<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.5: the night visit, and a definition of friendship<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 1 5 5  the night visit  and a definition of friendship he refuses the obvious reading of horikita s face and then accepts it as a baffling realization   in that moment  i had come to a rather baffling realization  he explains the seating outcome to himself   it was precisely because they might not make the best team that i d been appointed as a substitute  i supposed  her email asks him to room 1106  the girls  floor is open to boys  but entry is prohibited after 8 00 pm  her remark about eyes turns into self examination   so  was it like insight into a person s true self  when someone looked at me  would they see that i was insubstantial and lack ambition   i think you should do what you want  sakura   sakura  i think you ll be able to make friends with someone in no time   it might be presumptuous for me to say this  but i think that we re like friends  we are   well  why not go out with me for a while  if it s not a bother  of course  he picks up the fallen glasses  confirms there are no lenses  and hands them back without comment  the advice he gives her   for sudou  for kushida  for your classmates  throw all of those thoughts away  then  tell the truth for your own sake  do that  and sudou will be saved  that s enough  his reason for giving it   maybe i did it because i understood how it felt to be wanted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.5: the night visit, and a definition of friendship<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–177<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her email asks him to room 1106; the girls&#x27; floor is open to boys, but entry is prohibited after 8:00 PM.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think you should do what you want, Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura, I think you’ll be able to make friends with someone in no time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It might be presumptuous for me to say this, but I think that we’re like friends. We are,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He refuses the obvious reading of Horikita&#x27;s face and then accepts it as a baffling realization: &quot;In that moment, I had come to a rather baffling realization.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He explains the seating outcome to himself: &quot;It was precisely because they might not make the best team that I’d been appointed as a substitute, I supposed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Her remark about eyes turns into self-examination: &quot;So, was it like insight into a person’s true self? When someone looked at me, would they see that I was insubstantial and lack ambition?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, why not go out with me for a while? If it’s not a bother, of course.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He picks up the fallen glasses, confirms there are no lenses, and hands them back without comment.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The advice he gives her: &quot;For Sudou. For Kushida. For your classmates. Throw all of those thoughts away.&quot; then &quot;Tell the truth for your own sake. Do that, and Sudou will be saved. That’s enough.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His reason for giving it: &quot;Maybe I did it because I understood how it felt to be wanted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: the last day, and a screen he should not have seen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.6–5.7: proof, and what cannot be fixed by morning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 6 5 7  proof  and what cannot be fixed by morning  no  kushida is definitely right  that s sakura  here   you can barely see it  but the door to her dorm room is in this picture   good job noticing this  kushida  the link he makes alone   i flashed on a memory of the man who worked at the campus electronic store   the clerk  on the other hand  had been in incredibly high spirits  after all  here was his chance to get his favorite idol s real name and phone number on the form she had to fill out   in the end  the only option was to wait on an sos from the girl in question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.6–5.7: proof, and what cannot be fixed by morning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–188<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No, Kushida is definitely right. That’s Sakura. Here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You can barely see it, but the door to her dorm room is in this picture.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good job noticing this, Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The link he makes alone: &quot;I flashed on a memory of the man who worked at the campus electronic store.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The clerk, on the other hand, had been in incredibly high spirits. After all, here was his chance to get his favorite idol’s real name and phone number on the form she had to fill out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> &quot;In the end, the only option was to wait on an SOS from the girl in question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.5: the night visit, and a definition of friendship<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the check he makes first<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 open  the check he makes first the morning of the hearing  before anything else he confirms sakura came  and finds her in the usual corner   sakura sat quietly alone  so as not to get roped into other students  conversations   are you okay   don t forget what i said yesterday  testify for your own sake  more than anyone else s  the sentence is the volume s thesis carried forward from the club building  the testimony must belong to her  not to sudo or the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 open: the check he makes first<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.190<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The morning of the hearing; before anything else he confirms Sakura came, and finds her in the usual corner: &quot;Sakura sat quietly alone, so as not to get roped into other students’ conversations.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don’t forget what I said yesterday. Testify for your own sake, more than anyone else’s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The sentence is the volume’s thesis carried forward from the club building: the testimony must belong to her, not to Sudō or the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.6–5.7: proof, and what cannot be fixed by morning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the hearing he cannot fix<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the hearing he cannot fix class d s room before the 4 00 pm hearing  he watches sudo and horikita spar and reads sudo s cooperation as proof he does not hate her  his estimate of sakura is the chapter s first alarm   if she was in this psychological state before the meeting had even begun  she might not be able to speak satisfactorily  the student council room  three class c students  sakagami sensei  the president and secretary tachibana  horikita freezes at the word  student council  his read of the room before a word of evidence   considering they were brother and sister  the odds were not in our favor  he reads class c s testimony as invention   the veins on sudo s forehead make their account  rather obvious  as a lie   and horikita s silence as the real emergency   it was as if her mind was gone   get a grip on yourself  horikita  we re going to lose at this rate  you have to fight  he gets up  stands behind horikita  grips her sides  as hard as i could  and tickles her until she returns to herself  in front of the teachers and the student council  the provocation is deliberate and public  he accepts that he  might be killed later for doing this  but judged that no lesser stimulus would bring her back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the hearing he cannot fix<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–200<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s room before the 4:00 PM hearing; he watches Sudō and Horikita spar and reads Sudō’s cooperation as proof he does not hate her. The student council room: three Class C students, Sakagami-sensei, the president and Secretary Tachibana; Horikita freezes at the word &quot;student council.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Get a grip on yourself, Horikita. We’re going to lose at this rate. You have to fight!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His estimate of Sakura is the chapter’s first alarm: &quot;If she was in this psychological state before the meeting had even begun, she might not be able to speak satisfactorily.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His read of the room before a word of evidence: &quot;Considering they were brother and sister, the odds were not in our favor.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He reads Class C’s testimony as invention — the veins on Sudō’s forehead make their account &quot;rather obvious&quot; as a lie — and Horikita’s silence as the real emergency: &quot;It was as if her mind was gone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He gets up, stands behind Horikita, grips her sides &quot;as hard as I could&quot; and tickles her until she returns to herself, in front of the teachers and the student council.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The provocation is deliberate and public: he accepts that he &quot;might be killed later for doing this&quot; but judged that no lesser stimulus would bring her back.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the check he makes first<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the performance of giving up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the performance of giving up his conclusion about sakagami before the photos   no matter what response we volleyed back  i was convinced that he d do anything to block us   horikita  are we really out of options   i m not very smart  so i can t really come up with a solution  i do  however  think that we probably should accept the compromise that you have offered us  sakagami sensei   we have no definitive proof of sudou s innocence  i suppose i should say such evidence just doesn t exist  if this event had occurred in a classroom or the convenience store  a greater number of students would have been around to see it  and there probably would have been sound evidence  there s no record of anyone watching this scene unfold  since this event took place in the special building  where there weren t any people around  there s nothing we can do   i understand why we re having this discussion  no matter how much we appeal to the contrary  class c won t admit that they lied  sudou won t admit that he lied  either  we really would just keep going back and forth  honestly  it s getting to the point where i would ve been happier never having had this discussion in the first place  don t you agree  the surrender speech is a performance aimed at horikita  not at sakagami   i spoke as if we were accepting defeat  he had decided to speak  perhaps out of respect for sakura s earlier courage  the move depends on sakagami taking it literally  which he does   in other words  as a declaration of defeat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the performance of giving up<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.202–206<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Horikita, are we really out of options?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m not very smart, so I can’t really come up with a solution. I do, however, think that we probably should accept the compromise that you have offered us, Sakagami-sensei,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We have no definitive proof of Sudou’s innocence. I suppose I should say such evidence just doesn’t exist. If this event had occurred in a classroom or the convenience store, a greater number of students would have been around…<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His conclusion about Sakagami before the photos: &quot;no matter what response we volleyed back, I was convinced that he’d do anything to block us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We have no definitive proof of Sudou’s innocence. I suppose I should say such evidence just doesn’t exist. If this event had occurred in a classroom or the convenience store, a greater number of students would have been around to see it, and there probably would have been sound evidence. There’s no record of anyone watching this scene unfold. Since this event took place in the special building, where there weren’t any people around, there’s nothing we can do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand why we’re having this discussion. No matter how much we appeal to the contrary, Class C won’t admit that they lied. Sudou won’t admit that he lied, either. We really would just keep going back and forth. Honestly, it’s getting to the point where I would’ve been happier never having had this discussion in the first place. Don’t you agree?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The surrender speech is a performance aimed at Horikita, not at Sakagami: &quot;I spoke as if we were accepting defeat.&quot; He had decided to speak &quot;perhaps out of respect for Sakura’s earlier courage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The move depends on Sakagami taking it literally, which he does: &quot;In other words, as a declaration of defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the hearing he cannot fix<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor, and what he will not concede<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the corridor  and what he will not concede  it would ve ended the same even if you had stepped forward at the beginning  they would ve fought to discredit your testimony simply because the witness came from class d  the result would be the same   i m not exactly zhuge liang or kuroda kanbei  i don t have any plans   hyperbole  you mean  i don t think so   i believe her  i believe sakura s testimony   i didn t say that i want to believe her  i said i believe her  those mean different things   that s not up to me  your sister will prove it  if sakura isn t lying  then she will find a way to convince everyone  the first long conversation between them without a crisis forcing it  the narrator finds him  easy to talk to now  and credits  a superior understanding of human nature  he separates belief from wish in one sentence  and refuses the president s framing that his support is merely class loyalty","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor, and what he will not concede<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210–212<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It would’ve ended the same even if you had stepped forward at the beginning. They would’ve fought to discredit your testimony simply because the witness came from Class D. The result would be the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m not exactly Zhuge Liang or Kuroda Kanbei. I don’t have any plans.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hyperbole, you mean? I don’t think so.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I believe her. I believe Sakura’s testimony,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I didn’t say that I want to believe her. I said I believe her. Those mean different things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not up to me. Your sister will prove it. If Sakura isn’t lying, then she will find a way to convince everyone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The first long conversation between them without a crisis forcing it; the narrator finds him &quot;easy to talk to now&quot; and credits &quot;a superior understanding of human nature.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He separates belief from wish in one sentence, and refuses the president’s framing that his support is merely class loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the performance of giving up<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: leaving the hearing, and Class B’s offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 2  leaving the hearing  and class b s offer the walk back after the hearing  sakura has stopped crying and the silence between them is comfortable   i m glad  when i was a kid  i used to cry in front of people all the time   yeah  i cried a lot  maybe 10 or 20 times in front of other people   it s not just me  horikita  kushida  and sudou do  too  all of our classmates believe you  the entranceway  ichinose and kanzaki are waiting  and sakura s unfinished sentence is lost   were you waiting for us   sorry  sakura  can we continue this later   no  it s fine   well  if sudou even got as little as one day s suspension  class c would win  his framing of the offer   the compromise had been a trap  a sweet trap set to lure us to our defeat   i see  i think so  too   our leader gave us her decision  we ll fight to the bitter end   you re still willing to help us  kanzaki argues for the compromise and then stays to search for evidence anyway  the narrator s verdict is  these were really good people","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: leaving the hearing, and Class B’s offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.213–215<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The walk back after the hearing; Sakura has stopped crying and the silence between them is comfortable. The entranceway; Ichinose and Kanzaki are waiting, and Sakura’s unfinished sentence is lost.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m glad. When I was a kid, I used to cry in front of people all the time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah, I cried a lot. Maybe 10 or 20 times in front of other people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It’s not just me. Horikita, Kushida, and Sudou do, too. All of our classmates believe you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Were you waiting for us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, Sakura. Can we continue this later?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, it’s fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, if Sudou even got as little as one day’s suspension, Class C would win.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His framing of the offer: &quot;the compromise had been a trap. A sweet trap set to lure us to our defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. I think so, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Our leader gave us her decision. We’ll fight to the bitter end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re still willing to help us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Kanzaki argues for the compromise and then stays to search for evidence anyway; the narrator’s verdict is &quot;These were really good people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214–215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor, and what he will not concede<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the price of touching Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 2  the price of touching horikita  if it s not something really bothersome  sure  i ll help   wha  ah  ah  horikita answers the tickling in the hearing with a blow to his side that drops him into the corner  and warns him   i ll forgive you for touching me this time  however  next time i ll pay you back double  his private arithmetic after the blow  if  double  meant twice the force   that was unimaginable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the price of touching Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.218<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If it’s not something really bothersome, sure. I’ll help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Wha— Ah, ah!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Horikita answers the tickling in the hearing with a blow to his side that drops him into the corner, and warns him: &quot;I’ll forgive you for touching me this time. However, next time I’ll pay you back double.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His private arithmetic after the blow: if &quot;double&quot; meant twice the force, &quot;That was unimaginable!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: leaving the hearing, and Class B’s offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the morning walk to the retrial<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 0  the morning walk to the retrial summer morning on the tree lined path to school  horikita waits against the handrail specifically for him  and the case is decided the same day   were you waiting for someone  horikita   i guess if you wanted to confess your feelings  it d be best just to get the words out   everything will be decided today  two lines in this exchange carry no speaker tag   would you be happy if we d compromised  and  after horikita takes the responsibility onto herself   so you do worry about things like this  huh  the page says only  i didn t want to think about it  but horikita continued  so neither line is assigned   we have the strategy you proposed yesterday  ichinose will be there  too  we ll manage  he pats her shoulder lightly and walks on  he thinks about capturing the idyllic scene in a photograph but lacks the nerve   however  i didn t have the guts to take her picture   hmm  horikita begins  nothing  after we settle this case  and shuts her mouth  the sentence is never finished","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the morning walk to the retrial<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.220–221<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summer morning on the tree-lined path to school; Horikita waits against the handrail specifically for him, and the case is decided the same day.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Were you waiting for someone, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I guess if you wanted to confess your feelings, it’d be best just to get the words out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Everything will be decided today,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two lines in this exchange carry no speaker tag: &quot;Would you be happy if we’d compromised?&quot; and, after Horikita takes the responsibility onto herself, &quot;So you do worry about things like this, huh?&quot; The page says only &quot;I didn’t want to think about it, but Horikita continued&quot;, so neither line is assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We have the strategy you proposed yesterday. Ichinose will be there, too. We’ll manage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He pats her shoulder lightly and walks on.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He thinks about capturing the idyllic scene in a photograph but lacks the nerve: &quot;However, I didn’t have the guts to take her picture.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita begins &quot;Nothing. After we settle this case,&quot; and shuts her mouth; the sentence is never finished.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the price of touching Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: Sakura’s first greeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 1 7 2  sakura s first greeting in the classroom sakura is already at her desk  sitting up straight  as if ready for something  and gives her first morning greeting to both of them  the reply to horikita s  what s with her     maybe because of what happened yesterday  she took a step forward on the path to adulthood    carries no speaker tag  the page only says her next remark  shattered the lovely image i d created  so the line is not assigned  he judges the change smaller than it looks   there was no truly major difference between the today s sakura and yesterday s   well  as a loner who loves her solitude  you re very persuasive on this topic   perhaps she didn t come from solitude  but rather from hell  on not pushing sakura past what she can carry   we should take care with how we executed our strategy   sakura  are you heading back now   i m not participating   what s wrong   sakura  you don t really need to testify today  there s no need for you to be so worked up  right   what are you thinking about   hey  sakura  do you have any time later  i wanted to talk to you about something  the invitation feels  like they were being squeezed out of me  she answers that she has plans today  and he lets her go","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: Sakura’s first greeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.222–225<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the classroom Sakura is already at her desk, sitting up straight &quot;as if ready for something,&quot; and gives her first morning greeting to both of them.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well, as a loner who loves her solitude, you’re very persuasive on this topic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakura. Are you heading back now?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’m not participating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reply to Horikita’s &quot;What’s with her?&quot; — &quot;Maybe because of what happened yesterday, she took a step forward on the path to adulthood?&quot; — carries no speaker tag; the page only says her next remark &quot;shattered the lovely image I’d created&quot;, so the line is not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He judges the change smaller than it looks: &quot;There was no truly major difference between the today’s Sakura and yesterday’s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Perhaps she didn’t come from solitude, but rather from hell…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On not pushing Sakura past what she can carry: &quot;We should take care with how we executed our strategy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s wrong?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura, you don’t really need to testify today. There’s no need for you to be so worked up, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What are you thinking about?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey, Sakura. Do you have any time later? I wanted to talk to you about something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The invitation feels &quot;like they were being squeezed out of me&quot;; she answers that she has plans today, and he lets her go.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the morning walk to the retrial<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the special-building rendezvous and the camera trap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 2  the special building rendezvous and the camera trap after 3 40  in the special building  the three class c students arrive expecting a date or a confession from kushida   kushida won t be here  i asked her to send an email to compel you all to come   if i hadn t used an underhanded method  you would ve just ignored me  right  i wanted to talk to you   i have no intension of arguing  that would be a waste of time  i fully understand that neither class c nor class d will retract what they claimed yesterday   the school s waiting  right  go ahead and tell us the truth  after giving you a grace period  the student council president himself asked if you had lied  if you think back  don t you realize that the student council saw through everything  the bluff s second half is his  and he knows it is a bluff   of course  the student council had not seen through their lies  he nods along with ichinose s ultimatum   confirm the footage now and the three will be expelled  on the escort to the student council room   horikita had put everything together really well  he supplies the trap and the pressure   the luring email  the student council gambit  the nod to the ultimatum   and hands the open argument to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the special-building rendezvous and the camera trap<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.225–233<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After 3:40, in the special building: the three Class C students arrive expecting a date or a confession from Kushida.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kushida won’t be here. I asked her to send an email to compel you all to come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I hadn’t used an underhanded method, you would’ve just ignored me, right? I wanted to talk to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have no intension of arguing. That would be a waste of time. I fully understand that neither Class C nor Class D will retract what they claimed yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The school’s waiting, right? Go ahead and tell us the truth. After giving you a grace period, the student council president himself asked if you had lied. If you think back, don’t you realize that the student council saw through everything?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The bluff’s second half is his, and he knows it is a bluff: &quot;Of course, the student council had not seen through their lies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He nods along with Ichinose’s ultimatum — confirm the footage now and the three will be expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the escort to the student council room: &quot;Horikita had put everything together really well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> He supplies the trap and the pressure — the luring email, the student-council gambit, the nod to the ultimatum — and hands the open argument to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: Sakura’s first greeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.3–7.4: the fake cameras and the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 3 7 4  the fake cameras and the shuttered door  i was wondering what you were up to when you asked me to lend you some points yesterday   as long as you pay me back by graduation  it s fine  so what are you going to do now  wait in front of the student council room  sakura s  plans today  keep bothering him  he runs off before ichinose can say what she wanted to tell him  and she follows  tracking sakura s phone to the electronics store entrance  he signals ichinose to be quiet as a precaution   ah  looks like we caught them  that old guy s doing something naughty   me and my girlfriend saw everything  so we took pictures  if you show your face to that girl again  or send her any more disgusting letters  we ll expose you  got it   you don t know what i m talking about  you re not weaseling out of this  old man  if you so much as raise a hand at or even just ogle this idol  that ll be the end for you  i ll beat the shit out of you  got it  after the clerk loses his fight  he deliberately gives him time to run  then catches sakura before she can fall   you did really well   i m really glad that i exchanged contact information with you   that s not true  it was really cool when you threw those letters to the ground  ichinose asks who the  mystery person  is and his  that s  stops there  the page records that he did not want to hide anything from her but hesitated to speak without sakura s permission   sakura over here was an idol when she was in junior high  her name was shizuku  he tells ichinose the idol name only after sakura meets his eyes and gives him a slight nod   a little while ago  sorry  several other people in class realized  too   i think there s a possibility that people at school might panic when they notice but i think it ll be fine  the impulse to help unsettles him   was this the real me   it s nothing you have to apologize for  we don t have to talk about it  however  i think that now we have the type of relationship where we can talk about things  if you re suffering or if you feel lost  you can talk to me  you should consult horikita and kushida  too  on ichinose s warning about ryuuen   i didn t know who this ryuuen was  but he was undoubtedly a very dangerous opponent   yeah  i ll keep that in mind","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.3–7.4: the fake cameras and the shuttered door<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.234–241<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was wondering what you were up to when you asked me to lend you some points yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;As long as you pay me back by graduation, it’s fine. So what are you going to do now? Wait in front of the student council room?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ah, looks like we caught them! That old guy’s doing something naughty!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Sakura’s &quot;plans today&quot; keep bothering him; he runs off before Ichinose can say what she wanted to tell him, and she follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Tracking Sakura’s phone to the electronics-store entrance, he signals Ichinose to be quiet as a precaution.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Me and my girlfriend saw everything. So we took pictures. If you show your face to that girl again, or send her any more disgusting letters, we’ll expose you. Got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You don’t know what I’m talking about? You’re not weaseling out of this, old man. If you so much as raise a hand at or even just ogle this idol, that’ll be the end for you. I’ll beat the shit out of you. Got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After the clerk loses his fight, he deliberately gives him time to run, then catches Sakura before she can fall.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You did really well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m really glad that I exchanged contact information with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not true. It was really cool when you threw those letters to the ground.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ichinose asks who the &quot;mystery person&quot; is and his &quot;That’s…&quot; stops there: the page records that he did not want to hide anything from her but hesitated to speak without Sakura’s permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura over here was an idol when she was in junior high. Her name was Shizuku.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He tells Ichinose the idol name only after Sakura meets his eyes and gives him a slight nod.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A little while ago. Sorry. Several other people in class realized, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think there’s a possibility that people at school might panic when they notice…but I think it’ll be fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The impulse to help unsettles him: &quot;Was this the real me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s nothing you have to apologize for. We don’t have to talk about it. However, I think that now we have the type of relationship where we can talk about things. If you’re suffering or if you feel lost, you can talk to me. You should consult Horikita and Kushida, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On Ichinose’s warning about Ryuuen: &quot;I didn’t know who this Ryuuen was, but he was undoubtedly a very dangerous opponent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. I’ll keep that in mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the special-building rendezvous and the camera trap<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p252-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the corridor after the withdrawal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p252-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 6  the corridor after the withdrawal he waits outside the student council room  sudo leaves cheerful  then the president and secretary tachibana come out   looks like it went well   yeah    to sudo s proposal of a party that night  is that so   well  i guess miracles do happen   your little sister handled things well  i didn t do anything  the president holds still and looks him in the eyes  the page withholds what he makes of the answer   nah  i hate troublesome stuff  besides  being in the student council is no joke  i want to lead an ordinary student life at this school   well  i d just never do anything that i m not interested in   yo    greeted by the hardest glare he has seen from horikita  which she covers at once  what were the results   i m glad to hear that  looks like your strategy worked well   my puppet  what are you talking about   you re overthinking it  it s just coincidence   what do you mean  who am i  i m just a guy who dislikes trouble  right   well  i ll be heading back now    he turns on the feeling that it would be better not to be seen together with her he admits the involvement went too far and needs to be dialed back   i had to dial it back a little  i just wanted my life here to be peaceful  the black haired boy who stops in front of them has  black hair  styled so it was worn long  is about his height  and never fully turns to face them  the page does not name him here   i m done talking   you sort of forced me to  you helped sudou in this case  too  right   i m thinking  this is annoying  and  i don t have any motivation to do this  stuff like that  that s what i m thinking  even if you took back what you said just now  horikita  i do intend to live my life quietly  whether we aim for class a or whatever  that s it   i thought that i should help the first friends i ve ever made  probably  he suspects chabashira is behind horikita s new questions   i wouldn t be surprised if she knew about my past  his conclusion  walked to in the corridor   we d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as ryuuen  on the road ahead   in other words  it was fair to say that trying to reach class a in three years was hopeless  he turns the analysis on himself   i knew more about me than anyone else  i knew just how defective  just how foolish i was  i was a horrible human being","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the corridor after the withdrawal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.252–256<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He waits outside the student council room; Sudō leaves cheerful, then the president and Secretary Tachibana come out.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Looks like it went well&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah.&quot; — to Sudō’s proposal of a party that night<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is that so?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I guess miracles do happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Your little sister handled things well. I didn’t do anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The president holds still and looks him in the eyes; the page withholds what he makes of the answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nah, I hate troublesome stuff. Besides, being in the student council is no joke. I want to lead an ordinary student life at this school,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I’d just never do anything that I’m not interested in…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yo.&quot; — greeted by the hardest glare he has seen from Horikita, which she covers at once<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What were the results?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m glad to hear that. Looks like your strategy worked well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;My puppet? What are you talking about?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re overthinking it. It’s just coincidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What do you mean, who am I? I’m just a guy who dislikes trouble, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well. I’ll be heading back now.&quot; — he turns on the feeling that it would be better not to be seen together with her<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He admits the involvement went too far and needs to be dialed back: &quot;I had to dial it back a little. I just wanted my life here to be peaceful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The black-haired boy who stops in front of them has &quot;black hair, styled so it was worn long,&quot; is about his height, and never fully turns to face them; the page does not name him here.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m done talking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You sort of forced me to. You helped Sudou in this case, too. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m thinking ‘This is annoying,’ and ‘I don’t have any motivation to do this.’ Stuff like that. That’s what I’m thinking. Even if you took back what you said just now, Horikita, I do intend to live my life quietly. Whether we aim for Class A or whatever, that’s it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I thought that I should help the first friends I’ve ever made. Probably.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He suspects Chabashira is behind Horikita’s new questions: &quot;I wouldn’t be surprised if she knew about my past.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His conclusion, walked to in the corridor: &quot;We’d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as Ryuuen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the road ahead: &quot;In other words, it was fair to say that trying to reach Class A in three years was hopeless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He turns the analysis on himself: &quot;I knew more about me than anyone else. I knew just how defective, just how foolish I was. I was a horrible human being.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.3–7.4: the fake cameras and the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 0  the cruise  the first name fever  and the boundary deck of the luxury liner on the way to the school s private island  first years of class d around him after midterms and finals  the chapter is his first person account   the endless summer sea  the infinite blue skies  the perfectly clear air  prices the trip honestly  on his own it  would probably have cost me about 100 000 yen  even in the off season  shoved by a class a boy  hey  you re in the way  move it  you defects  and catches the railing  sudou answers back  class d is chased from the bow  reads the hierarchy and swallows it   although the situation was unfair  we didn t need any unnecessary trouble  so it was best to ignore it  notes hirata s arrival as rescue   i was saved by the appearance of my hero  hirata man  on hirata and karuizawa cooling off   they seemed to get along well whenever i saw them talking  feeds sudou s practice by inventing a wrong first name    tomiko  horikita tomiko    then corrects it to suzune  keeps the joke to himself  suspects horikita s hiding  a slight difference something felt out of place  but drops it   it would be silly to investigate further  best just to drop it  the chapter s thesis  stated before he understands it   i had yet to realize that this place was going to be the boundary between heaven and hell","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.0: the cruise, the first-name fever, and the boundary<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–23<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the luxury liner on the way to the school&#x27;s private island; first-years of Class D around him after midterms and finals.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">The chapter is his first-person account: &quot;The endless summer sea. The infinite blue skies. The perfectly clear air.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Prices the trip honestly: on his own it &quot;would probably have cost me about 100,000 yen, even in the off season.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Notes Hirata&#x27;s arrival as rescue: &quot;I was saved by the appearance of my hero, Hirata Man.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shoved by a Class A boy (&quot;Hey, you&#x27;re in the way. Move it, you defects.&quot;) and catches the railing; Sudou answers back, Class D is chased from the bow.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the hierarchy and swallows it: &quot;Although the situation was unfair, we didn&#x27;t need any unnecessary trouble, so it was best to ignore it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On Hirata and Karuizawa cooling off: &quot;They seemed to get along well whenever I saw them talking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Feeds Sudou&#x27;s practice by inventing a wrong first name — &quot;Tomiko. Horikita Tomiko.&quot; — then corrects it to Suzune; keeps the joke to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Suspects Horikita&#x27;s hiding (&quot;a slight difference—something felt out of place&quot;) but drops it: &quot;it would be silly to investigate further. Best just to drop it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s thesis, stated before he understands it: &quot;I had yet to realize that this place was going to be the boundary between heaven and hell.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner","w":"horikita-suzune hoshinomiya-chie ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1 2 2  the test is announced  and class d splits three ways beach landing  mashima sensei announces the deserted island special test from a white platform  works the rules the way the chapter needs them read  the penalties page  will determine whether you live or die  the watches are safety kit    the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe  first to ask the question that sets the economy   is it possible to get by without using any points    chabashira answers that the school  isn t involved in the test process at all  names the test s real shape   essentially  it was a contest of restraint  stands apart from the toilet fight  watching hirata get pulled apart   i stood a short distance away  watching the situation unfold  sidles up to her read of the class  she admits she can t see a solution and he agrees    i think the same  there s too much we don t know  given the season opening advice about confessing to a girl before the ocean  wishes she would leave his love life alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–46<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach landing; Mashima-sensei announces the deserted-island special test from a white platform.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">Names the test&#x27;s real shape: &quot;Essentially, it was a contest of restraint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Works the rules the way the chapter needs them read: the penalties page &quot;will determine whether you live or die&quot;; the watches are safety kit — &quot;the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> First to ask the question that sets the economy: &quot;is it possible to get by without using any points?&quot; — Chabashira answers that the school &quot;isn&#x27;t involved in the test process at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands apart from the toilet fight, watching Hirata get pulled apart: &quot;I stood a short distance away, watching the situation unfold.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sidles up to her read of the class; she admits she can&#x27;t see a solution and he agrees — &quot;I think the same. There&#x27;s too much we don&#x27;t know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Given the season-opening advice about confessing to a girl before the ocean; wishes she would leave his love life alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.0: the cruise, the first-name fever, and the boundary<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2 2 3  he volunteers  and horikita s isolation is priced walking from beach toward the forest with the tent party  horikita trails the group alone  her depression out loud    i can t be alone    and his answer that this test is the one her academics can t win  he watches her realise ike and sudou moved faster than she could  his standing theory of her  filed as interpretation not fact   horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother  she wasn t aiming for class a for her own sake  but rather  sought her older brother s approval  she blocks the probe    it doesn t feel good to have someone pry into your past    and he retreats cleanly  raises his hand for the search party for a stated system reason   without a role to fill in the class  you ll get cut off  paired by leftovers  logic with sakura and kouenji  notes the pairing works    i d be able to move without any difficulty","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.47–52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach toward the forest with the tent party; Horikita trails the group alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">His standing theory of her, filed as interpretation not fact: &quot;Horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother. She wasn&#x27;t aiming for Class A for her own sake, but rather, sought her older brother&#x27;s…<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her depression out loud — &quot;I can&#x27;t be alone&quot; — and his answer that this test is the one her academics can&#x27;t win; he watches her realise Ike and Sudou moved faster than she could.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His standing theory of her, filed as interpretation not fact: &quot;Horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother. She wasn&#x27;t aiming for Class A for her own sake, but rather, sought her older brother&#x27;s approval.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She blocks the probe — &quot;It doesn&#x27;t feel good to have someone pry into your past&quot; — and he retreats cleanly.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Raises his hand for the search party for a stated system reason: &quot;without a role to fill in the class, you&#x27;ll get cut off.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Paired by leftovers&#x27; logic with Sakura and Kouenji; notes the pairing works — &quot;I&#x27;d be able to move without any difficulty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  the forest team  and class a s leader in the open forest path with kouenji ahead and sakura behind  damp heat  unstable footing  talks to her because she is the only one left to talk to  she trips on roots and he pulls her up  brushing dirt from her hands  borrows sakura s handkerchief and ties it to a branch as a trail marker   the chapter s first quiet competence beat  slows his own pace so sakura won t feel like the problem   that way  sakura wouldn t feel like the problem  she probably saw through my ploy  but i didn t mind  hides them both when a class a boy leaves the cave  overhears katsuragi name himself leader and the cave as a spot  works out the fatal leak on the spot    they had clearly made their leader known to us    and takes the report on himself so sakura  who has poor communication skills  doesn t have to carry it  holds her hand through the hiding without meaning to  she goes  almost comatose  and he checks on her twice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.53–62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Forest path with Kouenji ahead and Sakura behind; damp heat, unstable footing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Hides them both when a Class A boy leaves the cave; overhears Katsuragi name himself leader and the cave as a spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Talks to her because she is the only one left to talk to; she trips on roots and he pulls her up, brushing dirt from her hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Borrows Sakura&#x27;s handkerchief and ties it to a branch as a trail marker — the chapter&#x27;s first quiet competence beat.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Slows his own pace so Sakura won&#x27;t feel like the problem: &quot;That way, Sakura wouldn&#x27;t feel like the problem. She probably saw through my ploy, but I didn&#x27;t mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Works out the fatal leak on the spot — &quot;They had clearly made their leader known to us&quot; — and takes the report on himself so Sakura, who has poor communication skills, doesn&#x27;t have to carry it.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Holds her hand through the hiding without meaning to; she goes &quot;almost comatose&quot; and he checks on her twice.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 4 2 5  the river camp  the leader vote  and horikita s favour back at the assembly point  ike s group reports a river with a possession device ten minutes away  answer for both of them to her question about kouenji    i can t control that guy  you know that    then deflects her glare when she asks what he said  in the leader vote  reads the room instead of speaking  kushida s nomination of horikita is  the least risky choice  since she was so desperate to reach class a  personally relieved sudou wasn t chosen   i was relieved that someone like sudou or ike wasn t the leader  she delegates the ike problem to him    i m relying on you because i know i can t do it    and he takes the timing as his own   i ll talk to him  but leave the timing to me  prices her isolation as the test s real subject   an academically brilliant girl was less useful than a normal student in a situation like this  and  this week would test horikita suzune s limits  and show her at her worst","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back at the assembly point; Ike&#x27;s group reports a river with a possession device ten minutes away.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">Prices her isolation as the test&#x27;s real subject: &quot;An academically brilliant girl was less useful than a normal student in a situation like this.&quot; and &quot;This week would test Horikita Suzune&#x27;s limits, and show her at her worst.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Answer for both of them to her question about Kouenji — &quot;I can&#x27;t control that guy. You know that.&quot; — then deflects her glare when she asks what he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> In the leader vote, reads the room instead of speaking: Kushida&#x27;s nomination of Horikita is &quot;the least risky choice, since she was so desperate to reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Personally relieved Sudou wasn&#x27;t chosen: &quot;I was relieved that someone like Sudou or Ike wasn&#x27;t the leader.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She delegates the Ike problem to him — &quot;I&#x27;m relying on you because I know I can&#x27;t do it&quot; — and he takes the timing as his own: &quot;I&#x27;ll talk to him, but leave the timing to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 5 2 6  branches  yamauchi s plan  and the bonfire evening at the river camp  hirata asks him to gather branches for a bonfire  after sudou and yamauchi refuse  sakura volunteers and he lets her  yamauchi then reverses and joins  yamauchi confides the switch from kushida to sakura as a body driven target plan  he refuses the ask    i d like to go back and start the bonfire while it s still early  declines on her behalf rather than leaving her alone with  some guy who only wanted to get into her pants  diagnoses the failed fire when yamauchi cannot   damp wood  branches too thick   and stays quiet so ike can be the one to fix it  explains the quiet help to sakura   building up ike and displaying his usefulness will be more helpful to the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.72–77<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening at the river camp; Hirata asks him to gather branches for a bonfire.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">After Sudou and Yamauchi refuse, Sakura volunteers and he lets her; Yamauchi then reverses and joins.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Yamauchi confides the switch from Kushida to Sakura as a body-driven target plan; he refuses the ask — &quot;I&#x27;d like to go back and start the bonfire while it&#x27;s still early.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Declines on her behalf rather than leaving her alone with &quot;some guy who only wanted to get into her pants.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Diagnoses the failed fire when Yamauchi cannot — damp wood, branches too thick — and stays quiet so Ike can be the one to fix it.<span class=\"pg\">p.84–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Explains the quiet help to Sakura: &quot;building up Ike and displaying his usefulness will be more helpful to the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 6 2 7  ibuki  and the decision not to leave her walking back with branches  a girl from another class sits against a tree with a red  swollen mark on her cheek  stops yamauchi from walking past her  the three of them agree to wait rather than leave an injured girl in the jungle  answers her  i m from class c  in other words  i m your enemy  with  that wasn t any reason not to help  says the camp location leak won t be a problem when she names the risk   the chapter never says why he is sure  introduces himself properly and holds the space while hirata works the crowd   sorry  can you wait a little longer  i m going to talk to him about you  watches hirata take ibuki in and wonders why he was the one left with her   i wondered if hirata had left me with her because he trusted me  or at least trusted me more than yamauchi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.78–86<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking back with branches; a girl from another class sits against a tree with a red, swollen mark on her cheek.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Stops Yamauchi from walking past her; the three of them agree to wait rather than leave an injured girl in the jungle.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Answers her &quot;I&#x27;m from Class C. In other words, I&#x27;m your enemy&quot; with &quot;That wasn&#x27;t any reason not to help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Says the camp-location leak won&#x27;t be a problem when she names the risk — the chapter never says why he is sure.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Introduces himself properly and holds the space while Hirata works the crowd: &quot;Sorry. Can you wait a little longer? I&#x27;m going to talk to him about you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Watches Hirata take Ibuki in and wonders why he was the one left with her: &quot;I wondered if Hirata had left me with her because he trusted me, or at least trusted me more than Yamauchi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke ibuki-mio kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 8  the points speech  the river vote  and kouenji s exit five o clock  kushida s group returns with fruit  the bonfire is up  and the class settles into its first night  credits ike  not himself  for the fire   you should be thanking ike  not me  tries to raise the ibuki report during the excitement and gets no opening   i didn t have any chance to butt in  keeps his word to her while the class votes on river water  raises his hand for the river last  with horikita  after everyone else   the chapter frames it as compliance  not conviction  backs the fishing rod plan as the cheap test it is   the cost was so minimal that it couldn t really hurt us  on kouenji s retirement   maybe he didn t care about reaching class a  if it made his life easier  losing thirty points didn t matter at all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.87–98<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Five o&#x27;clock; Kushida&#x27;s group returns with fruit, the bonfire is up, and the class settles into its first night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">On Kouenji&#x27;s retirement: &quot;Maybe he didn&#x27;t care about reaching Class A. If it made his life easier, losing thirty points didn&#x27;t matter at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Credits Ike, not himself, for the fire: &quot;You should be thanking Ike, not me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Tries to raise the Ibuki report during the excitement and gets no opening: &quot;I didn&#x27;t have any chance to butt in.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Keeps his word to her while the class votes on river water.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Raises his hand for the river last, with Horikita, after everyone else — the chapter frames it as compliance, not conviction.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Backs the fishing-rod plan as the cheap test it is: &quot;the cost was so minimal that it couldn&#x27;t really hurt us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  the camera in the luggage  the morning watch  kanzaki s visit pre dawn heat in the class d tent  ayanokoji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage  the island morning  the mesh tent keeps the night breeze  the luggage is stacked outside to save space  and dawn comes on hot  opens ibuki s singularly colored bag and finds a digital camera with a rental sticker    this item wasn t appropriate for a deserted island  checks the camera s power source    it had no data  and no sign that it d been used    returns it to the bag  and reasons out why she would carry it  the camera explains the dull sound he heard when she dropped the bag against a tree the day before  shares the early watch with hirata while the rest of the class sleeps on   i guess if i had to pick  school life s my priority  besides  i don t think it s possible to reach class a  after everyone is asleep  cuts one of the manual s five blank pages  replicates a simple island map  folds it into a small square and pockets it  reads the heart bedazzled gifts in hirata s pack as karuizawa s  meets kanzaki at the river with hirata and takes in the class b campsite directions  weighs that kanzaki  ichinose and horikita had worked together in the false accusation case   probably why he thinks they are still on good terms  reads the visit as reconnaissance    you could estimate the number of points spent just by the number of toilets  showers  and tents  the second spot update was postponed so ownership expires right after eight o clock  letting the roll call crowds camouflage the renewal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–104<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pre-dawn heat in the Class D tent; Ayanokōji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I guess if I had to pick, school life&#x27;s my priority. Besides, I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s possible to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The island morning: the mesh tent keeps the night breeze, the luggage is stacked outside to save space, and dawn comes on hot.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens Ibuki&#x27;s singularly colored bag and finds a digital camera with a rental sticker — “This item wasn&#x27;t appropriate for a deserted island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Checks the camera&#x27;s power source — “It had no data, and no sign that it&#x27;d been used.” — returns it to the bag, and reasons out why she would carry it.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The camera explains the dull sound he heard when she dropped the bag against a tree the day before.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Shares the early watch with Hirata while the rest of the class sleeps on.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After everyone is asleep, cuts one of the manual&#x27;s five blank pages, replicates a simple island map, folds it into a small square and pockets it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Reads the heart-bedazzled gifts in Hirata&#x27;s pack as Karuizawa&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Meets Kanzaki at the river with Hirata and takes in the Class B campsite directions.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Weighs that Kanzaki, Ichinose and Horikita had worked together in the false accusation case — probably why he thinks they are still on good terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Reads the visit as reconnaissance — “You could estimate the number of points spent just by the number of toilets, showers, and tents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The second spot update was postponed so ownership expires right after eight o&#x27;clock, letting the roll-call crowds camouflage the renewal.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ike-kanji ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  class c comes to provoke morning roll call over  exploration begins  two class c boys stride into the campsite eating chips  the campsite after roll call  the river base holding  class d setting out to explore  recognizes komiya and kondou and recalls their earlier fight with sudo as acting on ryuen s orders rather than just looking for a fight  stands with ike when the chips are tossed at his feet  neither takes the bait until hirata s group returns  files ibuki s worst case remark and decides telling horikita  seemed like a good idea  pulls the leader out of the tent    you ve got eyes on ryuuen  and you ve even been observing ichinose  people will remember that you re the student council president s younger sister  no matter what you do  you ll be a target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–107<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning roll call over, exploration begins; two Class C boys stride into the campsite eating chips.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Recognizes Komiya and Kondou and recalls their earlier fight with Sudō as acting on Ryūen&#x27;s orders rather than just looking for a fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The campsite after roll call, the river base holding, Class D setting out to explore.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Stands with Ike when the chips are tossed at his feet; neither takes the bait until Hirata&#x27;s group returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Files Ibuki&#x27;s worst-case remark and decides telling Horikita “seemed like a good idea.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pulls the leader out of the tent — “You&#x27;ve got eyes on Ryuuen, and you&#x27;ve even been observing Ichinose. People will remember that you&#x27;re the student council president&#x27;s younger sister. No matter what you do, you&#x27;ll be a target.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 2  ryuen s beach  spent to zero the class c beach  temporary toilets and showers  a tarp  a barbecue  chairs  a parasol  jet skis on the shoreline  the class c shore  cooking smoke  laughter  a hundred and fifty points or more already burned   it s up to you  horikita  the line names horikita as the one addressed  the translation never tags the speaker  stands through ryuen pouring out his water and throwing the warm bottle back at ishizaki without intervening  leaves with her after the first name call and the crotch grab provocation  stopping once on the way back to look over the class c camp  works out the zero points strategy  nothing left to penalize  and even guesses of every rival leader s identity could gain only  a maximum of 150 points   that s simple  he d just do what kouenji did  the plan at zero points is retirement    his physical condition was poor and he was mentally unstable  in that case  it s better to just retire  the walk back exchange never tags its speakers until horikita s final line  these lines are recorded here as the responses to her questions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach: temporary toilets and showers, a tarp, a barbecue, chairs, a parasol, jet skis on the shoreline.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It&#x27;s up to you, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That&#x27;s simple. He&#x27;d just do what Kouenji did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class C shore: cooking smoke, laughter, a hundred and fifty points or more already burned.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line names Horikita as the one addressed; the translation never tags the speaker.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands through Ryūen pouring out his water and throwing the warm bottle back at Ishizaki without intervening.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Leaves with her after the first-name call and the crotch-grab provocation, stopping once on the way back to look over the Class C camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Works out the zero-points strategy: nothing left to penalize, and even guesses of every rival leader&#x27;s identity could gain only “a maximum of 150 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The plan at zero points is retirement — “His physical condition was poor and he was mentally unstable. In that case, it&#x27;s better to just retire.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The walk-back exchange never tags its speakers until Horikita&#x27;s final line; these lines are recorded here as the responses to her questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  walking back from the class c shore on the path inland past the beach  he turns to scan the class c shore once more while the walk back is still arguing over what ryuen s spending means   the test is literally about freedom  ryuuen s way of thinking is one way to approach it  it seems like ibuki and another student rebelled  and because of that class c will lose twenty points a day  since he knew he d be losing that many points every day no matter what  he came up with a drastic strategy   since i didn t know when ryuuen had decided to spend all of class c s points  i could only guess   we ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up  ryuuen is most definitely wrong  i cannot possibly understand him   a zero point strategy  huh  i see  that s really interesting  the walk back exchange is never tagged  her line is confirmed by the narration that follows it  and both of his stand as the remarks she answers  reads winning as more than saving the class s own points  dissent inside the group would have to be silenced before a zero points route could work","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the path inland past the beach, he turns to scan the Class C shore once more while the walk back is still arguing over what Ryūen&#x27;s spending means.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The test is literally about freedom. Ryuuen’s way of thinking is one way to approach it. It seems like Ibuki and another student rebelled, and because of that Class C will lose twenty points a day. Since he knew he’d be losing…”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up. Ryuuen is most definitely wrong. I cannot possibly understand him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“A zero-point strategy, huh? I see. That’s really interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The test is literally about freedom. Ryuuen’s way of thinking is one way to approach it. It seems like Ibuki and another student rebelled, and because of that Class C will lose twenty points a day. Since he knew he’d be losing that many points every day no matter what, he came up with a drastic strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Since I didn’t know when Ryuuen had decided to spend all of Class C’s points, I could only guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The walk-back exchange is never tagged; her line is confirmed by the narration that follows it, and both of his stand as the remarks she answers.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Reads winning as more than saving the class&#x27;s own points: dissent inside the group would have to be silenced before a zero-points route could work.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune kaneda-satoru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 3  class b s camp at the well deep forest past the broken landmark tree  class b s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees  ichinose tying a cord  kanzaki sitting a little way off  class b s site   trees around a well  hammocks instead of tents  and a path of student tracks already beaten through the forest  reads the broken tree as a landmark the school left on purpose  which is why kanzaki s directions needed no detail   well  i suppose it s just what we d expect from class b   your class seems to be functioning well  despite obstacles   i m sorry if we re getting in the way  the three lines are untagged  ichinose takes up and answers each of them  she reads the visit as a request and welcomes them without any hint of protest   what s a water shower  i m a little curious about that  judges the water shower probably less effective than the temporary shower because it costs five points less  and passes on it   did you already know about them  water showers  i mean  class b s purchases itemize to exactly seventy points once the food is counted  sets that total against class d with koenji s retirement already deducted  weighs the foraging against the fruit kushida s group carried back for class d  watches the class b method in one pass  the well tested before anyone drinks  hot water on a gas can  unlimited vinyl sheets granted with the temporary toilet  and water sprinkled to pull the heat out of the soil  he stays silent while she lays out class d s side and runs the exchange  the visitors  questions about hard ground and the heat are never tagged and are left as a chapter attribution gap  names him as a class c student before ichinose can finish answering   a class c student  files him as the class c boy who resisted ryuen and was taken in by class b   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long  says farewell with horikita and leaves the camp  sets class d against class b on the way out  class d has selfish students like koenji who run off alone  and nobody with the power to step in  the two untagged verdict lines that follow the departure are left as a chapter attribution gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117–125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deep forest past the broken landmark tree: Class B&#x27;s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees, Ichinose tying a cord, Kanzaki sitting a little way off.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I suppose it’s just what we’d expect from Class B…”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Your class seems to be functioning well, despite obstacles.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry if we’re getting in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> Class B&#x27;s site — trees around a well, hammocks instead of tents, and a path of student tracks already beaten through the forest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the broken tree as a landmark the school left on purpose, which is why Kanzaki&#x27;s directions needed no detail.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The three lines are untagged; Ichinose takes up and answers each of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She reads the visit as a request and welcomes them without any hint of protest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s a water shower? I’m a little curious about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Judges the water shower probably less effective than the temporary shower because it costs five points less, and passes on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you already know about them? Water showers, I mean,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Class B&#x27;s purchases itemize to exactly seventy points once the food is counted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets that total against Class D with Kōenji&#x27;s retirement already deducted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Weighs the foraging against the fruit Kushida&#x27;s group carried back for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Watches the Class B method in one pass: the well tested before anyone drinks, hot water on a gas can, unlimited vinyl sheets granted with the temporary toilet, and water sprinkled to pull the heat out of the soil.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He stays silent while she lays out Class D&#x27;s side and runs the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The visitors&#x27; questions about hard ground and the heat are never tagged and are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Names him as a Class C student before Ichinose can finish answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A Class C student?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Files him as the Class C boy who resisted Ryūen and was taken in by Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Says farewell with Horikita and leaves the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets Class D against Class B on the way out: Class D has selfish students like Kōenji who run off alone, and nobody with the power to step in.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow the departure are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.4: the Class A cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 4  the class a cave the cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon s mouth  with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside  he steps over horikita and walks up to it  the class a site  a cave in the mountainside  its entrance hidden behind vinyl sheets joined into one giant tarp   let s go  i mean  it s class a  so of course we re going to be scared  there s nothing we can do about that   and what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot  we can barely see  and there s no one around  there s not much we can see unless we enter the cave   i haven t thought of anything  come on  don t worry  goes up openly rather than scouting from cover so that he can see inside   and finds the tarp already blocking the view  the opening line on the approach is untagged  horikita s two questions are recorded under her  recognizes yahiko as one of the two who found the cave on the first day  katsuragi is away  the closing judgment   that class a has to be left alone and cannot be investigated   is his  left untagged and recorded here without a quotation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.4: the Class A cave<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon&#x27;s mouth, with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside; he steps over Horikita and walks up to it.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Let’s go. I mean, it’s Class A, so of course we’re going to be scared. There’s nothing we can do about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“And what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot? We can barely see, and there’s no one around. There’s not much we can see unless we enter the cave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I haven’t thought of anything. Come on, don’t worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class A site: a cave in the mountainside, its entrance hidden behind vinyl sheets joined into one giant tarp.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Goes up openly rather than scouting from cover so that he can see inside — and finds the tarp already blocking the view.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening line on the approach is untagged; Horikita&#x27;s two questions are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Recognizes Yahiko as one of the two who found the cave on the first day; Katsuragi is away.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The closing judgment — that Class A has to be left alone and cannot be investigated — is his, left untagged and recorded here without a quotation.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 1  the walk with sakura third day  before noon  he slips out of base camp alone for the forest entrance to see what kouenji had been looking at  and sakura catches up  out of breath  the forest path out of base camp  marked by a handkerchief tied around a tree   didn t i tie a handkerchief around a tree  anyway  i thought i d just go and check something out  the line just above the quoted one prints  didn t had the time  kept as printed   isn t it better for you to stay back  won t it bother you if people start spreading rumors   it s not going to be particularly easy  right  i mean  after we went through all the trouble of coming to this island  i think you should have a little fun  though i m not one to talk about fun  myself  turns her request down with that excuse   she answers that this is fun  crouches and hides her face  and he takes her along after all  accepts her company on one condition  if they get into trouble later  she must not blame herself   well then  how about we go together  but i have a condition  if we get into trouble later  you won t blame yourself  okay   are you getting along well with the other girls  i mean  you can t really do things alone in this test  right   that s not true  you re making progress  sakura chan   it is true  maybe you can t see it  but you re definitely making progress little by little   it s okay  you ll make some friends really soon  sakura  then school will become much more fun  appeals from the bottom of his heart for the first time  choosing words and attitude together  the narration judges it the right method for someone who lacks confidence  her lines carry the narration tags or address him by name  his replies through the walk are untagged and recorded here   that reminds me  that guy  from the incident before it seems like he resigned   i didn t really do anything  you were saved because you got close to kushida  and because horikita and ichinose helped out  i was just a bystander  anyway  more importantly  nothing else weird has happened  right  credits kushida s proximity and horikita and ichinose s help with the stalker affair  his own part was bystander only   besides  even though you usually act nervous  you always had this really confident expression when you were an idol   a long time ago  but when you were featured in magazines you probably didn t take the pictures yourself  right  draws her out on the idol years until she describes erasing herself to endure the shoots  the narration reads her as scarred by the stalker but headed in a better direction   considering even kouenji s satisfaction  the school has probably been really good about keeping up the place  normally  an overseas jungle would be more dangerous  rests with her against one tree half an hour up the steep trail   the longest time alone with her since the landing   and reads the distance between them shortening toward friendship  the first relationship he has felt tilt that way   but if i m in the picture  wouldn t that spoil the scenery  watching her frame the shot with thumb and forefingers   preserving memories  huh  so that was why ibuki had a digital camera  his inference rather than a fact about ibuki  her reason for carrying a camera at school is applied to the class c girl","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.131–135<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Third day, before noon: he slips out of base camp alone for the forest entrance to see what Kouenji had been looking at, and Sakura catches up, out of breath.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Didn’t I tie a handkerchief around a tree? Anyway, I thought I’d just go and check something out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Isn’t it better for you to stay back? Won’t it bother you if people start spreading rumors?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s not going to be particularly easy, right? I mean, after we went through all the trouble of coming to this island, I think you should have a little fun… Though I’m not one to talk about fun, myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The forest path out of base camp, marked by a handkerchief tied around a tree.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line just above the quoted one prints “didn’t had the time”; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Turns her request down with that excuse — she answers that this is fun, crouches and hides her face, and he takes her along after all.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts her company on one condition: if they get into trouble later, she must not blame herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, how about we go together? But I have a condition. If we get into trouble later, you won’t blame yourself. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you getting along well with the other girls? I mean, you can’t really do things alone in this test, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not true. You’re making progress, Sakura-chan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It is true. Maybe you can’t see it, but you’re definitely making progress little by little.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s okay. You’ll make some friends really soon, Sakura. Then school will become much more fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Appeals from the bottom of his heart for the first time, choosing words and attitude together; the narration judges it the right method for someone who lacks confidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her lines carry the narration tags or address him by name; his replies through the walk are untagged and recorded here.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That reminds me… That guy, from the incident before…it seems like he resigned.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t really do anything. You were saved because you got close to Kushida, and because Horikita and Ichinose helped out. I was just a bystander. Anyway, more importantly, nothing else weird has happened, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Credits Kushida’s proximity and Horikita and Ichinose’s help with the stalker affair; his own part was bystander only.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, even though you usually act nervous, you always had this really confident expression when you were an idol.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A long time ago? But when you were featured in magazines you probably didn’t take the pictures yourself, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Draws her out on the idol years until she describes erasing herself to endure the shoots; the narration reads her as scarred by the stalker but headed in a better direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Considering even Kouenji’s satisfaction, the school has probably been really good about keeping up the place. Normally, an overseas jungle would be more dangerous.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Rests with her against one tree half an hour up the steep trail — the longest time alone with her since the landing — and reads the distance between them shortening toward friendship, the first relationship he has felt tilt that way.<span class=\"pg\">p.134–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if I’m in the picture, wouldn’t that spoil the scenery?”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Watching her frame the shot with thumb and forefingers: “Preserving memories, huh? So that was why Ibuki had a digital camera.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His inference rather than a fact about Ibuki: her reason for carrying a camera at school is applied to the Class C girl.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.4: the Class A cave<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 2  the caterpillar and the corn a hairy caterpillar drops into sakura s hair during the break  pointing it out might make her scream it into her clothes  so he has to remove it without telling her   sakura  there s something i want to ask you   you are you okay with bugs   yeah  bugs  like grasshoppers and dragonflies  those kinds of things   i see  well  all right then   hmm  anyway  don t move for the time being  okay  feigns a casual interest in bugs to learn what she can stand  then holds off acting until he has another way  reaches through his own revulsion   a city boy who hates insects   touches the caterpillar off her hair and throws it into the bushes  she never learns what happened   for the time being  let s investigate the area  but don t go too far  then let s check on each other regularly  if we don t concentrate  it s likely we ll get distracted   did you notice something  about twenty minutes from base camp by the handkerchief marker  the rise where kouenji had stood  finds nothing by sight  then works the soil  the roots  the leaves and the air with all five senses   so  this is what kouenji saw  reads the soil color under the corn and the weed cover around it as artificial cultivation   proof that school officials come and go on the island  the narration answers kouenji s silent gaze from the second day  he saw the corn at first glance and said nothing out of pride   sorry  sorry  i thought it would be okay  wait  what did you mean by  it s too soon   if we tie up the openings of my shirt  we can use it as a bag  that way  we could carry more at once  turns his shirt into a carry bag rather than leave the ears behind for another class to harvest while they are away  the bags line that opens the harvest is untagged   either speaker fits   and is left as an attribution gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.137–140<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A hairy caterpillar drops into Sakura’s hair during the break; pointing it out might make her scream it into her clothes, so he has to remove it without telling her.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sakura, there’s something I want to ask you…”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You…are you okay with bugs?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. Bugs. Like grasshoppers and dragonflies, those kinds of things”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, all right then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. Anyway, don’t move for the time being, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Feigns a casual interest in bugs to learn what she can stand, then holds off acting until he has another way.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reaches through his own revulsion — a city boy who hates insects — touches the caterpillar off her hair and throws it into the bushes; she never learns what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the time being, let’s investigate the area, but don’t go too far. Then let’s check on each other regularly. If we don’t concentrate, it’s likely we’ll get distracted.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you notice something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> About twenty minutes from base camp by the handkerchief marker: the rise where Kouenji had stood.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finds nothing by sight, then works the soil, the roots, the leaves and the air with all five senses.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, this is what Kouenji saw…”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the soil color under the corn and the weed cover around it as artificial cultivation — proof that school officials come and go on the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration answers Kouenji’s silent gaze from the second day: he saw the corn at first glance and said nothing out of pride.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, sorry. I thought it would be okay. Wait, what did you mean by ‘it’s too soon’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we tie up the openings of my shirt, we can use it as a bag. That way… we could carry more at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Turns his shirt into a carry bag rather than leave the ears behind for another class to harvest while they are away.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bags line that opens the harvest is untagged — either speaker fits — and is left as an attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei sakura-airi ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 3  katsuragi at the cornfield katsuragi and yahiko arrive at the thicket while sakura is staring at the corn   i m ayanokouji  from class d  this is sakura   there s nothing we can do  there s only the two of us here  recognized as the spy from yesterday   the second time the pair has met him   we appreciate the offer  but our class told us to be careful  they ll get mad if they find out we relied on class a for help  i m sorry  but we have to decline  refuses the partnership with a fabricated class order   the narration marks the reason a lie   in that case  i d have no choice but to give up what i m carrying right now  answers the watch offer by abandoning the spot rather than accepting help  katsuragi withdraws without force  leaves with her while she still looks worried  katsuragi s intentions unread  back at base camp  ike s greeting brings yamauchi running over  meets the shirtless with sakura accusation with a deflection  then leaves it unanswered   calm down  this is a misunderstanding  that s all  we didn t do  anything   i have to go talk with hirata  sorry  leaves yamauchi s rant to give hirata the report  soon afterward a team is organized and the class works the cornfield  the bag comes back full by one o clock  and the spot stays under katsuragi s eye   good or bad intentions left unknown  the camp s closing exchanges   the full bag  katsuragi being nearby   are untagged and left as attribution gaps","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.140–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi and Yahiko arrive at the thicket while Sakura is staring at the corn.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m Ayanokouji, from Class D. This is Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s nothing we can do. There’s only the two of us here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We appreciate the offer, but our class told us to be careful. They’ll get mad if they find out we relied on Class A for help. I’m sorry, but we have to decline.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Recognized as the spy from yesterday — the second time the pair has met him.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Refuses the partnership with a fabricated class order — the narration marks the reason a lie.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, I’d have no choice but to give up what I’m carrying right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Answers the watch-offer by abandoning the spot rather than accepting help; Katsuragi withdraws without force.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Leaves with her while she still looks worried, Katsuragi’s intentions unread.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Back at base camp, Ike’s greeting brings Yamauchi running over.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Meets the shirtless-with-Sakura accusation with a deflection, then leaves it unanswered.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down. This is a misunderstanding, that’s all. We didn’t do… anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have to go talk with Hirata. Sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Leaves Yamauchi’s rant to give Hirata the report; soon afterward a team is organized and the class works the cornfield.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The bag comes back full by one o’clock, and the spot stays under Katsuragi’s eye — good or bad intentions left unknown.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The camp’s closing exchanges — the full bag, Katsuragi being nearby — are untagged and left as attribution gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.5: the solo sweep toward Class A<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  the solo sweep toward class a fourth day  laughter has replaced complaint   corn  fish and fruit have the class ahead   when he borrows a ballpoint pen  takes his folded map and walks out of base camp  about 100 points spent in total  koenji s retirement included  at this pace the class ends the test with points left over  and even yukimura has no complaints  breaks the test down 80 20   eighty percent defensive cooperation  twenty percent offensive scouting   with the smaller share deciding outcomes the more  reads the balance as meaning class d now has to attack the other classes  and sets out for class a s area around the cave  the cliff below the cave  a ladder in a blind spot drops to a hut spot with fishing tackle  recalls the facilities seen from the ship  finds the ladder anyone would miss at first glance  and marks the hut s approximate position on his map  the hut spot means fish without borrowing equipment  the device shows class a occupying with four hours remaining  and the dusty tools show the gear itself has not been used  reads the unoccupied tower as deliberate   holding a visible facility risks observation  and katsuragi is too cautious for bait this sweet and this close   so  you won t occupy this spot out of more than a sense of prudence  the line is untagged  it voices his reading of the empty tower a moment before the ambush and is recorded as his  two class a boys spring the trap   one checks the terminal for a fresh claim  one puts a branch to his throat   and the search takes his pen and folded map   i m ayanokouji  from class d   give it back   i can t say   i can t say  if i did i may not be able to return to my class  holds the line through a rapid fire interrogation   three seconds  four seconds of silence   without naming anyone  the offer on the table    there s one more thing i talk to you about  if you tell us the identity of your leader  we re prepared to offer a generous reward  100 000 or 200 000 points    first come  first serve  signed by memorandum and paid after the test   you re asking for me to sell out my class for money   sorry  but i don t believe it  how would you pay someone  we don t   have any cell phones here  right   a memorandum  huh  let me ask you something for my own reference  can you tell me how many points i d get if i did tell you something   could i have someone trustworthy settle things  for example  someone like katsuragi  or perhaps sa  drops katsuragi s name as bait of his own   cut off at  sa  the sentence buys the reaction he was after   i ve heard rumors that katsuragi is class a s representative  their correction    don t make me laugh  sakayanagi is the representative of class a  not katsuragi  you can go now    marks the pair as katsuragi s enemies and puts who really leads class a in question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: the solo sweep toward Class A<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.144–148<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fourth day: laughter has replaced complaint — corn, fish and fruit have the class ahead — when he borrows a ballpoint pen, takes his folded map and walks out of base camp.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, you won’t occupy this spot out of more than a sense of prudence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m Ayanokouji, from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Give it back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> About 100 points spent in total, Kōenji&#x27;s retirement included; at this pace the class ends the test with points left over, and even Yukimura has no complaints.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Breaks the test down 80:20 — eighty percent defensive cooperation, twenty percent offensive scouting — with the smaller share deciding outcomes the more.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the balance as meaning Class D now has to attack the other classes, and sets out for Class A&#x27;s area around the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The cliff below the cave: a ladder in a blind spot drops to a hut spot with fishing tackle.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Recalls the facilities seen from the ship, finds the ladder anyone would miss at first glance, and marks the hut&#x27;s approximate position on his map.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The hut spot means fish without borrowing equipment; the device shows Class A occupying with four hours remaining, and the dusty tools show the gear itself has not been used.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the unoccupied tower as deliberate — holding a visible facility risks observation, and Katsuragi is too cautious for bait this sweet and this close.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is untagged; it voices his reading of the empty tower a moment before the ambush and is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Two Class A boys spring the trap — one checks the terminal for a fresh claim, one puts a branch to his throat — and the search takes his pen and folded map.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say. If I did…I may not be able to return to my class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Holds the line through a rapid-fire interrogation — three seconds, four seconds of silence — without naming anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The offer on the table — “There’s one more thing I talk to you about. If you tell us the identity of your leader, we’re prepared to offer a generous reward. 100,000 or 200,000 points.” — first-come, first-serve, signed by memorandum and paid after the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re asking for me to sell out my class for money?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I don’t believe it. How would you pay someone? We don’t … have any cell phones here, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A memorandum, huh? Let me ask you something for my own reference… Can you tell me how many points I’d get if I did tell you something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could I have someone trustworthy settle things? For example, someone like Katsuragi. Or perhaps Sa—”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Drops Katsuragi&#x27;s name as bait of his own — cut off at “Sa—”, the sentence buys the reaction he was after.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve heard rumors that Katsuragi is Class A’s representative.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Their correction — “Don’t make me laugh. Sakayanagi is the representative of Class A. Not Katsuragi. You can go now.” — marks the pair as Katsuragi&#x27;s enemies and puts who really leads Class A in question.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the ghost camp and the Class A question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 1  the ghost camp and the class a question at the emptied class c beach   yesterday s carnival now a ghost town   when ichinose and kanzaki arrive behind him   i m in charge of finding food  i was searching around the forest  and ended up here  his replies through the visit are untagged pov lines  the pair s strategy exchange runs untagged too  and only their addressee  or narration anchored lines are recorded on their pages   the rest are listed with the chapter s gaps  hides with the pair in the shade  takes her midday warning  and thanks her for the parting caution   i just happened to hear a little bit about this  but do katsuragi and sakayanagi in class a have opposing groups   oh  nothing  horikita just gave me an order  she said if i had time  to go and find out something  she wondered if this would be our chance to get back at class a  well  even though it s said they quarrel intensely  i imagine they ll come together during the test  puts the class a question to him and ichinose  what comes back is the pair s shared account  untagged between them  puts the questions in horikita s mouth so that his own interest in class a s split is not what the pair remember   i see  well  i ll tell horikita later  ah jeez  she told me to investigate on my own  she gets flustered working with others  well please pretend that you didn t hear that last part  it s going to be bothersome if she gets angry with me   it s about time for me to look for food  they ll be angry if i return empty handed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the ghost camp and the Class A question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.149–151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the emptied Class C beach — yesterday&#x27;s carnival now a ghost town — when Ichinose and Kanzaki arrive behind him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m in charge of finding food. I was searching around the forest, and ended up here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I just happened to hear a little bit about this, but do Katsuragi and Sakayanagi in Class A have opposing groups?”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, nothing. Horikita just gave me an order. She said if I had time, to go and find out something. She wondered if this would be our chance to get back at Class A. Well, even though it’s said they quarrel intensely, I imagine…”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His replies through the visit are untagged POV lines; the pair&#x27;s strategy exchange runs untagged too, and only their addressee- or narration-anchored lines are recorded on their pages — the rest are listed with the chapter&#x27;s gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Hides with the pair in the shade, takes her midday warning, and thanks her for the parting caution.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, nothing. Horikita just gave me an order. She said if I had time, to go and find out something. She wondered if this would be our chance to get back at Class A. Well, even though it’s said they quarrel intensely, I imagine they’ll come together during the test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Puts the Class A question to him and Ichinose; what comes back is the pair’s shared account, untagged between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Puts the questions in Horikita&#x27;s mouth so that his own interest in Class A&#x27;s split is not what the pair remember.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, I’ll tell Horikita later. Ah jeez, she told me to investigate on my own. She gets flustered working with others. Well…please pretend that you didn’t hear that last part. It’s going to be bothersome if she gets angry with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s about time for me to look for food. They’ll be angry if I return empty-handed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.5: the solo sweep toward Class A<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 2  the faculty room deal flashback to the first semester s closing ceremonies  chabashira calls him to the faculty room the moment homeroom ends  before summer vacation can start   i don t remember doing anything   why did you sound all sarcastic  the opening banter turns on sudou after he is named as the first speaker  the lines are recorded by turn   where do you think  i got called over by the teacher  so i don t really have a choice   don t say such nonsense  gets his wrists grabbed in both meaty hands for a wingman request there is no time to accept  reaches the faculty room to find chabashira waiting in the doorway   i don t understand why you called me over   so what did you want to talk to me about  i m busy planning my summer vacation right now   no  no  i was exaggerating when i said that  i have at least a few friends   before that  should we have tea  you must be thirsty  checks the kitchenette is empty first   the talk is to happen where there are no eyes   another abstract question  i see  is it okay if i say i think you re beautiful   umm  well  if you don t mind being compared to other teachers  i   think you don t care at all about class d s future  and that you re a cold   teacher with no interest in her students  that s my answer  gives her the unsoftened verdict against hoshinomiya and sakagami  and reads her bloodlust under the joke without taking it back   i must say that s surprising  i would ve thought you were more capable  chabashira sensei   i m guessing someone made a trivial mistake  right   i m not catching your drift  what does this have to do with me   what am i supposed to say to that  you re joking  right   he said to expel me  well  that s nonsense  i don t know who it was  but you ignored his request and won t have me expelled  right   i m sorry  but i don t intend to do anything   are you threatening me   can i go now  i won t listen to any more of this  reaches over the desk and grabs her collar to quote her own lesson back at her   the discomfort she made horikita feel  shoes in someone s home   you ll probably regret trying to use me  his answer is never spoken on the page  the warning reads as acceptance  but the scene closes on her line instead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.152–157<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Flashback to the first semester&#x27;s closing ceremonies: Chabashira calls him to the faculty room the moment homeroom ends, before summer vacation can start.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t remember doing anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why did you sound all sarcastic?”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Where do you think? I got called over by the teacher, so I don’t really have a choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>23 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening banter turns on Sudou after he is named as the first speaker; the lines are recorded by turn.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t say such nonsense—”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Gets his wrists grabbed in both meaty hands for a wingman request there is no time to accept.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reaches the faculty room to find Chabashira waiting in the doorway.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t understand why you called me over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what did you want to talk to me about? I’m busy planning my summer vacation right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, no, I was exaggerating when I said that. I have at least a few friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Before that, should we have tea? You must be thirsty,”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Checks the kitchenette is empty first — the talk is to happen where there are no eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Another abstract question, I see. Is it okay if I say I think you’re beautiful?”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Umm… Well, if you don’t mind being compared to other teachers, I … think you don’t care at all about Class D’s future, and that you’re a cold … teacher with no interest in her students. That’s my answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Gives her the unsoftened verdict against Hoshinomiya and Sakagami, and reads her bloodlust under the joke without taking it back.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I must say that’s surprising. I would’ve thought you were more capable, Chabashira-sensei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m guessing someone made a trivial mistake, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not catching your drift. What does this have to do with me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What am I supposed to say to that? You’re joking, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He said to expel me? Well, that’s nonsense. I don’t know who it was, but you ignored his request and won’t have me expelled. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, but I don’t intend to do anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you threatening me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I go now? I won’t listen to any more of this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Reaches over the desk and grabs her collar to quote her own lesson back at her — the discomfort she made Horikita feel, shoes in someone&#x27;s home.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ll probably regret trying to use me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His answer is never spoken on the page; the warning reads as acceptance, but the scene closes on her line instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the ghost camp and the Class A question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the underwear in Ike&#x27;s bag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p159-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"shinohara-satsuki hirata-yousuke ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  the underwear in ike s bag wakes before dawn to shinohara rousing the boys  karuizawa s underwear is missing from the luggage left outside the girls  tent   hey  boys  can you all gather around   well  this morning karuizawa san s underwear went missing  do you know what this means  goes with the boys when hirata rouses them  the girls glare from their cliques   well  there s no evidence that the boys stole it  maybe karuizawa lost it   i know that you re not the culprit  hirata kun  but for the time being  let s check the boys  luggage   let s just ignore what the girls said  i hate being treated like a suspect  i ll fight it  follows ike and yamauchi into the tent once hirata opens his own bag first   damn  i m so pissed  men are always being suspected of stuff  it s way too unreasonable   well  if i think calmly  no solid evidence suggests you re the culprit  ike  the thief would not keep stolen goods in their own bag  so someone planted the underwear to frame ike  takes ike s panic at face value and agrees to carry the planted evidence for him   ayanokouji  you believe me  right  that i didn t steal them   we have no other choice  you have to put it in your pocket  takes the balled up underwear from ike and stuffs it into his own back pocket   sorry  sorry  my bag got a little dirty  so i cleaned it off  sets his bag down for hirata s inspection and steps away  stands perfectly still while hirata pats him down and feels the cloth in his back pocket  the one boy who never doubts him   and the one who touches the evidence and says nothing   hirata  why didn t you tell them   that was the underwear in your pocket  right   sure  but is that really all right   if it s all right with you  may i hold onto the underwear  hands the evidence to hirata  who bags it in a vinyl toilet bag   but we did find out one piece of bad news here  if the underwear came out of ike kun s bag  then there s a high chance that the culprit is someone in our class  the theft happened between eight last night and seven this morning   likely around sunrise with no flashlight   and anyone in the class could have done it   you want me to find the culprit   well  i ll do what i can  just don t expect too much of me   i believe you re not the culprit  ayanokouji kun  that s why i saved you   if you do happen to find the culprit  i want you to tell me first  i definitely do not want you to tell anyone else   so  in other words  you re going to hide the truth   hide it  that s a poor choice of words  but there s nothing i can do about it if people take it that way  even if one of the guys turns out to the be the culprit  i think it s better that the truth be concealed   i understand  i ll report to you first  is that good   hirata yousuke  are you class d s hero  the printed line in hirata s speech reads  turns out to the be the culprit    kept as printed  hirata s contradiction   believe ayanokoji  then conceal the truth   reads as distrust  the suspect was handed the detective s role as a lifeline and a warning  hirata himself may be the culprit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the underwear in Ike&#x27;s bag<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.159–170<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wakes before dawn to Shinohara rousing the boys: Karuizawa&#x27;s underwear is missing from the luggage left outside the girls&#x27; tent.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Hey, boys. Can you all gather around?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Well, this morning…Karuizawa-san’s underwear went missing. Do you know what this means?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Well, there’s no evidence that the boys stole it. Maybe Karuizawa lost it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Goes with the boys when Hirata rouses them; the girls glare from their cliques.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know that you’re not the culprit, Hirata-kun. But for the time being, let’s check the boys’ luggage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s just ignore what the girls said. I hate being treated like a suspect. I’ll fight it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Follows Ike and Yamauchi into the tent once Hirata opens his own bag first.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn, I’m so pissed. Men are always being suspected of stuff. It’s way too unreasonable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if I think calmly, no solid evidence suggests you’re the culprit, Ike.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The thief would not keep stolen goods in their own bag, so someone planted the underwear to frame Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Takes Ike&#x27;s panic at face value and agrees to carry the planted evidence for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji, you believe me, right? That I didn’t steal them?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have no other choice. You have to put it in your pocket.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the balled-up underwear from Ike and stuffs it into his own back pocket.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, sorry. My bag got a little dirty, so I cleaned it off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sets his bag down for Hirata&#x27;s inspection and steps away.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands perfectly still while Hirata pats him down and feels the cloth in his back pocket.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The one boy who never doubts him — and the one who touches the evidence and says nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata. Why didn’t you tell them?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was the underwear in your pocket, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure, but…is that really all right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it’s all right with you, may I hold onto the underwear?”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands the evidence to Hirata, who bags it in a vinyl toilet bag.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But we did find out one piece of bad news here. If the underwear came out of Ike-kun’s bag, then there’s a high chance that the culprit is someone in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The theft happened between eight last night and seven this morning — likely around sunrise with no flashlight — and anyone in the class could have done it.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want me to find the culprit?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’ll do what I can. Just don’t expect too much of me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you’re not the culprit, Ayanokouji-kun. That’s why I saved you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you do happen to find the culprit, I want you to tell me first. I definitely do not want you to tell anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, in other words, you’re going to hide the truth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hide it? That’s a poor choice of words, but there’s nothing I can do about it if people take it that way. Even if one of the guys turns out to the be the culprit, I think it’s better that the truth be concealed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand. I’ll report to you first. Is that good?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Hirata Yousuke. Are you Class D’s hero?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The printed line in Hirata&#x27;s speech reads “turns out to the be the culprit” — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Hirata&#x27;s contradiction — believe Ayanokōji, then conceal the truth — reads as distrust: the suspect was handed the detective&#x27;s role as a lifeline and a warning; Hirata himself may be the culprit.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the faculty-room deal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p171-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p171-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the meeting that splits the camp returns from the tent into hirata s meeting  after horikita s objection the camp splits into a boys  side and a girls  side  stands mute while the boys volunteer and karuizawa rejects them one by one  she nominates him as the one other boy the girls can trust  over karuizawa s objections   ha ha ha  don t make me laugh  he s your only friend  isn t he  there s absolutely no way i can trust such a gloomy  lecherous wallflower  written off by most of the class as a gloomy loner  he lets the suspicion stand without excuses  she speaks up for him when no one else will   the only defense he gets  keeps silent through karuizawa s public excoriation of sakura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.171–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns from the tent into Hirata&#x27;s meeting; after Horikita&#x27;s objection the camp splits into a boys&#x27; side and a girls&#x27; side.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Ha ha ha! Don’t make me laugh. He’s your only friend, isn’t he? There’s absolutely no way I can trust such a gloomy, lecherous wallflower,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands mute while the boys volunteer and Karuizawa rejects them one by one.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She nominates him as the one other boy the girls can trust, over Karuizawa&#x27;s objections.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Written off by most of the class as a gloomy loner; he lets the suspicion stand without excuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> She speaks up for him when no one else will — the only defense he gets.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps silent through Karuizawa&#x27;s public excoriation of Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the underwear in Ike&#x27;s bag<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p180-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2–sec. 6.3: the stakes, Ibuki&#x27;s test, the fever<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p180-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 2 sec  6 3  the stakes  ibuki s test  the fever pitches the girls  second tent with hirata after the split  the other boys off playing or fishing   ah  it s okay  you don t have to apologize  hirata  if anything  i d feel bad to leave it all to you   this question might come off as weird  but why do you work so hard   i can do this  go  finishes the remaining stakes alone when the girls pull hirata away  works the stakes at his side and gets the straight answer about why he works so hard   well  i guess  our various troubles are never ending   i think i trust you  at the very least  i doubt you re the culprit  reads ibuki in the eyes and concludes she stole the underwear and planted it in ike s bag  tells her he trusts her in the same breath that his narration names her the culprit   that s rich  coming from you  this wouldn t have happened if you hadn t had recommended me unnecessarily  the printed line reads  hadn t had recommended    kept as printed   you re the only one in class who doesn t trust hirata  life s better when you stop believing that all people are two faced   yeah  well  i can count on him  at the very least  he s really reliable   well  hirata is a man of many talents  he helps when we can t bring guys and girls together during a dispute  don t you think that he s working hard to bring students together when no one else can   well  it seems like there were some unexpected expenditures  i can t give an exact number   i thought the girls were putting up with the heat unusually well  so this is how you re getting through it   i understand what you mean  but there s nothing i can really say about it  we can t get spent points back  and there aren t many days left before the test ends  karuizawa and the others probably won t spend any more points   so  you want me to work with you   understood  i don t know if i ll be useful  but i ll help   it s better for you to just accept favors in a straightforward way  as a guy  i m rather upset that the guys are being treated like thieves  that alone should be sufficient motivation  we re united in a common goal  accepts her partnership against the split   earlier the same morning  hirata had quietly asked for the same thing   our class is all messed up because of this  it s a shame  because we were doing really well   i wonder what the culprit s goal is  whoever that may be  did they intend to steal karuizawa s underwear  or did they want to throw our teamwork out the window  i feel like there s a hidden agenda   hey horikita  don t you think it s about time you confessed   your health has gone rapidly downhill since the test started  feels her forehead  a fever close to 38 c  hidden since the ship   you were really sick then  so you were actually sleeping  right   when you joined us on deck  your bangs were all disheveled  proof you d been lying on your side  also  it was incredibly hot on the boat  but you seemed like you were cold  even now  you re wearing long sleeves  and you re zipped all the way up  even an elementary school student could figure it out   i definitely don t plan to do that  anyway  do you intend to hide your condition  horikita has a fever near 38 c and is hiding it  reporting illness would hit the class with a bigger penalty","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2–sec. 6.3: the stakes, Ibuki&#x27;s test, the fever<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.180–189<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pitches the girls&#x27; second tent with Hirata after the split, the other boys off playing or fishing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ah, it’s okay. You don’t have to apologize, Hirata. If anything, I’d feel bad to leave it all to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This question might come off as weird, but why do you work so hard?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I can do this. Go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finishes the remaining stakes alone when the girls pull Hirata away.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Works the stakes at his side and gets the straight answer about why he works so hard.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I guess. Our various troubles are never-ending.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think I trust you, at the very least. I doubt you’re the culprit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reads Ibuki in the eyes and concludes she stole the underwear and planted it in Ike&#x27;s bag.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Tells her he trusts her in the same breath that his narration names her the culprit.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s rich, coming from you. This wouldn’t have happened if you hadn’t had recommended me unnecessarily.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The printed line reads “hadn’t had recommended” — kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re the only one in class who doesn’t trust Hirata. Life’s better when you stop believing that all people are two-faced.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Well, I can count on him, at the very least. He’s really reliable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well. Hirata is a man of many talents. He helps when we can’t bring guys and girls together during a dispute. Don’t you think that he’s working hard to bring students together when no one else can?”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it seems like there were some unexpected expenditures. I can’t give an exact number.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I thought the girls were putting up with the heat unusually well. So this is how you’re getting through it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what you mean, but there’s nothing I can really say about it. We can’t get spent points back, and there aren’t many days left before the test ends. Karuizawa and the others probably won’t spend any more points,”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you want me to work with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood. I don’t know if I’ll be useful, but I’ll help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s better for you to just accept favors in a straightforward way. As a guy, I’m rather upset that the guys are being treated like thieves. That alone should be sufficient motivation. We’re united in a common goal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accepts her partnership against the split — earlier the same morning, Hirata had quietly asked for the same thing.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our class is all messed up because of this. It’s a shame, because we were doing really well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder what the culprit’s goal is, whoever that may be. Did they intend to steal Karuizawa’s underwear, or did they want to throw our teamwork out the window? I feel like there’s a hidden agenda.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey Horikita, don’t you think it’s about time you confessed?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your health has gone rapidly downhill since the test started.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Feels her forehead: a fever close to 38°C, hidden since the ship.<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were really sick then, so you were actually sleeping, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When you joined us on deck, your bangs were all disheveled. Proof you’d been lying on your side. Also, it was incredibly hot on the boat, but you seemed like you were cold. Even now, you’re wearing long sleeves, and you’re zipped all the way up. Even an elementary school student could figure it out”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I definitely don’t plan to do that. Anyway, do you intend to hide your condition?”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Horikita has a fever near 38°C and is hiding it; reporting illness would hit the class with a bigger penalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p171-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the meeting that splits the camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: the sixth morning and the key card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p191-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 4  the sixth morning and the key card sixth day dawns overcast  he wakes with sudou s legs laid across his face   suzune i can t hold back anymore   gah  shut up  the hell  ayanokouji  don t wake me up like that  wakes to sudou dreaming out loud for suzune in his sleep  the class merges the collected food with bought emergency food  hirata organizes the last forage   hey  ibuki  why don t you come with us  too   today s the last day  if you don t want to  i won t pressure you   yamauchi  it d be good if you paid attention to the treetops  they might have fruit  also  we re pretty tall  so we need to be careful around here  diverts yamauchi s eyes off sakura by putting him on treetop duty   we don t really get along well  though  turns the group s eye onto how rarely he and horikita smile   a lot of it s due to genetics  it s the difference between people who smile often and those who don t smile at all   huh  of smiling  the smiling practice exchange runs untagged  his line sits between horikita s two  pairs off with horikita under her order to search in twos   can i see it for a second   it s actually convenient to do it here  it d be too suspicious at base camp   to be honest  i d been keeping quiet  i was with sakura earlier so she can back me up  but on the first day we saw students who had something like a key card   but i don t know if that was really the key card  i didn t see it well  i mean  you d probably laugh if i made a joke about him picking up a telephone card  right  inspects her leader card in the forest  then drops it in the dirt handing it back  the card front carries the leader s name   as chabashira said in ch 1   and horikita s reads  horikita suzune   no  i wonder  though  i thought i d know by looking  but  like it s a different color than i remember  the dropped card draws looks from kushida and ibuki  he covers it as a bug   oh  it s nothing  there was a bug that surprised me  sorry  sorry   look  yamauchi  i need to ask you something  could you come here for a second   the ground in this area is all muddy because of the rain  right  i want you to take this mud and smear it on horikita s hair  can you do that for me   if you do this  i m prepared to offer you sakura s e mail address  bribes yamauchi with sakura s e mail address to smear mud on horikita s hair  what the mud is for is not stated on this page  it follows the dropped key card","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.4: the sixth morning and the key card<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.191–199<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sixth day dawns overcast; he wakes with Sudou&#x27;s legs laid across his face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Suzune…I can’t hold back anymore…”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Gah, shut up… The hell? Ayanokouji, don’t wake me up like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, Ibuki. Why don’t you come with us, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Wakes to Sudou dreaming out loud for Suzune in his sleep.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The class merges the collected food with bought emergency food; Hirata organizes the last forage.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Today’s the last day. If you don’t want to, I won’t pressure you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yamauchi. It’d be good if you paid attention to the treetops. They might have fruit. Also, we’re pretty tall, so we need to be careful around here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Diverts Yamauchi&#x27;s eyes off Sakura by putting him on treetop duty.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We don’t really get along well, though,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Turns the group’s eye onto how rarely he and Horikita smile.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A lot of it’s due to genetics. It’s the difference between people who smile often and those who don’t smile at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh? Of smiling?”<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The smiling-practice exchange runs untagged; his line sits between Horikita&#x27;s two.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pairs off with Horikita under her order to search in twos.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I see it for a second?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s actually convenient to do it here. It’d be too suspicious at base camp.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I’d been keeping quiet. I was with Sakura earlier so she can back me up, but on the first day we saw students who had something like a key card.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I don’t know if that was really the key card. I didn’t see it well. I mean, you’d probably laugh if I made a joke about him picking up a telephone card, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Inspects her leader card in the forest, then drops it in the dirt handing it back.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The card front carries the leader&#x27;s name — as Chabashira said in ch.1 — and Horikita&#x27;s reads “Horikita Suzune”.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. I wonder, though. I thought I’d know by looking, but… like it’s a different color than I remember.”<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The dropped card draws looks from Kushida and Ibuki; he covers it as a bug.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, it’s nothing. There was a bug that surprised me. Sorry, sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Look, Yamauchi. I need to ask you something. Could you come here for a second?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The ground in this area is all muddy because of the rain, right? I want you to take this mud and smear it on Horikita’s hair. Can you do that for me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you do this, I’m prepared to offer you Sakura’s e-mail address.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Bribes Yamauchi with Sakura&#x27;s e-mail address to smear mud on Horikita&#x27;s hair.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> What the mud is for is not stated on this page; it follows the dropped key card.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p180-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2–sec. 6.3: the stakes, Ibuki&#x27;s test, the fever<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p200-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.5: the mud payoff<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p200-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki horikita-suzune ibuki-mio kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 5  the mud payoff yamauchi delivers the mud bribe  horikita seizes his pointing arm and throws him in front of the watching camp   you re absolutely going to do it  if you re lying  i won t agree  nods him on  then watches the throw without intervening   ha ha ha ha  you re all covered in mud  horikita  hilarious   don t worry  when the test is over  i will tell you  feels bad for sakura but pays yamauchi the address for the job   i m going to hold a grudge against you for the rest of my life  you d best prepare yourself  shields the beaten yamauchi behind his back as horikita threatens him   what about the river  that d be easy and fast  right   right  looks like i don t have any other choice  returns from the boys  luggage pile to see horikita washing the mud off in the river   whoa  looks like it s moving now  watches her and horikita come down to the river in swimsuits while the shower line waits","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p200-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.5: the mud payoff<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.200–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi delivers the mud bribe; Horikita seizes his pointing arm and throws him in front of the watching camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re absolutely going to do it? If you’re lying, I won’t agree.”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Ha ha ha ha! You’re all covered in mud, Horikita! Hilarious!”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t worry. When the test is over, I will tell you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Nods him on, then watches the throw without intervening.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Feels bad for Sakura but pays Yamauchi the address for the job.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to hold a grudge against you for the rest of my life. You’d best prepare yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shields the beaten Yamauchi behind his back as Horikita threatens him.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about the river? That’d be easy and fast, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. Looks like I don’t have any other choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Returns from the boys’ luggage pile to see Horikita washing the mud off in the river.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Whoa, looks like it’s moving now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Watches her and Horikita come down to the river in swimsuits while the shower line waits.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: the sixth morning and the key card<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p203-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.6: the confession in the forest<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p203-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 6  the confession in the forest horikita draws him into the forest and confesses that the leader s key card was stolen   ayanokouji kun  could you please come here for a moment   what s wrong  did something happen   follow me  we can t talk here   this happened because of my carelessness  i am aware that i made a mistake  okay   a mistake   it was stolen   w wait  your underwear was stolen  too   no  this is much  much worse  the key card  a complete blunder on my part   i wanted to talk to you because i trust you  i absolutely couldn t consult with someone who might be the culprit  this is so humiliating  i want  to die   such a huge failure   no  the one who stole it is to blame  right   even so  this is an issue of responsibility  it has nothing to do with me being sick or covered in mud   i wasn t supposed to let go of the card for a single second  but i   don t blame yourself  i doubt this ll be any consolation  but i think you did your absolute best   it s probably better if we don t make this information public  we should get to the truth first   yes  i think so  too   i suspect two people  either karuizawa san  or ibuki san   unfortunately  the chances of that are low  karuizawa was in front of the shower the whole time   you re sure about that   yeah  same goes for her flunkies  too   if that s the case  it s highly likely ibuki san is the culprit  it s possible she came to know about the card this morning  and the timing is just far too good   if we examine the timing and talk with ibuki  we can understand what happened  if we suspect ibuki  we shouldn t take our eyes off of her  her escape would probably be the worst case scenario  right   that s right  i m sorry  but can you go back to camp first  that way you can start following her immediately   sure  i understand  i ll keep an eye on her  leaves her in the forest and goes back to camp to keep ibuki in sight","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.6: the confession in the forest<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.203–205<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita draws him into the forest and confesses that the leader’s key card was stolen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Ayanokouji-kun. Could you please come here for a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s wrong? Did something happen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Follow me. We can’t talk here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This happened because of my carelessness. I am aware that I made a mistake. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A mistake?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was stolen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait, your underwear was stolen, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. This is much, much worse. The…key card. A complete blunder on my part.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to talk to you because I trust you. I absolutely couldn’t consult with someone who might be the culprit. This is so humiliating. I want… to die…”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Such a huge failure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, the one who stole it is to blame. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, this is an issue of responsibility. It has nothing to do with me being sick or covered in mud.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wasn’t supposed to let go of the card for a single second. But I…”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t blame yourself. I doubt this’ll be any consolation, but I think you did your absolute best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s probably better if we don’t make this information public. We should get to the truth first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I think so, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suspect two people. Either Karuizawa-san, or Ibuki-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, the chances of that are low. Karuizawa was in front of the shower the whole time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re sure about that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Same goes for her flunkies, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s the case, it’s highly likely Ibuki-san is the culprit. It’s possible she came to know about the card this morning, and the timing is just far too good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we examine the timing and talk with Ibuki, we can understand what happened. If we suspect Ibuki, we shouldn’t take our eyes off of her. Her escape would probably be the worst-case scenario, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. I’m sorry, but can you go back to camp first? That way you can start following her immediately.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure. I understand. I’ll keep an eye on her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Leaves her in the forest and goes back to camp to keep Ibuki in sight.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p200-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.5: the mud payoff<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p206-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.7: the fire and the breakdown<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p206-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei yamauchi-haruki sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 7  the fire and the breakdown smoke behind the temporary toilet  the survival manual is burning while the camp argues   what s that smoke  what in the world happened   this is serious  there s a fire  fire  something is burning behind the toilet   i can t see ibuki  the fire might have been her handiwork  where is she   she noticed the fire  and now she s just walking around  the answer carries no speaker tag  the narration has him the one tracking ibuki  so it is recorded as his  recognizes the half burned pages behind the toilet as the survival manual   did the manual get burned   yeah  it looks like it  who would do this  the confirmation is untagged as well  he is the one the narration shows examining the remains   i m responsible for this  the manual was in my bag  we piled the bags up in front of the tent and i didn t think that someone would steal anything in the daytime  but first  we need to extinguish this fire properly  tries to comfort hirata at the river  he answers with a quiet  thank you   we need to discuss this incident properly   right  most of class d witnessed the fire  i m sure they ll want to know the truth  the reply carries no speaker tag  it sits under his own call to discuss  so it is recorded as his   hey  who did this  is there a traitor in our class  the three line exchange that follows runs untagged between the sides and is left as a chapter attribution gap  takes hirata s water and puts out the last of the embers   at any rate  we don t have to worry about the fire spreading  the line carries no tag  it sits with his bottle shaking over the embers  so it is recorded as his  reads the first raindrops as the coming downpour while the camp splits into glaring sides   rain  huh   hey kanji  i can t see ibuki anywhere  notices a bag gone along with ibuki   hirata  tell us what to do   ike s calling for you   why why is this happening  it s just like back then   it d be good for you to help ike and the others  we have to keep our stuff dry   y yeah  we need to take care of everything quickly   ayanokouji  is hirata okay   looks like he s in shock  i suppose it s probably because of all these things going wrong one after the other   you know  in junior high there was this rich kid honor student  he had a lot of really heavy responsibilities  y know  anyway  he took so much on himself that one day  he ended up having a breakdown  after that  his class became a complete mess   you think there are signs of that with hirata   well  saying he s gonna have a breakdown would be an exaggeration  but i think there s danger there  the narration calls sudou s read surprisingly accurate  secures his share of the luggage  then sees both ibuki and horikita gone and sets out along the road to the beach","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.7: the fire and the breakdown<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.206–212<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Smoke behind the temporary toilet: the survival manual is burning while the camp argues.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “What’s that smoke? What in the world happened?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “This is serious. There’s a fire! Fire! Something is burning behind the toilet!”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I can’t see Ibuki. The fire might have been her handiwork. Where is she?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She noticed the fire, and now she’s just walking around.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The answer carries no speaker tag; the narration has him the one tracking Ibuki, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Recognizes the half-burned pages behind the toilet as the survival manual.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did the manual get burned?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. It looks like it. Who would do this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The confirmation is untagged as well; he is the one the narration shows examining the remains.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m responsible for this. The manual was in my bag. We piled the bags up in front of the tent and I didn’t think that someone would steal anything in the daytime. But first, we need to extinguish this fire properly…”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Tries to comfort Hirata at the river; he answers with a quiet “Thank you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We need…to discuss this incident properly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Right. Most of Class D witnessed the fire. I’m sure they’ll want to know the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reply carries no speaker tag; it sits under his own call to discuss, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, who did this? Is there a traitor in our class?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The three-line exchange that follows runs untagged between the sides and is left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes Hirata’s water and puts out the last of the embers.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At any rate, we don’t have to worry about the fire spreading.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line carries no tag; it sits with his bottle-shaking over the embers, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the first raindrops as the coming downpour while the camp splits into glaring sides.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Rain, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey Kanji, I can’t see Ibuki anywhere.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Notices a bag gone along with Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata, tell us what to do!”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ike’s calling for you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why…why is this happening? It’s just like back then…”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’d be good for you to help Ike and the others. We have to keep our stuff dry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-yeah. We need to take care of everything quickly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji. Is Hirata okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like he’s in shock. I suppose it’s probably because of all these things going wrong one after the other.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, in junior high there was this rich kid honor student. He had a lot of really heavy responsibilities, y’know? Anyway, he took so much on himself that one day, he ended up having a breakdown. After that, his class became a complete mess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You think there are signs of that with Hirata?”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, saying he’s gonna have a breakdown would be an exaggeration, but I think there’s danger there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration calls Sudou’s read surprisingly accurate.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Secures his share of the luggage, then sees both Ibuki and Horikita gone and sets out along the road to the beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p203-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.6: the confession in the forest<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p226-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.10: the footprints<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p226-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 10  the footprints follows two pairs of footprints deep into the forest and hears a distant flashlight exchange he cannot make out  kills his own light and closes on the signal   the page does not let him catch the conversation  finds horikita unconscious by a large tree with her key card on the ground  and lifts her into his arms  reads the excavated soil on her as proof that more than ibuki found her position","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p226-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.10: the footprints<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.226–227<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows two pairs of footprints deep into the forest and hears a distant flashlight exchange he cannot make out.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Kills his own light and closes on the signal — the page does not let him catch the conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q action\">Finds Horikita unconscious by a large tree with her key card on the ground, and lifts her into his arms.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the excavated soil on her as proof that more than Ibuki found her position.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p206-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.7: the fire and the breakdown<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p229-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.10: carrying Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p229-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 10  carrying horikita she wakes in his arms under a tree  fever high  and the night turns on the choice between carrying on and retiring   are you awake   ayano kouji kun   you have a high fever  don t push yourself   i knew it ibuki san stole my card   this isn t a test where you can just hide for twenty four hours a day  right  no matter what you do  you can be open to attack   i could ve avoided this if i knew how to rely on someone   when i was losing consciousness  i felt like i could hear ryuuen s voice  it s strange  i thought he d already retired   you were losing consciousness  maybe you had a dream   if it was a dream  it was a nightmare   i m sorry   why are you apologizing to me   there s no one i can apologize to except for you   if you think things are bad  then make some reliable friends  start there first   that s difficult advice  no one would want to be with me   it s unpleasant to be made fun of  though   it s just that you ve started to sound like you need allies   nobody would say that   i should have understood this a long time ago   don t talk  you re sick   i m going to try to get up to class a using my own abilities  i ll definitely recover from this failure   i m prepared to be hated by everyone else  this was all my mistake   according to this school s system  if you fight by yourself  you won t reach class a  we need to cooperate with our classmates  it s unavoidable   i can t accept that  no matter how hard it is  i m still alone   ah  shut up already  stop talking  right now  you won t be able to convince anyone  embraces her tightly as she talks of her dream   you can t bear every responsibility  you re not that strong  unfortunately   so you re telling me to give up  i have a dream to reach class a  a dream for my brother to acknowledge me   no one said you have to give up   if you can t fight by yourself  it s better to fight with a partner  i ll lend you a hand   why  you re not the kind of person who would say such things   well  why then  i wonder  decides against the emergency call   he does not know the wristwatch button  and a helicopter would give them away  takes the wrong route  slips on the collapsed soil  and curls around her to shield the fall down the slope  shelters under an overgrown tree with her head in his lap while the fever burns   it s already almost six o clock  horikita  you might think this will sound harsh  but you should retire  your body is probably at its limit   i can t do that  we can t afford to lose thirty points because of me  i was the one who confronted karuizawa san and the others about using points  right  it would make me look like such an idiot   not just that  the keycard was stolen from me  too  you understand what that means   class d will lose another fifty points  losing the leader s card means fifty more points  and the class would be left with only a few   just leave me here and head back  if you do  i ll be the only one absent from roll call   what are you planning to do   by tomorrow morning  i ll try to return by myself  somehow  if i can deal with my poor health during roll call  then i ll do something about retirement   things aren t that easy  you re feeling really weak now  and our teacher isn t kind enough to let you act your way past her  it will be impossible for you to get back to camp on your own   still  there s nothing else i can do   yes  that s the correct decision  everything was my responsibility   well then  i ll leave  but if things continue like this  our classmates will blame you   can you really make it back alone by tomorrow morning   yeah  i ll be fine   horikita  do you really think that not retiring is the right decision   of course i do  retiring isn t an option for me   hey  why do you think that we ve been backed into such a corner   i failed due to my negligence  that s all   you re wrong  you re completely wrong   go  because i think of you as my friend  please listen to my request  she catches herself the moment she says it and covers her mouth  takes her into his arms again when she loses consciousness   it would have been easier if you d just retired of your own free will   i have never thought of you as my friend  i ve never cared about you as a classmate  in this world  winning is everything  your methods don t matter   i don t care what i have to sacrifice  as long as i have my victory in the end  i ll be fine   you  hirata no  all other people are nothing more than tools  i was complicit in what drove you to this  so  don t blame yourself  horikita  you were useful to me  the monologue answers her friend line without ever being spoken to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.10: carrying Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.229–235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She wakes in his arms under a tree, fever high, and the night turns on the choice between carrying on and retiring.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you awake?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Ayano…kouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You have a high fever. Don’t push yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>58 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I knew it…Ibuki-san stole my card.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t a test where you can just hide for twenty-four hours a day, right? No matter what you do, you can be open to attack.”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I could’ve avoided this if I knew how to rely on someone…”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When I was losing consciousness, I felt like I could hear Ryuuen’s voice… It’s strange, I thought he’d already retired…”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were losing consciousness. Maybe you had a dream?”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If it was a dream, it was a nightmare…”<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why are you apologizing to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no one I can apologize to except for you…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you think things are bad, then make some reliable friends. Start there first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s difficult advice… No one would want to be with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s unpleasant to be made fun of, though…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s just that you’ve started to sound like you need allies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nobody would say that…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should have understood this a long time ago…”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t talk. You’re sick.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to try to get up to Class A using my own abilities. I’ll definitely recover from this failure…”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m prepared to be hated by everyone else… This was all my mistake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “According to this school’s system, if you fight by yourself, you won’t reach Class A. We need to cooperate with our classmates. It’s unavoidable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t accept that. No matter how hard it is, I’m still…alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, shut up already! Stop talking. Right now, you won’t be able to convince anyone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Embraces her tightly as she talks of her dream.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t bear every responsibility. You’re not that strong, unfortunately.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re telling me to give up? I have a dream to reach Class A, a dream for my brother to acknowledge me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No one said you have to give up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you can’t fight by yourself, it’s better to fight with a partner. I’ll lend you a hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why? You’re not the kind of person who would say such things…”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, why then? I wonder.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Decides against the emergency call — he does not know the wristwatch button, and a helicopter would give them away.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes the wrong route, slips on the collapsed soil, and curls around her to shield the fall down the slope.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shelters under an overgrown tree with her head in his lap while the fever burns.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s already almost six o’clock, Horikita. You might think this will sound harsh, but you should retire. Your body is probably at its limit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t do that. We can’t afford to lose thirty points because of me… I was the one who confronted Karuizawa-san and the others about using points, right? It would make me look like such an idiot…”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not just that… The keycard was stolen from me, too. You understand what that means?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Class D will lose another fifty points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Losing the leader’s card means fifty more points, and the class would be left with only a few.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just leave me here and head back. If you do, I’ll be the only one absent from roll call.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you planning to do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By tomorrow morning, I’ll…try to return by myself, somehow. If I can deal with my poor health during roll call, then I’ll do something about retirement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Things aren’t that easy. You’re feeling really weak now, and our teacher isn’t kind enough to let you act your way past her. It will be impossible for you to get back to camp on your own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Still, there’s nothing else I can do…”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. That’s the correct decision. Everything was my responsibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, I’ll leave. But if things continue like this, our classmates will blame you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you really make it back alone by tomorrow morning?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah… I’ll be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita. Do you really think that not retiring is the right decision?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I do. Retiring isn’t an option for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey. Why do you think that we’ve been backed into such a corner?”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I failed due to my negligence. That’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re wrong. You’re completely wrong.”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Go… Because I think of you as my friend, please listen to my request…”<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She catches herself the moment she says it and covers her mouth.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes her into his arms again when she loses consciousness.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would have been easier if you’d just retired of your own free will.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I have never thought of you as my friend. I’ve never cared about you as a classmate. In this world, winning is everything. Your methods don’t matter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I don’t care what I have to sacrifice. As long as I have my victory in the end, I’ll be fine.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “You, Hirata—no, all other people are nothing more than tools. I was complicit in what drove you to this. So, don’t blame yourself, Horikita. You were useful to me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The monologue answers her friend line without ever being spoken to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p226-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.10: the footprints<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p237-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.10: the ship at 7:58<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p237-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 10  the ship at 7 58 reaches the ship at the pier with the storm still on  minutes before roll call  walks the muddy road by the map in his head  picks her up again  and carries her up the ramp  a teacher stops him on the deck    you re prohibited from entering here  you ll be disqualified    and he answers the emergency   this is an emergency  she s got a high fever and has lost consciousness  please let her rest right away  the teacher brings a stretcher and asks    is she okay with retiring    and he confirms without hesitation   without question  however  allow me to confirm one thing  because it isn t eight o clock yet  this shouldn t have any effect on roll call  correct  it is 7 58  the teacher answers    you are certainly right  it is quite close  however  you re out   i understand  oh  one more thing  i d like to return this keycard  hands over the key card and leaves the ship before the rain lets up  class d loses thirty points to horikita s retirement and five more to his absence at roll call","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.10: the ship at 7:58<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.237–238<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reaches the ship at the pier with the storm still on, minutes before roll call.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“This is an emergency. She’s got a high fever and has lost consciousness. Please let her rest right away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Without question. However, allow me to confirm one thing. Because it isn’t eight o’clock yet, this shouldn’t have any effect on roll call, correct?”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I understand. Oh, one more thing. I’d like to return this keycard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Walks the muddy road by the map in his head, picks her up again, and carries her up the ramp.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A teacher stops him on the deck — “You’re prohibited from entering here. You’ll be disqualified.” — and he answers the emergency.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The teacher brings a stretcher and asks — “Is she okay with retiring?” — and he confirms without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> It is 7:58; the teacher answers — “You are certainly right. It is quite close. However, you’re out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands over the key card and leaves the ship before the rain lets up.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Class D loses thirty points to Horikita’s retirement and five more to his absence at roll call.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p229-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.10: carrying Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p240-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the results and the lone Class C<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p240-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru mashima-tomonari katsuragi-kouhei ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  the results and the lone class c the test ends at noon on august 7  at the rest area sudou asks how close he and horikita are  hirata brings paper cups  and ryuuen   the only class c student left   comes over to provoke   ayanokouji  you work pretty well with horikita  don t you  how close are you  really   there s nothing between us  we re just friends  nothing more  nothing less  untagged  it answers sudou s question in his own viewpoint  so it is recorded as his   even that makes me jealous  though  i still ain t her friend   but didn t horikita acknowledge you a little bit this time  runs untagged between sudou s lines   it could be either sudou or ayanokoji speaking   and is left out as a chapter attribution gap   i sure hope so  she still hasn t called me by my first name  after all   good work  both of you  thank you for everything you did this week  you really saved us  hands him and sudou the two paper cups he was carrying  the question that opens the chapter   how close he and horikita really are   i should be thanking you  you covered for me  the class loner  also  you covered for me being late for roll call  and the fact that horikita retired   i couldn t blame you when i heard the reason  besides  horikita san gave us some really important information   do you believe what she said  untagged  it sits between hirata s lines about horikita  so it is recorded as his   she isn t the type to speak irresponsibly  that s why you get along with her  right  the narration calls him the one who would protect an ally even if it risked his pure reputation   i d be lying if i said there wasn t any risk  but i had to help horikitasan   that s a friend   wait  what did you say  what are you talking about   i think you ll understand pretty soon  anyway  class c is really strange  they re on another level  and  why is he  so ryuuen kun didn t retire  run untagged between sudou s confusion and his own observation of the beach and are left out as chapter attribution gaps  finds class c emptied   ibuki nowhere on the sandy beach   with ryuuen alone  the only remaining student  cup in hand   oh  hey there  sycophants  what happened to suzune   i know you ve been chasing suzune s ass  we were together before  you know  drains his cup  then crushes it and throws it at ayanokoji s feet   throw that away for me   what a stupid thing to say  huh  pick up your own trash  jerk   but picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage   calm down  sudou kun  here  i ll throw it away   who are you  more importantly  where s suzune  i ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom   the next time you say something stupid  i ll kill you  sudou growled   what are you doing  and  huh  what s with you  getting all excited by yourself  huh  run untagged around sudou s tagged threat and are left out as chapter attribution gaps   horikita san retired yesterday  she s not here   retired  suzune  she doesn t seem like that kind of girl  untagged  hirata has just pulled sudou away and answers the question about horikita  so it is recorded as him   i thought you retired  ryuuen kun  and the interrupted reply  that s  are left out as chapter attribution gaps  the broken three quarter mark is kept as printed  the megaphone click cuts the argument short as mashima appears on the beach   it s fine  we don t mind if you want to keep relaxing  the test has already concluded  now we ve entered the summer vacation part of the trip  so it s all right if you loosen up   well then  to get straight to the point  i would like to announce the results of the special test   we will not accept any questions regarding the results  no exceptions  we would like you to accept the results you have been given  analyze them  and use them to help you for the next test  it is what it is  don t wet yourselves over these results  you must accept reality  you know   that s what we should be saying to you class c people  you used up all of your points  right  don t make us laugh   we have 125 points remaining  i think we ll be quite fine   ha  i m jealous of the nerve of you small fry  how you can be satisfied with that amount of points   so you re going to expose a class leader  untagged  the narration then has hirata and ayanokoji holding their faces still while sudou alone looks shocked  so the question is placed as his   that s right  i wrote it on the paper  didn t i  the name of class d s leader   also  those guys in a and b wrote the same thing  too  do you know what this means   hold on a minute  what are you talking about  huh  i if you re telling the truth  then  the page s own reading of the reveal  if the name holds  class d is hit with penalties and loses 100 points   it doesn t really matter whatever you say  class c is still going to stay at zero points  runs untagged between ryuuen s taunts and is left out as a chapter attribution gap   now  we will announce the rankings  the lowest class is class c  with zero points   bwah ha ha ha  hey  check it out  you guys have zero points after all   zero   in third place is class a  with 120 points  coming in second place is class b  with 140 points   has come in first with 225 points  this concludes the announcement  class d takes first with 225 points  class b second with 140  class a third with 120  class c last with zero   something is strange  what does this mean  the question follows the narration that he muttered it  recorded as his  the class a cry  what s the meaning of this  katsuragi  comes from unnamed voices and is left out as a chapter attribution gap   yahoo  we did it  in your face   hey  hey  hey  what s going on  hey  hey   i ll explain everything  well  ryuuen kun  if you ll excuse us  walks toward the boat with ike and sudou  sudou raises a middle finger and sticks out his tongue  and ryuuen can only watch in silence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p240-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the results and the lone Class C<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.240–245<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The test ends at noon on August 7; at the rest area Sudou asks how close he and Horikita are, Hirata brings paper cups, and Ryuuen — the only Class C student left — comes over to provoke.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Ayanokouji. You work pretty well with Horikita, don’t you? How close are you, really?”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s nothing between us. We’re just friends. Nothing more, nothing less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Even that makes me jealous, though. I still ain’t her friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>56 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Untagged; it answers Sudou’s question in his own viewpoint, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “But didn’t Horikita acknowledge you a little bit this time?” runs untagged between Sudou’s lines — it could be either Sudou or Ayanokōji speaking — and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I sure hope so. She still hasn’t called me by my first name, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good work, both of you. Thank you for everything you did this week. You really saved us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hands him and Sudou the two paper cups he was carrying.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The question that opens the chapter — how close he and Horikita really are.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should be thanking you. You covered for me, the class loner. Also, you covered for me being late for roll call, and the fact that Horikita retired.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I couldn’t blame you when I heard the reason. Besides, Horikita-san gave us some really important information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you believe what she said?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Untagged; it sits between Hirata’s lines about Horikita, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She isn’t the type to speak irresponsibly. That’s why you get along with her, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narration calls him the one who would protect an ally even if it risked his pure reputation.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d be lying if I said there wasn’t any risk, but I had to help Horikitasan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a friend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, what did you say? What are you talking about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “I think you’ll understand pretty soon. Anyway, Class C is really strange… They’re on another level.” and “Why is he…? So Ryuuen-kun didn’t retire?” run untagged between Sudou’s confusion and his own observation of the beach and are left out as chapter attribution gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finds Class C emptied — Ibuki nowhere on the sandy beach — with Ryuuen alone, the only remaining student, cup in hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, hey there, sycophants. What happened to Suzune?”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you’ve been chasing Suzune’s ass. We were together before, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Drains his cup, then crushes it and throws it at Ayanokōji’s feet.<span class=\"pg\">p.241–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Throw that away for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a stupid thing to say. Huh? Pick up your own trash, jerk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But picking up garbage seems like the perfect task for garbage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Calm down, Sudou-kun. Here, I’ll throw it away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who are you? More importantly, where’s Suzune? I’ve dreamed of squeezing her bottom.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The next time you say something stupid, I’ll kill you,” Sudou growled.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “What are you doing?” and “Huh? What’s with you? Getting all excited by yourself, huh?” run untagged around Sudou’s tagged threat and are left out as chapter attribution gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san retired yesterday. She’s not here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Retired? Suzune? She doesn’t seem like that kind of girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Untagged; Hirata has just pulled Sudou away and answers the question about Horikita, so it is recorded as him. “I thought you retired, Ryuuen-kun.” and the interrupted reply “That’s¾” are left out as chapter attribution gaps; the broken three-quarter mark is kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The megaphone click cuts the argument short as Mashima appears on the beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s fine. We don’t mind if you want to keep relaxing. The test has already concluded. Now we’ve entered the summer vacation part of the trip, so it’s all right if you loosen up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, to get straight to the point. I would like to announce the results of the special test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We will not accept any questions regarding the results, no exceptions. We would like you to accept the results you have been given, analyze them, and use them to help you for the next test. It is what it is. Don’t wet yourselves over these results. You must accept reality, you know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s what we should be saying to you Class C people. You used up all of your points, right? Don’t make us laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have 125 points remaining. I think we’ll be quite fine,”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha. I’m jealous of the nerve of you small fry. How you can be satisfied with that amount of points…”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re going to expose a class leader?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Untagged; the narration then has Hirata and Ayanokōji holding their faces still while Sudou alone looks shocked, so the question is placed as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. I wrote it on the paper, didn’t I? The name of Class D’s leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, those guys in A and B wrote the same thing, too. Do you know what this means?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hold on a minute. What are you talking about, huh?! I-If you’re telling the truth, then…”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The page’s own reading of the reveal: if the name holds, Class D is hit with penalties and loses 100 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “It doesn’t really matter whatever you say; Class C is still going to stay at zero points.” runs untagged between Ryuuen’s taunts and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now, we will announce the rankings. The lowest class is¾Class C, with zero points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Bwah ha ha ha! Hey, check it out! You guys have zero points after all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Zero?”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In third place is Class A, with 120 points. Coming in second place is Class B, with 140 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…has come in first with 225 points. This concludes the announcement.”<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class D takes first with 225 points, Class B second with 140, Class A third with 120, Class C last with zero.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Something is strange… What does this mean?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question follows the narration that he muttered it; recorded as his. The Class A cry “What’s the meaning of this, Katsuragi?!” comes from unnamed voices and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yahoo! We did it! In your face!”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, hey, hey, what’s going on?! Hey, hey!!”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll explain everything. Well, Ryuuen-kun, if you’ll excuse us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Walks toward the boat with Ike and Sudou; Sudou raises a middle finger and sticks out his tongue, and Ryuuen can only watch in silence.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p237-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.10: the ship at 7:58<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p245-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the deck and the apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p245-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ike-kanji sudou-ken horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  the deck and the apology on the ship s deck koenji greets them with a drink  horikita appears still pale  the class gathers  and karuizawa comes to apologize   hello  ladies and gentlemen  how was your week on the deserted island   you jerk  kouenji  we lost thirty points because of you  you know what i m talking about  don t you   calm down  little boy ike  i was in poor health  and was resting  i had no other choice  smooth  glossy skin from a week of tanning under a claim of poor health the page calls not the least bit credible  the thirty points ike howls about are the retirement penalty from the volume s second chapter   s suzune  are you feeling better now   i m not too bad  i can t say that i m back to full health  more than anything else  retiring was a big mistake on my part   don t worry about it  accepts the first name for one line  then withdraws the permission   by the way  sudou kun  don t just go around calling me by my first name without permission  understand   y y yeah   but what happened  why was class d ranked first  runs untagged before karuizawa s tagged line and is left out as a chapter attribution gap   well  karuizawa san  i think you should talk to horikita san first  don t you agree   horikita san  do you have a minute  the line is attributed only to  he  hirata has just proposed the talk  so it is recorded as him   yes  there s something that we re supposed to talk about  right  faces her to eat humble pie after the accusation about the points   i m sorry   ibuki san stole my underwear  ayanokouji kun told us everything   huh  the one word reply follows the narration that she was puzzled  recorded as hers   horikita san  when you noticed that ibuki san was the culprit  she tried to run because you questioned her  right  that s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick   i heard about it from hirata kun first  he said that you found out the leaders of class a and c  that s why we had so many points  so  i m sorry for everything i said  delivers the class s reading of the test   horikita found the leaders   to her face   wait a minute  i  you said i found out the leaders  identities  but i retired   wait  ayanokouji kun  what did you  both replies keep the printed three quarter marks  the classmates  praise lines    there s no need for you to be humble   horikita san  you were so incredibly awesome   when i heard that you d retired    run untagged from unnamed speakers and are left out as chapter attribution gaps   w wait a second  is hers  he withdraws while the crowd buries the key player in congratulations  and heads for his room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p245-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the deck and the apology<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.245–247<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the ship’s deck Kōenji greets them with a drink; Horikita appears still pale, the class gathers, and Karuizawa comes to apologize.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Hello, ladies and gentlemen. How was your week on the deserted island?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “You jerk, Kouenji! We lost thirty points because of you. You know what I’m talking about, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Calm down, little boy Ike. I was in poor health, and was resting. I had no other choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Smooth, glossy skin from a week of tanning under a claim of poor health the page calls not the least bit credible.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The thirty points Ike howls about are the retirement penalty from the volume’s second chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-Suzune. Are you feeling better now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not too bad. I can’t say that I’m back to full health. More than anything else, retiring was a big mistake on my part.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accepts the first name for one line, then withdraws the permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, Sudou-kun. Don’t just go around calling me by my first name without permission. Understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-y-yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “But…what happened? Why was Class D ranked first?” runs untagged before Karuizawa’s tagged line and is left out as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, Karuizawa-san, I think you should talk to Horikita-san first, don’t you agree?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is attributed only to “he”; Hirata has just proposed the talk, so it is recorded as him.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. There’s something that we’re supposed to talk about. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Faces her to eat humble pie after the accusation about the points.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ibuki-san stole my underwear. Ayanokouji-kun told us everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The one-word reply follows the narration that she was puzzled; recorded as hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita-san, when you noticed that Ibuki-san was the culprit, she tried to run because you questioned her, right? That’s why you ended up collapsing and getting sick…”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard about it from Hirata-kun first. He said that you found out the leaders of Class A and C. That’s why we had so many points. So, I’m…sorry for everything I said.”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Delivers the class’s reading of the test — Horikita found the leaders — to her face.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait a minute. I… You said I found out the leaders’ identities? But I retired¾”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Ayanokouji-kun, what did you¾”<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Both replies keep the printed three-quarter marks. The classmates’ praise lines — “There’s no need for you to be humble…”, “Horikita-san, you were so incredibly awesome!…”, “When I heard that you’d retired…” — run untagged from unnamed speakers and are left out as chapter attribution gaps; “W-wait a second!” is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He withdraws while the crowd buries the key player in congratulations, and heads for his room.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p240-1\">← Before: Ch.7: the results and the lone Class C<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p248-1\">→ After: Ch.7: the Icarus talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p248-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  the icarus talk chabashira intercepts him on the empty side of the ship and confirms  through the icarus myth  that the man who demanded his expulsion is his father   may i have a word with you   i don t really feel sociable  is it okay if i refuse  chabashira sensei   if you really don t want to  i can just start talking here  you don t mind if we stand outside  do you   it s hot  so please keep it brief   is it safe to say that for the time being  you re satisfied   yes  first  i d like to say that you did wonderfully  i m honestly impressed   well  tell me something  is it really true  did he demand i be expelled from school   do you have any basis for saying that the story is true   i know quite a lot about you  might not that be the reason  more than anything else  other teachers don t know about your true abilities  but i have no doubts  claims knowledge of his true abilities that the other teachers do not have   i m sure that you ve heard of this rather famous myth  the wings of icarus   why do you bring that up  i asked   icarus flew out of the tower where he was imprisoned in order to gain his freedom  however  that wasn t achieved through one person s abilities alone  it was because his father  daedalus  had constructed wings and instructed him to fly  he didn t fly because of his own intentions  don t you think that sounds exactly like your current predicament   i can t understand   that man no  your father said this   sooner or later  kiyotaka will gladly chase the means of his expulsion from school  you re welcoming your end  much like how icarus fell into the sea and died after his wings were burned  because he d flown too close to the sun  the man who demanded his expulsion from the school is named as his father  with the father s own words quoted   so  what do you plan to do  she asked   you should know  sensei  icarus won t heed daedalus  warnings  answers her myth with the myth   burned wings and all  he flies on for his freedom","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p248-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: the Icarus talk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.248–249<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira intercepts him on the empty side of the ship and confirms, through the Icarus myth, that the man who demanded his expulsion is his father.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “May I have a word with you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t really feel sociable. Is it okay if I refuse, Chabashira-sensei?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “If you really don’t want to, I can just start talking here. You don’t mind if we stand outside, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s hot, so please keep it brief.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it safe to say that for the time being, you’re satisfied?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. First, I’d like to say that you did wonderfully. I’m honestly impressed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, tell me something. Is it really true? Did he demand I be expelled from school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you have any basis for saying that the story is true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know quite a lot about you. Might not that be the reason, more than anything else? Other teachers don’t know about your true abilities. But I have no doubts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Claims knowledge of his true abilities that the other teachers do not have.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sure that you’ve heard of this rather famous myth, the wings of Icarus.”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you bring that up?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Icarus flew out of the tower where he was imprisoned in order to gain his freedom. However, that wasn’t achieved through one person’s abilities alone. It was because his father, Daedalus, had constructed wings and instructed him to fly. He didn’t fly because of his own intentions. Don’t you think that sounds exactly like your current predicament?”<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t understand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That man—no, your father—said this: ‘Sooner or later, Kiyotaka will gladly chase the means of his expulsion from school.’ You’re welcoming your end, much like how Icarus fell into the sea and died after his wings were burned, because he’d flown too close to the sun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The man who demanded his expulsion from the school is named as his father, with the father’s own words quoted.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, what do you plan to do?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should know, Sensei. Icarus won’t heed Daedalus’ warnings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Answers her myth with the myth — burned wings and all, he flies on for his freedom.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p245-1\">← Before: Ch.7: the deck and the apology<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p250-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.1: the whole explanation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p250-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 1  the whole explanation section 7 1 opens with horikita storming the lounge for the full story  he gives it on one condition   she never investigates him   what do these test results mean  what in the world happened   you look like you don t have any idea at all  untagged  it answers her question in his own viewpoint  so it is recorded as his   i just can t imagine it  i don t understand it at all  i have a mountain of questions   i ll tell you everything  however  my one condition is that you stay quiet on this matter  i won t compromise on this  sets the price of the story  her silence  with no compromise   what would you like to ask   what were you doing during the test  tell me  she said   when the special test was announced  i didn t focus on anything except for the additional rules  i roughly understood how to manage the 300 points  but you couldn t manipulate them as an individual   but the additional rules were really difficult to understand  if you did things normally  you wouldn t have been able to identify the leaders  right   yeah  first of all  i volunteered to join the search for the base camp  able to move freely  i planned to search out spot locations ahead of everyone else   you make it sound simple  but no one should have known the spot locations   that s not true  you didn t understand because you were ill and holed up inside the ship  but the school already gave us hints about the locations when we were sailing around the island  the circling ship   nearly three times a usual cruise s speed   and the phrase  significant scenery  were the school s hints about the spot locations  katsuragi and koenji had noticed the same hint   then  i reached the cave  i thought it was the most important base   the cave was the most important base  don t you think that the river and the well would have been more convenient  though   the spot itself wasn t what was important  its location was  the cave matters because the hut and the tower   two spots   sit near it  a perfect place to exercise control   but what advantage is there in going into the cave if you don t have a keycard   well  i d intended to explore various things  but in the end i discovered the leader s identity   well  i suppose that katsuragi kun was careless   no  that wasn t it   there was that guy  yahiko  remember  the one following katsuragi around  he was the leader  i saw katsuragi and yahiko at the cave  but i didn t see the moment they occupied it  after the two of them walked away  i checked if the cave was occupied or not  totsuka yahiko was class a s leader  katsuragi only displayed the card while the two were at the cave   wouldn t you have mistaken katsuragi kun as the leader  she asked   do you think that the leader would have shown off the card so carelessly in front of people   but why  why bother deliberately holding onto the card  then   because he didn t have any other choice  as far as i can tell  katsuragi is a calm and collected man  excessively cautious  there s no way he didn t understand the high risk of occupying a spot immediately after finding it  in other words  the person who occupied it was enticed by shortsighted greed   that s why there was another person   yes  the explanation then continues as narration  when katsuragi found the cave he did not intend to occupy it  but held the space down because yahiko had been careless  wanting insurance by displaying the card so a witness could be misled into taking him for the leader  the sentences are the page s  not a spoken quotation   so  aside from their base  class a held down at least two spots  but we didn t confirm how many they were occupying by the end of the test  if i correctly guessed the identity of their leader  though  i could invalidate all of their points   i m still not convinced  if he figured out the spot s location at such an early stage  and if he were acting alongside a lot of other people  shouldn t he have avoided trouble  even if he just had someone standing watch by the cave  it should have been sufficient claim of ownership  why would they occupy it   that was probably class a s disadvantage   their class appears perfect at first glance  but it actually has a huge schism in it  class a s internal schism is the reason katsuragi could not rely on other people   why the methods revealed class a so easily   that s why i excluded class a at that stage  and turned my attention toward class c  katsuragi was easy to understand  but with ryuuen  there were many unknown variables  to tell you the truth  he was gathering more information than i was  he d found out the identities of all of the leaders  read as the variable with more information than himself   the identities of all the leaders in hand   w wait  he found out the identities of all of the leaders  so not only class d  but also the leaders for classes b and a  but that s strange  we were far from being penalized  we ended up getting first place by a wide margin  how do you intend to explain that   this is a little difficult to explain  but the reason i made you retire is the answer   wait  the answer is you made me retire  what in the world did you do   oh  that reminds me  i didn t return it to the school yet  takes a single card out of his pocket and hands it to horikita  the engraved name reads  ayanokouji kiyotaka   this is a keycard  why do you   wait  why does  the leader card in his pocket bears his own name   the test had to be fair  the rules were fundamentally created to be fair  he then asks what would happen if a leader retired because of poor health  the sentence breaks across the page and is left unquoted   that s  the leader would be absent  so the rights of exclusive possession would disappear   wrong  in the manual  it says   it is impossible to change the leader without suitable justification  don t you think that retirement is suitable enough justification  the manual s leader change clause   retirement is suitable justification  the additional rules were made to be broken when someone is out through poor health or injury  with the base camp clause as the parallel case   so then  you made me  horikita suzune retired and he was appointed in her place   the leader the other classes were supposed to guess at the end  there can only be one   that s why even though class c knew you were the leader  we avoided penalties   but wait  ibuki san stole my card  but what if i d protected it really thoroughly   did you drop the card on purpose back then  well  i suppose that yamauchi kun s actions might have provided ibuki san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard  the mud bribe read back as the opening that let ibuki take the card   unless i knew what ibuki san was aiming for right at the start  i couldn t have done anything  ibuki was picked up by class d  but not by chance   the near coincidence of two people saved by two separate classes dissolved once kaneda in class b came out as a spy ryuuen had sent   besides  ibuki has a habit of looking people in the eye when she s lying  the bigger the lie  the more obvious the habit   she looked him straight in the eye even over the underwear theft   wait  when she lied she would look the person in the eye  isn t it usually the opposite   generally speaking  you avoid eye contact if you have a guilty conscience  however  it was the opposite for her  i think that she made eye contact to make the person think that the lie was the truth  she probably didn t even notice it herself   her goal was probably to find the keycard  but she might have intended to disrupt class d at the same time   but i have to wonder why ibuki san specifically stole my keycard  all she needed was to check my name   that was likely ibuki s intention from the start  however  she ran into unexpected trouble  ibuki carried a digital camera to take a picture of the keycard  a photo would have made the leader s identity clear to anyone and let her profit   to take a picture with the camera  why would she go so far   if she had a picture  then the leader s identity would have been clear for anyone to see  right  if she had convincing evidence  she would have profited   i don t quite understand  did ryuuen kun not trust ibuki san   that wasn t it  the rest of the answer   had the discussion stayed inside class c there would have been no need for the picture or the card theft   breaks across the page and is left unquoted  people outside class c did not trust ibuki s word alone   they wanted reliable evidence  which is why the camera and the card theft existed   from here on out  i don t have any evidence of what i m saying  think of it as my intuition  which i derived from the test results  at the end of the test  class a had 270 points  his own label  intuition from the results  with no evidence   class a ended the test with 270 points and had not used a single one  classes a and c were connected behind the scenes  class c sacrificed its own points and bought whatever class a needed  and by taking all of c s tools class a spent the week without using any points   ibuki s evidence went to someone in class a   by the way  i became aware of class c s leader after half of the students retired  it was certain that the leader would have remained on the island  right   even so  we weren t supposed to know who was left   no  i was almost one hundred percent sure that ryuuen was still on the island  ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact  ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation   no one else controlled it  and his mistake was trusting no one   my god  i don t even have the words  horikita answered  facing the truth  the test in one line  class a failed on its internal rift  class b ran defense only and paid for believing kaneda  class c sent spies and negotiated with a  and class d avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader  named the number one enemy   spies for the leaders  identities plus whatever the class a negotiations bought   i don t like this  you completely used me  like a pawn   yeah  i can t deny that  i wouldn t be surprised if you never want to speak to me ever again  accepts the charge without defense  he was aware of what he had done   well  i ll be heading back to my room now  i m really tired  i said   wait  we re not done talking   what  i just want to relax in my room  if possible   after you explain everything  there are still some things we need to talk about  right   well like what   the reason why you participated in this special test  was it to fight alone  i don t care that you used me this time  i want to know why you put in the effort when you dislike trouble   i wonder  her real question is his principles  not the test   the explanation so far was the less important part to her   i don t have any room for doubt  i understand your talents now  if you help me  aiming for class a seems a realistic enough goal  but what are your principles  why did you do this  names her own goal with him in it  class a  realistically  if his principles hold   because i was touched that you tried to fight all alone when you were ill   you wouldn t normally say that kind of thing  it s easy to spot the lie   well  what i mean is i don t feel like explaining it   i don t mind helping you get up to class a  however  i have one condition  do not investigate me  if you promise not to touch on this subject ever again  i will help you  the deal is struck  his help toward class a in exchange for his past staying buried   if you don t want to talk  there s nothing i can really do about that  if you ll help  i have no reason to refuse you  i m not interested in digging things up that are better left buried  after all  you dislike trouble  takes her hand without hesitation  the handshake is firm    i work for me  you do things for yourself    and the battle to raise the class from the bottom begins","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p250-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.1: the whole explanation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.250–258<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Section 7.1 opens with Horikita storming the lounge for the full story; he gives it on one condition — she never investigates him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What do these test results mean? What in the world happened?”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You look like you don’t have any idea at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I just can’t imagine it. I don’t understand it at all. I have a mountain of questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>100 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Untagged; it answers her question in his own viewpoint, so it is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll tell you everything. However, my one condition is that you stay quiet on this matter. I won’t compromise on this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Sets the price of the story: her silence, with no compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What would you like to ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What were you doing during the test? Tell me,” she said.<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the special test was announced, I didn’t focus on anything except for the additional rules. I roughly understood how to manage the 300 points, but you couldn’t manipulate them as an individual.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But the additional rules were really difficult to understand. If you did things normally, you wouldn’t have been able to identify the leaders. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. First of all, I volunteered to join the search for the base camp. Able to move freely, I planned to search out spot locations ahead of everyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You make it sound simple, but no one should have known the spot locations.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not true. You didn’t understand because you were ill and holed up inside the ship, but the school already gave us hints about the locations when we were sailing around the island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The circling ship — nearly three times a usual cruise’s speed — and the phrase “significant scenery” were the school’s hints about the spot locations; Katsuragi and Kōenji had noticed the same hint.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then, I reached the cave. I thought it was the most important base.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The cave was the most important base? Don’t you think that the river and the well would have been more convenient, though?”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The spot itself wasn’t what was important. Its location was.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The cave matters because the hut and the tower — two spots — sit near it, a perfect place to exercise control.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what advantage is there in going into the cave if you don’t have a keycard?”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’d intended to explore various things, but in the end I discovered the leader’s identity.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I suppose that Katsuragi-kun was careless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that wasn’t it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There was that guy, Yahiko, remember? The one following Katsuragi around? He was the leader. I saw Katsuragi and Yahiko at the cave, but I didn’t see the moment they occupied it. After the two of them walked away, I checked if the cave was occupied or not.”<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Totsuka Yahiko was Class A’s leader; Katsuragi only displayed the card while the two were at the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wouldn’t you have mistaken Katsuragi-kun as the leader?” she asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think that the leader would have shown off the card so carelessly in front of people?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But why? Why bother deliberately holding onto the card, then?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because he didn’t have any other choice. As far as I can tell, Katsuragi is a calm and collected man, excessively cautious. There’s no way he didn’t understand the high risk of occupying a spot immediately after finding it. In other words, the person who occupied it was enticed by shortsighted greed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s…why there was another person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The explanation then continues as narration: when Katsuragi found the cave he did not intend to occupy it, but held the space down because Yahiko had been careless, wanting insurance by displaying the card so a witness could be misled into taking him for the leader. The sentences are the page’s, not a spoken quotation.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, aside from their base, Class A held down at least two spots, but we didn’t confirm how many they were occupying by the end of the test. If I correctly guessed the identity of their leader, though, I could invalidate all of their points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m still not convinced. If he figured out the spot’s location at such an early stage, and if he were acting alongside a lot of other people, shouldn’t he have avoided trouble? Even if he just had someone standing watch by the cave, it should have been sufficient claim of ownership. Why would they occupy it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was probably Class A’s disadvantage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Their class appears perfect at first glance, but it actually has a huge schism in it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Class A’s internal schism is the reason Katsuragi could not rely on other people — why the methods revealed Class A so easily.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s why I excluded Class A at that stage, and turned my attention toward Class C. Katsuragi was easy to understand, but with Ryuuen, there were many unknown variables. To tell you the truth, he was gathering more information than I was. He’d found out the identities of all of the leaders.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Read as the variable with more information than himself — the identities of all the leaders in hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait, he found out the identities of all of the leaders… So not only Class D, but also the leaders for Classes B and A? But that’s strange. We were far from being penalized; we ended up getting first place by a wide margin. How do you intend to explain that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a little difficult to explain, but the reason I made you retire is the answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, the answer is you made me retire? What in the world did you do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, that reminds me. I didn’t return it to the school yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes a single card out of his pocket and hands it to Horikita; the engraved name reads “Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a keycard. Why do you…?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, why does…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The leader card in his pocket bears his own name.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The test had to be fair. The rules were fundamentally created to be fair.”<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He then asks what would happen if a leader retired because of poor health; the sentence breaks across the page and is left unquoted.<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s… The leader would be absent. So the rights of exclusive possession would disappear…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wrong. In the manual, it says, ‘It is impossible to change the leader without suitable justification.’ Don’t you think that retirement is suitable enough justification?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The manual’s leader-change clause — retirement is suitable justification; the additional rules were made to be broken when someone is out through poor health or injury, with the base-camp clause as the parallel case.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So then, you made me…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Horikita Suzune retired and he was appointed in her place — the leader the other classes were supposed to guess at the end, there can only be one.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s why even though Class C knew you were the leader, we avoided penalties.”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But wait. Ibuki-san stole my card, but what if I’d protected it really thoroughly?”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you drop the card on purpose back then? Well, I suppose that Yamauchi-kun’s actions might have provided Ibuki-san the opportunity to hatch a plan to steal the keycard…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The mud bribe read back as the opening that let Ibuki take the card.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unless I knew what Ibuki-san was aiming for right at the start, I couldn’t have done anything…”<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki was picked up by Class D, but not by chance — the near-coincidence of two people saved by two separate classes dissolved once Kaneda in Class B came out as a spy Ryuuen had sent.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, Ibuki has a habit of looking people in the eye when she’s lying.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The bigger the lie, the more obvious the habit — she looked him straight in the eye even over the underwear theft.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, when she lied she would look the person in the eye? Isn’t it usually the opposite?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Generally speaking, you avoid eye contact if you have a guilty conscience. However, it was the opposite for her. I think that she made eye contact to make the person think that the lie was the truth. She probably didn’t even notice it herself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Her goal was probably to find the keycard, but she might have intended to disrupt Class D at the same time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I have to wonder why Ibuki-san specifically stole my keycard. All she needed was to check my name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That was likely Ibuki’s intention from the start. However, she ran into unexpected trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki carried a digital camera to take a picture of the keycard; a photo would have made the leader’s identity clear to anyone and let her profit.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To take a picture…with the camera? Why would she go so far?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If she had a picture, then the leader’s identity would have been clear for anyone to see, right? If she had convincing evidence, she would have profited.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t quite understand… Did Ryuuen-kun not trust Ibuki-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That wasn’t it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The rest of the answer — had the discussion stayed inside Class C there would have been no need for the picture or the card theft — breaks across the page and is left unquoted.<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> People outside Class C did not trust Ibuki’s word alone — they wanted reliable evidence, which is why the camera and the card theft existed.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From here on out, I don’t have any evidence of what I’m saying. Think of it as my intuition, which I derived from the test results. At the end of the test, Class A had 270 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> His own label: intuition from the results, with no evidence — Class A ended the test with 270 points and had not used a single one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Classes A and C were connected behind the scenes: Class C sacrificed its own points and bought whatever Class A needed, and by taking all of C’s tools Class A spent the week without using any points — Ibuki’s evidence went to someone in Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, I became aware of Class C’s leader after half of the students retired. It was certain that the leader would have remained on the island, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even so, we weren’t supposed to know who was left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I was almost one hundred percent sure that Ryuuen was still on the island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Ibuki hiding a wireless transceiver in the ground proved someone was left on the island for her to contact; Ryuuen set it on a table unguarded while on vacation — no one else controlled it, and his mistake was trusting no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My god… I don’t even have the words,” Horikita answered, facing the truth.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The test in one line: Class A failed on its internal rift, Class B ran defense-only and paid for believing Kaneda, Class C sent spies and negotiated with A, and Class D avoided damage because he had been appointed the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Named the number one enemy — spies for the leaders’ identities plus whatever the Class A negotiations bought.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t like this. You completely used me, like a pawn.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I can’t deny that. I wouldn’t be surprised if you never want to speak to me ever again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accepts the charge without defense; he was aware of what he had done.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I’ll be heading back to my room now. I’m really tired,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. We’re not done talking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What? I just want to relax in my room, if possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After you explain everything. There are still some things we need to talk about, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well…like what?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The reason why you participated in this special test. Was it to fight alone? I don’t care that you used me this time. I want to know why you put in the effort when you dislike trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her real question is his principles, not the test — the explanation so far was the less important part to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t have any room for doubt. I understand your talents now. If you help me, aiming for Class A seems a realistic enough goal. But what are your principles? Why did you do this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Names her own goal with him in it: Class A, realistically, if his principles hold.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because I was touched that you tried to fight all alone when you were ill.”<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You wouldn’t normally say that kind of thing. It’s easy to spot the lie.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, what I mean is I don’t feel like explaining it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t mind helping you get up to Class A. However, I have one condition. Do not investigate me. If you promise not to touch on this subject ever again, I will help you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The deal is struck: his help toward Class A in exchange for his past staying buried.<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you don’t want to talk, there’s nothing I can really do about that. If you’ll help, I have no reason to refuse you. I’m not interested in digging things up that are better left buried. After all, you dislike trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Takes her hand without hesitation; the handshake is firm — “I work for me. You do things for yourself.” — and the battle to raise the class from the bottom begins.<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p248-1\">← Before: Ch.7: the Icarus talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 0  the cabin reverie and the horikita bridge three days after the island test  the cruise ship respite  ayanokoji s cabin reverie  hirata s interruption  and the deck lunch that follows  the rule he entered school under   contact with anyone outside is forbidden until graduation  chabashira s leverage rides on it   she threatened to expel him from this paradise unless he works toward class a  a  little devil  perched on his shoulder whispers that  it s better to get them before they get you  he spends a second imagining forcing chabashira to resign  then returns to blank thinking   sigh  if only i had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself  rates the boys aboard as  beasts sex starved carnivores  waiting like predators while the girls chatter   his anthropology of the vacation mood   i ll pass  i don t think i m on especially good terms with karuizawa s group  grades the friendship tiers  at the bottom strata   low level friends are only invited ten percent of the time    and he is the lowly friend   well  i don t particularly dislike the idea  but  didn t you already promise karuizawa  asks after karuizawa s recovered underwear and is satisfied with hirata s quiet resolution of the fiasco  reads hirata s invitation as carrying  some kind of ulterior motive  before the ask lands   but even if i can bring you both together  things won t be that easy  horikita is difficult  takes the go between job while admitting he usually just goes along with whatever horikita says    i ve never really forced my opinion on her  executes his  speedy escape  the moment karuizawa s group closes ranks over hirata  pressed into service as the horikita bridge over lunch  he takes the ask but not the urgency  declines her group  then watches her reclaim hirata anyway  the subject of hirata s request  he warns she will shut down if she senses manipulation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.12–20<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three days after the island test, the cruise-ship respite; Ayanokōji’s cabin reverie, Hirata’s interruption, and the deck lunch that follows.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sigh. If only I had the power to rotate the earth on its axis myself…”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll pass. I don’t think I’m on especially good terms with Karuizawa’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I don’t particularly dislike the idea, but… Didn’t you already promise Karuizawa?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The rule he entered school under: “Contact with anyone outside is forbidden until graduation.” Chabashira’s leverage rides on it — she threatened to expel him from this paradise unless he works toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A “little devil” perched on his shoulder whispers that “It’s better to get them before they get you”; he spends a second imagining forcing Chabashira to resign, then returns to blank thinking.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rates the boys aboard as “beasts—sex-starved carnivores” waiting like predators while the girls chatter — his anthropology of the vacation mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Grades the friendship tiers: at the bottom strata, “low-level friends are only invited ten percent of the time” — and he is the lowly friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Asks after Karuizawa’s recovered underwear and is satisfied with Hirata’s quiet resolution of the fiasco.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Hirata’s invitation as carrying “some kind of ulterior motive” before the ask lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But even if I can bring you both together, things won’t be that easy. Horikita is difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Takes the go-between job while admitting he usually just goes along with whatever Horikita says — “I’ve never really forced my opinion on her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Executes his “Speedy Escape” the moment Karuizawa’s group closes ranks over Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pressed into service as the Horikita bridge over lunch; he takes the ask but not the urgency.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Declines her group, then watches her reclaim Hirata anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.14, 20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The subject of Hirata’s request; he warns she will shut down if she senses manipulation.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  the koenji corridor and sakura s call corridor on the third deck  koenji dripping from the pool  the bellhop s fourth warning  and ayanokoji s escape route   do you want something from me  throws the bellhop s warning back at koenji    i passed the ball  if you will    to engineer his own escape  reads the ship s signboard map and fixes the layout in his head  nine decks plus a roof  guys on the third deck and girls on the fourth  the 24 hour lounge on the first  takes sakura s email call rather than kill time alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.21–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Corridor on the third deck: Kōenji dripping from the pool, the bellhop’s fourth warning, and Ayanokōji’s escape route.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you want something from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Throws the bellhop’s warning back at Kōenji — “I passed the ball, if you will” — to engineer his own escape.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the ship’s signboard map and fixes the layout in his head: nine decks plus a roof, guys on the third deck and girls on the fourth, the 24-hour lounge on the first.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes Sakura’s email call rather than kill time alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.0: the cabin reverie and the Horikita bridge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2  sakura s worry  kushida s interrupt  the school message second deck hallway  sakura s roommate appeal  kushida s interruption  the school s test message  and the chat with horikita  ship cabin roommates  hirata  koenji  and yukimura   sakura states it  he doesn t dispute it   you re worried because even though you want to get along with them  you don t think you can   it s no big deal  i don t mind it when you come to me for advice  whether i ll be of much help is another story   i m joking  don t you know by now that i m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff  compares messages with kushida  his call is 18 00  hers 20 40  her room two doors down from his   did you get a message from the school just now   chat line  the corpus prints it bare after  i typed   yeah  i did   untagged chat reply  the thread has only these two   my designated meeting time is 18 00  what about yours   chat   mine says 20 40  that seems like a pretty big difference   untagged chat reply   because your time is earlier  i look forward to hearing your report   untagged chat reply  the narration marks her replies instant   understood   chat  notes horikita s instant replies as unusual   she normally waits half a day  sometimes days  to read  keeps the horikita chat to himself when kushida draws near  deciding to wait and see  refuses her class c outing  lets her see the phone  shares nothing about the chat  receives her roommate appeal  can only offer limited help","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.26–31<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second-deck hallway: Sakura’s roommate appeal, Kushida’s interruption, the school’s test message, and the chat with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re worried because even though you want to get along with them, you don’t think you can?”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s no big deal. I don’t mind it when you come to me for advice. Whether I’ll be of much help is another story.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m joking. Don’t you know by now that I’m not the sort of person who joins in on stuff?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Ship cabin roommates: Hirata, Kōenji, and Yukimura — Sakura states it; he doesn’t dispute it.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Compares messages with Kushida: his call is 18:00, hers 20:40, her room two doors down from his.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you get a message from the school just now?” (chat line; the corpus prints it bare after “I typed.”)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I did.” (untagged chat reply; the thread has only these two)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My designated meeting time is 18:00. What about yours?” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Mine says 20:40. That seems like a pretty big difference.” (untagged chat reply)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because your time is earlier, I look forward to hearing your report.” (untagged chat reply; the narration marks her replies instant)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood.” (chat)<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Horikita’s instant replies as unusual — she normally waits half a day, sometimes days, to read.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps the Horikita chat to himself when Kushida draws near, deciding to wait and see.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Refuses her Class C outing, lets her see the phone, shares nothing about the chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Receives her roommate appeal; can only offer limited help.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the Kōenji corridor and Sakura’s call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action","w":"sotomura-hideo yukimura-teruhiko mashima-tomonari karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  the zodiac briefing opens room 204 on the second deck  mashima s briefing table  sotomura and yukimura already seated  karuizawa as the late fourth  takes the vacant seat beside yukimura and waits out the unseen fourth member  reads the setup as ominous   small groups  private rooms  a teacher who won t take questions   there was a storm coming  the curtain rising on a new test  classmate at the table  the professor greets him with  ayanokouji dono  the roommate beside him  he stays quiet while yukimura and karuizawa trade blows  the briefer  cold  unanswerable   impossible to read  the fourth member  she moves her chair away from him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.32–36<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Room 204 on the second deck: Mashima’s briefing table, Sotomura and Yukimura already seated, Karuizawa as the late fourth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Takes the vacant seat beside Yukimura and waits out the unseen fourth member.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the setup as ominous — small groups, private rooms, a teacher who won’t take questions: “There was a storm coming, the curtain rising on a new test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Classmate at the table; the Professor greets him with “Ayanokouji-dono.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The roommate beside him; he stays quiet while Yukimura and Karuizawa trade blows.<span class=\"pg\">p.32, 36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer: cold, unanswerable, “impossible to read.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The fourth member; she moves her chair away from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: Sakura’s worry, Kushida’s interrupt, the school message<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  the four outcomes and the traitor rules still at mashima s table  the group roster  the handout of four outcomes  and the werewolf detour  all read through ayanokoji s eyes   karuizawa  if you don t change your attitude toward the teachers  it might leave a mark on your permanent record  that wouldn t be good  right  depressed hearing karuizawa rank the three of them below hirata  though he tries not to care  knows ichinose from class b and ibuki from class c off the printed roster  of ibuki he thinks being in the same group  was a perverse kind of fate  has never heard of the party game werewolf   karuizawa s amazement lands on genuine ignorance  reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head  with answers accepted any time  no one would seriously aim for outcome  1  reduces the exam to four possibilities   the honest outcome  1  a wrong guess at the end  the traitor finding the vip  and the traitor misled   and wants to avoid the last one most of all  easily memorizes the prohibited actions list  phone theft  threats for vip information  impersonation by borrowed phone  and cross class discussion until the exam ends   each punishable up to expulsion  notes the school s anonymity design means any school sent message is  100  the truth  warns her about her permanent record  she brushes it off  the briefer he watches absorb karuizawa s interruptions without expression","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.37–49<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Still at Mashima’s table: the group roster, the handout of four outcomes, and the Werewolf detour, all read through Ayanokōji’s eyes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Karuizawa, if you don’t change your attitude toward the teachers, it might leave a mark on your permanent record. That wouldn’t be good, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Reads the traitor rules as flipping the test on its head: with answers accepted any time, no one would seriously aim for Outcome #1.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Reduces the exam to four possibilities — the honest Outcome #1, a wrong guess at the end, the traitor finding the VIP, and the traitor misled — and wants to avoid the last one most of all.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Depressed hearing Karuizawa rank the three of them below Hirata, though he tries not to care.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Knows Ichinose from Class B and Ibuki from Class C off the printed roster; of Ibuki he thinks being in the same group “was a perverse kind of fate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has never heard of the party game Werewolf — Karuizawa’s amazement lands on genuine ignorance.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Easily memorizes the prohibited-actions list: phone theft, threats for VIP information, impersonation by borrowed phone, and cross-class discussion until the exam ends — each punishable up to expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the school’s anonymity design means any school-sent message is “100% the truth.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns her about her permanent record; she brushes it off.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The briefer he watches absorb Karuizawa’s interruptions without expression.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the zodiac briefing opens<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the hallway split<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  the hallway split leaving mashima s room  yukimura s huddle plan collapses when karuizawa calls hirata and the professor declines   for the most part  i guess  i d like you to explain the things i don t fully understand later  though   to yukimura  who asked whether he understood  feigns incompleteness on purpose    i wasn t going to tell hirata anything more  in the later hallway talk   and lets yukimura s discontent pass unnoticed  agrees the ship may be bugged  accepts yukimura s secure location plan in principle  then reports the rabbit rules to horikita by chat and starts shaping a strategy alone  the one classmate who tries to build a three man huddle with him  yukimura sighs and drops it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the hallway split<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.50–51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaving Mashima’s room: Yukimura’s huddle plan collapses when Karuizawa calls Hirata and the Professor declines.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“For the most part, I guess. I’d like you to explain the things I don’t fully understand later, though.” (to Yukimura, who asked whether he understood)<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Feigns incompleteness on purpose — “I wasn’t going to tell Hirata anything more” in the later hallway talk — and lets Yukimura’s discontent pass unnoticed.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Agrees the ship may be bugged, accepts Yukimura’s secure-location plan in principle, then reports the Rabbit rules to Horikita by chat and starts shaping a strategy alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The one classmate who tries to build a three-man huddle with him; Yukimura sighs and drops it.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p37-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the four outcomes and the traitor rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 4  the wake up and the scattered explanations just before 20 30 he wakes in the third deck cabin to hirata s apology  and they step out together toward the evening s meetings   can t really say  i haven t been thinking about the exam like you  horikita  and yukimura have  i m not smart  either  so i haven t really noticed much   deflecting hirata s request for observations   yeah  i think you re right  hirata  it would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time  rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages  suspects the school s deliberately scattered briefings mean their  thinking  is already being tested  walks him to the second deck while sharing nothing of substance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.52–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Just before 20:30 he wakes in the third-deck cabin to Hirata’s apology, and they step out together toward the evening’s meetings.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Can’t really say. I haven’t been thinking about the exam like you, Horikita, and Yukimura have. I’m not smart, either, so I haven’t really noticed much.” (deflecting Hirata’s request for observations)<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah, I think you’re right, Hirata. It would definitely be more efficient to explain the test to all the students at the same time, rather than dividing us into groups and doing it in stages.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Suspects the school’s deliberately scattered briefings mean their “thinking” is already being tested.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Walks him to the second deck while sharing nothing of substance.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p50-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the hallway split<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 5  the 20 40 gathering at the second deck meeting place he watches katsuragi confront horikita  kanzaki intercede  ryuen prowl  and kushida arrive puzzled   who are those people   asking hirata to name the waiting students  burns morimiya and tokito s names and faces into memory on hirata s tip  then keeps to the line without making a fuss  notes katsuragi s entourage and horikita s changed standing  other classes now see her as  a puppet master  a mastermind who worked behind the scenes  credits horikita s cold shoulder resilience   the island win is his  but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden  expects a huge showdown between katsuragi and ryuen before the test begins  it doesn t come   well then  good luck   leaving hirata at the gathering  stands by as katsuragi threatens her class and kanzaki pulls him off  impressed she won t be shaken  watches the class a leader pivot from ignoring horikita to warning her  notes the demented chuckle and the docile lackeys trailing him  present when she wanders into the gathering  puzzled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.54–61<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the second-deck meeting place he watches Katsuragi confront Horikita, Kanzaki intercede, Ryūen prowl, and Kushida arrive puzzled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Who are those people?” (asking Hirata to name the waiting students)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Notes Katsuragi’s entourage and Horikita’s changed standing: other classes now see her as “a puppet master, a mastermind who worked behind the scenes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well then, good luck.” (leaving Hirata at the gathering)<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Burns Morimiya and Tokitō’s names and faces into memory on Hirata’s tip, then keeps to the line without making a fuss.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Credits Horikita’s cold-shoulder resilience — the island win is his, but she took the spotlight to keep him hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Expects a huge showdown between Katsuragi and Ryūen before the test begins; it doesn’t come.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Stands by as Katsuragi threatens her class and Kanzaki pulls him off; impressed she won’t be shaken.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Watches the Class A leader pivot from ignoring Horikita to warning her.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Notes the demented chuckle and the docile lackeys trailing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Present when she wanders into the gathering, puzzled.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: the wake-up and the scattered explanations<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 0  the 8 00 cafe and the ryuen interrupt blue ocean cafe on the ship s deck at 7 55   he meets horikita for the 8 00 vip message  then ryuen and ibuki sit down uninvited and pick at the island result until the coffee is done   i was waiting for an hour   teasing horikita  she arrived before the designated time anyway   i see  this really seems like an inevitable grouping   reading horikita s dragon list  reads the dragon roster as a  dream team  of class representatives   katsuragi  kanzaki  ryuuen   and a death match  notes koenji s abundance would not be contributed   but there s probably a gap between me and the professor  same as you and hirata  there are too many details that don t fit the score theory   i suppose neither of us was chosen  then   yeah  if you re chosen  then you could lead your group to any of the outcomes  weighs the vip s edge at 500 000 points and calls the school s  no disadvantages  line a lie   without the vip in the class the point gap widens   there are some things i can t yet see  like how some of the students i don t know will react  i won t know until i meet with them directly  but i thought of a way to lead us to victory   me too  can t wait to see what you do with your group  i answered   answering horikita s wish to see his results   ryuuen  i answered   his answer to who he is most wary of   of course  considering he s only a first year student  he s excellent  if you d asked me who the most excellent student was  then katsuragi would ve been my answer  but if you re asking who i m wary of  then it s ryuuen  by a mile  i answered  marks mashima s earlier  after thorough consideration  phrasing as proof the vip was chosen by a rule  not a roll  silences horikita with a finger on her lips the moment ryuen s shadow appears   i think we were being spied on  him suddenly meeting up with us is too convenient  i said   maybe she was forced to keep an eye on us  or maybe she just happened to see us by chance  if that s the case  it would help us  i said   a mistake  i muttered   after ryuen s  someone just like him  line lands too easily   i think we re done for the time being  i m still sleepy  so i m going to head back to my room  i muttered  works the whole cafe as cover  feeds horikita the strategy he will not show ryuen  then reads the encounter as a possible leak and files it away  the morning partner  he teases  trades wary lists  and parts with her report request  faces the man he called his top wary name  knows ryuen suspects him and that the meeting itself may have given the hint away  she is his rabbit groupmate and  he suspects  ryuen s lookout  names him the most excellent first year  but not the one he fears","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.63–77<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Blue Ocean café on the ship’s deck at 7:55 — he meets Horikita for the 8:00 VIP message, then Ryūen and Ibuki sit down uninvited and pick at the island result until the coffee is done.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I was waiting for an hour.” (teasing Horikita; she arrived before the designated time anyway)<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I see. This really seems like an inevitable grouping,” (reading Horikita’s Dragon list)<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But there’s probably a gap between me and the Professor, same as you and Hirata. There are too many details that don’t fit the score theory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the Dragon roster as a “dream team” of class representatives — Katsuragi, Kanzaki, Ryuuen — and a death match; notes Kōenji’s abundance would not be contributed.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose neither of us was chosen, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. If you’re chosen, then you could lead your group to any of the outcomes,”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Weighs the VIP’s edge at 500,000 points and calls the school’s “no disadvantages” line a lie — without the VIP in the class the point gap widens.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are some things I can’t yet see, like how some of the students I don’t know will react. I won’t know until I meet with them directly. But I thought of a way to lead us to victory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me too. Can’t wait to see what you do with your group,” I answered. (answering Horikita’s wish to see his results)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen,” I answered. (his answer to who he is most wary of)<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. Considering he’s only a first-year student, he’s excellent. If you’d asked me who the most excellent student was, then Katsuragi would’ve been my answer. But if you’re asking who I’m wary of, then it’s Ryuuen, by a mile,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Marks Mashima’s earlier “after thorough consideration” phrasing as proof the VIP was chosen by a rule, not a roll.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Silences Horikita with a finger on her lips the moment Ryūen’s shadow appears.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think we were being spied on. Him suddenly meeting up with us is too convenient,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe she was forced to keep an eye on us, or maybe she just happened to see us by chance. If that’s the case, it would help us,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A mistake,” I muttered. (after Ryūen’s “someone just like him” line lands too easily)<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think we’re done for the time being. I’m still sleepy, so I’m going to head back to my room,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Works the whole café as cover: feeds Horikita the strategy he will not show Ryūen, then reads the encounter as a possible leak and files it away.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The morning partner; he teases, trades wary-lists, and parts with her report request.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Faces the man he called his top wary name; knows Ryūen suspects him and that the meeting itself may have given the hint away.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> She is his Rabbit groupmate and, he suspects, Ryūen’s lookout.<span class=\"pg\">p.68, 76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Names him the most excellent first-year, but not the one he fears.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the 20:40 gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  observing the rabbit group meets yukimura and the professor outside the rabbit room  then sits through the first group discussion as ichinose and machida trade katsuragi s no discussion plan   no  i don t have a favorite speech pattern or anything  not especially  anyway  i answered   to the professor s moe dialect question   well  professor  what about you  do you have a speech pattern you like  i asked  follows the professor s dialect ranking as a way to kill time before the room fills   it s nothing  i said   on why karuizawa and ibuki sit apart   he expected a fight over the stolen underwear  notes the eleven person circle  the class clusters  and that karuizawa and ibuki isolate themselves  recognizes the class a boy who once offered him a deal to betray class d  jumps into the opening vote to bind the professor on camera   what do you say  professor   i agree  too  we re a group  like you said  and we could all use some private points  if it s possible  i d like us to work together  what do you say  professor  reads ichinose s  assume that no one here is the vip  as a narrowing question and clocks the answer order   ichinose  karuizawa  yukimura  manabe  hamaguchi   as the first suspect list   i mean  the strategy s fine  besides  i think most people here agree  and i ve never been good at talking  i answered  publicly backs katsuragi s plan while privately sure it is hiding something  lays low for the rest of the session  judges the room s low communication types as reactive and refuses to get impatient  watches her take the lead  tests her with the professor  and is last in her roll call  sits through the class a pitch and the silent withdrawal  notes the class b counter that holds the middle of the room  present when she turns on karuizawa with the rika charge  shares the room with her  sees her vote  her bluntness  and the phone slap that ends the half  walks in with him  tracks his swing from the convenient plan to ichinose  the dialect small talk partner outside  then the vote he drags the professor into","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.78–93<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Yukimura and the Professor outside the Rabbit room, then sits through the first group discussion as Ichinose and Machida trade Katsuragi’s no-discussion plan.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, I don’t have a favorite speech pattern or anything. Not especially, anyway,” I answered. (to the Professor’s moe-dialect question)<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, Professor, what about you? Do you have a speech pattern you like?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s nothing,” I said. (on why Karuizawa and Ibuki sit apart — he expected a fight over the stolen underwear)<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Follows the Professor’s dialect ranking as a way to kill time before the room fills.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the eleven-person circle, the class clusters, and that Karuizawa and Ibuki isolate themselves; recognizes the Class A boy who once offered him a deal to betray Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Jumps into the opening vote to bind the Professor on camera: “What do you say, Professor?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I agree, too. We’re a group, like you said, and we could all use some private points. If it’s possible, I’d like us to work together. What do you say, Professor?”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Ichinose’s “assume that no one here is the VIP” as a narrowing question and clocks the answer order — Ichinose, Karuizawa, Yukimura, Manabe, Hamaguchi — as the first suspect list.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean, the strategy’s fine. Besides, I think most people here agree, and I’ve never been good at talking,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Publicly backs Katsuragi’s plan while privately sure it is hiding something; lays low for the rest of the session.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges the room’s low-communication types as reactive and refuses to get impatient.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Watches her take the lead, tests her with the Professor, and is last in her roll call.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Sits through the Class A pitch and the silent withdrawal.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Notes the Class B counter that holds the middle of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Present when she turns on Karuizawa with the Rika charge.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Shares the room with her; sees her vote, her bluntness, and the phone slap that ends the half.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Walks in with him; tracks his swing from the convenient plan to Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The dialect small-talk partner outside, then the vote he drags the Professor into.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.0: the 8:00 café and the Ryūen interrupt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 2  the first discussion breaks up watches the manabe karuizawa phone fight resolve through machida s intervention  then leaves with the group and decides to pull sakura for a second opinion on the test  stays out of the middle of manabe s glare    i didn t want to get caught in the middle of anything  so i averted my eyes and got out of there   well  we re heading back  too  i want to talk to hirata about some things  i said   cover for slipping away   hey  yukimura  wasn t karuizawa acting strangely  i asked   hmm  perfect timing  i murmured   sakura s instant message  wants opinions from people other than hirata and horikita    i d probably gain insight after learning more about sakura s group  keeps clear of her after the phone slap  reads the fear under her tough girl act as off  then asks yukimura about it  answers her meet up message and heads for the bow  asks him first about karuizawa s mood","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.94–97<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches the Manabe–Karuizawa phone fight resolve through Machida’s intervention, then leaves with the group and decides to pull Sakura for a second opinion on the test.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, we’re heading back, too. I want to talk to Hirata about some things,” I said. (cover for slipping away)<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hey, Yukimura. Wasn’t Karuizawa acting strangely?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hmm. Perfect timing,” I murmured. (Sakura’s instant message)<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays out of the middle of Manabe’s glare — “I didn’t want to get caught in the middle of anything, so I averted my eyes and got out of there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wants opinions from people other than Hirata and Horikita — “I’d probably gain insight after learning more about Sakura’s group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Keeps clear of her after the phone slap.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Reads the fear under her tough-girl act as off, then asks Yukimura about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.94, 97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Answers her meet-up message and heads for the bow.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Asks him first about Karuizawa’s mood.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: observing the Rabbit group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 2  the bow with sakura meets sakura behind a pillar on the quiet bow deck  she stress mutters  hands him the cow group list  and they compete over who has fewer friends   sakura  what s the matter  i asked  trying not to surprise her   i didn t really hear anything  i just got here now   so  why did you call me out here  i asked  reads the cow roster   sawada  shimizu  nishi  yoshida   kobashi  ninomiya  watanabe   tokitou  nomura  yashima   ike  sakura  sudou  matsushita   and feels sympathy for her with sudou and ike as the class d boys  weighs helping her secretly against acting unnaturally   in a test like this  breaking the rules could mean death   sorry  i don t really have any friends  either  i said   by the way  there was something i wanted to ask you  sakura   has yamauchi gotten in touch with you at all since the discussion ended  island after action  he used sakura while using horikita  and manipulated yamauchi with a promise of her email he had not yet asked her for    since i d planted the seeds myself  if yamauchi made a move  i would have to act   for the time being  contact me if something s bothering you  you can tell me anything  i said   yeah  that s the least i can do  watches her develop quickly since the island   more assertive  eyes sparkling   and notes she has learned to stay positive without transforming completely  the loner pact and the standing contact offer  the unasked for favour that is about to explode  one of only two people who could help sakura from another class   already taken by his own group  the other name  not available either","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.97–102<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Sakura behind a pillar on the quiet bow deck; she stress-mutters, hands him the Cow group list, and they compete over who has fewer friends.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sakura? What’s the matter?” I asked, trying not to surprise her.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I didn’t really hear anything. I just got here now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, why did you call me out here?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the Cow roster — Sawada, Shimizu, Nishi, Yoshida / Kobashi, Ninomiya, Watanabe / Tokitou, Nomura, Yashima / Ike, Sakura, Sudou, Matsushita — and feels sympathy for her with Sudou and Ike as the Class D boys.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Weighs helping her secretly against acting unnaturally: “In a test like this, breaking the rules could mean death.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I don’t really have any friends, either,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, there was something I wanted to ask you, Sakura.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Has Yamauchi gotten in touch with you at all since the discussion ended?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Island after-action: he used Sakura while using Horikita, and manipulated Yamauchi with a promise of her email he had not yet asked her for — “Since I’d planted the seeds myself, if Yamauchi made a move, I would have to act.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the time being, contact me if something’s bothering you. You can tell me anything,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. That’s the least I can do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches her develop quickly since the island — more assertive, eyes sparkling — and notes she has learned to stay positive without transforming completely.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The loner pact and the standing contact offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The unasked-for favour that is about to explode.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> One of only two people who could help Sakura from another class — already taken by his own group.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> The other name; not available either.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p94-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: the first discussion breaks up<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 3  the yamauchi redirect choked by yamauchi haruki the moment he re enters the ship  the sakura email lie becomes a camera and points pep talk   wh what s the matter  i knew the reason  but asked as a formality   i never meant to go after her  well  this is kind of hard to say  but i lied to you before  i croaked   do you really think that a loner like me would know sakura s email address  i turned toward him  trying to show my sincerity   yeah  sorry   can you give me just a little more time  i asked   then are you going to make sakura tell you  i asked   you know  sakura said she hates guys that are all talk   of course she hates me  but it should be obvious why i couldn t give you her contact information  i don t want you to make the same mistake i did  yamauchi  if you forcibly asked her  it wouldn t go anywhere  it d be pointless   yeah  and i m sorry  but i know for sure that she doesn t hate you  i answered   did you know that sakura loves digital cameras  i ve heard that her camera doesn t work  and she doesn t have enough points to buy a new one  but what if you got one for her  yamauchi  if you gave it to her as a present  i asked   well  there a few options in this special test  if you were the vip and managed to make it through without being found out  or if you became a traitor and sold out your group  or if you managed to guide your group to clear the test  you d get enough points to buy tons of digital cameras  right   now  yamauchi haruki  you need to achieve real results  work hard  and show sakura how manly you are  only then would you be a guy who deserves to go out with a former idol   that s right  yamauchi  you can definitely do it  redirects the rage into the test as  a temporary fix  worries yamauchi might get too fired up and miss the vip  then deliberately withholds the caution   a missed target is fine  the bigger picture matters more  the mark  the lie  and the stimulus  her camera and her idol past become the bait  her contact stays protected","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.103–105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Choked by Yamauchi Haruki the moment he re-enters the ship; the Sakura-email lie becomes a camera-and-points pep talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wh-what’s the matter?” I knew the reason, but asked as a formality.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I never meant to go after her. Well, this is kind of hard to say, but…I lied to you before,” I croaked.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Do you really think that a loner like me would know Sakura’s email address?” I turned toward him, trying to show my sincerity.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you give me just a little more time?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then are you going to make Sakura tell you?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, Sakura said she hates guys that are all talk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course she hates me. But it should be obvious why I couldn’t give you her contact information. I don’t want you to make the same mistake I did, Yamauchi. If you forcibly asked her, it wouldn’t go anywhere. It’d be pointless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. And I’m sorry. But I know for sure that she doesn’t hate you,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you know that Sakura loves digital cameras? I’ve heard that her camera doesn’t work, and she doesn’t have enough points to buy a new one. But what if you got one for her, Yamauchi? If you gave it to her as a present?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there a few options in this special test. If you were the VIP and managed to make it through without being found out, or if you became a traitor and sold out your group, or if you managed to guide your group to clear the test, you’d get enough points to buy tons of digital cameras. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Now, Yamauchi Haruki, you need to achieve real results. Work hard, and show Sakura how manly you are. Only then would you be a guy who deserves to go out with a former idol.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right, Yamauchi. You can definitely do it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Redirects the rage into the test as “a temporary fix”; worries Yamauchi might get too fired up and miss the VIP, then deliberately withholds the caution — a missed target is fine, the bigger picture matters more.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The mark, the lie, and the stimulus.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her camera and her idol past become the bait; her contact stays protected.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: the bow with Sakura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei machida-kouji hamaguchi-tetsuya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 4  the second gathering and the manabe fuse sits the gloomy second rabbit discussion with class a absent  watches ichinose bait machida  then lies to manabe about seeing karuizawa fight to light a fuse  reads the alliance map  only class a guaranteed advancement  so b d against c a    like putting carnivores and herbivores together in the same cage  notes class a s phone use is legal and calm is katsuragi s maintained image    an exceptionally effective strategy  on being a lone wolf inside class a s walls   to be perfectly honest  i m the type to just sit things out  i m just a bystander  i said   to ichinose  the karuizawa write up  off since the test started   the ibuki reunion  the manabe confrontation  background character quiet where hirata and kushida stay themselves  she is irreplaceable for class d cohesion and he needs to know if she is useful   even if it meant being forceful  trails manabe s group to the elevator and plants the lie   i m not 100  sure  but i think i saw karuizawa fight with a girl from another class  i said  keeps it vague on purpose  had seen nothing and would have been exposed if he kept talking    now that the fuse was lit  manabe and the others would react  how would the newly docile karuizawa respond  i wanted to find out  reads her bait of machida through yukimura and karuizawa  charms him enough that he admits he would have had a crush if she were his classmate  the liar s target  the subject of both the write up and the planted story  watches him take ichinose s bait despite the no talk policy  the class b off switch when the hour ends    no  we didn t do much of anything  well  shall we","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.106–111<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits the gloomy second Rabbit discussion with Class A absent, watches Ichinose bait Machida, then lies to Manabe about seeing Karuizawa fight to light a fuse.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"machida-kouji.html\">Machida Kōji<\/a> · <a href=\"hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“To be perfectly honest, I’m the type to just sit things out. I’m just a bystander,” I said. (to Ichinose)<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the alliance map: only Class A guaranteed advancement, so B+D against C+A — “like putting carnivores and herbivores together in the same cage.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Class A’s phone use is legal and calm is Katsuragi’s maintained image — “an exceptionally effective strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> On being a lone wolf inside Class A’s walls.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The Karuizawa write-up: off since the test started — the Ibuki reunion, the Manabe confrontation, background-character quiet where Hirata and Kushida stay themselves; she is irreplaceable for Class D cohesion and he needs to know if she is useful, “even if it meant being forceful.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Trails Manabe’s group to the elevator and plants the lie: “I’m not 100% sure, but I think I saw Karuizawa fight with a girl from another class,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps it vague on purpose; had seen nothing and would have been exposed if he kept talking — “Now that the fuse was lit, Manabe and the others would react. How would the newly docile Karuizawa respond? I wanted to find out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Reads her bait of Machida through Yukimura and Karuizawa; charms him enough that he admits he would have had a crush if she were his classmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The liar’s target.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The subject of both the write-up and the planted story.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Machida Kōji<\/b> Watches him take Ichinose’s bait despite the no-talk policy.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> The Class B off-switch when the hour ends — “No, we didn’t do much of anything. Well, shall we?”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.3: the Yamauchi redirect<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 5  the cabin  the vip sheet  kouenji s exit returns near midnight to hirata  yukimura and a push uping kouenji  gets the two known vip names by phone  then walks out after kouenji ends the monkey group   yeah  a bit  ah  that reminds me  i wanted to talk to you for a minute  if you have the time   oh no  that s okay  you go first  hirata  we can talk about my thing later  meant to ask hirata about sakayanagi   a popular guy should have information   but waits   what  who  i asked   after hirata s two classmate vip whisper   hey  hirata  wouldn t it be better to give us that information by phone  we don t know who s listening in on our conversations  i said  reads the two names hirata turns the phone toward   dragon kushida  horse minami   then erases them  instant read  kushida as dragon vip is an enormous advantage and terrifying    once they knew her identity  she was at their mercy  admits his own limit  three days left  not enough eyes and ears even with hirata and kushida as ringleaders    it s impossible  i muttered   and resolves to get more people on his side  horikita and sakura included   it s impossible  i muttered   i m stepping out for a bit  i said  the trusted conduit for the vip sheet  rule reader who notes participation penalties  cabin partner  both read the vip math and both erupt at kouenji  watched end his own group with a traitor submission and walk into the bathroom    adieu  named dragon vip on the erased screen  her message   i m sorry  things seem really confusing right now  i m going to give you a call  one of the few eyes and ears he still counts on","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.112–116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns near midnight to Hirata, Yukimura and a push-uping Kouenji; gets the two known VIP names by phone, then walks out after Kouenji ends the Monkey group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah, a bit. Ah, that reminds me. I wanted to talk to you for a minute, if you have the time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh no, that’s okay. You go first, Hirata. We can talk about my thing later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What? Who?” I asked. (after Hirata’s two-classmate VIP whisper)<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Meant to ask Hirata about Sakayanagi — a popular guy should have information — but waits.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hirata. Wouldn’t it be better to give us that information by phone? We don’t know who’s listening in on our conversations,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the two names Hirata turns the phone toward — Dragon/Kushida, Horse/Minami — then erases them.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Instant read: Kushida as Dragon VIP is an enormous advantage and terrifying — “Once they knew her identity, she was at their mercy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Admits his own limit: three days left, not enough eyes and ears even with Hirata and Kushida as ringleaders — “It’s impossible,” I muttered — and resolves to get more people on his side, Horikita and Sakura included.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s impossible,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m stepping out for a bit,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The trusted conduit for the VIP sheet; rule-reader who notes participation penalties.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Cabin partner; both read the VIP math and both erupt at Kouenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Watched end his own group with a traitor submission and walk into the bathroom — “Adieu.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Named Dragon VIP on the erased screen.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her message: “I’m sorry. Things seem really confusing right now. I’m going to give you a call.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> One of the few eyes-and-ears he still counts on.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.4: the second gathering and the Manabe fuse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae hoshinomiya-chie mashima-tomonari ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 6  the starlit hug and the teachers  table wanders the dark deck alone  stumbles into kushida among the couples  takes her sudden hug  then overhears chabashira  hoshinomiya and mashima at the vending machines   that voice  kushida   are you alone  i asked  perhaps she was waiting to meet her boyfriend  just imagining that made my chest tighten and ache   i i see  i answered   aren t you cold  i asked   i m getting tired  that was a total lie  i didn t want to sleep in the slightest   good night  kushida   k k ku kushida  wh what s the matter  i squeaked   when she wraps her arms around his chest  totally flustered    i couldn t understand what was happening    then stands hand on chest with the warmth still there and cannot return to the room  hides and draws nearer to the teachers  sofa at the first level vending machines  overhears the three homeroom teachers  hoshinomiya s date talk  the ten year grudge  ichinose deliberately kept out of dragon and dropped into rabbit  ryuuen thrown into dragon because the class c grades would not justify another pick  and sakagami named as part of the class c evaluation problem  files the reconnaissance   apparently i was under heavy scrutiny    hoshinomiya was watching him from the island endgame onward  the starlit encounter and the hug she apologises for  at the teachers  table  the subject of hoshinomiya s  sae chan  needle  the class b homeroom who admits removing ichinose from dragon and watching him  the third teacher  orders hoshinomiya to stop spying on colleagues  classes  the student hoshinomiya placed in rabbit on purpose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.117–124<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wanders the dark deck alone, stumbles into Kushida among the couples, takes her sudden hug, then overhears Chabashira, Hoshinomiya and Mashima at the vending machines.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“That voice… Kushida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you…alone?” I asked. Perhaps she was waiting to meet her boyfriend. Just imagining that made my chest tighten and ache.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I-I see,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Aren’t you cold?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m getting tired.” That was a total lie. I didn’t want to sleep in the slightest.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good night, Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “K-K-Ku…Kushida? Wh-what’s the matter?” I squeaked. (when she wraps her arms around his chest)<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Totally flustered — “I couldn’t understand what was happening” — then stands hand on chest with the warmth still there and cannot return to the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hides and draws nearer to the teachers’ sofa at the first-level vending machines.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Overhears the three homeroom teachers: Hoshinomiya’s date talk, the ten-year grudge, Ichinose deliberately kept out of Dragon and dropped into Rabbit, Ryuuen thrown into Dragon because the Class C grades would not justify another pick, and Sakagami named as part of the Class C evaluation problem.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Files the reconnaissance: “Apparently I was under heavy scrutiny.” — Hoshinomiya was watching him from the island endgame onward.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The starlit encounter and the hug she apologises for.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> At the teachers’ table; the subject of Hoshinomiya’s “Sae-chan” needle.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> The Class B homeroom who admits removing Ichinose from Dragon and watching him.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The third teacher; orders Hoshinomiya to stop spying on colleagues’ classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The student Hoshinomiya placed in Rabbit on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p112-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.5: the cabin, the VIP sheet, Kouenji’s exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 0  the karuizawa brief and the planted phone face to face with horikita on day two  the kouenji traitor act is public  then he asks her for karuizawa intelligence and a recording phone sits under ryuuen s chair   unfortunately  it s the truth  kouenji just ended the test for his group  i said   that s an impossible task  besides  there s nothing i can do about it now  no use crying over spilt milk   it s true that my group is filled with troublesome opponents  but i ve no intention of falling behind  said horikita   reported  her line  he files ichinose and the class b trio as hoshinomiya s spies on him and keeps the subject off kouenji by changing it   i want information on karuizawa   yes  exactly  i nodded   i d like to know more about the people in my group  but it s not easy  i should be able find out whatever i need to about the professor and yukimura  but i m at a complete loss with karuizawa   there s that  but more than that  i can t understand karuizawa s behavior  that s why i m worried   horikita  i don t think it s good to write people off like that   you and karuizawa don t get along at all because you re both willful  so you see her as nothing more than a nuisance  you understand that she may also have strong points  too  outer inner self lecture   kushida  ibuki  himself as examples  anyone can have a secret self  horikita included  her brother  tagged by narration   but that s still just as superficial as their outside appearance  their innermost thoughts aren t going to be immediately apparent from that  for example  take kushida  ibuki  or even me  there s a difference between a person s outer and inner selves   almost everyone does  they may not be aware of it themselves  you do  too   i still can t really describe it  but so far i d say it s her ability to assume control  she can take the initiative  in fact  her position in class d is unshakeable  in the rabbit group that part of karuizawa stayed hidden   the reason he needs her true nature fast   hey  you two  having yourselves a nice date in the shade  let me in on the fun   ryuuen s approach  reported  lets ryuuen sit in and listen  works the phone under the chair with horikita without commenting on it  reads ryuuen s  fundamentals  speech as the same rule logic as midterms and the island test   he must have noticed the vip class pattern  if ryuuen s claim holds  he already has three vips and probably every class s    a quiz where you could turn the page over and find the answer written on the back  flips ryuuen off after the parting  leaves the recording phone alone   easy for you to say  it s not like i can find them   if you re not expecting too much  i ll do what i can  i answered  plans to mine hirata for dragon group detail instead of horikita   a different perspective  room scene  answers the vip probe  trades mutual denial  notes yukimura warming up while he fakes a chameleon s sociability   even if i did deny it and said you re wrong  what s the point in checking   i see  unfortunately  i m not the vip   i m not the vip  can i believe that you re not the vip  yukimura  yukimura reports karuizawa s denial of the vip role  ayanokoji does not press it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.125–133<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Face-to-face with Horikita on day two; the Kouenji traitor act is public, then he asks her for Karuizawa intelligence and a recording phone sits under Ryuuen’s chair.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Unfortunately, it’s the truth. Kouenji just ended the test for his group,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s an impossible task. Besides, there’s nothing I can do about it now. No use crying over spilt milk.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s true that my group is filled with troublesome opponents, but I’ve no intention of falling behind,” said Horikita. (reported; her line)<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He files Ichinose and the Class B trio as Hoshinomiya’s spies on him and keeps the subject off Kouenji by changing it.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want information on Karuizawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, exactly.” I nodded. “I’d like to know more about the people in my group, but it’s not easy. I should be able find out whatever I need to about the Professor and Yukimura, but I’m at a complete loss with Karuizawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s that. But more than that, I can’t understand Karuizawa’s behavior. That’s why I’m worried.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita, I don’t think it’s good to write people off like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You and Karuizawa don’t get along at all because you’re both willful, so you see her as nothing more than a nuisance. You understand that she may also have strong points, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Outer/inner self lecture — Kushida, Ibuki, himself as examples; anyone can have a secret self, Horikita included (her brother, tagged by narration).<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But that’s still just as superficial as their outside appearance. Their innermost thoughts aren’t going to be immediately apparent from that. For example, take Kushida, Ibuki, or even me. There’s a difference between a person’s outer and inner selves.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Almost everyone does. They may not be aware of it themselves. You do, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I still can’t really describe it, but so far I’d say it’s her ability to assume control. She can take the initiative. In fact, her position in Class D is unshakeable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> In the Rabbit group that part of Karuizawa stayed hidden — the reason he needs her true nature fast.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, you two. Having yourselves a nice date in the shade? Let me in on the fun.” (Ryuuen’s approach, reported)<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Lets Ryuuen sit in and listen; works the phone under the chair with Horikita without commenting on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.128-130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Reads Ryuuen’s “fundamentals” speech as the same rule-logic as midterms and the island test — he must have noticed the VIP-class pattern.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> If Ryuuen’s claim holds, he already has three VIPs and probably every class’s — “a quiz where you could turn the page over and find the answer written on the back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Flips Ryuuen off after the parting; leaves the recording phone alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Easy for you to say. It’s not like I can find them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re not expecting too much, I’ll do what I can,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Plans to mine Hirata for Dragon-group detail instead of Horikita — a different perspective.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Room scene: answers the VIP probe, trades mutual denial, notes Yukimura warming up while he fakes a chameleon’s sociability.<span class=\"pg\">p.131-133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I did deny it and said you’re wrong, what’s the point in checking?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Unfortunately, I’m not the VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not the VIP. Can I believe that you’re not the VIP, Yukimura?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Yukimura reports Karuizawa’s denial of the VIP role; Ayanokōji does not press it.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.6: the starlit hug and the teachers’ table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p139-1\">→ After: Ch.4: joining the wait and the honest opinion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p139-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  joining the wait and the honest opinion asked to come along on the katsuragi visit   then caught in the corridor by kushida  he asks to go along  ichinose agrees without wariness and wonders whether he wants to talk to katsuragi kun too  kushida asks what ayanokouji kun is doing there and whether he is waiting for horikita san  ichinose cites what ayanokouji said earlier to ryuuen  ryuuen mocks him as tagalong  and he answers with his honest opinion instead of the cheap trick  ichinose addresses horikita san and ayanokouji kun together  asking whether the test will create trust between people of different classes  ichinose on not hiding her identity  everything i do is for the sake of class b","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p139-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: joining the wait and the honest opinion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.139, p.143, p.148, p.150–151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Asked to come along on the Katsuragi visit — then caught in the corridor by Kushida.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He asks to go along; Ichinose agrees without wariness and wonders whether he wants to talk to Katsuragi-kun too.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida asks what Ayanokouji-kun is doing there and whether he is waiting for Horikita-san.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose cites what Ayanokouji said earlier to Ryuuen; Ryuuen mocks him as tagalong, and he answers with his honest opinion instead of the cheap trick.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose addresses Horikita-san and Ayanokouji-kun together, asking whether the test will create trust between people of different classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ichinose on not hiding her identity: everything I do is for the sake of Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p125-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the Karuizawa brief and the planted phone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hamaguchi-tetsuya yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 1  the deck vip exchange ends the deck walk with ichinose by denying his own vip role and vouching only for yukimura   karuizawa and sotomura left unsaid on purpose   i m not the vip  neither is yukimura  i can say that with absolutely certainty  unfortunately  i don t really know about karuizawa or the professor err  i mean  sotomura  it s not clear yet  personally  i agree with you on principle  withholds yukimura s karuizawa sotomura alibis   careless confirmation could cost ichinose s trust if either were the vip  accepts her  honest as much as possible  framing  decides the trap risk is smaller than the relationship cost of refusing  watches him take the confirmation and join the four non vip core   ten suspects left   you haven t checked with your own class yet  i observed  counts four cleared  himself  ichinose  hamaguchi  yukimura  against ten remaining  the vip will be concealing under pressure  the alibi he keeps half said   yukimura s denials accepted through attitude  not passed on wholesale","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.152–154<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ends the deck walk with Ichinose by denying his own VIP role and vouching only for Yukimura — Karuizawa and Sotomura left unsaid on purpose.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hamaguchi-tetsuya.html\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not the VIP. Neither is Yukimura, I can say that with absolutely certainty. Unfortunately, I don’t really know about Karuizawa or the Professor…err, I mean, Sotomura. It’s not clear yet. Personally, I agree with you on…”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You haven’t checked with your own class yet,” I observed.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not the VIP. Neither is Yukimura, I can say that with absolutely certainty. Unfortunately, I don’t really know about Karuizawa or the Professor…err, I mean, Sotomura. It’s not clear yet. Personally, I agree with you on principle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Withholds Yukimura’s Karuizawa/Sotomura alibis — careless confirmation could cost Ichinose’s trust if either were the VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Accepts her “honest as much as possible” framing; decides the trap risk is smaller than the relationship cost of refusing.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hamaguchi Tetsuya<\/b> Watches him take the confirmation and join the four non-VIP core — ten suspects left.<span class=\"pg\">p.152-154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Counts four cleared (himself, Ichinose, Hamaguchi, Yukimura) against ten remaining; the VIP will be concealing under pressure.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The alibi he keeps half-said — Yukimura’s denials accepted through attitude, not passed on wholesale.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p139-1\">← Before: Ch.4: joining the wait and the honest opinion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the night rounds<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p159-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  the night rounds named in the card table exit   invited back to the room by yukimura  yukimura and the professor get up to head back  and yukimura asks ayanokouji whether he is coming  the middle of the night call brings chabashira to the chilly pool deck  she apologises for keeping him waiting  and he apologises for calling so late  hoshinomiya acts overly familiar  his answer that he s fine because if he wasn t he wouldn t be here draws the not cute jab  the spy worry is his  ichinose might soon discover she was put into the group to find out about ayanokouji kiyotaka   and chabashira states he requested this location  the bridge cover  ayanokoji cites hirata s own wish to act as a bridge between horikita and the rest of the class   hirata picks it up at once  hirata opens the delicate karuizawa material  noting horikita told him to keep an eye on him too  karuizawa shouts at finding ayanokouji kun there  hirata says he asked him to come  apologising for not telling her first  hirata asks whether he has any ideas  then admits he has his limits and can t do everything  the creeped out confession  he s watched him since school started   the ayanokouji kun back then and now are like two different people","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the night rounds<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.159, p.166–168, p.170–172, p.176, p.178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in the card-table exit — invited back to the room by Yukimura.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Yukimura and the Professor get up to head back, and Yukimura asks Ayanokouji whether he is coming.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The middle-of-the-night call brings Chabashira to the chilly pool deck: she apologises for keeping him waiting, and he apologises for calling so late.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hoshinomiya acts overly familiar; his answer that he’s fine because if he wasn’t he wouldn’t be here draws the not-cute jab.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The spy worry is his: Ichinose might soon discover she was put into the group to find out about Ayanokouji Kiyotaka — and Chabashira states he requested this location.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bridge cover: Ayanokōji cites Hirata’s own wish to act as a bridge between Horikita and the rest of the class — Hirata picks it up at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata opens the delicate Karuizawa material, noting Horikita told him to keep an eye on him too.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa shouts at finding Ayanokouji-kun there; Hirata says he asked him to come, apologising for not telling her first.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hirata asks whether he has any ideas, then admits he has his limits and can’t do everything.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The creeped-out confession: he’s watched him since school started — the Ayanokouji-kun back then and now are like two different people.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: the deck VIP exchange<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the Sugimura bargain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 4  the sugimura bargain takes hirata s backstory and the fake dating motive  buys his silence for the karuizawa plan  and receives the class d vip s identity as a parting gift   but i do think you re amazing  ayanokouji kun  you re different from ike kun and yamauchi kun   hirata s line  in exchange   i m worse than them  named with yamauchi as the contrast class for  amazing    he ranks himself under both  same contrast line  the night s full read  smarter than imagined  pathological saviour drive  then the confidentiality bargain and the paper favour   is that really the truth  i asked   what was in it for me  karuizawa san wasn t being bullied  that s all i needed   hirata s line  reported   i believe you  but is there some deeper reason as well  i asked   you  hirata  i have a hard time imagining that   i understand what you re feeling  but the world isn t that simple    right  at this very moment  there s someone being bullied somewhere  and they might try to take their own life  just like sugimura kun  you can t stop them   so what are you going to do  then  you want to save both karuizawa and manabe  but that s not possible   if you promise not to get yourself involved  i m sure horikita will stay silent  i answered   hirata  since you have a large social network  i have a favor to ask  i handed hirata a piece of paper  the paper favour accepted without a displeased look   the social network lever for the manabe plan  accepts the elementary junior high bullying as the reason for the hyperventilation  the facade read locked in  the confidentiality pact runs through her   our philosophies are similar  gains hirata s cooperation    a power i d always wanted  each side feels they gained something","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the Sugimura bargain<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.179–183<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Takes Hirata’s backstory and the fake-dating motive, buys his silence for the Karuizawa plan, and receives the Class D VIP’s identity as a parting gift.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“But I do think you’re amazing, Ayanokouji-kun. You’re different from Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun.” (Hirata’s line, in exchange)<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m worse than them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is that really the truth?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Named with Yamauchi as the contrast class for “amazing” — he ranks himself under both.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Same contrast line.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The night’s full read: smarter than imagined, pathological saviour drive, then the confidentiality bargain and the paper favour.<span class=\"pg\">p.179-183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What was in it for me? Karuizawa-san wasn’t being bullied. That’s all I needed.” (Hirata’s line, reported)<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe you. But is there some deeper reason as well?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You, Hirata? I have a hard time imagining that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand what you’re feeling, but the world isn’t that simple, … right? At this very moment, there’s someone being bullied somewhere. And they might try to take their own life, just like Sugimura-kun. You can’t stop them.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181-182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what are you going to do, then? You want to save both Karuizawa and Manabe, but that’s not possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you promise not to get yourself involved, I’m sure Horikita will stay silent,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hirata. Since you have a large social network, I have a favor to ask.” I handed Hirata a piece of paper.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The paper favour accepted without a displeased look — the social-network lever for the Manabe plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Accepts the elementary/junior-high bullying as the reason for the hyperventilation; the façade read locked in.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The confidentiality pact runs through her; “Our philosophies are similar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Gains Hirata’s cooperation — “a power I’d always wanted”; each side feels they gained something.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the night rounds<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p184-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the farewell order<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p184-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  the farewell order named in sakura s goodbye   the last beat of the hour  sakura thanks ayanokouji kun and says her goodbyes  he bids farewell to her as she waves her hands adorably  then heads off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the farewell order<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.184<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Sakura’s goodbye — the last beat of the hour.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakura thanks Ayanokouji-kun and says her goodbyes; he bids farewell to her as she waves her hands adorably, then heads off.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the Sugimura bargain<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.0–5.2: the phone swap and the dam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"manabe-shiho yukimura-teruhiko horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 0 5 2  the phone swap and the dam final day  manabe kept obedient by the stairwell photo  ichinose s card hour  the 5 1 meet with horikita  the sleeping ichinose phone approach  then the group email show where his swapped phone opens the dam  reads manabe s constraint  the photo came  from a classmate  so she cannot pin the sub account on him or yukimura with certainty  the picture effect   obedient  no move against him  the other stairwell witness she might suspect  both kept outside certainty  the 5 1 night meet in person  chat leaves traces   i ll win  her anxiety leaking  hirata brought over  the introduce someone later plan   there haven t been any significant changes  at this rate  it looks like the vip is going to get away  how about you   i ll win  she replied flatly   her line  tagged   you sure you haven t made a mistake  i asked   no need  make whatever moves you like   you can t keep being scared of ryuuen forever  you know  i said   in that case  show your face when we discuss things  even if you don t talk  you can follow along  right   i d like to introduce you to someone else later  hirata  too  make sure to keep some time open before they announce the results  i said   think of it as compensation for putting yourself on the front lines  anyway  this person will be useful to us  already on their side  ayanokoji will handle him so horikita only has to keep up  the fear horikita won t name in detail   audience risk in the corridor  knows kushida is the dragon vip from hirata  treats horikita s confidence as solid victory for the 500 000  alone with her sleeping form  approaches the phone  abandons the peek  then takes the class a dream talk and the points screen admission   she must have gotten here early  huh  i asked out loud  the pervert risk test with his foot   gives up the peek   god  i m pathetic   oh  no  looks like you slept well   i should be asking you the same thing  when did you get here   any results  i asked   oh no  it s not a bother  i don t mind   well  yeah  of course i do  i ve thought about getting up to class a  no  wait i guess it d probably be more accurate to say that i must aim for class a   nowadays  you can t just enter college or get a job that easily  jobs  especially  i said   but this school  well  it does have an incredible amount of influence  right  most people who get anywhere in life succeed because   someone influential helps them  or are you not interested in that  ichinose   be that as it may  whether or not you can really earn twenty million points is another problem  even if you score well on the exams and save your points  it probably wouldn t be enough  i said   yeah  class d s financial situation is especially awful  even though horikita s trying her hardest  the points from the island test have yet to be deposited  actually  it s entirely possible we ll lose them in this test  i said   sorry  when you were using your phone earlier  i just happened to look at the screen  i was a little curious  so i was thinking of asking you about it   i don t plan on telling anyone else  besides  i might ve been mistaken  i won t pry   have you found a way to win this thing  i asked   to be honest  i have no idea  we haven t really been able to talk  which means we haven t been able to engage  i said   official answer  the phone swap trap  kushida horikita switch so a traitor submitting horikita loses   outcome  1 for class d   you re serious about this  huh  well  if you re all going to bet on that  i think i ll join in  too  i said   sure  after hearing hamaguchi out  i honestly don t think we have another option  i m really bad at communicating  so all i can do is show you the truth  i answered   wait  ayanokouji  there s no way this kind of strategy is going to work  said yukimura   his line  the dam image   his email show opens the hole so the muddy stream can run  the professor s  all alone with ichinose dono  barrages with yukimura on entry   yukimura isn t the vip  i heard as much earlier  i said  denying further would invite suspicion   stops because yukimura is the swapped vip  the withheld truth  he exchanged phones in secret  class d s 500 000 was already gambled on the swap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.0–5.2: the phone swap and the dam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.205–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Final day: Manabe kept obedient by the stairwell photo, Ichinose’s card hour, the 5.1 meet with Horikita, the sleeping-Ichinose phone approach, then the group email-show where his swapped phone opens the dam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“There haven’t been any significant changes. At this rate, it looks like the VIP is going to get away. How about you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll win,” she replied flatly. (her line, tagged)<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You sure you haven’t made a mistake?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>37 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Manabe’s constraint: the photo came “from a classmate,” so she cannot pin the sub-account on him or Yukimura with certainty.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The picture effect — obedient, no move against him.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The other stairwell witness she might suspect; both kept outside certainty.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The 5.1 night meet in person (chat leaves traces): “I’ll win,” her anxiety leaking, Hirata brought over, the introduce-someone-later plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.207-209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No need. Make whatever moves you like.”<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t keep being scared of Ryuuen forever, you know,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, show your face when we discuss things. Even if you don’t talk, you can follow along, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to introduce you to someone else later. Hirata, too. Make sure to keep some time open before they announce the results,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Think of it as compensation for putting yourself on the front lines. Anyway, this person will be useful to us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Already on their side; Ayanokōji will handle him so Horikita only has to keep up.<span class=\"pg\">p.207-208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The fear Horikita won’t name in detail — audience risk in the corridor.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Knows Kushida is the Dragon VIP from Hirata; treats Horikita’s confidence as solid victory for the 500,000.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Alone with her sleeping form; approaches the phone, abandons the peek, then takes the Class A dream talk and the points-screen admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.210-217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She must have gotten here early, huh?” I asked out loud.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The pervert-risk test with his foot — gives up the peek; “God, I’m pathetic.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210-212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, no. Looks like you slept well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I should be asking you the same thing. When did you get here?”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Any results?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh no, it’s not a bother. I don’t mind.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, yeah. Of course I do. I’ve thought about getting up to Class A. No, wait…I guess it’d probably be more accurate to say that I must aim for Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nowadays, you can’t just enter college or get a job that easily. Jobs, especially,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But this school… Well, it does have an incredible amount of influence, right? Most people who get anywhere in life succeed because … someone influential helps them. Or are you not interested in that, Ichinose?”<span class=\"pg\">p.214-215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Be that as it may, whether or not you can really earn twenty million points is another problem. Even if you score well on the exams and save your points, it probably wouldn’t be enough,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Class D’s financial situation is especially awful. Even though Horikita’s trying her hardest, the points from the island test have yet to be deposited. Actually, it’s entirely possible we’ll lose them in this test,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. When you were using your phone earlier, I just happened to look at the screen. I was a little curious, so I was thinking of asking you about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t plan on telling anyone else. Besides, I might’ve been mistaken. I won’t pry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Have you found a way to win this thing?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I have no idea. We haven’t really been able to talk, which means we haven’t been able to engage,” I said. (official answer)<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The phone-swap trap: Kushida–Horikita switch so a traitor submitting Horikita loses — Outcome #1 for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re serious about this, huh? Well, if you’re all going to bet on that, I think I’ll join in, too,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure. After hearing Hamaguchi out, I honestly don’t think we have another option. I’m really bad at communicating, so all I can do is show you the truth,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait, Ayanokouji. There’s no way this kind of strategy is going to work,” said Yukimura. (his line)<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The dam image — his email-show opens the hole so the muddy stream can run.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> The Professor’s “All alone with Ichinose-dono?” barrages with Yukimura on entry.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yukimura isn’t the VIP. I heard as much earlier,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Denying further would invite suspicion — stops because Yukimura is the swapped VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The withheld truth: he exchanged phones in secret; Class D’s 500,000 was already gambled on the swap.<span class=\"pg\">p.223-224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p184-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the farewell order<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: found out, then the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke sudou-ken ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 2 5 3  found out  then the cafe the password show settles yukimura s cover in the room  ichinose s call and sim lock lecture strip the double swap bare  then the 11 p m  cafe with karuizawa  hirata  horikita  sudou and ryuuen  the twelve group results  and a warning over class c s lead  names the real weakness of the password theatre  judging whose phone it was stayed hard  but the six digit unlock  wasn t the result of deduction  but rather of preconceived notions   i m sorry  yukimura kun  this happened because i came up with this idea at the very last minute  i muttered  takes the fall as the points grabber everyone now believes him to be  the long reveal chain  her call  the sim lecture  the hoshinomiya sensei unlock  the karuizawa guess  and the mutual  we re even   yeah  guess so  i answered   not especially  i can t do anything but believe  anyway  i m heading to my room   horikita  of course   a huge success  don t you mean a crushing defeat  we failed  hard  you saw through everything   i m sorry  sorry for trying to deceive you like that  especially after i agreed to be your ally  are you angry   i see  if you mean it  i m sure horikita will be relieved   the critical part   the same as you  i would ve tried to find out who the vip was  borrowed that person s phone  and had another one ready  then  i d step forward and claim to be the vip myself   so i ve been found out  huh   why did you think it was karuizawa  i asked   why didn t you say anything  at the very least  you could have exposed my lie  i said   machida   you ought to praise horikita  she just gave me directions  that s all  the full chain on the page  hirata told him karuizawa was the real vip  manabe s bullying of karuizawa opened the swap  he replicated email and call history  paid for a sim lock release  transferred his number  then swapped that phone with yukimura s  the trap s shape on the page  a simple person misses the swap  a clever person accuses him   but they never would have come to the conclusion that karuizawa was the real vip  the real vip and phone owner   the fact kept even from yukimura until ichinose named her  hirata s withheld knowledge  then the cafe approach about  that piece of paper   don t worry  i m positive that one of the guys from class a sent the school an email with my name  i answered   sorry for calling you so late   his line to karuizawa   she s the type to come at the very last second  we have another four minutes  i said   you re finally here  hey  who s that behind you  i asked  the cafe fifth wheel  his  one step behind  on the email  ryuuen s arrival makes him half threaten and then sink back on command   yeah  someone discovered his identity  i reasoned   minami  horse vip   minami kun was the horse group vip    two minami rows exist in the roster  which one is not settled on this page   is yamauchi okay  i asked   i don t know who it was  but betraying the group before he could was a fine move  i said  the planted sixth guest  the kushida reveal  the class a vip list  the explicit next target threat  ayanokoji s quiet  we might be in trouble   i mean  it s not really a difficult problem  if you just put your mind to it  it s relatively simple  i told everyone   putting aside how ryuuen found out the vips  identities  all he had to do was tell everyone  kushida is the vip  before the end of the test  right  of course  no one would believe what someone like ryuuen says  especially a group of such intelligent  gifted people  however  the final half hour was different  even if you answered incorrectly  there wasn t any risk to class points  as such  even someone who d been playing defensively like katsuragi could vote  right  if there was even a 1  chance that kushida was really the vip  then they would ve gotten outcome  1  which was the most convenient for everyone involved  the defensive player who could still vote in the riskless half hour   kouenji saved our asses    his betrayal email kept class c from taking everything  the stray bullets hit other vips   horikita  i think that we might be in trouble  i said   you ve got a point  i m probably overthinking things  don t worry  the premonition named as  something like excitement    first stirrings of wanting ryuuen as an opponent  the cafe debrief  the results  and the shared worry she talks him out of","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: found out, then the café<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.225–243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The password-show settles Yukimura’s cover in the room; Ichinose’s call and SIM-lock lecture strip the double swap bare; then the 11 p.m. café with Karuizawa, Hirata, Horikita, Sudou and Ryuuen, the twelve-group results, and a warning over Class C’s lead.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+3 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m sorry, Yukimura-kun. This happened because I came up with this idea at the very last minute,” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. Guess so,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Not especially. I can’t do anything but believe, anyway. I’m heading to my room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>36 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Names the real weakness of the password theatre: judging whose phone it was stayed hard, but the six-digit unlock “wasn’t the result of deduction, but rather of preconceived notions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Takes the fall as the points-grabber everyone now believes him to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The long reveal chain: her call, the SIM lecture, the Hoshinomiya-sensei unlock, the Karuizawa guess, and the mutual “we’re even.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225-233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A huge success? Don’t you mean a crushing defeat? We failed, hard. You saw through everything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry. Sorry for trying to deceive you like that, especially after I agreed to be your ally. Are you angry?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. If you mean it, I’m sure Horikita will be relieved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The critical part?”<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The same as you. I would’ve tried to find out who the VIP was, borrowed that person’s phone, and had another one ready. Then, I’d step forward and claim to be the VIP myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So I’ve been found out, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why did you think it was Karuizawa?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why didn’t you say anything? At the very least, you could have exposed my lie,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Machida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You ought to praise Horikita. She just gave me directions, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The full chain on the page: Hirata told him Karuizawa was the real VIP; Manabe’s bullying of Karuizawa opened the swap; he replicated email and call history, paid for a SIM lock release, transferred his number, then swapped that phone with Yukimura’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The trap’s shape on the page: a simple person misses the swap, a clever person accuses him, “But they never would have come to the conclusion that Karuizawa was the real VIP.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The real VIP and phone owner — the fact kept even from Yukimura until Ichinose named her.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata’s withheld knowledge, then the café approach about “that piece of paper.”<span class=\"pg\">p.231, 234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry. I’m positive that one of the guys from Class A sent the school an email with my name,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry for calling you so late.” (his line to Karuizawa)<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s the type to come at the very last second. We have another four minutes,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re finally here. Hey, who’s that behind you?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The café fifth wheel; his “one step behind” on the email; Ryuuen’s arrival makes him half-threaten and then sink back on command.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Someone discovered his identity,” I reasoned. (Minami, Horse VIP)<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Minami-kun was the Horse group VIP” — two Minami rows exist in the roster; which one is not settled on this page.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is Yamauchi okay?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know who it was, but betraying the group before he could was a fine move,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The planted sixth guest; the Kushida reveal; the Class A VIP list; the explicit next-target threat; Ayanokōji’s quiet “we might be in trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237-243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean, it’s not really a difficult problem. If you just put your mind to it, it’s relatively simple,” I told everyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Putting aside how Ryuuen found out the VIPs’ identities, all he had to do was tell everyone ‘Kushida is the VIP’ before the end of the test, right? Of course, no one would believe what someone like Ryuuen says. Especially a group of such intelligent, gifted people. However, the final half hour was different. Even if you answered incorrectly, there wasn’t any risk to class points. As such, even someone who’d been playing defensively like Katsuragi could vote, right? If there was even a 1% chance that Kushida was really the VIP, then they would’ve gotten Outcome #1, which was the most convenient for everyone involved.”<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The defensive player who could still vote in the riskless half hour.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Kouenji saved our asses” — his betrayal email kept Class C from taking everything; the stray bullets hit other VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita. I think that we might be in trouble,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve got a point. I’m probably overthinking things. Don’t worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The premonition named as “something like excitement” — first stirrings of wanting Ryuuen as an opponent.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The café debrief, the results, and the shared worry she talks him out of.<span class=\"pg\">p.235-243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.0–5.2: the phone swap and the dam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p244-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the author’s forward look<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p244-1","v":"y1v4","y":1,"o":4,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  the author s forward look the closing note turns the page on him by name  the second semester is about to begin  it s possible that a certain figure from ayanokouji kiyotaka s past will make an appearance in volume 5   and it won t just involve his classmates  the upperclassmen will get involved too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p244-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the author’s forward look<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4 · p.244<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The closing note turns the page on him by name.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The second semester is about to begin; it’s possible that a certain figure from Ayanokouji Kiyotaka’s past will make an appearance in Volume 5 — and it won’t just involve his classmates, the upperclassmen will get involved too.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4-p225-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: found out, then the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p10-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1  the collection frame one page first person frame before the vignettes  no character appears and no school business is named   only the narrator s case against end of summer melancholy   this is a selection of vignettes about students wavering in that space between childhood and adulthood  the frame s stance  refuses the end of vacation blues   the free years of life are the school years  and most of a life is spent sacrificing for society  the page prints no name  read as the series narrator s frame  following the first volume s opening monologue","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: the collection frame<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.10<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One-page first-person frame before the vignettes: no character appears and no school business is named — only the narrator’s case against end-of-summer melancholy.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">“This is a selection of vignettes about students wavering in that space between childhood and adulthood.”<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The frame’s stance: refuses the end-of-vacation blues — the free years of life are the school years, and most of a life is spent sacrificing for society.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page prints no name; read as the series narrator’s frame, following the first volume’s opening monologue.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p11-1\">→ After: Ch.2: the fortune-teller invite chain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p11-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  the fortune teller invite chain between the island and cruise tests he spends one of seven rest days alone in the dorm   no calls in either direction   until sudou rings about a keyaki mall fortune teller  a point check before the call  106 219 on hand  100 000 transferred to sudou ken  the page gives no reason for the move   well  i don t really care  i said aloud   definitely invite suzune out  too  the outing is a device to reach horikita   sudou routes the invitation through him and will not take no for an answer   in other words  you re talking about fortune tellers  ability to cold read  right  i asked  treats her claim of real power as a mechanism question   pushes until the explanation is on the table  fortune tellers work from past data  not force   i refuse  she answered  she talks him through cold reading  then declines the crowded outing  sudou s reply to the report is  then forget about it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the fortune-teller invite chain<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.11–17<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Between the island and cruise tests he spends one of seven rest days alone in the dorm — no calls in either direction — until Sudou rings about a Keyaki Mall fortune-teller.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I don’t really care,” I said aloud.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Definitely invite Suzune out, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In other words, you’re talking about fortune-tellers’ ability to cold read, right?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> A point check before the call: 106,219 on hand, 100,000 transferred to Sudou Ken; the page gives no reason for the move.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The outing is a device to reach Horikita — Sudou routes the invitation through him and will not take no for an answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Treats her claim of real power as a mechanism question — pushes until the explanation is on the table: fortune-tellers work from past data, not force.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse,” she answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She talks him through cold reading, then declines the crowded outing; Sudou’s reply to the report is “Then forget about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15–17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: the collection frame<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p18-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the couples-only floor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p18-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  the couples only floor at 9 30 the next morning the fifth floor is already a wall of couples  the booth s rule turns him away and puts ibuki mio in his path  crowd reflex on display  alone in an elevator he would hammer the close button  so he detours across the building for an empty car  the written notice and the attendant agree  guidance is for couples only   ukon sensei reads fortunes for couples  he reads her anxiety as hyper awareness   the difference is awareness   and tests it with the convenience store clerk  she concedes the point  then compares him to a future mass murderer   the difference between you now  and you then  is awareness  his loner s answer to the jibe   more or less    the comparison lands without flinching","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the couples-only floor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.18–27<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At 9:30 the next morning the fifth floor is already a wall of couples; the booth’s rule turns him away and puts Ibuki Mio in his path.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The difference between you now, and you then, is awareness.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Crowd reflex on display: alone in an elevator he would hammer the close button, so he detours across the building for an empty car.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The written notice and the attendant agree: guidance is for couples only — Ukon-sensei reads fortunes for couples.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> He reads her anxiety as hyper-awareness — the difference is awareness — and tests it with the convenience-store clerk; she concedes the point, then compares him to a future mass murderer.<span class=\"pg\">p.24–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His loner’s answer to the jibe: “More or less.” — the comparison lands without flinching.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the fortune-teller invite chain<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p28-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: no partner, then fate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p28-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2 2 3  no partner  then fate back in the dorm he researches tenchuusatsu and rejects every possible partner  only to meet ibuki at the booth again the next day  the list of refusals  horikita would decline  he lacks the courage to ask kushida  sakura would be ill at ease among couples  and the guys would not spend their last summer days on a paired reading   i wonder if tenchuusatsu is only being offered this month  i muttered  the second meeting turns from the booth s rule to belief itself  he asks directly whether she believes  and she answers that the over skeptical get nothing out of it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: no partner, then fate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.28–29<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back in the dorm he researches tenchuusatsu and rejects every possible partner, only to meet Ibuki at the booth again the next day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wonder if tenchuusatsu is only being offered this month?” I muttered.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The list of refusals: Horikita would decline, he lacks the courage to ask Kushida, Sakura would be ill at ease among couples, and the guys would not spend their last summer days on a paired reading.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The second meeting turns from the booth’s rule to belief itself: he asks directly whether she believes, and she answers that the over-skeptical get nothing out of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p18-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the couples-only floor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p30-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the pair proposal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p30-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  the pair proposal ibuki s belief speech closes  he proposes they pair up for the couples only booth   no relationship  no complications   in that case  why don t we go together  on his own feelings   i honestly felt absolutely nothing for ibuki    a flat line  first time customer ease  she worries the island grudge will stain him  he answers that the school runs on ability  not feelings  and that sabotage was a natural tactic under the circumstances   i don t think people like that would be admitted to this school in the first place   all i am is an unremarkable student    no ladder to climb  no rung to be kicked off  coasting with horikita is luck enough","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the pair proposal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.30–32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki’s belief speech closes; he proposes they pair up for the couples-only booth — no relationship, no complications.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“In that case, why don’t we go together?”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t think people like that would be admitted to this school in the first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> On his own feelings: “I honestly felt absolutely nothing for Ibuki.” — a flat line, first-time-customer ease.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> She worries the island grudge will stain him; he answers that the school runs on ability, not feelings, and that sabotage was a natural tactic under the circumstances.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “All I am is an unremarkable student.” — no ladder to climb, no rung to be kicked off; coasting with Horikita is luck enough.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p28-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2–2.3: no partner, then fate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: the reading<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p33-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"ukon ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 4  the reading after about fifteen minutes a pair at a time  the tent  thirty lux  hood  crystal ball  card reader   and the basic plan for both   i ll take the same  i replied  balance check before paying  roughly 6 000 points left    barely enough    and the basic plan deducts by card  price not printed  the reading turns on him  a broad  harsh childhood  then the pronouncement that he holds the fate tenchuusatsu  and the advice to go straight home without detours   i m not going to dismiss fortune telling from now on  i added","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4: the reading<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.33–37<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After about fifteen minutes a pair at a time, the tent: thirty lux, hood, crystal ball, card reader — and the Basic Plan for both.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#ukon\">Ukon<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll take the same,” I replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not going to dismiss fortune-telling from now on,” I added.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Balance check before paying: roughly 6,000 points left — “barely enough” — and the Basic Plan deducts by card, price not printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ukon<\/b> The reading turns on him: a broad “harsh childhood,” then the pronouncement that he holds the fate tenchuusatsu, and the advice to go straight home without detours.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the pair proposal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p38-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the detour and the elevator<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p38-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 5  the detour and the elevator they take the detour on purpose   to test the prediction   and the car grinds to a halt on the third floor  works the dead emergency line like a technician  backup battery alive  control panel likely dead  hearing impaired button silent too   apparently  our situation is far more serious than i originally thought    his own battery at four percent   a prank like this is evil  i muttered    the emergency number scribbled over with magic marker  picks the rescuer himself  the three idiots would make a scene  sakura would be flustered  kushida and karuizawa unsuited   the taciturn fellow it is  the phone dies mid call  admits the express mode push is theatre   he does not expect it to work  he is buying time and handing ibuki hope while she is on the verge of losing her cool   why don t you try pushing the button for your desired floor  plus the close door button at the same time  i suggested  the car moves   but the adults had used the remote from the first floor at the exact same moment  the pair s button work did nothing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p38-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the detour and the elevator<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.38–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">They take the detour on purpose — to test the prediction — and the car grinds to a halt on the third floor.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Apparently, our situation is far more serious than I originally thought.” — his own battery at four percent.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“A prank like this is evil,” I muttered. — the emergency number scribbled over with magic marker.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why don’t you try pushing the button for your desired floor, plus the close-door button at the same time?” I suggested.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Works the dead emergency line like a technician: backup battery alive, control panel likely dead, hearing-impaired button silent too.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Picks the rescuer himself: the three idiots would make a scene, Sakura would be flustered, Kushida and Karuizawa unsuited — the taciturn fellow it is; the phone dies mid-call.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Admits the express-mode push is theatre — he does not expect it to work; he is buying time and handing Ibuki hope while she is on the verge of losing her cool.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The car moves — but the adults had used the remote from the first floor at the exact same moment; the pair’s button work did nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: the reading<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p48-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Katsuragi at the doors<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p48-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  katsuragi at the doors outside stand two adults and katsuragi  who took the call and moved the elevator himself  the thanks run both ways  sudou  performed brilliantly  cooperation across classes is praised  and ayanokoji owes him his nerve  the friendship and the plan are treated as already told    the story of our friendship had begun a little while ago","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Katsuragi at the doors<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.48<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Outside stand two adults and Katsuragi, who took the call and moved the elevator himself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The thanks run both ways: Sudou “performed brilliantly,” cooperation across classes is praised, and Ayanokōji owes him his nerve.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The friendship and the plan are treated as already told — “The story of our friendship had begun a little while ago.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p38-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.5: the detour and the elevator<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p49-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the birthday invite and the empty wallet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p49-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  the birthday invite and the empty wallet one week before the elevator  kushida s group chat message asks the boys to celebrate inogashira s birthday  ak notes the class is broke until the september 1 deposit   next wednesday is inogashira san s birthday  inogashira is  a somewhat quiet  plain girl from class d  rather like sakura    ak s comparison for the reader  ike jumps at the invitation because he likes kushida and wants to be in her good graces  ak reads the event as his chance to get closer to her   let s get some presents for kokoro chan   well  i don t got any money  the class s promised special exam points will not be deposited until september 1  ak has almost nothing left after the fortune teller   isn t it all right if the guys just pool their points and buy her one present   we had been awarded 8 700 private points at the start of august  free meals and free water make going without spending possible  but most students run dry near month s end  as with the first month s 100 000 points  all three agree to the pooled gift and set out to buy it together","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the birthday invite and the empty wallet<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.49–50<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One week before the elevator, Kushida&#x27;s group-chat message asks the boys to celebrate Inogashira&#x27;s birthday; AK notes the class is broke until the September 1 deposit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Next Wednesday is Inogashira-san’s birthday.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Let’s get some presents for Kokoro-chan!”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Well, I don’t got any money.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Inogashira is “a somewhat quiet, plain girl from Class D, rather like Sakura” — AK&#x27;s comparison for the reader.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Ike jumps at the invitation because he likes Kushida and wants to be in her good graces; AK reads the event as his chance to get closer to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The class&#x27;s promised special-exam points will not be deposited until September 1; AK has almost nothing left after the fortune-teller.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t it all right if the guys just pool their points and buy her one present?”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> “We had been awarded 8,700 private points at the start of August.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Free meals and free water make going without spending possible, but most students run dry near month&#x27;s end, as with the first month&#x27;s 100,000 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> All three agree to the pooled gift and set out to buy it together.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p48-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Katsuragi at the doors<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: shopping with the two idiots<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p51-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki sudou-ken shinohara-satsuki katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  shopping with the two idiots the boys meet without kushida to buy inogashira s present  ike complains  yamauchi bickers  and ak mediates with sudou s share of the points   she s the most important person   remember  kushida never said that she d go with us   you wanted to go  so you should do the shopping   it ll be better if we shop together  right  sudou entrusted the boys with his share of the points for the gift  in the pink girls  shop  ak s first present buying attempt   a phone case   is rejected by yamauchi   you really have no sense when it comes to this stuff  ayanokouji  yamauchi researched the recipient s taste  ak has enough trouble remembering inogashira s name and face   kokoro chan likes the white bear series  so she should be happy with this present  ike stands frozen at the keychain shelf holding an orange character charm shinohara is known to like  then puts it back   if i remember correctly  didn t shinohara like that orange character   no way in hell  dude   shinohara isn t cute at all  and she has too much attitude  shinohara stands behind ike through the whole tirade  her friends  including kushida  are elsewhere in the store   you can just go ahead and die  ike  yamauchi spots katsuragi browsing the same store  the boys hide and watch him hesitate over a thin box   what s baldy got there  ak considers catching katsuragi shoplifting for later leverage  then rejects the idea himself   maybe he doesn t want anyone to see what he s buying  katsuragi picks a box and pays without noticing the class d boys watching him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: shopping with the two idiots<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.51–57<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The boys meet without Kushida to buy Inogashira&#x27;s present; Ike complains, Yamauchi bickers, and AK mediates with Sudou&#x27;s share of the points. Ike stands frozen at the keychain shelf holding an orange-character charm Shinohara is known to like, then puts it back. Yamauchi spots Katsuragi browsing the same store; the boys hide and watch him hesitate over a thin box.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “She’s the most important person!”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Remember, Kushida never said that she’d go with us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “You wanted to go, so you should do the shopping!”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’ll be better if we shop together, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou entrusted the boys with his share of the points for the gift.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In the pink girls&#x27; shop, AK&#x27;s first present-buying attempt — a phone case — is rejected by Yamauchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really have no sense when it comes to this stuff, Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Yamauchi researched the recipient&#x27;s taste; AK has enough trouble remembering Inogashira&#x27;s name and face.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kokoro-chan likes the white bear series, so she should be happy with this present.”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I remember correctly, didn’t Shinohara like that orange character?”<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No way in hell, dude!”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Shinohara isn’t cute at all, and she has too much attitude!”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shinohara stands behind Ike through the whole tirade; her friends, including Kushida, are elsewhere in the store.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can just go ahead and die, Ike!”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s baldy got there?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK considers catching Katsuragi shoplifting for later leverage, then rejects the idea himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe he doesn’t want anyone to see what he’s buying?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi picks a box and pays without noticing the Class D boys watching him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p49-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the birthday invite and the empty wallet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p58-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the chocolate and the date<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p58-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  the chocolate and the date ike and yamauchi inspect the box katsuragi bought  chocolate in cute wrapping  for a girl   the birthday is august 29   which girl has a birthday on the twenty ninth   do you know who it might be  ayanokouji  page 59 is a single line   ak has no clue either  and the date stays unmatched","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p58-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the chocolate and the date<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.58–59<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike and Yamauchi inspect the box Katsuragi bought: chocolate in cute wrapping, for a girl.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “The birthday is August 29.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Which girl has a birthday on the twenty-ninth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Do you know who it might be, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Page 59 is a single line — AK has no clue either, and the date stays unmatched.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p51-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: shopping with the two idiots<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: birthdays in AK&#x27;s room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p60-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 2  birthdays in ak s room after dinner ike  yamauchi  kushida and sudou gather in ak s room to identify katsuragi s august 29 birthday girl   kikyou chan  do you know the other girls  birthdays   i think i ve memorized the birthdates of everyone who s told me  more or less   if it s a first year girl  i should know everyone  but i can t think of anyone who fits  kushida  katsuragi is the famous class a class leader  and she was in his group on the ship test   katsuragi kun lost his hair completely when he was young  due to illness  kushida scolds ike for the baldy jokes  he apologizes to her and agrees to apologize to shinohara   you understand what you should do about it  right   i m sorry  kikyou chan   i never got the impression that katsuragi kun was the romantic sort   it couldn t possibly be horikita san  could it  sudou grabs ike by the collar at the horikita suggestion and demands suzune s birthday from ak   when is suzune s birthday   it s on february 15  ak is one of the few who knows kushida and horikita hate each other  yet kushida has her birthday   sounds like i ve snagged some good info  sudou keeps the february 15 date as leverage while ike wheezes in a headlock   how about we quit while we re ahead  and not get too carried away looking for whoever katsuragi s partner might be  okay   i absolutely hate the idea of katsuragi beating me   just because we ll probably lose to him doesn t mean we don t have a chance of winning   in basketball  you can use plays that are just barely allowed   a strong desire for victory is what really matters   if katsuragi giving a present to some girl will bring them closer  then we gotta stop him from doing it  kushida shuts the interference plan down  ike folds  and sudou has tournament practice as cover   kanji kun  you can t interfere   of course i m curious  but getting in the way is not okay   impossible   i have katsuragi kun s contact information   i asked him for it   if i suddenly contacted him  i think even katsuragi would be surprised   you stopped me from interfering in katsuragi s plans  so you gotta take responsibility   you gotta investigate   should i force you   i ll do some digging tomorrow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2: birthdays in AK&#x27;s room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.60–66<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After dinner Ike, Yamauchi, Kushida and Sudou gather in AK&#x27;s room to identify Katsuragi&#x27;s August 29 birthday girl.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Kikyou-chan, do you know the other girls’ birthdays?”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I think I’ve memorized the birthdates of everyone who’s told me, more or less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “If it’s a first-year girl, I should know everyone, but I can’t think of anyone who fits”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>30 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Kushida: Katsuragi is the famous Class A class leader, and she was in his group on the ship test.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi-kun lost his hair completely when he was young, due to illness.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kushida scolds Ike for the baldy jokes; he apologizes to her and agrees to apologize to Shinohara.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You understand what you should do about it, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, Kikyou-chan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never got the impression that Katsuragi-kun was the romantic sort”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It couldn’t possibly be Horikita-san, could it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou grabs Ike by the collar at the Horikita suggestion and demands Suzune&#x27;s birthday from AK.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When is Suzune’s birthday?”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s on February 15.”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> AK is one of the few who knows Kushida and Horikita hate each other, yet Kushida has her birthday.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sounds like I’ve snagged some good info,”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou keeps the February 15 date as leverage while Ike wheezes in a headlock.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How about we quit while we’re ahead, and not get too carried away looking for whoever Katsuragi’s partner might be, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I absolutely hate the idea of Katsuragi beating me!”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just because we’ll probably lose to him doesn’t mean we don’t have a chance of winning!”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In basketball, you can use plays that are just barely allowed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A strong desire for victory is what really matters.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If Katsuragi giving a present to some girl will bring them closer, then we gotta stop him from doing it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida shuts the interference plan down; Ike folds, and Sudou has tournament practice as cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kanji-kun, you can’t interfere,”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’m curious, but getting in the way is not okay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Impossible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have Katsuragi-kun’s contact information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I asked him for it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I suddenly contacted him, I think even Katsuragi would be surprised,”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You stopped me from interfering in Katsuragi’s plans, so you gotta take responsibility,”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You gotta investigate,”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Should I force you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll do some digging tomorrow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p58-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the chocolate and the date<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.3: the crossroads and the offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p67-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu tachibana-akane horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 3  the crossroads and the offer staking out the dorm crossroads for katsuragi  ak is intercepted by student council president horikita manabu and secretary tachibana   it s so hot  i feel like i could die   it s been a while   i guess the answer is horikita s brother  tachibana  third year secretary  speaks loudly and takes an instant dislike to ak s casual tone   president  this student really has a sour look on his face   do you even know who you re talking to   do you want to penalize me   ayanokouji  if you have no prior engagements  i d like you to accompany me  manabu insists on talking now rather than after the semester begins  ak caves to clear the request out of the way   let s just do this now   my instinct says not to leave you alone with this boy  president   the student council has received reports of the results from the island test  and the test on the ship   i know that you outsmarted the other classes on the island  and that class d s vip in the rabbit group successfully avoided detection   however  i think that you were responsible  manabu knows the island leader s name was changed to ak s   only the exam committee  the president and tachibana know  not the homeroom teachers   in the end  the leader s name was changed to yours   the homeroom teachers don t have this information  so you can relax   what exactly is the student council   the abilities of the person seated at the top are paramount   this school doesn t just shove all the students with superior abilities into class a   in that case  why do you reject horikita   she s a failure who belongs in class d  ak covers for suzune with the friends line  manabu rejects it outright   he knows his sister   she d never think of something like that  ak concludes manabu watches him for the same reason as chabashira  the 50  entrance scores and the resume discrepancy   stop fishing for information about my personal life   will you join the student council   ayanokouji  if you wish  i ll appoint you vice president  tachibana protests  a first year from class d as vice president is unprecedented  all seats were thought filled   this is completely unprecedented   we can t suddenly appoint this rude boy to the vice presidency   i ve said this already  but i refuse any position   when the time comes  i ll need the power to combat that change   president  you re talking about what ll happen when nagumo kun is elected president  right  tachibana names nagumo as the next student council president  ak infers from the timing that nagumo is a second year   there can be two student council vice presidents   there s no way nagumo kun would permit something like that   i m not doing it   well  if you want me to help you because you re worried about your sister  i might be able to squeeze you in for a consultation   please feel free to stop by the student council whenever you like  manabu gives up for now  ak reads even the president as wrestling with his own anxieties","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.3: the crossroads and the offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.67–73<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Staking out the dorm crossroads for Katsuragi, AK is intercepted by Student Council President Horikita Manabu and Secretary Tachibana.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s so hot, I feel like I could die…”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> “It’s been a while.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I guess the answer is Horikita’s brother,”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>38 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> Tachibana, third-year secretary, speaks loudly and takes an instant dislike to AK&#x27;s casual tone.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “President, this student really has a sour look on his face.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you even know who you’re talking to?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you want to penalize me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji, if you have no prior engagements, I’d like you to accompany me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Manabu insists on talking now rather than after the semester begins; AK caves to clear the request out of the way.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s just do this now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My instinct says not to leave you alone with this boy, President!”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The student council has received reports of the results from the island test, and the test on the ship.”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know that you outsmarted the other classes on the island, and that Class D’s VIP in the Rabbit group successfully avoided detection,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, I think that you were responsible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Manabu knows the island leader&#x27;s name was changed to AK&#x27;s — only the exam committee, the president and Tachibana know; not the homeroom teachers.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the end, the leader’s name was changed to yours.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The homeroom teachers don’t have this information, so you can relax.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What exactly is the student council?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The abilities of the person seated at the top are paramount.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This school doesn’t just shove all the students with superior abilities into Class A,”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, why do you reject Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’s a failure who belongs in Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> AK covers for Suzune with the friends line; Manabu rejects it outright — he knows his sister.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She’d never think of something like that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> AK concludes Manabu watches him for the same reason as Chabashira: the 50% entrance scores and the resume discrepancy.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop fishing for information about my personal life.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Will you join the student council?”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji, if you wish, I’ll appoint you vice president,”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Tachibana protests: a first-year from Class D as vice president is unprecedented; all seats were thought filled.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is completely unprecedented!”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We can’t suddenly appoint this rude boy to the vice presidency!”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve said this already, but I refuse any position,”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When the time comes, I’ll need the power to combat that change.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “President, you’re talking about what’ll happen when Nagumo-kun is elected president, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Tachibana names Nagumo as the next student council president; AK infers from the timing that Nagumo is a second-year.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There can be two student council vice presidents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no way Nagumo-kun would permit something like that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not doing it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if you want me to help you because you’re worried about your sister, I might be able to squeeze you in for a consultation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Please feel free to stop by the student council whenever you like.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Manabu gives up for now; AK reads even the president as wrestling with his own anxieties.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: birthdays in AK&#x27;s room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p74-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.4: trailing Katsuragi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p74-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 4  trailing katsuragi thirty minutes later ak tails katsuragi from the crossroads   toward the school building  which he enters in uniform   that s why he s wearing his uniform  huh  casual clothes are forbidden inside the school  the uniform was for entry  not fashion   did you meet katsuragi  at the keyaki chocolate shop ak knocks a stack of boxes over  katsuragi helps him re shelve them without a hint of dislike   what are you doing   i came here to buy a birthday present   two are better than one  ak judges katsuragi a good guy   the island corn goodwill is the reference   forbidding looks aside   are you giving your girlfriend a present   i don t have a girlfriend   are you buying a birthday present   one of the boxes of chocolates   you re required to wear your uniform if you enter the school   uh  well  i ve various private matters to attend to  katsuragi raises the shared disadvantage  students may not contact anyone on the outside  breaking it means expulsion   the stipulation that you can t contact anyone on the outside   don t you want to contact your parents or siblings   both the points system  and the quality of the facilities here  are things that ordinary students can only dream of   you re close with horikita  aren t you   it s not exactly what either of us wanted  but we were kind of forced into a partnership  i think  katsuragi apologizes if he offended and admits the store visit is his third   he agonizes over decisions when someone s feelings are involved   if i offended you  please forgive me   to tell you the truth  this is the third time i ve visited this store   is it strange to celebrate someone s birthday   who s the gift for   it s personal  katsuragi refuses to name the recipient  ak ends the chapter s first half with the school building and store return mysteries open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p74-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.4: trailing Katsuragi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.74–78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Thirty minutes later AK tails Katsuragi from the crossroads — toward the school building, which he enters in uniform.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s why he’s wearing his uniform, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Did you meet Katsuragi?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “What are you doing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>24 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Casual clothes are forbidden inside the school; the uniform was for entry, not fashion.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> At the Keyaki chocolate shop AK knocks a stack of boxes over; Katsuragi helps him re-shelve them without a hint of dislike.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I came here to buy…a birthday present,”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Two are better than one.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK judges Katsuragi a good guy — the island corn goodwill is the reference — forbidding looks aside.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you giving your girlfriend a present?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t have a girlfriend.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you buying a birthday present?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “One of the boxes of chocolates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re required to wear your uniform if you enter the school,”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Uh, well, I’ve various private matters to attend to,”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Katsuragi raises the shared disadvantage: students may not contact anyone on the outside; breaking it means expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The stipulation that you can’t contact anyone on the outside,”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you want to contact your parents or siblings?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Both the points system, and the quality of the facilities here, are things that ordinary students can only dream of,”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re close with Horikita, aren’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not exactly what either of us wanted, but we were kind of forced into a partnership, I think.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi apologizes if he offended and admits the store visit is his third — he agonizes over decisions when someone&#x27;s feelings are involved.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I offended you, please forgive me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, this is the third time I’ve visited this store.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it strange to celebrate someone’s birthday?”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who’s the gift for?”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s personal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Katsuragi refuses to name the recipient; AK ends the chapter&#x27;s first half with the school-building and store-return mysteries open.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p67-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.3: the crossroads and the offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p79-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.5: the self-gift theory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p79-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki katsuragi-kouhei ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 5  the self gift theory ak reports he found no girl with the august 29 birthday  ike and yamauchi pivot to a new theory   unfortunately  i couldn t find out who the present was for   i think he actually bought the gift for himself  the boys decide katsuragi bought girlish chocolates to look popular   an act for class a s leader   i did the same thing  back in junior high  ike s sympathy flips  they want to give katsuragi a present from others instead of letting him buy his own   we re going to get him a birthday present  ak doubts pity gifts will land and notes the open purchase in uniform still makes no sense under the self gift theory  ak is asked to put in about 1 500 points  his expenses for the week double  the contribution request and the celebrate tomorrow line are printed without speaker tags   are you really buying something  ak decides not to refuse  they agree to meet the next day and disperse","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.5: the self-gift theory<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.79–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">AK reports he found no girl with the August 29 birthday; Ike and Yamauchi pivot to a new theory.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Unfortunately, I couldn’t find out who the present was for,”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “I think he actually bought the gift for himself,”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “I did the same thing, back in junior high,”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The boys decide Katsuragi bought girlish chocolates to look popular — an act for Class A&#x27;s leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike&#x27;s sympathy flips: they want to give Katsuragi a present from others instead of letting him buy his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re going to get him a birthday present.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> AK doubts pity gifts will land and notes the open purchase in uniform still makes no sense under the self-gift theory.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> AK is asked to put in about 1,500 points; his expenses for the week double.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The contribution request and the celebrate-tomorrow line are printed without speaker tags.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you really buying something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> AK decides not to refuse; they agree to meet the next day and disperse.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p74-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.4: trailing Katsuragi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p83-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.6: Kushida joins, and the bench with Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p83-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sakura-airi horikita-suzune chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 6  kushida joins  and the bench with horikita the next afternoon kushida volunteers for the present run  ak walks out in uniform and peels off to talk to horikita  she offers to share the cost because katsuragi has done quite a bit for her too   i ll help out with the present s cost  of course  yamauchi is happier with kushida around even though he is aiming for sakura  ak leaves the group to approach horikita  reading alone outside  horikita is uneasy about the ryuuen loss  ak argues the first semester is over and panic over a small lead is pointless   even after we suffered so much at ryuuen kun s hands   look  we just finished the first semester of our first year   although you can t see what s directly beneath your feet  you re always looking far ahead   i think that it s preferable for you to fall until you hit rock bottom  he credits her academics  says she runs in circles on unusual tests  and ties the island display to his chabashira arrangement   you say there s an order to things  but if that s true  why did you go to all that trouble back on the island  he gave chabashira only a partial display of his abilities to buy time without making a splash   what are you reading today   none of your business   i refuse","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.6: Kushida joins, and the bench with Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.83–87<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The next afternoon Kushida volunteers for the present run; AK walks out in uniform and peels off to talk to Horikita. Horikita is uneasy about the Ryuuen loss; AK argues the first semester is over and panic over a small lead is pointless.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’ll help out with the present’s cost, of course,”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Even after we suffered so much at Ryuuen-kun’s hands?”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Look, we just finished the first semester of our first year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She offers to share the cost because Katsuragi has done quite a bit for her too.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Yamauchi is happier with Kushida around even though he is aiming for Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> AK leaves the group to approach Horikita, reading alone outside.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although you can’t see what’s directly beneath your feet, you’re always looking far ahead.”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think that it’s preferable for you to fall until you hit rock bottom,”<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He credits her academics, says she runs in circles on unusual tests, and ties the island display to his Chabashira arrangement.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You say there’s an order to things, but if that’s true, why did you go to all that trouble back on the island?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> He gave Chabashira only a partial display of his abilities to buy time without making a splash.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you reading today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “None of your business.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse.”<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p79-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.5: the self-gift theory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.7: the student council room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p88-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou katsuragi-kouhei ike-kanji horikita-manabu tachibana-akane ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 7  the student council room the four surround katsuragi to celebrate  kushida fronts  and he stays guarded   isn t it your birthday today  katsuragi kun   if you have an ulterior motive  please tell me  ike swears there is no ulterior motive  genuine sympathy on his face   i thought it was rather unusual to wear that uniform during summer vacation  katsuragi snaps to battle mode over the uniform question  then accepts ak s explanation   nothing to do with you   i think i must ve seen you with it at least three times so far   i have some business with the student council  ak name drops his connection to the president  katsuragi invites him along  they leave the others and knock on the council room door   it would seem we have some unexpected visitors   i heard that student requests go through the student council  outside contact is banned unless a compelling reason such as severe illness or injury  even one sided communication is refused   i d like to send a package and message to my family off campus   even if communication is one sided  it s still not permitted  tachibana  shipping was once permitted until students hid letters in packages  the ban is now complete   so  such contact is now completely banned   this school is all about fostering one s abilities  the points argument changes manabu s attitude  he asks who the package is for   since we re orphans  i m the only one who celebrates her birthday  the twin sister orphan backstory replaces the room s self gift and girlfriend theories outright   the things that are explicitly prohibited can t be easily altered using points   if school rules forbid something  you cannot circumvent them  even with points  rejected  katsuragi glances at ak once and leaves when ak signals he is staying  ak cites the sudou class c trial precedent and pushes manabu to overlook the request quietly   you want to resolve everything without involving the school   what a terrible delinquent you are  ak proves his read  manabu struck someone in public once and got away with it as long as the school did not know   i won t violate the rules for his sake   if you think so  you should have told katsuragi about the loophole before he left   i have no idea what you ll put in it  anyway  at the exit manabu disclaims the meeting officially and grants ak a free hand   even if you act behind the scenes  i won t investigate  ak walks out muttering that the president is shrewd   and suspects his involvement in what follows","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.7: the student council room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.88–94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The four surround Katsuragi to celebrate; Kushida fronts, and he stays guarded.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../world/student-council-room.html\">Student Council Room<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Isn’t it your birthday today, Katsuragi-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “If you have an ulterior motive, please tell me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I thought it was rather unusual to wear that uniform during summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>30 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike swears there is no ulterior motive; genuine sympathy on his face.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi snaps to battle mode over the uniform question, then accepts AK&#x27;s explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing to do with you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think I must’ve seen you with it at least three times so far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have some business with the student council.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> AK name-drops his connection to the president; Katsuragi invites him along; they leave the others and knock on the council room door.<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would seem we have some unexpected visitors.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I heard that student requests go through the student council,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Outside contact is banned unless a compelling reason such as severe illness or injury; even one-sided communication is refused.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to send a package and message to my family off-campus.”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if communication is one-sided, it’s still not permitted,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Tachibana: shipping was once permitted until students hid letters in packages; the ban is now complete.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, such contact is now completely banned,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This school is all about fostering one’s abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The points argument changes Manabu&#x27;s attitude; he asks who the package is for.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Since we’re orphans, I’m the only one who celebrates her birthday,”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The twin-sister-orphan backstory replaces the room&#x27;s self-gift and girlfriend theories outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The things that are explicitly prohibited can’t be easily altered using points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If school rules forbid something, you cannot circumvent them, even with points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Rejected, Katsuragi glances at AK once and leaves when AK signals he is staying.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> AK cites the Sudou–Class C trial precedent and pushes Manabu to overlook the request quietly.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You want to resolve everything without involving the school,”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a terrible delinquent you are,”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK proves his read: Manabu struck someone in public once and got away with it as long as the school did not know.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won’t violate the rules for his sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you think so, you should have told Katsuragi about the loophole before he left.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have no idea what you’ll put in it, anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> At the exit Manabu disclaims the meeting officially and grants AK a free hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you act behind the scenes, I won’t investigate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> AK walks out muttering that the president is shrewd — and suspects his involvement in what follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p83-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.6: Kushida joins, and the bench with Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.8: the offer in the lobby<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p95-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 8  the offer in the lobby in the dorm lobby katsuragi  depressed  tries to hand ak the rejected gift   i don t really care for sweets   it s wasted on me  ak stops him and says he has thought of a way to deliver the present to his sister   i ve thought of a way to deliver the present to your sister   i can t imagine there s a solution  in ak s spartan room he lays out the plan  a student carrying the gift off campus during a club tournament   you have quite a clean room  campus employees come and go but are strictly regulated  leaving without permission means expulsion   the punishment would be incredibly severe  katsuragi works out the exception himself  club tournaments let students travel to outside venues   club tournaments  hmm   there will be bag inspections   they wouldn t search every square inch of your body  ak confirms he has a talented  trustworthy individual in mind   sudou  tournament the day after tomorrow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.8: the offer in the lobby<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.95–97<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the dorm lobby Katsuragi, depressed, tries to hand AK the rejected gift. In AK&#x27;s spartan room he lays out the plan: a student carrying the gift off campus during a club tournament.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “I don’t really care for sweets,”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s wasted on me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve thought of a way to deliver the present to your sister.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> AK stops him and says he has thought of a way to deliver the present to his sister.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t imagine there’s a solution.”<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have quite a clean room.”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Campus employees come and go but are strictly regulated; leaving without permission means expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The punishment would be incredibly severe.”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi works out the exception himself: club tournaments let students travel to outside venues.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Club tournaments, hmm?”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There will be bag inspections,”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “They wouldn’t search every square inch of your body.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> AK confirms he has a talented, trustworthy individual in mind — Sudou, tournament the day after tomorrow.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.7: the student council room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p98-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.9: Sudou takes the job<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p98-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken katsuragi-kouhei horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 9  sudou takes the job an hour after club  ak and katsuragi pitch sudou  he rejects it flatly at first   seriously  who in their right mind would want to do something like that  a promised reward changes sudou s mind  he lays out the tournament logistics   they check our bags in the morning  before we get on the bus to the tournament  ak s transport  gift in the lunchbox  rolled bag in the water bottle   teachers do not check lunch contents  sudou has neither money nor time to mail it  ak hands him a post office invoice as prepaid cover   i ll pay you 100 000 points if you succeed  100 000 points is an incredible amount next to sudou s daily 1 000 2 000  katsuragi explains  twin sister  sickly  relatives caring for her since their parents and grandparents passed  he is the substitute parent   if i don t celebrate her birthday  who will   what am i gonna do if you decide to betray me  sudou s class c trap   near expulsion from the basketball club   is the reason for the caution  20 000 points now as advance  80 000 on completion  the advance proves katsuragi s complicity to both sides   i guess i m someone who ll take that risk  katsuragi stays suspicious even after sudou agrees   his nature  ak notes   katsuragi s the one who came asking for help  and now he doubts me  points will not go to sudou directly  katsuragi pays ak  who transfers after success   insurance against tracing  proof of delivery  a video from ak s phone hidden in the water bottle  since team phones are confiscated  katsuragi offers ak 10 000 points for carrying the phone  ak will borrow a third party s phone   ike s or yamauchi s for 5 000   to keep his own account clean   you know  you re a surprisingly shady guy  the run succeeds  bag check passed  gift mailed  video sent then deleted  sudou handles everything perfectly  ak wonders whether manabu arranged the blind spots   or watched the violation happen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.9: Sudou takes the job<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.98–104<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">An hour after club, AK and Katsuragi pitch Sudou; he rejects it flatly at first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Seriously, who in their right mind would want to do something like that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “They check our bags in the morning, before we get on the bus to the tournament.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “I’ll pay you 100,000 points if you succeed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> A promised reward changes Sudou&#x27;s mind; he lays out the tournament logistics.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK&#x27;s transport: gift in the lunchbox, rolled bag in the water bottle — teachers do not check lunch contents.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Sudou has neither money nor time to mail it; AK hands him a post office invoice as prepaid cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> 100,000 points is an incredible amount next to Sudou&#x27;s daily 1,000–2,000.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi explains: twin sister, sickly, relatives caring for her since their parents and grandparents passed; he is the substitute parent.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I don’t celebrate her birthday, who will?”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What am I gonna do if you decide to betray me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou&#x27;s Class C trap — near expulsion from the basketball club — is the reason for the caution.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> 20,000 points now as advance, 80,000 on completion; the advance proves Katsuragi&#x27;s complicity to both sides.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess I’m someone who’ll take that risk,”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Katsuragi stays suspicious even after Sudou agrees — his nature, AK notes.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi’s the one who came asking for help, and now he doubts me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Points will not go to Sudou directly: Katsuragi pays AK, who transfers after success — insurance against tracing.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Proof of delivery: a video from AK&#x27;s phone hidden in the water bottle, since team phones are confiscated.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Katsuragi offers AK 10,000 points for carrying the phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> AK will borrow a third party&#x27;s phone — Ike&#x27;s or Yamauchi&#x27;s for 5,000 — to keep his own account clean.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You know, you’re a surprisingly shady guy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Result<\/span> The run succeeds: bag check passed, gift mailed, video sent then deleted; Sudou handles everything perfectly.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> AK wonders whether Manabu arranged the blind spots — or watched the violation happen.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.8: the offer in the lobby<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3: after Katsuragi leaves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p105-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  after katsuragi leaves katsuragi exits ayanokoji s room and rides the elevator back to his floor  where two class d students wait with a birthday surprise  the closing scene runs entirely from katsuragi s side  ayanokoji appears only as the room s occupant","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: after Katsuragi leaves<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.105<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Katsuragi exits Ayanokōji&#x27;s room and rides the elevator back to his floor, where two Class D students wait with a birthday surprise.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">The closing scene runs entirely from Katsuragi&#x27;s side; Ayanokōji appears only as the room&#x27;s occupant.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p98-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.9: Sudou takes the job<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the water outage<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p108-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  the water outage  place dormitory  a water department failure at 6 pm cuts the dormitory until early morning  ak cooks fried rice without water and notices horikita s two missed calls  he calls back twice  she doesn t answer either time  and he returns to dinner   yeah  right  two of his texts get instant read receipts and no reply   she couldn t be  she s not really in danger  is she   i m worried  the next text gets no read receipt  he works through theories   battery  sleep  a teacher   and rejects them all   sorry for calling a bunch of times  she sounds tired  says she is mid something  a metallic thunk sounds  and she hangs up abruptly  about 9 00 p m  she texts to ask if he is awake and takes his call on the first ring   so  what s wrong   this isn t like you  he reads the turtle parable as her having no one else to go to   could you come to my room  past nine and on the girls  floor  he grabs only his phone and room key and goes   this is kinda scary   place dormitory  he slips onto the thirteenth floor undetected  her door is unlocked   you re being way too loud  in the bedroom he finds her right hand stuck inside a small water bottle   this water bottle got stuck because i tried to wash my hand  pulling only drags her closer  she has already fought the bottle alone for over two hours   it s no use   place cafeteria  the outage runs to twelve  the cafeteria is out of water and every vending machine is sold out   i ve never seen a completely sold out vending machine before  he offers ike or sudou as a water source  she refuses their water on principle  a second dry pull fails  the bottle only comes off with soap and water","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the water outage<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.108–119<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">[place:dormitory] A water-department failure at 6 PM cuts the dormitory until early morning; AK cooks fried rice without water and notices Horikita&#x27;s two missed calls.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yeah, right,”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She couldn’t be… She’s not really in danger, is she?”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m worried.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He calls back twice; she doesn&#x27;t answer either time, and he returns to dinner.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Two of his texts get instant read receipts and no reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The next text gets no read receipt; he works through theories — battery, sleep, a teacher — and rejects them all.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry for calling a bunch of times.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She sounds tired, says she is mid-something, a metallic thunk sounds, and she hangs up abruptly.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> About 9:00 P.M. she texts to ask if he is awake and takes his call on the first ring.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, what’s wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This isn’t like you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He reads the turtle parable as her having no one else to go to.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could you come to my room?”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Past nine and on the girls&#x27; floor, he grabs only his phone and room key and goes.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is kinda scary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> [place:dormitory] He slips onto the thirteenth floor undetected; her door is unlocked.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re being way too loud,”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In the bedroom he finds her right hand stuck inside a small water bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This water bottle got stuck because I tried to wash my hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pulling only drags her closer; she has already fought the bottle alone for over two hours.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s no use.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> [place:cafeteria] The outage runs to twelve; the cafeteria is out of water and every vending machine is sold out.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve never seen a completely sold-out vending machine before,”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He offers Ike or Sudou as a water source; she refuses their water on principle.<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A second dry pull fails; the bottle only comes off with soap and water.<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3: after Katsuragi leaves<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: the run for water<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p120-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 4 4 6  the run for water with every local source dry  ak proposes hirata and then kushida or sakura  horikita vetoes kushida on the spot  hirata doesn t pick up  and his chat stays unread   i m not getting a response   but that s just speculation on your part   you have to win at all costs   if kushida did manipulate you all into outcome  1  that s honestly amazing  he privately guesses ryuuen or katsuragi forced the dragon group s outcome   he can t tell which   besides  you re maturing  sakura s chat goes unread  he proposes the keyaki mall run   we ll head to keyaki mall for water  his friends are out for karaoke  so there is no cover from them   then you have to take a risk  too   let s get this over with  then  he covers the bottle with her handkerchief  then a folded bath towel  the towel and bag ideas die  they go out as they are   okay  no sign of anyone  let s go  he leads her to the emergency stairs  maezono s door opens three rooms behind them and kushida steps out unseen  the forgotten phone turns kushida back  she greets them and the east stairwell turns out to be locked and power out   oh  uh  we were just thinking of taking the stairs  horikita refuses the water offer by pressing the bottle into his back  students fill the lobby and a voice sounds on the stairs  forced back  he stands in front of the lobby camera as cover   well  we re safe for now  but this is just the beginning  the elevator stops at the fifth floor  kouenji boards and orders the top floor  kouenji never looks their way  sakura s reply finally arrives with water on offer   apparently  sakura has water   what a terrifying woman  the bottle comes off after a long struggle  he heads back to his own room   there it s off   before you go issuing warnings  isn t there something else you d like to say first   that s just so unlike you  horikita  alone  he tests the same bottle on his own hand and gets stuck   i i think i m trapped","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: the run for water<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.120–131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With every local source dry, AK proposes Hirata and then Kushida or Sakura; Horikita vetoes Kushida on the spot.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not getting a response.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“But that’s just speculation on your part.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You have to win at all costs.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>28 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hirata doesn&#x27;t pick up, and his chat stays unread.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If Kushida did manipulate you all into Outcome #1, that’s honestly amazing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He privately guesses Ryuuen or Katsuragi forced the Dragon group&#x27;s outcome — he can&#x27;t tell which.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, you’re maturing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sakura&#x27;s chat goes unread; he proposes the Keyaki Mall run.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll head to Keyaki Mall for water.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> His friends are out for karaoke, so there is no cover from them.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then you have to take a risk, too,”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s get this over with, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He covers the bottle with her handkerchief, then a folded bath towel.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The towel and bag ideas die; they go out as they are.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay, no sign of anyone. Let’s go,”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He leads her to the emergency stairs; Maezono&#x27;s door opens three rooms behind them and Kushida steps out unseen.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The forgotten phone turns Kushida back; she greets them and the east stairwell turns out to be locked and power-out.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, uh. We were just thinking of taking the stairs.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Horikita refuses the water offer by pressing the bottle into his back.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Students fill the lobby and a voice sounds on the stairs; forced back, he stands in front of the lobby camera as cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, we’re safe for now, but…this is just the beginning,”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The elevator stops at the fifth floor: Kouenji boards and orders the top floor.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Kouenji never looks their way; Sakura&#x27;s reply finally arrives with water on offer.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Apparently, Sakura has water.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a terrifying woman.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The bottle comes off after a long struggle; he heads back to his own room.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There—it’s off,”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Before you go issuing warnings, isn’t there something else you’d like to say first?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s just so unlike you, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Alone, he tests the same bottle on his own hand and gets stuck.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I-I think I’m trapped!”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the water outage<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the letter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p132-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 1  the letter yamauchi bursts in on the last days of vacation with a printed love letter and drafts ak to proofread and deliver it  ak lets him in with barley tea and admits he owes him one after the old phone number bargain  the debt runs to a promise ak made without sakura s consent that made yamauchi look foolish in horikita s eyes   and overly formal at the beginning   why is it printed  instead of handwritten   that s no good   are you seriously planning on confessing your love to her  he agrees to proofread and then to deliver after yamauchi claps  bows and begs   but what matters is how sakura feels   i ll deliver your letter   should i really hand the letter over for you   does an indirect love letter really have any value   look  i just think getting a confession of love from someone you can t see is scary   i think you should reconsider  sakura arrives  yamauchi flees the phone call  ak is left holding the letter   kushida called you here  right   to tell you the truth  i asked kushida for a favor   if you read the contents  you ll understand well enough  he hands the letter over and offers a text or call way to answer   yeah  a love letter  her stammering tells him she still thinks he wrote it  he catches her as she nearly topples and denies that horikita would be angry   just to repeat myself  this letter is from another guy   i already told you that i m the messenger  didn t i   just read it and answer  he refuses to read it with her  she leaves to read alone in her room   has no one ever confessed their feelings to you before   maybe the letter s from someone you like  yamauchi s belief rests on her averted eyes and heavy sighs  ak reads them as exhaustion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the letter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.132–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Yamauchi bursts in on the last days of vacation with a printed love letter and drafts AK to proofread and deliver it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“And overly formal at the beginning,”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why is it printed, instead of handwritten?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s no good.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> AK lets him in with barley tea and admits he owes him one after the old phone-number bargain.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The debt runs to a promise AK made without Sakura&#x27;s consent that made Yamauchi look foolish in Horikita&#x27;s eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you seriously planning on confessing your love to her?”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He agrees to proofread and then to deliver after Yamauchi claps, bows and begs.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what matters is how Sakura feels.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll deliver your letter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Should I really hand the letter over for you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Does an indirect love letter really have any value?”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Look, I just think getting a confession of love from someone you can’t see is scary,”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think you should reconsider.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sakura arrives; Yamauchi flees the phone call; AK is left holding the letter.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida called you here, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, I asked Kushida for a favor.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you read the contents, you’ll understand well enough,”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He hands the letter over and offers a text-or-call way to answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, a love letter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her stammering tells him she still thinks he wrote it.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He catches her as she nearly topples and denies that Horikita would be angry.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just to repeat myself, this letter is from another guy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already told you that I’m the messenger, didn’t I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just read it and answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He refuses to read it with her; she leaves to read alone in her room.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Has no one ever confessed their feelings to you before?”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe the letter’s from someone you like,”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Yamauchi&#x27;s belief rests on her averted eyes and heavy sighs; AK reads them as exhaustion.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: the run for water<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the night call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p144-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 2  the night call sakura s midnight texts turn into a phone call about tomorrow s answer  he lies about doing laundry so she will not feel she woke him   you can t sleep   if i can answer  i will   i ve never dated anyone  and i m not dating anyone currently   i have zero experience  same as you  they chat until she grows drowsy and the call ends","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the night call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.144–146<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakura&#x27;s midnight texts turn into a phone call about tomorrow&#x27;s answer.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You can’t sleep?”<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If I can answer, I will.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve never dated anyone, and I’m not dating anyone currently.”<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He lies about doing laundry so she will not feel she woke him.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have zero experience, same as you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> They chat until she grows drowsy and the call ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the letter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p147-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.3: the answer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p147-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 3  the answer at four they meet behind the school building  rain soaks them before yamauchi arrives  he refuses her handkerchief  she dries his hair and face anyway  the handkerchief is the one sakura lent him on the uninhabited island   just answer based on how you feel   of course  you can always hold off on answering  too   i see  i suppose you should  for yamauchi s sake   you have nothing to apologize for   if that s your preference  he stays because she grabs his sleeve and asks not to be left alone  yamauchi arrives stiff  ak explains his presence without blame  he watches the first confession he has ever seen in person break down  the phone yamauchi lends repays the help   a third party device on loan   it s okay  because we re friends  sun breaks through the rainclouds as yamauchi runs after sakura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p147-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.3: the answer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.147–152<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At four they meet behind the school building; rain soaks them before Yamauchi arrives.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Just answer based on how you feel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Of course, you can always hold off on answering, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I see. I suppose you should, for Yamauchi’s sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He refuses her handkerchief; she dries his hair and face anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The handkerchief is the one Sakura lent him on the uninhabited island.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have nothing to apologize for.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If that’s your preference,”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He stays because she grabs his sleeve and asks not to be left alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Yamauchi arrives stiff; AK explains his presence without blame.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He watches the first confession he has ever seen in person break down.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> The phone Yamauchi lends repays the help — a third-party device on loan.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s okay, because…we’re friends,”<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sun breaks through the rainclouds as Yamauchi runs after Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the night call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p153-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the rest-area deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p153-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  the rest area deal on a sweltering day he meets karuizawa at the deserted rest area between dorm and school   a clandestine spot  the cruise ship partnership left her vip identity hidden and 500 000 points coming in september   some students might get as many as 1 000 000 or 2 000 000 points   if you retain ten to twenty percent of your monthly points  that should be enough  he asks for a favor and hands her his unopened tea bottle  the cap joke lands poorly   does the school really not know that you were bullied before   i m not reopening old wounds for no reason   you realize that the world is magnificently rotten  don t you   from now on  you re forbidden to do anything that supports bullying others   prevent yourself from becoming a victim  stop   do i need a reason   i m asking for sakura s sake   i ll bring in hirata and even chabashira sensei to eliminate your enemies   i m always like this  i guess   what would you say is the specific difference between me right now  and the usual me  he compares himself at enrollment to liquid or moldable clay  not yet a full person   i want you to join us   i sympathize  but you basically can t refuse  can you   my decision s final   i still can t trust her   she makes an excellent cover for me  like a magic cloak of invisibility  he uses her as a conspicuous cover while acting entirely on his own since the ship  they head for the pool to take care of something in advance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the rest-area deal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.153–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On a sweltering day he meets Karuizawa at the deserted rest area between dorm and school — a clandestine spot.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Some students might get as many as 1,000,000 or 2,000,000 points,”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you retain ten to twenty percent of your monthly points, that should be enough,”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Does the school really not know that you were bullied before?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The cruise-ship partnership left her VIP identity hidden and 500,000 points coming in September.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He asks for a favor and hands her his unopened tea bottle; the cap joke lands poorly.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not reopening old wounds for no reason.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You realize that the world is magnificently rotten, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “From now on, you’re forbidden to do anything that supports bullying others.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “prevent yourself from becoming a victim, stop.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do I need a reason?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m asking for Sakura’s sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll bring in Hirata and even Chabashira-sensei to eliminate your enemies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m always like this, I guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What would you say is the specific difference between me right now, and the usual me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He compares himself at enrollment to liquid or moldable clay, not yet a full person.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want you to join us,”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I sympathize, but you basically can’t refuse, can you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My decision’s final.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I still can’t trust her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She makes an excellent cover for me, like a magic cloak of invisibility.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He uses her as a conspicuous cover while acting entirely on his own since the ship.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> They head for the pool to take care of something in advance.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p147-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.3: the answer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the invitations<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p163-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the invitations the night before  ike s group chat call to action recruits the girls for the pool   and sudou s friend line recruits ak  he answers the chat with a noncommittal promise to see what he can do   can t i call you without a reason   wait  wait   water bottle   you have a very unpleasant phone manner   we ll meet at 8 30 in the lobby  and plan to go our separate ways in the evening  he frames the coercion as cashing in the favor from the water bottle night  then calls sakura","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the invitations<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.163–165<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The night before: Ike&#x27;s group-chat call to action recruits the girls for the pool — and Sudou&#x27;s friend line recruits AK.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Can’t I call you without a reason?”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait, wait!”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Water bottle.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He answers the chat with a noncommittal promise to see what he can do.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have a very unpleasant phone manner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’ll meet at 8:30 in the lobby, and plan to go our separate ways in the evening,”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He frames the coercion as cashing in the favor from the water-bottle night, then calls Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p153-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the rest-area deal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p166-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2–6.3: the lobby and the lie<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p166-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 2 6 3  the lobby and the lie at 8 30 the group assembles  sudou is missing and his phone won t connect   there s still about ten seconds left until we were scheduled to meet   it s no use  the call s not connecting   several things happened  he backs sudou s alibi about post pool plans when horikita eyes ike s heavy bag   how d your club activities go  he watches sudou and horikita both for the same tendency  making enemies easily  karuizawa texts that she is in the locker room  he puts his phone away from ike s peek","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p166-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2–6.3: the lobby and the lie<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.166–171<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At 8:30 the group assembles; Sudou is missing and his phone won&#x27;t connect.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s still about ten seconds left until we were scheduled to meet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s no use. The call’s not connecting,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Several things happened,”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He backs Sudou&#x27;s alibi about post-pool plans when Horikita eyes Ike&#x27;s heavy bag.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How’d your club activities go?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He watches Sudou and Horikita both for the same tendency: making enemies easily.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Karuizawa texts that she is in the locker room; he puts his phone away from Ike&#x27;s peek.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the invitations<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p172-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: the pool<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p172-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami sakura-airi kanzaki-ryuuji shibata-sou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 4  the pool the club pool is ringed with food stalls run by upperclassmen  the crowd lifts the group s mood   i don t really like showing skin in front of people  ichinose pokes his rash guarded stomach  he credits katsuragi s payment for the funds  her full body touching makes him invent an excuse to leave  he walks beside sakura and smooths out the thanks with the word friend   we re friends  watching her mature  he thinks he might change too   as long as you re aware of that  isn t it enough  kanzaki singles him out of the rowdy group and he accepts the approach  shibata s proposal joins the class b trio  growing the party to thirteen  he watches the blond upperclassman s volleyball spike and reads real skill behind the looks","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p172-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.4: the pool<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.172–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The club pool is ringed with food stalls run by upperclassmen; the crowd lifts the group&#x27;s mood.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t really like showing skin in front of people.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“We’re friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“As long as you’re aware of that, isn’t it enough?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ichinose pokes his rash-guarded stomach; he credits Katsuragi&#x27;s payment for the funds.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her full-body touching makes him invent an excuse to leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He walks beside Sakura and smooths out the thanks with the word friend.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Watching her mature, he thinks he might change too.<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Kanzaki singles him out of the rowdy group and he accepts the approach.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Shibata&#x27;s proposal joins the Class B trio, growing the party to thirteen.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He watches the blond upperclassman&#x27;s volleyball spike and reads real skill behind the looks.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p166-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2–6.3: the lobby and the lie<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.6: Nagumo, the card, and the walk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p179-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  nagumo  the card  and the walk ayanokoji learns the blond player is nagumo  feints incompetence through the volleyball match  takes karuizawa s plastic object in a private deal by the pool  and ends the vacation on a sunset walk with horikita   what a brazen thing to say praising the president without revealing that he was her brother   wait  do you still think they assigned you to class d by mistake  i asked  he listens as ichinose argues that the school sorts on maturity and collaboration too  and privately notes horikita never announced a student council candidacy  with ichinose gazing at him from across the net  he deliberately fumbles his second receive into the water so no one can read his ability   er  i guess it showed the virtue of scoring quietly  rather than flamboyantly  i replied  it is the first time in his life he has played volleyball  he works out the receive in theory  then chooses to fail on purpose   ichinose was watching me closely  i answered  he calls karuizawa aside alone  saying the class could have been fractured and he wants to avoid that   i m going to have a first year student expelled  he names the three girls who know her past as the ideal candidates  then admits an unnecessary class d student would do   nothing that dramatic took place in my past   my life was a blank slate  he crushes the plastic object in his fist  tosses the bits into a garbage bin  and tells karuizawa he won t expel anyone from class d   i won t expel anyone from class d  he shoves karuizawa into the pool  and when she pulls him in he lets her hold him under rather than resist   did you have fun  i asked   this is really good  i said quietly  on the tree lined path at sunset she admits she had fun and keeps her vacation reflections a secret from him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Nagumo, the card, and the walk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.179–204<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji learns the blond player is Nagumo, feints incompetence through the volleyball match, takes Karuizawa&#x27;s plastic object in a private deal by the pool, and ends the vacation on a sunset walk with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wait. Do you still think they assigned you to Class D by mistake?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Er, I guess it showed the virtue of scoring quietly, rather than flamboyantly?” I replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ichinose was watching me closely,” I answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “What a brazen thing to say—praising the president without revealing that he was her brother.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> He listens as Ichinose argues that the school sorts on maturity and collaboration too, and privately notes Horikita never announced a student council candidacy.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> With Ichinose gazing at him from across the net, he deliberately fumbles his second receive into the water so no one can read his ability.<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> It is the first time in his life he has played volleyball; he works out the receive in theory, then chooses to fail on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He calls Karuizawa aside alone, saying the class could have been fractured and he wants to avoid that.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I&#x27;m going to have a first-year student expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> He names the three girls who know her past as the ideal candidates, then admits an unnecessary Class D student would do.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nothing that dramatic took place in my past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “My life was a blank slate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He crushes the plastic object in his fist, tosses the bits into a garbage bin, and tells Karuizawa he won&#x27;t expel anyone from Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I won&#x27;t expel anyone from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He shoves Karuizawa into the pool, and when she pulls him in he lets her hold him under rather than resist.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you have fun?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is…really good,” I said quietly.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> On the tree-lined path at sunset she admits she had fun and keeps her vacation reflections a secret from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p172-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: the pool<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.7: Operation Delta<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p205-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"action spoken","w":"sotomura-hideo karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  operation delta the three idiots pitch a peeping plan called operation delta in his room  he agrees to hold the human wall only on a one time condition  with a threat to report the scheme otherwise   why is it always  always my room   i can t just go out and spend precious points   call it whatever you want  but it s basically just peeping  he spots that the map s handwriting is not ike s and corners the group with a guess about the professor   did the professor have a hand in this peeping operation  by any chance  i asked   i m not interested  i replied   so  success or failure  promise me that operation delta is the only time you ll try this  he conditions his cooperation on the plan being a one time event  threatening to report it to the school if it is repeated   that s not it at all  he leaves the locker room early so the girls won t grow suspicious  leaving the three to recover the rc car  he had instructed karuizawa ahead of time to swap the memory card in the rc car  his instruction is what turns the recording into an empty card   the sabotage that annihilates the three s ambitions   if you could give that back to me after checking the contents  it would be a big help  i told them   if you want to turn back  now s the time  i warned them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: Operation Delta<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.205–223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The three idiots pitch a peeping plan called Operation Delta in his room; he agrees to hold the human wall only on a one-time condition, with a threat to report the scheme otherwise.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why is it always, always my room?”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I can’t just go out and spend precious points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Call it whatever you want, but it’s basically just peeping.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> He spots that the map’s handwriting is not Ike’s and corners the group with a guess about the Professor.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did the Professor have a hand in this peeping operation, by any chance?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not interested,” I replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, success or failure, promise me that Operation Delta is the only time you’ll try this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He conditions his cooperation on the plan being a one-time event, threatening to report it to the school if it is repeated.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not it at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He leaves the locker room early so the girls won’t grow suspicious, leaving the three to recover the RC car.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He had instructed Karuizawa ahead of time to swap the memory card in the RC car.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His instruction is what turns the recording into an empty card — the sabotage that annihilates the three’s ambitions.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you could give that back to me after checking the contents, it would be a big help,” I told them.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you want to turn back, now’s the time,” I warned them.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.6: Nagumo, the card, and the walk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p224-1\">→ After: Ch.8: a passing mention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p224-1","v":"y1v4.5","y":1,"o":5,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 8  a passing mention named only in the author s afterword  which points his future at the next volume  the author says the growing circle of girls around him may hide a future romantic development  the next volume will finally learn something about his past  with new rivals and a new special exam ahead  the bonus stories teased after the postscript promise the true motive behind his mysterious actions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p224-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8: a passing mention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V4.5 · p.224–225<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named only in the author’s afterword, which points his future at the next volume.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The author says the growing circle of girls around him may hide a future romantic development.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The next volume will finally learn something about his past, with new rivals and a new special exam ahead.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bonus stories teased after the postscript promise the true motive behind his mysterious actions.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v4_5-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.7: Operation Delta<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p13-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  the zodiac debrief at pallet back table of the crowded cafe pallet after summer vacation  ayanokoji sits with hirata  karuizawa and horikita  reviewing the cruise ship zodiac exam and its hidden vips  the rabbit group read alphabetically   ayanokouji kun  ichinose san  ibuki san  karuizawa san   made him the rabbit vip  the dragon group s fifth name was kushida san   i honestly don t have a clue    lied to the group when horikita asked what he thought  notices karuizawa has started calling hirata yousuke kun  he meets her gaze and she diverts her eyes  plays along as the cooperative nobody while hirata works to cement the four person group  exchanges the no presence   long shadows banter with her  she is not joking when she takes the bait  names sudou among the athletic students the festival is built to give their first real opening","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.13–15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back table of the crowded café Pallet after summer vacation: Ayanokōji sits with Hirata, Karuizawa and Horikita, reviewing the cruise-ship zodiac exam and its hidden VIPs.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I honestly don’t have a clue” — lied to the group when Horikita asked what he thought.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The rabbit group read alphabetically — Ayanokouji-kun, Ichinose-san, Ibuki-san, Karuizawa-san — made him the rabbit VIP; the dragon group’s fifth name was Kushida-san.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Notices Karuizawa has started calling Hirata Yousuke-kun; he meets her gaze and she diverts her eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Plays along as the cooperative nobody while Hirata works to cement the four-person group.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Exchanges the no-presence / long-shadows banter with her; she is not joking when she takes the bait.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Names Sudou among the athletic students the festival is built to give their first real opening.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the rules and the huddle<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  the rules and the huddle afternoon homeroom becomes a two hour session  chabashira announces the september sports festival and its handout  the class erupts  teases her about finally having an opportunity to get in touch with her brother on the red team  she glares and tells him to drop it   at least you have an opportunity to get in touch now  huh  watches the huddle from the side   ike and yamauchi push for personal chances against the class s interest  yamauchi is present at the huddle  no line of his is tagged in the translation   it s a sad fact of reality    answering horikita s complaint that only guys like these come to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the rules and the huddle<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.16–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Afternoon homeroom becomes a two-hour session: Chabashira announces the September sports festival and its handout; the class erupts.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“At least you have an opportunity to get in touch now, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s a sad fact of reality,” — answering Horikita’s complaint that only guys like these come to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Teases her about finally having an opportunity to get in touch with her brother on the Red Team; she glares and tells him to drop it.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Watches the huddle from the side — Ike and Yamauchi push for personal chances against the class’s interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Yamauchi is present at the huddle; no line of his is tagged in the translation.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the zodiac debrief at Pallet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: the Red Team assembly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2  the red team assembly over four hundred people gather in gymnasium 1  fujimaki takes red team command  first year class a assembles under katsuragi  ryuuen walks class c out  sakayanagi arisu is introduced  and ayanokoji and horikita argue strategy in the corner  notes that the student council president does not take red team command and wonders when he will make a move  takes the class a class d pact at face value   no shared competition details  only a promise not to get in each other s way  reads the gym s layout  a clear line between katsuragi s followers and nearly all the students sitting with sakayanagi  reconsiders which faction is superior  cites her as the kind who might put feelings aside for victory if ryuuen and class b reconcile  warns horikita that ryuuen likely already has one or more tactics in mind for the festival   the school has never once called the festival a  special exam   i think the sports festival is supposed to do the same with our physical abilities   you re looking for loopholes   you re not thinking big enough    his read on horikita s tunnel vision   we need to make sure that we re prepared  that s all there is to it   there s a good chance that he has a plan in place   we have to think like that to rise to class a s level  has studied ryuuen s strategies and thought processes ever since the fight that nearly got sudou expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2: the Red Team assembly<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.26–34<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Over four hundred people gather in Gymnasium 1: Fujimaki takes Red Team command, first-year Class A assembles under Katsuragi, Ryuuen walks Class C out, Sakayanagi Arisu is introduced, and Ayanokōji and Horikita argue strategy in the corner.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The school has never once called the festival a ‘special exam.’”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I think the sports festival is supposed to do the same with our physical abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re looking for loopholes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Notes that the student council president does not take Red Team command and wonders when he will make a move.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Takes the Class A–Class D pact at face value — no shared competition details, only a promise not to get in each other’s way.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reads the gym’s layout: a clear line between Katsuragi’s followers and nearly all the students sitting with Sakayanagi; reconsiders which faction is superior.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Cites her as the kind who might put feelings aside for victory if Ryuuen and Class B reconcile.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Warns Horikita that Ryuuen likely already has one or more tactics in mind for the festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re not thinking big enough,” — his read on Horikita’s tunnel vision.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We need to make sure that we’re prepared. That’s all there is to it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s a good chance that he has a plan in place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We have to think like that to rise to Class A’s level,”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has studied Ryuuen’s strategies and thought processes ever since the fight that nearly got Sudou expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the rules and the huddle<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the gate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  the gate after class he stays behind alone with a file on his phone   whatever it showed  he decides no traps are necessary   then runs into chabashira spraying water at the main gate   are you on duty today   don t you think that s an exaggeration   no  nothing like that    to chabashira s guess that he already has an eccentric strategy in place   i m free to decide my own path  she warns that if he shows no results soon she ll stop covering for him  the confrontation was only a matter of time  blank page inside the dialogue  page number and watermark only  p 38 is likewise blank","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the gate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.35–38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After class he stays behind alone with a file on his phone — whatever it showed, he decides no traps are necessary — then runs into Chabashira spraying water at the main gate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Are you on duty today?”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t you think that’s an exaggeration?”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, nothing like that,” — to Chabashira’s guess that he already has an eccentric strategy in place.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m free to decide my own path.”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She warns that if he shows no results soon she’ll stop covering for him; the confrontation was only a matter of time.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page inside the dialogue (page number and watermark only); p.38 is likewise blank.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p26-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: the Red Team assembly<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3: The blackboard vote, the betrayal warning, the roster<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3  the blackboard vote  the betrayal warning  the roster class 1 d homeroom  hirata chalks two systems for the sports festival while ayanokoji narrates the class s first real strategy meeting of the volume   we began making comprehensive preparations for the sports festival  which was only one month away  lets horikita s jab about his phone pass  then stays out of the debate   well  if i just leave it to you and hirata  you ll sort out our problems  right   relax  it s my policy to abstain from voting   the other students aren t all as ambitious as you    he votes for no one while the class splits 16 13  after class he texts karuizawa    no matter what  object to horikita s plan  then ask kushida for her opinion    and meets her at the main entrance   when it comes to improvising  you re quite fast on your feet   besides  i m under no compunction to answer your questions   i m not personally interested in reaching class a  tells karuizawa   one of our classmates will betray us during this sports festival   yes  i ve prepared   now then  i wonder what class a has in mind    katsuragi will be solid  and sakayanagi would be good for the white team and for class d  life jacket parable  in a crisis the able bodied are favored  so  just because sakayanagi wasn t physically active didn t mean she was harmless   karuizawa was better at reading people than i d imagined  probably because of her past  measures 60 6 kilograms of grip strength on the first try   second in the class behind sudou s 82 4  with koenji set aside   having aimed carefully at the average  stops the meter just over 60 once he has worked out that 60 is roughly the average he was aiming for   i see  so  60 was high  then  wins the first round and the second and final round of rock paper scissors despite praying to lose  and is picked for the scavenger hunt team against his wishes  admits the roster problem    many participants were chosen against their will    and horikita answers that the class s athletic gap is to blame","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3: The blackboard vote, the betrayal warning, the roster<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.39–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class 1-D homeroom: Hirata chalks two systems for the sports festival while Ayanokōji narrates the class’s first real strategy meeting of the volume.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Relax. It’s my policy to abstain from voting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The other students aren’t all as ambitious as you,” — he votes for no one while the class splits 16–13.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“When it comes to improvising, you’re quite fast on your feet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “We began making comprehensive preparations for the sports festival, which was only one month away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lets Horikita’s jab about his phone pass, then stays out of the debate: “Well, if I just leave it to you and Hirata, you’ll sort out our problems, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After class he texts Karuizawa — “No matter what, object to Horikita’s plan. Then ask Kushida for her opinion.” — and meets her at the main entrance.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, I’m under no compunction to answer your questions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not personally interested in reaching Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Unverified<\/span> Tells Karuizawa: “One of our classmates will betray us during this sports festival.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I’ve prepared.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Now then, I wonder what Class A has in mind?” — Katsuragi will be solid, and Sakayanagi would be good for the White Team and for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Life-jacket parable: in a crisis the able-bodied are favored, so “just because Sakayanagi wasn’t physically active didn’t mean she was harmless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Karuizawa was better at reading people than I’d imagined, probably because of her past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Measures 60.6 kilograms of grip strength on the first try — second in the class behind Sudou’s 82.4, with Kōenji set aside — having aimed carefully at the average.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Stops the meter just over 60 once he has worked out that 60 is roughly the average he was aiming for.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I see. So, 60 was high, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Wins the first round and the second and final round of rock-paper-scissors despite praying to lose, and is picked for the scavenger-hunt team against his wishes.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Admits the roster problem — “Many participants were chosen against their will,” — and Horikita answers that the class’s athletic gap is to blame.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p35-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: the gate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p42-1\">→ After: Ch.3–9: passing mentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p42-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 9  passing mentions named across class strategy and festival margins where he is not the section s focus  class d s blackboard vote and grip strength context name him among the planners  entrance betrayal warning pages keep him in the room s orbit  letter plan margins  he is present but the beat tracks horikita s plan  kushida s sonoda kun remark sits in a scene he observes  strategy talk with horikita and kushida names him as the third party  festival opening  he is among the class ranks  not a named actor  capture the flag charge and its aftermath name him in the rush  hurdle results page  ike demands his place  he answers third  lunch and leak talk margins after the punch cover  dorm walk with karuizawa after the class falls apart  nurse s office aftermath  chabashira s report names him in the cover story  scavenger hunt absence math when sudou and horikita are missing  three legged staging  he is the substitute conversation s other half  ally bargain close with sudou already stamped in ch8 s main rows  horikita s hallway wait names his direction home after the festival  ryuuen s appointment scene  she prepared to face him as well as ryuuen  after the counter recording  the mastermind hypothesis lands on him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3–9: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.42, 49, 74, 79, 81, 88, 101–102, 111, 129, 133, 146, 165, 173, 179, 194–195, 201<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named across class strategy and festival margins where he is not the section’s focus.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Class D’s blackboard vote and grip-strength context name him among the planners.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Entrance-betrayal warning pages keep him in the room’s orbit.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Letter-plan margins; he is present but the beat tracks Horikita’s plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida’s Sonoda-kun remark sits in a scene he observes.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Strategy talk with Horikita and Kushida names him as the third party.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Festival opening; he is among the class ranks, not a named actor.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Capture-the-flag charge and its aftermath name him in the rush.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hurdle results page: Ike demands his place; he answers third.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Lunch and leak-talk margins after the punch cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Dorm walk with Karuizawa after the class falls apart.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nurse’s office aftermath; Chabashira’s report names him in the cover story.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Scavenger-hunt absence math when Sudou and Horikita are missing.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Three-legged staging; he is the substitute conversation’s other half.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ally-bargain close with Sudou already stamped in ch8’s main rows.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita’s hallway wait names his direction home after the festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen’s appointment scene: she prepared to face him as well as Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After the counter-recording, the mastermind hypothesis lands on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p39-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3: The blackboard vote, the betrayal warning, the roster<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4: The Ryuuen read, the partner lesson, the two problems<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4  the ryuuen read  the partner lesson  the two problems first independent practice on the athletic grounds  class a and b watch from the windows  class c does not  and ayanokoji and horikita talk strategy at the edge of the field  reads the missing reconnaissance as the tell   he s making it obvious by not bothering to do any reconnaissance   normally  when someone has a secret plan in place  they do whatever it takes to ensure that their enemies don t figure it out  lets her pin him down on his pe record    nope  i m not confident    after she calls his scores average   i m sorry to disappoint  but what you see is what you get   would i do something so pointless    when she asks if he is holding back like he did on tests   you ll learn the answer to that soon enough  pairs with hirata for three legged practice after horikita s partnership with onodera collapses  finds the rhythm quickly   hirata s praise makes the awkward drill feel simple  invites himself as her three legged partner   partner with me for the three legged race  outpaces her on purpose  then gives the lesson   this wasn t about fast or slow   the important thing is to work with your partner  names his two problems for the class  horikita  who cannot keep a partner  and kushida  whose rooftop darkness and hatred of horikita must be confronted   therefore  the only way to resolve the issue was to have them confront one another  the praise after sakura s last place finish    you really gave it your all    carries no speaker tag  sakura s reply addresses ayanokouji kun  so it is recorded here rather than assigned outright","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4: The Ryuuen read, the partner lesson, the two problems<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.54–67<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">First independent practice on the athletic grounds: Class A and B watch from the windows, Class C does not, and Ayanokōji and Horikita talk strategy at the edge of the field.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Normally, when someone has a secret plan in place, they do whatever it takes to ensure that their enemies don’t figure it out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reads the missing reconnaissance as the tell: “He’s making it obvious by not bothering to do any reconnaissance,”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Lets her pin him down on his PE record — “Nope, I’m not confident.” — after she calls his scores average.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m sorry to disappoint, but what you see is what you get.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Would I do something so pointless?” — when she asks if he is holding back like he did on tests.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’ll learn the answer to that soon enough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Pairs with Hirata for three-legged practice after Horikita’s partnership with Onodera collapses.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Finds the rhythm quickly — Hirata’s praise makes the awkward drill feel simple.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Invites himself as her three-legged partner: “Partner with me for the three-legged race.”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Outpaces her on purpose, then gives the lesson: “This wasn’t about fast or slow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “The important thing is to work with your partner.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Names his two problems for the class: Horikita, who cannot keep a partner, and Kushida, whose rooftop darkness and hatred of Horikita must be confronted.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Therefore, the only way to resolve the issue was to have them confront one another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The praise after Sakura’s last-place finish — “You really gave it your all.” — carries no speaker tag; Sakura’s reply addresses Ayanokouji-kun, so it is recorded here rather than assigned outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p42-1\">← Before: Ch.3–9: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5: The invitation, the theory, the exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ike-kanji sudou-ken shibata-sou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5  the invitation  the theory  the exit two weeks before the festival  ayanokoji recruits horikita and kushida for a saturday reconnaissance   the first move against  the bomb waiting to go off inside class d   hang out with me today   you ll understand better if you come with me   kushida  do you have a minute   by the way  horikita will be coming  too   doing a little reconnaissance isn t a bad thing  wouldn t you agree  the theory  flat out   one other person was significantly involved in the outcome on the cruise ship   but what about kushida herself  what if she intentionally exposed her identity   only kushida knows    which is why she is invited   you and kushida seem to have some kind of connection  elevator parting   you re free to choose whether or not you come tomorrow  but if you want to lead the class  think about it  probes ike and yamauchi for sakayanagi rumors and gets nothing usable  deflects the message suspicion    absolutely not  so relax  leaves the three to their noodle talk    sorry  guys  i ve got plans  owns the setup when kushida calls it   why do you think that   it s like i half believe it  and half don t  asks the question outright   why don t you and horikita like each other  tells hirata the truth of the outing    we re spying  sets the stage for horikita s vip question  then leaves the two girls alone  glosses horikita s brother trouble for the group    some stuff happened  i guess horikita and her brother aren t really on speaking terms","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5: The invitation, the theory, the exit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.68–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two weeks before the festival, Ayanokōji recruits Horikita and Kushida for a Saturday reconnaissance — the first move against “the bomb waiting to go off inside Class D.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hang out with me today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’ll understand better if you come with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Kushida, do you have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “By the way, Horikita will be coming, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Doing a little reconnaissance isn’t a bad thing, wouldn’t you agree?”<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The theory, flat out: “One other person was significantly involved in the outcome on the cruise ship,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “But what about Kushida herself? What if she intentionally exposed her identity?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Only Kushida knows.” — which is why she is invited.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You and Kushida seem to have some kind of connection.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Elevator parting: “You’re free to choose whether or not you come tomorrow, but if you want to lead the class, think about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Probes Ike and Yamauchi for Sakayanagi rumors and gets nothing usable.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Deflects the message suspicion — “Absolutely not, so relax.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Leaves the three to their noodle talk — “Sorry, guys. I’ve got plans.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Owns the setup when Kushida calls it: “Why do you think that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “It’s like I half believe it, and half don’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Asks the question outright: “Why don’t you and Horikita like each other?”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Tells Hirata the truth of the outing — “We’re spying.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Sets the stage for Horikita’s VIP question, then leaves the two girls alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Glosses Horikita’s brother trouble for the group — “Some stuff happened. I guess Horikita and her brother aren’t really on speaking terms.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4: The Ryuuen read, the partner lesson, the two problems<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6: festival day, first events<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji sakura-airi horikita-suzune yukimura-teruhiko katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6  festival day  first events sports festival day opens  fujimaki s speech  medical cottage and facing team tents  a camera on the 100 metre finish line  class d marches in jerseys   all right  time to really show off for kikyou chan  shouted ike as he walked directly behind me  tells horikita he drew the seventh group for the 100 metre dash  his only aim is not to come in last  watches sudou win group one by a landslide and hirata take first in group seven  he finishes fifth  keeping his pace inconspicuous  spots sudou missing from the seat and runs with hirata toward the cottage as sudou confronts koenji  when sakura asks if he watched her race  he answers  you did well  without admitting he had been chasing sudou  after the girls  dash he asks whether she reached out to koenji  she lets slip  i never hated her or anything  about kushida and clamps down  holds third in the hurdles and trades talk with kanzaki  who reports ichinose s read of him as calm for a high schooler  gives yukimura room after seventh and seventh  then turns to the girls  hurdles  in capture the flag he brings up the rear with ike and yukimura while sudou tears into the defense  after sudou is dropped he keeps his distance  walks back with hirata and katsuragi exchanging apologies after the flag falls  talks sudou out of a new scandal  recalling the fight that almost got him expelled  and accepts class c will call the stomp heat of the moment  pulls in the d a tug of war under hirata and katsuragi  after ryuuen s rope drop he is thrown backward with the rest  takes third in the obstacle heat to avoid sudou s wrath  then watches sudou edge shibata for first  leaves hirata in charge of the group and goes to horikita after her fall  he judges that another such  accident  would be too much to believe  treats the stacked mishaps as deliberate and takes hirata s uneasy agreement as confirmation someone is working the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6: festival day, first events<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.86–114<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sports festival day opens: Fujimaki’s speech, medical cottage and facing team tents, a camera on the 100-metre finish line; Class D marches in jerseys.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “All right, time to really show off for Kikyou-chan!” shouted Ike as he walked directly behind me.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Tells Horikita he drew the seventh group for the 100-metre dash; his only aim is not to come in last.<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Watches Sudou win group one by a landslide and Hirata take first in group seven; he finishes fifth, keeping his pace inconspicuous.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Spots Sudou missing from the seat and runs with Hirata toward the cottage as Sudou confronts Kōenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> When Sakura asks if he watched her race, he answers “You did well,” without admitting he had been chasing Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> After the girls’ dash he asks whether she reached out to Kōenji; she lets slip “I never hated her or anything” about Kushida and clamps down.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Holds third in the hurdles and trades talk with Kanzaki, who reports Ichinose’s read of him as calm for a high schooler.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Gives Yukimura room after seventh-and-seventh, then turns to the girls’ hurdles.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In capture the flag he brings up the rear with Ike and Yukimura while Sudou tears into the defense; after Sudou is dropped he keeps his distance.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Walks back with Hirata and Katsuragi exchanging apologies after the flag falls.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Talks Sudou out of a new scandal, recalling the fight that almost got him expelled, and accepts Class C will call the stomp heat-of-the-moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pulls in the D/A tug-of-war under Hirata and Katsuragi; after Ryuuen’s rope-drop he is thrown backward with the rest.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes third in the obstacle heat to avoid Sudou’s wrath, then watches Sudou edge Shibata for first.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Leaves Hirata in charge of the group and goes to Horikita after her fall; he judges that another such “accident” would be too much to believe.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Treats the stacked mishaps as deliberate and takes Hirata’s uneasy agreement as confirmation someone is working the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5: The invitation, the theory, the exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.7–6.10: observation, cavalry, and the plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 7 6 10  observation  cavalry  and the plan second half opens mid conversation with injured horikita after the obstacle fall  ayanokoji then runs three legged  watches the cavalry battles  confronts the leak with karuizawa  and sends horikita after sudou  learns kinoshita called horikita s name to force the collision  notes horikita has thirty points to his twenty seven   i ll do everything i can  watches sudou carry ike to three legged first  then pairs with hirata for their own first place  sees horikita and kushida fade to last in the girls  three legged as the leg injury tells  later names the stack of hard matchups as deliberate  stays through the ten minute break observing class a s two faction split and asks hirata what kind of student sakayanagi is   amazing that they ve gotten this far with such internal discord  reads her silence and single focus on katsuragi as willingness to lose points for his downfall  serves as a right side horse under hirata s jockey in the boys  cavalry  holds position while sudou crashes the line and hirata twice grabs ryuuen s headband  watches the one on one bait take sudou  then the hair gel trick that makes the stolen headband unprovable  explains the leak  the fixed matchups and the horikita crush to karuizawa  answers  no intention of winning  with  do nothing   she s being targeted   win  i have no intention of winning  keeps distance while sudou punches hirata and walks off  tells karuizawa the mess has nothing to do with him  takes third in the 200 metre dash  then delivers the  burden  and  weapon  confrontation that is meant to wake horikita and send her for sudou   you re nothing but a burden   how long do you plan to be useless  horikita   i m calling you useless because you are useless  calls her useless on purpose so she will reclaim sudou as her asset for class a s climb  at lunch he lies to hirata and karuizawa that the traitor acts on horikita s orders  the morning ends with horikita and sudou both missing   i ve taken stock of the traitor s moral fiber   yeah  everything is going according to horikita s plan  runs a deliberate double game  full analysis for his inner circle  controlled misinformation for the class  and one surgical pressure campaign on horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.7–6.10: observation, cavalry, and the plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.115–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second half opens mid-conversation with injured Horikita after the obstacle fall; Ayanokōji then runs three-legged, watches the cavalry battles, confronts the leak with Karuizawa, and sends Horikita after Sudou.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll do everything I can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Amazing that they’ve gotten this far with such internal discord,”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She’s being targeted,”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Learns Kinoshita called Horikita’s name to force the collision; notes Horikita has thirty points to his twenty-seven.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Watches Sudou carry Ike to three-legged first, then pairs with Hirata for their own first place.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sees Horikita and Kushida fade to last in the girls’ three-legged as the leg injury tells; later names the stack of hard matchups as deliberate.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stays through the ten-minute break observing Class A’s two-faction split and asks Hirata what kind of student Sakayanagi is.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119, sec. 6.7<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reads her silence and single focus on Katsuragi as willingness to lose points for his downfall.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Serves as a right-side horse under Hirata’s jockey in the boys’ cavalry; holds position while Sudou crashes the line and Hirata twice grabs Ryuuen’s headband.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–129, sec. 6.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Watches the one-on-one bait take Sudou, then the hair-gel trick that makes the stolen headband unprovable.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Explains the leak, the fixed matchups and the Horikita crush to Karuizawa; answers “no intention of winning” with “do nothing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Win? I have no intention of winning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Keeps distance while Sudou punches Hirata and walks off; tells Karuizawa the mess has nothing to do with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Takes third in the 200-metre dash, then delivers the “burden” and “weapon” confrontation that is meant to wake Horikita and send her for Sudou.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–139, sec. 6.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re nothing but a burden.”<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How long do you plan to be useless, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m calling you useless because you are useless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls her useless on purpose so she will reclaim Sudou as her asset for Class A’s climb.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> At lunch he lies to Hirata and Karuizawa that the traitor acts on Horikita’s orders; the morning ends with Horikita and Sudou both missing.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–142, sec. 6.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve taken stock of the traitor’s moral fiber,”<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. Everything is going according to Horikita’s plan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Runs a deliberate double game: full analysis for his inner circle, controlled misinformation for the class, and one surgical pressure campaign on Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6: festival day, first events<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7: the beatdown already landed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7  the beatdown already landed horikita walks to the nurse s office still stinging from ayanokouji s earlier speech  horikita admits he was absolutely right and she had no reply","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7: the beatdown already landed<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.144<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita walks to the nurse’s office still stinging from Ayanokouji’s earlier speech.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita admits he was absolutely right and she had no reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p115-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.7–6.10: observation, cavalry, and the plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: declines the search<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 2  declines the search on the field after horikita s failed search  ayanokouji notes her breath and refuses to come along   you sound like you re out of breath   is your leg all right   i ll pass  i d only end up getting in your way  she treats sudou as an asset she accepts  he lets her go alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.2: declines the search<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.158<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the field after Horikita’s failed search, Ayanokouji notes her breath and refuses to come along.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“You sound like you’re out of breath,”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is your leg all right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll pass. I’d only end up getting in your way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She treats Sudou as an asset she accepts; he lets her go alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7: the beatdown already landed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1\">→ After: Ch.8 sec. 8: the scavenger hunt draws<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 8 sec  8  the scavenger hunt draws second half opens with ayanokouji stuck in the scavenger hunt after losing rock paper scissors  while sudou and horikita are both missing   you re participating in the scavenger hunt  right  ayanokouji kun   i d rather not  if possible   hirata  you don t need my opinion to make a sound decision  right   we need 100 000 points to put in a substitute  i ll figure something out with the points  i think we d do well substituting ike kun or yamauchi kun   that s because  if they do happen to take first place  they ll be able to put points toward their tests  right   so  that muscle headed moron won t be participating in the scavenger hunt  huh   no idea  that has nothing to do with me   ayanokouji  lend me your left foot  your left foot   my left foot   your shoe  dude  your shoe  that s my item   if i give it to you  i can t run anymore  though  ike takes first on a lucky draw  ayanokouji s own lots are  ten friends  then  a person you love  he redraws to a table clock and finishes last   i d like to request a change","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8 sec. 8: the scavenger hunt draws<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.160–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second half opens with Ayanokouji stuck in the scavenger hunt after losing rock-paper-scissors, while Sudou and Horikita are both missing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “You’re participating in the scavenger hunt, right, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d rather not, if possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hirata, you don’t need my opinion to make a sound decision, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We need 100,000 points to put in a substitute. I’ll figure something out with the points. I think we’d do well substituting Ike-kun or Yamauchi-kun,”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s because, if they do happen to take first place, they’ll be able to put points toward their tests. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, that muscle-headed moron won’t be participating in the scavenger hunt, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No idea. That has nothing to do with me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji! Lend me your left foot! Your left foot!”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My left foot?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your shoe, dude! Your shoe! That’s my item!”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I give it to you, I can’t run anymore, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Ike takes first on a lucky draw; Ayanokouji’s own lots are “Ten friends” then “A person you love”; he redraws to a table clock and finishes last.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to request a change.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p158-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: declines the search<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1\">→ After: Ch.8 sec. 8.2: the points crisis and Kushida<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke chabashira-sae kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 8 sec  8 2  the points crisis and kushida after a lost four way tug of war  hirata has paid three substitutes  kushida volunteers for the three legged race and ayanokouji takes sudou s place   hirata  are you going to pay for the next competition  too   yeah  i am  we need it  hirata has paid twice for sudou and once for horikita  another substitute would push his total to 500 000 points   well  sudou aside  horikita should be able to repay you   hey  hirata  could i go in as sudou s substitute  i ll pay the points  i can t guarantee i ll be much help  but i ll try   so  you re going to be sudou s substitute  ayanokouji   rather unusual  since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines  ties him into the three legged pair  then he names her as the traitor who photographed the participation table   it s you  you re the traitor who leaked class d s participation table to class c   come on  ayanokouji kun  what s the matter with you  even as a joke  that s a cruel thing to say   i saw you  you took a picture with your phone of the participation table we drew on the blackboard   i suppose there s nothing i can do  now that i ve been found out  yes  i leaked the participation table   i wanted to expel her  expel horikita suzune  that s what   i m going to get horikita san expelled  no matter what you say  i won t change my mind   oh  but i reconsidered one thing  i added you to the list of people i want expelled  ayanokouji kun  open blackmail leverage  the uniform he touched on the cruise ship  she admits she gambled on ryuuen  three legged race run in silent hostility after the confession","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8 sec. 8.2: the points crisis and Kushida<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.168–175<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After a lost four-way tug-of-war, Hirata has paid three substitutes; Kushida volunteers for the three-legged race and Ayanokouji takes Sudou’s place.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Hirata, are you going to pay for the next competition, too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Yeah, I am. We need it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, Sudou aside, Horikita should be able to repay you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Hirata has paid twice for Sudou and once for Horikita; another substitute would push his total to 500,000 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, Hirata. Could I go in as Sudou’s substitute? I’ll pay the points. I can’t guarantee I’ll be much help, but I’ll try,”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you’re going to be Sudou’s substitute, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Rather unusual, since you tend to prefer watching on the sidelines.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Ties him into the three-legged pair, then he names her as the traitor who photographed the participation table.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s you. You’re the traitor who leaked Class D’s participation table to Class C.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come on, Ayanokouji-kun. What’s the matter with you? Even as a joke, that’s a cruel thing to say,”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I saw you. You took a picture with your phone of the participation table we drew on the blackboard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose there’s nothing I can do, now that I’ve been found out. Yes. I leaked the participation table,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wanted to expel her. Expel Horikita Suzune. That’s what,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m going to get Horikita-san expelled, no matter what you say. I won’t change my mind,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, but I reconsidered one thing. I added you to the list of people I want expelled, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Open blackmail leverage: the uniform he touched on the cruise ship; she admits she gambled on Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Three-legged race run in silent hostility after the confession.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p160-1\">← Before: Ch.8 sec. 8: the scavenger hunt draws<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p181-1\">→ After: Ch.9 sec. 9: the relay anchor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p181-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken ike-kanji miyake-akito horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 9 sec  9  the relay anchor sudou returns for the 1200 metre relay  after miyake s ankle withdrawal ayanokouji volunteers as substitute and is made anchor   the final event  huh  i guess we need to choose a substitute for this one  too  speaker untagged before sudou s entrance  recorded under hirata s field   yeah  sorry  my bad  it took way longer to take a dump than i thought   it s not like it s your fault i lost or anything  i m just no good at sports  really  sorry i wasn t useful   if you haven t decided on a sub for the relay  please let me run   to tell you the truth  i twisted my ankle before lunch during the 200 meter dash  i thought it would feel better after i rested  but it still hurts   in that case  would it be okay if i ran  i ll pay the points to go in as a substitute  of course   i support him  i ve been watching everyone  and i think ayanokouji will do well  named anchor after hirata s plan  sudou first  hirata second  three girls  ayanokoji last  meets the president on the track  offers to race him seriously if he gives up second place   to think that you re the anchor   i m just a substitute  originally  your sister planned to be in this position   i ve observed your class   i suppose  if anything s changed  it would be your sister   i keep an eye on every class  no exceptions   you probably won t be around to see this  but our class will become stronger   i m not interested in such a fanciful future   in that case  would you be interested in learning exactly what kind of person i am   interesting  first serious run of his life  closes on the frontrunners in a one on one against horikita manabu  blocked by a fallen runner before the line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p181-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 sec. 9: the relay anchor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.181–188<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudou returns for the 1200-metre relay; after Miyake’s ankle withdrawal Ayanokouji volunteers as substitute and is made anchor.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “The final event, huh? I guess we need to choose a substitute for this one, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Yeah, sorry. My bad. It took way longer to take a dump than I thought.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “It’s not like it’s your fault I lost or anything. I’m just no good at sports, really. Sorry I wasn’t useful,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Speaker untagged before Sudou’s entrance; recorded under Hirata’s field.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you haven’t decided on a sub for the relay, please let me run,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, I twisted my ankle before lunch during the 200-meter dash. I thought it would feel better after I rested, but it still hurts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, would it be okay if I ran? I’ll pay the points to go in as a substitute, of course.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I support him. I’ve been watching everyone, and I think Ayanokouji will do well,”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Named anchor after Hirata’s plan: Sudou first, Hirata second, three girls, Ayanokōji last.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Meets the president on the track; offers to race him seriously if he gives up second place.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To think that you’re the anchor,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m just a substitute. Originally, your sister planned to be in this position,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve observed your class,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose, if anything’s changed, it would be your sister.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I keep an eye on every class. No exceptions,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You probably won’t be around to see this, but our class will become stronger,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not interested in such a fanciful future,”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, would you be interested in learning exactly what kind of person I am?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> First serious run of his life: closes on the frontrunners in a one-on-one against Horikita Manabu; blocked by a fallen runner before the line.<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p168-1\">← Before: Ch.8 sec. 8.2: the points crisis and Kushida<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p189-1\">→ After: Ch.9 sec. 9.1: attention and the first-name bargain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p189-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei sudou-ken horikita-suzune kamuro-masumi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 9 sec  9 1  attention and the first name bargain after the race karuizawa  sudou and horikita crowd him  the scoreboard brings red team victory and class d fourth among first years   you were super fast   wasn t it just that my opponent was slow   ayanokouji  you really are super fast  dude  whoa  have you been holding back until now   running s pretty much my only specialty  but i overdid it  that s the power of being fired up  huh   that still doesn t explain it  though  that speed  you liar  a calm class a girl from the cavalry battle summons him to the front gate at five o clock   because i have something to talk to you about  at five o clock  go to the front gate   this time  we were defeated soundly  completely   this class is going to get stronger  then we ll definitely climb the ranks to the upper classes  she says she must first  get down on my knees    the ryuuen appointment he is not told about","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p189-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 sec. 9.1: attention and the first-name bargain<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.189–193<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the race Karuizawa, Sudou and Horikita crowd him; the scoreboard brings Red Team victory and Class D fourth among first-years.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “You were super fast.”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wasn’t it just that my opponent was slow?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Ayanokouji! You really are super fast, dude. Whoa! Have you been holding back until now?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Running’s pretty much my only specialty, but I overdid it. That’s the power of being fired up, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That still doesn’t explain it, though. That speed. You liar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> A calm Class A girl from the cavalry battle summons him to the front gate at five o’clock.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because I have something to talk to you about. At five o’clock, go to the front gate.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This time, we were defeated soundly. Completely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This class is going to get stronger. Then we’ll definitely climb the ranks to the upper classes,”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She says she must first “get down on my knees” — the Ryuuen appointment he is not told about.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p181-1\">← Before: Ch.9 sec. 9: the relay anchor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p202-1\">→ After: Ch.9 sec. 9.4: the White Room greeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p202-1","v":"y1v5","y":1,"o":6,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 9 sec  9 4  the white room greeting at the special building kamuro delivers him to sakayanagi  who names the white room and claims eight years and 243 days of knowledge of him   you drew quite a lot of attention in that final relay  ayanokouji kiyotaka kun   after seeing you run  i remembered something  i called you here because i wanted to share the shock i felt with you   it s been quite a long time  ayanokouji kun  eight years and 243 days  actually   it s unpleasant  isn t it  when only your opponent knows your secrets   this is a reunion  i just wanted to come give you a proper greeting   to be honest  i never thought i d see you again  but now  all the mysteries have been cleared away   so  you were the one pulling the strings   what are you talking about  there are lots of smart people in my class   i ve found little pleasure in this boring school life   can you bury me   i ll be able to realize my dearest wish by destroying the greatest masterpiece that your father ever made  both want his destruction  her wish  and the old man s loss   passing mention   p 102  capture the flag charge and its aftermath continue on this page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 sec. 9.4: the White Room greeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V5 · p.202–204<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the special building Kamuro delivers him to Sakayanagi, who names the White Room and claims eight years and 243 days of knowledge of him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “You drew quite a lot of attention in that final relay, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “After seeing you run, I remembered something. I called you here because I wanted to share the shock I felt with you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “It’s been quite a long time, Ayanokouji-kun. Eight years and 243 days, actually.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s unpleasant, isn’t it? When only your opponent knows your secrets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is a reunion. I just wanted to come give you a proper greeting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be honest, I never thought I’d see you again. But now, all the mysteries have been cleared away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you were the one pulling the strings.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you talking about? There are lots of smart people in my class,”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve found little pleasure in this boring school life.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you bury me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll be able to realize my dearest wish by destroying the greatest masterpiece that your father ever made.”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Both want his destruction: her wish, and the old man’s loss. [passing mention] (p.102) Capture-the-flag charge and its aftermath continue on this page.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v5-p189-1\">← Before: Ch.9 sec. 9.1: attention and the first-name bargain<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p2-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1 8  passing mentions named across contents pages and margins where he is not the section s focus  contents list chapter 7 s title with his group formation already ahead of it  movie plan margins name him among the invited five  spy suspect talk  hiyori asks how much time he spends with horikita  kushida task margins  he would not risk the secret with her help unchecked  hasebe s satou question and the nickname debate name him  group naming session  yukimuu  miyacchi  ayanon  hasebe pairs him with yukimura as fellow loners  the ayanokouji group is named after him  he objects  kiyopon nickname discussion with haruka  sakura s blush at kiyopon  first name rule settles  group founding line  five members  looking forward to it  movie outing walk with airi at his side  karuizawa greets the party by name at the theater  keisei cites him as witness to the no leak method  karuizawa demands whose side he is on after the cinema quarrel  ike s exam chat approach in the hallway  the fraud letter mailbox revelation reaches him by name  kushida s rooftop recount places him at the karaoke table  author s postscript names ayanokouji kiyotaka s past as a volume seven draw","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p2-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1–8: passing mentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.2, 137, 141, 145–146, 148–150, 152, 154–155, 159, 161, 165–166, 168–169, 204, 210<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named across contents pages and margins where he is not the section’s focus.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Contents list Chapter 7’s title with his group formation already ahead of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.2<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Movie-plan margins name him among the invited five.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Spy-suspect talk: Hiyori asks how much time he spends with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida-task margins; he would not risk the secret with her help unchecked.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hasebe’s Satou question and the nickname debate name him.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Group-naming session: Yukimuu, Miyacchi, Ayanon.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hasebe pairs him with Yukimura as fellow loners.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The Ayanokouji Group is named after him; he objects.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kiyopon nickname discussion with Haruka.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakura’s blush at Kiyopon; first-name rule settles.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Group founding line: five members, looking forward to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Movie outing walk with Airi at his side.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa greets the party by name at the theater.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Keisei cites him as witness to the no-leak method.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Karuizawa demands whose side he is on after the cinema quarrel.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ike’s exam-chat approach in the hallway.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The fraud-letter mailbox revelation reaches him by name.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida’s rooftop recount places him at the karaoke table.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Author’s postscript names Ayanokouji Kiyotaka’s past as a volume-seven draw.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p14-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2: student council handover<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p14-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"narration spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2  student council handover mid october  student council election ceremony  horikita manabu hands over and nagumo miyabi is sworn in as president   hello  i m nagumo  second year class a  student council president horikita  i sincerely appreciate the strict yet kind guidance you ve shown me  the younger horikita no longer shrinks from her brother  she remains steadfast watching him leave the stage   allow me to introduce myself again  my name is nagumo miyabi  and i will be assuming the position of student council president at the tokyo metropolitan advanced nurturing high school  i sincerely look forward to working with all of you  nagumo pledges indefinite terms for student council officers  annuls the october general election  lifts size limits  and allows majority vote removal   to bring this school into the future  i intend to thoroughly destroy the past   a revolution is coming  students with real ability will rise to the top  and students without any will fall  second years shout delight at the announcement  first years do not know the second third year tension behind it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2: student council handover<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.14–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mid-October: student council election ceremony; Horikita Manabu hands over and Nagumo Miyabi is sworn in as president.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “Hello. I’m Nagumo, second-year Class A. Student Council President Horikita, I sincerely appreciate the strict yet kind guidance you’ve shown me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “Allow me to introduce myself again. My name is Nagumo Miyabi, and I will be assuming the position of student council president at the Tokyo Metropolitan Advanced Nurturing High School. I sincerely look forward to working with…”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> “To bring this school into the future, I intend to thoroughly destroy the past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The younger Horikita no longer shrinks from her brother; she remains steadfast watching him leave the stage.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Allow me to introduce myself again. My name is Nagumo Miyabi, and I will be assuming the position of student council president at the Tokyo Metropolitan Advanced Nurturing High School. I sincerely look forward to working with all of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Nagumo pledges indefinite terms for student-council officers, annuls the October general election, lifts size limits, and allows majority-vote removal.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A revolution is coming. Students with real ability will rise to the top, and students without any will fall.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Second-years shout delight at the announcement; first years do not know the second/third-year tension behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p2-1\">← Before: Ch.1–8: passing mentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p17-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: changed classmates and Satou’s approach<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p17-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei satou-maya sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  changed classmates and satou s approach second semester  class d is coalescing  ayanokouji finds himself alone when ike  yamauchi and the professor leave for keyaki mall  sudou now takes notes after horikita s check in and softens toward ike and yamauchi   your dear friends ike kun and yamauchi kun haven t been inviting you out much  isn t that right  horikita explains the friend group fracture  they resented that he hid his excellence  not the excellence itself   people tend to fundamentally resent those who excel  in your case  though  they resent you because you concealed your excellence  karuizawa casts a strange look  then follows horikita out of the classroom  satou waits for him alone and asks to talk elsewhere  sakura makes a sound as if to speak  then neither speaks nor follows  in the gym passage satou asks whether he has a girlfriend and proposes exchanging phone numbers as friends","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: changed classmates and Satou’s approach<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.17–19<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Second semester: Class D is coalescing; Ayanokouji finds himself alone when Ike, Yamauchi and the Professor leave for Keyaki Mall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Your dear friends Ike-kun and Yamauchi-kun haven’t been inviting you out much. Isn’t that right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “People tend to fundamentally resent those who excel. In your case, though, they resent you because you concealed your excellence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sudou now takes notes after Horikita’s check-in and softens toward Ike and Yamauchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita explains the friend-group fracture: they resented that he hid his excellence, not the excellence itself.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Karuizawa casts a strange look, then follows Horikita out of the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Satou waits for him alone and asks to talk elsewhere.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Sakura makes a sound as if to speak, then neither speaks nor follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> In the gym passage Satou asks whether he has a girlfriend and proposes exchanging phone numbers as friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2: student council handover<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p21-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the “confession”<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p21-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"satou-maya sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  the  confession  satou registers his number  blushes  and runs off after saying the relay made him look cool   ayanokouji is left stunned   i thought the best guy in class was  you know  hirata kun  but since he s karuizawa san s boyfriend  there s nothing i can do about that  right   to be honest  after getting a good look at you  you re even cooler than hirata kun  and more mature and gentler  too  recalling yamauchi s earlier confession to sakura puts his own situation in perspective  he feels nothing for satou either way and notes she never actually asked him to go out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the “confession”<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.21<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Satou registers his number, blushes, and runs off after saying the relay made him look cool — Ayanokouji is left stunned.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> “I thought the best guy in class was, you know, Hirata-kun. But since he’s Karuizawa-san’s boyfriend, there’s nothing I can do about that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> “To be honest, after getting a good look at you, you’re even cooler than Hirata-kun, and more mature and gentler, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Recalling Yamauchi’s earlier confession to Sakura puts his own situation in perspective.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> He feels nothing for Satou either way and notes she never actually asked him to go out.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: changed classmates and Satou’s approach<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: Katsuragi’s corridor warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p22-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"narration spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  katsuragi s corridor warning walking back  ayanokouji is stopped by katsuragi  with yahiko  about his relay speed and class a s problems   sorry  but you go on ahead  i have a little something to discuss with ayanokouji   i have enough problems right now  i simply can t afford to focus on other classes   he ll do anything for the sake of winning  even if that means resorting to blackmail or violence  katsuragi warns horikita off underestimating ryuuen  ayanokouji recalls the rumor of katsuragi and ryuuen teaming up   i regret it  even though i felt that i had no other options at the time  i should never have gotten involved with ryuuen  ayanokouji notes sakayanagi knew him and chooses not to stir that pot  october totals after the sports festival  class a 874  b 753  c 542  d 262  class a had peaked at 1 124 after the island test   i admit we re in a bad situation  i didn t understand how the school was structured  and my inability to grasp the point system didn t help  ayanokouji promises to warn horikita about ryuuen  class b is the peaceful one  class c is a dictatorship  class a is split between two factions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: Katsuragi’s corridor warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.22–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking back, Ayanokouji is stopped by Katsuragi (with Yahiko) about his relay speed and Class A’s problems.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Sorry, but you go on ahead. I have a little something to discuss with Ayanokouji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “I have enough problems right now. I simply can’t afford to focus on other classes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “He’ll do anything for the sake of winning. Even if that means resorting to blackmail or violence.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Katsuragi warns Horikita off underestimating Ryuuen; Ayanokouji recalls the rumor of Katsuragi and Ryuuen teaming up.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I regret it. Even though I felt that I had no other options at the time, I should never have gotten involved with Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Ayanokouji notes Sakayanagi knew him and chooses not to stir that pot.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> October totals after the sports festival: Class A 874, B 753, C 542, D 262 (Class A had peaked at 1,124 after the island test).<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I admit we’re in a bad situation. I didn’t understand how the school was structured, and my inability to grasp the point system didn’t help”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokouji promises to warn Horikita about Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Class B is the peaceful one; Class C is a dictatorship; Class A is split between two factions.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p21-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the “confession”<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p25-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: Karuizawa’s phone call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p25-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"satou-maya karuizawa-kei manabe-shiho ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2  karuizawa s phone call that night karuizawa phones  she already knew about satou because satou told her in advance   satou san herself  she told me in advance that she was going to confess to you  karuizawa frames it as risk to her own standing if ayanokouji dates satou   she was threatened into serving him and needs the protection to continue   you are  though  you didn t say that you were turning her down  ew  i can see right through you  he asks whether manabe and the class c girls have bothered her since the cruise  they have not  for now  manabe s group does not know karuizawa s past   ryuuen is the one pulling strings behind them  she mollifies when he says he is putting satou on hold  both agree to erase call and email records  he withholds the coming danger from karuizawa for now so as not to pressure her  blank page  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2: Karuizawa’s phone call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.25–28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">That night Karuizawa phones: she already knew about Satou because Satou told her in advance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “You are, though. You didn’t say that you were turning her down. Ew! I can see right through you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> “Satou-san herself. She told me in advance that she was going to confess to you”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Karuizawa frames it as risk to her own standing if Ayanokouji dates Satou — she was threatened into serving him and needs the protection to continue.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> He asks whether Manabe and the Class C girls have bothered her since the cruise; they have not, for now.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Manabe’s group does not know Karuizawa’s past — Ryuuen is the one pulling strings behind them.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She mollifies when he says he is putting Satou on hold; both agree to erase call and email records.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> He withholds the coming danger from Karuizawa for now so as not to pressure her.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: Katsuragi’s corridor warning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p30-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3: midterm results and the Paper Shuffle rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p30-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae sudou-ken horikita-suzune ike-kanji hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke yamauchi-haruki sotomura-hideo satou-maya inogashira-kokoro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3  midterm results and the paper shuffle rules chabashira posts midterms  class d has matured  no one fails this round  her warning about expulsion for failing grades is genuine  surveillance cameras watch for reactions   the school will expel you immediately if you fail the midterm or final exam  i told you as much before  so i imagine it s fresh in your memory  sudou s jump from bottom to twelfth  average 57  with sports festival points stripped still remarkable  horikita tutored the failing group  her score to him  64  so mediocre  he keeps the mediocre student cover  ike s school evaluation  spending money  food  games  girls  his quiz wail  his frustration about question creation  exemplary school liking answer  partner system questions  400 question workload flusters him  named with horikita as an excellent student who could still be at risk depending on partner  recalls kouenji also refused to give up the bus seat  yamauchi bottoms the list  english 43  later jabs at partnering with the bottom student  sports festival penalty  needs ten extra points per subject  named in the low score climb with inogashira and sotomura  named in the low score climb  midterm short test paper shuffle rules  700 point aggregate  60 per subject  question creation  class vs class 50 point swings  nomination lots  passing grade 40 per subject  sports festival over 100 scores capped at perfect  bottom ten lose 10 per subject  final exam  pairs from short test  under 60 combined in any subject expels both  aggregate target historically  700  cheating expels both partners  class writes 400 questions for another class  higher class score takes 50 points   paper shuffle  named as the usual title for this exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3: midterm results and the Paper Shuffle rules<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.30–39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira posts midterms; Class D has matured; no one fails this round.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+5 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “The school will expel you immediately if you fail the midterm or final exam. I told you as much before, so I imagine it’s fresh in your memory.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Her warning about expulsion for failing grades is genuine; surveillance cameras watch for reactions.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou’s jump from bottom to twelfth (average 57) with sports-festival points stripped still remarkable; Horikita tutored the failing group.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her score to him: 64 “so mediocre”; he keeps the mediocre-student cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike’s school evaluation (spending money, food, games, girls); his quiz wail; his frustration about question creation.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Exemplary school-liking answer; partner-system questions; 400-question workload flusters him.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–36, 38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Named with Horikita as an excellent student who could still be at risk depending on partner.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Recalls Kouenji also refused to give up the bus seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Yamauchi bottoms the list (English 43); later jabs at partnering with the bottom student.<span class=\"pg\">p.31, 37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Sports-festival penalty: needs ten extra points per subject.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Named in the low-score climb with Inogashira and Sotomura.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Inogashira Kokoro<\/b> Named in the low-score climb.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Midterm→short test→Paper Shuffle rules, 700-point aggregate, 60 per subject, question creation, class-vs-class 50-point swings, nomination lots.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Passing grade 40 per subject; sports-festival over-100 scores capped at perfect; bottom ten lose 10 per subject.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Final exam: pairs from short test; under 60 combined in any subject expels both; aggregate target historically ~700.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Cheating expels both partners; class writes 400 questions for another class; higher class score takes 50 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Paper Shuffle” named as the usual title for this exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p25-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: Karuizawa’s phone call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: meeting call and Kushida’s invitation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p40-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  meeting call and kushida s invitation after class horikita asks ayanokouji to fetch hirata  he weighs distancing from her now that ryuuen and ichinose want the hidden hand identified  named as wanting the identity of the person pulling horikita s strings  same  wants that identity after the relay  her three key points breakdown of chabashira s hints impresses him  she is becoming the class commander  arrives  calls karuizawa over  the group moves to pallet  hugs hirata s arm to demand pallet  releases it when eyes meet ayanokouji s  asks to join  horikita planned to invite her anyway  ayanokouji flags the sports festival betrayal risk  asks to peek in on club first  horikita agrees  keeps him for the pallet talk  intermediary between hirata and karuizawa  offers everything she knows about kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: meeting call and Kushida’s invitation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.40–42<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After class Horikita asks Ayanokouji to fetch Hirata; he weighs distancing from her now that Ryuuen and Ichinose want the hidden hand identified.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as wanting the identity of the person pulling Horikita’s strings.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Same: wants that identity after the relay.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her three-key-points breakdown of Chabashira’s hints impresses him; she is becoming the class commander.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Arrives; calls Karuizawa over; the group moves to Pallet.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Hugs Hirata’s arm to demand Pallet; releases it when eyes meet Ayanokouji’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Asks to join; Horikita planned to invite her anyway; Ayanokouji flags the sports-festival betrayal risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Asks to peek in on club first; Horikita agrees.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Keeps him for the Pallet talk: intermediary between Hirata and Karuizawa; offers everything she knows about Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3: midterm results and the Paper Shuffle rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the junior-high incident on the walk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p43-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  the junior high incident on the walk on a detour away from pallet  horikita begins the kushida story   first day bus  same junior high in another prefecture  same junior high  she did not remember horikita then  bus seat scene with the elderly woman and kouenji s refusal  also refused the bus seat   not the cause of kushida s hate  junior high  incredibly popular  same level of influence as the student council   in february of our third year  just as graduation approached  one entire class fell apart  a certain female student triggered an incident that destroyed her class  school buried it  rumors of slander  bullying  violence   then silence  kushida believes horikita knows everything  tension is one sided misunderstanding  ayanokouji frames lies as the weapon that could destroy a class  kushida threatened any means to drive horikita out   katsuragi  sakayanagi  ichinose  and already an alliance with ryuuen  named on kushida s expulsion list  named on kushida s expulsion list  named on kushida s expulsion list  already allied with kushida to entrap horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the junior-high incident on the walk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.43–48<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On a detour away from Pallet, Horikita begins the Kushida story — first-day bus, same junior high in another prefecture.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “In February of our third year, just as graduation approached, one entire class fell apart.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Same junior high; she did not remember Horikita then; bus seat scene with the elderly woman and Kouenji’s refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Also refused the bus seat — not the cause of Kushida’s hate.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Junior high: incredibly popular, same level of influence as the student council.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> A certain female student triggered an incident that destroyed her class; school buried it; rumors of slander, bullying, violence — then silence.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida believes Horikita knows everything; tension is one-sided misunderstanding; Ayanokouji frames lies as the weapon that could destroy a class.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida threatened any means to drive Horikita out — Katsuragi, Sakayanagi, Ichinose, and already an alliance with Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Named on Kushida’s expulsion list.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named on Kushida’s expulsion list.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named on Kushida’s expulsion list.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Already allied with Kushida to entrap Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: meeting call and Kushida’s invitation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p48-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: expel-or-befriend, then the Ryuuen question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p48-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru manabe-shiho karuizawa-kei sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  expel or befriend  then the ryuuen question ayanokouji suggests giving up on kushida for class a  horikita refuses and owns the problem as her responsibility  horikita cites sudou s turnaround as proof people with something to offer should not be abandoned  the prior decision not to let him fail is cited back at ayanokouji  ayanokouji s warning  as long as suzune is here  kushida will sabotage and class d may pay   she s an excellent student  not only can she win people s hearts and minds  she s also a keen observer  if we make her our ally  she ll be a great asset  horikita asks what he did to ryuuen at the sports festival  he confirms recording ryuuen s class c strategy talk  narration  horikita does not know about manabe and friends harassing karuizawa on the cruise  the cruise ship trouble is the unspoken source of his class c access  named again as someone who knows his past  chabashira had mentioned a man who wanted to see him  roundabout words of thanks  warns ryuuen has him on the list   i m starting to understand you less and less","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: expel-or-befriend, then the Ryuuen question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.48–51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokouji suggests giving up on Kushida for Class A; Horikita refuses and owns the problem as her responsibility.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “She’s an excellent student. Not only can she win people’s hearts and minds, she’s also a keen observer. If we make her our ally, she’ll be a great asset.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Horikita cites Sudou’s turnaround as proof people with something to offer should not be abandoned.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The prior decision not to let him fail is cited back at Ayanokouji.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Ayanokouji’s warning: as long as Suzune is here, Kushida will sabotage and Class D may pay.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Horikita asks what he did to Ryuuen at the sports festival; he confirms recording Ryuuen’s Class C strategy talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Narration: Horikita does not know about Manabe and friends harassing Karuizawa on the cruise.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The cruise-ship trouble is the unspoken source of his Class C access.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named again as someone who knows his past; Chabashira had mentioned a man who wanted to see him.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Roundabout words of thanks; warns Ryuuen has him on the list; “I’m starting to understand you less and less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p43-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the junior-high incident on the walk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p52-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: Pallet strategy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p52-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 2  pallet strategy at pallet  horikita  ayanokouji  hirata  karuizawa  kushida and sudou  short test s partner selection significance  glares at horikita for lateness   wow  you just ignored me  typical  soccer club anxiety absent  eyes shine for the meeting  proposes checking rules with upperclassmen  offers an upperclassman she is close to  tasked with senior inquiry  leaves saying she will ask and report back  whispers to ayanokouji  bangs forehead  then restrained one on one logic about attacking class c  pairs appear balanced high low  average students most at risk  only one or two pairs expelled historically  odd number question  average student risk   thinking about it is a waste of time  nomination plan  target class c  hirata s lottery worst case  a d  b c wins lots  c b  d c loses   a  writes the imaginary nomination matrix  agrees with horikita s plan after sudou s point  observant and restrained  defeat opponents one on one  closest class c makes most sense  academic gap a b and b c needs investigation  accepts hirata s agreement  asks ayanokouji what he will do  offers to adjust his score to team with a specific person and join study meetings  but will not be a leader  blank page  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2: Pallet strategy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.52–58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Pallet: Horikita, Ayanokouji, Hirata, Karuizawa, Kushida and Sudou; short test’s partner-selection significance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Glares at Horikita for lateness; “Wow, you just ignored me. Typical.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Soccer club anxiety absent; eyes shine for the meeting; proposes checking rules with upperclassmen.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Offers an upperclassman she is close to; tasked with senior inquiry; leaves saying she will ask and report back.<span class=\"pg\">p.53, 55, 58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Whispers to Ayanokouji; bangs forehead; then restrained one-on-one logic about attacking Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.53–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Pairs appear balanced high+low; average students most at risk; only one or two pairs expelled historically.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Odd-number question; average-student risk; “thinking about it is a waste of time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Nomination plan: target Class C; Hirata’s lottery worst-case (A→D, B→C wins lots, C→B, D→C loses → A).<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Writes the imaginary nomination matrix; agrees with Horikita’s plan after Sudou’s point.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Observant and restrained: defeat opponents one-on-one; closest class C makes most sense.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Academic gap A&gt;B and B&gt;C needs investigation; accepts Hirata’s agreement; asks Ayanokouji what he will do.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Offers to adjust his score to team with a specific person and join study meetings, but will not be a leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p48-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: expel-or-befriend, then the Ryuuen question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p60-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4: Class C’s “X” hunt (named only)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p60-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko manabe-shiho hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4  class c s  x  hunt  named only  cold open in class c  ryuuen names a class d mind that thinks like him and vows to smoke out the hidden mind the island and sports festival failures are read as one hidden hand  classes a and b set aside to hit class d  the class still centres on horikita as the visible front  x is hypothesised as someone who let suzune suffer on purpose  in the spy debrief  karuizawa s cruise ship bullying is the leverage that forced manabe s group to spy  named with ayanokouji as the only ones present for the bullying photo  both dismissed as mere pawns by ryuuen  manabe s group names yukimura and ayanokouji as the class d witnesses who saw them with karuizawa  floated as a capable alternative mastermind and dismissed  ayanokouji is discussed as a suspect throughout  he does not appear in the room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4: Class C’s “X” hunt (named only)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.60–70<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Cold open in Class C: Ryuuen names a Class D mind that thinks like him and vows to smoke out the hidden mind<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"manabe-shiho.html\">Manabe Shiho<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The island and sports-festival failures are read as one hidden hand; Classes A and B set aside to hit Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The class still centres on Horikita as the visible front; X is hypothesised as someone who let Suzune suffer on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.62, 67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> In the spy debrief, Karuizawa’s cruise-ship bullying is the leverage that forced Manabe’s group to spy.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Named with Ayanokouji as the only ones present for the bullying photo; both dismissed as mere pawns by Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> Manabe’s group names Yukimura and Ayanokouji as the Class D witnesses who saw them with Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> floated as a capable alternative mastermind and dismissed.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokouji is discussed as a suspect throughout; he does not appear in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p52-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: Pallet strategy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p74-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4: Ryuuen’s next move targets him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p74-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4  ryuuen s next move targets him after the yukimura ayanokouji photo dead end  ryuuen decides to try using one of them and sends a text  how about we try using him    the text is the chapter s closing hook  addressee not printed on these pages  one of the two photo names  both still treated as possible pawns  blank page  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p74-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4: Ryuuen’s next move targets him<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the Yukimura/Ayanokouji photo dead-end, Ryuuen decides to try using one of them and sends a text.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> How about we try using him? — the text is the chapter’s closing hook; addressee not printed on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> One of the two photo names; both still treated as possible pawns.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p60-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4: Class C’s “X” hunt (named only)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p76-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5: the quiet middleman<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p76-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken ike-kanji satou-maya kushida-kikyou miyake-akito yukimura-teruhiko hasebe-haruka sakura-airi ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5  the quiet middleman homeroom strategy meeting  ayanokoji watches horikita take the podium with hirata as her support for the first time  portmann s premature birth metaphor frames her as still underdeveloped but full of possibility  she bows an apology for the sports festival  reads sudou s embarrassed smile after horikita s look as the one thing she gained   his alliance  notes ike need not study  a blank sheet would only raise class d s risk if taken seriously   aren t you worried that you re wrong about how the pairs are selected  her confidence keeps ike and the others standing tall  class d is changing  paired with satou for the final exam  she smiles his way  he raises a hand to acknowledge   god really does have a bad sense of humor  warns that satou might fail  he must keep his own scores high from here  speaker line kept as narrative   printed wording differs at the cite  there don t appear to be any blatant problems with the pairings  study session plan  kushida attends both and tutors the fifty point worriers  asked to manage miyake and hasebe into yukimura s group  horikita s request morphs into a threat he can only nod to   i ll do what i can  middleman between yukimura and the pair  at pallet  pressed on his own ability and refuses to overclaim  fielded hasebe s romance probe and her decision to stay  relays the provisional questions idea to horikita  short utterance  nope  finds sakura watching him  invites her to sit with the group  then keeps his distance so she must choose  class c phones at the cafe counter  feels their gaze and sakura s presence before leaving for the bathroom  dorm call  tests the school s question standards  asked to manage her sessions too   a word he does not understand   that s not what we agreed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5: the quiet middleman<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.76–103<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Homeroom strategy meeting; Ayanokōji watches Horikita take the podium with Hirata as her support for the first time.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+4 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Aren’t you worried that you’re wrong about how the pairs are selected?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“God really does have a bad sense of humor.”<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll do what I can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Portmann’s premature-birth metaphor frames her as still underdeveloped but full of possibility; she bows an apology for the sports festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Reads Sudou’s embarrassed smile after Horikita’s look as the one thing she gained — his alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Notes Ike need not study; a blank sheet would only raise Class D’s risk if taken seriously.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her confidence keeps Ike and the others standing tall; Class D is changing.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Paired with Satou for the final exam; she smiles his way; he raises a hand to acknowledge.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Warns that Satou might fail; he must keep his own scores high from here.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Speaker line kept as narrative — printed wording differs at the cite: There don’t appear to be any blatant problems with the pairings,<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Study-session plan: Kushida attends both and tutors the fifty-point worriers.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Asked to manage Miyake and Hasebe into Yukimura’s group; Horikita’s request morphs into a threat he can only nod to.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Middleman between Yukimura and the pair; at Pallet, pressed on his own ability and refuses to overclaim.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Fielded Hasebe’s romance probe and her decision to stay; relays the provisional-questions idea to Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Short utterance: Nope.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Finds Sakura watching him; invites her to sit with the group, then keeps his distance so she must choose.<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Class C phones at the café counter; feels their gaze and Sakura’s presence before leaving for the bathroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Dorm call: tests the school’s question standards; asked to manage her sessions too — a word he does not understand.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not what we agreed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p74-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4: Ryuuen’s next move targets him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p104-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.5–5.9: eavesdrop, library, the bet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p104-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru satou-maya ichinose-honami kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 5 5 9  eavesdrop  library  the bet continues the dorm call on study group management and kushida  ryuuen s dummy account email closes the night  pressed on kushida and question leaks  told to face the worst case for class d s lifeline   it d certainly be difficult to rule out any possibility of leaks if we factored in kushida  wait  aren t you and her both participating in the evening study sessions   our test questions and answers are class d s lifeline  if that information leaks  we re doomed   i m not worried about the  creating questions  part  if anything  i fear what comes after we submit them to the school  if you give the final questions and answers to chabashira sensei the day before the test  then they ll be out there  ready to be stolen   you have to  this is about all of class d  no matter how much we study  if our opponents get a hundred points across the board  we have no hope of winning  email arrives   what are you    first reply since the sports festival message  dummy account  no answer given  library awkwardness as study partners  her crush read  midterm near fifty across the board   i ve been a few times   well  it s more like i come here to kill time   i don t mind  horikita and kushida are the ones tutoring  and they should be happy to have more people   you should ask horikita   my test scores are only slightly different from satou s  so there s probably not that much i can teach her  besides  i wanted to get some tutoring myself   yeah a little  since we seem to be about the same level  we should study together  library territorial rules  joint class b study group  drawled invitation to take care of satou san  corner talk on friendship criteria  proposes ichinose as kushida mediator  she declines   i was pretty close to failing  i might need your help   i understand that your classmates are unconditional allies  i do think it s necessary to be friends with everyone in your boat  so to speak  however  are the class a  c  and d students your friends   then what if we re in trouble  what if we came to you  begging you to lend us a million points   sheesh  your generosity knows no bounds  you ll really help anyone   although i appreciate that  i have my doubts  so  if i came crying to you  begging for help  mediator pitch rejected    i m going to settle things with kushida myself   i believe i found the puzzle piece you ll need to reconcile with kushida   so  why not get a good person to mediate between you two  frankly  i think nothing will come from a one on one conversation with kushida  she would never reveal her true nature to anyone in class d   i don t think this ll resolve everything  i m just saying it s a step in the right direction  right now  you and kushida aren t even on good enough terms to talk  if ichinose mediated  you could probably have an actual conversation  eavesdrops the pocket phone confrontation  joins the bet  demands the junior high incident told aloud   looks like i m getting in the way  offers to side bet that horikita wins  kushida s extra condition is his expulsion if she loses   can i join this wager  i bet that horikita will win   it started out that way  but now it does have something to do with me  besides  i eavesdropped on your conversation   i want you to tell me the specifics of this junior high incident   it s my right to ask for this much  i don t know any details  and yet you re trying to get me expelled  you re acting on the belief that horikita knows about the incident  right  so  just explain it to us right now  as long as you beat horikita on the test  the school will kick us both out  and you won t have to worry   well  i am  i can t accept that kushida s threatening my whole life here on a selfish whim   haven t i already passed the point of no return  pressed for why the gamble is worth it  blog  secrets  and the class destroying truth weapon laid out   i m just an average person  what you d call a jack of all trades  master of none  if i had to pick something  i guess i m a little faster than average   do you want to remain as you are right now  after kushida leaves  ryuuen wants her brought low  not expelled  danger is accepted when something is staked on the outcome   are you sure about this  kushida s involved with ryuuen   but what if kushida lies to get the questions from him  she might say that she wants to improve her personal score  and keep our bet s details secret   you re probably right  but this is dangerous   there s no turning back from this  we definitely need to win  would see through a kushida lie about math answers  wants to know why  blank page  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p104-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.5–5.9: eavesdrop, library, the bet<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.104–130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Continues the dorm call on study-group management and Kushida; Ryuuen’s dummy-account email closes the night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’d certainly be difficult to rule out any possibility of leaks if we factored in Kushida. Wait, aren’t you and her both participating in the evening study sessions?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Our test questions and answers are Class D’s lifeline. If that information leaks, we’re doomed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not worried about the ‘creating questions’ part. If anything, I fear what comes after we submit them to the school. If you give the final questions and answers to Chabashira-sensei the day before the test, then they’ll be…”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pressed on Kushida and question leaks; told to face the worst case for Class D’s lifeline.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not worried about the ‘creating questions’ part. If anything, I fear what comes after we submit them to the school. If you give the final questions and answers to Chabashira-sensei the day before the test, then they’ll be out there, ready to be stolen,”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have to. This is about all of Class D. No matter how much we study, if our opponents get a hundred points across the board, we have no hope of winning,”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Email arrives: “What are you?” — first reply since the sports-festival message; dummy account, no answer given.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Library awkwardness as study partners; her crush read; midterm near-fifty across the board.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve been a few times,”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it’s more like I come here to kill time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t mind. Horikita and Kushida are the ones tutoring, and they should be happy to have more people.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You should ask Horikita,”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My test scores are only slightly different from Satou’s, so there’s probably not that much I can teach her. Besides, I wanted to get some tutoring myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah…a little. Since we seem to be about the same level, we should study together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Library territorial rules; joint Class B study group; drawled invitation to take care of Satou-san.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Corner talk on friendship criteria; proposes Ichinose as Kushida mediator; she declines.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was pretty close to failing. I might need your help,”<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I understand that your classmates are unconditional allies. I do think it’s necessary to be friends with everyone in your boat, so to speak. However, are the Class A, C, and D students your friends?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then what if we’re in trouble? What if we came to you, begging you to lend us a million points?”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sheesh. Your generosity knows no bounds. You’ll really help anyone?”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Although I appreciate that, I have my doubts. So, if I came crying to you, begging for help…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Mediator pitch rejected — “I’m going to settle things with Kushida myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I believe I found the puzzle piece you’ll need to reconcile with Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, why not get a good person to mediate between you two? Frankly, I think nothing will come from a one-on-one conversation with Kushida. She would never reveal her true nature to anyone in Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t think this’ll resolve everything. I’m just saying it’s a step in the right direction. Right now, you and Kushida aren’t even on good enough terms to talk. If Ichinose mediated, you could probably have an actual conversation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Eavesdrops the pocket-phone confrontation; joins the bet; demands the junior-high incident told aloud.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks like I’m getting in the way,”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Offers to side-bet that Horikita wins; Kushida’s extra condition is his expulsion if she loses.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can I join this wager? I bet that Horikita will win,”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It started out that way. But now it does have something to do with me. Besides, I eavesdropped on your conversation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I want you to tell me the specifics of this junior high incident.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s my right to ask for this much. I don’t know any details, and yet you’re trying to get me expelled. You’re acting on the belief that Horikita knows about the incident, right? So, just explain it to us right now. As long as you beat Horikita on the test, the school will kick us both out, and you won’t have to worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I am. I can’t accept that Kushida’s threatening my whole life here on a selfish whim,”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Haven’t I already passed the point of no return?”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Pressed for why the gamble is worth it; blog, secrets, and the class-destroying truth weapon laid out.<span class=\"pg\">p.125–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m just an average person. What you’d call a jack of all trades, master of none. If I had to pick something, I guess I’m a little faster than average.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you want to remain as you are right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> After Kushida leaves: Ryuuen wants her brought low, not expelled; danger is accepted when something is staked on the outcome.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you sure about this? Kushida’s involved with Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what if Kushida lies to get the questions from him? She might say that she wants to improve her personal score, and keep our bet’s details secret,”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re probably right. But this is dangerous.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no turning back from this. We definitely need to win.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Would see through a Kushida lie about math answers; wants to know why.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p76-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5: the quiet middleman<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.0: fifth session pulled wider<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p132-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko hasebe-haruka miyake-akito ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 0  fifth session pulled wider fifth yukimura session with miyake and hasebe  moved from pallet to the keyaki mall cafe because clubs have stopped for the final   we should ve met in the library   no way  it s easier to do it here  right  miyacchi   that s a mediocre student s mindset  think about what you can do first  and challenge yourself  yukimura drafts him into the group as well  his grades are fine but his partner is satou  so both must prepare or both are kicked out   just do it  ayanokouji kun  let s all die together  fifth session in a row  yukimura s finish the material method beats horikita s fixed time method for these two  and now pulls him in for satou prep  still in the study trio  she treats the humanities packet as torture and drags him in with a vengeful spirit bit  archery club tension noted  miyake wants free time after club but stays for the session","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.0: fifth session pulled wider<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.132–134<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fifth Yukimura session with Miyake and Hasebe, moved from Pallet to the Keyaki Mall café because clubs have stopped for the final.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “We should’ve met in the library,”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> “No way. It’s easier to do it here. Right, Miyacchi?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “That’s a mediocre student’s mindset. Think about what you can do first, and challenge yourself,”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Yukimura drafts him into the group as well: his grades are fine but his partner is Satou, so both must prepare or both are kicked out.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just do it, Ayanokouji-kun. Let’s all die together,”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Fifth session in a row; Yukimura’s finish-the-material method beats Horikita’s fixed-time method for these two, and now pulls him in for Satou prep.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Still in the study trio; she treats the humanities packet as torture and drags him in with a vengeful-spirit bit.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Archery club tension noted; Miyake wants free time after club but stays for the session.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–134<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p104-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.5–5.9: eavesdrop, library, the bet<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p156-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: group chat, Horikita call, birthday notice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p156-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei hasebe-haruka sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 4  group chat  horikita call  birthday notice the new group s chat proposes a movie  ayanokoji joins  then takes horikita s exam prep call and karuizawa s texts the same night   i ll join you   yeah  me too   it s still only ten o clock  do you need something   tomorrow  huh   i ll talk it over with keisei  is it okay if we re late  we should also get in touch with hirata and karuizawa ahead of time  if we need to   i m busy before that  i m going to a movie with my study group   seems like you know it  anyway  i have a favor i d like to ask of you   i ll explain when it s done  it s for your own sake  sends karuizawa a detailed errand against hiyori s sugar story  then notes her profile birthday march 8 after she is the first to notice his  exam prep invitation  he answers with keisei and the movie conflict rather than a yes or no  errand order plus the belated birthday cake sticker  he deletes the texts and remembers march 8  movie ticket plan from her group chat  airi texts that she wants to go too  keisei agreed conditional on akito  ayanokoji will talk it over with him about the exam prep","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p156-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 sec. 6.4: group chat, Horikita call, birthday notice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.156–158<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The new group’s chat proposes a movie; Ayanokōji joins, then takes Horikita’s exam-prep call and Karuizawa’s texts the same night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll join you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah, me too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s still only ten o’clock. Do you need something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Tomorrow, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll talk it over with Keisei. Is it okay if we’re late? We should also get in touch with Hirata and Karuizawa ahead of time, if we need to,”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m busy before that. I’m going to a movie with my study group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Seems like you know it. Anyway, I have a favor I’d like to ask of you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll explain when it’s done. It’s for your own sake.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Sends Karuizawa a detailed errand against Hiyori’s sugar story, then notes her profile birthday March 8 after she is the first to notice his.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Exam-prep invitation; he answers with Keisei and the movie conflict rather than a yes or no.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Errand order plus the belated birthday cake sticker; he deletes the texts and remembers March 8.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Movie ticket plan from her group chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Airi texts that she wants to go too.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Keisei agreed conditional on Akito; Ayanokōji will talk it over with him about the exam prep.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.0: fifth session pulled wider<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p177-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the envelope, the trap, the counter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p177-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae satou-maya hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 0  the envelope  the trap  the counter three days before the final  horikita carries class d s confidential question envelope  ryuuen shadows them to the staff room   oh  sorry   what are our chances   i think we should be safe   what s the matter  horikita   yeah  they definitely are   you knew this was coming  reads ryuuen s two goals as beating class d and smoking out the puppet master behind horikita  ordinary study and hard problems tactics are the ceiling if he wants overall points  something still feels off about ryuuen s unflustered calm even as the plan looks hole free  after the counter is revealed  he would never have imagined horikita devising it  and could not have come up with it himself  underestimates her plan until she lifts her head  admits he had no idea  notes her determination for the remaining kushida score bet  shadows the submission  later answers the photo threat with an open invitation to play the game  reads the bet stakes  if kushida had class c s answers she would likely perfect math and horikita would drop out on one wrong answer  locks eyes with her instead of following horikita out   a silent prompt she does not need  exam morning greeting and partner pep talk  morning walk  hirata names him as the one pulling horikita s strings and offers backup  he neither confirms nor fully denies  watches the satou greeting  hirata flags her growing attention  keisei s predicted questions prove right on the money during the first subject","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p177-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the envelope, the trap, the counter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.177–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Three days before the final; Horikita carries Class D’s confidential question envelope; Ryuuen shadows them to the staff room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Oh, sorry,”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are our chances?”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I think we should be safe,”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s the matter, Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. They definitely are,”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You knew this was coming?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Reads Ryuuen’s two goals as beating Class D and smoking out the puppet master behind Horikita; ordinary study-and-hard-problems tactics are the ceiling if he wants overall points.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Something still feels off about Ryuuen’s unflustered calm even as the plan looks hole-free.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> After the counter is revealed: he would never have imagined Horikita devising it, and could not have come up with it himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Underestimates her plan until she lifts her head; admits he had no idea; notes her determination for the remaining Kushida score bet.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Shadows the submission; later answers the photo threat with an open invitation to play the game.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Reads the bet stakes: if Kushida had Class C’s answers she would likely perfect math and Horikita would drop out on one wrong answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Locks eyes with her instead of following Horikita out — a silent prompt she does not need.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Exam-morning greeting and partner pep talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Morning walk; Hirata names him as the one pulling Horikita’s strings and offers backup; he neither confirms nor fully denies.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Watches the Satou greeting; Hirata flags her growing attention.<span class=\"pg\">p.188–189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Keisei’s predicted questions prove right on the money during the first subject.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p156-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.4: group chat, Horikita call, birthday notice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p194-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.4: the photo and the open challenge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p194-1","v":"y1v6","y":1,"o":7,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 4  the photo and the open challenge after the first exam day  watches horikita s near perfect math claim and sudou s apology  later alone receives ryuuen s photograph by phone   looks like you re all finished   what score would you say you got for the math portion   it s possible that you might ve written something incorrectly or missed an answer  though  is there a chance that your score is any lower than ninety eight   well  that s amazing   by the way  what are your plans with kushida   she probably assumes that her score is lower than she expected  don t you think   are you worried about him   so  if that time came  would you have prostrated yourself before   kushida and begged for forgiveness   what   so  manabe and her friends spilled the beans  huh   come at me with everything you ve got  i ll play your game  convinces himself horikita won the bet from kushida s face alone  kaneda s questions were hard enough that even keisei might not top ninety  reads ryuuen s photo as a declaration of war  he has the circumstances and will go after the person in the picture  fed up with the obsessive hunt  answers in kind  despite himself  feels a little excited at the open challenge  scores talk  follow into the hallway  then the special building bet settlement with kushida  present for the bet confirmation  notes she got up and left quickly   her score fear is real  receives the photo threat  returns the favour by accepting the game outright  skeptical look about staying with horikita  apology is sincere  in the photograph ryuuen sends   the leverage on ayanokoji  hiyori named as having been with ryuuen when he ran into ayanokoji earlier  no scene here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.4: the photo and the open challenge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V6 · p.194–201<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the first exam day, watches Horikita’s near-perfect math claim and Sudou’s apology; later alone receives Ryuuen’s photograph by phone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Looks like you’re all finished,”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What score would you say you got for the math portion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s possible that you might’ve written something incorrectly or missed an answer, though. Is there a chance that your score is any lower than ninety-eight?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, that’s amazing.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “By the way, what are your plans with Kushida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She probably assumes that her score is lower than she expected, don’t you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you worried about him?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, if that time came, would you have prostrated yourself before”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Kushida and begged for forgiveness?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, Manabe and her friends spilled the beans, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Come at me with everything you’ve got. I’ll play your game,”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Convinces himself Horikita won the bet from Kushida’s face alone; Kaneda’s questions were hard enough that even Keisei might not top ninety.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Reads Ryuuen’s photo as a declaration of war: he has the circumstances and will go after the person in the picture; fed up with the obsessive hunt, answers in kind.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Despite himself, feels a little excited at the open challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Scores talk, follow into the hallway, then the special-building bet settlement with Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Present for the bet confirmation; notes she got up and left quickly — her score fear is real.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Receives the photo threat; returns the favour by accepting the game outright.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Skeptical look about staying with Horikita; apology is sincere.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> In the photograph Ryuuen sends — the leverage on Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hiyori named as having been with Ryuuen when he ran into Ayanokōji earlier; no scene here.<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v6-p177-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the envelope, the trap, the counter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p14-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko miyake-akito ryuuen-kakeru komiya-kyogo ishizaki-daichi horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sakayanagi-arisu karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke sudou-ken ibuki-mio kamuro-masumi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  the winter mall group and the class a tail narrates the keyaki mall meetup with yukimura  hasebe and sakura while miyake is at club  later corners kamuro alone   no  i don t know anything about it   well  it s pretty popular worldwide  it s not that strange a hobby  defends instagram enough to keep sakura from sinking  he smooths the dismissal for her  reads her hurt over the instagram jab and answers so she will not be depressed  she always reacts when he helps  repeats horikita s island read for the group under the official credit that credits her  inner note  of all of them akito is most bothered by ryuuen s surveillance  inner analysis  surveillance tightened since the exam  treading lightly means he is close to naming the mastermind  island points were not wasted   traded to class a  names the class c follower at the mall and later watches him peel off toward the restaurant  named with komiya at archery club  glaring at miyake  credits her with seeing through ryuuen on the island   the moves were his  the story is hers  withholds her betrayal from the group retelling  names her as kamuro s boss in the confrontation  inner note  ryuuen s list probably includes her  she could supply the final evidence  named only as half of class d s sole couple  inner note  sudou would blow his top at the girlfriend joke  island spy in the retelling he keeps to the official version  confronts her tailing with photo proof  offers mutual silence  she leaves without denying ryuuen s interest in him  photographed kamuro over a week without her noticing  turns her tail into a non aggression bargain  reads sakayanagi s leverage as  dynamite   can i have a minute   you ve been following me  what do you want   then i suppose i ll report this to sakayanagi  i ll tell her you re not really very good at tailing me   feel free to tail me as much as you like  i won t say a word  and i won t rat on you to sakayanagi  in exchange  i want you to keep quiet  don t tell anyone other than sakayanagi what you know about me  keeps the group s morale light while tracking class c  official story always credited to horikita  confronts class a alone with evidence rather than force  blank page  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the winter mall group and the Class A tail<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.14–30<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Narrates the Keyaki Mall meetup with Yukimura, Hasebe and Sakura while Miyake is at club; later corners Kamuro alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"komiya-kyogo.html\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+9 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No. I don’t know anything about it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, it’s pretty popular worldwide. It’s not that strange a hobby,”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Can I have a minute?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Defends Instagram enough to keep Sakura from sinking; he smooths the dismissal for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Reads her hurt over the Instagram jab and answers so she will not be depressed; she always reacts when he helps.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Repeats Horikita’s island read for the group under the official credit that credits her.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Inner note: of all of them Akito is most bothered by Ryuuen’s surveillance.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Inner analysis: surveillance tightened since the exam; treading lightly means he is close to naming the mastermind; island points were not wasted — traded to Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> Names the Class C follower at the mall and later watches him peel off toward the restaurant.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18, 28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Named with Komiya at archery club, glaring at Miyake.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Credits her with seeing through Ryuuen on the island — the moves were his, the story is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Withholds her betrayal from the group retelling.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Names her as Kamuro’s boss in the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Inner note: Ryuuen’s list probably includes her; she could supply the final evidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Named only as half of Class D’s sole couple.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Inner note: Sudou would blow his top at the girlfriend joke.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Island spy in the retelling he keeps to the official version.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> Confronts her tailing with photo proof; offers mutual silence; she leaves without denying Ryuuen’s interest in him.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Photographed Kamuro over a week without her noticing; turns her tail into a non-aggression bargain; reads Sakayanagi’s leverage as “dynamite.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been following me. What do you want?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Then I suppose I’ll report this to Sakayanagi. I’ll tell her you’re not really very good at tailing me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Feel free to tail me as much as you like. I won’t say a word, and I won’t rat on you to Sakayanagi. In exchange, I want you to keep quiet. Don’t tell anyone other than Sakayanagi what you know about me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps the group’s morale light while tracking Class C; official story always credited to Horikita; confronts Class A alone with evidence rather than force.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank page (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p32-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1–3.5: library lunch, group gossip, the father’s office<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p32-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken shiina-hiyori hasebe-haruka sakura-airi miyake-akito yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke hirata-yousuke satou-maya chabashira-sae ayanokouji-atsuomi matsuo komiya-kyogo ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1 3 5  library lunch  group gossip  the father s office narrates the day after the winter meetup  sudou s tail report  horikita s decoy talk  the shiina library lunch  the group s mastermind speculation  then chabashira s summons to atsuomi   there aren t any exams in the immediate future   in other words  he s looking for you   nope   i will  as much as i can  decoy bargain made explicit  she lends him farewell  my lovely and claims the grin  he wonders if she ever talks about anything but class a  listens to the tail report  notes his maturity under horikita s ignore first rule  library hand off becomes cafeteria lunch  he keeps her unreadable and files her as a possible class c probe  group chat initiator  she teases the shiina lunch as a pre christmas romance  worried about the lunch rumor  later asks whether he is the mastermind  skips club for the mall  quick to spot komiya  offers a shoulder if class c troubles him  suspected then cleared as mastermind candidate  island and zodiac help only  group rules him out   retired day one of the island test  named as a possible mastermind  bound to stay neutral  turns down her tea invitation because chabashira is waiting  urgent stairwell summons  she is visibly nervous before the principal s door  father in the principal s office  drop out demand  matsuo leverage  white room resumed   he refuses to quit  named as the butler who steered him to the school and was destroyed for it  still watching the mall group  named in the archery club tail pattern  the hunt for the mastermind structures half the chapter even when he is off page  her paper shuffle betrayal cited as the pattern horikita learned from  with sudou and yamauchi when the report lands  same casual circle  reads atsuomi s missing bodyguards  government leash and fear of public scandal  names the rebellious phase as the real reason enrolment stuck   first of all  there s no evidence that what you say is the truth   if he really is dead  then that s all the more reason for me to stay in school  matsuo helped me enroll  even though he knew you d punish him  i must honor his wishes   i can t imagine you ll be able to do anything  considering that the government backs this school   because of my insatiable curiosity  my inquisitive spirit  and also  because i want to decide my path for myself  it s that simple  keeps the official strategist fiction  reads shiina as unknown quantity  refuses the drop out demand without raising his voice  credits freedom and curiosity over the white room s single path  blank pages  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1–3.5: library lunch, group gossip, the father’s office<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.32–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Narrates the day after the winter meetup: Sudou’s tail report, Horikita’s decoy talk, the Shiina library lunch, the group’s mastermind speculation, then Chabashira’s summons to Atsuomi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+13 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“There aren’t any exams in the immediate future,”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In other words, he’s looking for you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nope.”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>27 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I will. As much as I can,”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Decoy bargain made explicit; she lends him Farewell, My Lovely and claims the grin; he wonders if she ever talks about anything but Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Listens to the tail report; notes his maturity under Horikita’s ignore-first rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Library hand-off becomes cafeteria lunch; he keeps her unreadable and files her as a possible Class C probe.<span class=\"pg\">p.39–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Group-chat initiator; she teases the Shiina lunch as a pre-Christmas romance.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Worried about the lunch rumor; later asks whether he is the mastermind.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Skips club for the mall; quick to spot Komiya; offers a shoulder if Class C troubles him.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Suspected then cleared as mastermind candidate; island and zodiac help only.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Group rules him out — retired day one of the island test.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Named as a possible mastermind; bound to stay neutral.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Turns down her tea invitation because Chabashira is waiting.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Urgent stairwell summons; she is visibly nervous before the principal’s door.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> Father in the principal’s office; drop-out demand; Matsuo leverage; White Room resumed — he refuses to quit.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsuo<\/b> Named as the butler who steered him to the school and was destroyed for it.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> Still watching the mall group.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Named in the archery-club tail pattern.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The hunt for the mastermind structures half the chapter even when he is off-page.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–36, 49–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Her Paper Shuffle betrayal cited as the pattern Horikita learned from.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> With Sudou and Yamauchi when the report lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Same casual circle.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads Atsuomi’s missing bodyguards, government leash and fear of public scandal; names the rebellious phase as the real reason enrolment stuck.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “First of all, there’s no evidence that what you say is the truth,”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If he really is dead, then that’s all the more reason for me to stay in school. Matsuo helped me enroll, even though he knew you’d punish him. I must honor his wishes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t imagine you’ll be able to do anything, considering that the government backs this school,”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because of my insatiable curiosity, my inquisitive spirit. And also, because I want to decide my path for myself. It’s that simple,”<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps the official strategist fiction; reads Shiina as unknown quantity; refuses the drop-out demand without raising his voice; credits freedom and curiosity over the White Room’s single path.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Blank pages (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.40, 58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p14-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the winter mall group and the Class A tail<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p65-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.6–3.8: chairman, Chabashira unmasked, Karuizawa cut off, Manabu’s bridge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p65-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi sakayanagi-arisu chabashira-sae karuizawa-kei horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou hasebe-haruka sakura-airi miyake-akito yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 6 3 8  chairman  chabashira unmasked  karuizawa cut off  manabu s bridge finishes the office fight with his father  survives chairman sakayanagi s admission revelations  unmasks chabashira on the walk out  ends the karuizawa pipeline by phone  then takes manabu s number over tea   this is the last thing i ll say to you  kiyotaka  consider very carefully before answering me  which would you prefer  to run away from this school of your own free will  or to have your parent force you to leave   i don t know if there s any help for a man like you  but i have no intention of giving up  this school is developing its students  talents  even if it goes about it differently from you  i expect to learn a lot here   worthless bottom feeders  not at all  this is a place where i may discover whether human beings are made equal or not  i find that quite interesting   if you call yourself a parent  why not come by the school now and again   it s pointless to probe me so clumsily  i understand everything   almost everything you ve told me has been a lie  chabashira sensei   yes  the chairman said nothing about you  chabashira sensei  but your involvement in this matter has become clear   at the very least  i think i m done taking my turn onstage   you ll never see your dream come true  not a smart choice   just wondering what you re up to   i never intended to take control  never have and never will   yeah  i ll leave it all to horikita and hirata  i don t want the hassle of ryuuen discovering my identity  i m done  you ve been a great help to me for instance  that time at karaoke  and getting in touch with kushida  i ve imposed on you quite a lot   this will probably be the last time i call you   it s only natural  since i don t need anything from you now  besides  no one knows that we ve been talking  it ll be suspicious if we continue to make pointless contact   of course  i ll help you if you ever need me to  i made a promise  and i ll honor it  you can contact me if there s an emergency  but please delete all traces of our conversations  i already deleted your contact information   a clean room s such a great thing   i d like time to think about putting your little sister on the student council and manipulating her behind the scenes   if i decide to cooperate  i ll contact you   i know  i know  i m not gonna wimp out after suggesting we all do it again  free will answer closes the drop out demand  parting jab about visiting school  father s admission story  later walks past with ichinose without eye contact  bluffs the chairman quote  exposes her class a obsession  accepts her rule threat as empty  final call   pipeline cut  emergency exception only  notes how shaken she will be  takes the bridge offer far enough to get a number  refuses to commit  named through manabu as the coming expulsions threat  forced onto the student council  later walks with sakayanagi  enemy if promoted read  still the one problem  cutting karuizawa is meant to break the thread to him  named with horikita as who he will leave class d to  cited as past karuizawa help  karaoke and walk home group  karaoke first timer  ichinose unease  club check then mall  only member who prefers the cold  spicy takoyaki streak  class a vow to sakayanagi pair  reads the fifty point smokescreen and recommendation admission from sakayanagi alone  turns chabashira s leverage into a hostage situation of her own ambition  chooses free will over the white room path  cold cuts karuizawa while calling it a promise kept  still refuses the stage even while taking manabu s number to think it over  short pages  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.6–3.8: chairman, Chabashira unmasked, Karuizawa cut off, Manabu’s bridge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.65–97<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Finishes the office fight with his father, survives Chairman Sakayanagi’s admission revelations, unmasks Chabashira on the walk out, ends the Karuizawa pipeline by phone, then takes Manabu’s number over tea.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+8 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“This is the last thing I’ll say to you, Kiyotaka. Consider very carefully before answering me. Which would you prefer? To run away from this school of your own free will, or to have your parent force you to leave?”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t know if there’s any help for a man like you, but I have no intention of giving up. This school is developing its students’ talents, even if it goes about it differently from you. I expect to learn a lot here,”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Worthless bottom-feeders? Not at all. This is a place where I may discover whether human beings are made equal or not. I find that quite interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you call yourself a parent, why not come by the school now and again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s pointless to probe me so clumsily. I understand everything,”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Almost everything you’ve told me has been a lie, Chabashira-sensei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. The chairman said nothing about you, Chabashira-sensei. But your involvement in this matter has become clear.”<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At the very least, I think I’m done taking my turn onstage,”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ll never see your dream come true. Not a smart choice.”<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just wondering what you’re up to,”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never intended to take control. Never have and never will,”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I’ll leave it all to Horikita and Hirata. I don’t want the hassle of Ryuuen discovering my identity; I’m done. You’ve been a great help to me—for instance, that time at karaoke, and getting in touch with Kushida. I’ve imposed on you quite a lot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This will probably be the last time I call you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s only natural, since I don’t need anything from you now. Besides, no one knows that we’ve been talking. It’ll be suspicious if we continue to make pointless contact,”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course, I’ll help you if you ever need me to. I made a promise, and I’ll honor it. You can contact me if there’s an emergency, but please delete all traces of our conversations. I already deleted your contact information.”<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A clean room’s such a great thing,”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like time to think about putting your little sister on the student council and manipulating her behind the scenes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I decide to cooperate, I’ll contact you,”<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know, I know. I’m not gonna wimp out after suggesting we all do it again,”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> Free-will answer closes the drop-out demand; parting jab about visiting school.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Father’s admission story; later walks past with Ichinose without eye contact.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–69, 94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Bluffs the chairman quote, exposes her Class A obsession, accepts her rule-threat as empty.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Final call — pipeline cut, emergency exception only; notes how shaken she will be.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Takes the bridge offer far enough to get a number; refuses to commit.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Named through Manabu as the coming expulsions threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Forced onto the student council; later walks with Sakayanagi; enemy-if-promoted read.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88, 94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Still the one problem; cutting Karuizawa is meant to break the thread to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.76, 78–79, 85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Named with Horikita as who he will leave Class D to.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Cited as past Karuizawa help.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Karaoke and walk-home group.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Karaoke first-timer; Ichinose unease.<span class=\"pg\">p.91–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Club check then mall; only member who prefers the cold.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Spicy takoyaki streak; Class A vow to Sakayanagi pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the fifty-point smokescreen and recommendation admission from Sakayanagi alone; turns Chabashira’s leverage into a hostage situation of her own ambition.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Chooses free will over the White Room path; cold-cuts Karuizawa while calling it a promise kept; still refuses the stage even while taking Manabu’s number to think it over.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Short pages (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.72, 93, 97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1–3.5: library lunch, group gossip, the father’s office<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.4: the smoke-out observer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p100-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  the smoke out observer narrates the classroom storm  follows the path to the rest area  and files ryuuen s narrowed list as preparation nearly complete   maybe  i said   wouldn t it be better if you stayed behind  hirata  if you come  other students might follow  if people like ike and yamauchi join in  it ll add fuel to the fire   horikita s coming  keisei and akito are too  in the worst case scenario  if it looks like things are getting violent  i ll call you   keisei  huh  okay  just don t do anything rash  sound good  hirata looked puzzled at the way i referred to yukimura  but went back inside the classroom   could be a serious fight   should we head back too  horikita  i asked  reads the classroom raid as a strategy he cannot yet parse  files the grand finale tease  sends him back to calm the class  promises a call if violence looms  low prior on him as mastermind  admires the  moron with a paltry intellect  comeback  walks the path together  agrees the show is over  watches the class a arrival and the kick block  keeps the trailing group small  clocks shoes at the entrance as the time check  observer first  names ryuuen s preparations as nearly complete without acting on it  short pages  page number only","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: the smoke-out observer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.100–118<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Narrates the classroom storm, follows the path to the rest area, and files Ryuuen’s narrowed list as preparation nearly complete.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Maybe,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Wouldn’t it be better if you stayed behind, Hirata? If you come, other students might follow. If people like Ike and Yamauchi join in, it’ll add fuel to the fire,”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Horikita’s coming. Keisei and Akito are too. In the worst-case scenario, if it looks like things are getting violent, I’ll call you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Keisei? Huh. Okay. Just don’t do anything rash, sound good?” Hirata looked puzzled at the way I referred to Yukimura, but went back inside the classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could be a serious fight,”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Should we head back too, Horikita?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reads the classroom raid as a strategy he cannot yet parse; files the grand-finale tease.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Sends him back to calm the class; promises a call if violence looms.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Low prior on him as mastermind; admires the “moron with a paltry intellect” comeback.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Walks the path together; agrees the show is over.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Watches the Class A arrival and the kick-block.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Keeps the trailing group small; clocks shoes at the entrance as the time check.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Observer first; names Ryuuen’s preparations as nearly complete without acting on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Short pages (page number only).<span class=\"pg\">p.105, 119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p65-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.6–3.8: chairman, Chabashira unmasked, Karuizawa cut off, Manabu’s bridge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p142-1\">→ After: Ch.5 half2: the name she will not say<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p142-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 half2  the name she will not say named kiyotaka inside karuizawa s pov   the promise to protect her is her final defense against the darkness  ryuuen says x cut all ties when identity was about to be exposed  karuizawa refuses to believe it at first  her pov  yousuke kun s lowest floor call was kiyotaka s instruction  the save was a setup  she concludes she was caught in his trap and abandoned at the crucial moment  starts to speak the name    k t    then turns it into  k knock it off  never gives the name   no matter how many times you ask me i ll never  ever tell you  creep   i ll never give you the name  she counts him with yousuke kun as the ones who protected her  no regrets  though she still hoped he would come  the girl who keeps his name behind her teeth  the man who tries to extract that name  the other protector in her accounting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 half2: the name she will not say<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.142, 146–150<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “No matter how many times you ask me…I’ll never, ever tell you… creep.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I’ll never give you the name.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Named Kiyotaka inside Karuizawa’s POV — the promise to protect her is her final defense against the darkness.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen says X cut all ties when identity was about to be exposed; Karuizawa refuses to believe it at first.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her POV: Yousuke-kun’s lowest-floor call was Kiyotaka’s instruction; the save was a setup.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She concludes she was caught in his trap and abandoned at the crucial moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Starts to speak the name — “K…t…” — then turns it into “K-knock…it…off.” Never gives the name.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She counts him with Yousuke-kun as the ones who protected her; no regrets, though she still hoped he would come.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The girl who keeps his name behind her teeth.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The man who tries to extract that name.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The other protector in her accounting.<span class=\"pg\">p.147, 150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.4: the smoke-out observer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p154-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the emergency address and the English door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p154-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-manabu karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio ishizaki-daichi yamada-albert sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  the emergency address and the english door walks with the mall group while the rooftop crisis runs at two  leaves them to meet chabashira  then climbs to the roof  received karuizawa s emergency text that morning  does not reply  knowing ryuuen s only goal was to lure him   nothing s going on   nothing s up  you were about to ask something  that s all   she just invited me to hang out with her  that s all   i don t know how to answer that   i m happy to stay here  airi  but i get why people want to go off campus   sorry   i m heading back   to tell you the truth  i pulled an all nighter  and i m kind of beat  let s hang out again over the winter break   hello  i need to talk to you about something  do you have a moment   yes  but there re still a few loose ends that need tying up  i d like to discuss this in person  can we meet at school   understood  i ll be there in a few minutes   i was just wondering  why do you want to make it to class a so badly that you d go so far as to use me to do it   i can t imagine that s all there is to it  if you really aimed for class a from the very beginning  you d never have put class d at a disadvantage the way you did   you hesitated  right  you weren t sure this class really had the ability to aim for class a  you weren t sure it was even worth trying   if you won t answer  then you might as well give up on trying to use me   this is crucial  if you don t take action now  class d will never make it to class a  if anything  it s unlikely we ll even reach class c   it s already two p m  ryuuen is putting on a very interesting show right about now  after calling karuizawa to the roof   so  even you don t know  sensei  karuizawa was horribly bullied in the past   this is the first i m hearing of it   that information will probably be all over the school tomorrow  when that happens  karuizawa will retreat into her shell  and maybe even voluntarily drop out of school  if we can prove class c was responsible  we might be able to retaliate  but the damage done to each class will be unfathomable   so  you ll help me   naturally   can you really afford to turn me down   there s no guarantee that i won t do anything to sabotage class d in the future  is there  i m more than capable of ensuring we never rise through the ranks   if you do this for me  i promise i ll do nothing to hinder or sabotage class d going forward  i think that s significant  don t you   relax   i had no intention of recruiting your assistance   i was just testing you  that s all  so  why not come observe this little drama s conclusion   what are you planning  ayanokouji  how long do you intend to wait  chabashira s line  his answer is below   let s chat   i d like to discuss something that happened shortly after we started school  back when we wanted you to sell us one point for sudou s test   there s nothing you cannot buy with private points  that s what you said  right   if purchasing points was permissible  there would never be any expulsions  would there  any time someone got a failing grade  someone else could cover for them the way we did   true  but that s a flaw in the system  isn t it  if salvation through private points is always an option  it dramatically lowers the danger of expulsion based on test performance   back when i asked you to sell us that single point  you added a value to it  chabashira sensei   no  that s not what i mean  i m asking whether exchanging one test point for one hundred thousand private points was something you came up with on the spot  or if you had some basis for attaching that price to it  at the time  i thought you sounded like you came up with it off the top of your head  but since then  i ve come to doubt you arbitrarily decided that on your own without consulting the school   this school has taken great care to legislate  in writing  all matters related to points  hasn t it  it s not far fetched to think that it might ve anticipated someone trying to purchase a test score increase  i would believe it   that s right  if you can answer  please do   should i interpret that to mean you can t answer   very well  i ll happily draw my own conclusions  the school prepared a manual to consult in every conceivable situation  it was determined in advance that it cost one hundred thousand private points to purchase one test point  if we go from there  it begs the question  can we can purchase one test point for a hundred thousand private points on more than one occasion   is the hundred thousand points per test point rate only available for a limited time after we ve enrolled  does the price go up every time we make a purchase  or are we only allowed to make such a purchase once  the more i think about it  the more questions i have  please tell me if i m correct   there is  i just need to ask you directly  sensei   how many points would i need to buy one test point on the next midterm right now   as a teacher  you re obligated to answer that question  right  if you won t  i ll go ahead and ask another teacher  and if they answer me  i ll report to the school that class d s homeroom teacher is discriminating against us  don t forget that i can do that   a few students are already doing just that  aren t they  look at ichinose and ryuuen  both accumulating private points  chabashira s line  the answer that follows is hers   so  you truly can t answer my question   not at all  i was just having a friendly chat   i suppose it s time  wouldn t you say  time for this game to be over   i m heading to the roof   it doesn t matter  even if ryuuen learns that i orchestrated all class d s strategies so far  he now gains nothing  if anything  he might assume i m involved next time  and end up sabotaging himself   i see  well  you were certainly correct that it s easier for people to become attached to something if they have a goal to strive for  but you needn t worry  i choose to stay here  i have no intention of going back to being under that man s control   it s not a pipe dream  class d is about to rise to class c  soon  horikita will unite our class  i m sure of it   such skepticism is unbecoming of a teacher  horikita is more than capable of leading class d   ultimately   horikita is starting to mature  the same goes for many of our classmates  continue to guide them as their teacher  and our position as class c will be secure and so might our path to class a   yes   i can t guarantee it  at most  i can say i ll deal with the situation based on my evaluation of ryuuen s personality and behavior   well then  thank you very much for accompanying me this far   he s here as a witness  after all  ryuuen will try to win by any means necessary  and i d like to avoid this becoming violent   does the former student council president look like someone who d ever do that sort of thing   there will be a person on the rooftop who will witness what happens there  as long as that holds true  then we ll be fine   a few minutes after i head up  i d like you to stop halfway up the stairs  there s no need for you to talk to the students who come back down from the roof  nor is it necessary to punish them  just make sure they see you on their way down  i need them to be aware you were here   of course  if i go back on my word  you may choose to forget what happens here today   hmm  who knows   i ll be back in ten or twenty minutes   may i pass   don t panic  i m the one you want   i m ending this today  no one else will interfere   i intend to crush ryuuen  he doesn t stand a chance without your help   sorry i m late   what do you mean   why  i made a promise  didn t i  i promised that i d save you   karuizawa emailed me  she said she wanted me to save her   it s precisely because i was the most suspicious that i did things that way  or perhaps it was because i had no other method available to me other than using horikita   i m the person you ve been searching for   am i in a dilemma   i only came here because karuizawa asked for help  if you want proof that i m x  you could just wait until the next exam and see what i do   awful things   what i ll do  there s nothing i can do   i ve already admitted to it  but if you won t believe me  then allow me to explain  ibuki   the island exam  you were instructed to take pictures of our leader s keycard  but your digital camera got damaged somehow  am i wrong   it was me  i used water to short circuit the camera without causing visible damage  when i met you in the forest  ibuki  your fingers were covered in dirt  there were signs that you were digging nearby  when i returned to the spot later that night  i found a wireless transceiver  that was so you could communicate with ryuuen  right   trick   there s no trick i can pull in a situation like this  you already know karuizawa s big secret    you took plenty of precautions to corner me  right   indeed  i can t exactly report what you just did to karuizawa to the school  either   okay  well  are you satisfied  if so  i ll be taking karuizawa back with me   sorry  ryuuen  i can t fulfil your expectations   i was just dancing in the palm of your hand  that s all   i may have revealed myself to you  but that doesn t mean i m in trouble  only horikita and karuizawa from class d know who i am  so if this information makes its way to other classes  i ll know one of you leaked it   if you spread word of my actions  i ll report everything that happened here to the school   i can  all i have to do is sacrifice karuizawa   you assumed from the start that i d abandon karuizawa  but when i showed up here  you started talking as though you thought i wasn t going to  am i wrong   you heard her  believe what you like  but if you spill the beans about me to the other classes  it ll be war  extracts from chabashira that private point prices are pre set and disclosure is conditional   one system mystery closed without her ever confirming a number  walks into ryuuen s own trap  proves x with ibuki s camera detail  and turns the reveal into a mutual assured destruction stalemate  tests before he strikes  keeps the stair witness in his back pocket  would rather burn his quiet life than leave karuizawa  the teacher he tests  then tells he is stepping back  the witness he arranged  the promise he keeps  the hunter who becomes the show  the doubter he proves wrong  the panicked class c  the door he opens in english  the alternate witness he did not need","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p154-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the emergency address and the English door<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.154–156, 166, 174<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks with the mall group while the rooftop crisis runs at two; leaves them to meet Chabashira, then climbs to the roof.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nothing’s going on,”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Nothing’s up. You were about to ask something, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She just invited me to hang out with her, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>103 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Received Karuizawa’s emergency text that morning; does not reply, knowing Ryuuen’s only goal was to lure him.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t know how to answer that…”<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m happy to stay here, Airi. But I get why people want to go off campus,”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry,”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m heading back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To tell you the truth, I pulled an all-nighter, and I’m kind of beat. Let’s hang out again over the winter break,”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hello. I need to talk to you about something. Do you have a moment?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes, but there’re still a few loose ends that need tying up. I’d like to discuss this in person. Can we meet at school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Understood. I’ll be there in a few minutes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was just wondering. Why do you want to make it to Class A so badly that you’d go so far as to use me to do it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t imagine that’s all there is to it. If you really aimed for Class A from the very beginning, you’d never have put Class D at a disadvantage the way you did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You hesitated, right? You weren’t sure this class really had the ability to aim for Class A. You weren’t sure it was even worth trying.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you won’t answer, then you might as well give up on trying to use me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is crucial. If you don’t take action now, Class D will never make it to Class A. If anything, it’s unlikely we’ll even reach Class C.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s already two p.m. Ryuuen is putting on a very interesting show right about now, after calling Karuizawa to the roof.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, even you don’t know, Sensei? Karuizawa was horribly bullied in the past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is the first I’m hearing of it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That information will probably be all over the school tomorrow. When that happens, Karuizawa will retreat into her shell, and maybe even voluntarily drop out of school. If we can prove Class C was responsible, we might be able to retaliate, but the damage done to each class will be unfathomable,”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you’ll help me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Naturally.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Can you really afford to turn me down?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no guarantee that I won’t do anything to sabotage Class D in the future, is there? I’m more than capable of ensuring we never rise through the ranks.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you do this for me, I promise I’ll do nothing to hinder or sabotage Class D going forward. I think that’s significant, don’t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Relax,”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I had no intention of recruiting your assistance.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was just testing you, that’s all. So, why not come observe this little drama’s conclusion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you planning, Ayanokouji? How long do you intend to wait?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira’s line; his answer is below.<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s chat,”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to discuss something that happened shortly after we started school, back when we wanted you to sell us one point for Sudou’s test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing you cannot buy with private points. That’s what you said, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If purchasing points was permissible, there would never be any expulsions, would there? Any time someone got a failing grade, someone else could cover for them the way we did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “True. But that’s a flaw in the system, isn’t it? If salvation through private points is always an option, it dramatically lowers the danger of expulsion based on test performance,”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Back when I asked you to sell us that single point, you added a value to it, Chabashira-sensei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, that’s not what I mean. I’m asking whether exchanging one test point for one hundred thousand private points was something you came up with on the spot, or if you had some basis for attaching that price to it. At the time, I thought you sounded like you came up with it off the top of your head, but since then, I’ve come to doubt you arbitrarily decided that on your own without consulting the school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This school has taken great care to legislate, in writing, all matters related to points, hasn’t it? It’s not far-fetched to think that it might’ve anticipated someone trying to purchase a test score increase. I would believe it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s right. If you can answer, please do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Should I interpret that to mean you can’t answer?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Very well. I’ll happily draw my own conclusions. The school prepared a manual to consult in every conceivable situation. It was determined in advance that it cost one hundred thousand private points to purchase one test point. If we go from there, it begs the question: can we can purchase one test point for a hundred thousand private points on more than one occasion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is the hundred thousand points per test point rate only available for a limited time after we’ve enrolled? Does the price go up every time we make a purchase? Or are we only allowed to make such a purchase once? The more I think about it, the more questions I have. Please tell me if I’m correct.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is. I just need to ask you directly, Sensei.”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How many points would I need to buy one test point on the next midterm right now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “As a teacher, you’re obligated to answer that question, right? If you won’t, I’ll go ahead and ask another teacher. And if they answer me, I’ll report to the school that Class D’s homeroom teacher is discriminating against us. Don’t forget that I can do that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A few students are already doing just that, aren’t they? Look at Ichinose and Ryuuen, both accumulating private points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira’s line; the answer that follows is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you truly can’t answer my question?”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not at all. I was just having a friendly chat,”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose it’s time, wouldn’t you say? Time for this game to be over.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m heading to the roof,”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It doesn’t matter. Even if Ryuuen learns that I orchestrated all Class D’s strategies so far, he now gains nothing. If anything, he might assume I’m involved next time, and end up sabotaging himself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, you were certainly correct that it’s easier for people to become attached to something if they have a goal to strive for. But you needn’t worry. I choose to stay here. I have no intention of going back to being under that man’s control.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not a pipe dream. Class D is about to rise to Class C. Soon, Horikita will unite our class. I’m sure of it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Such skepticism is unbecoming of a teacher. Horikita is more than capable of leading Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ultimately,”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita is starting to mature. The same goes for many of our classmates. Continue to guide them as their teacher, and our position as Class C will be secure…and so might our path to Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t guarantee it. At most, I can say I’ll deal with the situation based on my evaluation of Ryuuen’s personality and behavior.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, thank you very much for accompanying me this far.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He’s here as a witness. After all, Ryuuen will try to win by any means necessary, and I’d like to avoid this becoming violent.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Does the former student council president look like someone who’d ever do that sort of thing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There will be a person on the rooftop who will witness what happens there. As long as that holds true, then we’ll be fine,”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A few minutes after I head up, I’d like you to stop halfway up the stairs. There’s no need for you to talk to the students who come back down from the roof, nor is it necessary to punish them. Just make sure they see you on their way down. I need them to be aware you were here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course. If I go back on my word, you may choose to forget what happens here today,”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. Who knows?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll be back in ten or twenty minutes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “May I pass?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t panic. I’m the one you want,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m ending this today. No one else will interfere,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I intend to crush Ryuuen. He doesn’t stand a chance without your help,”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry I’m late,”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean, ‘why’? I made a promise, didn’t I? I promised that I’d save you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Karuizawa emailed me. She said she wanted me to save her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s precisely because I was the most suspicious that I did things that way. Or perhaps it was because I had no other method available to me other than using Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m the person you’ve been searching for.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Am I in a dilemma?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I only came here because Karuizawa asked for help. If you want proof that I’m X, you could just wait until the next exam and see what I do,”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Awful things?”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What I’ll do? There’s nothing I can do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve already admitted to it. But if you won’t believe me, then allow me to explain, Ibuki,”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The island exam. You were instructed to take pictures of our leader’s keycard, but your digital camera got damaged somehow. Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was me. I used water to short-circuit the camera without causing visible damage. When I met you in the forest, Ibuki, your fingers were covered in dirt. There were signs that you were digging nearby. When I returned to the spot later that night, I found a wireless transceiver. That was so you could communicate with Ryuuen, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Trick?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s no trick I can pull in a situation like this. You already know Karuizawa’s big secret. … You took plenty of precautions to corner me. Right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.172–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Indeed. I can’t exactly report what you just did to Karuizawa to the school, either,”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. Well, are you satisfied? If so, I’ll be taking Karuizawa back with me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, Ryuuen. I can’t fulfil your expectations.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was just dancing in the palm of your hand. That’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I may have revealed myself to you, but that doesn’t mean I’m in trouble. Only Horikita and Karuizawa from Class D know who I am, so if this information makes its way to other classes, I’ll know one of you leaked it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you spread word of my actions, I’ll report everything that happened here to the school,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can. All I have to do is sacrifice Karuizawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You assumed from the start that I’d abandon Karuizawa. But when I showed up here, you started talking as though you thought I wasn’t going to. Am I wrong?”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You heard her. Believe what you like, but if you spill the beans about me to the other classes, it’ll be war,”<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Extracts from Chabashira that private-point prices are pre-set and disclosure is conditional — one system mystery closed without her ever confirming a number.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Walks into Ryuuen’s own trap, proves X with Ibuki’s camera detail, and turns the reveal into a mutual-assured-destruction stalemate.<span class=\"pg\">p.166–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Tests before he strikes; keeps the stair witness in his back pocket; would rather burn his quiet life than leave Karuizawa.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The teacher he tests, then tells he is stepping back.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The witness he arranged.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The promise he keeps.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The hunter who becomes the show.<span class=\"pg\">p.166–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The doubter he proves wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.166–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> The panicked Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> The door he opens in English.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> The alternate witness he did not need.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p142-1\">← Before: Ch.5 half2: the name she will not say<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p175-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the fight he planned, the pawn he keeps<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p175-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei ibuki-mio ishizaki-daichi yamada-albert horikita-manabu chabashira-sae ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu manabe-shiho sudou-ken komiya-kyogo kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  the fight he planned  the pawn he keeps watches ryuuen choose violence over a draw  then wins the rooftop brawl and keeps karuizawa under control   i agree  ayanokouji might actually sacrifice her  ibuki s line  ayanokoji does not dispute the mutual destruction frame   violence is a powerful tool  i can t argue with that  however  you have to be stronger than your opponent for that to work to your advantage  understand   the four of you won t be enough to stop me   don t worry  karuizawa   there s nothing to be anxious about   i don t really care   if you re going to do this  you better take it seriously   just as i thought  that hurts   ayanokouji  ishizaki s shout  the next line is ayanokoji s   if you re going to come at me  don t shout   are you serious  ibuki   ryuuen s always been the sort to use violence  do you think i d voluntarily allow him to engineer a situation where he could rampage without repercussion   you still don t get it  do you   our confrontation here was determined long in advance  i knew that  when faced with a stalemate  ryuuen kakeru would resort to violence to settle things   if i never intended to reveal my identity  i wouldn t have used manabe during the sports festival  i knew you d identify her as the obvious culprit once you heard that recording  that is what led you here  right  i anticipated that you d question them  and learn that i was blackmailing them for bullying karuizawa   you were convinced that a link existed between karuizawa and me  you had ishizaki  komiya  and the others tail class d students  and moved openly against kouenji yourself  thinking that it would put pressure on x  i imagine you genuinely enjoyed yourself  but you actually gave me some time to think   to be more precise  you were dancing in mine   you really don t know   violence isn t a tool only you and your goons possess   i m impressed you re still keeping your cool after seeing that play out   nope   sorry  but i won t let you hit me   not bad  ryuuen   so  you re saying if we keep doing this over and over  you ll win eventually   aren t you afraid of losing   no fear  huh   teach me about pain  then   unfortunately  i don t  get  anything   this is just pain   that s not it  ryuuen  that s not what i m saying   i was testing a hypothesis  i wanted to see whether i could feel that fear you talked about   i ve never looked down on anyone  whether other people succeed or   fail has nothing to do with me   you said you ve never felt fear  didn t you  ryuuen   isn t this enough  ryuuen   sorry  i put you in a really difficult situation  are you hurt   are you disillusioned with me now   yeah  i suppose you re right  so why didn t you sell me out to ryuuen   don t think about it anymore  what happened today  what s happened so far  you can think about that stuff later  the only thing that s for certain right now  in this moment  is that your curse has been lifted  manabe no  no one will dig up your past again  as for what s to come  well  you can just keep going the way you always have   you ve managed to overcome your past and create an identity as the person you are now   starting tomorrow  you can just pick up where you left off   i hurt you  i won t ask you to forgive me  but please remember just one thing  if something like what happened today happens again  i will come save you   a few steps below us  the student council president well  the former student council president and chabashira sensei are waiting  they know the circumstances to a certain degree  so they should be able to handle things  including taking care of your soaked uniform   i ve still got a few things to tidy up here  besides  we don t want to be seen together  it s best if you go first   do you think this is over  ayanokouji  ryuuen s line   it s over   surely you re not about to say you want to keep going   are you going to report me to the school   let me give you some advice  i don t recommend it  the former student council president is waiting on the stairs as we speak  he may not know all the details of what happened here  but it s obvious you were the one setting a trap  ryuuen especially since you were caught on video spraypainting the surveillance camera  i  on the other hand  was at keyaki mall when you did that  i can produce many alibis as i need to prove it   yes  i knew you wouldn t stop attacking me until i struck you at least once   yeah  i do  there s a reason i defeated you  ryuuen  you made a mistake choosing the order of your foes  if you d cut your teeth fighting ichinose  and then katsuragi and sakayanagi  you might ve been closer to my level by the time you chose to challenge me  but your curiosity got the better of you  you overplayed your hand   i d like to say i d be happy to have a rematch  but i m done drawing   target someone else   i d like to avoid that  but yes   your overconfidence in relying on my identity and karuizawa s past was your undoing  if you d been less reckless  you would ve either mounted a larger scale attack or posted more lookouts   not necessarily  as long as you make no further attempts to attack us  i won t use this incident to advance myself   maybe   but what are you going to do  you can t undo what happened  ryuuen   oh  that sounds serious  taking responsibility and all   because you hate me  divide the remaining points among everyone  once the school expels me  i bet katsuragi and sakayanagi will void our contract  but there s nothing to be done about that  ryuuen s line to ibuki   are you sure  i think you ll come to regret this   why do you care  ryuuen s line   if you leave without knowing why you lost  you won t grow   are you really fine with not knowing why you lost to me   let it go  there s no point trying to save me  you ve got nothing to gain by sparing me now that i know about you and karuizawa  i could expose you at any time  ryuuen s line   true enough  if i must name a reason for sparing you it ll work to class d s advantage to have you crush sakayanagi and ichinose for us  besides  if your contract with katsuragi remains in place  class a will continue to hemorrhage points  most importantly  though  if you suddenly drop out of school  sakayanagi and ichinose will assume that x beat you  that spells trouble for me down the line   so  trust me  this is to my benefit  even if word of what happened up here gets out  i took no noticeable injuries  it would just look like you guys fought among yourselves  wouldn t it   allow me to add just one thing   you are free to drop out of school of your own volition and you re free to doubt me  but i have absolutely no intention of telling anyone about today unless you force my hand  the former student council president has similarly promised to keep it to himself  nothing about this situation is forcing you to withdraw but if you do  i won t stop you  takes albert s punch  drops ishizaki and ibuki with controlled force  then outlasts ryuuen until the knockout   no critical injuries taken by plan  explains the whole trap  manabe recording   ryuuen s trail   planned violence  tests whether he can feel fear under pain and concludes he cannot  keeps karuizawa as a controlled pawn  arranges alibis and stair witness  spares ryuuen only because a live class c leader serves class d better than a expelled one  the opponent he beats  then deliberately keeps  the promise kept and the dependency managed  dropped with a neck throw after her kick flurry  fist catch and knee kick  caught the first heavy punch on purpose  stair witness whose presence blocks ryuuen s report option  waiting below with the former president  named as the foe ryuuen should have fought first  and as someone to crush later  named in the order of foes lecture and the contract math  same   special treat for ryuuen  class a hemorrhage if contract holds  the sports festival lever and the past that is now safe  the known fighter ishizaki is not  named among the tailed class d students  the open move against him that bought ayanokoji thinking time","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p175-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the fight he planned, the pawn he keeps<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.175–178, 180–188, 190–195<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches Ryuuen choose violence over a draw; then wins the rooftop brawl and keeps Karuizawa under control.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+8 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I agree. Ayanokouji might actually sacrifice her,”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Violence is a powerful tool. I can’t argue with that. However, you have to be stronger than your opponent for that to work to your advantage. Understand?”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The four of you won’t be enough to stop me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>87 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ibuki’s line; Ayanokōji does not dispute the mutual-destruction frame.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t worry, Karuizawa,”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing to be anxious about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t really care,”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re going to do this, you better take it seriously,”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just as I thought. That hurts,”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokouji!”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ishizaki’s shout; the next line is Ayanokōji’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re going to come at me, don’t shout,”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you serious, Ibuki?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ryuuen’s always been the sort to use violence. Do you think I’d voluntarily allow him to engineer a situation where he could rampage without repercussion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You still don’t get it, do you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Our confrontation here was determined long in advance. I knew that, when faced with a stalemate, Ryuuen Kakeru would resort to violence to settle things.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If I never intended to reveal my identity, I wouldn’t have used Manabe during the sports festival. I knew you’d identify her as the obvious culprit once you heard that recording. That is what led you here, right? I anticipated that you’d question them, and learn that I was blackmailing them for bullying Karuizawa,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were convinced that a link existed between Karuizawa and me. You had Ishizaki, Komiya, and the others tail Class D students, and moved openly against Kouenji yourself, thinking that it would put pressure on X. I imagine you genuinely enjoyed yourself, but you actually gave me some time to think.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “To be more precise, you were dancing in mine,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You really don’t know?”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Violence isn’t a tool only you and your goons possess,”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m impressed you’re still keeping your cool after seeing that play out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Nope.”<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I won’t let you hit me,”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not bad, Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you’re saying if we keep doing this over and over, you’ll win eventually?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Aren’t you afraid of losing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No fear, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Teach me about pain, then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I don’t ‘get’ anything,”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This is just pain.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not it, Ryuuen. That’s not what I’m saying.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was testing a hypothesis. I wanted to see whether I could feel that fear you talked about,”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve never looked down on anyone. Whether other people succeed or … fail has nothing to do with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You said you’ve never felt fear, didn’t you, Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Isn’t this enough, Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I put you in a really difficult situation. Are you hurt?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you disillusioned with me now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, I suppose you’re right. So why didn’t you sell me out to Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t think about it anymore. What happened today, what’s happened so far. You can think about that stuff later. The only thing that’s for certain right now, in this moment, is that your curse has been lifted. Manabe…no, no one will dig up your past again. As for what’s to come, well, you can just keep going the way you always have,”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve managed to overcome your past and create an identity as the person you are now,”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Starting tomorrow, you can just pick up where you left off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I hurt you. I won’t ask you to forgive me. But please remember just one thing. If something like what happened today happens again, I will come save you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A few steps below us, the student council president—well, the former student council president—and Chabashira-sensei are waiting. They know the circumstances to a certain degree, so they should be able to handle things, including taking care of your soaked uniform,”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve still got a few things to tidy up here. Besides, we don’t want to be seen together. It’s best if you go first.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you think this…is over, Ayanokouji?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s over,”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Surely you’re not about to say you want to keep going?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you going to report me to the school?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let me give you some advice. I don’t recommend it. The former student council president is waiting on the stairs as we speak. He may not know all the details of what happened here, but it’s obvious you were the one setting a trap, Ryuuen…especially since you were caught on video spraypainting the surveillance camera. I, on the other hand, was at Keyaki Mall when you did that. I can produce many alibis as I need to prove it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yes. I knew you wouldn’t stop attacking me until I struck you at least once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, I do. There’s a reason I defeated you, Ryuuen. You made a mistake choosing the order of your foes. If you’d cut your teeth fighting Ichinose, and then Katsuragi and Sakayanagi, you might’ve been closer to my level by the time you chose to challenge me. But your curiosity got the better of you. You overplayed your hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to say I’d be happy to have a rematch, but I’m done drawing … Target someone else,”<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’d like to avoid that, but yes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your overconfidence in relying on my identity and Karuizawa’s past was your undoing. If you’d been less reckless, you would’ve either mounted a larger-scale attack or posted more lookouts,”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not necessarily. As long as you make no further attempts to attack us, I won’t use this incident to advance myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe,”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But what are you going to do? You can’t undo what happened, Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? That sounds serious. Taking responsibility and all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Because you hate me. Divide the remaining points among everyone. Once the school expels me, I bet Katsuragi and Sakayanagi will void our contract, but there’s nothing to be done about that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen’s line to Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you sure? I think you’ll come to regret this,”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you care?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you leave without knowing why you lost, you won’t grow,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you really fine with not knowing why you lost to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let it go. There’s no point trying to save me. You’ve got nothing to gain by sparing me now that I know about you and Karuizawa. I could expose you at any time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ryuuen’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “True enough. If I must name a reason for sparing you…it’ll work to Class D’s advantage to have you crush Sakayanagi and Ichinose for us. Besides, if your contract with Katsuragi remains in place, Class A will continue to hemorrhage points. Most importantly, though, if you suddenly drop out of school, Sakayanagi and Ichinose will assume that X beat you. That spells trouble for me down the line,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, trust me, this is to my benefit. Even if word of what happened up here gets out, I took no noticeable injuries. It would just look like you guys fought among yourselves, wouldn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Allow me to add just one thing,”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You are free to drop out of school of your own volition and you’re free to doubt me. But I have absolutely no intention of telling anyone about today unless you force my hand. The former student council president has similarly promised to keep it to himself. Nothing about this situation is forcing you to withdraw—but if you do, I won’t stop you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Takes Albert’s punch, drops Ishizaki and Ibuki with controlled force, then outlasts Ryuuen until the knockout — no critical injuries taken by plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Explains the whole trap: Manabe recording → Ryuuen’s trail → planned violence; tests whether he can feel fear under pain and concludes he cannot.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps Karuizawa as a controlled pawn, arranges alibis and stair witness, spares Ryuuen only because a live Class C leader serves Class D better than a expelled one.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The opponent he beats, then deliberately keeps.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The promise kept and the dependency managed.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Dropped with a neck throw after her kick flurry.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Fist-catch and knee kick.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> Caught the first heavy punch on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Stair witness whose presence blocks Ryuuen’s report option.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Waiting below with the former president.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Named as the foe Ryuuen should have fought first, and as someone to crush later.<span class=\"pg\">p.181, 192, 195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Named in the order-of-foes lecture and the contract math.<span class=\"pg\">p.192, 195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Same — special treat for Ryuuen, Class A hemorrhage if contract holds.<span class=\"pg\">p.192, 195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Manabe Shiho<\/b> The sports-festival lever and the past that is now safe.<span class=\"pg\">p.181, 190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The known fighter Ishizaki is not.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> Named among the tailed Class D students.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The open move against him that bought Ayanokōji thinking time.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p154-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the emergency address and the English door<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the mirror and the tool<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p205-1","v":"y1v7","y":1,"o":8,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami katsuragi-kouhei hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 2  the mirror and the tool ayanokoji pov on the rumors of ryuuen s abdication  sees his own first week self in the dragon boy  rumors  ryuuen abandoned class c s leadership  ishizaki and the others no longer his entourage  he talks to no one   it was like looking in a mirror a mirror of the person i d been when i first started at this school  i wondered whether there would come a day when ryuuen regained what he lost  i was sure of one thing  though  he and i were similar  final line of the chapter body   and i could still use him  author postscript  ayanokoji  seems to have settled things with ryuuen for the time being  reads the fallen tyrant as a mirror and a future asset  not a broken rival  the similar man he can still use  postscript confirms the truce holds for now  part of the entourage that dissolved in the rumors  named in the postscript teaser as a coming story  same  same  same","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the mirror and the tool<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7 · p.205–206<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji POV on the rumors of Ryuuen’s abdication; sees his own first-week self in the dragon boy.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It was like looking in a mirror—a mirror of the person I’d been when I first started at this school. I wondered whether there would come a day when Ryuuen regained what he lost. I was sure of one thing, though. He and I were…”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Rumors: Ryuuen abandoned Class C’s leadership; Ishizaki and the others no longer his entourage; he talks to no one.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was like looking in a mirror—a mirror of the person I’d been when I first started at this school. I wondered whether there would come a day when Ryuuen regained what he lost. I was sure of one thing, though. He and I were similar.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Final line of the chapter body: “And I could still use him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Author postscript: Ayanokōji “seems to have settled things with Ryuuen for the time being.”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the fallen tyrant as a mirror and a future asset, not a broken rival.<span class=\"pg\">p.205–206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The similar man he can still use; postscript confirms the truce holds for now.<span class=\"pg\">p.205–206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Part of the entourage that dissolved in the rumors.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named in the postscript teaser as a coming story.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Same.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Same.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Same.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7-p175-1\">← Before: Ch.6: the fight he planned, the pawn he keeps<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p11-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1  christmas date setup december 25  snowing  ayanokoji grooms for a date with sato maya and wonders whether he can ever feel love   i ve been here over eight months now  huh  falling in love with someone  considering them precious  sharing happiness merely by being together  elation  i wondered whether i d ever be able to experience such strong feelings  chapter frames the winter vacation story as beginning december 23  this chapter is a one page flash forward to christmas day","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Christmas date setup<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.11<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">December 25, snowing; Ayanokōji grooms for a date with Satō Maya and wonders whether he can ever feel love.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve been here over eight months now, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Falling in love with someone. Considering them precious. Sharing happiness merely by being together. Elation. I wondered whether I’d ever be able to experience such strong feelings.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chapter frames the winter-vacation story as beginning December 23; this chapter is a one-page flash-forward to Christmas Day.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p13-1\">→ After: Ch.2: the object of the crush and the night call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p13-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei satou-maya horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  the object of the crush and the night call named throughout karuizawa s pov  he is the boy sato will date on christmas day and the man who saved karuizawa off the roof  goaded manabe into bullying her  then saved her  that night he calls to task her with investigating satou   i want to ask you something   i need you to investigate something for me  karuizawa   i want to know who she usually hangs out with  what her behavior patterns are  i d also appreciate it if you could fill me in on her personality  hobbies  and likes and dislikes   not very well informed  eh  so  there re lots of things that even you  the girls  de facto leader  don t know   do whatever you think would be best  please  i leave everything in your hands    then hangs up without answering why  the girl he is dating on the 25th  he wants covert intel on her before the date  karuizawa notes he  only ever seemed to talk to horikita san  flat  apathetic tone on the phone  no apology after the roof  tasks her then hangs up  karuizawa reads it as collecting info to make the date go well or to turn satou into a pawn","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the object of the crush and the night call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.13–14, 17–34<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named throughout Karuizawa’s POV; he is the boy Satō will date on Christmas Day and the man who saved Karuizawa off the roof.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I want to ask you something.”<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I need you to investigate something for me, Karuizawa.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I want to know who she usually hangs out with. What her behavior patterns are. I’d also appreciate it if you could fill me in on her personality, hobbies, and likes and dislikes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Goaded Manabe into bullying her, then saved her; that night he calls to task her with investigating Satou.<span class=\"pg\">p.12, 32–34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not very well-informed, eh? So, there’re lots of things that even you, the girls’ de facto leader, don’t know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do whatever you think would be best, please. I leave everything in your hands,” — then hangs up without answering why.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> The girl he is dating on the 25th; he wants covert intel on her before the date.<span class=\"pg\">p.17, 33–34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Karuizawa notes he “only ever seemed to talk to Horikita-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Flat, apathetic tone on the phone; no apology after the roof; tasks her then hangs up; Karuizawa reads it as collecting info to make the date go well or to turn Satou into a pawn.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Christmas date setup<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p27-1\">→ After: coverage passes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p27-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka coverage passes name hit threads outside his own dialogue blocks  satou s jealousy  kushida s cafe call  sakura s gloves  and karuizawa s tool talk  passing mention  satou s internal line    it wasn t kiyotaka  passing mention  named in the double date logistics  passing mention  named in the bookstore senior couple tangent  passing mention   if you re not hanging with us  kiyopon    hasebe s warning  passing mention   good morning  ayanokouji kun  said kushida at the cafe  passing mention  kushida asks if he should join the christmas group  passing mention  kushida asks if she may call him by given name  passing mention   see you later  ayanokouji kun    kushida s gentle exit  passing mention  sakura s glove goodbye    good night  kiyotaka kun  passing mention  sakura s morning greeting at the meet spot  passing mention  hirata and satou call him kind  he deflects  passing mention   what you did for karuizawa san    hirata s thanks  passing mention  hirata floats the student council invitation  passing mention   you re not like normal guys  kiyotaka    karuizawa after the confession  passing mention  karuizawa asks if he only views people as tools  passing mention   hey  kiyotaka  sorry to bother you    gift hesitation talk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">coverage passes<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.27, 30, 66, 71, 96, 98, 100, 102, 106, 108, 117, 129, 132, 147, 150, 164<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Name-hit threads outside his own dialogue blocks: Satou’s jealousy, Kushida’s café call, Sakura’s gloves, and Karuizawa’s tool talk.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Satou’s internal line — “it wasn’t Kiyotaka.”<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: named in the double-date logistics.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: named in the bookstore senior-couple tangent.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “If you’re not hanging with us, Kiyopon…” — Hasebe’s warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun,” said Kushida at the café.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Kushida asks if he should join the Christmas group.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Kushida asks if she may call him by given name.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “See you later, Ayanokouji-kun.” — Kushida’s gentle exit.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Sakura’s glove goodbye — “Good night, Kiyotaka-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Sakura’s morning greeting at the meet spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Hirata and Satou call him kind; he deflects.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “what you did for Karuizawa-san” — Hirata’s thanks.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Hirata floats the student-council invitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “you’re not like normal guys, Kiyotaka.” — Karuizawa after the confession.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: Karuizawa asks if he only views people as tools.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Passing mention: “Hey, Kiyotaka. Sorry to bother you…” — gift hesitation talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2: the object of the crush and the night call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p35-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the pharmacy bag and Sakayanagi’s Ichinose pitch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p35-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu kamuro-masumi ichinose-honami horikita-suzune kouenji-rokusuke hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  the pharmacy bag and sakayanagi s ichinose pitch december 23 morning  keyaki mall  ayanokoji leaves a store with a small paper bag of something he s never used  then runs into sakayanagi arisu   i ve never used this stuff before   i ll pass  thanks  you re conspicuous  and i don t like drawing attention   well  they re an efficient unit  even if it s because they suffer under a dictator   so  you already selected your pawns  huh   i ve also discovered your true identity  you re the school chairman s daughter  she knows his white room history  he refuses her third semester play and deflects onto class b  present when sakayanagi cold reads the ichinose parallel  he leaves without eye contact  topic of the pitch  he agrees she is a model student and notes she seems to have no secret mean streak  declines to play sakayanagi  considers telling horikita about the ichinose threat  later  names him as a talented puppet master candidate against ryuuen  cites hirata as the best example that bringing people together is not general skill  internal note  the hidden self is usually not as extreme as kushida s  dragon boy as sakayanagi s label  the rooftop fight is what she is probing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: the pharmacy bag and Sakayanagi’s Ichinose pitch<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.35–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">December 23 morning, Keyaki Mall; Ayanokōji leaves a store with a small paper bag of something he’s never used, then runs into Sakayanagi Arisu.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ve never used this stuff before,”<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll pass, thanks. You’re conspicuous, and I don’t like drawing attention,”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, they’re an efficient unit, even if it’s because they suffer under a dictator,”<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, you already selected your pawns, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve also discovered your true identity. You’re the school chairman’s daughter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She knows his White Room history; he refuses her third-semester play and deflects onto Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> Present when Sakayanagi cold-reads the Ichinose parallel; he leaves without eye contact.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Topic of the pitch; he agrees she is a model student and notes she seems to have no secret mean streak.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Declines to play Sakayanagi; considers telling Horikita about the Ichinose threat, later.<span class=\"pg\">p.37, 43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Names him as a talented puppet-master candidate against Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Cites Hirata as the best example that bringing people together is not general skill.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Internal note: the hidden self is usually not as extreme as Kushida’s.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Dragon Boy as Sakayanagi’s label; the rooftop fight is what she is probing.<span class=\"pg\">p.36, 49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p27-1\">← Before: coverage passes<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p73-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the snow bench with Ryuuen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p73-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-manabu kushida-kikyou nagumo-miyabi sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 0  the snow bench with ryuuen december 24 before seven  bench near keyaki mall  ayanokoji meets ryuuen alone in heavy snow  then horikita manabu arrives on cue   i needed to meet you when i was sure no one else would be around   i d like you to hold off on that  if possible  i d rather live peacefully  fighting you again would just be a pain   what  did i break you that badly after just one defeat  i asked   interestingly enough  it seems that class a will attack class b once the third semester begins  we could take class a out with a single strike while they re focused on that   in the third semester  class d will be promoted to class c  i said   however  we ll probably fall back down to d when i get kushida kikyou expelled   my policy is to avoid choices with low probabilities of success   if you re afraid of someone outsmarting you  then you simply have to outsmart them first  that s all there is to it  ryuuen  shared interest deal without paper  strike class a  groundwork via kaneda and hiyori  ryuuen s price is class a spoils  the debt  stop nagumo  receives the briefs  agrees to name himself to the undercover second year  the inside cancer he will slow  then expel at the cost of class d s promotion  the man he must stop  accepts manabu s mission  her class a b plan is the fifty fifty intel  he may look up expulsion infractions  non aggression pair with class b  idealist contrast in the nagumo debate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the snow bench with Ryuuen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.73–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">December 24 before seven, bench near Keyaki Mall; Ayanokōji meets Ryuuen alone in heavy snow, then Horikita Manabu arrives on cue.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I needed to meet you when I was sure no one else would be around.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’d like you to hold off on that, if possible. I’d rather live peacefully. Fighting you again would just be a pain,”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What? Did I break you that badly after just one defeat?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Interestingly enough, it seems that Class A will attack Class B once the third semester begins. We could take Class A out with a single strike while they’re focused on that,”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In the third semester, Class D will be promoted to Class C,” I said. “However, we’ll probably fall back down to D when I get Kushida Kikyou expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “My policy is to avoid choices with low probabilities of success,”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re afraid of someone outsmarting you, then you simply have to outsmart them first. That’s all there is to it, Ryuuen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Shared-interest deal without paper: strike Class A, groundwork via Kaneda and Hiyori; Ryuuen’s price is Class A spoils.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The debt: stop Nagumo; receives the briefs; agrees to name himself to the undercover second year.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The inside cancer he will slow, then expel at the cost of Class D’s promotion.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The man he must stop; accepts Manabu’s mission.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Her Class A–B plan is the fifty-fifty intel; he may look up expulsion infractions.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Non-aggression pair with Class B; idealist contrast in the Nagumo debate.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p35-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the pharmacy bag and Sakayanagi’s Ichinose pitch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p107-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the double date forms<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p107-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"satou-maya karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 1  the double date forms christmas day  ayanokoji meets satou for a one on one movie  then hirata and karuizawa force a spontaneous double date   just go with the flow  i guess   if you three are okay with it  i don t have any objections  i said   that s a tricky question  i said   his type   there s nothing going on between horikita and me  i mean  we re both doing our own thing on christmas  the christmas date  rejects her confession honestly  still wants to hang out again  sees through her double date scheme  later the bush eavesdrop and nagumo manabu briefing walk  saint of the double date  white room cannot explain romance  hirata s creed that everyone else being happy is enough  grabbed by the arm   won t you play with me  online game special test tease  debt and sibling revelation to karuizawa  mission to dethrone nagumo","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the double date forms<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.107–120<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Christmas Day; Ayanokōji meets Satou for a one-on-one movie, then Hirata and Karuizawa force a spontaneous double date.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Just go with the flow, I guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you three are okay with it, I don’t have any objections,” I said.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s a tricky question,” I said. (his type)<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing going on between Horikita and me. I mean, we’re both doing our own thing on Christmas.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> The Christmas date; rejects her confession honestly; still wants to hang out again.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Sees through her double-date scheme; later the bush eavesdrop and Nagumo/Manabu briefing walk.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Saint of the double date; White Room cannot explain romance; Hirata’s creed that everyone else being happy is enough.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Grabbed by the arm; “Won’t you play with me?”; online-game special-test tease.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Debt and sibling revelation to Karuizawa; mission to dethrone Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p73-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the snow bench with Ryuuen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p154-1\">→ After: Ch.6: the Kiriyama meet and the Kei Christmas gift<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p154-1","v":"y1v7.5","y":1,"o":9,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto karuizawa-kei nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  the kiriyama meet and the kei christmas gift dusk after the double date  ayanokoji and karuizawa wait at an isolated campus spot  vice president kiriyama arrives instead of the expected contact  sec  6 1 walks back to the dorms with the partner talk and gift exchange   they re late  i replied   she s trustworthy  she s my partner  i replied   tell us what you want  i said   we ll decide how to go about it   what do you think of what vice president kiriyama said  i asked   if your value lay only in your relationship with hirata  i d tell you to never break up with him  the fact that i didn t is my answer   i ll call you kei from here on out   i am indeed kidding   i played a major part in what happened to you on the roof  it was cruel  if you wanted to take a swing at me  i wouldn t resist  to tell the truth  i avoided contacting you because i thought it would stress you out to hear me  sounds like i was wrong  though   i intend to avoid drawing attention from here on out  however  there may be times when i need to move covertly  when i do  please help me  secret meet  accepts karuizawa as partner  agrees to help stop nagumo  burner e mail only  official partner  first name basis  kei  cold medicine gift reveals he saw the double date plot  nudged her off hirata on purpose  target of kiriyama s intel  ayanokoji already on nagumo s list after the relay  kiriyama admired him  intel would go to him if nagumo falls  bought cold medicine for karuizawa on the 23rd after seeing her with satou at keyaki mall  admits the roof hurt her  asks for covert help going forward","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p154-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: the Kiriyama meet and the Kei Christmas gift<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V7.5 · p.154–170<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Dusk after the double date: Ayanokōji and Karuizawa wait at an isolated campus spot; Vice President Kiriyama arrives instead of the expected contact; sec. 6.1 walks back to the dorms with the partner talk and gift exchange.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“They’re late,” I replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She’s trustworthy. She’s my partner,” I replied.<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Tell us what you want,” I said. “We’ll decide how to go about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you think of what Vice President Kiriyama said?” I asked.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If your value lay only in your relationship with Hirata, I’d tell you to never break up with him. The fact that I didn’t is my answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll call you Kei from here on out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am indeed kidding.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I played a major part in what happened to you on the roof. It was cruel. If you wanted to take a swing at me, I wouldn’t resist, to tell the truth. I avoided contacting you because I thought it would stress you out to hear me. Sounds like I was wrong, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I intend to avoid drawing attention from here on out. However, there may be times when I need to move covertly. When I do, please help me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Secret meet; accepts Karuizawa as partner; agrees to help stop Nagumo; burner e-mail only.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Official partner; first-name basis (“Kei”); cold-medicine gift reveals he saw the double-date plot; nudged her off Hirata on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Target of Kiriyama’s intel; Ayanokōji already on Nagumo’s list after the relay.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Kiriyama admired him; intel would go to him if Nagumo falls.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Bought cold medicine for Karuizawa on the 23rd after seeing her with Satou at Keyaki Mall; admits the roof hurt her; asks for covert help going forward.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v7_5-p107-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the double date forms<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p11-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"inner spoken","w":"chabashira-sae hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  the bus briefing and his safety list third semester road trip  ayanokoji rides the class c bus in a school mandated jersey and listens to chabashira s mixed training camp briefing while ike talks across the aisle   i m sorry  you are class c now  allow me to give you newly promoted students an overview of the special exam   yes  the penalty is expulsion  overall ranking uses the large group s average  but expulsions turn on each small group s average under the school s threshold    that was troubling  on the solidarity rule  a representative cannot casually drag an enemy class down unless someone was already  on the verge of dropping out anyway  and peers would know who that was  texts a certain individual to learn whether the student council helped design this exam   no reply is recorded on these pages  class penalty for an expulsion is 100 class points  a class without enough points floors at zero until the debt is paid  watches hirata buy into the lifeline question  notes the class cannot afford to extend it   private points are not pocket money  you d do well to remember that  reads chabashira s warning as school policy that still disrupts cohesion  recalls that he and horikita once pooled points to save sudou   a prior precedent for sharing  replies to her text with  none  then  guys and girls are going to be separated in this exam  i can t help with anything  do your best  messages kei the bare minimum  she replies with a blank receipt  he sends protective tricks because she could be made a sacrificial representative and is not currently strong in scores or standing   i had to narrow down the list of people i wanted to safeguard    kei  hirata  horikita  student council entanglement  then keisei  akito  haruka and airi  nagumo s grade level moves are the only outside thread he plans to watch  plans to keep an eye on nagumo during the rare mixed grade exam  claims he does not care about winning this exam   only passing it safely   while still engineering small interventions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the bus briefing and his safety list<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.11–32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Third-semester road trip; Ayanokōji rides the Class C bus in a school-mandated jersey and listens to Chabashira’s Mixed Training Camp briefing while Ike talks across the aisle.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “I’m sorry. You are Class C now. Allow me to give you newly promoted students an overview of the special exam.”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Yes. The penalty is expulsion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “private points are not pocket money. You’d do well to remember that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Overall ranking uses the large group’s average, but expulsions turn on each small group’s average under the school’s threshold — “That was troubling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the solidarity rule: a representative cannot casually drag an enemy class down unless someone was already “on the verge of dropping out anyway,” and peers would know who that was.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Texts a certain individual to learn whether the student council helped design this exam — no reply is recorded on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Class penalty for an expulsion is 100 class points; a class without enough points floors at zero until the debt is paid.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Watches Hirata buy into the lifeline question; notes the class cannot afford to extend it.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Reads Chabashira’s warning as school policy that still disrupts cohesion; recalls that he and Horikita once pooled points to save Sudou — a prior precedent for sharing.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Replies to her text with “None,” then “Guys and girls are going to be separated in this exam. I can’t help with anything. Do your best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Messages Kei the bare minimum; she replies with a blank receipt; he sends protective tricks because she could be made a sacrificial representative and is not currently strong in scores or standing.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> “I had to narrow down the list of people I wanted to safeguard.” — Kei, Hirata, Horikita (student-council entanglement), then Keisei, Akito, Haruka and Airi; Nagumo’s grade-level moves are the only outside thread he plans to watch.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Plans to keep an eye on Nagumo during the rare mixed-grade exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Claims he does not care about winning this exam — only passing it safely — while still engineering small interventions.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: arrival and the Class A pitch<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p33-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei kanzaki-ryuuji hirata-yousuke ike-kanji kaneda-satoru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2  arrival and the class a pitch the bus climbs the mountain road  phones are surrendered by syllabary order  ayanokoji disembarks into cold air before the camp grounds   i m not cut out for this  rare honest slip   special exams still do not suit him because he so rarely had to cooperate with others before  reads the terrain like the uninhabited island test  flags ike s scouting and sudou s strength as assets in the wild  horikita seems to want to speak to him as the lines split  but the queue separates boys and girls before she can  gymnasium  every grade s boys assemble  class a moves first  notes katsuragi inside matoba s fourteen and that matoba   not katsuragi   speaks  katsuragi is pre announced as the group s representative who will eat a last place solidarity hit alone  tracks kanzaki refusing the five minute ultimatum and correctly predicts class a returns once the window closes  joins hirata and keisei s huddle  volunteers that class a might be trusted to protect one nervous class c student  stays silent when no b or d candidate steps up  watches ike and yamauchi take hirata s bait for the safe class a seat  yamauchi wins the rock paper scissors  hears kaneda s all four class siege  accepts that ryuuen s absence is deliberate and that kaneda is the one holding class d s line","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2: arrival and the Class A pitch<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.33–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The bus climbs the mountain road; phones are surrendered by syllabary order; Ayanokōji disembarks into cold air before the camp grounds. Gymnasium: every grade’s boys assemble; Class A moves first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m not cut out for this…”<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rare honest slip — special exams still do not suit him because he so rarely had to cooperate with others before.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the terrain like the uninhabited-island test; flags Ike’s scouting and Sudou’s strength as assets in the wild.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita seems to want to speak to him as the lines split, but the queue separates boys and girls before she can.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Notes Katsuragi inside Matoba’s fourteen and that Matoba — not Katsuragi — speaks; Katsuragi is pre-announced as the group’s representative who will eat a last-place solidarity hit alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Tracks Kanzaki refusing the five-minute ultimatum and correctly predicts Class A returns once the window closes.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Joins Hirata and Keisei’s huddle; volunteers that Class A might be trusted to protect one nervous Class C student; stays silent when no B or D candidate steps up.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Watches Ike and Yamauchi take Hirata’s bait for the safe Class A seat; Yamauchi wins the rock-paper-scissors.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Hears Kaneda’s all-four-class siege; accepts that Ryuuen’s absence is deliberate and that Kaneda is the one holding Class D’s line.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p11-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: the bus briefing and his safety list<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3–2.6: group six, Nagumo’s draft, Kōenji, cafeteria<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p44-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko miyake-akito hirata-yousuke ryuuen-kakeru kanzaki-ryuuji nagumo-miyabi kouenji-rokusuke hashimoto-masayoshi ishizaki-daichi ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei sakayanagi-arisu satou-maya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3 2 6  group six  nagumo s draft  koenji  cafeteria gym group forming after the class a pitch  ayanokoji watches the four class math  ends in a ten person mixed group  faces nagumo s early draft and the cafeteria hour  keisei and akito check his plan  he bats the question back  later he shoves keisei forward as the delayed group s rock paper scissors proxy and keisei ends up representative  akito says his head is not his strong suit and sticks with keisei  ayanokoji suspects akito s ryuuen bid is a cover for taking the seat no one wants  tracks hirata inviting ryuuen into the c heavy group and the silence that follows   goodwill cannot carry a group test  reads ryuuen s proud solitude as someone who will not defy the school but will not cooperate either  no one wants him  including ishizaki  accepts kanzaki s risk logic   ryuuen s cost should sit with class d  maps the eighty first year boys into four main fifteen person groups plus two leftover tens on paper before the gym finishes  nagumo calls him out after the draft  deduces the delayed groups were the balanced three four class mixes  and ayanokoji still plans to keep him under observation at meals   kouenji is going to be a problem too  reads koenji s boycott threat as possibly deliberate contradiction  agrees with nagumo that the class a cash plan is the real story  notes koenji never needed class a if his only goal was graduation  shares a bottom bunk under hashimoto and introduces himself with a light handshake  ishizaki refuses eye contact until ayanokoji stands beside yukimura  later ayanokoji walks out of the sniping rather than escalate  sits near ichinose at the one hour cafeteria  answers her greeting honestly  tells her not to work herself too hard and leaves before the hour ends  assumes kei and horikita may be looking for him but avoids conspicuous contact   sakayanagi and nagumo might be watching  names her as a possible cafeteria watcher  notes hirata and sato s christmas outing is known to nagumo as a special relationship marker  closes the chapter with the island refrain   i m not suited to this at all    the shared hour is for well liked students with communication skills he does not have","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3–2.6: group six, Nagumo’s draft, Kōenji, cafeteria<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.44–76<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gym group-forming after the Class A pitch; Ayanokōji watches the four-class math, ends in a ten-person mixed group, faces Nagumo’s early draft and the cafeteria hour.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+7 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Kouenji is going to be a problem too”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Keisei and Akito check his plan; he bats the question back; later he shoves Keisei forward as the delayed group’s rock-paper-scissors proxy and Keisei ends up representative.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45, 55, 61–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Akito says his head is not his strong suit and sticks with Keisei; Ayanokōji suspects Akito’s Ryuuen bid is a cover for taking the seat no one wants.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45, 50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Tracks Hirata inviting Ryuuen into the C-heavy group and the silence that follows — goodwill cannot carry a group test.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reads Ryuuen’s proud solitude as someone who will not defy the school but will not cooperate either; no one wants him, including Ishizaki.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Accepts Kanzaki’s risk logic — Ryuuen’s cost should sit with Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Maps the eighty first-year boys into four main fifteen-person groups plus two leftover tens on paper before the gym finishes.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo calls him out after the draft, deduces the delayed groups were the balanced three/four-class mixes, and Ayanokōji still plans to keep him under observation at meals.<span class=\"pg\">p.52, 61, 72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Reads Kōenji’s boycott threat as possibly deliberate contradiction; agrees with Nagumo that the Class A cash plan is the real story; notes Kōenji never needed Class A if his only goal was graduation.<span class=\"pg\">p.51, 63–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Shares a bottom bunk under Hashimoto and introduces himself with a light handshake.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Ishizaki refuses eye contact until Ayanokōji stands beside Yukimura; later Ayanokōji walks out of the sniping rather than escalate.<span class=\"pg\">p.51, 69–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Sits near Ichinose at the one-hour cafeteria; answers her greeting honestly; tells her not to work herself too hard and leaves before the hour ends.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Assumes Kei and Horikita may be looking for him but avoids conspicuous contact — Sakayanagi and Nagumo might be watching.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Names her as a possible cafeteria watcher.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Notes Hirata and Satō’s Christmas outing is known to Nagumo as a special relationship marker.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Closes the chapter with the island refrain: “I’m not suited to this at all.” — the shared hour is for well-liked students with communication skills he does not have.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: arrival and the Class A pitch<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p77-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1–3.6: first morning, dojo, PE, hallway<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p77-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke yukimura-teruhiko ishizaki-daichi hashimoto-masayoshi nagumo-miyabi sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1 3 6  first morning  dojo  pe  hallway six a m  wake up in group six s dorm  ayanokoji watches koenji s training bait  ishizaki s temper  and hashimoto s peacemaking through cleaning  zazen  breakfast  pe and the sakayanagi bump  tracks koenji s dawn training and lotus ease  slows to jog beside him and asks him to ease the group s pace    ayanokouji boy    gets nothing  concludes threats and pleas are meaningless to him   it would be nice if the group could score reasonably well  i d like to avoid expulsion  notes yukimura s clock panic and cooking proposals  draws him into the dojo talk on peacemaking and befriending ishizaki and albert  reads ishizaki s hierarchy rise post ryuuen and his hurtful standoffishness as damage  wants to peel another layer off the school with him and albert  credits hashimoto as the most qualified to hold the group together   class a poise and clear assessment   but unwilling to lead  cites nagumo s cross class pull as the model  yukimura answers that only class a graduates laugh last  asks  are you okay  after yamauchi s bump  hears the ichinose treasurer rumor and deflects    that has nothing to do with me  defends ichinose against the selfish points reading while sakayanagi talks past him  realizes he wants the group safe from expulsion enough to move on koenji sooner rather than later  rules out pure observation  would rather give yukimura the bare minimum than watch him fail as representative under solidarity risk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p77-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1–3.6: first morning, dojo, PE, hallway<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.77–93<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Six a.m. wake-up in group six’s dorm; Ayanokōji watches Kōenji’s training bait, Ishizaki’s temper, and Hashimoto’s peacemaking through cleaning, zazen, breakfast, PE and the Sakayanagi bump.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“It would be nice if the group could score reasonably well. I’d like to avoid expulsion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Tracks Kōenji’s dawn training and lotus ease; slows to jog beside him and asks him to ease the group’s pace — “Ayanokouji Boy” — gets nothing; concludes threats and pleas are meaningless to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.77–79, 83, 87–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Notes Yukimura’s clock panic and cooking proposals; draws him into the dojo talk on peacemaking and befriending Ishizaki and Albert.<span class=\"pg\">p.79, 84–85, 89–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Reads Ishizaki’s hierarchy rise post-Ryuuen and his hurtful standoffishness as damage; wants to peel another layer off the school with him and Albert.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 85, 89–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Credits Hashimoto as the most qualified to hold the group together — Class A poise and clear assessment — but unwilling to lead.<span class=\"pg\">p.79, 85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Cites Nagumo’s cross-class pull as the model; Yukimura answers that only Class A graduates laugh last.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Asks “Are you okay?” after Yamauchi’s bump; hears the Ichinose-treasurer rumor and deflects — “That has nothing to do with me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.92–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Defends Ichinose against the selfish-points reading while Sakayanagi talks past him.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Realizes he wants the group safe from expulsion enough to move on Kōenji sooner rather than later; rules out pure observation.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Would rather give Yukimura the bare minimum than watch him fail as representative under solidarity risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3–2.6: group six, Nagumo’s draft, Kōenji, cafeteria<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p96-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.7–3.9: the marked deck<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p96-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi kouenji-rokusuke totsuka-yahiko hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 7 3 9  the marked deck nagumo s card visit to group six  ayanokoji is pulled in for the fifth old maid and reads the stacked senior play  nagumo never looks at him until he calls him in  the final offer is a marked joker   ayanokoji picks the right hand winning card after a two second feint of thought   i like the one on the right  i ll take that one  maps the notch on the joker  the win spread predictions  and the sealed box first deal to conclude the deck is marked  declines to expose it  watches koenji s bait question to nagumo land and nagumo s amiable non answer  yahiko swaps in for yukimura and signals the tag out  they share the last first year wins  hashimoto volunteers when no one else will and steadies the first years after losses  refuses the talk back nagumo wants from him  wins without showing the marked card    you lost  is left for ishikura to say","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p96-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 sec. 3.7–3.9: the marked deck<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.96–109<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nagumo’s card visit to group six; Ayanokōji is pulled in for the fifth Old Maid and reads the stacked senior play.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I like the one on the right. I’ll take that one”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo never looks at him until he calls him in; the final offer is a marked joker — Ayanokōji picks the right-hand winning card after a two-second feint of thought.<span class=\"pg\">p.100, 104, 107–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Maps the notch on the joker, the win-spread predictions, and the sealed-box first deal to conclude the deck is marked; declines to expose it.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Watches Kōenji’s bait question to Nagumo land and Nagumo’s amiable non-answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.98, 105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Yahiko swaps in for Yukimura and signals the tag-out; they share the last first-year wins.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Hashimoto volunteers when no one else will and steadies the first-years after losses.<span class=\"pg\">p.99, 103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Refuses the talk-back Nagumo wants from him; wins without showing the marked card — “You lost” is left for Ishikura to say.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p77-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1–3.6: first morning, dojo, PE, hallway<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p110-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1–4.3: cooking, window, Kiriyama, Kei, bath<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p110-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi kouenji-rokusuke hashimoto-masayoshi yamada-albert ichinose-honami sakayanagi-arisu kiriyama-ikuto ishikura nagumo-miyabi karuizawa-kei kanzaki-ryuuji ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 1 4 3  cooking  window  kiriyama  kei  bath third camp morning through night bath  cook duty fracture  ichinose s group through the glass  kiriyama s confrontation  dinner intel with karuizawa  kanzaki s ryuuen report  watches the oversalted soup and koenji hunt  notes the ishizaki koenji relationship wrecked beyond repair  tracks koenji s half hour bathroom absence and later the classroom clash where he refuses group judgment  credits hashimoto and albert as the team s cooking trump cards  takes the easy prep station beside albert  silent eye language knife handoff while dicing vegetables  window watch  ichinose slows to run support beside lagging wang mei yu with shiina alongside  notes sakayanagi s crush ichinose vow shows no surface sign from the third floor view  present through the second year encirclement  reads kiriyama as lumping first years together for nagumo s score s sake  watches ishikura defuse the bullying risk and nagumo s open class a   horikita removal offer get refused  files nagumo s guileless or performed plan speech in front of everyone  dinner seat by design  she answers group maps and ryuuen fear  he calls her kei and warns  a storm is coming  bathhouse exchange   kanzaki s no rumor report through miyake s three days is taken as probably true  reassures kei ryuuen won t act carelessly against her  frames him as  somewhat domesticated  wants a better handle on the girls  groups  treats manners and ethics as macguffin   necessary but not the point   but this exam  let s just say a storm is coming  has memorized first year names to faces from exam necessity  quizzes kei to prove it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1–4.3: cooking, window, Kiriyama, Kei, bath<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.110–128<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Third camp morning through night bath: cook-duty fracture, Ichinose’s group through the glass, Kiriyama’s confrontation, dinner intel with Karuizawa, Kanzaki’s Ryuuen report.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+6 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“But this exam… Let’s just say a storm is coming.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Watches the oversalted soup and Kōenji hunt; notes the Ishizaki–Kōenji relationship wrecked beyond repair.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Tracks Kōenji’s half-hour bathroom absence and later the classroom clash where he refuses group judgment.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112, 116–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Credits Hashimoto and Albert as the team’s cooking trump cards; takes the easy prep station beside Albert.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> Silent eye-language knife handoff while dicing vegetables.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Window watch: Ichinose slows to run support beside lagging Wang Mei-Yu with Shiina alongside.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Notes Sakayanagi’s crush-Ichinose vow shows no surface sign from the third-floor view.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Present through the second-year encirclement; reads Kiriyama as lumping first-years together for Nagumo’s score’s sake.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Watches Ishikura defuse the bullying risk and Nagumo’s open Class A / Horikita-removal offer get refused.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Files Nagumo’s guileless-or-performed plan speech in front of everyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Dinner seat by design; she answers group maps and Ryuuen fear; he calls her Kei and warns “a storm is coming.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Bathhouse exchange — Kanzaki’s no-rumor report through Miyake’s three days is taken as probably true.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reassures Kei Ryuuen won’t act carelessly against her; frames him as “somewhat domesticated.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Wants a better handle on the girls’ groups; treats manners and ethics as MacGuffin — necessary but not the point.<span class=\"pg\">p.120, 126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Has memorized first-year names-to-faces from exam necessity; quizzes Kei to prove it.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p96-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.7–3.9: the marked deck<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p129-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.5: the note and the corridor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p129-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji sudou-ken kouenji-rokusuke ryuuen-kakeru horikita-manabu nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 4 4 5  the note and the corridor bathhouse exit and kanzaki s class c offer  later 1 a m   25  note and the morse light corridor meeting with horikita manabu  accepts the offer to keep class c relations  files kanzaki s honesty read of horikita as integrity  not naivety  dodges the size question  waves off sudou s  last rites  offer when the chant forces his hand  refuses the bait until ryuuen s trap closes  drops the towel to a near stalemate koenji still claims by experience  reads ryuuen s planted hidden power line and  take it off  chant as a malicious trap he cannot escape without losing bath time  meets in the pitch black corridor  lies that nagumo shows no strange sign  takes the student council rules power and the  he might lose  verdict  withholds concern about nagumo s public challenge and lax lesson discipline from manabu  files the never broken promise certainty  decides this exam is observation only   no special exam tricks   to fade into the background  defense only if someone tries to expel him  exam components named  zazen manners posture  long distance relay  four criterion speech  ethics written essay  cleaning cooking tardiness scoring still unclear   he might lose  lies to manabu about nagumo while knowing several concerns  reads the meeting risk as worth the information","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p129-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.5: the note and the corridor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.129–147<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Bathhouse exit and Kanzaki’s Class C offer; later 1 a.m. “25” note and the Morse-light corridor meeting with Horikita Manabu.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“He might lose”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Accepts the offer to keep Class C relations; files Kanzaki’s honesty read of Horikita as integrity, not naivety.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Dodges the size question; waves off Sudou’s “last rites” offer when the chant forces his hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.130, 139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Refuses the bait until Ryuuen’s trap closes; drops the towel to a near-stalemate Kōenji still claims by experience.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reads Ryuuen’s planted hidden-power line and “Take it off!” chant as a malicious trap he cannot escape without losing bath time.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Meets in the pitch-black corridor; lies that Nagumo shows no strange sign; takes the student-council rules power and the “He might lose” verdict.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Withholds concern about Nagumo’s public challenge and lax lesson discipline from Manabu; files the never-broken-promise certainty.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Decides this exam is observation only — no special-exam tricks — to fade into the background; defense only if someone tries to expel him.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Exam components named: zazen manners/posture, long-distance relay, four-criterion speech, ethics written essay; cleaning/cooking/tardiness scoring still unclear.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Lies to Manabu about Nagumo while knowing several concerns; reads the meeting risk as worth the information.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p110-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1–4.3: cooking, window, Kiriyama, Kei, bath<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p153-1\">→ After: Ch.6 half 1: the slope, Kōenji, and the Ayanokōji Group dinner<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p153-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke yukimura-teruhiko hashimoto-masayoshi ishizaki-daichi hasebe-haruka sakura-airi miyake-akito chabashira-sae nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 half 1  the slope  koenji  and the ayanokoji group dinner day five 18 km course walk as group representative s escort  pov runs the retrieval of koenji and the dinner table after   kouenji went off on some other path back there  i ll go call him back   no matter who goes  we might not be able to bring him back   i m here to keep you from potentially getting expelled via the solidarity rule  why did you take this detour   about the exam  i want you to help the group   what do you mean  what s how what is   what time is it  sensei   it was just good timing that the two of us were running near you   you might be right about that   grab a breather  i ll take your spot   hey  we help each other out when we re in trouble   i ll handle it   even if keisei injures himself as a result  chases the forest detour to stop solidarity expulsion  grabs his arm  accepts the dragon boy read and leaves him to the boar  takes keisei s leave at the turnaround  carries the sprained leg with hashimoto   don t feel embarrassed  refuses his help offer on koenji  later partners the carry  rates him the group s right distance glue  p 172 half 2  blocked from helping keisei  ishizaki speaks to him for the first time then backs away  reunited at dinner  her group with sakura report steadies the boys  side  bashful  been a while  same group as hasebe  presses the ryuuen groups report  ends on the girls are fine reassurance  turnaround roll call exchange  waits with her for koenji  will not actively make a move but takes the private koenji chance  waits past everyone for the tail end  takes keisei s cleaning slot  absorbs ishizaki s order without a scene  cannot clear the dragon boy misunderstanding    too bad  that s not going to happen  not present  miyacchi s report that ryuuen is acting normal is the dinner intel he keeps","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 half 1: the slope, Kōenji, and the Ayanokōji Group dinner<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.153–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Day-five 18 km course walk as group representative’s escort; POV runs the retrieval of Kōenji and the dinner table after.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+3 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Kouenji went off on some other path back there. I’ll go call him back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No matter who goes, we might not be able to bring him back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m here to keep you from potentially getting expelled via the solidarity rule. Why did you take this detour?”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “About the exam. I want you to help the group.”<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What do you mean? What’s how what is?”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What time is it, sensei?”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was just good timing that the two of us were running near you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You might be right about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Grab a breather. I’ll take your spot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hey, we help each other out when we’re in trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll handle it”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if Keisei injures himself as a result?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Chases the forest detour to stop solidarity expulsion; grabs his arm; accepts the Dragon Boy read and leaves him to the boar.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Takes Keisei’s leave at the turnaround; carries the sprained leg with Hashimoto; “Don’t feel embarrassed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155, 161–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Refuses his help offer on Kōenji; later partners the carry; rates him the group’s right-distance glue (p.172 half 2).<span class=\"pg\">p.160–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Blocked from helping Keisei; Ishizaki speaks to him for the first time then backs away.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Reunited at dinner; her group-with-Sakura report steadies the boys’ side.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Bashful “been a while”; same group as Hasebe.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Presses the Ryuuen-groups report; ends on the girls-are-fine reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Turnaround roll call exchange; waits with her for Kōenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.160–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Will not actively make a move but takes the private Kōenji chance; waits past everyone for the tail end.<span class=\"pg\">p.157, 160–161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes Keisei’s cleaning slot; absorbs Ishizaki’s order without a scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Cannot clear the Dragon Boy misunderstanding — “Too bad. That’s not going to happen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Not present; Miyacchi’s report that Ryuuen is acting normal is the dinner intel he keeps.<span class=\"pg\">p.165–166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p129-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.5: the note and the corridor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.6 half 2: Asahina and the first real night<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p170-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"asahina-nazuna karuizawa-kei kiriyama-ikuto nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu hashimoto-masayoshi ishizaki-daichi yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 half 2  asahina and the first real night cleaning veto aftermath  the asahina charm approach at dinner  and the pitch dark group talk that ends the chapter   even if keisei injures himself as a result   keisei  you need to stop trying to shoulder everything alone  you can t change anything in the one or two days we have left  if you make an error in judgment now  you might regret it later   look  just don t forget that i m here  if you re in trouble  i ll help   hmm   oh  sorry  i was just thinking i d seen that charm before  please don t mind me   oh  that so  did you happen to drop it a while back  by any chance   maybe  i picked it up on my way back to the dorm  uh when was that  again   do you know me   wait  were you there too   i m pretty fast  but to be honest i don t really have anything else going for me  maybe i ve caught president nagumo s eye through some kind of misunderstanding   how can i get nagumo senpai to stop paying attention to me   i see  that might be one option   so if nagumo s ever defeated  that would be trouble  huh   so you were joking  senpai   among all the second years i ve met until now  you seem to be the most straightforward one  asahina senpai   it s not about being shallow or deep  what matters is how much you ve been influenced by him   in that case  think of this as nonsense from a first year   are you sure  it might be seen as rebelling against nagumo senpai  you know   out of the girls in your grade level  how many would you say are especially close with nagumo senpai   what about the people who act as nagumo senpai s eyes and ears   well  as a senpai  it s okay to help a first year out a bit  right   what about when you met up with the first  and third year groups  did you decide things randomly then too   are there any first  or third years who were selected to join that girls  large group that stand out in particular   you have a lot of faith in nagumo senpai  huh   you were a big help  charm re accident  five minute corridor pitch  takes her nagumo picture and second year unity intel  tasks kei on asahina  limits direct contact to avoid relationship suspicion  left a clue for him  blocked because he is in nagumo s group  the real target of the asahina probe   true intentions toward horikita s brother  needs nagumo s intent toward him  asahina s fair square line read against manabu s own trust  private grade  could hold the group at the right distance  harder to read than sakayanagi or katsuragi  pushes the injury question  gets  that s that  advice against shouldering alone   don t forget that i m here  will not deepen into the boys  group   fading into the background is the point  small risk for the asahina contact  plays the uppity first year on purpose  reads nagumo s clues popping up strategy as different from sakayanagi and ryuuen  confirm whether nagumo fights above the board while manufacturing shadow fear","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 half 2: Asahina and the first real night<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.170–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Cleaning veto aftermath, the Asahina charm approach at dinner, and the pitch-dark group talk that ends the chapter.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Even if Keisei injures himself as a result?”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Keisei, you need to stop trying to shoulder everything alone. You can’t change anything in the one or two days we have left. If you make an error in judgment now, you might regret it later”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Look, just don’t forget that I’m here. If you’re in trouble, I’ll help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm?”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, sorry. I was just thinking I’d seen that charm before. Please don’t mind me”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh, that so? Did you happen to drop it a while back, by any chance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe… I picked it up on my way back to the dorm, uh…when was that, again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you know me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. Were you there too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m pretty fast, but to be honest I don’t really have anything else going for me. Maybe I’ve caught President Nagumo’s eye through some kind of misunderstanding”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “How can I get Nagumo-senpai to stop paying attention to me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. That might be one option”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So if Nagumo’s ever defeated, that would be trouble, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you were joking, senpai?”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Among all the second-years I’ve met until now, you seem to be the most straightforward one, Asahina-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not about being shallow or deep. What matters is how much you’ve been influenced by him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In that case, think of this as nonsense from a first-year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you sure? It might be seen as rebelling against Nagumo-senpai, you know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Out of the girls in your grade level, how many would you say are especially close with Nagumo-senpai?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about the people who act as Nagumo-senpai’s eyes and ears?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, as a senpai, it’s okay to help a first-year out a bit, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What about when you met up with the first- and third-year groups? Did you decide things randomly then too?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are there any first- or third-years who were selected to join that girls’ large group that stand out in particular?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You have a lot of faith in Nagumo-senpai, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You were a big help,”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Charm re-accident; five-minute corridor pitch; takes her Nagumo picture and second-year unity intel.<span class=\"pg\">p.173–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Tasks Kei on Asahina; limits direct contact to avoid relationship suspicion.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Left a clue for him; blocked because he is in Nagumo’s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> The real target of the Asahina probe — true intentions toward Horikita’s brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.173–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Needs Nagumo’s intent toward him; Asahina’s fair-square line read against Manabu’s own trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.173, 180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Private grade: could hold the group at the right distance; harder to read than Sakayanagi or Katsuragi.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Pushes the injury question; gets “that’s that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Advice against shouldering alone; “don’t forget that I’m here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Will not deepen into the boys’ group — fading into the background is the point; small risk for the Asahina contact.<span class=\"pg\">p.173–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Plays the uppity first-year on purpose; reads Nagumo’s clues-popping-up strategy as different from Sakayanagi and Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.178–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Confirm whether Nagumo fights above the board while manufacturing shadow-fear.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p153-1\">← Before: Ch.6 half 1: the slope, Kōenji, and the Ayanokōji Group dinner<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p186-1\">→ After: Ch.7 half 1: the relay math and Ichinose’s tell<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p186-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke ichinose-honami sakayanagi-arisu karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 half 1  the relay math and ichinose s tell last full day   dorm relay plan  dusting  final dinner with ichinose  kei s paper   then i ll try to do what i can  i don t know how fast i can run it  though   is that okay  kiyotaka   just don t expect too much from me   is something bothering you   you re facing a difficult problem  huh   that s a really roundabout question   i guess it seems different from the exams we ve had until now  a little tougher  there s a high risk of expulsion   i guess   yeah   you re talking about your classmates   if a classmate were expelled  what would you intend to do   why do you say that   it was a hypothetical question   sorry  you re giving me way too much credit  my language skills aren t that advanced  takes the relay volunteer   just don t expect too much  watches the bare minimum bargain  private expulsion math read  final dinner probe  the  intend  tell  watches her walk off alone  reads her move behind ichinose s collapse  takes the paper slip  shreds it across bins  ishizaki sudou comparison in the open  notes hashimoto kept the group from collapsing  hypothetical framing that ichinose catches  watches the smile that is not there today  understand what sakayanagi did to the girls before tomorrow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p186-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 half 1: the relay math and Ichinose’s tell<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.186–196<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Last full day — dorm relay plan, dusting, final dinner with Ichinose, Kei’s paper.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Then…I’ll try to do what I can. I don’t know how fast I can run it, though”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is that okay, Kiyotaka?”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Just don’t expect too much from me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is something bothering you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re facing a difficult problem, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s a really roundabout question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess it seems different from the exams we’ve had until now. A little tougher. There’s a high risk of expulsion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah.”<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re talking about your classmates?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If a classmate were expelled, what would you intend to do?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do you say that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It was a hypothetical question.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. You’re giving me way too much credit. My language skills aren’t that advanced.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Takes the relay volunteer; “Just don’t expect too much.”<span class=\"pg\">p.186–189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Watches the bare-minimum bargain; private-expulsion math read.<span class=\"pg\">p.188–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Final-dinner probe; the “intend” tell; watches her walk off alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reads her move behind Ichinose’s collapse.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Takes the paper slip; shreds it across bins.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ishizaki–Sudou comparison in the open; notes Hashimoto kept the group from collapsing.<span class=\"pg\">p.186–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Hypothetical framing that Ichinose catches; watches the smile that is not there today.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Understand what Sakayanagi did to the girls before tomorrow.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.6 half 2: Asahina and the first real night<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p196-1\">→ After: Ch.7 half 2: the note, the courtyard, the other stairs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p196-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"spoken","w":"tachibana-akane karuizawa-kei hashimoto-masayoshi nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 half 2  the note  the courtyard  the other stairs takes kei s slip  finds tachibana crying  trails hashimoto at midnight  exits the corridor the long way when nagumo plays his name   if you re in some kind of trouble maybe you should talk to the former student council president   if you re crying even though you re not in trouble  that might be a problem in and of itself   true  we don t get much private time  huh   for the record  i m on former president horikita s side   just consider the fact that it s better if we re not enemies   worry  huh  is there really anything to worry about when it comes to that guy   i know a little bit about how the second years  particularly nagumo  are his enemies   wait  you mean the class conflict among the third years is still ongoing   so even he s just a normal student   so you re depressed by the current situation   that depends on how tenacious you are  doesn t it   if you say so  i must be mistaken   i suppose this means it s checkmate if i don t make a move  huh  courtyard probing  the  horikita kun  slip noted  her back read as checkmate  the slip that starts the chain  shredded across bins  trails the midnight exit  takes the other stairs so the name play does not land on him  eavesdrops the abstain demand and ayanokoji name beat  withdraws before hashimoto returns  hears the rebuke from the opposite end of the corridor triangle  lies about being on former president horikita s side to gain trust  reads self sacrifice as an error in judgment  follows without a flashlight  picks the far stairs    i didn t like where this conversation was headed  make a move on tachibana s trouble before it is truly checkmate","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p196-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 half 2: the note, the courtyard, the other stairs<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.196–211<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Takes Kei’s slip; finds Tachibana crying; trails Hashimoto at midnight; exits the corridor the long way when Nagumo plays his name.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you’re in some kind of trouble…maybe you should talk to the former student council president?”<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If you’re crying even though you’re not in trouble, that might be a problem in and of itself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“True. We don’t get much private time, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the record, I’m on Former President Horikita’s side.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just consider the fact that it’s better if we’re not enemies.”<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Worry, huh? Is there really anything to worry about when it comes to that guy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know a little bit about how the second-years, particularly Nagumo, are his enemies”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. You mean the class conflict among the third-years is still ongoing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So even he’s just a normal student.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re depressed by the current situation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That depends on how tenacious you are, doesn’t it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you say so, I must be mistaken.”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I suppose this means it’s checkmate if I don’t make a move, huh?”<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> Courtyard probing; the “Horikita-kun” slip noted; her back read as checkmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The slip that starts the chain; shredded across bins.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Trails the midnight exit; takes the other stairs so the name play does not land on him.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Eavesdrops the abstain demand and Ayanokōji-name beat; withdraws before Hashimoto returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Hears the rebuke from the opposite end of the corridor triangle.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Lies about being on Former President Horikita’s side to gain trust; reads self-sacrifice as an error in judgment.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Follows without a flashlight; picks the far stairs — “I didn’t like where this conversation was headed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Make a move on Tachibana’s trouble before it is truly checkmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p186-1\">← Before: Ch.7 half 1: the relay math and Ichinose’s tell<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p215-1\">→ After: Ch.8: named as the distant reliable<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p215-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 8  named as the distant reliable named in suzune s powerless close   the one she could most often rely on   ayanokouji kun seemed like the one i could most often rely on  but he and i had grown more distant of late  probably because i forced him to talk about the student council in front of kushida san  distance after the student council reveal  still weighed against keeping kushida close  the reason for the distance   forced talk in front of her  named only   no dialogue this chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8: named as the distant reliable<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.215<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named in Suzune’s powerless close — the one she could most often rely on.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> “Ayanokouji-kun seemed like the one I could most often rely on, but he and I had grown more distant of late, probably because I forced him to talk about the student council in front of Kushida-san.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Distance after the student-council reveal; still weighed against keeping Kushida close.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The reason for the distance — forced talk in front of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Named only — no dialogue this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p196-1\">← Before: Ch.7 half 2: the note, the courtyard, the other stairs<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p216-1\">→ After: Ch.9 half 1: the sandbag and the van<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p216-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"","w":"yukimura-teruhiko hashimoto-masayoshi kouenji-rokusuke ishizaki-daichi sotomura-hideo hirata-yousuke nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 9 half 1  the sandbag and the van final camp day as one of the temporary guys  alliance  narrates the whole exam from briefing through the results open  handshake circle around the representative  steadies him after zazen  confirms the  95 written plan  plays along on the ryuuen probe without confirming anything  keeps nagumo s overnight interest to himself  reads his flawless zazen  refuses the van offer to run 2 4 km on a whim    i can t change keisei s strategy on my own  takes the fourth place baton  runs the gap to third for the handoff to koenji  shocked when the professor drops the archaic act after a zazen warning  marker side talk  not the anchor  hirata s  no one will be expelled  line taken at face value for now  reads the  boys  qualifier and the smiling second place as a live plot  not a loss  perfect zazen by his own read  deliberately misses one hard written question for a solid 95 so the school does not see successive perfect scores  turns down koenji s whim because trust on a whim can reverse on a whim  cold close  dead last for the large group would not touch him   still hopes no one is expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 half 1: the sandbag and the van<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.216–228<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Final camp day as one of the temporary guys’ alliance; narrates the whole exam from briefing through the results open.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Handshake circle around the representative; steadies him after zazen; confirms the ~95 written plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.216, 220–222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Plays along on the Ryuuen probe without confirming anything; keeps Nagumo’s overnight interest to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Reads his flawless zazen; refuses the van offer to run 2.4 km on a whim — “I can’t change Keisei’s strategy on my own.”<span class=\"pg\">p.219, 223–224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Takes the fourth-place baton; runs the gap to third for the handoff to Kōenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Shocked when the Professor drops the archaic act after a zazen warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Marker-side talk: not the anchor; Hirata’s “no one will be expelled” line taken at face value for now.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Reads the “boys” qualifier and the smiling second place as a live plot, not a loss.<span class=\"pg\">p.227–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Perfect zazen by his own read; deliberately misses one hard written question for a solid 95 so the school does not see successive perfect scores.<span class=\"pg\">p.219, 221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Turns down Kōenji’s whim because trust on a whim can reverse on a whim.<span class=\"pg\">p.223–224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Cold close: dead last for the large group would not touch him — still hopes no one is expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p215-1\">← Before: Ch.8: named as the distant reliable<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p229-1\">→ After: Ch.9 half 2: the trap read aloud<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p229-1","v":"y1v8","y":1,"o":10,"k":"inner spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu tachibana-akane karuizawa-kei asahina-nazuna ichinose-honami ishikura ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 9 half 2  the trap read aloud gym floor as the girls  results land  later the corridor debrief with karuizawa after he walks out on the showdown  names the trap as set before the school knew  explains the class b representative  the collusion  and the twenty million advance to ishikura  calls the strategy formidable and checkmate in advance  silent mind address on the no representative order and the airtight defense hole  watches the lifeline spent  exits when nothing he can do remains  the only female student manabu deeply connected to   the knife s limited targets   prepared to accept  cost of one hundred class points  corridor walk through of the whole strategy  answers her soft voice fear of the same situation with no lifeline with  i won t let you get expelled  names her as one of the three info sources behind the tachibana conclusion  same info source list  reads nagumo ishikura collusion and the class b payout from the pair s calm   look  i get it    the full reconstruction of manabu s protective orders and nagumo s malice   it s quite a formidable strategy  nagumo had a checkmate set up by the time his enemy got in the game   you don t even need me to answer  do you  i won t let you get expelled  no matter what methods i have to use  both classes run the lifeline at once  the chapter ends on school wide expulsions  one after another","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.9 half 2: the trap read aloud<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V8 · p.229–241<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gym floor as the girls’ results land; later the corridor debrief with Karuizawa after he walks out on the showdown.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+1 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">“Look, I get it…” — the full reconstruction of Manabu’s protective orders and Nagumo’s malice.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“It’s quite a formidable strategy. Nagumo had a checkmate set up by the time his enemy got in the game.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You don’t even need me to answer, do you? I won’t let you get expelled. No matter what methods I have to use.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Names the trap as set before the school knew; explains the Class B representative, the collusion, and the twenty-million advance to Ishikura; calls the strategy formidable and checkmate-in-advance.<span class=\"pg\">p.231–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Silent mind-address on the no-representative order and the airtight-defense hole; watches the lifeline spent; exits when nothing he can do remains.<span class=\"pg\">p.231–237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> The only female student Manabu deeply connected to — the knife’s limited targets; “prepared to accept” cost of one hundred class points.<span class=\"pg\">p.232–233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Corridor walk-through of the whole strategy; answers her soft-voice fear of the same situation with no lifeline with “I won’t let you get expelled.”<span class=\"pg\">p.237–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Names her as one of the three info sources behind the Tachibana conclusion.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Same info source list.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishikura<\/b> Reads Nagumo–Ishikura collusion and the Class B payout from the pair’s calm.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Effect<\/span> Both classes run the lifeline at once; the chapter ends on school-wide expulsions “one after another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.240–241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v8-p216-1\">← Before: Ch.9 half 1: the sandbag and the van<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p24-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka name raised at the end of the council visit as the sakayanagi nagumo audience ends  nagumo asks about ayanokoji  nagumo raises the name  sakayanagi says she is only somewhat familiar with it  nagumo drops the topic and refuses her offer to investigate   ayanokoji  i am somewhat familiar with that name  he s a 1st year  is he not  ayanokoji does not appear in person  only named in the closing exchange","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Name raised at the end of the council visit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As the Sakayanagi–Nagumo audience ends, Nagumo asks about Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “Ayanokōji…? I am somewhat familiar with that name. He’s a 1st year, is he not?”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo raises the name; Sakayanagi says she is only somewhat familiar with it; Nagumo drops the topic and refuses her offer to investigate.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji does not appear in person; only named in the closing exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p28-1\">→ After: Morning after the breakup; the slander note<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p28-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka morning after the breakup  the slander note early morning class c  karuizawa holds court with the girls  horikita quizzes ayanokoji on who dumped whom as the bell nears   you re rather late to school today  ayanokoji kun   so  which one of them dumped the other  the fake relationship was kei s  if hirata had done the dumping it would mean a problem with kei and could put her status at risk   so hirata likely suggested the public shape that protects her  partner for the morning analysis  she shows him the ichinose slander note and forces the standings notebook onto his desk  observes the breakup s effect on the girls  group  concludes kei can only lose command if someone inside the class truly wins hirata   unlikely  notes hirata boxed in by classmates with no misery  ike and sudo do not tease him   the class has moved past that  there s no doubt sakayanagi is behind the slander campaign  the school cannot trace diffuse word of mouth beyond warning perpetrators   recently  i ve been hearing slander directed at her  treats the four written accusations as defamation in society but weak as a school crime inside the isolated campus  the note s four lines   violence  compensated dating  theft and robbery  drug usage   are written text  not spoken","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Morning after the breakup; the slander note<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.28–32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Early morning Class C; Karuizawa holds court with the girls; Horikita quizzes Ayanokōji on who dumped whom as the bell nears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’re rather late to school today, Ayanokōji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“So, which one of them dumped the other?”<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Recently, I’ve been hearing slander directed at her.”<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The fake relationship was Kei’s; if Hirata had done the dumping it would mean a problem with Kei and could put her status at risk — so Hirata likely suggested the public shape that protects her.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Partner for the morning analysis; she shows him the Ichinose slander note and forces the standings notebook onto his desk.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Observes the breakup’s effect on the girls’ group; concludes Kei can only lose command if someone inside the class truly wins Hirata — unlikely.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Notes Hirata boxed in by classmates with no misery; Ike and Sudō do not tease him — the class has moved past that.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> There’s no doubt Sakayanagi is behind the slander campaign; the school cannot trace diffuse word-of-mouth beyond warning perpetrators.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Treats the four written accusations as defamation in society but weak as a school-crime inside the isolated campus.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The note’s four lines — violence, compensated dating, theft and robbery, drug usage — are written text, not spoken.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p24-1\">← Before: Name raised at the end of the council visit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p33-1\">→ After: Watching Sakayanagi and Yamauchi; the cafe study plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p33-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakayanagi-arisu hasebe-haruka yukimura-teruhiko sakura-airi miyake-akito ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka watching sakayanagi and yamauchi  the cafe study plan sakayanagi enters class c and names yamauchi  the ayanokoji group follows to the corridor and cafe  horikita blocks yamauchi s exit  ayanokoji stands aside   yamauchi does not heed the warning  analyzes sakayanagi s hair touching as a deliberate image rather than genuine interest  while allowing that boldness makes either possible   yamauchi and sakayanagi haven t interacted until now  it s too abrupt  isn t it too much to call it romance  cafe conversation led by haruka  he gives the rational counter that romance needs a foundation  yukimura sets the study plan   start after the practice test on the 15th  ayanokoji agrees the exam will be written  chabashira gave no special explanation for the end of year exam  so a failing grade means expulsion as usual  airi asks whether karuizawa is cute  he answers he never paid attention to her  takes miyake s club time call about the class a b quarrel  haruka proposes going to find him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Watching Sakayanagi and Yamauchi; the cafe study plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.33–42<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakayanagi enters Class C and names Yamauchi; the Ayanokōji Group follows to the corridor and cafe.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yamauchi and Sakayanagi haven’t interacted until now, it’s too abrupt. Isn’t it too much to call it romance?”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">Chabashira gave no special explanation for the end-of-year exam, so a failing grade means expulsion as usual.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Horikita blocks Yamauchi’s exit; Ayanokōji stands aside — Yamauchi does not heed the warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Analyzes Sakayanagi’s hair-touching as a deliberate image rather than genuine interest, while allowing that boldness makes either possible.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Cafe conversation led by Haruka; he gives the rational counter that romance needs a foundation.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Yukimura sets the study plan — start after the practice test on the 15th; Ayanokōji agrees the exam will be written.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Airi asks whether Karuizawa is cute; he answers he never paid attention to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.38–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Takes Miyake’s club-time call about the Class A–B quarrel; Haruka proposes going to find him.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p28-1\">← Before: Morning after the breakup; the slander note<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p43-1\">→ After: Gymnasium: Hashimoto against Kanzaki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p43-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi kanzaki-ryuuji miyake-akito ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka gymnasium  hashimoto against kanzaki gymnasium off the school building   hashimoto and kanzaki face off with miyake standing between them  the ayanokoji group arrives  watches hashimoto evade and eventually admit spreading rumors without claiming origin  concludes from his manner that the rumors aren t all lies  kanzaki asks his input  he advises staying until told to leave   a third party can keep a fight civil   isn t it fine until they tell us to leave  if at some point  this turns into a fight  the presence of a third party can help keep things civil  miyake called them over  ayanokoji stays as observer at his side  concludes from hashimoto s speech that the circulating rumors about ichinose  aren t all lies  notes defamation libel grounds if truth does not conflict with public interest  temporarily sets aside his position as a student and reads the situation from society s point of view   ichinose could sue regardless of truth where reputation damage is shown  quoted from hashimoto  ichinose s reply to kanzaki was neither affirmation nor denial of the rumors","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Gymnasium: Hashimoto against Kanzaki<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.43–50<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gymnasium off the school building — Hashimoto and Kanzaki face off with Miyake standing between them; the Ayanokōji Group arrives.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">Temporarily sets aside his position as a student and reads the situation from society’s point of view — Ichinose could sue regardless of truth where reputation damage is shown.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Watches Hashimoto evade and eventually admit spreading rumors without claiming origin; concludes from his manner that the rumors aren’t all lies.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Kanzaki asks his input; he advises staying until told to leave — a third party can keep a fight civil.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> “Isn’t it fine until they tell us to leave? If at some point, this turns into a fight, the presence of a third party can help keep things civil.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Miyake called them over; Ayanokōji stays as observer at his side.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Concludes from Hashimoto’s speech that the circulating rumors about Ichinose “aren’t all lies”; notes defamation/libel grounds if truth does not conflict with public interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Quoted from Hashimoto: Ichinose’s reply to Kanzaki was neither affirmation nor denial of the rumors.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p33-1\">← Before: Watching Sakayanagi and Yamauchi; the cafe study plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p51-1\">→ After: Gym exit, tail, and Mii-chan’s interception<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p51-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi miyake-akito ryuuen-kakeru wang-mei-yu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka gym exit  tail  and mii chan s interception gymnasium dispersal after hashimoto and kanzaki separate  then the dorm path thursday evening  feels incongruity   hashimoto no longer treats him as at the training camp  later confirms via front camera that hashimoto is tailing him into the cafe  if sakayanagi were monitoring him she would have used kamuro  not hashimoto  the tail may be hashimoto s own judgment  goes along with the delinquent talk  concludes miyake s ease with confrontation comes from growing up around fights  listens to miyake s history with ryuuen s neighbouring middle school and drops the thread    somebody else s problem  accepts mii chan s first ever face to face consultation  lets her choose the venue   keyaki mall cafe  for now ignores hashimoto and focuses on mii chan s conversation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Gym exit, tail, and Mii-chan’s interception<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.51–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Gymnasium dispersal after Hashimoto and Kanzaki separate; then the dorm path Thursday evening.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"wang-mei-yu.html\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">If Sakayanagi were monitoring him she would have used Kamuro, not Hashimoto; the tail may be Hashimoto’s own judgment.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Feels incongruity — Hashimoto no longer treats him as at the training camp; later confirms via front camera that Hashimoto is tailing him into the cafe.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Goes along with the delinquent talk; concludes Miyake’s ease with confrontation comes from growing up around fights.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Listens to Miyake’s history with Ryuuen’s neighbouring middle school and drops the thread — “somebody else’s problem.”<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/b> Accepts Mii-chan’s first-ever face-to-face consultation; lets her choose the venue — Keyaki Mall cafe.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> For now ignores Hashimoto and focuses on Mii-chan’s conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p43-1\">← Before: Gymnasium: Hashimoto against Kanzaki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p56-1\">→ After: The Hirata question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p56-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke wang-mei-yu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the hirata question asked who hirata likes after the karuizawa breakup  answers honestly that there is nobody and advises patience because hirata will be careful next time   i don t think so  asks mii chan when she started liking hirata and delivers a cold read of confess soon odds    you re probably going to be rejected if you get impatient and confess to him so soon  coach for her first crush  her communication still needs the work airi also needs  and he does not break the ice until she starts  her compliment that he is approachable is met with his own note that he is only running an unconscious analysis of what will be useful to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Hirata question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.56–62<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"wang-mei-yu.html\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t think so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Asked who Hirata likes after the Karuizawa breakup; answers honestly that there is nobody and advises patience because Hirata will be careful next time.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Asks Mii-chan when she started liking Hirata and delivers a cold read of confess-soon odds — “you’re probably going to be rejected if you get impatient and confess to him so soon.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/b> Coach for her first crush; her communication still needs the work Airi also needs, and he does not break the ice until she starts.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her compliment that he is approachable is met with his own note that he is only running an unconscious analysis of what will be useful to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p51-1\">← Before: Gym exit, tail, and Mii-chan’s interception<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p63-1\">→ After: Reading buddies, mailbox, Hiyori’s ask<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p63-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori wang-mei-yu ichinose-honami horikita-suzune ayanokouji-atsuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka reading buddies  mailbox  hiyori s ask cover story about china  lobby wait where she asks him to cooperate on helping ichinose  he declines the direct lever  names pingyao ancient city when hiyori mentions the great wall   surprises mii chan  parted at the elevator after the china detour  sees her walking alone to the dorms  with hiyori  refuses to name sakayanagi or hashimoto as sources  wary the rumors may be closer to truth than they appear  answers her text and agrees to the seven o clock meeting with ichinose  checks his mailbox regularly ever since his father visited the school   expects possible contact   cooperate  huh  if that s the case  then you should consult horikita   i don t have any influence over class c at all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Reading buddies, mailbox, Hiyori’s ask<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.63–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"wang-mei-yu.html\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Cooperate, huh? If that’s the case, then you should consult Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I don’t have any influence over Class C at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Cover story about China; lobby wait where she asks him to cooperate on helping Ichinose; he declines the direct lever.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Names Pingyao Ancient City when Hiyori mentions the Great Wall — surprises Mii-chan.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/b> Parted at the elevator after the China detour.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Sees her walking alone to the dorms; with Hiyori, refuses to name Sakayanagi or Hashimoto as sources; wary the rumors may be closer to truth than they appear.<span class=\"pg\">p.53, 66–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Answers her text and agrees to the seven o’clock meeting with Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> Checks his mailbox regularly ever since his father visited the school — expects possible contact.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p56-1\">← Before: The Hirata question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p69-1\">→ After: The three-way meeting and the elevator<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p69-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the three way meeting and the elevator horikita s room at seven   ichinose arrives in the neighbouring elevator  witnesses her name sakayanagi  her refusal to deny the rumors  and her  clean up my own mess  line  later pulled into the elevator for a walk  advises her to do nothing after she asks for a genuine opinion  notes horikita changing but still losing sight of herself  helping ichinose may pull sakayanagi s eye to class c  if class b falls first  that is an upside for class c   you should leave it alone  closing assessment  horikita s changes are too extreme right now  she must get along with others before she can reach her true self  waves him into the elevator    can you keep me company for a little bit    and takes him outside the lobby","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p69-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The three-way meeting and the elevator<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.69–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita’s room at seven — Ichinose arrives in the neighbouring elevator.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">Helping Ichinose may pull Sakayanagi’s eye to Class C; if Class B falls first, that is an upside for Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You should leave it alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Witnesses her name Sakayanagi, her refusal to deny the rumors, and her “clean up my own mess” line; later pulled into the elevator for a walk.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Advises her to do nothing after she asks for a genuine opinion; notes Horikita changing but still losing sight of herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Closing assessment: Horikita’s changes are too extreme right now; she must get along with others before she can reach her true self.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Waves him into the elevator — “Can you keep me company for a little bit?” — and takes him outside the lobby.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p63-1\">← Before: Reading buddies, mailbox, Hiyori’s ask<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p76-1\">→ After: The night walk and the 1 a.m. call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p76-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-atsuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the night walk and the 1 a m  call dark rest area on the way to the school buildings   ichinose walks him back after the elevator  accepts her apology without pressing  parts first so they do not arrive together   why are you apologizing  the everyday life he was looking for may look like this   passively drifting with busy surroundings  close to an answer  just past one in the morning   unknown on campus number  school phones dial only an approved list and accept only other school phones  the call therefore comes from campus   i m going to hang up if you don t say anything   ayanokouji kiyotaka    the caller s line  recorded as received   even if you re just going to say my name  reads it as that man s strategy begun   if the goal were forcing him out  surprise would suit better  the warning means threat   that man  is there anything outside of his reach    father named as the mover   in other words  you ve finally started to take action","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p76-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The night walk and the 1 a.m. call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.76–78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Dark rest area on the way to the school buildings — Ichinose walks him back after the elevator. Just past one in the morning — unknown on-campus number.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Why are you apologizing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’m going to hang up if you don’t say anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ayanokouji Kiyotaka.” — the caller’s line, recorded as received.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Accepts her apology without pressing; parts first so they do not arrive together.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The everyday life he was looking for may look like this — passively drifting with busy surroundings, close to an answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> School phones dial only an approved list and accept only other school phones; the call therefore comes from campus.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if you’re just going to say my name…”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Reads it as that man’s strategy begun — if the goal were forcing him out, surprise would suit better; the warning means threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> “That man… Is there anything outside of his reach?” — father named as the mover.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, you’ve finally started to take action…?”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p69-1\">← Before: The three-way meeting and the elevator<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p79-1\">→ After: The criminal letter in the lobby<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p79-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko ichinose-honami kamuro-masumi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the criminal letter in the lobby friday after school  dorm lobby   crowd around the mailboxes  katsuragi back in his old spot with yahiko  approach and debrief  asks what the commotion is  hears katsuragi s rough read that sakayanagi is the favourite  yahiko presses him to check his own mailbox  he agrees   what s with all the commotion   i ll go check to make sure  opens his mailbox to the same four fold letter as earlier in the year    ichinose honami is a criminal  unattributed  personal printer font  watches her read the line for dozens of seconds while about ten others stand around  notices her watching the class b reactions  follows him into the elevator","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The criminal letter in the lobby<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.79–83<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Friday after school, dorm lobby — crowd around the mailboxes, Katsuragi back in his old spot with Yahiko.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s with all the commotion?”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll go check to make sure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Approach and debrief: asks what the commotion is; hears Katsuragi’s rough read that Sakayanagi is the favourite.<span class=\"pg\">p.79–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Yahiko presses him to check his own mailbox; he agrees.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Opens his mailbox to the same four-fold letter as earlier in the year — 『Ichinose Honami is a criminal.』 unattributed, personal-printer font.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Watches her read the line for dozens of seconds while about ten others stand around.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> Notices her watching the Class B reactions; follows him into the elevator.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p76-1\">← Before: The night walk and the 1 a.m. call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p84-1\">→ After: Room 401 with Kamuro<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p84-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"kamuro-masumi sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka room 401 with kamuro room 401   kamuro gets on at the fourth floor and talks her way inside  host of the uninvited visit  grants the room and the drink while taking control of the conversation   is there something you want from me   there isn t anyone who can bother us here  talking in your room was for the best  lays out the full read  some rumors are true  so ichinose will not fight the letters or the hidden truth would surface   her strategy is to continue to ignore it so that the rumors don t end up as anything more than suspicion  reasoning  sakayanagi already knows about him  so kamuro is not here to catch him off guard for her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p84-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Room 401 with Kamuro<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.84–89<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Room 401 — Kamuro gets on at the fourth floor and talks her way inside.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is there something you want from me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There isn’t anyone who can bother us here. Talking in your room was for the best.”<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Her strategy is to continue to ignore it so that the rumors don’t end up as anything more than suspicion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> Host of the uninvited visit; grants the room and the drink while taking control of the conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.84–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Lays out the full read: some rumors are true, so Ichinose will not fight the letters or the hidden truth would surface.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Reasoning: Sakayanagi already knows about him, so Kamuro is not here to catch him off guard for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p79-1\">← Before: The criminal letter in the lobby<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p89-1\">→ After: Hearing Kamuro out; Manabu’s call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p89-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kamuro-masumi horikita-manabu kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hearing kamuro out  manabu s call listens to her whole story without admitting belief  takes the stolen beer as proof and concedes it   to be honest  there s no absolute guarantee that what you said is true   you showed me the real thing  i can t not believe you  takes the unexpected call on the way to the convenience store  learns kushida asked nagumo for help expelling suzune   tracks it against her broken non interference word  reconsiders whether ignoring ichinose is still right   or whether to take advantage of the opportunity  judges manabu s information network impressive while staying cautious of kiriyama as its source   i wonder what happened that prompted her to change strategies","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p89-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hearing Kamuro out; Manabu’s call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.89–100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“To be honest, there’s no absolute guarantee that what you said is true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You showed me the real thing. I can’t not believe you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wonder what happened that prompted her to change strategies?”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> Listens to her whole story without admitting belief; takes the stolen beer as proof and concedes it.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Takes the unexpected call on the way to the convenience store.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Learns Kushida asked Nagumo for help expelling Suzune — tracks it against her broken non-interference word.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Reconsiders whether ignoring Ichinose is still right — or whether to take advantage of the opportunity.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Judges Manabu’s information network impressive while staying cautious of Kiriyama as its source.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p84-1\">← Before: Room 401 with Kamuro<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p101-1\">→ After: Ending Manabu’s call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p101-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu hashimoto-masayoshi kushida-kikyou nagumo-miyabi sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ending manabu s call takes the rest of the call  notes nagumo told hashimoto about him at the camp   what s the possibility that nagumo got in touch with hashimoto  realises hashimoto s behaviour change traces to camp end information about him  deduces the leak from a change in hashimoto s behaviour between the start and end of the training camp  learns kushida listed his name to nagumo as a troublesome existence  judges him all bases covered and unsuitable for a wait and see approach   decides to move first  rates a follower s distrust as low risk  sakayanagi s thumbs down ends any matter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ending Manabu’s call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.101–102<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“What’s the possibility that Nagumo got in touch with Hashimoto?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Takes the rest of the call; notes Nagumo told Hashimoto about him at the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Realises Hashimoto’s behaviour change traces to camp-end information about him.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Deduces the leak from a change in Hashimoto’s behaviour between the start and end of the training camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Learns Kushida listed his name to Nagumo as a troublesome existence.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Judges him all-bases-covered and unsuitable for a wait-and-see approach — decides to move first.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Rates a follower’s distrust as low risk: Sakayanagi’s thumbs-down ends any matter.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p89-1\">← Before: Hearing Kamuro out; Manabu’s call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p103-1\">→ After: Valentine’s morning and after class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p103-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi hirata-yousuke sudou-ken ike-kanji horikita-suzune chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka valentine s morning and after class monday  february 14   phone back on after the shower  airi s text and kei s missed call  answers her morning text  then promises the ayanokoji group after six   sorry  i was in the shower so i didn t notice your messages  there isn t much time right now  can we talk at school  elevator encounter with six chocolates waiting  parts to avoid the girls   i ve never been given chocolates before    muttered aloud  then surprised at his own desire  gives the flat answer about horikita and is released from the glare   i didn t get anything from her  there s no chance she d give me anything  nods along the shinohara gossip when ike asks him directly  deflects her kushida talk with ridicule  then leaves   how s it going with kushida   glad to hear it  see you  hears the provisional test briefing before asking horikita about kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Valentine’s morning and after class<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.103–109<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Monday, February 14 — phone back on after the shower; Airi’s text and Kei’s missed call.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“[Sorry. I was in the shower so I didn’t notice your messages. There isn’t much time right now. Can we talk at school?]”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I didn’t get anything from her. There’s no chance she’d give me anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“How’s it going with Kushida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Answers her morning text, then promises the Ayanokōji Group after six.<span class=\"pg\">p.103, 109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Elevator encounter with six chocolates waiting; parts to avoid the girls.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “I’ve never been given chocolates before…” — muttered aloud, then surprised at his own desire.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Gives the flat answer about Horikita and is released from the glare.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Nods along the Shinohara gossip when Ike asks him directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Deflects her Kushida talk with ridicule, then leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Glad to hear it. See you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Hears the provisional-test briefing before asking Horikita about Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p101-1\">← Before: Ending Manabu’s call<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p109-1\">→ After: The quiet Class B and the tail turned<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p109-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the quiet class b and the tail turned class b classroom after school   ichinose absent  the three usual contacts gone  tracks her absence back to the events of days ago  suspects only she can disprove kamuro s premise  gets her room number from dormitory management on a pretext while walking  feels the tail by day and evening and decides the watch is exactly what makes showing his move worthwhile   if nagumo abandoned ichinose and sided with sakayanagi  it would be possible  notes even the closest ally did not know the secret  means to confirm things with ichinose in person today  her floor s knot of friends blocks it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p109-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The quiet Class B and the tail turned<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.109–111<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class B classroom after school — Ichinose absent, the three usual contacts gone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“If Nagumo abandoned Ichinose and sided with Sakayanagi, it would be possible.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Tracks her absence back to the events of days ago; suspects only she can disprove Kamuro’s premise.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Gets her room number from dormitory management on a pretext while walking.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Feels the tail by day and evening and decides the watch is exactly what makes showing his move worthwhile.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Notes even the closest ally did not know the secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Means to confirm things with Ichinose in person today; her floor’s knot of friends blocks it.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p103-1\">← Before: Valentine’s morning and after class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p112-1\">→ After: Five o’clock with Kei<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p112-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-atsuomi hirata-yousuke nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka five o clock with kei cold  unpopular meeting place a short walk from the dorms   chosen so the lobby cannot be used  gives her the unknown number errand and receives her valentine chocolate  the unregistered number from the night call is what he wants checked  tried calling the number back  the other side is always off   yeah  that s why i called you out here today  but  don t be careless with how you go about it   this is an easier question than i imagined  so much so that i feel like i m being tricked into giving a wrong answer  the chocolate was originally meant for yousuke  kei says  ayanokoji says it never crossed his mind   sorry  it never crossed my mind  names the march special exam as the danger beyond passing the end of term tests  only after the first year curriculum is cleared is kei safe   the battle runs to the bitter end","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Five o’clock with Kei<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.112–117<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Cold, unpopular meeting place a short walk from the dorms — chosen so the lobby cannot be used.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Yeah. That’s why I called you out here today. But, don’t be careless with how you go about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This is an easier question than I imagined. So much so that I feel like I’m being tricked into giving a wrong answer.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Sorry. It never crossed my mind.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Gives her the unknown-number errand and receives her Valentine chocolate.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> The unregistered number from the night call is what he wants checked.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Tried calling the number back; the other side is always off.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The chocolate was originally meant for Yousuke, Kei says; Ayanokōji says it never crossed his mind.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Names the March special exam as the danger beyond passing the end-of-term tests.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Only after the first-year curriculum is cleared is Kei safe — the battle runs to the bitter end.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p109-1\">← Before: The quiet Class B and the tail turned<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p128-1\">→ After: The confrontation he anticipated<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p128-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi karuizawa-kei hasebe-haruka sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the confrontation he anticipated sensing hashimoto closing in from behind while alone with kei  lets the plan run for his own benefit  gives the introduction  the library book cover  and finally contact information   the tail stays unresolved in either direction   he s class a s hashimoto  i was grouped together with him during the training camp   she just gave me this chocolate by coincidence  i didn t come out here expecting to get anything   no  i was originally intending on heading over to the library  but just before i could head out  karuizawa called me and i agreed to meet up with her  that s all  produces two library books from the bag as proof the outing was unplanned  passes her the baton deliberately   a test of how well she can keep up with him   well  it ll be better for you to just speak honestly here  karuizawa  if we continue to hide something here  i think it ll just be troublesome for you afterward  if that guy ends up thinking we re dating  you d be troubled  right   i m fine with giving it to you as long as you never use that nickname you just came up with ever again  let hashimoto s picture of him stay uncertain   if only it would stay that way   i never expected to get five of them  the square box with haruka s first name on it waits at his door with airi s  the group chat says akito and keisei got the same  the round box carries airi s name   two of the five chocolates at his desk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The confrontation he anticipated<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.128–133<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sensing Hashimoto closing in from behind while alone with Kei; lets the plan run for his own benefit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“He’s Class A’s Hashimoto. I was grouped together with him during the training camp.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“She just gave me this chocolate by coincidence. I didn’t come out here expecting to get anything.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“…No, I was originally intending on heading over to the library. But just before I could head out, Karuizawa called me and I agreed to meet up with her, that’s all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Gives the introduction, the library-book cover, and finally contact information — the tail stays unresolved in either direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Produces two library books from the bag as proof the outing was unplanned.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Passes her the baton deliberately — a test of how well she can keep up with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, it’ll be better for you to just speak honestly here, Karuizawa. If we continue to hide something here, I think it’ll just be troublesome for you afterward. If that guy ends up thinking we’re dating, you’d be troubled, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m fine with giving it to you as long as you never use that nickname you just came up with ever again.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Let Hashimoto’s picture of him stay uncertain — if only it would stay that way.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I never expected to get five of them…”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> The square box with Haruka’s first name on it waits at his door with Airi’s; the group chat says Akito and Keisei got the same.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The round box carries Airi’s name — two of the five chocolates at his desk.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p112-1\">← Before: Five o’clock with Kei<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p134-1\">→ After: The sickroom after ten<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p134-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the sickroom after ten hoodie  elevator camera avoided  unannounced at ichinose s door   text sent only to check she was awake  presses the visit through  accepts her mask  and is the first face to face visitor she has had since falling ill   ichinose  it s me  ayanokoji   something important has come up  i was hoping i could speak with you about it in person  is that alright   to be honest  it seems like things might get troublesome if i m seen by another girl right now   sorry  i definitely got a bit forceful  you don t look like you re doing very well   i apologize for coming by at such a bad time   so  have you been to the infirmary  horikita s ahead of time contact arrangement gets him the room number  ichinose s phone shows her worried exchanges with horikita  the fever is real  not a dodge of the rumors   he can tell from her voice  the cough and the mask  plenty of visits in both directions lately  and not one of them about a love affair   the record the crush rumor runs opposite to","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p134-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The sickroom after ten<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.134–137<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hoodie, elevator camera avoided, unannounced at Ichinose’s door — text sent only to check she was awake.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Ichinose, it’s me. Ayanokōji.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Something important has come up. I was hoping I could speak with you about it in person, is that alright?”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“To be honest, it seems like things might get troublesome if I’m seen by another girl right now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Presses the visit through, accepts her mask, and is the first face-to-face visitor she has had since falling ill.<span class=\"pg\">p.134–137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. I definitely got a bit forceful. You don’t look like you’re doing very well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I apologize for coming by at such a bad time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, have you been to the infirmary?”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita’s ahead-of-time contact arrangement gets him the room number; Ichinose’s phone shows her worried exchanges with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.134, 137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The fever is real, not a dodge of the rumors — he can tell from her voice, the cough and the mask.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Plenty of visits in both directions lately, and not one of them about a love affair — the record the crush rumor runs opposite to.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p128-1\">← Before: The confrontation he anticipated<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p137-1\">→ After: The four rumors and the provisional exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p137-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hondou-ryoutaro sudou-ken karuizawa-kei kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the four rumors and the provisional exam exam morning  the classroom loud with talk that has nothing to do with studying  reads horikita s memo of the four forum rumors with her  denies the crush line  summarizes the hashimoto encounter  and agrees to the after school meeting with kanzaki   where did this gossip come from   the ones in the school s app  right   no it is not   there are only a few people who know about my relationship with karuizawa as it is now anyway  nods in response to hondo s plea for backup instead of speaking up himself   no  i don t  confirms the denial for sudo  who has overheard the exchange with horikita anyway  concedes her exposure is the real problem while declaring the rumor about himself no big deal   it s not that big of a deal to me  on the other hand  karuizawa is most likely going to be facing some problems  meets him after school at keyaki mall s southern entrance  with horikita   the spot furthest from the school  worried about ichinose as a friend  and letting the class a shadow draw closer is exactly the development he wants","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The four rumors and the provisional exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.137–146<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Exam morning, the classroom loud with talk that has nothing to do with studying.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hondou-ryoutaro.html\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Where did this gossip come from?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“The ones in the school’s app, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No it is not.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reads Horikita’s memo of the four forum rumors with her, denies the crush line, summarizes the Hashimoto encounter, and agrees to the after-school meeting with Kanzaki.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are only a few people who know about my relationship with Karuizawa as it is now anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hondō Ryōtaro<\/b> Nods in response to Hondō’s plea for backup instead of speaking up himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I don’t.”<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Confirms the denial for Sudō, who has overheard the exchange with Horikita anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Concedes her exposure is the real problem while declaring the rumor about himself no big deal.<span class=\"pg\">p.143–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s not that big of a deal to me. On the other hand, Karuizawa is most likely going to be facing some problems.”<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Meets him after school at Keyaki Mall’s southern entrance, with Horikita — the spot furthest from the school.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Worried about Ichinose as a friend, and letting the Class A shadow draw closer is exactly the development he wants.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p134-1\">← Before: The sickroom after ten<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p149-1\">→ After: The call: rumor as insurance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p149-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the call  rumor as insurance back in his room after school  kei calls about the crush rumor naming them both   maybe hashimoto spread it after what happened yesterday  or maybe some other student saw us together   well  it s fine  isn t it  it would be terrible for you if our positions were reversed   a rumor like  kei has a crush on me  would be pretty troublesome  right  if it ended up like that  i think everyone would be much more suspicious of you than me since you just broke up with hirata  the rumor is the information he is indirectly planting for the tail   contact with kei now has cover  the rumor acts as insurance  talking to her from here on reads as the rumor playing out   that being said  thanks to this rumor  it should be easier for the two of us to get in contact with each other moving forward  if i start talking to you now  people will assume that it s because of the rumor  and we could leave it at that   anyway  don t worry about it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The call: rumor as insurance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.149–150<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back in his room after school, Kei calls about the crush rumor naming them both.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Maybe Hashimoto spread it after what happened yesterday. Or maybe some other student saw us together.”<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, it’s fine, isn’t it? It would be terrible for you if our positions were reversed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“A rumor like ‘Kei has a crush on me’ would be pretty troublesome, right? If it ended up like that, I think everyone would be much more suspicious of you than me since you just broke up with Hirata.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> The rumor is the information he is indirectly planting for the tail — contact with Kei now has cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> The rumor acts as insurance: talking to her from here on reads as the rumor playing out.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That being said, thanks to this rumor, it should be easier for the two of us to get in contact with each other moving forward. If I start talking to you now, people will assume that it’s because of the rumor, and we could leave it at that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, don’t worry about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p137-1\">← Before: The four rumors and the provisional exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p151-1\">→ After: Off-campus standoff: watching, testing, pocketing the ID card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p151-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka off campus standoff  watching  testing  pocketing the id card friday  february 18  three days after the provisional exam  classes a  c and d gather on the road off campus over the forum rumors  the ayanokoji group a step behind  he spots class a and class d leaving campus  warns miyake that something like the kanzaki hashimoto clash may be starting  and follows with the rest of the group   i was eighty to ninety percent certain that she really was behind it all  picks up the student id card ibuki dropped  notices one particular detail on its photo  and puts the card in his pocket   no  it s nothing  more importantly  it seems like stopping this fight should be our top priority   that s true  then i guess it s better to just let akito handle it   i hate to say it  but i suspect you as well  hashimoto   there s nothing going on between us  the crush rumor and hashimoto s secret meeting sighting both concern him and karuizawa  he denies anything is going on between them   his actions were an act  done for the sake of testing me   even though he had been keeping an eye on me  thanks to this testimony  he would now end up with an incorrect conclusion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Off-campus standoff: watching, testing, pocketing the ID card<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.151–164<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Friday, February 18, three days after the provisional exam; Classes A, C and D gather on the road off campus over the forum rumors, the Ayanokōji Group a step behind.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, it’s nothing. More importantly, it seems like stopping this fight should be our top priority.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s true. Then I guess it’s better to just let Akito handle it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I hate to say it, but I suspect you as well, Hashimoto.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He spots Class A and Class D leaving campus, warns Miyake that something like the Kanzaki–Hashimoto clash may be starting, and follows with the rest of the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “I was eighty to ninety percent certain that she really was behind it all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Picks up the student ID card Ibuki dropped, notices one particular detail on its photo, and puts the card in his pocket.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There’s nothing going on between us.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> The crush rumor and Hashimoto’s secret-meeting sighting both concern him and Karuizawa; he denies anything is going on between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “His actions were an act, done for the sake of testing me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Even though he had been keeping an eye on me, thanks to this testimony, he would now end up with an incorrect conclusion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p149-1\">← Before: The call: rumor as insurance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p164-1\">→ After: The night call to Horikita Manabu<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p164-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the night call to horikita manabu that night he phones the former student council president to report what he noticed on two students  id cards   there s one thing i wanted to ask you   it s rather unusual for you to contact me  he hopes never to have to use the knowledge  if the future where it becomes useful comes at all  if nagumo lends his influence over the second years to the third year class b  the elder horikita may not be in a safe position  he notes nagumo goes for weak points that are easy to exploit  the way he targeted tachibana akane during the training camp   if the student council were to provide nagumo backup  they d be able to cover up his actions to some degree  right   if you re asking about that  it s been taken care of","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p164-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The night call to Horikita Manabu<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.164–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">That night he phones the former student council president to report what he noticed on two students’ ID cards.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s one thing I wanted to ask you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> “It’s rather unusual for you to contact me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“If the student council were to provide Nagumo backup, they’d be able to cover up his actions to some degree, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He hopes never to have to use the knowledge, if the future where it becomes useful comes at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> If Nagumo lends his influence over the second-years to the third-year Class B, the elder Horikita may not be in a safe position.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> He notes Nagumo goes for weak points that are easy to exploit, the way he targeted Tachibana Akane during the training camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re asking about that, it’s been taken care of.”<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p151-1\">← Before: Off-campus standoff: watching, testing, pocketing the ID card<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p166-1\">→ After: Mock exam results, then the rush to Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p166-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka mock exam results  then the rush to class b february 24  the day before the end of year exam  ichinose is back after more than a week away  and the ayanokoji group gathers for the mock exam keisei wrote  scores 90 on keisei s mock exam  the other three land around 80   well  the tests keisei made were flawless  didn t you manage to score about the same  with ichinose back  sakayanagi would have to make her move today  a direct attack to bring her down before tomorrow s exam   i ll come along just in case  though  i don t think that i ll be much help","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p166-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mock exam results, then the rush to Class B<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.166–168<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">February 24, the day before the end-of-year exam; Ichinose is back after more than a week away, and the Ayanokōji Group gathers for the mock exam Keisei wrote.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, the tests Keisei made were flawless. Didn’t you manage to score about the same?”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I’ll come along just in case. Though, I don’t think that I’ll be much help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Scores 90 on Keisei’s mock exam; the other three land around 80.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> With Ichinose back, Sakayanagi would have to make her move today, a direct attack to bring her down before tomorrow’s exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p164-1\">← Before: The night call to Horikita Manabu<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p168-1\">→ After: In Class B for the confession<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p168-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka in class b for the confession enters class b with miyake and keisei as shibata confronts sakayanagi  sakayanagi brought only kamuro and hashimoto  there is no sign of kito or anyone else from class a  sakayanagi shows a satisfied smile as ichinose says she is a criminal  watches from outside the circle with keisei and akito  both struck by a student like ichinose admitting to a crime","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">In Class B for the confession<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.168–174<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Enters Class B with Miyake and Keisei as Shibata confronts Sakayanagi. Watches from outside the circle with Keisei and Akito, both struck by a student like Ichinose admitting to a crime.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">Sakayanagi shows a satisfied smile as Ichinose says she is a criminal.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakayanagi brought only Kamuro and Hashimoto; there is no sign of Kitō or anyone else from Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p166-1\">← Before: Mock exam results, then the rush to Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p176-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Ichinose’s confession and the Kushida negotiation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p176-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami shibata-sou nagumo-miyabi chabashira-sae horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  ichinose s confession and the kushida negotiation class b classroom  ichinose confesses to the class how she stole a hair clip for her sister  hashimoto asks if she was caught   are you saying you got caught   i just left the department store with the hair clip  it was the first time i ever shoplifted  the first time i ever committed a crime   in the end  the store didn t hand me over to the police  but  in the blink of an eye  the commotion still spread  so i closed myself off  sakayanagi brushes aside the sympathy  shoplifting is a crime born of self interest  she demands ichinose return the pooled points and step down   really  what a trivial  boorish farce  are you trying to gain sympathy by bringing up all these needless details about your past   take this opportunity to return the private points to your classmates and step down as the leader of class b   however  i ve never been persecuted for it  in other words  there s effectively no reason for me to atone for my sin now   i refuse to keep looking back  i won t let my past control me anymore  ichinose asks the class to follow her to the end  class b cheers in unity  sakayanagi laughs that the rumors will not disappear   despite being so shameless  everyone  will you follow me until the very end   you already have our support  right   i see  it seems you ve managed to successfully trick your classmates  nagumo  hoshinomiya and chabashira enter  chabashira announces the school will punish anyone spreading meaningless rumors   you re correct  this dispute does only involve the first years  however  as of today  it is against the rules to spread irresponsible rumors   moving forward  anyone found spreading meaningless rumors may be subjected to punishment   in other words  the school s finally taking action  horikita observes that the school s move saves every class  sakayanagi s simultaneous framing backfired  ayanokoji s phone rings with an unregistered number  sakayanagi went a bit too far   she attempted to frame each class with the same strategy at the same time  but it backfired because it attracted the school s attention   let s withdraw here  now that the school has made their move  our presence is no longer necessary  ayanokoji answers the call  it is sakayanagi  asking him to meet at the first floor entryway  sakayanagi confronts ayanokoji alone at the entryway  she accuses him of protecting ichinose behind the scenes and asks why   it seems as though  without me noticing  you ve gone and made your move behind the scenes   why did you decide to protect ichinose san   wait  i don t understand what you re talking about  ayanokoji reveals his deduction  kamuro stole the beer can months ago  sakayanagi admits she wanted him involved and orchestrated ichinose s downfall to lure him out   she presented me with a can of alcohol as proof of her shoplifting  but  she hadn t stolen it that day  kamuro had stolen it when she first enrolled here   it didn t matter to me if ichinose san broke down along the way  but if there was even a slight chance that you may decide to intervene  i was hoping that you would seize the opportunity to do so  sakayanagi proposes a competition over exam rankings  ayanokoji accepts  she will drop out and her father the chairman will be guarantor if she loses  and his identity as class c s mastermind will be exposed if he loses   let s have a competition  ayanokoji kun   while you may claim that it wouldn t cause much damage  i d expose you as the mastermind leading class c from the shadows   if you re really alright with those conditions  i ll agree to it  flashback to february 11 midnight  ayanokoji calls kushida to his room  she brings valentine chocolate  kushida enters  ayanokoji asks for personal information about first years to stop the ichinose rumors  kushida resists betraying friends   i m on good terms with ichinose san as well  if there s anything i can do for her  i d want to do that   i can t just betray my friends  ayanokoji explains the plan  escalate rumors so the school cannot sit back  class a would be first suspect  ayanokoji reveals he knows kushida is recording  phone and backup recorder  she stops the recording   even if i don t say anything  you should probably understand  a cell phone  voice recorder  maybe even both   so you already knew  that i ve been recording  kushida asks for horikita s withdrawal as her condition  ayanokoji refuses  he offers half of all future private points  kushida considers   horikita suzune s withdrawal from school   unacceptable  kushida accepts the deal  she takes out a backup voice recorder  ayanokoji s true defense is making himself useful to her   alright  i m on board   i have all the evidence i need right here  if you betray me at all  you know what will happen  yes  kushida begins sharing secrets  crushes  hatreds  family circumstances  past delinquency  ayanokoji s true aim is to gauge her information network in order to remove her from the school  saving ichinose  responding to sakayanagi s provocation  diverting hashimoto s attention  the looming threat of nagumo   all of these were only one piece of the puzzle  the one thing he truly wanted was to ascertain the quantity and quality of information held by kushida kikyo  all for the sake of removing her from the school  kushida shares more  she has a terrifying understanding of the character and personalities of the students around her  kushida explains the surface group chat versus the hidden group chat that badmouths excluded members  dozens of such two faced groups exist  she leaves   for example  there s this group chat  we ll call it group a  there s a second group chat  made by the same girls  let s call that one group b   it s late  i m going home  i m looking forward to the outcome of our agreement  ayanokoji kun  sakayanagi challenges him to a ranking competition with mutual stakes  he accepts  negotiates for her secrets  offers half his future private points  she accepts and provides both recordings as insurance  defends her behind the scenes  her confession and the school s intervention resolve the rumor crisis  horikita observes the school s move and agrees they should withdraw","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p176-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Ichinose’s confession and the Kushida negotiation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.176–200<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class B classroom: Ichinose confesses to the class how she stole a hair clip for her sister; Hashimoto asks if she was caught. Sakayanagi brushes aside the sympathy: shoplifting is a crime born of self-interest; she demands Ichinose return the pooled points and step down. Ichinose asks the class to follow her to the end; Class B cheers in unity; Sakayanagi laughs that the rumors will not disappear. Nagumo, Hoshinomiya and Chabashira enter; Chabashira announces the school will punish anyone spreading meaningless rumors. Horikita observes that the school’s move saves every class; Sakayanagi’s simultaneous framing backfired; Ayanokōji’s phone rings with an unregistered number. Ayanokōji answers the call: it is Sakayanagi, asking him to meet at the first-floor entryway. Sakayanagi confronts Ayanokōji alone at the entryway; she accuses him of protecting Ichinose behind the scenes and asks why. Ayanokōji reveals his deduction: Kamuro stole the beer can months ago; Sakayanagi admits she wanted him involved and orchestrated Ichinose’s downfall to lure him out. Sakayanagi proposes a competition over exam rankings; Ayanokōji accepts; she will drop out and her father the chairman will be guarantor if she loses, and his identity as Class C’s mastermind will be exposed if he loses. Flashback to February 11 midnight: Ayanokōji calls Kushida to his room; she brings Valentine chocolate. Kushida enters; Ayanokōji asks for personal information about first-years to stop the Ichinose rumors; Kushida resists betraying friends. Ayanokōji explains the plan: escalate rumors so the school cannot sit back; Class A would be first suspect. Ayanokōji reveals he knows Kushida is recording (phone and backup recorder); she stops the recording. Kushida asks for Horikita’s withdrawal as her condition; Ayanokōji refuses; he offers half of all future private points; Kushida considers. Kushida accepts the deal; she takes out a backup voice recorder; Ayanokōji’s true defense is making himself useful to her. Kushida begins sharing secrets: crushes, hatreds, family circumstances, past delinquency; Ayanokōji’s true aim is to gauge her information network in order to remove her from the school. Kushida shares more: she has a terrifying understanding of the character and personalities of the students around her. Kushida explains the surface group chat versus the hidden group chat that badmouths excluded members; dozens of such two-faced groups exist; she leaves.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"shibata-sou.html\">Shibata Sō<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> “Are you saying you got caught?”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I just left the department store with the hair clip. It was the first time I ever shoplifted, the first time I ever committed a crime.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“In the end, the store didn’t hand me over to the police. But, in the blink of an eye, the commotion still spread, so I closed myself off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>35 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really, what a trivial, boorish farce. Are you trying to gain sympathy by bringing up all these needless details about your past?”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Take this opportunity to return the private points to your classmates and step down as the leader of Class B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “However, I’ve never been persecuted for it. In other words, there’s effectively no reason for me to atone for my sin now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I refuse to keep looking back. I won’t let my past control me anymore.”<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Despite being so shameless… everyone, will you follow me until the very end?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You already have our support, right!?”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. It seems you’ve managed to successfully trick your classmates.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re correct. This dispute does only involve the first-years. However, as of today, it is against the rules to spread irresponsible rumors.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Moving forward, anyone found spreading meaningless rumors may be subjected to punishment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In other words, the school’s finally taking action.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Sakayanagi went a bit too far — she attempted to frame each class with the same strategy at the same time, but it backfired because it attracted the school’s attention.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s withdraw here. Now that the school has made their move, our presence is no longer necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It seems as though, without me noticing, you’ve gone and made your move behind the scenes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why did you decide to protect Ichinose-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Wait. I don’t understand what you’re talking about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “She presented me with a can of alcohol as proof of her shoplifting. But, she hadn’t stolen it that day. Kamuro had stolen it when she first enrolled here.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It didn’t matter to me if Ichinose-san broke down along the way, but if there was even a slight chance that you may decide to intervene, I was hoping that you would seize the opportunity to do so.”<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Let’s have a competition, Ayanokōji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “While you may claim that it wouldn’t cause much damage, I’d expose you as the mastermind leading Class C from the shadows.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you’re really alright with those conditions, I’ll agree to it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m on good terms with Ichinose-san as well. If there’s anything I can do for her, I’d want to do that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t just betray my friends.”<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I don’t say anything, you should probably understand. A cell phone… Voice recorder… Maybe even both?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you already knew? That I’ve been recording?”<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Horikita Suzune’s withdrawal from school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unacceptable.”<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Alright, I’m on board.”<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have all the evidence I need right here. If you betray me at all… you know what will happen, yes?”<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Saving Ichinose, responding to Sakayanagi’s provocation, diverting Hashimoto’s attention, the looming threat of Nagumo — all of these were only one piece of the puzzle; the one thing he truly wanted was to ascertain the quantity and quality of information held by Kushida Kikyō, all for the sake of removing her from the school.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For example, there’s this group chat, we’ll call it group A… there’s a second group chat, made by the same girls. Let’s call that one group B.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s late, I’m going home. I’m looking forward to the outcome of our agreement, Ayanokōji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Sakayanagi challenges him to a ranking competition with mutual stakes; he accepts.<span class=\"pg\">p.183–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Negotiates for her secrets: offers half his future private points; she accepts and provides both recordings as insurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.186–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Defends her behind the scenes; her confession and the school’s intervention resolve the rumor crisis.<span class=\"pg\">p.176–180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita observes the school’s move and agrees they should withdraw.<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p168-1\">← Before: In Class B for the confession<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p201-1\">→ After: Epilogue: The rumors, the door, and Valentine’s Day<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p201-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kiriyama-ikuto ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  the rumors  the door  and valentine s day after kushida leaves  ayanokoji prepares the rumors he will spread for each class  using her intelligence as the source  the fact that nagumo and kushida had come into contact was learned coincidentally  there was no reason not to make use of it  february 14  valentine s day  ayanokoji turns off his phone the night before to arrange a secret meeting with kei and an exchange of chocolate  giving hashimoto a hint that something is happening  hashimoto confronts ayanokoji and kei in person  hashimoto s stalking sessions stop the next day  ayanokoji meets hiyori shiina at the library as a preface for the rumors  hiyori and ayanokoji s conversation at the library consists of idle chatter about books  it serves as a preface for the rumors that will spread the following day  after most students leave  ayanokoji meets kiriyama  second year vice president  at the school building and reveals his plan to save ichinose  kiriyama resists posting rumors on the forums  ayanokoji argues it would create a new relationship and that ichinose is a valuable asset for the student council   i see  so you re telling me to post the rumors with my own phone  there d be no benefit in that for me at all   that s not true  there are benefits in this for you  ayanokoji reveals kushida has already established contact with nagumo  kiriyama  lost in thought  agrees to cooperate   why do you  horikita senpai s really placed a lot of trust in someone like you  hasn t he  kiriyama posts the rumors  ayanokoji notes the groundwork is complete  only ichinose s spirit remains to be crushed  ichinose is still absent on february 18  ayanokoji visits ichinose s room during lunch break  she asks him to come back later  he sits with his back to the door and waits   i m sorry ayanokoji kun  you went to the trouble of coming to see me  but would you please come back again sometime later  ayanokoji returns on monday the 21st  ichinose does not respond  he sits with his back to the door until lunch break ends  tuesday  ayanokoji returns again  ichinose is still absent  he sits with his back to the door  wednesday  ayanokoji visits with coffee  ichinose speaks for the first time in days  she asks why he never asks her anything while others try to convince her   why haven t you been saying anything to me  or asking me anything   compared to someone like me  students who are far more worried about you have already tried to convince you many times now  ayanokoji reveals he knows about her crime  he tells her she saves others but cannot save herself  he becomes her  door   i already know about the crime you ve committed   i am your door now  you can t see my face  and you can t touch me  i m just a door  ichinose asks if it is okay to be pathetic  ayanokoji tells her everyone has the right to be forgiven  she begins confessing through the door   even though i m so pathetic  is it really okay   who has the right to deny you of it   i  was a shoplifter  ichinose confesses everything  the shoplifting  the half year shut in  nagumo s knowledge  sakayanagi s approach  her inability to show weakness  ayanokoji listens without consoling or reprimanding  ichinose sobs  he says nothing  because her opponent is herself  end of year exam day  ichinose greets ayanokoji with a beaming smile  she thanks him for helping her get back on her feet   good morning  ayanokoji kun   and it s all thanks to you  ayanokoji kun  for helping me get back on my feet   i was just the trigger  in the end  you re the only one who can overcome your own past  ichinose says she will face her sins head on  ayanokoji offers to listen if she loses sight of herself again   but  i ll live my life  properly facing it head on from this day forward  ichinose catches up to nagumo and thanks him for recruiting her to the student council  nagumo looks at ayanokoji with displeasure   good morning  nagumo senpai   don t you resent me  honami   no such thing  i m grateful to you  president nagumo  ichinose gives ayanokoji valentine s chocolate  he accepts   this may be a bit late now but here  valentines chocolate  w would you accept it  short story  the first gift  ichinose buys valentine chocolate at keyaki mall for ayanokoji  it is her first gift since birth  short story  a special day for students  karuizawa gives ayanokoji valentine chocolate  lying that she bought it for hirata   what day is it today  alright  5  4  3   i actually prepared this for yousuke kun but that s no longer necessary  uses her intelligence as the source for the rumors  arranges a secret meeting and chocolate exchange to give hashimoto a hint  karuizawa later gives him valentine chocolate  meets her at the library as a preface for the rumors  recruits him to post the rumors on the school forums  visits her room repeatedly until she confesses  she gives him valentine chocolate  nagumo looks at him with displeasure  knowing he interfered","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p201-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: The rumors, the door, and Valentine’s Day<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.201–225<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After Kushida leaves, Ayanokōji prepares the rumors he will spread for each class, using her intelligence as the source. February 14, Valentine’s Day: Ayanokōji turns off his phone the night before to arrange a secret meeting with Kei and an exchange of chocolate, giving Hashimoto a hint that something is happening. Hashimoto confronts Ayanokōji and Kei in person; Hashimoto’s stalking sessions stop the next day; Ayanokōji meets Hiyori Shiina at the library as a preface for the rumors. After most students leave, Ayanokōji meets Kiriyama (second-year vice president) at the school building and reveals his plan to save Ichinose. Kiriyama resists posting rumors on the forums; Ayanokōji argues it would create a new relationship and that Ichinose is a valuable asset for the student council. Ayanokōji reveals Kushida has already established contact with Nagumo; Kiriyama, lost in thought, agrees to cooperate. Kiriyama posts the rumors; Ayanokōji notes the groundwork is complete; only Ichinose’s spirit remains to be crushed; Ichinose is still absent on February 18. Ayanokōji visits Ichinose’s room during lunch break; she asks him to come back later; he sits with his back to the door and waits. Ayanokōji returns on Monday the 21st; Ichinose does not respond; he sits with his back to the door until lunch break ends. Tuesday: Ayanokōji returns again; Ichinose is still absent; he sits with his back to the door. Wednesday: Ayanokōji visits with coffee; Ichinose speaks for the first time in days; she asks why he never asks her anything while others try to convince her. Ayanokōji reveals he knows about her crime; he tells her she saves others but cannot save herself; he becomes her “door.” Ichinose asks if it is okay to be pathetic; Ayanokōji tells her everyone has the right to be forgiven; she begins confessing through the door. Ichinose confesses everything: the shoplifting, the half-year shut-in, Nagumo’s knowledge, Sakayanagi’s approach, her inability to show weakness. Ayanokōji listens without consoling or reprimanding; Ichinose sobs; he says nothing, because her opponent is herself. End-of-year exam day: Ichinose greets Ayanokōji with a beaming smile; she thanks him for helping her get back on her feet. Ichinose says she will face her sins head on; Ayanokōji offers to listen if she loses sight of herself again. Ichinose catches up to Nagumo and thanks him for recruiting her to the student council; Nagumo looks at Ayanokōji with displeasure. Ichinose gives Ayanokōji Valentine’s chocolate; he accepts. Short story “The First Gift”: Ichinose buys Valentine chocolate at Keyaki Mall for Ayanokōji; it is her first gift since birth. Short story “A Special Day for Students”: Karuizawa gives Ayanokōji Valentine chocolate, lying that she bought it for Hirata.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama-ikuto.html\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “I see. So you’re telling me to post the rumors with my own phone? There’d be no benefit in that for me at all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“That’s not true. There are benefits in this for you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> “Why do you…… Horikita-senpai’s really placed a lot of trust in someone like you, hasn’t he?”<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The fact that Nagumo and Kushida had come into contact was learned coincidentally; there was no reason not to make use of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hiyori and Ayanokōji’s conversation at the library consists of idle chatter about books; it serves as a preface for the rumors that will spread the following day.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry Ayanokōji-kun. You went to the trouble of coming to see me, but would you please come back again sometime later?”<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why haven’t you been saying anything to me, or asking me anything?”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Compared to someone like me, students who are far more worried about you have already tried to convince you many times now.”<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I already know about the crime you’ve committed.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I am your door now. You can’t see my face, and you can’t touch me. I’m just a door.”<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even though I’m so pathetic… Is it really okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Who has the right to deny you of it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I… was a shoplifter.”<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good morning, Ayanokōji-kun!”<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “And it’s all thanks to you, Ayanokōji-kun. For helping me get back on my feet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was just the trigger. In the end, you’re the only one who can overcome your own past.”<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But, I’ll live my life, properly facing it head on from this day forward.”<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Good morning, Nagumo-senpai.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you resent me, Honami?”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No such thing, I’m grateful to you, President Nagumo.”<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This may be a bit late now but here, Valentines chocolate… W-would you accept it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What day is it today? Alright, 5, 4, 3---”<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I actually prepared this for Yousuke-kun but that’s no longer necessary.”<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Uses her intelligence as the source for the rumors.<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Arranges a secret meeting and chocolate exchange to give Hashimoto a hint; Karuizawa later gives him Valentine chocolate.<span class=\"pg\">p.201, 224–225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Meets her at the library as a preface for the rumors.<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama Ikuto<\/b> Recruits him to post the rumors on the school forums.<span class=\"pg\">p.202–204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Visits her room repeatedly until she confesses; she gives him Valentine chocolate.<span class=\"pg\">p.206–219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo looks at him with displeasure, knowing he interfered.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p176-1\">← Before: Epilogue: Ichinose’s confession and the Kushida negotiation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p226-1\">→ After: Short story: Kamuro’s Intention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p226-1","v":"y1v9","y":1,"o":11,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kamuro-masumi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka short story  kamuro s intention kamuro visits ayanokoji s room  she asks for a drink and tests his defensiveness   give me something to drink  it s going to take a while  kamuro asks about yamauchi and the letter calling ichinose a criminal  ayanokoji says he is not interested   that letter about ichinose earlier  what do you think   i haven t a clue  besides  i m not interested  kamuro tries to unsettle him  she was sent by sakayanagi to assess whether he can be used  sakayanagi told her to keep an eye on ayanokoji  she has no idea what he is capable of  kamuro visits his room to test and assess him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p226-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short story: Kamuro’s Intention<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V9 · p.226–228<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kamuro visits Ayanokōji’s room; she asks for a drink and tests his defensiveness. Kamuro asks about Yamauchi and the letter calling Ichinose a criminal; Ayanokōji says he is not interested. Kamuro tries to unsettle him; she was sent by Sakayanagi to assess whether he can be used.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kamuro-masumi.html\">Kamuro Masumi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> “Give me something to drink. It’s going to take a while.”<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> “That letter about Ichinose earlier. What do you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“I haven’t a clue. Besides, I’m not interested.”<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Sakayanagi told her to keep an eye on Ayanokōji; she has no idea what he is capable of.<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamuro Masumi<\/b> Kamuro visits his room to test and assess him.<span class=\"pg\">p.226–228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v9-p201-1\">← Before: Epilogue: The rumors, the door, and Valentine’s Day<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p6-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka prologue  hirata s monologue mentioned by hirata as someone he may be similar to   a shadow  not the center of class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p6-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Prologue: Hirata’s monologue<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.6–10<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mentioned by Hirata as someone he may be similar to — a shadow, not the center of class.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p12-1\">→ After: Ch.1: Exam results and the hallway encounter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p12-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1  exam results and the hallway encounter encounters nagumo and manabu in the hallway  nagumo tests him about forum rumors   well  i have no idea  but at the end of the day  they ve caused me nothing but trouble  horikita watches from a distance  nagumo reveals he called her here  horikita asks what was discussed  he tells her to face her brother before he graduates   don t you want to try and face him at least once before he graduates  nagumo tests him about forum rumors  he deflects  manabu backs him up against nagumo  tells her to face her brother  she refuses  uses the time between classes for a bathroom break and encounters nagumo and horikita manabu in the hallway on the way back   somehow   is that so  straightens up in response to nagumo s remark about attitude toward the student council president   i m not particularly interested  ultimately  i don t have the time to be worrying about my upperclassmen  looks over his shoulder and sees horikita suzune watching from a distance   are you the one who called her here  nagumo   you don t understand anything  there s no way that my brother would look after me  going out of my way to approach him when i know i would be treated cruelly is just plain stupid   really  well  maybe you re right  it was a difficult conversation for her  she becomes docile and meek like a lamb in front of her brother  it would be meaningless if she didn t have the courage to face him herself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Exam results and the hallway encounter<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.12–29<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Encounters Nagumo and Manabu in the hallway; Nagumo tests him about forum rumors. Horikita watches from a distance; Nagumo reveals he called her here. Horikita asks what was discussed; he tells her to face her brother before he graduates. Looks over his shoulder and sees Horikita Suzune watching from a distance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Well, I have no idea. But at the end of the day, they’ve caused me nothing but trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Don’t you want to try and face him at least once before he graduates?”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Somehow.”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Nagumo tests him about forum rumors; he deflects.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Manabu backs him up against Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Tells her to face her brother; she refuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Uses the time between classes for a bathroom break and encounters Nagumo and Horikita Manabu in the hallway on the way back.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Is that so?”<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Straightens up in response to Nagumo’s remark about attitude toward the student council president.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m not particularly interested. Ultimately, I don’t have the time to be worrying about my upperclassmen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you the one who called her here, Nagumo?”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You don’t understand anything. There’s no way that my brother would look after me. Going out of my way to approach him when I know I would be treated cruelly is just plain stupid.”<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Really? Well, maybe you’re right.”<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> It was a difficult conversation for her; she becomes docile and meek like a lamb in front of her brother.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> It would be meaningless if she didn’t have the courage to face him herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p6-1\">← Before: Prologue: Hirata’s monologue<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p30-1\">→ After: Ch.2: The Class Vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p30-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei yukimura-teruhiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  the class vote chabashira announces the supplementary exam  the class is tense  koenji provokes sudo  hirata mediates  horikita and ayanokoji discuss the cruelty of the exam  ayanokoji group at cafe  keisei proposes mutual praise votes  keisei identifies koenji  ike  yamauchi  sudo as likely censure targets  horikita visits ryuen  he claims he could survive if he wanted  ryuen sees through horikita s weakness  ryuen reveals he accepted defeat by ishizaki  horikita says ryuen is doomed  ayanokoji agrees  kei calls ayanokoji  she has a group of seven girls  kei and ayanokoji discuss likely censure targets  ayanokoji intends to accept whatever outcome the class reaches  the exam is cruel  the class had always cooperated until now  he intends to accept whatever outcome the class reaches  discusses exam cruelty  leaves with her  horikita visits ryuen  he sees through her  phone call  she has seven girl group  keisei proposes mutual praise votes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p30-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: The Class Vote<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.30–84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira announces the supplementary exam; the class is tense. Kōenji provokes Sudō; Hirata mediates. Horikita and Ayanokōji discuss the cruelty of the exam. Ayanokōji Group at cafe: Keisei proposes mutual praise votes. Keisei identifies Kōenji, Ike, Yamauchi, Sudō as likely censure targets. Horikita visits Ryūen; he claims he could survive if he wanted. Ryūen sees through Horikita’s weakness. Ryūen reveals he accepted defeat by Ishizaki. Horikita says Ryūen is doomed; Ayanokōji agrees. Kei calls Ayanokōji; she has a group of seven girls. Kei and Ayanokōji discuss likely censure targets. Ayanokōji intends to accept whatever outcome the class reaches.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">The exam is cruel; the class had always cooperated until now.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">He intends to accept whatever outcome the class reaches.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses exam cruelty; leaves with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.50, 73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Horikita visits Ryūen; he sees through her.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Phone call; she has seven-girl group.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Keisei proposes mutual praise votes.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Exam results and the hallway encounter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p85-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Morning conversations and after-school meetings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p85-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami asahina-nazuna sakayanagi-arisu hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  morning conversations and after school meetings checks the ayanokoji group chat  keisei proposes arriving early to collect information  the group agrees and haruka volunteers for the next day  ichinose joins ayanokoji on the walk to school  she admits the exam is tough for class b and considers bearing the risk herself   in the face of such a terrible exam  i really have no choice but to do something  don t i  ichinose offers to use her cross class praise vote on ayanokoji  he declines   since i have a praise vote i can use on someone in another class  i could use it on you  asahina nazuna borrows ayanokoji and reveals ichinose asked nagumo for points  nagumo s condition is a relationship   the condition he set for lending the points to her  is for the two of them to get into a relationship  classroom atmosphere is tense  haruka messages that nothing unusual has happened  overhears sakayanagi and kamuro discuss sakayanagi s father s suspension and the supplementary exam  sakayanagi tells kamuro she knows ayanokoji from long ago   i simply know him from a long time ago  is this answer not acceptable enough  sakayanagi asks to postpone their match for this exam and promises not to cast censure votes for ayanokoji   for this exam  i won t do anything that would put you at a disadvantage  that is to say  i absolutely won t cast you any censure votes  sakayanagi says she has already decided class a will expel katsuragi kohei   katsuragi kohei kun  meets hirata and goes to his room  hirata cannot find a way to avoid an expulsion   if  if there s a way to save the class  please tell me   ayanokoji kun  do you think it s fine for someone to be expelled  morning walk  she considers bearing the risk and offers her praise vote  reveals ichinose asked nagumo for points and his condition  postpones their match  promises no censure votes  reveals katsuragi as class a target  hirata seeks a way to avoid expulsion   if you have business with me  i ll hear you out   he consented immediately   i ll ask just to make sure  but there s no way she d be lent enough private points with no strings attached  is there   are the conditions he s set too harsh  like an obscenely high interest rate   is it alright  for you to be telling me this   you re overestimating me  there s no way i can afford to make up for class b s lack of points   i can t do anything about it  follows horikita after class but stops when she tells him to leave her alone   it wouldn t be troublesome for us to take in another person   could i bother you for a moment  ayanokoji kun   sure  meets sakayanagi and kamuro and agrees to speak with sakayanagi at the special building   i have plans to meet up with a friend at keyaki mall in around half an hour   was that okay   not particularly   going so far as to have kamuro head back without you  what are you looking to talk to me about   make whatever decision you want   if my classmates were to focus their censure votes on me  there wouldn t be a next time in the first place   perhaps it s possible that your subordinates betray you before our match can even happen   you decided early on who d be removed  sounds like the right decision   a reasonable choice   is it alright for you to be telling me this  about who you re targeting   what are you planning to do with class c   sorry  it s about time i go  meets hirata and goes to his dorm room to talk   between being sent to the uninhabited island and being forced to participate in the training camp  it was quite the tiring year   yeah  i think so too   it sounds difficult  in an exam like this one  the more you think about your classmates  the harder it gets   it would be nice if nobody s expelled when the exam is over  but that s difficult in this case","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Morning conversations and after-school meetings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.85–132<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Checks the Ayanokōji Group chat: Keisei proposes arriving early to collect information; the group agrees and Haruka volunteers for the next day. Ichinose joins Ayanokōji on the walk to school; she admits the exam is tough for Class B and considers bearing the risk herself. Ichinose offers to use her cross-class praise vote on Ayanokōji; he declines. Asahina Nazuna borrows Ayanokōji and reveals Ichinose asked Nagumo for points; Nagumo’s condition is a relationship. Classroom atmosphere is tense; Haruka messages that nothing unusual has happened. Overhears Sakayanagi and Kamuro discuss Sakayanagi’s father’s suspension and the supplementary exam. Sakayanagi tells Kamuro she knows Ayanokōji from long ago. Sakayanagi asks to postpone their match for this exam and promises not to cast censure votes for Ayanokōji. Sakayanagi says she has already decided Class A will expel Katsuragi Kōhei. Meets Hirata and goes to his room; Hirata cannot find a way to avoid an expulsion.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “In the face of such a terrible exam… I really have no choice but to do something, don’t I?”<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Since I have a praise vote I can use on someone in another class, I could use it on you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> “The condition he set for lending the points to her… is for the two of them to get into a relationship.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>38 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I simply know him from a long time ago. Is this answer not acceptable enough?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For this exam, I won’t do anything that would put you at a disadvantage. That is to say, I absolutely won’t cast you any censure votes.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi Kōhei-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If… if there’s a way to save the class, please tell me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ayanokōji-kun, do you think it’s fine for someone to be expelled?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Morning walk; she considers bearing the risk and offers her praise vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.89–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Reveals Ichinose asked Nagumo for points and his condition.<span class=\"pg\">p.97–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Postpones their match; promises no censure votes; reveals Katsuragi as Class A target.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata seeks a way to avoid expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If you have business with me, I’ll hear you out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “He consented immediately?”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll ask just to make sure, but there’s no way she’d be lent enough private points with no strings attached, is there?”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are the conditions he’s set too harsh? Like an obscenely high interest rate?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it alright? For you to be telling me this?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re overestimating me. There’s no way I can afford to make up for Class B’s lack of points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t do anything about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Follows Horikita after class but stops when she tells him to leave her alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It wouldn’t be troublesome for us to take in another person.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “…Could I bother you for a moment, Ayanokōji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Meets Sakayanagi and Kamuro and agrees to speak with Sakayanagi at the special building.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have plans to meet up with a friend at Keyaki Mall in around half an hour.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Was that okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Not particularly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Going so far as to have Kamuro head back without you, what are you looking to talk to me about?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Make whatever decision you want.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If my classmates were to focus their censure votes on me, there wouldn’t be a next time in the first place.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Perhaps it’s possible that your subordinates betray you before our match can even happen.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You decided early on who’d be removed? Sounds like the right decision.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A reasonable choice?”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is it alright for you to be telling me this? About who you’re targeting?”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What are you planning to do with Class C?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry. It’s about time I go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Meets Hirata and goes to his dorm room to talk.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Between being sent to the uninhabited island and being forced to participate in the training camp, it was quite the tiring year.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah, I think so too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It sounds difficult. In an exam like this one, the more you think about your classmates, the harder it gets.”<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would be nice if nobody’s expelled when the exam is over. But that’s difficult in this case.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p30-1\">← Before: Ch.2: The Class Vote<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p148-1\">→ After: Ch.4: The target and the mastermind<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p148-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou tachibana-akane yamauchi-haruki sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  the target and the mastermind walks to school with sudo  sudo says he does not want to be expelled  notices the classroom atmosphere has shifted to unusual unity  horikita notices the change  ayanokoji messages keisei about a possible large group  ayanokoji group discusses the large group at lunch  hirata looks distraught  receives a message and leaves to meet someone  meets horikita manabu and tachibana akane at a rest area  manabu explains third years need private points for their own exams  ayanokoji and manabu discuss suzune and nagumo s moves   i ll do what i can  kei calls to warn that around half the class plans to vote him out   everyone s gonna vote you out of school  calls horikita manabu to propose a strategy  calls kushida  she reveals yamauchi is the tentative mastermind   is that so   do you know how many people are going to vote against me   thanks for letting me know this  decides to contact horikita manabu and calls him about the supplemental exam   i need to talk to you about the supplemental exam  it s fairly important   something happened in my class  a large group was formed and they ve decided on who exactly they ll be trying to expel   me   more than half of my class has already agreed to vote against me  offers manabu a proposal and secures his cooperation for the next day  calls kushida to find out who the mastermind is   could it be that you re the mastermind  kushida   it s yamauchi kun   you ve been a great help  kushida   it s yamauchi kun   sakayanagi san from class a seems to be the one supporting yamauchi kun  ends the call with kushida  decides to relay information to manabu  meets him  later calls to propose strategy  present at the meeting  warns him he is the target  reveals yamauchi as tentative mastermind  named as tentative mastermind  named as supporting yamauchi behind the scenes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: The target and the mastermind<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.148–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks to school with Sudō; Sudō says he does not want to be expelled. Notices the classroom atmosphere has shifted to unusual unity. Horikita notices the change; Ayanokōji messages Keisei about a possible large group. Ayanokōji Group discusses the large group at lunch; Hirata looks distraught. Receives a message and leaves to meet someone. Meets Horikita Manabu and Tachibana Akane at a rest area. Manabu explains third-years need private points for their own exams. Ayanokōji and Manabu discuss Suzune and Nagumo’s moves. Kei calls to warn that around half the class plans to vote him out. Calls Horikita Manabu to propose a strategy. Calls Kushida; she reveals Yamauchi is the tentative mastermind. Ends the call with Kushida; decides to relay information to Manabu.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> “I’ll do what I can.”<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “everyone’s gonna vote you out of school.”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is that so?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you know how many people are going to vote against me?”<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thanks for letting me know this.”<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Decides to contact Horikita Manabu and calls him about the supplemental exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I need to talk to you about the supplemental exam. It’s fairly important.”<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Something happened in my class. A large group was formed and they’ve decided on who exactly they’ll be trying to expel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “More than half of my class has already agreed to vote against me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Offers Manabu a proposal and secures his cooperation for the next day.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Calls Kushida to find out who the mastermind is.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could it be that you’re the mastermind, Kushida?”<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’ve been a great help, Kushida.”<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sakayanagi-san from Class A seems to be the one supporting Yamauchi-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Meets him; later calls to propose strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–167, 171–173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> Present at the meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Warns him he is the target.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Reveals Yamauchi as tentative mastermind.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Named as tentative mastermind.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named as supporting Yamauchi behind the scenes.<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p85-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Morning conversations and after-school meetings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p182-1\">→ After: Ch.5: Good and Evil<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p182-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke horikita-manabu yamauchi-haruki kushida-kikyou kouenji-rokusuke sudou-ken ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  good and evil in the morning classroom  most students glance at ayanokoji and look away  he realises the large group has begun acting to expel him  sudo arrives with horikita  horikita asks ayanokoji what he did and he denies doing anything  horikita meets her brother manabu at the special building  as relayed in the chapter  to seek courage before the vote  after school  horikita stands before the class and nominates yamauchi haruki for expulsion   for this special exam  i have decided that we should expel yamauchi haruki kun  horikita exposes yamauchi s collusion with sakayanagi and his targeting of ayanokoji  koenji supports hearing her out  kushida retracts her support for yamauchi after the class turns against him  sudo objects to expelling yamauchi  hirata later refuses to accept the discussion and breaks down  chabashira closes by telling the class to think carefully before voting tomorrow  the ayanokoji group goes to the cafe to discuss the fallout and plans to cast censure votes for yamauchi  ayanokoji finds hirata on a bench and talks with him alone   could i entrust it to you  hirata says he can no longer lead the class  ayanokoji listens as hirata struggles with the idea of leaving someone behind  confronts the class and nominates yamauchi  meets suzune and helps her find resolve  chapter scene  breaks down in class and later asks ayanokoji to lead the class  exposed as mastermind colluding with sakayanagi and targeting ayanokoji  retracts her support for yamauchi when blamed  supports horikita s nomination to avoid his own risk  objects to expelling yamauchi but backs down  drawn into accusations and questions yamauchi s ties to sakayanagi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p182-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Good and Evil<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.182–237<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the morning classroom, most students glance at Ayanokōji and look away; he realises the large group has begun acting to expel him. Sudō arrives with Horikita; Horikita asks Ayanokōji what he did and he denies doing anything. Horikita meets her brother Manabu at the special building (as relayed in the chapter) to seek courage before the vote. After school, Horikita stands before the class and nominates Yamauchi Haruki for expulsion. Horikita exposes Yamauchi’s collusion with Sakayanagi and his targeting of Ayanokōji; Kōenji supports hearing her out. Kushida retracts her support for Yamauchi after the class turns against him. Sudō objects to expelling Yamauchi; Hirata later refuses to accept the discussion and breaks down. Chabashira closes by telling the class to think carefully before voting tomorrow. The Ayanokōji Group goes to the cafe to discuss the fallout and plans to cast censure votes for Yamauchi. Ayanokōji finds Hirata on a bench and talks with him alone. Hirata says he can no longer lead the class; Ayanokōji listens as Hirata struggles with the idea of leaving someone behind.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “For this special exam… I have decided that we should expel Yamauchi Haruki-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Could I entrust it to you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Confronts the class and nominates Yamauchi.<span class=\"pg\">p.184, 197–225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Meets Suzune and helps her find resolve (chapter scene).<span class=\"pg\">p.186–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Breaks down in class and later asks Ayanokōji to lead the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.221–237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Exposed as mastermind colluding with Sakayanagi and targeting Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Retracts her support for Yamauchi when blamed.<span class=\"pg\">p.206–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Supports Horikita’s nomination to avoid his own risk.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Objects to expelling Yamauchi but backs down.<span class=\"pg\">p.184, 216–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Drawn into accusations and questions Yamauchi’s ties to Sakayanagi.<span class=\"pg\">p.206, 211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p148-1\">← Before: Ch.4: The target and the mastermind<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p286-1\">→ After: Epilogue: The dropouts and the deals behind them<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p286-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke yamauchi-haruki sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami ibuki-mio ishizaki-daichi horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  the dropouts and the deals behind them on the morning of the class poll  ayanokoji and horikita discuss whether either of them acted before the vote  hirata apologises to horikita and says he has decided she is necessary for the class  hirata volunteers to be expelled  ayanokoji recognises this as the answer hirata had reached   i want everyone to cast a censure vote for me  koenji provokes yamauchi before the results  chabashira enters to announce class c s votes  chabashira announces ayanokoji received 42 praise votes  placing first in class c  yamauchi is announced expelled with 33 censure votes  koenji stops yamauchi s attack and chabashira orders yamauchi to leave  horikita confronts ayanokoji after class  asking how much he anticipated and whether he told her brother about sakayanagi and yamauchi  at the bulletin board  ayanokoji sees the expulsions  totsuka yahiko  class a  none  class b  yamauchi haruki  class c  manabe shiho  class d  ryuen and katsuragi discuss the results at the board  ryuen then takes ayanokoji behind the school building  flashback  ishizaki and ibuki come to ayanokoji s room asking how to prevent ryuen s expulsion  flashback  ayanokoji arranges for ichinose to come to his room and brokers a deal using ryuen s private points to secure class b s praise votes for ryuen  ichinose agrees to ask class b to cast 40 praise votes for ryuen in exchange for the points transferred by ibuki  ayanokoji explains to ryuen that he used the situation to build trust with ichinose  ichinose calls to report class b avoided expulsion by paying 20 million points to negate kanzaki s expulsion  ayanokoji meets sakayanagi at the special building  acting director tsukishiro appears  kicks sakayanagi s cane  and restrains ayanokoji while delivering a message from his father  ayanokoji proposes to sakayanagi that they have their match in the next exam  volunteers to be expelled and is devastated after yamauchi s expulsion  expelled from class c after the class poll  meets her and agrees to face her in the next exam  speaks with him and reflects on saving him via ichinose and class d  brokers the deal to save ryuen and later speaks with her by phone  works with her and ishizaki to transfer ryuen s points and target manabe  seeks help to save ryuen and cooperates in the plan  discusses the morning of the vote and confronts him afterward","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p286-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: The dropouts and the deals behind them<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.286–362<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the morning of the Class Poll, Ayanokōji and Horikita discuss whether either of them acted before the vote. Hirata apologises to Horikita and says he has decided she is necessary for the class. Hirata volunteers to be expelled; Ayanokōji recognises this as the answer Hirata had reached. Kōenji provokes Yamauchi before the results; Chabashira enters to announce Class C’s votes. Chabashira announces Ayanokōji received 42 praise votes, placing first in Class C. Yamauchi is announced expelled with 33 censure votes; Kōenji stops Yamauchi’s attack and Chabashira orders Yamauchi to leave. Horikita confronts Ayanokōji after class, asking how much he anticipated and whether he told her brother about Sakayanagi and Yamauchi. At the bulletin board, Ayanokōji sees the expulsions: Totsuka Yahiko (Class A), none (Class B), Yamauchi Haruki (Class C), Manabe Shiho (Class D). Ryūen and Katsuragi discuss the results at the board; Ryūen then takes Ayanokōji behind the school building. Flashback: Ishizaki and Ibuki come to Ayanokōji’s room asking how to prevent Ryūen’s expulsion. Flashback: Ayanokōji arranges for Ichinose to come to his room and brokers a deal using Ryūen’s private points to secure Class B’s praise votes for Ryūen. Ichinose agrees to ask Class B to cast 40 praise votes for Ryūen in exchange for the points transferred by Ibuki. Ayanokōji explains to Ryūen that he used the situation to build trust with Ichinose. Ichinose calls to report Class B avoided expulsion by paying 20 million points to negate Kanzaki’s expulsion. Ayanokōji meets Sakayanagi at the special building; acting director Tsukishiro appears, kicks Sakayanagi’s cane, and restrains Ayanokōji while delivering a message from his father. Ayanokōji proposes to Sakayanagi that they have their match in the next exam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+2 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I want everyone to cast a censure vote for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Volunteers to be expelled and is devastated after Yamauchi’s expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.288–291, 304–311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Expelled from Class C after the Class Poll.<span class=\"pg\">p.301–309<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Meets her and agrees to face her in the next exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.354–361<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Speaks with him and reflects on saving him via Ichinose and Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.316–318, 347–348<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Brokers the deal to save Ryūen and later speaks with her by phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.335–346, 349–353<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Works with her and Ishizaki to transfer Ryūen’s points and target Manabe.<span class=\"pg\">p.319–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Seeks help to save Ryūen and cooperates in the plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.319–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses the morning of the vote and confronts him afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–287, 311–315<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p182-1\">← Before: Ch.5: Good and Evil<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p287-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Added voice lines<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p287-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  added voice lines denies having done anything when horikita asks   does it look like i ve done something  tells ishizaki and ibuki the exam is not simple enough to save someone just by wanting to   this exam isn t so simple that you can save someone just because you want to  teases ichinose about having started dating nagumo otherwise   would ve started dating nagumo  talks with her on the morning of the vote  advises him on saving ryuen  speaks with her by phone after the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p287-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Added voice lines<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.287, 332, 350<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Denies having done anything when Horikita asks. Tells Ishizaki and Ibuki the exam is not simple enough to save someone just by wanting to. Teases Ichinose about having started dating Nagumo otherwise.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Does it look like I’ve done something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“This exam isn’t so simple that you can save someone just because you want to.”<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Would’ve started dating Nagumo?”<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Talks with her on the morning of the vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.287<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Advises him on saving Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.332<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Speaks with her by phone after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p286-1\">← Before: Epilogue: The dropouts and the deals behind them<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p366-1\">→ After: Short Stories<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p366-1","v":"y1v10","y":1,"o":12,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka short stories meets ichinose in the morning and agrees to walk to school with her  in horikita s perspective after the exam  ayanokoji speaks briefly with koenji and walks away as horikita stops him  meets sakayanagi  who asks to postpone their duel past the class poll  receives ichinose in his room at night and responds to her questions  walks to school with her and talks with her in his room  is stopped by her in the corridor after the exam  agrees to her request to postpone their match","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p366-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short Stories<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V10 · p.366–376<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ichinose in the morning and agrees to walk to school with her. In Horikita’s perspective after the exam, Ayanokōji speaks briefly with Kōenji and walks away as Horikita stops him. Meets Sakayanagi, who asks to postpone their duel past the Class Poll. Receives Ichinose in his room at night and responds to her questions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Walks to school with her and talks with her in his room.<span class=\"pg\">p.366–369, 375–376<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Is stopped by her in the corridor after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.370–371<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Agrees to her request to postpone their match.<span class=\"pg\">p.373–374<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v10-p287-1\">← Before: Epilogue: Added voice lines<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p7-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka prologue  seen in sakayanagi s memory in sakayanagi s childhood memory  a boy identified as ayanokoji kiyotaka calmly solves tasks and defeats opponents at chess in the white room  sakayanagi s father says he is the director s son and has lived in the facility since birth  this is recounted in sakayanagi s monologue  she observes him through glass during her childhood visit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Prologue: Seen in Sakayanagi’s memory<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.7–12<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In Sakayanagi’s childhood memory, a boy identified as Ayanokōji Kiyotaka calmly solves tasks and defeats opponents at chess in the White Room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakayanagi’s father says he is the director’s son and has lived in the facility since birth; this is recounted in Sakayanagi’s monologue.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She observes him through glass during her childhood visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p13-1\">→ After: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.1 — Depth review: graduation ceremony &amp; the Tsukishiro meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p13-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"inner spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko sakayanagi-arisu mashima-tomonari chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 1  vol  11 5 ch 1   depth review  graduation ceremony   the tsukishiro meeting attends the third years  graduation ceremony  curious whether manabu horikita graduated from class a or nagumo stopped him   i will explain that now   if i said that i m the reason why tsukishiro replaced chairman sakayanagi after being confined for suspected wrongdoing  what would you say  mashima sensei   yeah  even if i told you  it wouldn t be of any help  no  it would be meaningless   heh  even if it doesn t stop tsukishiro completely  if it ll restrain him  then it ll be a good result  considers explaining the white room from the start but judges the adults could not understand it  and that the matter has already been covered up  reckons his class gained 347 points over the year   the fastest in the grade  well above class a s 191   despite the demotion to class d  talks with keisei on the morning of the ceremony  they mutually admit responsibility over the failed katsuragi plan  stages the secret meeting with teachers  walks with her afterward and notes her happiness at mashima s righteousness being a weakness  wins him over as an ally against tsukishiro s exam interference  briefs her and enlists her help","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.1 — Depth review: graduation ceremony &amp; the Tsukishiro meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Attends the third-years&#x27; graduation ceremony, curious whether Manabu Horikita graduated from Class A or Nagumo stopped him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I will explain that now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I said that I&#x27;m the reason why Tsukishiro replaced Chairman Sakayanagi after being confined for suspected wrongdoing, what would you say, Mashima-sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. Even if I told you, it wouldn&#x27;t be of any help… no, it would be meaningless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Heh. Even if it doesn&#x27;t stop Tsukishiro completely, if it&#x27;ll restrain him, then it&#x27;ll be a good result.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Considers explaining the White Room from the start but judges the adults could not understand it, and that the matter has already been covered up.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reckons his class gained 347 points over the year — the fastest in the grade, well above Class A&#x27;s 191 — despite the demotion to Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Talks with Keisei on the morning of the ceremony; they mutually admit responsibility over the failed Katsuragi plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Stages the secret meeting with teachers; walks with her afterward and notes her happiness at Mashima&#x27;s righteousness being a weakness.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Wins him over as an ally against Tsukishiro&#x27;s exam interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.64–79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Briefs her and enlists her help.<span class=\"pg\">p.64–80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p7-1\">← Before: Prologue: Seen in Sakayanagi’s memory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Event Selection Exam announced<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p27-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji sudou-ken shinohara-satsuki chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  event selection exam announced attends homeroom as chabashira announces the event selection exam after yamauchi s expulsion  receives photos of the event rule handout from horikita  ike and sudo question him about receiving 42 praise votes in the class poll  horikita explains sakayanagi s plan on his behalf  volunteers to become the class commander to clear suspicions and because he holds a protection point  horikita supports him taking the commander role despite objections  receives the rules from her and is defended and steered into the commander role by her  is questioned by him and later supported when he volunteers  is questioned by him about the praise votes  faces her objection to him becoming commander  hears her explain the event selection exam rules","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Event Selection Exam announced<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.27–54<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Attends homeroom as Chabashira announces the Event Selection Exam after Yamauchi’s expulsion. Receives photos of the event-rule handout from Horikita. Ike and Sudō question him about receiving 42 praise votes in the Class Poll. Horikita explains Sakayanagi’s plan on his behalf. Volunteers to become the class commander to clear suspicions and because he holds a protection point. Horikita supports him taking the commander role despite objections.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Receives the rules from her and is defended and steered into the commander role by her.<span class=\"pg\">p.42, 47–54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Is questioned by him and later supported when he volunteers.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Is questioned by him about the praise votes.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Faces her objection to him becoming commander.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Hears her explain the Event Selection Exam rules.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p13-1\">← Before: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.1 — Depth review: graduation ceremony &amp; the Tsukishiro meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p55-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Opponents and Kei’s visit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p55-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami kaneda-satoru karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  opponents and kei s visit leaves during lunch to contact others before returning to class c s meeting  leaves the classroom as commander and heads to the multipurpose room with chabashira  tells chabashira he volunteered to be commander  attends the commanders  meeting with sakayanagi  ichinose  and kaneda  kaneda chooses class b  leaving class c matched against class a  listens as the teachers explain the commander interface and rules for exam day  returns to his dorm thinking he needs information about class c and plans to consult others  invites kei into his room in the evening  asks kei about the internal state of the class and considers consulting hirata and kushida later  gives kei a necklace as a birthday and white day present  walks with her to the multipurpose room and discusses becoming commander  faces her as class c s commander when the matchup becomes class c vs class a  meets her at the commanders  meeting  present as he chooses class b  meets her in his room  gathers information  and gives her a necklace","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Opponents and Kei’s visit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.55–92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves during lunch to contact others before returning to Class C’s meeting. Leaves the classroom as commander and heads to the multipurpose room with Chabashira. Tells Chabashira he volunteered to be commander. Attends the commanders’ meeting with Sakayanagi, Ichinose, and Kaneda. Kaneda chooses Class B, leaving Class C matched against Class A. Listens as the teachers explain the commander interface and rules for exam day. Returns to his dorm thinking he needs information about Class C and plans to consult others. Invites Kei into his room in the evening. Asks Kei about the internal state of the class and considers consulting Hirata and Kushida later. Gives Kei a necklace as a birthday and White Day present.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Walks with her to the multipurpose room and discusses becoming commander.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Faces her as Class C’s commander when the matchup becomes Class C vs Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Meets her at the commanders’ meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Present as he chooses Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Meets her in his room, gathers information, and gives her a necklace.<span class=\"pg\">p.74–92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Event Selection Exam announced<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p93-1\">→ After: Ch.4: Class preparation, Hirata, and Hoshinomiya<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p93-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"hasebe-haruka sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko miyake-akito horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke wang-mei-yu hashimoto-masayoshi hoshinomiya-chie chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  class preparation  hirata  and hoshinomiya the day after the matchups  eats lunch with the ayanokoji group and asks about the previous day s class discussion  apologizes for losing the lottery matchup choice while thinking he would have chosen class a anyway  observes hirata s aimless  withdrawn state in the cafeteria  talks with horikita in the morning about leaving hirata out of the exam for now and the risks of forcing him  suggests to horikita that mii chan s concern for hirata may be love  leaves the classroom to follow horikita and mii chan after the discussion is interrupted  tells horikita he will go after mii chan because someone who wants to leave hirata alone should not be the one to approach him  catches up to mii chan and walks with her as she follows hirata  tells mii chan she is right not to leave hirata alone and encourages her to reach out  returns to school and encounters hashimoto  who has been watching class c  on the way to school  is stopped by hoshinomiya sensei for a conversation  listens as hoshinomiya asks about his relationship status and talks about romance in the dorms  tells hoshinomiya that dating across rival classes could cause problems  reports to chabashira that he and hoshinomiya were talking about room sharing  eats lunch and discusses the exam with her in the ayanokoji group  eats lunch and discusses the exam with her in the ayanokoji group  discusses class a s information advantage and exam strategy with him  discusses the matchup and hirata s state with him  discusses hirata and class strategy with her  goes after mii chan instead of her  observes his withdrawal and considers how to handle him  follows and encourages her to reach out to hirata  is observed by him and speaks briefly with him  talks with her on the way to school  answers her after hoshinomiya leaves","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p93-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: Class preparation, Hirata, and Hoshinomiya<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.93–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The day after the matchups, eats lunch with the Ayanokōji Group and asks about the previous day’s class discussion. Apologizes for losing the lottery/matchup choice while thinking he would have chosen Class A anyway. Observes Hirata’s aimless, withdrawn state in the cafeteria. Talks with Horikita in the morning about leaving Hirata out of the exam for now and the risks of forcing him. Suggests to Horikita that Mii-chan’s concern for Hirata may be love. Leaves the classroom to follow Horikita and Mii-chan after the discussion is interrupted. Tells Horikita he will go after Mii-chan because someone who wants to leave Hirata alone should not be the one to approach him. Catches up to Mii-chan and walks with her as she follows Hirata. Tells Mii-chan she is right not to leave Hirata alone and encourages her to reach out. Returns to school and encounters Hashimoto, who has been watching Class C. On the way to school, is stopped by Hoshinomiya-sensei for a conversation. Listens as Hoshinomiya asks about his relationship status and talks about romance in the dorms. Tells Hoshinomiya that dating across rival classes could cause problems. Reports to Chabashira that he and Hoshinomiya were talking about room sharing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+4 more<\/span><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Eats lunch and discusses the exam with her in the Ayanokōji Group.<span class=\"pg\">p.93–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Eats lunch and discusses the exam with her in the Ayanokōji Group.<span class=\"pg\">p.93–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Discusses Class A’s information advantage and exam strategy with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.93–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Discusses the matchup and Hirata’s state with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.93–109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses Hirata and class strategy with her; goes after Mii-chan instead of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.125–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Observes his withdrawal and considers how to handle him.<span class=\"pg\">p.108, 125–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/b> Follows and encourages her to reach out to Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.144–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Is observed by him and speaks briefly with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Talks with her on the way to school.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Answers her after Hoshinomiya leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p55-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Opponents and Kei’s visit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p124-1\">→ After: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.2 — Depth review: the date with Hiyori<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p124-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 1  vol  11 5 ch 2   depth review  the date with hiyori meets hiyori at keyaki mall on the first day of spring break  she is already waiting and shows him the new library books   good morning   yes  but  since it s you i m asking  i don t think i need to elaborate on it   why do you think that   hiyori  can you help me pass on a message   tell ryuuen that if it were me  i would have been able to secure more than 5 wins  using a better method  please pass that on to him   it seems that i should change my evaluation of her  judges hiyori more dangerous than ishizaki or ibuki because she could keep those three from going out of control  and chose not to answer her directly because she would not exploit the situation  revises his view of hiyori from a same year student to a friend with mutual interests  accepts her question about changing ryuen  tests her reasoning  then entrusts her with the message to ryuen  deliberately upsets kei afterward by arranging the meeting in front of her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.2 — Depth review: the date with Hiyori<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Hiyori at Keyaki Mall on the first day of spring break; she is already waiting and shows him the new library books.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. But, since it&#x27;s you I&#x27;m asking, I don&#x27;t think I need to elaborate on it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why do you think that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hiyori, can you help me pass on a message?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Tell Ryuuen that if it were me, I would have been able to secure more than 5 wins, using a better method. Please pass that on to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It seems that I should change my evaluation of her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Judges Hiyori more dangerous than Ishizaki or Ibuki because she could keep those three from going out of control, and chose not to answer her directly because she would not exploit the situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Revises his view of Hiyori from a same-year student to a friend with mutual interests.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Accepts her question about changing Ryūen, tests her reasoning, then entrusts her with the message to Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Deliberately upsets Kei afterward by arranging the meeting in front of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p93-1\">← Before: Ch.4: Class preparation, Hirata, and Hoshinomiya<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p144-1\">→ After: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.3 — Depth review: the challenge and the confessions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p144-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 1  vol  11 5 ch 3   depth review  the challenge and the confessions anticipates ichinose s meeting and the question of whether the class b class d cooperation will continue into the second year   i m happy that you invited me  but i ll have to refuse  it s more fun being opponents than allies anyway   because i thought our best chance of winning came from opposing class a   what do you think  why would i go out of my way to set this up  can you guess   maybe  that s why i used class b as a sacrifice   i wanted to talk to you and look at your senseless  severe face at the same time   i meant what i meant  i would have done a better job if it were up to me  observes horikita s improved patience and judgement when she let his arranged  class a  story stand without questioning it in front of ichinose  deliberately exposed himself as the one who asked ichinose for class a to test how much horikita had grown  is confronted about acting alone to target class a  admits he ignored her orders but holds back his true reasons  sakayanagi  the white room  meets him after the message via hiyori  warns him his laxative ploy was too obvious and that he must grow stronger  declines his  ultimate strategy  to transfer to class d  her message to ryuen prompted this meeting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.3 — Depth review: the challenge and the confessions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Anticipates Ichinose&#x27;s meeting and the question of whether the Class B–Class D cooperation will continue into the second year.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m happy that you invited me, but I&#x27;ll have to refuse. It&#x27;s more fun being opponents than allies anyway.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Because I thought our best chance of winning came from opposing Class A&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What do you think? Why would I go out of my way to set this up, can you guess?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Maybe. That&#x27;s why I used Class B as a sacrifice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wanted to talk to you and look at your senseless, severe face at the same time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I meant what I meant. I would have done a better job if it were up to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Observes Horikita&#x27;s improved patience and judgement when she let his arranged &quot;Class A&quot; story stand without questioning it in front of Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Deliberately exposed himself as the one who asked Ichinose for Class A to test how much Horikita had grown.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Is confronted about acting alone to target Class A; admits he ignored her orders but holds back his true reasons (Sakayanagi, the White Room).<span class=\"pg\">p.182–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Meets him after the message via Hiyori; warns him his laxative ploy was too obvious and that he must grow stronger.<span class=\"pg\">p.206–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Declines his &quot;ultimate strategy&quot; to transfer to Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Her message to Ryūen prompted this meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p124-1\">← Before: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.2 — Depth review: the date with Hiyori<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.5: Information, preparation, and Katsuragi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p170-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"hasebe-haruka miyake-akito sakura-airi yukimura-teruhiko ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji shibata-sou kushida-kikyou horikita-manabu tachibana-akane horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  information  preparation  and katsuragi walks with the ayanokoji group and encounters shibata  ichinose  and kanzaki discussing class d s harassment  speaks for his group when ichinose invites them to eat together at the cafe  declines ichinose s offer to pay  saying they will pay for themselves  stops with his group to overhear ike inviting shinohara out for white day  approaches kushida after school to ask about her lack of involvement in the exam  asks kushida for cooperation and information  but accepts her decision to stay uninvolved while not interfering  delivers white day return gifts early in the morning and runs into ichinose at the dorm mailboxes  confirms his gift to ichinose and asks about class d s harassment of class b  meets horikita manabu and tachibana on the way to school and discusses suzune and the special exam  resolves inwardly to make horikita change for real  tells the class he can play chess more or less but has never played go  joins keisei and horikita in the hallway to discuss intelligence gathering  goes to horikita s room after her call and is served dinner  reviews horikita s exam notebook and suggests she be the one to play chess in class a s event  accompanies keisei to meet katsuragi  asks katsuragi whether sakayanagi would let him participate despite being wary of him  advises keisei not to tell horikita immediately that they contacted katsuragi  walks and eats with her in the ayanokoji group  walks and eats with him in the ayanokoji group  walks and eats with her in the ayanokoji group  eats with him  discusses information gathering  and meets katsuragi together  eats with her group and later meets her on white day morning  hears his concerns about class d s harassment  hears his account of class d s harassment  questions her about involvement in the exam  talks with him about suzune and his future  encounters her with horikita manabu  discusses strategy with her and reviews her notebook  meets him with keisei to seek information on class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Information, preparation, and Katsuragi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.170–280<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks with the Ayanokōji Group and encounters Shibata, Ichinose, and Kanzaki discussing Class D’s harassment. Speaks for his group when Ichinose invites them to eat together at the café. Declines Ichinose’s offer to pay, saying they will pay for themselves. Stops with his group to overhear Ike inviting Shinohara out for White Day. Approaches Kushida after school to ask about her lack of involvement in the exam. Asks Kushida for cooperation and information, but accepts her decision to stay uninvolved while not interfering. Delivers White Day return gifts early in the morning and runs into Ichinose at the dorm mailboxes. Confirms his gift to Ichinose and asks about Class D’s harassment of Class B. Meets Horikita Manabu and Tachibana on the way to school and discusses Suzune and the special exam. Resolves inwardly to make Horikita change for real. Tells the class he can play chess more or less but has never played Go. Joins Keisei and Horikita in the hallway to discuss intelligence gathering. Goes to Horikita’s room after her call and is served dinner. Reviews Horikita’s exam notebook and suggests she be the one to play chess in Class A’s event. Accompanies Keisei to meet Katsuragi. Asks Katsuragi whether Sakayanagi would let him participate despite being wary of him. Advises Keisei not to tell Horikita immediately that they contacted Katsuragi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+6 more<\/span><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Walks and eats with her in the Ayanokōji Group.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Walks and eats with him in the Ayanokōji Group.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Walks and eats with her in the Ayanokōji Group.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Eats with him, discusses information gathering, and meets Katsuragi together.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–191, 240–247, 271–280<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Eats with her group and later meets her on White Day morning.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–183, 208–216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Hears his concerns about Class D’s harassment.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shibata Sō<\/b> Hears his account of Class D’s harassment.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Questions her about involvement in the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Talks with him about Suzune and his future.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> Encounters her with Horikita Manabu.<span class=\"pg\">p.217, 229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses strategy with her and reviews her notebook.<span class=\"pg\">p.240–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Meets him with Keisei to seek information on Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.271–280<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p144-1\">← Before: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.3 — Depth review: the challenge and the confessions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p217-1\">→ After: Ch.5: Manabu and Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p217-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  manabu and horikita greets manabu on the way to school   is the special exam going well  says horikita is the last person to talk about kindness   you of all people are telling me that  says horikita didn t think he d read her notebook so seriously   dinner aside  you didn t think i d read through this so seriously  did you  asks horikita to play chess   about that  i d like you to be the one to take part in it  says horikita s fascination with chess is not just about knowing the rules   your fascination with the chess event isn t just because you know the rules  is it  says he doesn t know much about the class   i don t really know all that much about our class anyway  talks with him about suzune  has dinner with her and discusses the notebook","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p217-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Manabu and Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.217–229, 248–270<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Greets Manabu on the way to school. Says Horikita is the last person to talk about kindness. Says Horikita didn’t think he’d read her notebook so seriously. Asks Horikita to play chess. Says Horikita’s fascination with chess is not just about knowing the rules. Says he doesn’t know much about the class.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Is the special exam going well?”<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You of all people are telling me that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Dinner aside, you didn’t think I’d read through this so seriously, did you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “About that, I’d like you to be the one to take part in it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Your fascination with the chess event isn’t just because you know the rules, is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t really know all that much about our class anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Talks with him about Suzune.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Has dinner with her and discusses the notebook.<span class=\"pg\">p.248–270<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.5: Information, preparation, and Katsuragi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p237-1\">→ After: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.4 — Depth review: Manabu&#x27;s farewell and the &quot;parting gifts&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p237-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 1  vol  11 5 ch 4   depth review  manabu s farewell and the  parting gifts  waits at the school s main entrance at 11 40 for manabu horikita s noon departure  suzune has not yet arrived   sorry  if only i could have done more for you when you were on the student council   i don t think that s very reasonable considering the fact you ve stayed in class a for three whole years   perhaps what nagumo wants to do isn t necessarily wrong   i plan to observe what nagumo wants to do  if he really plans to change the entire grade  no  the entire school into a meritocracy  i ll have to witness it first before making any judgements   i simply just don t like attracting attention to myself   it s hard to say  there s been an increase in things that attracted my attention   i understand yeah  i will think about this more carefully  speaks with manabu as an equal   discusses nagumo s meritocracy  the pooled points gamble to reach class a  and receives his  parting gift  evaluation  shares a long farewell  receives his private phone number  his challenge not to disappoint him  and a handshake  asks why he hides his abilities  march class points given by manabu  nagumo s class a 1491  class b 889  class c 280  class d 76  manabu gives ayanokoji his own and tachibana s phone numbers to memorise  to be deleted later","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.4 — Depth review: Manabu&#x27;s farewell and the &quot;parting gifts&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits at the school&#x27;s main entrance at 11:40 for Manabu Horikita&#x27;s noon departure; Suzune has not yet arrived.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sorry. If only I could have done more for you when you were on the student council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t think that&#x27;s very reasonable considering the fact you&#x27;ve stayed in Class A for three whole years.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Perhaps what Nagumo wants to do isn&#x27;t necessarily wrong.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I plan to observe what Nagumo wants to do. If he really plans to change the entire grade, no, the entire school into a meritocracy, I&#x27;ll have to witness it first before making any judgements.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I simply just don&#x27;t like attracting attention to myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s hard to say. There&#x27;s been an increase in things that attracted my attention.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand….yeah. I will think about this more carefully.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Speaks with Manabu as an equal — discusses Nagumo&#x27;s meritocracy, the pooled-points gamble to reach Class A, and receives his &quot;parting gift&quot; evaluation.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Shares a long farewell; receives his private phone number, his challenge not to disappoint him, and a handshake; asks why he hides his abilities.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> March class points given by Manabu: Nagumo&#x27;s Class A 1491, Class B 889, Class C 280, Class D 76.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Manabu gives Ayanokōji his own and Tachibana&#x27;s phone numbers to memorise, to be deleted later.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p217-1\">← Before: Ch.5: Manabu and Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p281-1\">→ After: Ch.6: Hirata’s recovery<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p281-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke wang-mei-yu kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  hirata s recovery tells horikita to focus on unifying class c while he follows after mii chan and hirata  watches from a distance as mii chan confronts hirata on the way to the dormitories  observes as koenji intervenes in the confrontation and hirata leaves  retrieves mii chan s bag and follows koenji and mii chan to the dormitory entrance  speaks with koenji in the lobby about why he provoked hirata and about participation in the exam  searches for hirata and finds him on an outside bench  asks hirata to talk and presses him to explain his past and his feelings about yamauchi s expulsion  tells hirata he is responsible for not saving yamauchi if he claims he wants to save everyone  forcing him to confront his ideals  tells hirata he can rely on classmates when troubled and places a hand on his shoulder as hirata breaks down  tells horikita that hirata s recovery was a collective effort when she asks what happened  advises her to focus on the class and later explains hirata s change to her  observes  confronts  and supports him through his breakdown and recovery  watches her confrontation with hirata and helps her afterward  observes his intervention and speaks with him at the dormitory","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p281-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Hirata’s recovery<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.281–317<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tells Horikita to focus on unifying Class C while he follows after Mii-chan and Hirata. Watches from a distance as Mii-chan confronts Hirata on the way to the dormitories. Observes as Kōenji intervenes in the confrontation and Hirata leaves. Retrieves Mii-chan’s bag and follows Kōenji and Mii-chan to the dormitory entrance. Speaks with Kōenji in the lobby about why he provoked Hirata and about participation in the exam. Searches for Hirata and finds him on an outside bench. Asks Hirata to talk and presses him to explain his past and his feelings about Yamauchi’s expulsion. Tells Hirata he is responsible for not saving Yamauchi if he claims he wants to save everyone, forcing him to confront his ideals. Tells Hirata he can rely on classmates when troubled and places a hand on his shoulder as Hirata breaks down. Tells Horikita that Hirata’s recovery was a collective effort when she asks what happened.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"wang-mei-yu.html\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Advises her to focus on the class and later explains Hirata’s change to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.282, 315–317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Observes, confronts, and supports him through his breakdown and recovery.<span class=\"pg\">p.283–311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Wang Mei-Yu<\/b> Watches her confrontation with Hirata and helps her afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.283–293<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Observes his intervention and speaks with him at the dormitory.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–294<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p237-1\">← Before: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.4 — Depth review: Manabu&#x27;s farewell and the &quot;parting gifts&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p282-1\">→ After: Ch.6: Searching for Hirata<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p282-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  searching for hirata says he wonders whether hirata has changed   i wonder about that  asks hirata for some time   can you spare some time  says it is not horikita s fault yamauchi was expelled   there s something i want to make clear to you  it s not horikita s fault that yamauchi got expelled from the school  and  of course  it s not my fault either  confronts him on the bench","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p282-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Searching for Hirata<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.282, 295–306<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Says he wonders whether Hirata has changed. Asks Hirata for some time. Says it is not Horikita’s fault Yamauchi was expelled.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“I wonder about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Can you spare some time?”<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“There’s something I want to make clear to you. It’s not Horikita’s fault that Yamauchi got expelled from the school, and, of course, it’s not my fault either.”<span class=\"pg\">p.305<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Confronts him on the bench.<span class=\"pg\">p.295–308<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p281-1\">← Before: Ch.6: Hirata’s recovery<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p318-1\">→ After: Ch.7: Commander against Class A (events 1–5)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p318-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru sudou-ken sotomura-hideo kouenji-rokusuke matsushita-chiaki katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  commander against class a  events 1 5  before homeroom  horikita tells him to act freely as commander and rely on her preparation  leaves for the multipurpose room to fulfill his commander duties  arrives and meets sakayanagi and ichinose while waiting for the exam to begin  witnesses ryuen arrive as substitute commander for class d  speaks briefly with sakayanagi before the exam begins  selects class c s five events and begins the commander matchup against sakayanagi  chooses class c s basketball lineup without sudo  then substitutes sudo in at halftime  class c wins the event  selects sotomura for the typing event  class c wins  chooses to give up on the english test to preserve resources  class a wins  fields class c s strongest available lineup for the math test  class a wins narrowly  selects koenji and matsushita for flash mental arithmetic and intervenes on the final question  but class a wins  recognizes class c is behind 2 3 after five events  receives her final instructions and preparation notes before acting as commander  faces her as class c s commander throughout the first five events  meets her before the exam and witnesses the shock of ryuen s arrival  sees him appear as class d s substitute commander  substitutes him into the basketball match  leading to a class c win  selects him for typing and secures a class c win  selects him for flash mental arithmetic but he refuses to participate seriously  relies on her in flash mental arithmetic  competes against him in flash mental arithmetic and loses the event","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p318-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: Commander against Class A (events 1–5)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.318–367<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Before homeroom, Horikita tells him to act freely as commander and rely on her preparation. Leaves for the multipurpose room to fulfill his commander duties. Arrives and meets Sakayanagi and Ichinose while waiting for the exam to begin. Witnesses Ryūen arrive as substitute commander for Class D. Speaks briefly with Sakayanagi before the exam begins. Selects Class C’s five events and begins the commander matchup against Sakayanagi. Chooses Class C’s basketball lineup without Sudō, then substitutes Sudō in at halftime; Class C wins the event. Selects Sotomura for the typing event; Class C wins. Chooses to give up on the English test to preserve resources; Class A wins. Fields Class C’s strongest available lineup for the math test; Class A wins narrowly. Selects Kōenji and Matsushita for Flash Mental Arithmetic and intervenes on the final question, but Class A wins. Recognizes Class C is behind 2–3 after five events.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"sotomura-hideo.html\">Sotomura Hideo<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+3 more<\/span><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Receives her final instructions and preparation notes before acting as commander.<span class=\"pg\">p.318–320<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Faces her as Class C’s commander throughout the first five events.<span class=\"pg\">p.321–367<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Meets her before the exam and witnesses the shock of Ryūen’s arrival.<span class=\"pg\">p.321–328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Sees him appear as Class D’s substitute commander.<span class=\"pg\">p.324–328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Substitutes him into the basketball match, leading to a Class C win.<span class=\"pg\">p.339–347<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Selects him for typing and secures a Class C win.<span class=\"pg\">p.349–350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Selects him for Flash Mental Arithmetic but he refuses to participate seriously.<span class=\"pg\">p.359–366<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Relies on her in Flash Mental Arithmetic.<span class=\"pg\">p.359–365<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Competes against him in Flash Mental Arithmetic and loses the event.<span class=\"pg\">p.359–366<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p282-1\">← Before: Ch.6: Searching for Hirata<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p329-1\">→ After: Ch.7: Facing Sakayanagi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p329-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7  facing sakayanagi asks whether sakayanagi is afraid to wake from her dream   aren t you afraid to wake up from your dream  says horikita warned him not to say too much   horikita warned me not to say anything excessive to you  clarifies that horikita may not be the one instructing him   no  i just said that horikita warned me  the instructions could ve come from somebody else  faces her in the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p329-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7: Facing Sakayanagi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.329–337<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Asks whether Sakayanagi is afraid to wake from her dream. Says Horikita warned him not to say too much. Clarifies that Horikita may not be the one instructing him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“Aren’t you afraid to wake up from your dream?”<span class=\"pg\">p.329<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“Horikita warned me not to say anything excessive to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“No, I just said that Horikita warned me... The instructions could’ve come from somebody else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Faces her in the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.329–345<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p318-1\">← Before: Ch.7: Commander against Class A (events 1–5)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p351-1\">→ After: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.5 — Depth review: the truth about Matsushita (Ayanokōji&#x27;s POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p351-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"matsushita-chiaki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 1  vol  11 5 ch 5   depth review  the truth about matsushita  ayanokoji s pov  confronts matsushita  she has deduced his hidden ability and pressed about his relationship with kei   i ve got one request  my thing with karuizawa   i know  i won t tell anyone  no matter what  notes that if matsushita spread the kei rumour or withheld cooperation it would only hurt her  so the matter is contained  confirmed she had seen through him  extracted her silence about his relationship with kei in exchange for information  the chapter is mostly matsushita s first person narration  pp 296 307  the confrontation is resolved by p 351","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p351-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.5 — Depth review: the truth about Matsushita (Ayanokōji&#x27;s POV)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Confronts Matsushita; she has deduced his hidden ability and pressed about his relationship with Kei.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve got one request, my thing with Karuizawa-&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> &quot;I know. I won&#x27;t tell anyone, no matter what.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes that if Matsushita spread the Kei rumour or withheld cooperation it would only hurt her, so the matter is contained.<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Confirmed she had seen through him; extracted her silence about his relationship with Kei in exchange for information.<span class=\"pg\">p.296–351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The chapter is mostly Matsushita&#x27;s first-person narration (pp.296–307); the confrontation is resolved by p.351.<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p329-1\">← Before: Ch.7: Facing Sakayanagi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p355-1\">→ After: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Epilogue — Depth review: the confession to Kei<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p355-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 1  vol  11 5 epilogue   depth review  the confession to kei calls kei and asks her to come to his room  saying he has remembered what he wanted to tell her   it s me  i m sorry to call you   if you don t like it  then just ignore it   will you go out with me   i don t mean that  i mean to ask you if you would go out with me   that was a joke   i wanted to try to see if you were jealous  kei   because i wanted to prevent you from becoming someone else s girlfriend   that s right  i like karuizawa kei   i don t plan to do that  at least for now  staged the cafe scene with hiyori and the hints about her to make kei jealous  then proposed   a calculated but genuine confession  confesses his feelings  has her say she likes him in return  and embraces her   a major step in their relationship  used the book date with hiyori as the setup to provoke kei s jealousy  reflects that he is  learning to fall in love  through kei   something the white room could not teach   and that the relationship is also necessary for her growth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p355-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Epilogue — Depth review: the confession to Kei<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Calls Kei and asks her to come to his room, saying he has remembered what he wanted to tell her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s me. I&#x27;m sorry to call you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.357<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you don&#x27;t like it, then just ignore it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.364<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Will you go out with me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.364<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t mean that. I mean to ask you if you would go out with me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.365<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That was a joke.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.365<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wanted to try to see if you were jealous, Kei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.366<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Because I wanted to prevent you from becoming someone else&#x27;s girlfriend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.366<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s right, I like Karuizawa Kei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.366<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t plan to do that, at least for now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.370<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Staged the café scene with Hiyori and the hints about her to make Kei jealous, then proposed — a calculated but genuine confession.<span class=\"pg\">p.365–366<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Confesses his feelings, has her say she likes him in return, and embraces her — a major step in their relationship.<span class=\"pg\">p.355–373<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Used the book date with Hiyori as the setup to provoke Kei&#x27;s jealousy.<span class=\"pg\">p.365<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Reflects that he is &quot;learning to fall in love&quot; through Kei — something the White Room could not teach — and that the relationship is also necessary for her growth.<span class=\"pg\">p.370–372<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p351-1\">← Before: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Ch.5 — Depth review: the truth about Matsushita (Ayanokōji&#x27;s POV)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p400-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Chess match and aftermath<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p400-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune hashimoto-masayoshi hoshinomiya-chie sakagami-kazuma tsukishiro karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou ike-kanji sotomura-hideo ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  chess match and aftermath notes class c won the sixth archery event to tie the score 3 3 before the final chess event is drawn  selects horikita to play the on board chess match against hashimoto  watches horikita gain an advantage  then intervenes as commander when sakayanagi enters the match  takes over from horikita and battles sakayanagi through the remainder of the chess game  stops giving instructions when defeat becomes unavoidable  class a wins the chess event and the exam 4 3  receives hoshinomiya s comments about his displayed abilities after the exam  exchanges words with sakayanagi after the match as she expresses satisfaction  hears from acting director tsukishiro that class d defeated class b 5 2  learns from tsukishiro that his final chess instruction was altered by outside interference  agrees to sakayanagi s request to replay the final chess position in the library  replays the position and wins the recreated game against sakayanagi  walks back to the dorms with sakayanagi as they talk before parting  appears in karuizawa s white day birthday short story as the giver of the necklace  appears in kushida s short story as she reflects on him after he questions her lack of support  appears in horikita s short story playing a vr game with horikita  ike  and sotomura  faces her in the decisive chess match  learns of tsukishiro s interference  and replays the final position with her  selects her for chess and later appears with her in the vr short story  faces him as horikita s opponent in the chess event  is observed and questioned by her during and after the exam  competes under his proctoring and hears the result announced  is told by him about the exam outcome and the interference in the chess match  is remembered in her short story as giving her the necklace  is reflected on in her short story  plays the vr game with him in horikita s short story  plays the vr game with him in horikita s short story","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p400-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Chess match and aftermath<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.400–476<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Notes Class C won the sixth archery event to tie the score 3–3 before the final chess event is drawn. Selects Horikita to play the on-board chess match against Hashimoto. Watches Horikita gain an advantage, then intervenes as commander when Sakayanagi enters the match. Takes over from Horikita and battles Sakayanagi through the remainder of the chess game. Stops giving instructions when defeat becomes unavoidable; Class A wins the chess event and the exam 4–3. Receives Hoshinomiya’s comments about his displayed abilities after the exam. Exchanges words with Sakayanagi after the match as she expresses satisfaction. Hears from Acting Director Tsukishiro that Class D defeated Class B 5–2. Learns from Tsukishiro that his final chess instruction was altered by outside interference. Agrees to Sakayanagi’s request to replay the final chess position in the library. Replays the position and wins the recreated game against Sakayanagi. Walks back to the dorms with Sakayanagi as they talk before parting. Appears in Karuizawa’s White Day/birthday short story as the giver of the necklace. Appears in Kushida’s short story as she reflects on him after he questions her lack of support. Appears in Horikita’s short story playing a VR game with Horikita, Ike, and Sotomura.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+3 more<\/span><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Faces her in the decisive chess match, learns of Tsukishiro’s interference, and replays the final position with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.400–454<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Selects her for chess and later appears with her in the VR short story.<span class=\"pg\">p.402–429, 470–476<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Faces him as Horikita’s opponent in the chess event.<span class=\"pg\">p.402–429<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Is observed and questioned by her during and after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.403, 430–432<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">sakagami-kazuma<\/b> Competes under his proctoring and hears the result announced.<span class=\"pg\">p.404, 429, 431<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Is told by him about the exam outcome and the interference in the chess match.<span class=\"pg\">p.433–444<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Is remembered in her short story as giving her the necklace.<span class=\"pg\">p.456–458<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Is reflected on in her short story.<span class=\"pg\">p.464–466<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Plays the VR game with him in Horikita’s short story.<span class=\"pg\">p.470–476<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sotomura Hideo<\/b> Plays the VR game with him in Horikita’s short story.<span class=\"pg\">p.470–476<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p355-1\">← Before: Year 1, Vol. 11.5 Epilogue — Depth review: the confession to Kei<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p430-1\">→ After: Epilogue: After the exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p430-1","v":"y1v11","y":1,"o":13,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  after the exam is asked whether he hid his abilities   the heck  does this mean you ve been hiding your abilities until now  says sakayanagi won  so there is nothing more   you re the one who won  what more could there be to it  says he lost at the end of the day   what are you talking about  at the end of the day  i lost  asks about a chessboard in the library   did you know that there s a chessboard in the library  says sakayanagi is honest about her defeat   you sure are honest about it  says he was objectively stating facts   that s not it  i was just objectively stating the facts  says sakayanagi is honest   fufu  how honest  says he will put the chessboard away   i ll put it away  just sit there and wait for a bit  speaks with her after the exam  is confronted by him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p430-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: After the exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11 · p.430, 439–450<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is asked whether he hid his abilities. Says Sakayanagi won, so there is nothing more. Says he lost at the end of the day. Asks about a chessboard in the library. Says Sakayanagi is honest about her defeat. Says he was objectively stating facts. Says Sakayanagi is honest. Says he will put the chessboard away.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">“The heck? Does this mean you’ve been hiding your abilities until now?”<span class=\"pg\">p.430<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“You’re the one who won. What more could there be to it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.439<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">“What are you talking about? At the end of the day, I lost.”<span class=\"pg\">p.441<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you know that there’s a chessboard in the library?”<span class=\"pg\">p.445<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You sure are honest about it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.446<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not it. I was just objectively stating the facts.”<span class=\"pg\">p.447<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Fufu, how honest.”<span class=\"pg\">p.449<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ll put it away. Just sit there and wait for a bit.”<span class=\"pg\">p.450<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Speaks with her after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.439–450<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Is confronted by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.439–444<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11-p400-1\">← Before: Epilogue: Chess match and aftermath<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p13-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"action spoken","w":"yukimura-teruhiko chabashira-sae sakayanagi-arisu horikita-suzune horikita-manabu tsukishiro nagumo-miyabi asahina-nazuna mashima-tomonari hoshinomiya-chie sakagami-kazuma ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1  graduation ceremony and farewells on march 24  ayanokoji attends the third year graduation ceremony curious about the outcome of horikita manabu and nagumo s conflict and the ceremony itself  in the elevator  yukimura keisei greets him and talks about class d s demotion after the final exam   good morning  keisei blames himself for pushing the katsuragi recruitment and says he told horikita about it  keisei explains that horikita did not blame him and discusses the risk of katsuragi betraying class a  keisei asks why ayanokoji did not report his katsuragi plan to horikita  ayanokoji downplays it  keisei reflects on horikita s leadership and how he has changed since enrolling  during the ceremony  graduates are called to the stage  horikita manabu gives the representative address as a class a graduate  back in class after the ceremony  chabashira praises the class s growth despite their demotion   okay  even though we can mention this tomorrow during the closing ceremony  let s briefly summarise what happened this year    after class  ayanokoji asks horikita suzune whether she will see her brother  she initially says she has no plans  suzune decides she may see her brother and asks ayanokoji to wait while he kills time until the graduates  meeting ends  in a flashback to the previous night  ayanokoji calls chairman sakayanagi from his room  in a flashback to the previous night  ayanokoji calls chairman sakayanagi from his room and identifies himself  ayanokoji asks chairman sakayanagi about his house arrest and explains he is calling because of circumstances affecting his own status  ayanokoji tells chairman sakayanagi that acting director tsukishiro is acting against him and asks the chairman to return to the school  in the present  ayanokoji meets sakayanagi arisu while waiting and they head to a meeting room  ayanokoji attends a meeting with sakayanagi  tsukishiro  mashima  chabashira  sakagami  and hoshinomiya concerning the chess exam  sakayanagi states that ayanokoji originally won the chess match  prompting a dispute over the process and tsukishiro s role   i was originally the loser of that chess game  ayanokouji kun came out victorious  mashima and the teachers decide the matter must be reported despite tsukishiro s denials  after the meeting  ayanokoji finds horikita suzune waiting near the gym for the third years to emerge from the graduates  meeting  as more graduates gather  ayanokoji urges suzune to approach her brother and pushes her forward  ayanokoji watches nagumo miyabi congratulate horikita manabu as asahina nazuna and other student council members stand nearby  nagumo approaches suzune after parting from manabu  and their exchange draws attention to her as manabu s sister  ayanokoji listens as nagumo and asahina discuss the outcome of nagumo s conflict with horikita manabu  ayanokoji observes the farewells as the graduates  send off continues around them  talks with keisei before and after the ceremony  discusses seeing her brother and stays with her during the farewell gathering  watches his graduation speech and later observes him among graduates  meets her and participates in the confrontation over the chess exam  confronts him in the meeting over exam interference  observes his exchange with horikita manabu and later with suzune and asahina  sees her with nagumo during the farewell gathering  hears her address in class and later attends the meeting  present in the meeting about exam interference  present in the meeting about exam interference  present in the meeting about exam interference","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: Graduation ceremony and farewells<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.13–120<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On March 24, Ayanokōji attends the third-year graduation ceremony curious about the outcome of Horikita Manabu and Nagumo’s conflict and the ceremony itself. In the elevator, Yukimura Keisei greets him and talks about Class D’s demotion after the final exam. Keisei blames himself for pushing the Katsuragi recruitment and says he told Horikita about it. Keisei explains that Horikita did not blame him and discusses the risk of Katsuragi betraying Class A. Keisei asks why Ayanokōji did not report his Katsuragi plan to Horikita; Ayanokōji downplays it. Keisei reflects on Horikita’s leadership and how he has changed since enrolling. During the ceremony, graduates are called to the stage; Horikita Manabu gives the representative address as a Class A graduate. Back in class after the ceremony, Chabashira praises the class’s growth despite their demotion. After class, Ayanokōji asks Horikita Suzune whether she will see her brother; she initially says she has no plans. Suzune decides she may see her brother and asks Ayanokōji to wait while he kills time until the graduates’ meeting ends. In a flashback to the previous night, Ayanokōji calls Chairman Sakayanagi from his room. Ayanokōji asks Chairman Sakayanagi about his house arrest and explains he is calling because of circumstances affecting his own status. Ayanokōji tells Chairman Sakayanagi that Acting Director Tsukishiro is acting against him and asks the chairman to return to the school. In the present, Ayanokōji meets Sakayanagi Arisu while waiting and they head to a meeting room. Ayanokōji attends a meeting with Sakayanagi, Tsukishiro, Mashima, Chabashira, Sakagami, and Hoshinomiya concerning the chess exam. Sakayanagi states that Ayanokōji originally won the chess match, prompting a dispute over the process and Tsukishiro’s role. Mashima and the teachers decide the matter must be reported despite Tsukishiro’s denials. After the meeting, Ayanokōji finds Horikita Suzune waiting near the gym for the third-years to emerge from the graduates’ meeting. As more graduates gather, Ayanokōji urges Suzune to approach her brother and pushes her forward. Ayanokōji watches Nagumo Miyabi congratulate Horikita Manabu as Asahina Nazuna and other student council members stand nearby. Nagumo approaches Suzune after parting from Manabu, and their exchange draws attention to her as Manabu’s sister. Ayanokōji listens as Nagumo and Asahina discuss the outcome of Nagumo’s conflict with Horikita Manabu. Ayanokōji observes the farewells as the graduates’ send-off continues around them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> <span class=\"n\">+4 more<\/span><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “Good morning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Okay, even though we can mention this tomorrow during the closing ceremony, let’s briefly summarise what happened this year. “<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “I was originally the loser of that chess game, Ayanokouji-kun came out victorious.”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> In a flashback to the previous night, Ayanokōji calls Chairman Sakayanagi from his room and identifies himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Talks with Keisei before and after the ceremony.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses seeing her brother and stays with her during the farewell gathering.<span class=\"pg\">p.32–33, 89–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Watches his graduation speech and later observes him among graduates.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–28, 94–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Meets her and participates in the confrontation over the chess exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Confronts him in the meeting over exam interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Observes his exchange with Horikita Manabu and later with Suzune and Asahina.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Sees her with Nagumo during the farewell gathering.<span class=\"pg\">p.94–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Hears her address in class and later attends the meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31, 47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Present in the meeting about exam interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Present in the meeting about exam interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">sakagami-kazuma<\/b> Present in the meeting about exam interference.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.2: Date Hiyori<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p121-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ike-kanji shinohara-satsuki karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  date hiyori at the start of spring break  ayanokoji reflects on campus life during the break and his situation after the end of year exam  he notes his contract requires him to hand over half his private points to kushida each month and considers how that relationship may change  ayanokoji meets shiina hiyori at keyaki mall  she has arrived early carrying newly added library books   hello  ayanokouji kun  he and hiyori take seats at a crowded cafe and prepare to talk about books  ike kanji and shinohara satsuki sit nearby  hiyori recognizes them as ayanokoji s classmates  ayanokoji listens as ike and shinohara discuss the drop in private points  class d s demotion  and ike s sense of responsibility for the loss  he hears ike express fear of becoming the next expulsion candidate and shinohara respond seriously  ike begins to say something important to shinohara before being interrupted when she notices ayanokoji and hiyori  after an awkward exchange and argument  ike and shinohara leave the cafe  hiyori asks ayanokoji about the end of year exam and whether he changed ryuen  she explains she connected ryuen s withdrawal and later behavior  including inquiries involving ishizaki and ibuki  hiyori discusses class c s risky strategy against class b and asks for ayanokoji s view  ayanokoji asks hiyori to pass ryuen a message that he could have secured more than five wins by a better method  after parting with hiyori  ayanokoji meets karuizawa kei at keyaki mall  kei  concerned about rumors  leaves after ayanokoji says he will contact her later  meets her at the cafe to discuss books and ryuen  overhears his conversation with shinohara  overhears her conversation with ike  meets her briefly after the cafe meeting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: Date Hiyori<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.121–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the start of spring break, Ayanokōji reflects on campus life during the break and his situation after the end-of-year exam. He notes his contract requires him to hand over half his private points to Kushida each month and considers how that relationship may change. Ayanokōji meets Shiina Hiyori at Keyaki mall; she has arrived early carrying newly added library books. He and Hiyori take seats at a crowded café and prepare to talk about books. Ike Kanji and Shinohara Satsuki sit nearby; Hiyori recognizes them as Ayanokōji’s classmates. Ayanokōji listens as Ike and Shinohara discuss the drop in private points, Class D’s demotion, and Ike’s sense of responsibility for the loss. He hears Ike express fear of becoming the next expulsion candidate and Shinohara respond seriously. Ike begins to say something important to Shinohara before being interrupted when she notices Ayanokōji and Hiyori. After an awkward exchange and argument, Ike and Shinohara leave the café. Hiyori asks Ayanokōji about the end-of-year exam and whether he changed Ryūen. She explains she connected Ryūen’s withdrawal and later behavior, including inquiries involving Ishizaki and Ibuki. Hiyori discusses Class C’s risky strategy against Class B and asks for Ayanokōji’s view. Ayanokōji asks Hiyori to pass Ryūen a message that he could have secured more than five wins by a better method. After parting with Hiyori, Ayanokōji meets Karuizawa Kei at Keyaki mall. Kei, concerned about rumors, leaves after Ayanokōji says he will contact her later.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara-satsuki.html\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> “Hello, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Meets her at the café to discuss books and Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.124–142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Overhears his conversation with Shinohara.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Overhears her conversation with Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Meets her briefly after the café meeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.1: Graduation ceremony and farewells<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Lost Lamb<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p144-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune ibuki-mio ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  lost lamb during spring break  ayanokoji receives a message from ichinose honami asking to meet and to include horikita suzune  he contacts horikita  who insists on meeting the same day despite his concern about her brother s departure  on the way to keyaki mall  ayanokoji shares an elevator and walk with ibuki mio  ishizaki daichi joins them and accidentally reveals he and ibuki are meeting ryuen kakeru  ishizaki proposes that ayanokoji transfer to class d as an  ultimate strategy  to reach class a  ayanokoji refuses ishizaki s proposal and parts from ibuki and ishizaki at the mall  he meets horikita at the mall before the meeting with ichinose  ayanokoji and horikita meet ichinose at the cafe to discuss the end of year exam and the future relationship between their classes  after the cafe meeting  horikita challenges ayanokoji to compete in a written exam subject of her choosing after april  ayanokoji accepts horikita s challenge and they agree on the terms  ayanokoji meets ryuen at keyaki mall after hiyori relays his message  he tells ryuen he could have secured more than five wins with a better strategy in the end of year exam  ryuen declares he will eventually return to target ichinose and sakayanagi  ayanokoji responds and they briefly clash when ryuen attacks  ayanokoji advises ryuen to be less obvious in his methods  and they part after ryuen says he will defeat him  in heavy rain  ayanokoji finds ichinose standing alone outside and approaches her with umbrellas  when ichinose refuses to leave the rain  ayanokoji closes his umbrella and stays with her until she agrees to return  he brings ichinose to his room to warm up and encourages her to talk about her worries  ayanokoji promises to meet ichinose again one year later and tells her to keep moving forward  he reflects that if ichinose falls in the second year  he will be the one to finish her off  meets her to discuss class relations and later comforts her in the rain and in his room  arranges and attends the meeting with ichinose and accepts her written exam challenge  encounters her on the way to keyaki mall  hears his proposal and learns of plans involving ryuen  infers his return and later meets him at the mall","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Lost Lamb<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.144–236<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">During spring break, Ayanokōji receives a message from Ichinose Honami asking to meet and to include Horikita Suzune. He contacts Horikita, who insists on meeting the same day despite his concern about her brother’s departure. On the way to Keyaki mall, Ayanokōji shares an elevator and walk with Ibuki Mio. Ishizaki Daichi joins them and accidentally reveals he and Ibuki are meeting Ryūen Kakeru. Ishizaki proposes that Ayanokōji transfer to Class D as an “ultimate strategy” to reach Class A. Ayanokōji refuses Ishizaki’s proposal and parts from Ibuki and Ishizaki at the mall. He meets Horikita at the mall before the meeting with Ichinose. Ayanokōji and Horikita meet Ichinose at the café to discuss the end-of-year exam and the future relationship between their classes. After the café meeting, Horikita challenges Ayanokōji to compete in a written exam subject of her choosing after April. Ayanokōji accepts Horikita’s challenge and they agree on the terms. Ayanokōji meets Ryūen at Keyaki mall after Hiyori relays his message. He tells Ryūen he could have secured more than five wins with a better strategy in the end-of-year exam. Ryūen declares he will eventually return to target Ichinose and Sakayanagi; Ayanokōji responds and they briefly clash when Ryūen attacks. Ayanokōji advises Ryūen to be less obvious in his methods, and they part after Ryūen says he will defeat him. In heavy rain, Ayanokōji finds Ichinose standing alone outside and approaches her with umbrellas. When Ichinose refuses to leave the rain, Ayanokōji closes his umbrella and stays with her until she agrees to return. He brings Ichinose to his room to warm up and encourages her to talk about her worries. Ayanokōji promises to meet Ichinose again one year later and tells her to keep moving forward. He reflects that if Ichinose falls in the second year, he will be the one to finish her off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Meets her to discuss class relations and later comforts her in the rain and in his room.<span class=\"pg\">p.144–148, 162–190, 216–236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Arranges and attends the meeting with Ichinose and accepts her written-exam challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.147–148, 160–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Encounters her on the way to Keyaki mall.<span class=\"pg\">p.150–156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Hears his proposal and learns of plans involving Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Infers his return and later meets him at the mall.<span class=\"pg\">p.153, 206–214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p121-1\">← Before: Ch.2: Date Hiyori<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p237-1\">→ After: Ch.4: From a Brother to a Sister<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p237-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  from a brother to a sister on march 31  ayanokoji arrives early at the school s main entrance to see horikita manabu off  manabu arrives before noon  suzune has not yet appeared  while waiting  ayanokoji and manabu talk about the past year  the student council  and nagumo s influence  manabu discusses the school s class system and the chances for lower classes  and they consider nagumo s meritocratic ideas  as noon passes  manabu decides not to call suzune and prepares to leave on schedule  manabu asks ayanokoji why he hides his abilities and advises him to leave something behind at the school  suzune arrives late and calls out to her brother as he is about to depart  ayanokoji observes suzune s changed appearance with short hair and watches the siblings reunite  manabu tells suzune she has returned to her former self  suzune says she will no longer chase his shadow and will find her own path  ayanokoji listens as manabu explains why he pushed suzune away and acknowledges her potential  the siblings share a final embrace and farewell  manabu apologizes for lying about preferring her long hair  manabu tells suzune he will wait for her outside the main entrance two years later and departs  after the farewell  ayanokoji walks back with suzune and asks about her decision to cut her hair  when suzune tries to leave alone  ayanokoji stays with her as she breaks down in tears over parting from her brother  after she recovers  ayanokoji proposes that if he wins their written exam contest  suzune will join the student council  he tells suzune about his contract with kushida and says he will leave decisions about kushida to her  after parting from suzune  ayanokoji reflects on manabu s words and his own future at the school  sees him off  talks with him  and reflects on his parting words  waits with her for manabu  witnesses their farewell  and talks with her afterward","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p237-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: From a Brother to a Sister<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.237–295<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On March 31, Ayanokōji arrives early at the school’s main entrance to see Horikita Manabu off. Manabu arrives before noon; Suzune has not yet appeared. While waiting, Ayanokōji and Manabu talk about the past year, the student council, and Nagumo’s influence. Manabu discusses the school’s class system and the chances for lower classes, and they consider Nagumo’s meritocratic ideas. As noon passes, Manabu decides not to call Suzune and prepares to leave on schedule. Manabu asks Ayanokōji why he hides his abilities and advises him to leave something behind at the school. Suzune arrives late and calls out to her brother as he is about to depart. Ayanokōji observes Suzune’s changed appearance with short hair and watches the siblings reunite. Manabu tells Suzune she has returned to her former self; Suzune says she will no longer chase his shadow and will find her own path. Ayanokōji listens as Manabu explains why he pushed Suzune away and acknowledges her potential. The siblings share a final embrace and farewell; Manabu apologizes for lying about preferring her long hair. Manabu tells Suzune he will wait for her outside the main entrance two years later and departs. After the farewell, Ayanokōji walks back with Suzune and asks about her decision to cut her hair. When Suzune tries to leave alone, Ayanokōji stays with her as she breaks down in tears over parting from her brother. After she recovers, Ayanokōji proposes that if he wins their written-exam contest, Suzune will join the student council. He tells Suzune about his contract with Kushida and says he will leave decisions about Kushida to her. After parting from Suzune, Ayanokōji reflects on Manabu’s words and his own future at the school.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Sees him off, talks with him, and reflects on his parting words.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–270, 294–295<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Waits with her for Manabu, witnesses their farewell, and talks with her afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–293<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Lost Lamb<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p324-1\">→ After: Ch.5: Tsukishiro and Matsushita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p324-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"tsukishiro matsushita-chiaki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  tsukishiro and matsushita at keyaki mall  ayanokoji is approached by acting director tsukishiro  who speaks with him after dismissing nearby workers  tsukishiro pressures ayanokoji to drop out and return to his father  while ayanokoji refuses  ayanokoji notices matsushita following him as tsukishiro mentions her presence  tsukishiro discusses the white room s history and its results  and ayanokoji questions him about it  tsukishiro proposes a  game  a white room student will enroll as a freshman  and if ayanokoji identifies that student by the end of april  tsukishiro will give up  ayanokoji accepts the challenge on the surface and states his confidence regarding the white room  after tsukishiro leaves  ayanokoji deliberately lets matsushita follow him and then confronts her  matsushita questions him about the mental arithmetic event and about seeing him with hirata during the class vote  ayanokoji admits to holding back to some extent but downplays his abilities and deflects her suspicions  he explains karuizawa s interest as a result of his confession rather than his hidden strength and asks matsushita to keep it secret  is confronted and pressured by him at the mall  is followed by her and then confronted  deflects her questions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p324-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Tsukishiro and Matsushita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.324–351<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Keyaki mall, Ayanokōji is approached by Acting Director Tsukishiro, who speaks with him after dismissing nearby workers. Tsukishiro pressures Ayanokōji to drop out and return to his father, while Ayanokōji refuses. Ayanokōji notices Matsushita following him as Tsukishiro mentions her presence. Tsukishiro discusses the White Room’s history and its results, and Ayanokōji questions him about it. Tsukishiro proposes a “game”: a White Room student will enroll as a freshman, and if Ayanokōji identifies that student by the end of April, Tsukishiro will give up. Ayanokōji accepts the challenge on the surface and states his confidence regarding the White Room. After Tsukishiro leaves, Ayanokōji deliberately lets Matsushita follow him and then confronts her. Matsushita questions him about the mental arithmetic event and about seeing him with Hirata during the Class Vote. Ayanokōji admits to holding back to some extent but downplays his abilities and deflects her suspicions. He explains Karuizawa’s interest as a result of his confession rather than his hidden strength and asks Matsushita to keep it secret.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Is confronted and pressured by him at the mall.<span class=\"pg\">p.324–338<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Is followed by her and then confronted; deflects her questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.327, 339–351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p237-1\">← Before: Ch.4: From a Brother to a Sister<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p352-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Confession and reflections<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p352-1","v":"y1v11.5","y":1,"o":14,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  confession and reflections near the end of spring break  ayanokoji reflects on unresolved issues involving tsukishiro  matsushita  horikita  ichinose  and the coming year  he calls karuizawa kei and asks her to come to his room  kei visits his room and they discuss rumors involving sato and matsushita about their relationship  ayanokoji stops kei from leaving and confesses to her  asking her to go out with him  after kei asks for confirmation  ayanokoji tells her he likes her and hears her answer  he embraces kei in his room  later  ayanokoji and kei sit together under cherry blossoms on campus and view them  in ryuen s recollection  ayanokoji meets ryuen at keyaki mall and responds to his message about the end of year exam  ayanokoji tells ryuen he could have done better and warns about the risks of ryuen s methods  he avoids ryuen s sudden attacks during their confrontation  ayanokoji advises ryuen to grow and be less careless  then parts from him  confesses to her  becomes her boyfriend  and views cherry blossoms with her  meets and clashes with him in ryuen s account","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p352-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Confession and reflections<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.5 · p.352–370, 381–398<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Near the end of spring break, Ayanokōji reflects on unresolved issues involving Tsukishiro, Matsushita, Horikita, Ichinose, and the coming year. He calls Karuizawa Kei and asks her to come to his room. Kei visits his room and they discuss rumors involving Satō and Matsushita about their relationship. Ayanokōji stops Kei from leaving and confesses to her, asking her to go out with him. After Kei asks for confirmation, Ayanokōji tells her he likes her and hears her answer. He embraces Kei in his room. Later, Ayanokōji and Kei sit together under cherry blossoms on campus and view them. In Ryūen’s recollection, Ayanokōji meets Ryūen at Keyaki mall and responds to his message about the end-of-year exam. Ayanokōji tells Ryūen he could have done better and warns about the risks of Ryūen’s methods. He avoids Ryūen’s sudden attacks during their confrontation. Ayanokōji advises Ryūen to grow and be less careless, then parts from him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Confesses to her, becomes her boyfriend, and views cherry blossoms with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.355–370, 399–423<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Meets and clashes with him in Ryūen’s account.<span class=\"pg\">p.396–404<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_5-p324-1\">← Before: Ch.5: Tsukishiro and Matsushita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_75-p3-1","v":"y1v11.75","y":1,"o":15,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka short story  the first phone call on the final night of spring break  ayanokoji reflects on school resuming and on issues awaiting him in the new year  at 10 pm he receives a scheduled phone call from karuizawa kei  ayanokoji and kei talk awkwardly at first about their new relationship  he tells kei he waited for her call  and they continue talking about everyday matters  ayanokoji shares trivial topics in response to kei s request  and their call continues for about an hour  they try to end the call for the night but kei calls back  upset by how abruptly he ended it  ayanokoji explains why he ended the call without hesitation  and they end the conversation more calmly  he reflects on their changed relationship and looks ahead to the start of the new school term  speaks with her by phone on the last night of spring break","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_75-p3-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Short story: The First Phone Call<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.75 · p.3–14<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the final night of spring break, Ayanokōji reflects on school resuming and on issues awaiting him in the new year. At 10 PM he receives a scheduled phone call from Karuizawa Kei. Ayanokōji and Kei talk awkwardly at first about their new relationship. He tells Kei he waited for her call, and they continue talking about everyday matters. Ayanokōji shares trivial topics in response to Kei’s request, and their call continues for about an hour. They try to end the call for the night but Kei calls back, upset by how abruptly he ended it. Ayanokōji explains why he ended the call without hesitation, and they end the conversation more calmly. He reflects on their changed relationship and looks ahead to the start of the new school term.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Speaks with her by phone on the last night of spring break.<span class=\"pg\">p.4–14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_75-p3-2\">→ After: Year 1, Vol. 11.75 SS — Depth review: the first phone call with Kei<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_75-p3-2","v":"y1v11.75","y":1,"o":15,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka year 1  vol  11 75 ss   depth review  the first phone call with kei on the last night of spring break  reflects on the coming second year   the horikita bet and the white room first year tsukishiro mentioned   karuizawa kei   i was waiting for your call   it s normal for a boyfriend to wait expectantly for a call from his lover  isn t it   of course we are   we should probably end this call soon   good night  kei   it s true i hanged up without hesitation  but  that wasn t because i thought lightly of you   it s a bit sad to end the conversation  true  but that just means we can see each other tomorrow  deliberately practices being a boyfriend  clumsy but genuine   finds the trivial conversation novel and even fun  still holds the wish for a calm school life  but accepts that academic  sports and love currents will all rage    that s the fun part of school life  has their first call since the confession  learns to handle her feelings and agrees to keep the relationship secret at school  notes the possibility that the white room first year has already enrolled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_75-p3-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Year 1, Vol. 11.75 SS — Depth review: the first phone call with Kei<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V11.75 · <\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the last night of spring break, reflects on the coming second year — the Horikita bet and the White Room first-year Tsukishiro mentioned.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Karuizawa Kei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.4<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was waiting for your call.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.5<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s normal for a boyfriend to wait expectantly for a call from his lover, isn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.5<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course we are.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.6<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should probably end this call soon.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Good night, Kei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s true I hanged up without hesitation. But, that wasn&#x27;t because I thought lightly of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s a bit sad to end the conversation, true. But that just means we can see each other tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately practices being a boyfriend, clumsy but genuine — finds the trivial conversation novel and even fun.<span class=\"pg\">p.5–8<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Still holds the wish for a calm school life, but accepts that academic, sports and love currents will all rage — &quot;that&#x27;s the fun part of school life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Has their first call since the confession; learns to handle her feelings and agrees to keep the relationship secret at school.<span class=\"pg\">p.4–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Notes the possibility that the White Room first-year has already enrolled.<span class=\"pg\">p.3<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v11_75-p3-1\">← Before: Short story: The First Phone Call<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p7-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"tsukishiro nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka prologue  targeted by tsukishiro tsukishiro reviews ayanokoji s white room data and plans his expulsion before the end of april  tsukishiro calls him a monster and wonders how a fair fight between white room students would turn out  is targeted by him  is to be opposed by her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Prologue: Targeted by Tsukishiro<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.7–11<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tsukishiro reviews Ayanokōji’s White Room data and plans his expulsion before the end of April. Tsukishiro calls him a monster and wonders how a fair fight between White Room students would turn out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Is targeted by him.<span class=\"pg\">p.7–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Is to be opposed by her.<span class=\"pg\">p.7–11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p12-1\">→ After: Ch.1: School overview<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p12-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1  school overview states he is a class d student with 275 class points at the start of his second year  notes class a  sakayanagi  1119  class b  ichinose  542  and class c  ryuen  540  class point totals  leads class a with 1119 points  leads class b with 542 points  leads class c with 540 points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1: School overview<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.12–15<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">States he is a Class D student with 275 class points at the start of his second year. Notes Class A (Sakayanagi, 1119), Class B (Ichinose, 542), and Class C (Ryūen, 540) class point totals.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Leads Class A with 1119 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Leads Class B with 542 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Leads Class C with 540 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p7-1\">← Before: Prologue: Targeted by Tsukishiro<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p17-1\">→ After: Opening ceremony: Miyake&#x27;s advice; Class D&#x27;s first-year reflection<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p17-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"miyake-akito hasebe-haruka sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka opening ceremony  miyake s advice  class d s first year reflection arrives in the new second year classroom  instructed by the blackboard monitor to sit in last year s seat   the back window seat   i ve been a little worried about you cuz you didn t really hang out with the group all that much over spring break   my bad  i ll hang out with you guys more often moving forward  the chalk blackboard has been replaced by a large  brand new monitor  the room is otherwise the same  and the opening ceremony will be in the gym followed by a two hour homeroom briefing  miyake notes haruka and airi were also worried about him  he decides he has  found myself a truly good friend  after miyake s good natured advice  reflects on class d s first year  given 1000 points  100 000 month  they squandered it with tardiness and dozing  receiving the lowest assessment and dropping to zero points by may 1   the school s unspoken first  special exam  testing whether they d do what was needed without being told  sees the class slowly piece itself back together after hitting bottom  they rose to class c once but fell back to d after the end of term exam  ending the year at 275 points  receives friendly advice about the group  resolves to spend more time with them  was worried about him over spring break  was thinking about him a lot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Opening ceremony: Miyake&#x27;s advice; Class D&#x27;s first-year reflection<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.17–19<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives in the new second-year classroom, instructed by the blackboard-monitor to sit in last year&#x27;s seat — the back window seat.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve been a little worried about you cuz you didn&#x27;t really hang out with the group all that much over spring break.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My bad. I&#x27;ll hang out with you guys more often moving forward.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The chalk blackboard has been replaced by a large, brand-new monitor; the room is otherwise the same, and the opening ceremony will be in the gym followed by a two-hour homeroom briefing.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Miyake notes Haruka and Airi were also worried about him; he decides he has &quot;found myself a truly good friend&quot; after Miyake&#x27;s good-natured advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Reflects on Class D&#x27;s first year: given 1000 points (¥100,000/month) they squandered it with tardiness and dozing, receiving the lowest assessment and dropping to zero points by May 1 — the school&#x27;s unspoken first &quot;special exam&quot; testing whether they&#x27;d do what was needed without being told.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees the class slowly piece itself back together after hitting bottom; they rose to Class C once but fell back to D after the end-of-term exam, ending the year at 275 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Receives friendly advice about the group; resolves to spend more time with them.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Was worried about him over spring break.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Was thinking about him a lot.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.1: School overview<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p18-1\">→ After: Ch.2: New stage<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p18-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"miyake-akito horikita-suzune ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2  new stage miyake warns him he neglected the group over spring break  reflects on class d s first year and 275 class points  agrees to the competition with horikita over a written exam subject  agrees to help horikita find partners  is told horikita trusts him the most  agrees to attend ichinose s meet and greet  receives his advice  discusses the exam with her  notes her meet and greet message","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: New stage<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.18, 20, 51–65<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Miyake warns him he neglected the group over spring break. Reflects on Class D’s first year and 275 class points. Agrees to the competition with Horikita over a written exam subject. Agrees to help Horikita find partners. Is told Horikita trusts him the most. Agrees to attend Ichinose’s meet-and-greet.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Receives his advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses the exam with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Notes her meet-and-greet message.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p17-1\">← Before: Opening ceremony: Miyake&#x27;s advice; Class D&#x27;s first-year reflection<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p20-1\">→ After: Karuizawa&#x27;s entrance; Horikita&#x27;s short hair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p20-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka karuizawa s entrance  horikita s short hair watches karuizawa enter to a lively  g mornin  and gather the girls around her   he began dating kei just the other day  known only to her  horikita enters to a commotion  her once long black hair now short  not reaching her shoulders   cut after reconciling with her brother manabu and bidding farewell to her former self  she takes the seat right next to ayanokoji   s suzune  wha  what s up with your hair   horikita san  that is  quite the drastic makeover  i m surprised   is it really so strange that i chose to get a haircut    horikita  this year  as a second year student  i ll be fighting to bring class d to the top  i wanted to do what i could in order to make that happen  reads the true meaning in kushida s  i guess i ll do the opposite and try growing my hair out    disgust that her hair is now the same length as the person she hates  and senses her raging emotions  observes the reaction to her haircut  already knowing about it in advance  secretly dating her  perceives her concealed hostility behind innocent words","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Karuizawa&#x27;s entrance; Horikita&#x27;s short hair<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.20–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches Karuizawa enter to a lively &quot;G&#x27;mornin&#x27;~&quot; and gather the girls around her — he began dating Kei just the other day, known only to her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;S-Suzune…? Wha… What&#x27;s up with your hair!?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Horikita-san, that is… quite the drastic makeover. I&#x27;m surprised.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is it really so strange that I chose to get a haircut?&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Horikita enters to a commotion, her once-long black hair now short, not reaching her shoulders — cut after reconciling with her brother Manabu and bidding farewell to her former self; she takes the seat right next to Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This year, as a second-year student, I&#x27;ll be fighting to bring Class D to the top. I wanted to do what I could in order to make that happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Reads the true meaning in Kushida&#x27;s &quot;I guess I&#x27;ll do the opposite and try growing my hair out&quot; — disgust that her hair is now the same length as the person she hates, and senses her raging emotions.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Observes the reaction to her haircut, already knowing about it in advance.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Secretly dating her.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Perceives her concealed hostility behind innocent words.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p18-1\">← Before: Ch.2: New stage<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p25-1\">→ After: The digitalized school; the Paper Shuffle–style exam announced<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p25-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the digitalized school  the paper shuffle style exam announced on monday  examines the new 12 inch tablet replacing textbooks  with charging ports  portable batteries  and school wireless  notes the first years are now around but he hasn t spoken to any  he moved from the back window seat to the hallway side back desk   seats can now be chosen with private points  a 12 inch tablet holds all materials  supports graphics photos and globalized english use   now  i ll give you guys an overview of the next special exam   the bottom line is that the exam will take the form of a written test where you second years will be partnering up with the newly admitted first years   this special exam will primarily focus on your test taking and communication skills   this particular exam is about helping you build cooperative relationships  so do well to keep that in mind   you can think of this exam as an improved version of the paper shuffle exam  where you were partnered up from among your classmates  suspects tsukishiro or nagumo is behind the school s changes  reasons the exam breaks the year barrier deliberately for communication  and sees oaa as the tool making cross year partnerships practical  matching faces to names and gauging ability  follows the reasoning skeptically   doubts chabashira s grade skipping explanation is the whole story  and sees how weaker students will be abandoned as smart students pair off  delivers the exam briefing  he reads between the lines of her scripted explanation  suspects he may be behind the sudden school changes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The digitalized school; the Paper Shuffle–style exam announced<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.25–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On Monday, examines the new 12-inch tablet replacing textbooks, with charging ports, portable batteries, and school wireless; notes the first-years are now around but he hasn&#x27;t spoken to any.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Now, I&#x27;ll give you guys an overview of the next special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;The bottom line is that the exam will take the form of a written test where you second-years will be partnering up with the newly admitted first-years.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;This special exam will primarily focus on your test-taking and communication skills.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He moved from the back window seat to the hallway-side back desk ( seats can now be chosen with private points); a 12-inch tablet holds all materials, supports graphics/photos and globalized English use.<span class=\"pg\">p.25–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;this particular exam is about helping you build cooperative relationships, so do well to keep that in mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can think of this exam as an improved version of the Paper Shuffle exam, where you were partnered up from among your classmates.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Suspects Tsukishiro or Nagumo is behind the school&#x27;s changes; reasons the exam breaks the year barrier deliberately for communication, and sees OAA as the tool making cross-year partnerships practical (matching faces to names and gauging ability).<span class=\"pg\">p.40–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Follows the reasoning skeptically — doubts Chabashira&#x27;s grade-skipping explanation is the whole story, and sees how weaker students will be abandoned as smart students pair off.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Delivers the exam briefing; he reads between the lines of her scripted explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Suspects he may be behind the sudden school changes.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p20-1\">← Before: Karuizawa&#x27;s entrance; Horikita&#x27;s short hair<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p44-1\">→ After: Exam rewards, rules, and the expulsion condition<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p44-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka exam rewards  rules  and the expulsion condition five subjects  100 points each  500 total  class rewards 50 30 10 0 by average  individual rewards   top five pairs  100 000  top 30   10 000  a pair scoring under 500 expels the second year  the first year loses private points for three months  deliberately lowering scores  or forcing another to  expels the offender regardless of year  one partnership application per day via oaa  accept   final and irreversible  except expulsion serious illness  profiles show results at 8 00 am next day  partner identity not listed  unpaired students get a random partner at 8 00 am on exam day but suffer a 5  score penalty  the three leftover first years  from three second year expulsions  have scores doubled with the same 5  penalty  analyzes that his own expulsion is certain unless his partner scores at least 1 point   even with his own full marks  a partner s zero dooms him  the anti throwing rule is  indispensable  to legitimize the exam and protect average students  recognizes this is an  exceedingly difficult  exam for him specifically  notes the rules make blatant misbehavior impossible","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Exam rewards, rules, and the expulsion condition<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.44–49<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Five subjects, 100 points each (500 total); class rewards 50/30/10/0 by average; individual rewards — top five pairs ¥100,000, top 30% ¥10,000.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> A pair scoring under 500 expels the second-year; the first-year loses private points for three months. Deliberately lowering scores (or forcing another to) expels the offender regardless of year.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> One partnership application per day via OAA; accept = final and irreversible (except expulsion/serious illness); profiles show results at 8:00 AM next day; partner identity not listed.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Unpaired students get a random partner at 8:00 AM on exam day but suffer a 5% score penalty; the three leftover first-years (from three second-year expulsions) have scores doubled with the same 5% penalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Analyzes that his own expulsion is certain unless his partner scores at least 1 point — even with his own full marks, a partner&#x27;s zero dooms him; the anti-throwing rule is &quot;indispensable&quot; to legitimize the exam and protect average students.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Recognizes this is an &quot;exceedingly difficult&quot; exam for him specifically; notes the rules make blatant misbehavior impossible.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p25-1\">← Before: The digitalized school; the Paper Shuffle–style exam announced<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p49-1\">→ After: The White Room student threat; Ayanokōji&#x27;s C rating<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p49-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the white room student threat  ayanokoji s c rating realizes the anti throwing rule is meaningless against the white room transfer student  who plans to be expelled anyway and would take a 0 without hesitation if paired with him  concludes he already faces at least a 1 in 160 chance of expulsion  suspects tsukishiro concocted the rules with a small loophole allowing flexible  biased enforcement  and would expel ayanokoji without batting an eye if he partnered with someone who didn t take the exam seriously  notes his own oaa academic ability is a c   he can t freely choose a partner  and must avoid the white room student who may be  lying in wait  for someone with a similar rating  judges this  more challenging than any other special exam  certain he devised the rules to target him via the white room agent","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The White Room student threat; Ayanokōji&#x27;s C rating<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.49–50<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Realizes the anti-throwing rule is meaningless against the White Room transfer student, who plans to be expelled anyway and would take a 0 without hesitation if paired with him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Concludes he already faces at least a 1-in-160 chance of expulsion; suspects Tsukishiro concocted the rules with a small loophole allowing flexible, biased enforcement, and would expel Ayanokōji without batting an eye if he partnered with someone who didn&#x27;t take the exam seriously.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes his own OAA Academic Ability is a C — he can&#x27;t freely choose a partner, and must avoid the White Room student who may be &quot;lying in wait&quot; for someone with a similar rating; judges this &quot;more challenging than any other special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Certain he devised the rules to target him via the White Room agent.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p44-1\">← Before: Exam rewards, rules, and the expulsion condition<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p57-1\">→ After: The hallway talk with Horikita: reaffirming the bet; OAA strategy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p57-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the hallway talk with horikita  reaffirming the bet  oaa strategy is called out to the hallway by horikita at lunch  who wants to discuss matters unsuitable for the classroom   there are 4 students in our class that have an e rating in academic ability  make that 12 if you include those with d ratings   the question then becomes  how many of the first year honor students can we draw to our side  horikita s count  17 b or higher first years in class a  13 in b  13 in c  11 in d   54 total  the class with the most of these wins  the one stuck with d  or lower loses  recalls the spring break bet  if he wins the written exam subject  horikita joins the student council  if she wins  he must use the abilities he s hidden all year for the class   with a rated students unlikely to top 90  a draw is impossible  readily agrees to settle the bet on this exam  analyzes the oaa data with horikita and expects sakayanagi  ryuen and ichinose to make their first move that day  reaffirms their competition and strategizes in perfect sync  she looks up the oaa numbers and prioritizes the d e rated students  expects her to attack first   class a has the fewest academically weak students  expects him to make a move  expects her to make a move","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The hallway talk with Horikita: reaffirming the bet; OAA strategy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.57–59<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is called out to the hallway by Horikita at lunch, who wants to discuss matters unsuitable for the classroom.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There are 4 students in our class that have an E rating in Academic Ability. Make that 12 if you include those with D ratings.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The question then becomes, how many of the first-year honor students can we draw to our side?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s count: 17 B-or-higher first-years in Class A, 13 in B, 13 in C, 11 in D — 54 total; the class with the most of these wins, the one stuck with D+ or lower loses.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Recalls the spring-break bet: if he wins the written-exam subject, Horikita joins the Student Council; if she wins, he must use the abilities he&#x27;s hidden all year for the class — with A-rated students unlikely to top 90, a draw is impossible.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Readily agrees to settle the bet on this exam; analyzes the OAA data with Horikita and expects Sakayanagi, Ryūen and Ichinose to make their first move that day.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reaffirms their competition and strategizes in perfect sync; she looks up the OAA numbers and prioritizes the D/E-rated students.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Expects her to attack first — Class A has the fewest academically weak students.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Expects him to make a move.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Expects her to make a move.<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p49-1\">← Before: The White Room student threat; Ayanokōji&#x27;s C rating<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.3: Observing and strategizing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p66-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune housen-kazuomi amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  observing and strategizing observes the meet and greet and ichinose s strategy  watches ryuen and hosen confront each other  notes hosen s strength and nanase s control over him  watches yagami greet kushida  negotiates with class 1 d students at keyaki mall  agrees with horikita s three goals  is asked to cook for amasawa s test  agrees to cook for amasawa tomorrow  strategizes with her  observes his confrontation  is set up for her cooking test","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3: Observing and strategizing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.66–141<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Observes the meet-and-greet and Ichinose’s strategy. Watches Ryūen and Hōsen confront each other. Notes Hōsen’s strength and Nanase’s control over him. Watches Yagami greet Kushida. Negotiates with Class 1-D students at Keyaki Mall. Agrees with Horikita’s three goals. Is asked to cook for Amasawa’s test. Agrees to cook for Amasawa tomorrow.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Strategizes with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Observes his confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Is set up for her cooking test.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–141<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p57-1\">← Before: The hallway talk with Horikita: reaffirming the bet; OAA strategy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p67-1\">→ After: The meet-and-greet: reading each class&#x27;s intentions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p67-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the meet and greet  reading each class s intentions attends the gym meet and greet with horikita and sudo  scanning which second years came   sakayanagi absent  only hashimoto from class a  likely recon  about half of class b present  ichinose  kanzaki  nobody from class c  notes sakayanagi s weak legs and limited range of motion   hashimoto compensates for her and is likely her reconnaissance here  ichinose avoids mentioning the special exam  focusing on casual friendship to melt the first years   walls of ice  horikita calls it  a dazzling approach  and admits class d can t replicate it   instead of prioritizing the special exam  she s focusing on building up relationships based on mutual trust   are you thinking of a similar strategy yourself   a strategy based on private points would be too much for our class to handle  from this one gathering he can roughly grasp the intentions of each class  sees the oaa app as horikita s constant companion as she observes first years  gleaning an idea  observes quietly  concedes he horikita sudo can t out socialize class b  that would take hirata or kushida  follows horikita s lead when she decides to leave  her trusting relationship building approach is  dazzling  she is well known and favored by first years  observes her strategizing and accepts her decision to leave the meet and greet  sees him scouting the event for sakayanagi class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The meet-and-greet: reading each class&#x27;s intentions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.67–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Attends the gym meet-and-greet with Horikita and Sudō, scanning which second-years came — Sakayanagi absent, only Hashimoto from Class A (likely recon); about half of Class B present (Ichinose, Kanzaki); nobody from Class C.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Instead of prioritizing the special exam, she&#x27;s focusing on building up relationships based on mutual trust.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you thinking of a similar strategy yourself?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;A strategy based on private points would be too much for our class to handle.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Notes Sakayanagi&#x27;s weak legs and limited range of motion — Hashimoto compensates for her and is likely her reconnaissance here.<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Ichinose avoids mentioning the special exam, focusing on casual friendship to melt the first-years&#x27; &quot;walls of ice&quot;; Horikita calls it &quot;a dazzling approach&quot; and admits Class D can&#x27;t replicate it.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> From this one gathering he can roughly grasp the intentions of each class; sees the OAA app as Horikita&#x27;s constant companion as she observes first-years, gleaning an idea.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Observes quietly, concedes he/Horikita/Sudō can&#x27;t out-socialize Class B (that would take Hirata or Kushida); follows Horikita&#x27;s lead when she decides to leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her trusting relationship-building approach is &quot;dazzling&quot;; she is well-known and favored by first-years.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Observes her strategizing and accepts her decision to leave the meet-and-greet.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Sees him scouting the event for Sakayanagi/Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.67, 74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Observing and strategizing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p71-1\">→ After: Horikita&#x27;s real target: the first-years who didn&#x27;t attend<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p71-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka horikita s real target  the first years who didn t attend  more than half of the students invited to this didn t even attend  those are the students i m going to negotiate with   the students from class 1 d didn t attend the event at all   if there s someone we can negotiate with at the class level  it isn t necessary to try and bargain with people at the individual level  understands none of class 1 d attended  reflecting the will of the class   clear evidence a leader controls it  realizes horikita plans class level cooperation between class 2 d and 1 d  abandoning the inter class competition  notes her strategy is essentially the same as ichinose s  give up class points to prevent expulsions  beneath different approaches  watches hashimoto leave after finishing recon  hashimoto discusses nanase as a possible class 1 d contact","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p71-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Horikita&#x27;s real target: the first-years who didn&#x27;t attend<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.71–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;More than half of the students invited to this didn&#x27;t even attend. Those are the students I&#x27;m going to negotiate with.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;The students from Class 1-D didn&#x27;t attend the event at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;If there&#x27;s someone we can negotiate with at the class level, it isn&#x27;t necessary to try and bargain with people at the individual level.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Understands none of Class 1-D attended, reflecting the will of the class — clear evidence a leader controls it; realizes Horikita plans class-level cooperation between Class 2-D and 1-D, abandoning the inter-class competition.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes her strategy is essentially the same as Ichinose&#x27;s (give up class points to prevent expulsions) beneath different approaches; watches Hashimoto leave after finishing recon.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Hashimoto discusses Nanase as a possible Class 1-D contact.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p67-1\">← Before: The meet-and-greet: reading each class&#x27;s intentions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p77-1\">→ After: The Class 1-D hallway clash: Ryūen, Hōsen, Shiba, Yagami<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p77-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"housen-kazuomi ryuuen-kakeru nanase-tsubasa yagami-takuya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the class 1 d hallway clash  ryuen  hosen  shiba  yagami follows horikita to the first year floor  ryuen appears beside her with a daring look  taunting  you re awfully late  eh suzune  watches hosen and nanase clash with ryuen  hosen offers to let ryuen pair with him only if he prostrates himself  and ryuen retorts that he works only with humans   if you prostrate yourself to me  i suppose i could let you pair up with me  ryuen paisen   sorry  but i only work together with humans  i have no intention of being with a wild gorilla  the eloquent first year  yagami  defuses the situation with a proverb  a wise man keeps away from danger  class 1 d s homeroom teacher shiba katsunori arrives in a suit to break it up  and hosen backs down surprisingly easily  nanase bows an apology and gives ayanokoji an inquisitive  probing look before leaving  ryuen taunts horikita  he and hosen size each other up without coming to blows  the overwhelming first year delinquent  controls class 1 d  she gives him a probing look   as if testing him   then flees after hosen  the eloquent first year who fends off hosen and apologizes on behalf of the first years","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p77-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Class 1-D hallway clash: Ryūen, Hōsen, Shiba, Yagami<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.77–102<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows Horikita to the first-year floor; Ryūen appears beside her with a daring look, taunting &quot;You&#x27;re awfully late, eh Suzune?&quot; Watches Hōsen and Nanase clash with Ryūen; Hōsen offers to let Ryūen pair with him only if he prostrates himself, and Ryūen retorts that he works only with humans.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> &quot;If you prostrate yourself to me, I suppose I could let you pair up with me, Ryūen-paisen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Sorry, but I only work together with humans. I have no intention of being with a wild gorilla.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The eloquent first-year (Yagami) defuses the situation with a proverb (&quot;A wise man keeps away from danger&quot;); Class 1-D&#x27;s homeroom teacher Shiba Katsunori arrives in a suit to break it up, and Hōsen backs down surprisingly easily; Nanase bows an apology and gives Ayanokōji an inquisitive, probing look before leaving.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen taunts Horikita; he and Hōsen size each other up without coming to blows.<span class=\"pg\">p.77–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> The overwhelming first-year delinquent; controls Class 1-D.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She gives him a probing look — as if testing him — then flees after Hōsen.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> The eloquent first-year who fends off Hōsen and apologizes on behalf of the first-years.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p71-1\">← Before: Horikita&#x27;s real target: the first-years who didn&#x27;t attend<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p102-1\">→ After: Yagami reunites with Kushida; the A-rating partnership offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p102-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"yagami-takuya kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka yagami reunites with kushida  the a rating partnership offer watches yagami takuya spot kushida and recognize her from middle school  she genuinely doesn t remember him at first   don t you recognize me  i suppose it s understandable if you don t but  it s me  yagami takuya   i know this is sudden  but if it s you  kushida senpai  then i d have no complaints  would you be willing to partner up with me   would you really be fine with someone like me  you should pair up with someone who s better at studying  yagami kun   i don t know my left from right at this school yet  so i d like to partner with somebody i can trust  wondering whether yagami knows about kushida s middle school past  she destroyed her class  he has an a academic rating and wants someone he can trust  so kushida puts his offer on hold  notes kushida didn t pay attention to classmates she wasn t interested in  a boy could hardly forget someone as eye catching as her  yagami offers to partner with her  she is wary and defers her answer  he asks her if yagami might know kushida s secret  she says there s no guarantee","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p102-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Yagami reunites with Kushida; the A-rating partnership offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.102–106<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches Yagami Takuya spot Kushida and recognize her from middle school; she genuinely doesn&#x27;t remember him at first.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> &quot;Don&#x27;t you recognize me? I suppose it&#x27;s understandable if you don&#x27;t but, it&#x27;s me, Yagami Takuya.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> &quot;I know this is sudden, but if it&#x27;s you, Kushida-senpai, then I&#x27;d have no complaints. Would you be willing to partner up with me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Would you really be fine with someone like me? You should pair up with someone who&#x27;s better at studying, Yagami-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t know my left from right at this school yet, so I&#x27;d like to partner with somebody I can trust.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Wondering whether Yagami knows about Kushida&#x27;s middle-school past (she destroyed her class); he has an A Academic rating and wants someone he can trust, so Kushida puts his offer on hold.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Kushida didn&#x27;t pay attention to classmates she wasn&#x27;t interested in; a boy could hardly forget someone as eye-catching as her.<span class=\"pg\">p.103–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Yagami offers to partner with her; she is wary and defers her answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He asks her if Yagami might know Kushida&#x27;s secret; she says there&#x27;s no guarantee.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p77-1\">← Before: The Class 1-D hallway clash: Ryūen, Hōsen, Shiba, Yagami<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p108-1\">→ After: Miyake&#x27;s account of Hōsen&#x27;s delinquent reputation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p108-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"miyake-akito housen-kazuomi hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka miyake s account of hosen s delinquent reputation joins the ayanokoji group  haruka  akito  keisei  sakura  after hosen s departure  haruka calls hosen  super scary   one hell of a guy just enrolled here  this school might get pretty stormy moving forward   hosen is so strong that sudo and ryuen can t even compare to him   hosen had beaten him to a pulp in a one on one and sent him to the hospital   i m one to choose my opponent before i fight with someone  and there s no way that i d choose to fight hosen  learns akito was a former delinquent  bad temper until second year of middle school  then channelled it into archery  and grew up near the middle schools of ryuen and hosen  akito refuses to fight hosen  acknowledging his strength  his friend  reveals his delinquent past and hosen s fearsome reputation  reputed to have hospitalized a gang leader two years his senior  miyake rates him above sudo and ryuen  calls hosen scary and teases akito about being a delinquent","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Miyake&#x27;s account of Hōsen&#x27;s delinquent reputation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.108–110<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Joins the Ayanokōji group (Haruka, Akito, Keisei, Sakura) after Hōsen&#x27;s departure; Haruka calls Hōsen &quot;super scary.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;One hell of a guy just enrolled here. This school might get pretty stormy moving forward.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;Hōsen is so strong that Sudō and Ryūen can&#x27;t even compare to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;Hōsen had beaten him to a pulp in a one-on-one and sent him to the hospital.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m one to choose my opponent before I fight with someone, and there&#x27;s no way that I&#x27;d choose to fight Hōsen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Learns Akito was a former delinquent (bad temper until second year of middle school, then channelled it into archery) and grew up near the middle schools of Ryūen and Hōsen; Akito refuses to fight Hōsen, acknowledging his strength.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> His friend; reveals his delinquent past and Hōsen&#x27;s fearsome reputation.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Reputed to have hospitalized a gang leader two years his senior; Miyake rates him above Sudō and Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Calls Hōsen scary and teases Akito about being a delinquent.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p102-1\">← Before: Yagami reunites with Kushida; the A-rating partnership offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p111-1\">→ After: Sudō&#x27;s partner search; Shiratori&#x27;s 500,000-point demand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p111-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken shiratori housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudo s partner search  shiratori s 500 000 point demand walks with horikita and sudo to keyaki mall  she avoids the first year floor after the lunchtime trouble and hosen  approaches class 1 d students kaga  mikami and shiratori  b  or higher   we re searching for partners for the upcoming special exam  you guys don t have partners yet  right   500 000  if you give me 500 000 points  i ll happily partner up with you right here  right now    shiratori  it s natural to desire points  but is chasing after short sighted greed really worth it   you guys are in class d  just the same as us  i don t believe the higher ranked classes would ve approached you so easily    a bluff  before you arrived  we were consulted by another class of second year students    shiratori notices all three first years agreed from the start to wait a week  deduces hosen instructed class 1 d to hold out for 500 000 and use the deadline penalty as a weapon to wring maximum points from desperate second years   a reckless strategy disregarding the future  reads the situation sharply   sees shiratori leak the buyout info under horikita s bluff  notes shiratori calls hosen when asked to gather classmates  confirming hosen controls 1 d  and recognizes the point exchange mindset now permeates the first years  likely sakayanagi and ryuen s doing  accompanies her  listens as she negotiates using sudo s a  physical rating as leverage and sets three goals  watches him get ticked off at shiratori s tactful jab about his e  rating and carelessly reveal he lacks 500 000 points  class 1 d a rated first year who demands 500 000 points to partner with sudo  confirmed as the one controlling class 1 d  holding out for maximum points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p111-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sudō&#x27;s partner search; Shiratori&#x27;s 500,000-point demand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.111–123<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks with Horikita and Sudō to Keyaki Mall (she avoids the first-year floor after the lunchtime trouble and Hōsen); approaches Class 1-D students Kaga, Mikami and Shiratori (B− or higher).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"shiratori.html\">Shiratori<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;We&#x27;re searching for partners for the upcoming special exam. You guys don&#x27;t have partners yet, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;500,000. If you give me 500,000 points, I&#x27;ll happily partner up with you right here, right now.&quot; — Shiratori<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s natural to desire points, but is chasing after short-sighted greed really worth it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You guys are in Class D, just the same as us. I don&#x27;t believe the higher-ranked classes would&#x27;ve approached you so easily.&quot; — a bluff<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Before you arrived, we were consulted by another class of second-year students.&quot; — Shiratori<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Notices all three first-years agreed from the start to wait a week; deduces Hōsen instructed Class 1-D to hold out for 500,000 and use the deadline penalty as a weapon to wring maximum points from desperate second-years — a reckless strategy disregarding the future.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the situation sharply — sees Shiratori leak the buyout info under Horikita&#x27;s bluff, notes Shiratori calls Hōsen when asked to gather classmates (confirming Hōsen controls 1-D), and recognizes the point-exchange mindset now permeates the first-years (likely Sakayanagi and Ryūen&#x27;s doing).<span class=\"pg\">p.111–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accompanies her; listens as she negotiates using Sudō&#x27;s A+ physical rating as leverage and sets three goals.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Watches him get ticked off at Shiratori&#x27;s tactful jab about his E+ rating and carelessly reveal he lacks 500,000 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiratori<\/b> Class 1-D A-rated first-year who demands 500,000 points to partner with Sudō.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Confirmed as the one controlling Class 1-D, holding out for maximum points.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p108-1\">← Before: Miyake&#x27;s account of Hōsen&#x27;s delinquent reputation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p122-1\">→ After: Horikita&#x27;s three goals<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p122-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka horikita s three goals  the most important one is to not let anyone get expelled   the next is that we try to get third place or higher in the overall class ranking   the third is to avoid participating in any monetary exchanges  reasons that even first place yields only 50 class points   just over 2 million points spread across the year   not worth spending the class s entire reserve  sets principled goals  no expulsions  third place or higher  no monetary exchanges   declining to fight a points bidding war","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p122-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Horikita&#x27;s three goals<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.122–123<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;The most important one is to not let anyone get expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;The next is that we try to get third place or higher in the overall class ranking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;The third is to avoid participating in any monetary exchanges.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Reasons that even first place yields only 50 class points — just over 2 million points spread across the year — not worth spending the class&#x27;s entire reserve.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sets principled goals: no expulsions, third place or higher, no monetary exchanges — declining to fight a points bidding war.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–123<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p111-1\">← Before: Sudō&#x27;s partner search; Shiratori&#x27;s 500,000-point demand<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p142-1\">→ After: Ch.4: White Room threat and Amasawa test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p142-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"nanase-tsubasa horikita-suzune amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  white room threat and amasawa test reflects on the white room enforcer threat  is approached by nanase on the way to school  discusses cooperation with nanase  reports to horikita and discusses class 1 d strategy  cooks tom yum goong for amasawa using a wireless earpiece  learns amasawa will partner with sudo  reflects on amasawa and the white room threat  is approached by her  discusses strategy with her  cooks for her test","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p142-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4: White Room threat and Amasawa test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.142–193<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reflects on the White Room enforcer threat. Is approached by Nanase on the way to school. Discusses cooperation with Nanase. Reports to Horikita and discusses Class 1-D strategy. Cooks tom yum goong for Amasawa using a wireless earpiece. Learns Amasawa will partner with Sudō. Reflects on Amasawa and the White Room threat.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Is approached by her.<span class=\"pg\">p.148–155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses strategy with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Cooks for her test.<span class=\"pg\">p.160–189<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p122-1\">← Before: Horikita&#x27;s three goals<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p143-1\">→ After: The partner-formation race; narrowing down the White Room agent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p143-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"tsukishiro ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the partner formation race  narrowing down the white room agent on day three  checks the 8 am oaa refresh   56 pairs formed of a maximum 157  class 2 b  ichinose  drove pairings  and not a single class 1 d student has paired up  reasons that first years see classmates as rivals and will leave him  a c rating  until the high rated students are taken  concludes tsukishiro s enforcer is waiting for him to hesitate  so any student who approaches him is a  big red flag  works through ways to identify the white room agent   physique  white room children can t be obese  but the agent could have gained lost weight  academic rating  they could deliberately hold an e  class affiliation  no help    and concludes there s no way to narrow the list  decides to investigate every first year with his own eyes and reach out to all he meets  knows the enforcer is instructed to pair with him to expel him  assumes ordinary students may also be bribed with college admission  credits her class with driving most of the pairings","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p143-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The partner-formation race; narrowing down the White Room agent<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.143–147<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On day three, checks the 8 AM OAA refresh — 56 pairs formed of a maximum 157; Class 2-B (Ichinose) drove pairings, and not a single Class 1-D student has paired up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons that first-years see classmates as rivals and will leave him (a C rating) until the high-rated students are taken; concludes Tsukishiro&#x27;s enforcer is waiting for him to hesitate, so any student who approaches him is a &quot;big red flag.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143–147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Works through ways to identify the White Room agent — physique (White Room children can&#x27;t be obese, but the agent could have gained/lost weight), academic rating (they could deliberately hold an E), class affiliation (no help) — and concludes there&#x27;s no way to narrow the list; decides to investigate every first-year with his own eyes and reach out to all he meets.<span class=\"pg\">p.144–147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Knows the enforcer is instructed to pair with him to expel him; assumes ordinary students may also be bribed with college admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.144–147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Credits her class with driving most of the pairings.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p142-1\">← Before: Ch.4: White Room threat and Amasawa test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p148-1\">→ After: Testing Nanase on the morning walk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p148-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka testing nanase on the morning walk walks to school and is called out by nanase tsubasa   certain she timed her approach  since no first year would speak to him by coincidence   good morning to you  ayanokoji senpai   do you need something from those two  would you like me to call out to them for you   have you decided on your partner for this special exam yet   my apologies  but i m unable to answer that   if it s okay with you  how about we have our fellow d classes work together to find suitable partners for each other   i am in agreement  as much as possible  i would like to cooperate with you  ayanokoji senpai   hosen  wasn t it  it seems like that guy s got a lot of influence over class 1 d  huh  nanase has a b academic rating with all other ratings c  or better   an  ideal partner    and still unpaired on day three  likely class 1 d s plan  he wonders why someone so well rounded was placed in class d  suspecting a latent  problem  notes her earlier probing gaze is now gone   completely natural    doesn t know if she s the white room agent  probes her gently  why unpaired  hosen s influence  while offering d class cooperation  testing her authenticity  tests her as a possible white room enforcer  she agrees in principle to cooperate but is hesitant about her classmates and the top 30  reward  brings him up to probe nanase s knowledge of class 1 d s control","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Testing Nanase on the morning walk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.148–152<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks to school and is called out by Nanase Tsubasa — certain she timed her approach, since no first-year would speak to him by coincidence.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Good morning to you, Ayanokōji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Do you need something from those two? Would you like me to call out to them for you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Have you decided on your partner for this special exam yet?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;My apologies, but I&#x27;m unable to answer that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If it&#x27;s okay with you, how about we have our fellow D Classes work together to find suitable partners for each other?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I am in agreement. As much as possible, I would like to cooperate with you, Ayanokōji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hōsen… wasn&#x27;t it? It seems like that guy&#x27;s got a lot of influence over Class 1-D, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Nanase has a B Academic rating with all other ratings C+ or better — an &quot;ideal partner&quot; — and still unpaired on day three (likely Class 1-D&#x27;s plan); he wonders why someone so well-rounded was placed in Class D, suspecting a latent &quot;problem.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Notes her earlier probing gaze is now gone, &quot;completely natural&quot; — doesn&#x27;t know if she&#x27;s the White Room agent; probes her gently (why unpaired, Hōsen&#x27;s influence) while offering D-Class cooperation, testing her authenticity.<span class=\"pg\">p.148–152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Tests her as a possible White Room enforcer; she agrees in principle to cooperate but is hesitant about her classmates and the top-30% reward.<span class=\"pg\">p.148–152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Brings him up to probe Nanase&#x27;s knowledge of Class 1-D&#x27;s control.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p143-1\">← Before: The partner-formation race; narrowing down the White Room agent<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p176-1\">→ After: The Amasawa cooking test: tom yum goong via earpiece<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p176-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the amasawa cooking test  tom yum goong via earpiece brings amasawa ichika and groceries back to his room  she sets strict rules   no phone  a dish made from memory   and tasks him with tom yum goong   anyway  i m super picky about taste  if it s not yummy enough  the deal s off  okay   oh  looking up anything on your phone is against the rules  okay   the dish you re gonna make is  tom yum goong   could you make it for me  please  seeenpai   your tom yum goong  yeah  i guess it was just barely good enough   i ll pair up with sudo senpai  outta respect for your efforts  had horikita teach him knife techniques  slicing  shredding  dicing  chopping  overnight   not recipes  hides a  2cm wireless earpiece  with horikita feeding him recipe steps in real time from her room via sudo s phone  held in his bag  and plans discrete signals  places the phone on his bed and leaves the tv on as cover  leaves out cilantro deliberately  ayanokoji serves the dish and peels an apple with a petty knife to demonstrate skill  amasawa eats every bite  calls it  just barely good enough  and cleans the kitchen meticulously  carefully orchestrates every detail   seats her where she can see but with the tv distraction  anticipates her rules  and uses the earpiece to compensate for lacking recipe knowledge  still can t tell if she s the white room agent  cooks for her to win sudo a partner  finds her speech and conduct hard to fake for a white room dropout but remains suspicious of select quirks  her real time earpiece instructions make the cooking possible  they debrief afterward  his phone is used for the relay  amasawa submits a partnership application to him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p176-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Amasawa cooking test: tom yum goong via earpiece<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.176–188<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Brings Amasawa Ichika and groceries back to his room; she sets strict rules — no phone, a dish made from memory — and tasks him with tom yum goong.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;Anyway, I&#x27;m super picky about taste~ If it&#x27;s not yummy enough, the deal&#x27;s off, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;Oh, looking up anything on your phone is against the rules, okay~?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;The dish you&#x27;re gonna make is… tom yum goong!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Could you make it for me~? Please, Seeenpai~?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Your tom yum goong—… Yeah, I guess it was just barely good enough.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll pair up with Sudō-senpai, outta respect for your efforts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Had Horikita teach him knife techniques (slicing, shredding, dicing, chopping) overnight — not recipes; hides a &lt;2cm wireless earpiece, with Horikita feeding him recipe steps in real time from her room via Sudō&#x27;s phone (held in his bag), and plans discrete signals; places the phone on his bed and leaves the TV on as cover.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Leaves out cilantro deliberately; Ayanokōji serves the dish and peels an apple with a Petty knife to demonstrate skill; Amasawa eats every bite, calls it &quot;just barely good enough,&quot; and cleans the kitchen meticulously.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Carefully orchestrates every detail — seats her where she can see but with the TV distraction, anticipates her rules, and uses the earpiece to compensate for lacking recipe knowledge; still can&#x27;t tell if she&#x27;s the White Room agent.<span class=\"pg\">p.176–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Cooks for her to win Sudō a partner; finds her speech and conduct hard to fake for a White Room dropout but remains suspicious of select quirks.<span class=\"pg\">p.176–189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her real-time earpiece instructions make the cooking possible; they debrief afterward.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His phone is used for the relay; Amasawa submits a partnership application to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p148-1\">← Before: Testing Nanase on the morning walk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p188-1\">→ After: The debrief with Horikita; hiding the Class 1-A strategy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p188-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the debrief with horikita  hiding the class 1 a strategy  i get the feeling that we were saved by amasawa s merciful judgment  though   it was just a formality   neither of us know what kind of person that amasawa girl really is   your way of thinking is  how do i put it  extremely calculated  and yet clever  explains he asked amasawa to be an intermediary only as a  formality    acting as if grasping at straws so she won t realize class 2 d gave up on class 1 a from the start and never intended to win the competition  horikita notes his thinking has changed   he now shares specifics he wouldn t have before  he stays guarded  deciding to be suspicious of any student who comes close  noting hosen and nanase locked eyes with him first  and rules out already paired students only tentatively  praises his cleverness and asks what changed in him  he deflects  receives her message   may we meet up after school tomorrow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p188-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The debrief with Horikita; hiding the Class 1-A strategy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.188–193<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I get the feeling that we were saved by Amasawa&#x27;s merciful judgment, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It was just a formality.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Neither of us know what kind of person that Amasawa girl really is.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Your way of thinking is… How do I put it…? Extremely calculated, and yet clever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Explains he asked Amasawa to be an intermediary only as a &quot;formality&quot; — acting as if grasping at straws so she won&#x27;t realize Class 2-D gave up on Class 1-A from the start and never intended to win the competition.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Horikita notes his thinking has changed — he now shares specifics he wouldn&#x27;t have before; he stays guarded, deciding to be suspicious of any student who comes close (noting Hōsen and Nanase locked eyes with him first), and rules out already-paired students only tentatively.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Praises his cleverness and asks what changed in him; he deflects.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Receives her message: &quot;[May we meet up after school tomorrow?]&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p176-1\">← Before: The Amasawa cooking test: tom yum goong via earpiece<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p204-1\">→ After: Ch.5: Nanase, Amasawa, and partners<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p204-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"nanase-tsubasa sakayanagi-arisu tsubaki-sakurako utomiya-riku ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  nanase  amasawa  and partners meets nanase in the library  is tested by nanase  learns class 1 d has 800 class points  reflects on partner odds and white room threat  meets sakayanagi at keyaki mall  meets tsubaki and utomiya  declines their offer but keeps contact  meets her in the library  speaks with her  meets her  meets him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p204-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5: Nanase, Amasawa, and partners<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.204–269<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Nanase in the library. Is tested by Nanase. Learns Class 1-D has 800 class points. Reflects on partner odds and White Room threat. Meets Sakayanagi at Keyaki Mall. Meets Tsubaki and Utomiya. Declines their offer but keeps contact.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Meets her in the library.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Speaks with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.259–261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> Meets her.<span class=\"pg\">p.268–275<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> Meets him.<span class=\"pg\">p.268–275<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p188-1\">← Before: The debrief with Horikita; hiding the Class 1-A strategy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p205-1\">→ After: Library: the Class 1-D negotiation begins<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p205-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori nanase-tsubasa horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka library  the class 1 d negotiation begins brings horikita to the library to meet the class 1 d students nanase is bringing  en route  notes 17 more pairs  73 total  and that two class 1 d students finally paired   reading it as hosen s orders a gag order   i m a little annoyed  i thought hosen kun would wait and see how the situation developed for a little while longer    horikita  there s a fine line between them actually not knowing anything and them having a gag order in place  hiyori  in the library  thoughtfully suggests the far end seats so they won t disturb patrons and can spot anyone approaching  ayanokoji is vaguely concerned about her  ryuen s class  nanase arrives alone  hosen not with her  she fumbles her self introduction  starting with the masculine  boku  before correcting to  watashi   a detail flagged by the translation  sees in nanase an honest  straightforward  upright personality  that reminded me of ichinose  stays alert to whether hosen will appear  and suspects the two class 1 d pairings were bought with large points  she advises them on seating  he notes her situation with concern  the negotiation with her  her upright honesty and  i will never yield to violence  conviction impress him despite suspicion about her identity  they probe whether the other has been studying for their bet  each worries the other is neglecting it to use as an excuse","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Library: the Class 1-D negotiation begins<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.205–215<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Brings Horikita to the library to meet the Class 1-D students Nanase is bringing; en route, notes 17 more pairs (73 total) and that two Class 1-D students finally paired — reading it as Hōsen&#x27;s orders/a gag order.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m a little annoyed. I thought Hōsen-kun would wait and see how the situation developed for a little while longer.&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s a fine line between them actually not knowing anything and them having a gag order in place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hiyori, in the library, thoughtfully suggests the far-end seats so they won&#x27;t disturb patrons and can spot anyone approaching; Ayanokōji is vaguely concerned about her (Ryūen&#x27;s class).<span class=\"pg\">p.206–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Nanase arrives alone (Hōsen not with her); she fumbles her self-introduction, starting with the masculine &quot;Boku&quot; before correcting to &quot;Watashi&quot; (a detail flagged by the translation).<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees in Nanase an honest, straightforward, upright personality &quot;that reminded me of Ichinose&quot;; stays alert to whether Hōsen will appear, and suspects the two Class 1-D pairings were bought with large points.<span class=\"pg\">p.205–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> She advises them on seating; he notes her situation with concern.<span class=\"pg\">p.206–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> The negotiation with her; her upright honesty and &quot;I will never yield to violence&quot; conviction impress him despite suspicion about her identity.<span class=\"pg\">p.205–215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> They probe whether the other has been studying for their bet; each worries the other is neglecting it to use as an excuse.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p204-1\">← Before: Ch.5: Nanase, Amasawa, and partners<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p209-1\">→ After: Nanase confirms Hōsen&#x27;s control; the 15-pair proposal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p209-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa horikita-suzune housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase confirms hosen s control  the 15 pair proposal  many students have already begun taking action in accordance with hosen kun s orders   an act of betrayal   you re not afraid of hosen kun  nanase san   yes    an immediate  unfazed answer  at this point  i believe that approximately fifteen students would find it difficult to search for a partner on their own   i m hoping that you and i can decide on a combination of fifteen sets of partners and get this over with all at once   hosen kun would never allow us to help you out for free  especially not now   the only thing i know for sure is that hosen isn t just collecting points for himself  reasons hosen isn t hoarding points personally   if he were  he d actively help low rated classmates find partners  concludes he imposes rules to control the class  not for profit  is struck by nanase s fearless resolve and the  same look  in her eyes  as when she vowed never to yield to violence  recognizes she may be the only one able to bring class 1 d over  negotiates with her  she confirms hosen controls the class and that most struggling students are c d rated  making equal pairing difficult  nanase confirms he orders the class and takes no compensation   pure control","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p209-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase confirms Hōsen&#x27;s control; the 15-pair proposal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.209–214<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Many students have already begun taking action in accordance with Hōsen-kun&#x27;s orders.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;an act of betrayal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re not afraid of Hōsen-kun, Nanase-san?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes.&quot; — an immediate, unfazed answer<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;At this point, I believe that approximately fifteen students would find it difficult to search for a partner on their own.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m hoping that you and I can decide on a combination of fifteen sets of partners and get this over with all at once.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hōsen-kun would never allow us to help you out for free. Especially not now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The only thing I know for sure is that Hōsen isn&#x27;t just collecting points for himself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons Hōsen isn&#x27;t hoarding points personally — if he were, he&#x27;d actively help low-rated classmates find partners; concludes he imposes rules to control the class, not for profit.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Is struck by Nanase&#x27;s fearless resolve and the &quot;same look&quot; in her eyes (as when she vowed never to yield to violence); recognizes she may be the only one able to bring Class 1-D over.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Negotiates with her; she confirms Hōsen controls the class and that most struggling students are C/D-rated, making equal pairing difficult.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Nanase confirms he orders the class and takes no compensation — pure control.<span class=\"pg\">p.209–214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p205-1\">← Before: Library: the Class 1-D negotiation begins<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p246-1\">→ After: Tutoring Kei; revealing his intended 400-point score<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p246-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ishigami-kyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka tutoring kei  revealing his intended 400 point score administers five 10 minute diagnostic test sheets  created by keisei  to karuizawa in his room to gauge her abilities  after 50 minutes she collapses  exhausted   you ll definitely be attending yosuke s study sessions starting tomorrow   if you don t study  you ll only be a stone s throw from being expelled   you need to score 501 points to pass this special exam   you re like this with your fighting skills too   i don t want to stand out  so i don t put in the effort with my grades   400 points   the equivalent of an a rating in academic ability   there hasn t been a problem i couldn t solve ever since i enrolled here  diagnoses kei as capable but held back by her bullying interrupted middle school education  tells her he intends to score 400  an a equivalent  in the exam   saving one subject for his bet with horikita   and assures her no problem at the school has ever stumped him  tutors her into hirata s study sessions  she questions why he hides his abilities  uses keisei s diagnostic sheets","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tutoring Kei; revealing his intended 400-point score<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.246–249<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Administers five 10-minute diagnostic test sheets (created by Keisei) to Karuizawa in his room to gauge her abilities; after 50 minutes she collapses, exhausted.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;ll definitely be attending Yōsuke&#x27;s study sessions starting tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;if you don&#x27;t study, you&#x27;ll only be a stone&#x27;s throw from being expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You need to score 501 points to pass this special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re like this with your fighting skills too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t want to stand out, so I don&#x27;t put in the effort with my grades.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;400 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The equivalent of an A rating in Academic Ability.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There hasn&#x27;t been a problem I couldn&#x27;t solve ever since I enrolled here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Diagnoses Kei as capable but held back by her bullying-interrupted middle-school education; tells her he intends to score 400 (an A-equivalent) in the exam — saving one subject for his bet with Horikita — and assures her no problem at the school has ever stumped him.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Tutors her into Hirata&#x27;s study sessions; she questions why he hides his abilities.<span class=\"pg\">p.246–249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Uses Keisei&#x27;s diagnostic sheets.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p209-1\">← Before: Nanase confirms Hōsen&#x27;s control; the 15-pair proposal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p252-1\">→ After: The red hair; Amasawa&#x27;s interruption<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p252-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"narration spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the red hair  amasawa s interruption studies with kei  she finds a long red strand of hair on the floor  and the intercom shows amasawa at the lobby   kei  furious  lets her up to confirm the hair s owner   a red hair  a freaking long hair at that   who did you have over   is this that one thing  jealousy   i m your girlfriend kiyotaka  i have the right to stick my nose in all sorts of stuff   girlfriend   ayanokoji senpai is my  how should i put it  my exclusive  personal chef  realizes he must clean thoroughly after inviting girls over  manages the situation by letting amasawa search for her lost hair tie  keeping kei quiet with a finger to her lips  and re explaining the cooking  notes he learned kei wants their relationship kept secret yet nearly exposed it  his girlfriend   fiercely jealous over the red hair  he tutors her and calms her  shows up unannounced looking for a hair tie  teases that he has a  cute girlfriend  and proposes they all eat together next time","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The red hair; Amasawa&#x27;s interruption<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.252–260<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Studies with Kei; she finds a long red strand of hair on the floor, and the intercom shows Amasawa at the lobby — Kei, furious, lets her up to confirm the hair&#x27;s owner.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;A red hair! A freaking long hair at that!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;Who did you have over!?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is this that one thing? Jealousy…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m your girlfriend Kiyotaka! I have the right to stick my nose in all sorts of stuff!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Girlfriend?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Ayanokōji-senpai is my… How should I put it… My exclusive, personal chef?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Realizes he must clean thoroughly after inviting girls over; manages the situation by letting Amasawa search for her lost hair tie, keeping Kei quiet with a finger to her lips, and re-explaining the cooking; notes he learned Kei wants their relationship kept secret yet nearly exposed it.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend — fiercely jealous over the red hair; he tutors her and calms her.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Shows up unannounced looking for a hair tie; teases that he has a &quot;cute girlfriend&quot; and proposes they all eat together next time.<span class=\"pg\">p.255–260<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p246-1\">← Before: Tutoring Kei; revealing his intended 400-point score<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p261-1\">→ After: The week in review; Sakayanagi&#x27;s warning and offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p261-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the week in review  sakayanagi s warning and offer reviews the week  105 pairs  70  formed  class 1 a leaderless with 34 40 paired  1 b 33 40  1 d  hosen s iron fist  only 8  1 c secretly saved by ichinose s meet and greet  a hidden mediator  realizes the white room enforcer gives off  no scent  and blending in is their weapon  recalls he himself once put on a  slightly impertinent student  act before reverting to his true self   his opponent is different  hiding identity on purpose   it seems you ve been quite proactive about interacting with the first year students recently  ayanokoji kun   the white room might send somebody  an enforcer of sorts to infiltrate the first year students   they may even be willing to expose your true abilities to everyone   i ve decided to abandon my old way of thinking  i don t plan on hiding anything from now on   if you still haven t found a partner yet  how about i help you out and save you some time   i acknowledge your abilities  but i ll decide my own fate for myself  sakayanagi sees through him but he declines her offer of  safe  partners  choosing to decide his own fate  his top priority is continuing his school life  so he abandons hiding his abilities  she warns him about the enforcer and offers help  knowing he needs to decide soon  he refuses  and she looks forward to their rematch   she never believed he d be expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p261-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The week in review; Sakayanagi&#x27;s warning and offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.261–267<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reviews the week: 105 pairs (70%) formed; Class 1-A leaderless with 34/40 paired, 1-B 33/40, 1-D (Hōsen&#x27;s iron fist) only 8, 1-C secretly saved by Ichinose&#x27;s meet-and-greet (a hidden mediator).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;It seems you&#x27;ve been quite proactive about interacting with the first-year students recently, Ayanokōji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;the White Room might send somebody… an enforcer of sorts to infiltrate the first-year students.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;they may even be willing to expose your true abilities to everyone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Realizes the White Room enforcer gives off &quot;no scent&quot; and blending in is their weapon; recalls he himself once put on a &quot;slightly impertinent student&quot; act before reverting to his true self — his opponent is different, hiding identity on purpose.<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ve decided to abandon my old way of thinking. I don&#x27;t plan on hiding anything from now on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you still haven&#x27;t found a partner yet, how about I help you out and save you some time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I acknowledge your abilities, but I&#x27;ll decide my own fate for myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sakayanagi sees through him but he declines her offer of &quot;safe&quot; partners, choosing to decide his own fate; his top priority is continuing his school life, so he abandons hiding his abilities.<span class=\"pg\">p.265–267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She warns him about the enforcer and offers help, knowing he needs to decide soon; he refuses, and she looks forward to their rematch — she never believed he&#x27;d be expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.265–267<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p252-1\">← Before: The red hair; Amasawa&#x27;s interruption<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p286-1\">→ After: Ch.6: Self-stabbing and conditions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p286-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"housen-kazuomi horikita-suzune sudou-ken nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6  self stabbing and conditions lets the knife pierce his palm to expose hosen s plan  explains hosen s framing plan  imposes two conditions  equal cooperation and partnership  calls chabashira for help  learns about the 20 million point bounty  confronts him  negotiates with him  protects horikita with him  hears her explanation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p286-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6: Self-stabbing and conditions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.286–343<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lets the knife pierce his palm to expose Hōsen’s plan. Explains Hōsen’s framing plan. Imposes two conditions: equal cooperation and partnership. Calls Chabashira for help. Learns about the 20-million-point bounty.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Confronts him.<span class=\"pg\">p.290–331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Negotiates with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–343<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Protects Horikita with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.286–343<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Hears her explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.333–335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p261-1\">← Before: The week in review; Sakayanagi&#x27;s warning and offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p287-1\">→ After: Preparing for the Hōsen meeting; the Karaoke parlor plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p287-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka preparing for the hosen meeting  the karaoke parlor plan on sunday near 8 30 p m  heads with horikita  and sudo  whom he backed so he can act if things turn violent  to the karaoke parlor   chosen for its privacy and the stage it sets   if i confess to her right now  d ya think suzune would accept it    sudo  probably not   say you put in all the effort and become the most distinguished student in our class  and yet  horikita still doesn t look at you  what would you do then  recognizes hosen as both crisis and opportunity   he won t be swayed by class a s brand  points  or ichinose s trust  so class d has a chance  wants hosen as a partner because his  problematic behavior  means he doesn t need to stand out  ideal if he were tsukishiro s enforcer  observes sudo s genuine growth   aiming for 250  points  e c  diligent  no longer late  proud of solving problems and of suzune s praise  tests his resolve and finds it real  backs his joining the meeting as a backup  tests his feelings for horikita  goes early to the karaoke room with her  she stages the half finished drinks food to look as though they d been enjoying themselves  to deny hosen the satisfaction of thinking they waited anxiously","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p287-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Preparing for the Hōsen meeting; the Karaoke parlor plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.287–292<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On Sunday near 8:30 p.m., heads with Horikita (and Sudō, whom he backed so he can act if things turn violent) to the karaoke parlor — chosen for its privacy and the stage it sets.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I confess to her right now, d&#x27;ya think Suzune would accept it?&quot; — Sudō<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Probably not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Say you put in all the effort and become the most distinguished student in our class… and yet, Horikita still doesn&#x27;t look at you. What would you do then?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Recognizes Hōsen as both crisis and opportunity — he won&#x27;t be swayed by Class A&#x27;s brand, points, or Ichinose&#x27;s trust, so Class D has a chance; wants Hōsen as a partner because his &quot;problematic behavior&quot; means he doesn&#x27;t need to stand out (ideal if he were Tsukishiro&#x27;s enforcer).<span class=\"pg\">p.287–292<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Observes Sudō&#x27;s genuine growth — aiming for 250+ points (E→C), diligent, no longer late, proud of solving problems and of Suzune&#x27;s praise; tests his resolve and finds it real.<span class=\"pg\">p.288–291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Backs his joining the meeting as a backup; tests his feelings for Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.288–291<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Goes early to the karaoke room with her; she stages the half-finished drinks/food to look as though they&#x27;d been enjoying themselves, to deny Hōsen the satisfaction of thinking they waited anxiously.<span class=\"pg\">p.287–292<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p286-1\">← Before: Ch.6: Self-stabbing and conditions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p296-1\">→ After: The negotiation turns violent; Hōsen&#x27;s knife plot exposed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p296-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"narration spoken","w":"housen-kazuomi nanase-tsubasa amasawa-ichika sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the negotiation turns violent  hosen s knife plot exposed at the karaoke room  hosen arrives with nanase  slouches across three seats  and demands  equal  cooperation while treating class 1 d as his property   so  from what nanase s told me  sounds like you lot want my class to help ya out   it s slightly different from that  we re looking to have our two classes collaborate with each other  there would be no difference in status between us  a relationship of equality so to speak   five million points  that much  and all your problems ll go away   if you submit to me right here  right now  an  fork over the points  i ll let ayanokoji live   you were going to stab yourself in the thigh with my own knife  after that  you d raise a fuss to the school about your injury  and use that as evidence to get me expelled  that was your plan  wasn t it  hosen sucker punches sudo  who turned away at horikita s distress  slaps horikita  then draws a knife  ayanokoji charges in and deliberately lets the blade pierce his own palm   stopping hosen from using the knife on himself to frame him  he reveals he bought the only such petty knife  and that amasawa helped refine the plot  deduced the pseudo special exam s premise  expel him for 20 million points  and that hosen s  knife  was the very one ayanokoji bought   held blade up and reverse gripped to drive into his own thigh  by getting stabbed himself he turns the trap back on hosen  whose fingerprints plus the prior purchase attempt ensure his own expulsion if exposed  calm under a knife    lowered my stance  rushed the opponent rather than flee  accepted a self inflicted wound as  the best way to completely shut you down  spares hosen in exchange for equal cooperation and partnership with him  outsmarts and physically bests him  then offers him a deal   equal class cooperation plus himself as partner  leveraging hosen s pride  claims ryuen is better  to keep him compliant  she intervenes to stop hosen s knife  reveals the whole meeting was a ploy from the start  and later explains the 20 million point bounty  identifies her as the one who refined hosen s knife plot   she stopped him buying the knife at the mall and later used a supposed lost hair tie as an excuse to retrieve it from his room  hosen s blow leaves him nearly fainting  he recovers  and is relieved proud of ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p296-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The negotiation turns violent; Hōsen&#x27;s knife plot exposed<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.296–320<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the karaoke room, Hōsen arrives with Nanase, slouches across three seats, and demands &quot;equal&quot; cooperation while treating Class 1-D as his property.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> &quot;So? From what Nanase&#x27;s told me, sounds like you lot want my class to help ya out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s slightly different from that. We&#x27;re looking to have our two classes collaborate with each other. There would be no difference in status between us, a relationship of equality so to speak.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> &quot;Five million points. That much, and all your problems&#x27;ll go away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.322<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you submit to me right here, right now, an&#x27; fork over the points─ I&#x27;ll let Ayanokōji live.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.325<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;You were going to stab yourself in the thigh with my own knife. After that, you&#x27;d raise a fuss to the school about your injury, and use that as evidence to get me expelled. That was your plan, wasn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.331<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hōsen sucker-punches Sudō (who turned away at Horikita&#x27;s distress), slaps Horikita, then draws a knife. Ayanokōji charges in and deliberately lets the blade pierce his own palm — stopping Hōsen from using the knife on himself to frame him; he reveals he bought the only such Petty knife, and that Amasawa helped refine the plot.<span class=\"pg\">p.321–330<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Deduced the pseudo-special exam&#x27;s premise (expel him for 20 million points) and that Hōsen&#x27;s &quot;knife&quot; was the very one Ayanokōji bought — held blade-up and reverse-gripped to drive into his own thigh; by getting stabbed himself he turns the trap back on Hōsen, whose fingerprints plus the prior purchase attempt ensure his own expulsion if exposed.<span class=\"pg\">p.329–335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm under a knife — &quot;lowered my stance,&quot; rushed the opponent rather than flee, accepted a self-inflicted wound as &quot;the best way to completely shut you down&quot;; spares Hōsen in exchange for equal cooperation and partnership with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.329–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Outsmarts and physically bests him, then offers him a deal — equal class cooperation plus himself as partner, leveraging Hōsen&#x27;s pride (claims Ryūen is better) to keep him compliant.<span class=\"pg\">p.296–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She intervenes to stop Hōsen&#x27;s knife, reveals the whole meeting was a ploy from the start, and later explains the 20-million-point bounty.<span class=\"pg\">p.326–328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Identifies her as the one who refined Hōsen&#x27;s knife plot — she stopped him buying the knife at the mall and later used a supposed lost hair tie as an excuse to retrieve it from his room.<span class=\"pg\">p.334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Hōsen&#x27;s blow leaves him nearly fainting; he recovers, and is relieved/proud of Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.321–338<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p287-1\">← Before: Preparing for the Hōsen meeting; the Karaoke parlor plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p338-1\">→ After: Aftermath: the knife stays in; Nanase&#x27;s 20-million reveal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p338-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka aftermath  the knife stays in  nanase s 20 million reveal  no  i know it isn t exactly pleasant to look at  but it s better to leave the knife where it is for now   we were told that the student who manages to expel ayanokoji kiyotaka of class 2 d will receive a bulk sum of 20 million private points  that s the special exam that was given to us   for the sake of my class  of class 1 d  i chose to cooperate with hosen kun knowing full well just how awful his methods truly were   i  simply didn t believe a person like you would be suitable for this school  ayanokoji senpai  refuses to let horikita pull the knife out  risk of hemorrhaging  tells the others not to worry  nanase uses the masculine katakana  boku  in her final line   the translation s notes flag a deliberate link to ayanokoji s own unusual first person pronoun  keeps calm with a knife through his hand  accepts nanase s bare minimum explanation  and is left puzzling over her undisguised hatred   the white room agent s true motive still hidden  she loses her cool at the sight of the knife and presses nanase for answers  he calms her  she reveals the 20 million bounty and that she cooperated for class 1 d s sake   then directs a sudden  unexplained hatred at him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p338-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Aftermath: the knife stays in; Nanase&#x27;s 20-million reveal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.338–341<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No. I know it isn&#x27;t exactly pleasant to look at, but it&#x27;s better to leave the knife where it is for now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.338<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;We were told that the student who manages to expel Ayanokōji Kiyotaka of Class 2-D will receive a bulk sum of 20 million private points. That&#x27;s the special exam that was given to us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.340<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;For the sake of my class, of Class 1-D, I chose to cooperate with Hōsen-kun knowing full well just how awful his methods truly were.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.341<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I*… simply didn&#x27;t believe a person like you would be suitable for this school, Ayanokōji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.341<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Refuses to let Horikita pull the knife out (risk of hemorrhaging); tells the others not to worry. Nanase uses the masculine katakana &quot;boku&quot; in her final line — the translation&#x27;s notes flag a deliberate link to Ayanokōji&#x27;s own unusual first-person pronoun.<span class=\"pg\">p.338<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps calm with a knife through his hand; accepts Nanase&#x27;s bare-minimum explanation, and is left puzzling over her undisguised hatred — the White Room agent&#x27;s true motive still hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.338–341<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She loses her cool at the sight of the knife and presses Nanase for answers; he calms her.<span class=\"pg\">p.338–341<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She reveals the 20-million bounty and that she cooperated for Class 1-D&#x27;s sake — then directs a sudden, unexplained hatred at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.340–341<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p296-1\">← Before: The negotiation turns violent; Hōsen&#x27;s knife plot exposed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p344-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Perfect score and Tsukishiro<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p344-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  perfect score and tsukishiro scores a perfect 100 in math  explains he deliberately showed his ability  is interrupted by chabashira  meets tsukishiro and learns the enforcer disobeyed orders  is warned the enforcer is acting independently  is called by her  meets him and learns the truth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p344-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Perfect score and Tsukishiro<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.344–357<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Scores a perfect 100 in math. Explains he deliberately showed his ability. Is interrupted by Chabashira. Meets Tsukishiro and learns the enforcer disobeyed orders. Is warned the enforcer is acting independently.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Is called by her.<span class=\"pg\">p.349–352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Meets him and learns the truth.<span class=\"pg\">p.352–357<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p338-1\">← Before: Aftermath: the knife stays in; Nanase&#x27;s 20-million reveal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p345-1\">→ After: After the knife; the results and the perfect math score<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p345-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka after the knife  the results and the perfect math score on monday tuesday  nanase and horikita finalize the inter class agreement  all 157 pairs formed  koenji unexpectedly agrees to partner with nanase  his bandaged hand is kept confidential by chabashira and mashima  still can t identify the white room student  reconsiders everyone   hosen could be an imposter who took the real hosen s identity  ryuen and akito never met him in person  nanase s method of approaching him is suspicious  and amasawa may simply have wanted the 20 million bounty  feels he must stay wary of all first years he came into contact with    if i showed even the slightest hint of weakness  i could be swallowed whole  on may 1 results day  no expulsions  lowest combined score 579  chabashira had deliberately lowered the score estimates  horikita scored 87 in math  next was keisei s 84  but ayanokoji placed just above her with a perfect 100   the only student to break 90 in any subject  deliberately refused to cut corners  a perfect score carried a risk  to show  a glimpse of this side of myself beforehand    making the first move to save trouble later against tsukishiro  notes sudo s calm surprise  he knew of the hosen incident  their math competition   she scored 87  he 100  she admits defeat but is frustrated  he instantly agreed to partner with nanase at her request  surprising him and horikita","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p345-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">After the knife; the results and the perfect math score<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.345–348<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On Monday/Tuesday, Nanase and Horikita finalize the inter-class agreement; all 157 pairs formed. Kōenji unexpectedly agrees to partner with Nanase. His bandaged hand is kept confidential by Chabashira and Mashima.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Still can&#x27;t identify the White Room student; reconsiders everyone — Hōsen could be an imposter who took the real Hōsen&#x27;s identity (Ryūen and Akito never met him in person), Nanase&#x27;s method of approaching him is suspicious, and Amasawa may simply have wanted the 20-million bounty.<span class=\"pg\">p.345–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Feels he must stay wary of all first-years he came into contact with — &quot;If I showed even the slightest hint of weakness, I could be swallowed whole.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.345–346<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> On May 1 results day: no expulsions (lowest combined score 579); Chabashira had deliberately lowered the score estimates; Horikita scored 87 in math (next was Keisei&#x27;s 84), but Ayanokōji placed just above her with a perfect 100 — the only student to break 90 in any subject.<span class=\"pg\">p.346–348<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately refused to cut corners (a perfect score carried a risk) to show &quot;a glimpse of this side of myself beforehand&quot; — making the first move to save trouble later against Tsukishiro; notes Sudō&#x27;s calm surprise (he knew of the Hōsen incident).<span class=\"pg\">p.348<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Their math competition — she scored 87, he 100; she admits defeat but is frustrated.<span class=\"pg\">p.346–350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> He instantly agreed to partner with Nanase at her request, surprising him and Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.345<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p344-1\">← Before: Epilogue: Perfect score and Tsukishiro<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p349-1\">→ After: Keisei and Horikita after class; Chabashira&#x27;s summons<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p349-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"ishigami-kyou chabashira-sae horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka keisei and horikita after class  chabashira s summons  kiyotaka  do you have a moment   theory of measurement  lebesgue integrals  maybe sometime around college  i think   it s frustrating  but i admit defeat  the events of these last couple days have pretty much forced me to recognize your abilities   how awfully cold  where would you be if not for my help the other day   i see i ve interrupted you  but it s urgent  acting director tsukishiro is asking for you  come  deflects keisei s questions  horikita cuts in  gives horikita a vague answer about the college level concepts  can t reveal he learned them as a child  and is summoned by chabashira to tsukishiro  tries to question him about the perfect score  horikita pushes him aside  she concedes the bet after the demonstration of his abilities  he deflects her questions  she helped keep the knife incident confidential and now summons him  he has already secretly won her to his side","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p349-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Keisei and Horikita after class; Chabashira&#x27;s summons<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.349–351<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> &quot;Kiyotaka, do you have a moment?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Theory of measurement, Lebesgue integrals… maybe sometime around college, I think?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s frustrating, but I admit defeat. The events of these last couple days have pretty much forced me to recognize your abilities.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How awfully cold. Where would you be if not for my help the other day?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see I&#x27;ve interrupted you, but it&#x27;s urgent. Acting Director Tsukishiro is asking for you. Come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deflects Keisei&#x27;s questions (Horikita cuts in), gives Horikita a vague answer about the college-level concepts (can&#x27;t reveal he learned them as a child), and is summoned by Chabashira to Tsukishiro.<span class=\"pg\">p.349–351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Tries to question him about the perfect score; Horikita pushes him aside.<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She concedes the bet after the demonstration of his abilities; he deflects her questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She helped keep the knife incident confidential and now summons him; he has already secretly won her to his side.<span class=\"pg\">p.350–351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p345-1\">← Before: After the knife; the results and the perfect math score<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p351-1\">→ After: Tsukishiro&#x27;s office: the enforcer &quot;disobeyed orders&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p351-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"spoken","w":"tsukishiro chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka tsukishiro s office  the enforcer  disobeyed orders  goes alone to the reception office  tsukishiro  acting director  asks whether he s identified the student he sent  referencing their end of april promise   now that april has come to a close  have you managed to figure out who the student i sent is   unfortunately  i still don t have any idea of who it might be   i see  so that child has managed to stay hidden quite well  it seems   acting director tsukishiro  could it be that you miscalculated something   in fact  i m almost tempted to start thinking that there isn t even a white room student amongst the first years at all   it s true that i had planned on guaranteeing your expulsion this time around  however  that child simply disregarded it   do take care  ayanokoji kun  pressures tsukishiro by suggesting he miscalculated or acted forcefully  deduces gains an admission that the enforcer disobeyed orders   raising the possibility that the relationship between tsukishiro and the white room student isn t simple  or that  that man  is pulling strings  weighs both options as equally likely and stays wary of tsukishiro s deceit  plays dumb  i won t speak of things i m not certain of  hides that chabashira is on his side  and stands his ground despite tsukishiro s veiled warning that he might be  better off choosing to get expelled  walks away calmly  their end of april reckoning   he can t name the enforcer  tsukishiro admits the student acted independently  both probe each other  she walked him to the office  worried tsukishiro might forcibly remove him  he reassures her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p351-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tsukishiro&#x27;s office: the enforcer &quot;disobeyed orders&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.351–356<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Goes alone to the reception office; Tsukishiro (Acting Director) asks whether he&#x27;s identified the student he sent, referencing their end-of-April promise.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> &quot;Now that April has come to a close, have you managed to figure out who the student I sent is?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Unfortunately, I still don&#x27;t have any idea of who it might be.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.353<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> &quot;I see. So that child has managed to stay hidden quite well, it seems.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.353<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Acting Director Tsukishiro, could it be that you miscalculated something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.354<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In fact, I&#x27;m almost tempted to start thinking that there isn&#x27;t even a White Room student amongst the first-years at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.354<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s true that I had planned on guaranteeing your expulsion this time around. However, that child simply disregarded it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.355<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do take care, Ayanokōji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.355<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Pressures Tsukishiro by suggesting he miscalculated or acted forcefully; deduces/gains an admission that the enforcer disobeyed orders — raising the possibility that the relationship between Tsukishiro and the White Room student isn&#x27;t simple, or that &quot;that man&quot; is pulling strings; weighs both options as equally likely and stays wary of Tsukishiro&#x27;s deceit.<span class=\"pg\">p.354–356<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Plays dumb (&quot;I won&#x27;t speak of things I&#x27;m not certain of&quot;), hides that Chabashira is on his side, and stands his ground despite Tsukishiro&#x27;s veiled warning that he might be &quot;better off choosing to get expelled&quot;; walks away calmly.<span class=\"pg\">p.352–356<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Their end-of-April reckoning — he can&#x27;t name the enforcer; Tsukishiro admits the student acted independently; both probe each other.<span class=\"pg\">p.351–356<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She walked him to the office, worried Tsukishiro might forcibly remove him; he reassures her.<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p349-1\">← Before: Keisei and Horikita after class; Chabashira&#x27;s summons<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p356-1\">→ After: Final class standings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p356-1","v":"y2v1","y":2,"o":16,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka final class standings special exam overall ranking  1st class 2 a  725 avg  2nd 2 c  673  3rd 2 d  640  4th 2 b  621    class d achieved horikita s goal of third place or higher  class points as of may 1  2 a  sakayanagi  1169  2 b  ryuen  565  note  corpus labels swapped  2 c  ichinose  539  2 d  horikita  283","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p356-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Final class standings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V1 · p.356–357<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Special Exam Overall Ranking: 1st Class 2-A (725 avg), 2nd 2-C (673), 3rd 2-D (640), 4th 2-B (621) — Class D achieved Horikita&#x27;s goal of third place or higher.<span class=\"pg\">p.356<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Class points as of May 1: 2-A (Sakayanagi) 1169, 2-B (Ryūen) 565 [note: corpus labels swapped], 2-C (Ichinose) 539, 2-D (Horikita) 283.<span class=\"pg\">p.357<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v1-p351-1\">← Before: Tsukishiro&#x27;s office: the enforcer &quot;disobeyed orders&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p6-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p6-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.6-354<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1\">→ After: After Tsukishiro&#x27;s office; Chabashira&#x27;s carelessness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka after tsukishiro s office  chabashira s carelessness leaves the reception room after tsukishiro  breathing a short sigh  his left hand  from hosen s knife  still wounded  he reflects he  escaped to this school  but a chain now follows him forever   only expulsion could free him   looks like you re done talking   you ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on   there s no use in acting in advance  i ll start from this stage   this is going to be hard for you  prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions   can we stop here  if i m walking with a teacher alone from now on  it ll attract a lot of unnecessary attention  notes chabashira waiting for him after tsukishiro s summons is careless  tsukishiro might suspect a trap  her caution differs from his because she sees tsukishiro only as ayanokoji s father s connection  not knowing the white room s background  sees through her joy at his perfect score  keeps his distance from chabashira yet relies on her   she is overflowing with joy beneath a poker face and  despite her distance from students  might actually be the closest to them  secretly allied  she worries about the attention his perfect score will bring  he casts her from his mind as easy to manipulate  just left his office  the  chain  he can t escape","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">After Tsukishiro&#x27;s office; Chabashira&#x27;s carelessness<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.23–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves the reception room after Tsukishiro, breathing a short sigh; his left hand (from Hōsen&#x27;s knife) still wounded, he reflects he &quot;escaped to this school&quot; but a chain now follows him forever — only expulsion could free him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Looks like you&#x27;re done talking?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;ll be a bit of a celebrity from now on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s no use in acting in advance. I&#x27;ll start from this stage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is going to be hard for you. Prepare yourself to be bombarded with questions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can we stop here? If I&#x27;m walking with a teacher alone from now on, it&#x27;ll attract a lot of unnecessary attention.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Notes Chabashira waiting for him after Tsukishiro&#x27;s summons is careless (Tsukishiro might suspect a trap); her caution differs from his because she sees Tsukishiro only as Ayanokōji&#x27;s father&#x27;s connection, not knowing the White Room&#x27;s background; sees through her joy at his perfect score.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps his distance from Chabashira yet relies on her — she is overflowing with joy beneath a poker face and, despite her distance from students, might actually be the closest to them.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Secretly allied; she worries about the attention his perfect score will bring; he casts her from his mind as easy to manipulate.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Just left his office; the &quot;chain&quot; he can&#x27;t escape.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p6-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1\">→ After: The class confronts him; Horikita&#x27;s cover story<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ishigami-kyou horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the class confronts him  horikita s cover story returns to the classroom to find students who didn t have club activities still waiting for him  keisei leads the charge  resentful  with haruka and airi gathered around   you  what s with the 100 points in math   you re the only one in the entire year   well  let me explain this   yukimura kun and i  no  the entire 2nd year couldn t get this perfect score  so how was ayanokouji kun able to achieve that   it s hard not to be suspicious  if i were a student who knew nothing  i would definitely feel the same way  however  that isn t the case here  had hoped most students would have left  realizes horikita stayed back  having not answered his call  specifically to smooth things over   an accurate judgment  and he is grateful  she steps in to speak for him  using a mystifying expression to gather attention and defuse the cheating accusation  presses him resentfully about the perfect score  he wanted to talk right after school","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The class confronts him; Horikita&#x27;s cover story<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.27–30<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns to the classroom to find students who didn&#x27;t have club activities still waiting for him; Keisei leads the charge, resentful, with Haruka and Airi gathered around.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> &quot;You… what&#x27;s with the 100 points in math?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re the only one in the entire year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Well, let me explain this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yukimura-kun and I- no, the entire 2nd year couldn&#x27;t get this perfect score, so how was Ayanokouji-kun able to achieve that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;it&#x27;s hard not to be suspicious. If I were a student who knew nothing, I would definitely feel the same way… However, that isn&#x27;t the case here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Had hoped most students would have left; realizes Horikita stayed back (having not answered his call) specifically to smooth things over — an accurate judgment, and he is grateful.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She steps in to speak for him, using a mystifying expression to gather attention and defuse the cheating accusation.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Presses him resentfully about the perfect score; he wanted to talk right after school.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p23-1\">← Before: After Tsukishiro&#x27;s office; Chabashira&#x27;s carelessness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1\">→ After: Keyaki Mall: Ichinose and Kanzaki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka keyaki mall  ichinose and kanzaki arrives at 6 30 a m   before the agreed 7  to wait alone in front of keyaki mall   his  special skill  of emptying his mind  learns airi is already leaving the dorm via the group chat   ayanokouji kun  are you waiting for someone   i m waiting for my friends to go eat   you actually got a perfect score in math  that s amazing   judging from last year s oaa  you shouldn t have the strength to get a full score   there s a lot of reasons for this  it was only after discussing with my comrades that i decided to hide the fact that i m good at math   ayanokouji kun is not our enemy   i want for you to trust your classmates  put their safety first and continue the fight   i won t ever let you get expelled   you are the same too  you certainly have such a weapon yourself  gives the explanation he knows ichinose kanzaki can fill in  judges kanzaki s guardedness correct and ichinose s trust unusual  ignites a  blazing fire  in ichinose s eyes to keep her from stopping  and analyzes that her inclusiveness kills her classmates  individuality  encourages her after class b s fall  promises never to let her be expelled   she departs embarrassed but resolved to stay  he is openly hostile suspicious  presses about other hidden abilities  he leaves first  ayanokoji notes his reaction is understandable given class b s fall","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Keyaki Mall: Ichinose and Kanzaki<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.46–52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives at 6:30 a.m. (before the agreed 7) to wait alone in front of Keyaki Mall — his &quot;special skill&quot; of emptying his mind; learns Airi is already leaving the dorm via the group chat.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, are you waiting for someone?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m waiting for my friends to go eat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;You actually got a perfect score in math, that&#x27;s amazing!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Judging from last year&#x27;s OAA, you shouldn&#x27;t have the strength to get a full score.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s a lot of reasons for this. It was only after discussing with my comrades that I decided to hide the fact that I&#x27;m good at math.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun is not our enemy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I want for you to trust your classmates, put their safety first and continue the fight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I won&#x27;t ever let you get expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You are the same too. You certainly have such a weapon yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Gives the explanation he knows Ichinose/Kanzaki can fill in; judges Kanzaki&#x27;s guardedness correct and Ichinose&#x27;s trust unusual; ignites a &quot;blazing fire&quot; in Ichinose&#x27;s eyes to keep her from stopping, and analyzes that her inclusiveness kills her classmates&#x27; individuality.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Encourages her after Class B&#x27;s fall; promises never to let her be expelled — she departs embarrassed but resolved to stay.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> He is openly hostile/suspicious, presses about other hidden abilities; he leaves first; Ayanokōji notes his reaction is understandable given Class B&#x27;s fall.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p27-1\">← Before: The class confronts him; Horikita&#x27;s cover story<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1\">→ After: The group after Ichinose; Sudō&#x27;s questions<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the group after ichinose  sudo s questions  what were you talking about with ichinose san just now   my perfect score in math   so you were hiding the fact you re good at studying because of suzune s strategy  right   is the fact that you re good at fighting also a secret   that was the first time i ve ever felt scared in a fight  gives the group a sensible reason  notices haruka is  off  and doesn t ask further  declines to point out sudo s romantic view of horikita  admits sudo fought bravely against hosen  she asks about the ichinose conversation then quickly returns to her usual expression   something feels off  he accepts the explanation that he hid his ability for horikita s strategy  is more interested in his fighting secret  and describes hosen as a monster who scared him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The group after Ichinose; Sudō&#x27;s questions<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.53–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> &quot;What were you talking about with Ichinose-san just now?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My perfect score in math.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;So you were hiding the fact you&#x27;re good at studying because of Suzune&#x27;s strategy, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;is the fact that you&#x27;re good at fighting also a secret?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That was the first time I&#x27;ve ever felt scared in a fight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Gives the group a sensible reason; notices Haruka is &quot;off&quot; and doesn&#x27;t ask further; declines to point out Sudō&#x27;s romantic view of Horikita; admits Sudō fought bravely against Hōsen.<span class=\"pg\">p.53–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She asks about the Ichinose conversation then quickly returns to her usual expression — something feels off.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He accepts the explanation that he hid his ability for Horikita&#x27;s strategy, is more interested in his fighting secret, and describes Hōsen as a monster who scared him.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p46-1\">← Before: Keyaki Mall: Ichinose and Kanzaki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1\">→ After: OAA updates; analyzing the 20-million bounty with Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune tsukishiro amasawa-ichika nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka oaa updates  analyzing the 20 million bounty with horikita on a mid may morning waits for horikita  reviewing the updated oaa  his own academics jumped to a   81  from the perfect math score  overall b   62  sudo s academics rose to c  54  overall b   63  notes sudo s physical a   96  and amazing growth from a first year overall c  47    his overall now exceeds keisei and akito  others with low adaptability social scores all improved   thanks again  because of your quick witted speech  i didn t need to be baptized under the attentive eyes of my classmates for this to end    horikita  it s nothing  i just thought that it would be good for the class in the future   is your left hand alright now    horikita  not at all  i passed by housen and nanase once  but i didn t say anything   that  if someone gets you expelled  they get 20 million points  is that true    horikita  the other possibility is that it wasn t really a special exam  in other words  someone offered to pay 20 million private points in order to get me expelled  rules out a first year funded bounty  no trust capital  and reasons someone in the same or higher grade with 20 million points and first year trust is behind it  chabashira knew nothing  considers nagumo a possibility but doubts he d use unknown first years  notes nagumo s title would remove first years  doubts  feigns ignorance about what he d have done without horikita s intervention  appraises the brave first years who made a massive move without wavering  carefully hides that he has already secretly won chabashira to his side  walks to school with her  thanks her for the cover story  and reasons through the bounty together  she suspects nagumo  notes the white room student still hasn t acted    out of tsukishiro s control    and wonders what they re thinking  considers her almost certainly aware of the 20 million bounty  given she teamed with hosen  discusses him as a possible bounty source  plans for horikita to join the student council to investigate  and to observe his meritocratic reforms","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">OAA updates; analyzing the 20-million bounty with Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.65–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On a mid-May morning waits for Horikita, reviewing the updated OAA: his own Academics jumped to A− (81) from the perfect math score, overall B− (62); Sudō&#x27;s Academics rose to C (54) overall B− (63).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Thanks again. Because of your quick-witted speech, I didn&#x27;t need to be baptized under the attentive eyes of my classmates for this to end.&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s nothing; I just thought that it would be good for the class in the future.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is your left hand alright now?&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Notes Sudō&#x27;s physical A+ (96) and amazing growth from a first-year overall C (47) — his overall now exceeds Keisei and Akito; others with low adaptability/social scores all improved.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Not at all. I passed by Housen and Nanase once, but I didn&#x27;t say anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That, if someone gets you expelled, they get 20 million points, is that true?&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The other possibility is that it wasn&#x27;t really a special exam. In other words, someone offered to pay 20 million private points in order to get me expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Rules out a first-year-funded bounty (no trust/capital) and reasons someone in the same or higher grade with 20 million points and first-year trust is behind it; Chabashira knew nothing; considers Nagumo a possibility but doubts he&#x27;d use unknown first-years; notes Nagumo&#x27;s title would remove first-years&#x27; doubts.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Feigns ignorance about what he&#x27;d have done without Horikita&#x27;s intervention; appraises the brave first-years who made a massive move without wavering; carefully hides that he has already secretly won Chabashira to his side.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Walks to school with her, thanks her for the cover story, and reasons through the bounty together; she suspects Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Notes the White Room student still hasn&#x27;t acted — &quot;out of Tsukishiro&#x27;s control&quot; — and wonders what they&#x27;re thinking.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Considers her almost certainly aware of the 20-million bounty, given she teamed with Hōsen.<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Discusses him as a possible bounty source; plans for Horikita to join the student council to investigate, and to observe his meritocratic reforms.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p53-1\">← Before: The group after Ichinose; Sudō&#x27;s questions<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p72-1\">→ After: Why Horikita should join the student council<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p72-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka why horikita should join the student council  i m preparing after school to go to the student council  and ask president nagumo about joining it    horikita  that s not the only reason  right   what your brother thinks is completely different from what nagumo thinks   now  i just want to see nagumo s reforms   if nagumo is going in the wrong direction  there s a need to stop him   will you come with me    horikita explains manabu valued tradition and opposed nagumo s reforms  the class is a community that should share the same fate  refuses to judge who s right  wanting only to observe   but would have horikita  manabu s sister  stop nagumo if needed  won her compliance via their bet  his values  tradition  shared class fate  differ from nagumo s  ayanokoji relays manabu s words from before graduation  she asks him to accompany her to the nagumo meeting as evidence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Why Horikita should join the student council<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.72–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m preparing after school to go to the student council, and ask President Nagumo about joining it.&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;that&#x27;s not the only reason, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What your brother thinks is completely different from what Nagumo thinks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Now, I just want to see Nagumo&#x27;s reforms.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Nagumo is going in the wrong direction, there&#x27;s a need to stop him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;will you come with me?&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Explains Manabu valued tradition and opposed Nagumo&#x27;s reforms (&quot;the class is a community that should share the same fate&quot;); refuses to judge who&#x27;s right, wanting only to observe — but would have Horikita (Manabu&#x27;s sister) stop Nagumo if needed; won her compliance via their bet.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> His values (tradition, shared class fate) differ from Nagumo&#x27;s; Ayanokōji relays Manabu&#x27;s words from before graduation.<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She asks him to accompany her to the Nagumo meeting as evidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p65-1\">← Before: OAA updates; analyzing the 20-million bounty with Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1\">→ After: The Nagumo meeting; Horikita joins; Nagumo&#x27;s challenge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi horikita-suzune kiriyama ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the nagumo meeting  horikita joins  nagumo s challenge accompanies horikita to the student council office  nagumo  president  and kiriyama  vice president  react with surprise to her request to join   well  what a turn of events  i don t really want to obediently say yes   welcome to the student council  from today onward  i want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries  suzune   as a congratulations for joining  i ll tell you something interesting  the past presidents of the student council have always graduated in class a   don t worry  i don t plan to graduate outside of class a   are you going to join the student council by the way  ayanokouji   i ll pass  my personality isn t suited to being on the council   i ll play with you  so look forward to it  observes nagumo see through horikita s half truths yet accept her  open to anyone  unlike manabu  declines nagumo s casual invitation  reads his parting  i ll play with you  as  an order from the strong to the weak  he invites him to the council and declares he ll  play  with him over summer   a veiled challenge  vice president  surprised at nagumo inviting ayanokoji  shakes horikita s hand","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Nagumo meeting; Horikita joins; Nagumo&#x27;s challenge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.75–81<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Accompanies Horikita to the student council office; Nagumo (president) and Kiriyama (vice president) react with surprise to her request to join.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> &quot;Well, what a turn of events! I don&#x27;t really want to obediently say yes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> &quot;Welcome to the student council. From today onward, I want you to work for me as a member of the council without any worries, Suzune.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> &quot;As a congratulations for joining, I&#x27;ll tell you something interesting. The past presidents of the student council have always graduated in Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t worry. I don&#x27;t plan to graduate outside of Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you going to join the student council by the way? Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll pass, my personality isn&#x27;t suited to being on the council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll play with you, so look forward to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Observes Nagumo see through Horikita&#x27;s half-truths yet accept her (open to anyone, unlike Manabu); declines Nagumo&#x27;s casual invitation; reads his parting &quot;I&#x27;ll play with you&quot; as &quot;an order from the strong to the weak.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He invites him to the council and declares he&#x27;ll &quot;play&quot; with him over summer — a veiled challenge.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> Vice president; surprised at Nagumo inviting Ayanokōji; shakes Horikita&#x27;s hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, 80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p72-1\">← Before: Why Horikita should join the student council<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1\">→ After: Mid-June morning: Nanase&#x27;s apology and the ongoing bounty<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa housen-kazuomi karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka mid june morning  nanase s apology and the ongoing bounty walking to school looking at the blue sky  is greeted by nanase  who may have deliberately waited for him  reflects summer is his favorite season and that the white room student still hasn t moved   i ve always felt sorry for what i did to you  ayanokouji senpai   senpai  do you hate me   i don t have any reason to hate you  it was for the special exam  right   besides  i saw how you were trying to protect me  nanase   no  the exam is still going on  the deadline is the start of the second semester   because of what happened last time  i m convinced that even with a plan  it might not work out that easily   and since even someone like housen failed  people judged that it wouldn t work out without good preparation  reasons it was fortunate hosen  who attracts all the attention  was the first to act  the other three first year classes now know of the bounty and are waiting to act with preparation  decides not to press nanase  she can t betray the insiders and only admitted the exam s existence to avoid disadvantaging class 1 d  recalls that he and kei still haven t kissed again   an  invisible wall  from the knife incident   but doesn t rush  letting her remove it naturally for her growth  notes nanase has shed her naivety and speaks of living  without regrets  she apologizes  reveals the bounty runs until second semester and that hosen has grown  more well behaved  toward first years  focusing on ayanokoji  and warns him not to leave regrets  now fixated on ayanokoji  let me fight the 2nd years  his attention shifted from first years  which helped them  still hasn t kissed again after the knife incident","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Mid-June morning: Nanase&#x27;s apology and the ongoing bounty<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.110–116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking to school looking at the blue sky, is greeted by Nanase, who may have deliberately waited for him; reflects summer is his favorite season and that the White Room student still hasn&#x27;t moved.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve always felt sorry for what I did to you, Ayanokouji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Senpai, do you hate me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t have any reason to hate you. It was for the special exam, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Besides, I saw how you were trying to protect me, Nanase.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, the exam is still going on. The deadline is the start of the second semester.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Because of what happened last time, I&#x27;m convinced that even with a plan, it might not work out that easily.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;And since even someone like Housen failed, people judged that it wouldn&#x27;t work out without good preparation?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons it was fortunate Hōsen (who attracts all the attention) was the first to act; the other three first-year classes now know of the bounty and are waiting to act with preparation; decides not to press Nanase (she can&#x27;t betray the insiders and only admitted the exam&#x27;s existence to avoid disadvantaging Class 1-D).<span class=\"pg\">p.112–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Recalls that he and Kei still haven&#x27;t kissed again — an &quot;invisible wall&quot; from the knife incident — but doesn&#x27;t rush, letting her remove it naturally for her growth; notes Nanase has shed her naivety and speaks of living &quot;without regrets.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She apologizes, reveals the bounty runs until second semester and that Hōsen has grown &quot;more well-behaved&quot; toward first-years (focusing on Ayanokōji), and warns him not to leave regrets.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Now fixated on Ayanokōji (&quot;Let me fight the 2nd years&quot;); his attention shifted from first-years, which helped them.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Still hasn&#x27;t kissed again after the knife incident.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p75-1\">← Before: The Nagumo meeting; Horikita joins; Nagumo&#x27;s challenge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1\">→ After: The island survival exam announced; rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the island survival exam announced  rules in homeroom  chabashira teases a luxury cruise  aug 4 11  before revealing the  uninhabited island survival  special exam   bigger  two weeks  all school years competing together   you will have to participate in the  uninhabited island survival  special exam and compete with each other   the exam this year is very different from the previous one  it s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before   not all the rules will be made public today   a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other   which means  the students in the 2nd year  are our allies  small groups of up to 3  2nd 3rd years  or 4  1st years  same year only  formed by july 16  mixed gender groups need  2 girls per 3  50  in big groups  groups can t change  big groups of up to 6 form after the exam starts  the exam requires all abilities  academic  physical  mental  communication  if a member drops out the group continues   the more people  the more chances to survive  rewards  1st place 300 class points   1m private   1 protection point  2nd 200   500k  3rd 100   250k  top 50  50k  top 70  10k   collected from bottom groups  years  split by class  notices chabashira dangles the cruise then yanks it back   a tactic that works because the class has learned how to brace itself  realizes rewards penalties are given by group per class  so a mixed class winning group won t change standings  delivers the exam briefing  he notes she wants class d to prove they re different from a year ago","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The island survival exam announced; rules<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.117–132<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In homeroom, Chabashira teases a luxury cruise (Aug 4–11) before revealing the &quot;Uninhabited Island Survival&quot; special exam — bigger, two weeks, all school years competing together.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;You will have to participate in the &#x27;Uninhabited Island Survival&#x27; special exam and compete with each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;the exam this year is very different from the previous one. It&#x27;s probably going to be tougher and more unforgiving than any other special exam before.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;not all the rules will be made public today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;a maximum of 6 people to form a big group to work with each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Which means… the students in the 2nd year, are our allies…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Small groups of up to 3 (2nd/3rd years) or 4 (1st years), same-year only, formed by July 16; mixed-gender groups need ≥2 girls per 3 (≥50% in big groups); groups can&#x27;t change; big groups of up to 6 form after the exam starts.<span class=\"pg\">p.125–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The exam requires all abilities (academic, physical, mental, communication); if a member drops out the group continues — the more people, the more chances to survive.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Rewards: 1st place 300 class points + 1M private + 1 Protection Point; 2nd 200 + 500k; 3rd 100 + 250k; top 50% 50k, top 70% 10k — collected from bottom groups&#x27; years, split by class.<span class=\"pg\">p.130–131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notices Chabashira dangles the cruise then yanks it back — a tactic that works because the class has learned how to brace itself; realizes rewards/penalties are given by group per class, so a mixed-class winning group won&#x27;t change standings.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Delivers the exam briefing; he notes she wants Class D to prove they&#x27;re different from a year ago.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–132<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p110-1\">← Before: Mid-June morning: Nanase&#x27;s apology and the ongoing bounty<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1\">→ After: Ishizaki&#x27;s group proposal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi shiina-hiyori yamada-albert ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ishizaki s group proposal is approached by ishizaki daichi  class 2 c  at school  who proposes forming a group for the island exam  ayanokoji follows him and meets albert and hiyori   let s cut to the chase  here s my proposal  let s form a group for the next   form a group  can you give me more details   when the exam starts  you ll combine your group with another three person group from class b  so it ll be a perfect six person group   hiyori  did you carefully explain the exam rules to ishizaki  realizes the plan was ishizaki s own  not ryuen s    ishizaki tenses when asked  understands why ibuki hangs around him  hiyori and albert support him  declines to commit for now  knowing forming a group would draw others in  reads the group formation dynamics sharply  recognizes the rules mean same year grouping and that ryuen couldn t object to intra class grouping  his proposal   a 3 person small group with ishizaki albert hiyori combining with another class b group  ayanokoji declines to commit  supports ishizaki s plan  listens with interest  ishizaki s classmate  part of the proposed group  ayanokoji checks whether ryuen decided the invitation  it was ishizaki s own idea","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ishizaki&#x27;s group proposal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.152–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is approached by Ishizaki Daichi (Class 2-C) at school, who proposes forming a group for the island exam; Ayanokōji follows him and meets Albert and Hiyori.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"yamada-albert.html\">Yamada Albert<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> &quot;Let&#x27;s cut to the chase, here&#x27;s my proposal…. Let&#x27;s form a group for the next&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Form…a group? Can you give me more details?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> &quot;when the exam starts, you&#x27;ll combine your group with another three person group from Class B, so it&#x27;ll be a perfect six person group.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hiyori, did you carefully explain the exam rules to Ishizaki?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes the plan was Ishizaki&#x27;s own (not Ryūen&#x27;s) — Ishizaki tenses when asked; understands why Ibuki hangs around him; Hiyori and Albert support him; declines to commit for now, knowing forming a group would draw others in.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the group-formation dynamics sharply; recognizes the rules mean same-year grouping and that Ryūen couldn&#x27;t object to intra-class grouping.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> His proposal — a 3-person small group with Ishizaki/Albert/Hiyori combining with another Class B group; Ayanokōji declines to commit.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Supports Ishizaki&#x27;s plan; listens with interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamada Albert<\/b> Ishizaki&#x27;s classmate, part of the proposed group.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ayanokōji checks whether Ryūen decided the invitation; it was Ishizaki&#x27;s own idea.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p117-1\">← Before: The island survival exam announced; rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p169-1\">→ After: Class D group formation; Matsushita&#x27;s offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p169-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"matsushita-chiaki ike-kanji horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka class d group formation  matsushita s offer fields classmates  questions about grouping   ike asks  wanting to pair with shinohara  then matsushita approach him with an offer   did you judge that your odds of survival are the highest if you grouped up  matsushita  holding a  trial card  that makes a group more likely to be expelled  offers to help ayanokoji despite the danger  saying she chose him because he seemed unlikely to be snapped up quickly  he decides not to settle his group  at least for this month  suspecting the others are scheming  is wary of committing early  others will get involved  watches ike shinohara dynamics and notes horikita has become  more difficult to deal with  considers relying on horikita but knows as leader she must avoid favoritism  she offers to assist him despite the risk of her trial card  he declined to decide immediately  he wants to group with shinohara  asks ayanokoji s advice  considers relying on her but recognizes her position  she plans to select two from class d","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Class D group formation; Matsushita&#x27;s offer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.169–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fields classmates&#x27; questions about grouping — Ike asks (wanting to pair with Shinohara), then Matsushita approach him with an offer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> &quot;Did you judge that your odds of survival are the highest if you grouped up&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Matsushita (holding a &quot;trial card&quot; that makes a group more likely to be expelled) offers to help Ayanokōji despite the danger, saying she chose him because he seemed unlikely to be snapped up quickly; he decides not to settle his group &quot;at least for this month,&quot; suspecting the others are scheming.<span class=\"pg\">p.182–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Is wary of committing early (others will get involved); watches Ike/Shinohara dynamics and notes Horikita has become &quot;more difficult to deal with&quot;; considers relying on Horikita but knows as leader she must avoid favoritism.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> She offers to assist him despite the risk of her trial card; he declined to decide immediately.<span class=\"pg\">p.182–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He wants to group with Shinohara; asks Ayanokōji&#x27;s advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Considers relying on her but recognizes her position; she plans to select two from Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ishizaki&#x27;s group proposal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p250-1\">→ After: Yagami&#x27;s revelation: Nagumo and Tsukishiro behind the bounty<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p250-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"yagami-takuya kushida-kikyou nagumo-miyabi tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka yagami s revelation  nagumo and tsukishiro behind the bounty walks with yagami and kushida to keyaki mall  yagami  having joined the student council  reveals he asked nagumo about the previous island exam  and starts explaining the bounty   there s something i want to tell you  ayanokouji senpai  there s a special exam that only a very small of 1st year students have been informed about   in april  i received a notification about this  however  since i wasn t interested in getting paid for setting people up  i decided not to participate   for the sake of protecting the first year students  i was going to be a complete bystander   it all started when i was contacted by president nagumo of the student council   the first year students there were takahashi osamu kun and ishigami kyou kun from class a  me from class b  utomiya riku kun from class c  and housen kazuomi kun and nanase tsubasa san from class d  a total of 6 students   the student council president nagumo senpai told the six of us that he ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled   president nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years   in fact  i ve already confirmed with my own eyes that he has 20 million points   when the student council president announced the exam  the acting director was also present  learns the six first years summoned by nagumo  takahashi  ishigami  yagami  utomiya  hosen  nanase  amasawa s absence noted  the claimed random 1 in 157 selection is judged false  tsukishiro s presence confirms nagumo and the acting director are behind the 20 million bounty   giving horikita a clear direction  prudent   neither confirms nor denies  lets yagami talk  judges he isn t lying but weighs the risk to class 2 d  notes yagami is a defensive fighter who pre emptively strikes  spots tsubaki observing them from behind  he defects  revealing the whole bounty scheme to warn him  partly to protect kushida  is present  surprised by the revelation  ayanokoji worries the information could affect her  confirmed as the one who summoned the first years and offered the bounty  ayanokoji doubts the  random selection  story  his presence at the announcement confirms his involvement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p250-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Yagami&#x27;s revelation: Nagumo and Tsukishiro behind the bounty<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.250–258<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks with Yagami and Kushida to Keyaki Mall; Yagami (having joined the student council) reveals he asked Nagumo about the previous island exam, and starts explaining the bounty.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> &quot;there&#x27;s something I want to tell you, Ayanokouji-senpai. There&#x27;s a special exam that only a very small of 1st year students have been informed about.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> &quot;In April, I received a notification about this. However, since I wasn&#x27;t interested in getting paid for setting people up, I decided not to participate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> &quot;For the sake of protecting the first year students, I was going to be a complete bystander.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It all started when I was contacted by President Nagumo of the student council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The first year students there were Takahashi Osamu-kun and Ishigami Kyou-kun from Class A, me from Class B, Utomiya Riku-kun from Class C, and Housen Kazuomi-kun and Nanase Tsubasa-san from Class D. A total of 6 students.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The student council president Nagumo-senpai told the six of us that he&#x27;ll give 20 million points to the student who got him expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;President Nagumo said that the student was selected at random from the 2nd years&#x27;.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In fact, I&#x27;ve already confirmed with my own eyes that he has 20 million points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When the student council president announced the exam, the acting director was also present.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Learns the six first-years summoned by Nagumo (Takahashi, Ishigami, Yagami, Utomiya, Hōsen, Nanase); Amasawa&#x27;s absence noted; the claimed random 1-in-157 selection is judged false; Tsukishiro&#x27;s presence confirms Nagumo and the acting director are behind the 20-million bounty — giving Horikita a clear direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.254–257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Prudent — neither confirms nor denies, lets Yagami talk; judges he isn&#x27;t lying but weighs the risk to Class 2-D; notes Yagami is a defensive fighter who pre-emptively strikes; spots Tsubaki observing them from behind.<span class=\"pg\">p.250–258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> He defects, revealing the whole bounty scheme to warn him (partly to protect Kushida).<span class=\"pg\">p.250–258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Is present; surprised by the revelation; Ayanokōji worries the information could affect her.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Confirmed as the one who summoned the first-years and offered the bounty; Ayanokōji doubts the &quot;random selection&quot; story.<span class=\"pg\">p.254–257<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> His presence at the announcement confirms his involvement.<span class=\"pg\">p.257<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p169-1\">← Before: Class D group formation; Matsushita&#x27;s offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1\">→ After: Utomiya and Tsubaki&#x27;s plot to expel Hōsen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"utomiya-riku tsubaki-sakurako housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka utomiya and tsubaki s plot to expel hosen at the convenience store  tsubaki and utomiya approach him  utomiya reveals they want to take hosen by surprise on the island and force him out of class 1 d   we want to take housen by surprise on the uninhabited island exam   in class c  a boy named hatano was expelled from the school  i think housen had something to do with it   are you trying to force housen out of the school   if you re able to get housen expelled from this school   did you ever consider that i might be housen s comrade   if we get you expelled  news of that ll spread throughout the school  sees through their plan  hosen lacks points and would be forced out if he can t get the bounty  pretends not to know about yagami s disclosure or his own role  neither he nor tsubaki mentions their separate contact with him  declines to be drawn in  wants to force hosen out  hatano s expulsion cost class c 100 points  and offers him a deal  ayanokoji is wary  facilitated the contact  didn t mention yagami s disclosure  target of their plot  ayanokoji is asked about his past partnership with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Utomiya and Tsubaki&#x27;s plot to expel Hōsen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.264–270<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the convenience store, Tsubaki and Utomiya approach him; Utomiya reveals they want to take Hōsen by surprise on the island and force him out of Class 1-D.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> &quot;We want to take Housen by surprise on the uninhabited island exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.266<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> &quot;In Class C, a boy named Hatano was expelled from the school. I think Housen had something to do with it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you trying to force Housen out of the school?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;if you&#x27;re able to get Housen expelled from this school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did you ever consider that I might be Housen&#x27;s comrade?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If we get you expelled, news of that&#x27;ll spread throughout the school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees through their plan (Hōsen lacks points and would be forced out if he can&#x27;t get the bounty); pretends not to know about Yagami&#x27;s disclosure or his own role; neither he nor Tsubaki mentions their separate contact with him; declines to be drawn in.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> Wants to force Hōsen out (Hatano&#x27;s expulsion cost Class C 100 points), and offers him a deal; Ayanokōji is wary.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> Facilitated the contact; didn&#x27;t mention Yagami&#x27;s disclosure.<span class=\"pg\">p.264–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Target of their plot; Ayanokōji is asked about his past partnership with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.266–270<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p250-1\">← Before: Yagami&#x27;s revelation: Nagumo and Tsukishiro behind the bounty<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1\">→ After: Kanzaki&#x27;s appeal about Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kanzaki s appeal about ichinose on the way to keyaki mall  summoned by ryuen  runs into kanzaki with two 2 liter bottles  kanzaki  growing more wary as his opinion rises  probes whether ayanokoji and horikita will act as  reinforcements   you and horikita  are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class s groups   ayanokouji  ichinose seems to trust you a lot  but can  we  really trust you   although we ve broken off the alliance  i don t consider ichinose to be an enemy   kanazki  what do you want from me   i m simply going to come out and ask you for help  ichinose trusts you a lot  that is why i want you to tell her yourself  the way she is right now  she isn t good enough   sorry  but i can t help you  i d like to keep seeing her own way of dealing with things   well  fundamentally speaking  one has to care of their own class by themselves  isn t that right  sees through kanzaki s attempt to get a statement for ichinose to hear  is briefly conflicted about telling him his fear that ichinose s next fall would be her last  but stops himself  it would only contaminate them  notes a cornered rat can bite the cat  desperately asks him to warn ichinose  admits he was  too childish  and walks away  refuses to help because she must see things her own way  worries about her fragility","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kanzaki&#x27;s appeal about Ichinose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.294–297<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the way to Keyaki Mall (summoned by Ryūen), runs into Kanzaki with two 2-liter bottles; Kanzaki (growing more wary as his opinion rises) probes whether Ayanokōji and Horikita will act as &quot;reinforcements.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You and Horikita, are both of you going to act as reinforcements for your class&#x27;s groups?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokouji, Ichinose seems to trust you a lot, but can &#x27;we&#x27; really trust you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Although we&#x27;ve broken off the alliance, I don&#x27;t consider Ichinose to be an enemy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Kanazki, what do you want from me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m simply going to come out and ask you for help. Ichinose trusts you a lot. That is why I want you to tell her yourself: the way she is right now, she isn&#x27;t good enough.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, but I can&#x27;t help you. I&#x27;d like to keep seeing her own way of dealing with things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, fundamentally speaking, one has to care of their own class by themselves. Isn&#x27;t that right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees through Kanzaki&#x27;s attempt to get a statement for Ichinose to hear; is briefly conflicted about telling him his fear that Ichinose&#x27;s next fall would be her last, but stops himself (it would only contaminate them); notes a cornered rat can bite the cat.<span class=\"pg\">p.294–297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Desperately asks him to warn Ichinose; admits he was &quot;too childish&quot; and walks away.<span class=\"pg\">p.294–297<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Refuses to help because she must see things her own way; worries about her fragility.<span class=\"pg\">p.296–297<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p264-1\">← Before: Utomiya and Tsubaki&#x27;s plot to expel Hōsen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1\">→ After: Ryūen and Katsuragi&#x27;s meeting; buying Katsuragi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"katsuragi-kouhei ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ryuen and katsuragi s meeting  buying katsuragi arrives at the keyaki mall cafe to find ryuen  who summoned him  with katsuragi of class a   an oil and water pair  the atmosphere peculiar   you said there was someone else  were you talking about ayanokouji   you never had the vibe of an ordinary student  ayanokouji  but that was quite the trick you hid up your sleeve   then  let me make this simple for you  i m not going to tell you anything about this  you bastard   don t you want to crawl back to the top again   don t you think it ll be an interesting development if we manage to get sakayanagi expelled from the next special exam   the most important thing about this special exam is to not lose any points from the 2nd year   come to class b  katsuragi   this is your fate  accept it  sees ryuen s real aim  exploit katsuragi s buried vendetta against sakayanagi  and the totsuka expulsion wound  use  20 million points  5m to nullify his contract   class funds  to bring him to class b   never truly to expel sakayanagi  but to climb past class a  katsuragi signs the prepared contract  plays dumb  i echoed katsuragi and shrugged  watches the maneuvering  pours diluted coffee and when asked says he wondered what it d taste like 3 4x diluted  baffling them   a strange  detached presence  invites him  for his trial card  and uses him as a wedge against katsuragi  he refuses to join the group  the class a outsider  signs ryuen s contract to transfer to class b","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ryūen and Katsuragi&#x27;s meeting; buying Katsuragi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.298–311<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives at the Keyaki Mall café to find Ryūen (who summoned him) with Katsuragi of Class A — an oil-and-water pair; the atmosphere peculiar.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> &quot;You said there was someone else, were you talking about Ayanokouji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;You never had the vibe of an ordinary student, Ayanokouji, but that was quite the trick you hid up your sleeve.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.298<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> &quot;Then, let me make this simple for you. I&#x27;m not going to tell you anything about this, you bastard.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t you want to crawl back to the top again?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don&#x27;t you think it&#x27;ll be an interesting development if we manage to get Sakayanagi expelled from the next special exam?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.301<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The most important thing about this special exam is to not lose any points from the 2nd year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Come to Class B, Katsuragi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.308<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is your fate. Accept it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Sees Ryūen&#x27;s real aim: exploit Katsuragi&#x27;s buried vendetta against Sakayanagi (and the Totsuka-expulsion wound), use ~20 million points (5M to nullify his contract + class funds) to bring him to Class B — never truly to expel Sakayanagi, but to climb past Class A; Katsuragi signs the prepared contract.<span class=\"pg\">p.301–311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Plays dumb (&quot;I echoed Katsuragi and shrugged&quot;), watches the maneuvering; pours diluted coffee and when asked says he wondered what it&#x27;d taste like 3–4x diluted, baffling them — a strange, detached presence.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Invites him (for his Trial card) and uses him as a wedge against Katsuragi; he refuses to join the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–311<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> The Class A outsider; signs Ryūen&#x27;s contract to transfer to Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.298–311<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p294-1\">← Before: Kanzaki&#x27;s appeal about Ichinose<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p313-1\">→ After: Selling the Trial card for the Half Off card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p313-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka selling the trial card for the half off card  why  it s the trial card he received   sell it to me   i have one condition  make a student in your class that has a half off card exchange their card with one of our students that has the free ride card  refuses to join ryuen s group but agrees to sell the trial card  500 000 points  on condition a half off card is swapped to class d   to keep kei safe  limiting relief cost to 1 million if she s hit with the penalty  with the trial card and first place ryuen could gain 450 class points  pushing class b past 1000  sells him the trial card in exchange for the half off card swap  arranges the half off card so she can be protected in the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p313-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Selling the Trial card for the Half Off card<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.313–314<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why, it&#x27;s the Trial card he received.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Sell it to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have one condition. Make a student in your class that has a Half Off card exchange their card with one of our students that has the Free Ride card.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Refuses to join Ryūen&#x27;s group but agrees to sell the Trial card (~500,000 points) on condition a Half Off card is swapped to Class D — to keep Kei safe (limiting relief cost to 1 million if she&#x27;s hit with the penalty); with the Trial card and first place Ryūen could gain 450 class points, pushing Class B past 1000.<span class=\"pg\">p.313–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Sells him the Trial card in exchange for the Half Off card swap.<span class=\"pg\">p.313–314<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Arranges the Half Off card so she can be protected in the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p298-1\">← Before: Ryūen and Katsuragi&#x27;s meeting; buying Katsuragi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1\">→ After: Arranging a partner for Ibuki; the &quot;go alone&quot; debate with Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ibuki-mio ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka arranging a partner for ibuki  the  go alone  debate with horikita  give me some time  i think i have an idea   what are you going to do about your group    horikita  i know you re doing that so you can act as the situation demands  but what if you get sick and are eliminated   you had a problem with your health during the uninhabited island exam last year   but  my risks and your risks are different   how about grouping up with her for the special exam  horikita  arranges for the unpaired ibuki  class b  to group with horikita  two girls can merge with another small group later  argues with horikita about going solo  citing her prior year illness and winter fever versus his perfect attendance  and wins her agreement to hear ibuki out  debates the risks of going alone  proposes she group with ibuki  she agrees to hear her out  left unpaired  he finds her a partner in horikita  calls him about ibuki being alone  he promises to help","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Arranging a partner for Ibuki; the &quot;go alone&quot; debate with Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.315–318<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Give me some time. I think I have an idea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What are you going to do about your group?&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I know you&#x27;re doing that so you can act as the situation demands. But what if you get sick and are eliminated?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You had a problem with your health during the uninhabited island exam last year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But, my risks and your risks are different.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How about grouping up with her for the special exam, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Arranges for the unpaired Ibuki (Class B) to group with Horikita (two girls can merge with another small group later); argues with Horikita about going solo, citing her prior-year illness and winter fever versus his perfect attendance, and wins her agreement to hear Ibuki out.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Debates the risks of going alone; proposes she group with Ibuki; she agrees to hear her out.<span class=\"pg\">p.316–318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Left unpaired; he finds her a partner in Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–318<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Calls him about Ibuki being alone; he promises to help.<span class=\"pg\">p.315–316<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p313-1\">← Before: Selling the Trial card for the Half Off card<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1\">→ After: The eve of the island exam; Kōenji&#x27;s deal with Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"ishigami-kyou chabashira-sae kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune tsubaki-sakurako ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the eve of the island exam  koenji s deal with horikita on the last day of the first semester  waits in the classroom  keisei comes to his seat  grim about surviving the island  you might as well ask me to catch a cloud  and vows to help his comrades despite being in a different group   honestly  surviving on an uninhabited island isn t something very good at   my perfect attendance record at least until now is one of the few things that i m proud of   you re starting to sound a bit sarcastic lately  you know  notes the girl specific hardships of the exam  promises keisei he ll lend a hand  chabashira warns the class not to be complacent and wishes none disappear  watches koenji negotiate with horikita  he fears the island exam and worries about ayanokoji going solo  6 million point penalty  vows to protect his comrades  gives the final checklist and a warning  hopes no one is expelled  negotiates with horikita for  full freedom  in exchange for a top result  ayanokoji admires her  beautifully added condition   if he fails to get first  he must contribute in future exams  she extracts a no lose deal from koenji  hopes class 2 d can take first while he takes 2nd 3rd to jump to class b  among the first year  up and coming  threats  with hosen  eyeing first place  competitors for first place include sakayanagi  ichinose  ryuen  first years hosen and amasawa  and third years nagumo  kiriyama and kiryuin  ayanokoji himself intends a high spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The eve of the island exam; Kōenji&#x27;s deal with Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.327–335<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the last day of the first semester, waits in the classroom; Keisei comes to his seat, grim about surviving the island (&quot;you might as well ask me to catch a cloud&quot;) and vows to help his comrades despite being in a different group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> &quot;Honestly, surviving on an uninhabited island isn&#x27;t something very good at.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.327<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My perfect attendance record at least until now is one of the few things that I&#x27;m proud of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re starting to sound a bit sarcastic lately, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.328<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the girl-specific hardships of the exam, promises Keisei he&#x27;ll lend a hand; Chabashira warns the class not to be complacent and wishes none disappear; watches Kōenji negotiate with Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.327–335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> He fears the island exam and worries about Ayanokōji going solo (6-million-point penalty); vows to protect his comrades.<span class=\"pg\">p.327–328<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Gives the final checklist and a warning; hopes no one is expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.328–329<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Negotiates with Horikita for &quot;full freedom&quot; in exchange for a top result; Ayanokōji admires her &quot;beautifully added condition&quot; (if he fails to get first, he must contribute in future exams).<span class=\"pg\">p.330–334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She extracts a no-lose deal from Kōenji; hopes Class 2-D can take first while he takes 2nd/3rd to jump to Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.330–334<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> Among the first-year &quot;up and coming&quot; threats (with Hōsen) eyeing first place.<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Competitors for first place include Sakayanagi, Ichinose, Ryūen, first-years Hōsen and Amasawa, and third-years Nagumo, Kiriyama and Kiryūin; Ayanokōji himself intends a high spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.335<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p315-1\">← Before: Arranging a partner for Ibuki; the &quot;go alone&quot; debate with Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p336-1\">→ After: Tsukishiro&#x27;s bombshell: Nanase is the enforcer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p336-1","v":"y2v2","y":2,"o":17,"k":"spoken","w":"tsukishiro nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka tsukishiro s bombshell  nanase is the enforcer in late july  tsukishiro   acting director  watches buses enter the school and presses a first year student to expel ayanokoji by any means in the island exam   please  are you done with your analysis yet  prolonging it anymore won t help you   you re saying i should  expel ayanokouji kiyotaka   i want you to expel ayanokouji kiyotaka by any means necessary  is that clear   once everything is taken care of  you will also return to your previous life   i m expecting great things from you  nanase tsubasa san  tsukishiro admits he pressured for budget increases and silenced school authorities over the exam s strict rules  with the allegations against chairman sakayanagi cleared  his tenure as temporary chairman is ending  so he s prepared  splendid fireworks  confirms nanase tsubasa is the white room enforcer sent to expel him   the girl s left hand clenches with  natural power  and tsukishiro smiles  expecting great things  revealed as the white room student   the mystery of the agent is solved for the reader  desperate to expel ayanokoji before losing his position  he and the enforcer will return to the place they re supposed to be","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p336-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tsukishiro&#x27;s bombshell: Nanase is the enforcer<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V2 · p.336–337<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In late July, Tsukishiro ( Acting Director) watches buses enter the school and presses a first-year student to expel Ayanokōji by any means in the island exam.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> &quot;Please, are you done with your analysis yet? Prolonging it anymore won&#x27;t help you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;re saying I should— expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.336<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> &quot;I want you to expel Ayanokouji Kiyotaka by any means necessary, is that clear?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Once everything is taken care of, you will also return to your previous life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m expecting great things from you— Nanase Tsubasa-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Tsukishiro admits he pressured for budget increases and silenced school authorities over the exam&#x27;s strict rules; with the allegations against Chairman Sakayanagi cleared, his tenure as temporary chairman is ending, so he&#x27;s prepared &quot;splendid fireworks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Confirms Nanase Tsubasa is the White Room enforcer sent to expel him — the girl&#x27;s left hand clenches with &quot;natural power,&quot; and Tsukishiro smiles, expecting great things.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Revealed as the White Room student — the mystery of the agent is solved for the reader.<span class=\"pg\">p.337<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Desperate to expel Ayanokōji before losing his position; he and the enforcer will return to the place they&#x27;re supposed to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.336–337<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v2-p327-1\">← Before: The eve of the island exam; Kōenji&#x27;s deal with Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p7-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.7-368<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p9-1\">→ After: Arriving at the island; Hirata&#x27;s resolve<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p9-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka arriving at the island  hirata s resolve on july 20  sails toward a much larger deserted island under a blue sky   the exam site for the next two weeks  temperature near 40 c   this is a much bigger island than the last one  just like mashima sensei said it d be   we ll only have to stay there for two weeks  but some students might end up having to retire at some point   i wonder if people used to live here   securing water will probably be our first priority   have you resolved yourself  yosuke   i ll put forth every effort so i have no regrets  that s the only thing i can do for the class  notes hirata s clenched fists on the railing   he yearns for peace but knows casualties are unavoidable  asks him pointedly if he s resolved  and he nods once  he voices worry about retirements heatstroke  ayanokoji tests his resolve and is answered with determination","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Arriving at the island; Hirata&#x27;s resolve<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.9–11<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On July 20, sails toward a much larger deserted island under a blue sky — the exam site for the next two weeks; temperature near 40°C.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;This is a much bigger island than the last one, just like Mashima-sensei said it&#x27;d be.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;ll only have to stay there for two weeks, but some students might end up having to retire at some point.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I wonder if people used to live here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Securing water will probably be our first priority.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Have you resolved yourself, Yōsuke?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll put forth every effort so I have no regrets. That&#x27;s the only thing I can do for the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Hirata&#x27;s clenched fists on the railing — he yearns for peace but knows casualties are unavoidable; asks him pointedly if he&#x27;s resolved, and he nods once.<span class=\"pg\">p.9–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He voices worry about retirements/heatstroke; Ayanokōji tests his resolve and is answered with determination.<span class=\"pg\">p.9–11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p7-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p11-1\">→ After: A secret &quot;date&quot; with Kei on the ship<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p11-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka a secret  date  with kei on the ship on july 19  day before landing  meets karuizawa on the aft deck of the luxury liner  saint venus   12 stories  700  capacity  for a rare secret moment alone   such an amazing view  huh    kei  it still kinda doesn t feel real   not that  i m talking  bout how it doesn t feel real that i m goin  out with you   how about you  kiyotaka  does it feel real to you   depending on what we re told about the special exam in the upcoming briefing session  there might be a few things i ll need you to do for me  notes they ve dated since spring break but never had a real date due to hiding the relationship  called her out primarily to brief her on possible exam tasks   yet physically meeting  just because we re dating  is a  different  interesting experience  his girlfriend  they steal time alone on the ship  and he prepares to give her instructions for the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">A secret &quot;date&quot; with Kei on the ship<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.11–14<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On July 19 (day before landing), meets Karuizawa on the aft deck of the luxury liner &quot;Saint Venus&quot; (12 stories, 700+ capacity) for a rare secret moment alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Such an amazing view, huh…?&quot; — Kei<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It still kinda doesn&#x27;t feel real…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Not that… I&#x27;m talking &#x27;bout how it doesn&#x27;t feel real that I&#x27;m goin&#x27; out with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How about you, Kiyotaka? Does it feel real to you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Depending on what we&#x27;re told about the special exam in the upcoming briefing session, there might be a few things I&#x27;ll need you to do for me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes they&#x27;ve dated since spring break but never had a real date due to hiding the relationship; called her out primarily to brief her on possible exam tasks — yet physically meeting &quot;just because we&#x27;re dating&quot; is a &quot;different, interesting experience.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend; they steal time alone on the ship, and he prepares to give her instructions for the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p9-1\">← Before: Arriving at the island; Hirata&#x27;s resolve<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p14-1\">→ After: The briefing: Ibuki and Kitō beside him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p14-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio kitou-hayato ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the briefing  ibuki and kito beside him at the movie theater briefing  sits near the back as a solo participant  ibuki ends up beside him  then kito takes the seat beyond her   ugh  why the hell are you sitting here   you didn t sit there on purpose  right   i m goin  somewhere else  so don t you dare follow me  got it  notices they followed the same logic  back seats for solo students  with nowhere else to sit  ibuki reluctantly remains  sandwiched between kito and myself    she d rather tolerate him than mix with the groups  sits beside him  refuses to follow him  but is forced to stay next to him  takes the seat that would have let ibuki escape","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The briefing: Ibuki and Kitō beside him<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.14–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the movie-theater briefing, sits near the back as a solo participant; Ibuki ends up beside him, then Kitō takes the seat beyond her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;…Ugh. Why the hell are you sitting here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You didn&#x27;t sit there on purpose, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m goin&#x27; somewhere else, so don&#x27;t you dare follow me, got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notices they followed the same logic (back seats for solo students); with nowhere else to sit, Ibuki reluctantly remains &quot;sandwiched between Kitō and myself&quot; — she&#x27;d rather tolerate him than mix with the groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Sits beside him, refuses to follow him, but is forced to stay next to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Takes the seat that would have let Ibuki escape.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p11-1\">← Before: A secret &quot;date&quot; with Kei on the ship<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p16-1\">→ After: The exam rules: points, watches, and twelve tables<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p16-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"mashima-tomonari ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the exam rules  points  watches  and twelve tables  starting tomorrow  your stay on the island will last for the next two weeks   the first three groups to arrive at area c8 will receive an  early bird bonus  with the first receiving 10 points  the second receiving 5 points  and the third receiving 3 points   should a group fail to reach a designated area three times in a row  they will lose one point   starting tomorrow  all students will be required to wear one of these watches until the end of the exam   the school will continuously monitor the wearer s body temperature  heart rate  blood pressure  blood oxygen level  sleep cycle  stress levels  and so on  groups of up to 6  bottom five groups face expulsion  nullifiable by points  6m solo  2m person in a 3 group  points via  basic movement  to designated areas   early bird 10 5 3   1 arrival per member  4 areas day  3 on first last  one randomly placed  3 consecutive misses cost points  one member reaching suffices  but early bird needs all  all wear health monitoring watches  warning alerts at abnormal metrics  emergency alert   24h checkup or retirement  gps summons staff after 5 min  watches can t be removed  points stop  and 12 different  tables  assign each group different designated area sequences so groups scatter  considers tsukishiro could tamper with his watch to make it malfunction and block his points   but only once or twice before it looks suspicious  as long as he stockpiles points he can avoid the bottom without competing for the top  delivers the exam briefing with hoshinomiya  he listens critically  already factoring in sabotage","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The exam rules: points, watches, and twelve tables<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.16–27<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> &quot;Starting tomorrow, your stay on the island will last for the next two weeks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> &quot;The first three groups to arrive at area C8 will receive an &#x27;Early Bird Bonus&#x27;, with the first receiving 10 points, the second receiving 5 points, and the third receiving 3 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> &quot;should a group fail to reach a designated area three times in a row, they will lose one point.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Starting tomorrow, all students will be required to wear one of these watches until the end of the exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;the school will continuously monitor the wearer&#x27;s body temperature, heart rate, blood pressure, blood oxygen level, sleep cycle, stress levels, and so on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Groups of up to 6; bottom five groups face expulsion (nullifiable by points: 6M solo, 2M/person in a 3-group); points via &quot;Basic Movement&quot; to designated areas — Early Bird 10/5/3 + 1 Arrival per member; 4 areas/day (3 on first/last), one randomly placed; 3 consecutive misses cost points; one member reaching suffices (but Early Bird needs all).<span class=\"pg\">p.16–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> All wear health-monitoring watches (Warning Alerts at abnormal metrics, Emergency Alert → 24h checkup or retirement, GPS summons staff after 5 min); watches can&#x27;t be removed (points stop) and 12 different &quot;Tables&quot; assign each group different designated-area sequences so groups scatter.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Considers Tsukishiro could tamper with his watch to make it malfunction and block his points — but only once or twice before it looks suspicious; as long as he stockpiles points he can avoid the bottom without competing for the top.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Delivers the exam briefing with Hoshinomiya; he listens critically, already factoring in sabotage.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p14-1\">← Before: The briefing: Ibuki and Kitō beside him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p43-1\">→ After: Disembarking: provisions, the first designated area, Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p43-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka disembarking  provisions  the first designated area  horikita at 8 40 a m  docks on the island  157 groups  36 first year 4 person  81 three person  32 two person  8 solo    five will be expelled  starting area d9  chose provisions totaling 4 960 points  tent  2l water  three 500ml bottles  12 portable meals  flashlight  battery charger  pot  lighter  paper cups   leaving backpack space for more  disembarkation order  first years first  then class a  gives second third years and class d a 15 30 minute disadvantage  first years finish around 9 00 when the first area is announced   good morning  did you sleep well yesterday   i see you re still patronizing me about what happened last year   there s no use getting worked up at this point  it d just be a waste of energy   mine is f9  looks like the two of us have different tables   i won t worry about you anymore  then  at least try to manage a decently high ranking  deliberately waits  30 min at the harbor to observe the flow  no need to rush without early bird ambitions  worries about money  can t afford a hat  has a contract with kushida  couldn t raise funds for kei alone  recognizes horikita has grown  leagues ahead  of a year ago  chats before departing  their tables differ  his d7  hers f9  so they go separate ways  he warns her about going solo and worries she ll be troubled if he s expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Disembarking: provisions, the first designated area, Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.43–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At 8:40 a.m. docks on the island; 157 groups (36 first-year 4-person, 81 three-person, 32 two-person, 8 solo) — five will be expelled. Starting area D9.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Good morning. Did you sleep well yesterday?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I see you&#x27;re still patronizing me about what happened last year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s no use getting worked up at this point. It&#x27;d just be a waste of energy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Chose provisions totaling 4,960 points: tent, 2L water, three 500ml bottles, 12 portable meals, flashlight, battery charger, pot, lighter, paper cups — leaving backpack space for more.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Disembarkation order (first-years first, then Class A) gives second/third-years and Class D a 15–30 minute disadvantage; first-years finish around 9:00 when the first area is announced.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Mine is F9. Looks like the two of us have different Tables.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I won&#x27;t worry about you anymore, then. At least try to manage a decently high ranking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately waits ~30 min at the harbor to observe the flow (no need to rush without Early Bird ambitions); worries about money (can&#x27;t afford a hat, has a contract with Kushida, couldn&#x27;t raise funds for Kei alone); recognizes Horikita has grown &quot;leagues ahead&quot; of a year ago.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Chats before departing; their Tables differ (his D7, hers F9) so they go separate ways; he warns her about going solo and worries she&#x27;ll be troubled if he&#x27;s expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p16-1\">← Before: The exam rules: points, watches, and twelve tables<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p50-1\">→ After: Kiryūin-senpai at the starting area<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p50-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"kiryuin-sakura nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kiryuin senpai at the starting area notices no third years passing  turns back and sees class 3 b disembarking  calm and composed  can t find nagumo but is approached by kiryuin   you re still here  ayanokoji   but you re alone  right  you should be fine to think it over while you walk   there s something  enchanting about seeing the entire student body scatter throughout the uninhabited island   though there are more than 400 of us  we re nothing but insignificant specks of dust in comparison   d7    his first area  she has the same destination politely declines kiryuin s offer to explain the area system  treating her as a  direct competitor  judges her keen eyed and  like him  tackling the exam alone   she seems to look forward to it  third year who also goes solo  they share the d7 destination for the first interval and she proposes traveling together  searches for him among the third years but can t find him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p50-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiryūin-senpai at the starting area<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.50–52<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Notices no third-years passing; turns back and sees Class 3-B disembarking, calm and composed; can&#x27;t find Nagumo but is approached by Kiryūin.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">kiryuin-sakura<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;re still here, Ayanokōji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;But you&#x27;re alone, right? You should be fine to think it over while you walk.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s something… enchanting about seeing the entire student body scatter throughout the uninhabited island.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Though there are more than 400 of us, we&#x27;re nothing but insignificant specks of dust in comparison.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;D7.&quot; — his first area; she has the same destination<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Politely declines Kiryūin&#x27;s offer to explain the area system, treating her as a &quot;direct competitor&quot;; judges her keen-eyed and, like him, tackling the exam alone — she seems to look forward to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">kiryuin-sakura<\/b> Third-year who also goes solo; they share the D7 destination for the first interval and she proposes traveling together.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Searches for him among the third-years but can&#x27;t find him.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p43-1\">← Before: Disembarking: provisions, the first designated area, Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p53-1\">→ After: First day: Tasks, Sudō&#x27;s grip strength, Hoshinomiya<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p53-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka first day  tasks  sudo s grip strength  hoshinomiya travels from d9 to d7  about 50 minutes for him  encounters nanase and her class 1 d group  amasawa  hosen  then multiple tasks appear  tasks  fire starting  5 3 2 points  geography test in d8  10 points  he arrives too late to register for most   sudo kun has changed an awful lot  don tcha think  i wonder who s responsible   just for the record  it wasn t me   just like how katsuragi kun transferred to class 2 b  ayanokoji kun can transfer over to my class   i wouldn t be able to come up with 20 million points even if i saved up until the day i graduate  watches the grip strength measurement task  third year oshio first  sudo  who split from ike hondo to secure a spot  takes first   his group gains 5 points to a likely 8  while ayanokoji earned only 1  attributes sudo s growth mainly to horikita  hoshinomiya  dropped to class c  having lost her cool  proposes he transfer to her class  he declines with reasoned logic  his former class a teacher  now class 2 c  keeps him at a task site as an excuse to talk  he finds her childlike and wants to avoid meeting her again  takes first in the grip strength task  ayanokoji credits horikita for his growth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">First day: Tasks, Sudō&#x27;s grip strength, Hoshinomiya<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.53–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Travels from D9 to D7 (about 50 minutes for him); encounters Nanase and her Class 1-D group (Amasawa, Hōsen), then multiple Tasks appear.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> &quot;Sudō-kun has changed an awful lot, don&#x27;tcha think? I wonder who&#x27;s responsible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just for the record, it wasn&#x27;t me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> &quot;Just like how Katsuragi-kun transferred to Class 2-B, Ayanokōji-kun can transfer over to my class!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Tasks: fire-starting (5/3/2 points), Geography Test in D8 (10 points); he arrives too late to register for most.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wouldn&#x27;t be able to come up with 20 million points even if I saved up until the day I graduate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches the Grip Strength Measurement Task (third-year Oshio first); Sudō (who split from Ike/Hondō to secure a spot) takes first — his group gains 5 points to a likely 8, while Ayanokōji earned only 1; attributes Sudō&#x27;s growth mainly to Horikita. Hoshinomiya (dropped to Class C, having lost her cool) proposes he transfer to her class; he declines with reasoned logic.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> His former Class A teacher (now Class 2-C), keeps him at a Task site as an excuse to talk; he finds her childlike and wants to avoid meeting her again.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Takes first in the grip-strength Task; Ayanokōji credits Horikita for his growth.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p50-1\">← Before: Kiryūin-senpai at the starting area<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p68-1\">→ After: First-day tally; Nanase; camping and water Task analysis<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p68-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"narration spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka first day tally  nanase  camping and water task analysis  afterward  i made my way to two other new task sites that showed up   second time today huh   how did it go for you today   when it comes to designated areas  the three of us earned 8 points  i didn t manage to make it to the second area in time  but i took first place in a task instead  so we re at 13 points altogether  his first day  only 2 points from basic movement  1 each at b7 and d7  for a total of 3    one of the lowest ranked groups  camps near e7 in an open area  avoiding direct sunlight  pours water into a paper cup to avoid mouth bacteria contaminating the bottle  analyzes 68 tasks that day  14 giving mineral water  8 of them  competitive relief tasks   2l 1 5l 1l 500ml by arrival order  3 2 1 points  evenly distributed   a reliable  unbiased water supply if they continue  unfazed by his low rank  only day one  methodical about health  water handling  camp site  and about reading the exam s hidden structures  crosses paths a second time  she reports 13 points  their conversation is almost a status report   she s  taking action on her own   no hosen amasawa","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">First-day tally; Nanase; camping and water Task analysis<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.68–71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Second time today huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How did it go for you today?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;when it comes to designated areas, the three of us earned 8 points. I didn&#x27;t manage to make it to the second area in time, but I took first place in a Task instead, so we&#x27;re at 13 points altogether.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Afterward, I made my way to two other new Task sites that showed up&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> His first day: only 2 points from Basic Movement (1 each at B7 and D7) for a total of 3 — &quot;one of the lowest-ranked groups.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Camps near E7 in an open area (avoiding direct sunlight); pours water into a paper cup to avoid mouth bacteria contaminating the bottle; analyzes 68 Tasks that day, 14 giving mineral water, 8 of them &quot;competitive relief Tasks&quot; (2L/1.5L/1L/500ml by arrival order, 3/2/1 points) evenly distributed — a reliable, unbiased water supply if they continue.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Unfazed by his low rank (only day one); methodical about health (water handling, camp site) and about reading the exam&#x27;s hidden structures.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Crosses paths a second time; she reports 13 points; their conversation is almost a status report — she&#x27;s &quot;taking action on her own&quot; (no Hōsen/Amasawa).<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p53-1\">← Before: First day: Tasks, Sudō&#x27;s grip strength, Hoshinomiya<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p75-1\">→ After: Day two hot streak; Nanase asks to tag along<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p75-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa housen-kazuomi amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka day two hot streak  nanase asks to tag along wakes at 6 30 in his shady camp  the first area of day two is e8   right next to camp   and he wins first place  10 points  recovering day one s deficit   ayanokoji senpai  it seems we meet again    nanase  by any chance  do you think that we might share the same table   if it s not too much trouble  would you perhaps allow me to accompany you for a while   both hosen kun and amasawa san felt that we would be better off if we all acted independently  so everything more or less fell apart   you d ultimately lose points by doing that  nanase   you re not uncertain because you think i might hold you back  it s more that you re not able to trust me  isn t it   alright  if that s what you want  then go ahead  racks up 23 points on day two  10 5 5  for 26 total  notes even a hot streak barely matches a steady 3 person group  18 pts  suspicious that he and nanase have met 3 times   more than coincidence suggests  but no proof  notes her group  hosen amasawa  has broken down into independent action  allows her to tag along because refusing wouldn t stop her following  and her presence offers a chance to probe her  she asks to accompany him  claims her group dissolved  defers bonuses tasks to him  he agrees mainly to  find out exactly what nanase was capable of  nanase says he wanted independent action  likewise wanted independent action","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Day two hot streak; Nanase asks to tag along<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.75–82<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Wakes at 6:30 in his shady camp; the first area of day two is E8 — right next to camp — and he wins first place (10 points), recovering day one&#x27;s deficit.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokōji-senpai, it seems we meet again.&quot; — Nanase<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;By any chance, do you think that we might share the same Table?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If it&#x27;s not too much trouble, would you perhaps allow me to accompany you for a while?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Both Hōsen-kun and Amasawa-san felt that we would be better off if we all acted independently, so everything more or less fell apart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;d ultimately lose points by doing that, Nanase.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;you&#x27;re not uncertain because you think I might hold you back, it&#x27;s more that you&#x27;re not able to trust me, isn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Alright. If that&#x27;s what you want, then go ahead.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Racks up 23 points on day two (10+5+5) for 26 total; notes even a hot streak barely matches a steady 3-person group (18 pts); suspicious that he and Nanase have met 3 times — more than coincidence suggests, but no proof; notes her group (Hōsen/Amasawa) has broken down into independent action; allows her to tag along because refusing wouldn&#x27;t stop her following, and her presence offers a chance to probe her.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She asks to accompany him, claims her group dissolved, defers bonuses/Tasks to him; he agrees mainly to &quot;find out exactly what Nanase was capable of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Nanase says he wanted independent action.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Likewise wanted independent action.<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p68-1\">← Before: First-day tally; Nanase; camping and water Task analysis<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p82-1\">→ After: The anime quiz; Sudō&#x27;s group wins; Ike&#x27;s funk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p82-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hondou-ryoutarou ike-kanji nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the anime quiz  sudo s group wins  ike s funk heads with nanase to a quiz task at f8  he wanted football juggling at e5 but changed route for her    up to 12 groups  multiple choice  genre revealed as  anime   yo  ayanokoji  there s only three spots left   what the hell is this   forreal  this is uber mega easy  the questions  e g   correct title of the thirteenth episode of tv anime mobile samurai bombdam  opening theme of  dashu sea chicken  are entirely outside his knowledge   he guesses  gets 4 20  20  worse than random  nanase gets 5  sudo s group wins with 95  thanks to ike and hondo s trivia knowledge  genuinely puzzled by the anime genre  observes ike listless and hondo struggling to converse with him  worries about ike s mental state  shinohara now with komiya  but doubts sudo can give  delicate emotional support  concludes sudo s group is fine on points and that worrying about them is getting ahead of himself  warns him when nanase  an  enemy  who worked with hosen  tags along  sudo reluctantly backs off  they agree to camp together at g9 beach at 5 30  notices he s  out of it    a lasting impact from shinohara   and worries about him  she sees through his concern for sudo s group  discerns ike may be  sick  and repeatedly asks him to disregard her presence when choosing routes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p82-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The anime quiz; Sudō&#x27;s group wins; Ike&#x27;s funk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.82–92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Heads with Nanase to a quiz Task at F8 (he wanted Football Juggling at E5 but changed route for her) — up to 12 groups, multiple-choice, genre revealed as &quot;Anime.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Yo! Ayanokōji! There&#x27;s only three spots left!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;…What the hell is this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">hondou-ryoutarou<\/b> &quot;Forreal!? This is uber-mega-easy!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The questions (e.g. &quot;correct title of the Thirteenth episode of TV Anime Mobile Samurai Bombdam,&quot; opening theme of &quot;Dashu Sea Chicken&quot;) are entirely outside his knowledge — he guesses, gets 4/20 (20%, worse than random); Nanase gets 5; Sudō&#x27;s group wins with 95% thanks to Ike and Hondō&#x27;s trivia knowledge.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Genuinely puzzled by the anime genre; observes Ike listless and Hondō struggling to converse with him, worries about Ike&#x27;s mental state (Shinohara now with Komiya) but doubts Sudō can give &quot;delicate emotional support&quot;; concludes Sudō&#x27;s group is fine on points and that worrying about them is getting ahead of himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Warns him when Nanase (an &quot;enemy&quot; who worked with Hōsen) tags along; Sudō reluctantly backs off; they agree to camp together at G9 beach at 5:30.<span class=\"pg\">p.84–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Notices he&#x27;s &quot;out of it&quot; — a lasting impact from Shinohara — and worries about him.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She sees through his concern for Sudō&#x27;s group, discerns Ike may be &quot;sick,&quot; and repeatedly asks him to disregard her presence when choosing routes.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p75-1\">← Before: Day two hot streak; Nanase asks to tag along<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p93-1\">→ After: Same Table confirmed; camping plan; beach meetup<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p93-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka same table confirmed  camping plan  beach meetup  before that  nanase  i want to see your tablet   it seems i have the same table as senpai after all   no  i m not going to go out of my way for the arrival bonus this time   once we re done with the tasks  i think we ll head to h9 to set up camp  his fourth  random  designation is i7  requiring crossing a mountain  chooses to skip it for math english tasks at g8 g9  nanase s tablet confirms the same i7   same table  plans to camp at h9 to avoid starting in the next designated area centered on i7  agrees to sudo s proposal to meet at the g9 beach at 5 30   an unexpected but not bad chance to reach ike without seeming to have ulterior motives  confirms same table  she agrees to all route camp decisions  without a single complaint  proposes the beach meetup  ayanokoji accepts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p93-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Same Table confirmed; camping plan; beach meetup<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.93–96<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Before that, Nanase, I want to see your tablet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;It seems I have the same Table as Senpai after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No, I&#x27;m not going to go out of my way for the Arrival Bonus this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Once we&#x27;re done with the Tasks, I think we&#x27;ll head to H9 to set up camp.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> His fourth (random) designation is I7, requiring crossing a mountain; chooses to skip it for Math/English Tasks at G8/G9; Nanase&#x27;s tablet confirms the same I7 — same Table.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Plans to camp at H9 to avoid starting in the next designated area centered on I7; agrees to Sudō&#x27;s proposal to meet at the G9 beach at 5:30 — an unexpected but not bad chance to reach Ike without seeming to have ulterior motives.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Confirms same Table; she agrees to all route/camp decisions &quot;without a single complaint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Proposes the beach meetup; Ayanokōji accepts.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p82-1\">← Before: The anime quiz; Sudō&#x27;s group wins; Ike&#x27;s funk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p110-1\">→ After: Morning: Nanase&#x27;s worry about Ike; traveling together<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p110-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa sudou-ken ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka morning  nanase s worry about ike  traveling together woken at 6 by nanase outside his tent  worried she said too much to ike the previous night  he reassures her she  called it like it was   it s about ike senpai  do you think i said a little too much last night   i feel like ike senpai is in a sort of precarious position right now   sudo  what designated area did you get   we got i8 so if you two are goin  the same way we can head out together   well  anyway  i guess i ll lead  so you all can just follow me    ike suspects nanase s concern  about staying with sudo s group  might be genuine or artificial   possibly to keep him from the designated areas  notes traveling with them risks being unable to take extreme measures  his own routes  observes ike has become more lively  but judges most of his growth superficial   a false show of courage isn t all that different from the real thing  she worries about ike and her words to him  he probes whether her feelings are genuine  now leading and lively  his growth is a  first step  that may regress  their areas differ but routes overlap  they travel together","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p110-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Morning: Nanase&#x27;s worry about Ike; traveling together<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.110–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Woken at 6 by Nanase outside his tent, worried she said too much to Ike the previous night; he reassures her she &quot;called it like it was.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s about Ike-senpai. Do you think I said a little too much last night…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I feel like Ike-senpai is in a sort-of precarious position right now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sudō, what designated area did you get?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We got I8 so if you two are goin&#x27; the same way we can head out together.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, anyway. I guess I&#x27;ll lead, so you all can just follow me.&quot; — Ike<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Suspects Nanase&#x27;s concern (about staying with Sudō&#x27;s group) might be genuine or artificial — possibly to keep him from the designated areas; notes traveling with them risks being unable to take extreme measures (his own routes); observes Ike has become more lively, but judges most of his growth superficial — a false show of courage isn&#x27;t all that different from the real thing.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She worries about Ike and her words to him; he probes whether her feelings are genuine.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Now leading and lively; his growth is a &quot;first step&quot; that may regress.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Their areas differ but routes overlap; they travel together.<span class=\"pg\">p.113–114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p93-1\">← Before: Same Table confirmed; camping plan; beach meetup<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p116-1\">→ After: Beach Flags: Nanase&#x27;s physical prowess; Kiriyama<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p116-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama nanase-tsubasa nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka beach flags  nanase s physical prowess  kiriyama arrives at j9 just before 9  second random area is j5  they reach it first  he gets early bird  nanase arrival bonus  then return to j6 where a  beach flags showdown  task is being set up  beach flags  lifeguard training event    8 boys 8 girls  one per group  single elimination  first place 6 points   choice of reward  all participants a 500ml water bottle  at the task  kiriyama  student council vp  rushes to grab the last male slot  ayanokoji is shut out but encourages nanase to enter   if senpai can t participate then i ll sit this one out as well    nanase  since you re surrendering all of the early bird bonuses to me  the gap between our points is only going to get wider   ayanokoji  don t say anything unnecessary  watches all 15 competitors are third years  abnormal   likely tied to kiriyama nagumo  kiriyama wins the boys  bracket decisively  nanase  in a blue green bikini  the only first year  dominates the girls    reacting in  perfect sync  with the gun  beating tomioka  c  and then tokunaga  b  in the final  with strength and energy to spare  concludes her true physical ability exceeds the oaa s b  she wins beach flags decisively  her reflexes are  several magnitudes faster  her oaa rating appears understated  white room conditioning  grabs the last male slot  wins the boys  event  warns ayanokoji not to say anything  nagumo is nearby  is in the ocean  messing about  with third years   kiriyama didn t want ayanokoji to see","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Beach Flags: Nanase&#x27;s physical prowess; Kiriyama<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.116–121<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives at J9 just before 9; second random area is J5; they reach it first (he gets Early Bird, Nanase Arrival bonus), then return to J6 where a &quot;Beach Flags Showdown&quot; Task is being set up. At the Task, Kiriyama (student council VP) rushes to grab the last male slot; Ayanokōji is shut out but encourages Nanase to enter.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If Senpai can&#x27;t participate then I&#x27;ll sit this one out as well.&quot; — Nanase<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Since you&#x27;re surrendering all of the Early Bird Bonuses to me, the gap between our points is only going to get wider.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> &quot;Ayanokōji, don&#x27;t say anything unnecessary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Beach Flags (lifeguard training event) — 8 boys/8 girls, one per group, single-elimination; first place 6 points + choice of reward, all participants a 500ml water bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches all 15 competitors are third-years (abnormal — likely tied to Kiriyama/Nagumo); Kiriyama wins the boys&#x27; bracket decisively; Nanase (in a blue-green bikini, the only first-year) dominates the girls&#x27; — reacting in &quot;perfect sync&quot; with the gun, beating Tomioka (C+) and then Tokunaga (B+) in the final &quot;with strength and energy to spare&quot;; concludes her true Physical Ability exceeds the OAA&#x27;s B+.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She wins Beach Flags decisively; her reflexes are &quot;several magnitudes faster&quot;; her OAA rating appears understated (White Room conditioning).<span class=\"pg\">p.120–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> Grabs the last male slot, wins the boys&#x27; event, warns Ayanokōji not to say anything (Nagumo is nearby).<span class=\"pg\">p.120–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Is in the ocean &quot;messing about&quot; with third-years — Kiriyama didn&#x27;t want Ayanokōji to see.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p110-1\">← Before: Morning: Nanase&#x27;s worry about Ike; traveling together<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p130-1\">→ After: Nagumo and Asahina&#x27;s veiled warnings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p130-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi asahina-nazuna kiriyama ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nagumo and asahina s veiled warnings goes to the shoreline where nagumo beckons  nagumo swims with asahina and others  having rented swimsuits and a beach ball   i ll say it again just to be sure  don t get in my way  got it   from what i saw  it didn t look like you were able to participate in that task   how about you come take a swim with us   the real event starts tomorrow    the day top 10 bottom 10 rankings are announced  first and second years have no right to stand on the winners  podium   horikita senpai would probably be fairly disappointed if you self destructed and got yourself expelled   word is that you re working alone  nagumo has a strategy to prevent first second years from reaching the top  to be enacted if needed  asahina starts to whisper that if nagumo comes after him things could get dicey  advising him to meet other groups   cut short when nagumo returns  ayanokoji infers nagumo has a strategy only he can implement  warns him not to get in his way  hints at a strategy against lower years  knows about horikita  class 2 c s mii chan  tries to warn him about nagumo coming after him  repeated the  don t get in my way  warning earlier","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p130-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo and Asahina&#x27;s veiled warnings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.130–132<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Goes to the shoreline where Nagumo beckons; Nagumo swims with Asahina and others, having rented swimsuits and a beach ball.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ll say it again just to be sure: Don&#x27;t get in my way, got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;From what I saw, it didn&#x27;t look like you were able to participate in that Task.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How about you come take a swim with us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;the real event starts tomorrow.&quot; — the day top-10/bottom-10 rankings are announced<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;First and second-years have no right to stand on the winners&#x27; podium.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horikita-senpai would probably be fairly disappointed if you self-destructed and got yourself expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Word is that you&#x27;re working alone?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Nagumo has a strategy to prevent first/second-years from reaching the top (to be enacted if needed); Asahina starts to whisper that if Nagumo comes after him things could get dicey, advising him to meet other groups — cut short when Nagumo returns; Ayanokōji infers Nagumo has a strategy only he can implement.<span class=\"pg\">p.130–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Warns him not to get in his way; hints at a strategy against lower years; knows about Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.130–132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Class 2-C&#x27;s Mii-chan; tries to warn him about Nagumo coming after him.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> Repeated the &quot;don&#x27;t get in my way&quot; warning earlier.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p116-1\">← Before: Beach Flags: Nanase&#x27;s physical prowess; Kiriyama<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p135-1\">→ After: Water shortage; probing Nanase about middle school<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p135-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka water shortage  probing nanase about middle school both down to one bottle of water    this is our first major hurdle  he considers returning to the starting area to rehydrate  too risky with nanase  who d have to retire if she fell ill   ayanokoji senpai  why did you decide to take part in the exam alone   i don t have many friends  so i couldn t find anyone to group up with   back when you faced off against hosen kun  your movements were different from those of a normal high school student   if you managed to notice something like that  then you re not exactly a normal high school student either  nanase   in the past  i get the sense that i used to smile more   after all  an incident took place that i believe changed me forever  they probe each other   she notes his white room like movements  he notes a white room student never attended middle school  so asks about hers  she claims she smiled more and spoke to others more before  an incident  changed her  light dark  he chooses not to pry  sensing she s baiting him  deliberates whether a person s core nature can truly change  mutual probing  her  incident  and shift from light to dark hint at her past  and her role","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p135-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Water shortage; probing Nanase about middle school<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.135–138<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Both down to one bottle of water — &quot;this is our first major hurdle&quot;; he considers returning to the starting area to rehydrate (too risky with Nanase, who&#x27;d have to retire if she fell ill).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Ayanokōji-senpai, why did you decide to take part in the exam alone?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t have many friends, so I couldn&#x27;t find anyone to group up with.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Back when you faced off against Hōsen-kun, your movements were different from those of a normal high school student.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you managed to notice something like that, then you&#x27;re not exactly a normal high school student either, Nanase.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In the past─ I get the sense that I used to smile more.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;After all, an incident took place that I believe changed me forever…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> They probe each other — she notes his White Room-like movements; he notes a White Room student never attended middle school, so asks about hers; she claims she smiled more and spoke to others more before &quot;an incident&quot; changed her (light→dark); he chooses not to pry, sensing she&#x27;s baiting him; deliberates whether a person&#x27;s core nature can truly change.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Mutual probing; her &quot;incident&quot; and shift from light to dark hint at her past (and her role).<span class=\"pg\">p.135–138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p130-1\">← Before: Nagumo and Asahina&#x27;s veiled warnings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p164-1\">→ After: Night search: Komiya and Kinoshita fallen; finding Shinohara<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p164-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji nanase-tsubasa komiya shinohara ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka night search  komiya and kinoshita fallen  finding shinohara woken before dawn  the group  him  nanase  sudo  ike  hondo  sets out with three flashlights  he arranges the formation  putting ike at the rear   nanase  ike  and i will each take a flashlight   is that  komiya    sudo he concludes it would be safest to assume shinohara was caught up in a similar accident to komiya and kinoshita  he says he checked komiya and kinoshita s gps earlier  finds komiya and kinoshita  class 2 b  at the bottom of a steep  narrow slope  both with injured left legs and emergency alerts  shinohara and their backpacks are missing  shinohara is found alive higher up the slope  ike charges up after hearing her voice  ayanokoji follows  leaving his tablet with nanase  calm and organized in the crisis   directs the search formation  assesses the injuries and footprints  prevents ike from running off recklessly  and carefully avoids letting shinohara see him  conjure up a fabricated story   he doubts her account  restrains him from rushing off  supports him reaching shinohara  she accompanies him  points out an  out of place  sound  a phone vibration  later comes to find them and leads the way back  finds him injured at the bottom of the slope  finds her alive but frantic","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p164-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Night search: Komiya and Kinoshita fallen; finding Shinohara<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.164–180<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Woken before dawn; the group (him, Nanase, Sudō, Ike, Hondō) sets out with three flashlights; he arranges the formation, putting Ike at the rear.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#komiya\">Komiya<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara.html\">Shinohara<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nanase, Ike, and I will each take a flashlight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is that… Komiya!?&quot; — Sudō<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He concludes it would be safest to assume Shinohara was caught up in a similar accident to Komiya and Kinoshita.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He says he checked Komiya and Kinoshita&#x27;s GPS earlier.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Finds Komiya and Kinoshita (Class 2-B) at the bottom of a steep, narrow slope, both with injured left legs and Emergency Alerts; Shinohara and their backpacks are missing. Shinohara is found alive higher up the slope. Ike charges up after hearing her voice; Ayanokōji follows, leaving his tablet with Nanase.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and organized in the crisis — directs the search formation, assesses the injuries and footprints, prevents Ike from running off recklessly, and carefully avoids letting Shinohara see him &quot;conjure up a fabricated story&quot; (he doubts her account).<span class=\"pg\">p.164–180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Restrains him from rushing off; supports him reaching Shinohara.<span class=\"pg\">p.172, 178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She accompanies him, points out an &quot;out-of-place&quot; sound (a phone vibration), later comes to find them and leads the way back.<span class=\"pg\">p.166–189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya<\/b> Finds him injured at the bottom of the slope.<span class=\"pg\">p.169–179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> Finds her alive but frantic.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p135-1\">← Before: Water shortage; probing Nanase about middle school<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p180-1\">→ After: Shinohara&#x27;s claim of a &quot;third party&quot;; the GPS contradiction<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p180-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"shinohara nanase-tsubasa chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka shinohara s claim of a  third party  the gps contradiction  somebody  i saw somebody push  he reasons that if someone had pushed komiya  there would be more evidence than a single injury  reasons with nanase that shinohara s story of an  unknown third party  is inconsistent   a pusher would have finished the job  and komiya didn t notice anyone  nanase reaches the same conclusion  suspects the culprit might not be a student  teachers don t wear watches gps  and asks chabashira to investigate discreetly  they discuss the testimony  she agrees someone likely pushed them but is skeptical of shinohara s framing  shows him gps data   only shinohara s signal was nearby at 4 56 24 am  komiya s emergency alert  so the school concludes she fabricated the third party  he whispers a request for a discreet investigation  her claim of being pushed  he doubts it but investigates","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p180-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Shinohara&#x27;s claim of a &quot;third party&quot;; the GPS contradiction<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.180–192<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shinohara.html\">Shinohara<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> &quot;Somebody… I saw somebody push─&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He reasons that if someone had pushed Komiya, there would be more evidence than a single injury.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons with Nanase that Shinohara&#x27;s story of an &quot;unknown third party&quot; is inconsistent — a pusher would have finished the job, and Komiya didn&#x27;t notice anyone; Nanase reaches the same conclusion; suspects the culprit might not be a student (teachers don&#x27;t wear watches/GPS) and asks Chabashira to investigate discreetly.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> They discuss the testimony; she agrees someone likely pushed them but is skeptical of Shinohara&#x27;s framing.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Shows him GPS data — only Shinohara&#x27;s signal was nearby at 4:56:24 AM (Komiya&#x27;s Emergency Alert), so the school concludes she fabricated the third party; he whispers a request for a discreet investigation.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> Her claim of being pushed; he doubts it but investigates.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p164-1\">← Before: Night search: Komiya and Kinoshita fallen; finding Shinohara<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p199-1\">→ After: Ike&#x27;s confession; the plan to save Shinohara<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p199-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji shinohara sudou-ken komiya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ike s confession  the plan to save shinohara  in order to guarantee that you save shinohara  she ll have to join up with a group with at least three slots for extra group members   it s not like it s impossible  there is one idea that comes to mind that has a high probability of working out   i ll be setting up a contingency plan of sorts just in case something goes wrong   we might be forced to make a tough choice about who to save   sudo  take care of ike and the others  watches ike finally declare he ll save shinohara  whether you like it or not   an inelegant but heartfelt  confession  decides not to reveal his plan  it would weaken their resolve  instructs ike to protect her and earn points  and sets up a  contingency plan  while warning they may have to abandon her if others also fall into the bottom five  entrusts sudo to watch ike  his growth moves him to protect shinohara  ayanokoji supports and warns him  works to save her  arranges the rescue plan  entrusted to take care of ike and the others    the one capable of making the most sensible decisions  his parting words to ike  show me how much of a man you are  entrust shinohara to his rival   ayanokoji realizes komiya knew shinohara cared for ike","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ike&#x27;s confession; the plan to save Shinohara<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.199–207<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara.html\">Shinohara<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#komiya\">Komiya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;In order to guarantee that you save Shinohara, she&#x27;ll have to join up with a group with at least three slots for extra group members.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not like it&#x27;s impossible. There is one idea that comes to mind that has a high probability of working out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll be setting up a contingency plan of sorts just in case something goes wrong.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;we might be forced to make a tough choice about who to save.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudō, take care of Ike and the others.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches Ike finally declare he&#x27;ll save Shinohara &quot;whether you like it or not&quot; (an inelegant but heartfelt &quot;confession&quot;); decides not to reveal his plan (it would weaken their resolve), instructs Ike to protect her and earn points, and sets up a &quot;contingency plan&quot; while warning they may have to abandon her if others also fall into the bottom five; entrusts Sudō to watch Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> His growth moves him to protect Shinohara; Ayanokōji supports and warns him.<span class=\"pg\">p.201–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> Works to save her; arranges the rescue plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Entrusted to take care of Ike and the others — &quot;the one capable of making the most sensible decisions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya<\/b> His parting words to Ike (&quot;Show me how much of a man you are&quot;) entrust Shinohara to his rival — Ayanokōji realizes Komiya knew Shinohara cared for Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p180-1\">← Before: Shinohara&#x27;s claim of a &quot;third party&quot;; the GPS contradiction<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p207-1\">→ After: Day four: standings revealed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p207-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka day four  standings revealed on day four the top 10 bottom 10 groups are revealed with detailed breakdowns  7 of the bottom 10 are from class 3 b and 3 d  last place is a class 3 d trio with 21 points  one member retired sick on day one  checks the standings first thing  more important than the leaders  to gauge expulsion risk  notes his own group is half an hour behind for g3 and can t get early bird","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Day four: standings revealed<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.207–208<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> On day four the top-10/bottom-10 groups are revealed with detailed breakdowns; 7 of the bottom 10 are from Class 3-B and 3-D; last place is a Class 3-D trio with 21 points (one member retired sick on day one).<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Checks the standings first thing (more important than the leaders) to gauge expulsion risk; notes his own group is half an hour behind for G3 and can&#x27;t get Early Bird.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p199-1\">← Before: Ike&#x27;s confession; the plan to save Shinohara<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p211-1\">→ After: Rankings and the Ryūen/Katsuragi strategy meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p211-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka rankings and the ryuen katsuragi strategy meeting reviews standings   shinohara s group sinking toward last  top groups led by nagumo s class 3 a group and kiriyama s  koenji in 4th with 126 points  most from early bird  his own point total 52   i m just your travelling companion  ayanokoji senpai  please don t feel   it just so happens that i ve been looking for you  ryuen   komiya and kinoshita retired   sorry nanase  but i can t let you listen to the rest of this conversation   kuku  i see  with a plan like that there really is a way for shinohara to survive   you ve got balls changing shit up like this   if you run into ichinose  can you tell her the plan as well  finds ryuen and katsuragi fishing  taking a break   katsuragi has learned to control ryuen  tells them of the retirements and shinohara s fabricated claim  dismisses nanase  then shares his secret strategy to save shinohara  keeping it from her and the first years to avoid a cross year confrontation  ryuen agrees   their interests align since shinohara s group spans both classes  strategically secretive   deliberately excludes nanase  trusts ryuen to tell katsuragi  asks him to inform ichinose  and doubts sakayanagi will help  she s not the type to sit back and let the first years look down on her  shares his rescue strategy  ryuen agrees to cooperate  now a full class 2 b member   part of the fishing break  reacts to the retirements  she accompanies him  he dismisses her for the secret discussion   she understands  predicts she won t easily lend a hand but will act if first years look down on her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p211-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Rankings and the Ryūen/Katsuragi strategy meeting<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.211–219<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reviews standings — Shinohara&#x27;s group sinking toward last; top groups led by Nagumo&#x27;s Class 3-A group and Kiriyama&#x27;s; Kōenji in 4th with 126 points (most from Early Bird); his own point total 52.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m just your travelling companion, Ayanokōji-senpai. Please don&#x27;t feel&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It just so happens that I&#x27;ve been looking for you, Ryūen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Komiya and Kinoshita retired.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry Nanase, but I can&#x27;t let you listen to the rest of this conversation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Kuku, I see. With a plan like that there really is a way for Shinohara to survive.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;ve got balls changing shit up like this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you run into Ichinose, can you tell her the plan as well?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Finds Ryūen and Katsuragi fishing (taking a break — Katsuragi has learned to control Ryūen); tells them of the retirements and Shinohara&#x27;s fabricated claim; dismisses Nanase, then shares his secret strategy to save Shinohara (keeping it from her and the first-years to avoid a cross-year confrontation); Ryūen agrees — their interests align since Shinohara&#x27;s group spans both classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Strategically secretive — deliberately excludes Nanase, trusts Ryūen to tell Katsuragi, asks him to inform Ichinose, and doubts Sakayanagi will help (&quot;she&#x27;s not the type to sit back and let the first-years look down on her&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.211–219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Shares his rescue strategy; Ryūen agrees to cooperate.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Now a full Class 2-B member — part of the fishing break; reacts to the retirements.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She accompanies him; he dismisses her for the secret discussion — she understands.<span class=\"pg\">p.212, 218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Predicts she won&#x27;t easily lend a hand but will act if first-years look down on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p207-1\">← Before: Day four: standings revealed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p220-1\">→ After: The Tug of War with Kōenji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p220-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the tug of war with koenji detours to a tug of war task at c5 s summit  5 pts participation  10 more to win  arrives to find koenji already there  having traveled light without a tablet   koenji  the same koenji from your class who s currently in fourth place overall   ah  such a splendidly handsome man i am  these drops of masculine beauty trickling down my magnificent body   it seeeeems that my opponent is you  ayanokoji boy   that it does   fufu  so you re a man who thinks about things from the perspective of efficiency  hmmmm   quit overselling your worth inside that head of yours   to win at tug of war  one needs not these paltry parlor tricks  but raw  unbridled power  initially plans to concede  giving koenji 15 pts to rise to 2nd benefits class 2 d  then decides to make it look competitive  applies physics  grip friction  foot friction  gravity  in a brief counter pull  but koenji s raw power overwhelms him   they re  just about evenly matched  he loses only because of weight  deliberately stops to lose  and concedes  his first direct one on one competition with a classmate  koenji sees through his efficiency thinking  he lets koenji win so their class benefits  she wins her category by default  only girl  puzzled by koenji s self talk  notes he s  just as outstanding as i thought","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Tug of War with Kōenji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.220–229<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Detours to a Tug of War Task at C5&#x27;s summit (5 pts participation, 10 more to win); arrives to find Kōenji already there, having traveled light without a tablet.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Kōenji…? The same Kōenji from your class who&#x27;s currently in fourth place overall?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;Ah… such a splendidly handsome man I am, these drops of masculine beauty trickling down my magnificent body.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;It seeeeems that my opponent is you, Ayanokōji-boy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That it does.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Fufu, so you&#x27;re a man who thinks about things from the perspective of efficiency, hmmmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;quit overselling your worth inside that head of yours.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;To win at Tug of War, one needs not these paltry parlor tricks, but raw, unbridled power.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Initially plans to concede (giving Kōenji 15 pts to rise to 2nd benefits Class 2-D), then decides to make it look competitive; applies physics (grip friction, foot friction, gravity) in a brief counter-pull, but Kōenji&#x27;s raw power overwhelms him — they&#x27;re &quot;just about evenly matched,&quot; he loses only because of weight; deliberately stops to lose, and concedes.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> His first direct one-on-one competition with a classmate; Kōenji sees through his efficiency-thinking; he lets Kōenji win so their class benefits.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She wins her category by default (only girl); puzzled by Kōenji&#x27;s self-talk; notes he&#x27;s &quot;just as outstanding as I thought.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224–229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p211-1\">← Before: Rankings and the Ryūen/Katsuragi strategy meeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p234-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi at the harbor; Kōenji&#x27;s dominance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p234-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sakayanagi at the harbor  koenji s dominance  good day to you  ayanokoji kun  it seems the weather is going to be   how do you know about nanase   it seems to me that koenji kun has been surprisingly motivated during  meets sakayanagi  in class a s top ten group  at the harbor  she knows about nanase  they discuss koenji s unusual motivation   ayanokoji realizes she s perceptive about him and koenji  she knows of nanase and observes koenji s motivation  takes third in a swimming task  behind onodera  narrowly missing first  ayanokoji notes her effort and that koenji  winning task after task  has become a strong  hard to control element moving alone without the human resources to capitalize at the end","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p234-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi at the harbor; Kōenji&#x27;s dominance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.234–245<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;Good day to you, Ayanokōji-kun. It seems the weather is going to be&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How do you know about Nanase?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;It seems to me that Kōenji-kun has been surprisingly motivated during&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Meets Sakayanagi (in Class A&#x27;s top-ten group) at the harbor; she knows about Nanase; they discuss Kōenji&#x27;s unusual motivation — Ayanokōji realizes she&#x27;s perceptive about him and Kōenji.<span class=\"pg\">p.234–237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She knows of Nanase and observes Kōenji&#x27;s motivation.<span class=\"pg\">p.234–237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Takes third in a swimming Task (behind Onodera), narrowly missing first; Ayanokōji notes her effort and that Kōenji (winning Task after Task) has become a strong, hard-to-control element moving alone without the human resources to capitalize at the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.242–245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p220-1\">← Before: The Tug of War with Kōenji<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p260-1\">→ After: Day six: the cliff climb with Nanase<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p260-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka day six  the cliff climb with nanase on day six  takes first at b6  then faces a  10m cliff en route to random area c3  chooses the direct path through a4 b4 to secure early bird   i m guessing that most of the other groups we re up against are going to go through c4 or take a detour down and around   i guess that s the end of the line   even if you can  there s no point if it takes up all your stamina just to get to the top   take my hand   if i went ahead and you got injured  it d leave a bad taste in my mouth   no  this is my first time doing something like this    on rock climbing experience deliberately pushes the risky route  lets nanase try first  then when she insists on following despite fatigue  climbs back down and guides her up  inefficient but safe    thinks she resembles  a loyal dog chasing after its owner  admits he has no climbing experience  reaches c3 first and gets early bird  she falls  insists on following  and he helps her scale the cliff   her resolve and fatigue both notable  the skies turn cloudy windy   a shift from the earlier clear weather  foreshadowing a storm","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p260-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Day six: the cliff climb with Nanase<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.260–266<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On day six, takes first at B6, then faces a ~10m cliff en route to random area C3; chooses the direct path through A4/B4 to secure Early Bird.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m guessing that most of the other groups we&#x27;re up against are going to go through C4 or take a detour down and around.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I guess that&#x27;s the end of the line.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Even if you can, there&#x27;s no point if it takes up all your stamina just to get to the top.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.262<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Take my hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.263<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If I went ahead and you got injured, it&#x27;d leave a bad taste in my mouth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, this is my first time doing something like this.&quot; — on rock-climbing experience<span class=\"pg\">p.264<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately pushes the risky route; lets Nanase try first, then when she insists on following despite fatigue, climbs back down and guides her up (inefficient but safe) — thinks she resembles &quot;a loyal dog chasing after its owner&quot;; admits he has no climbing experience; reaches C3 first and gets Early Bird.<span class=\"pg\">p.260–266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She falls, insists on following, and he helps her scale the cliff — her resolve and fatigue both notable.<span class=\"pg\">p.260–266<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The skies turn cloudy/windy — a shift from the earlier clear weather, foreshadowing a storm.<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p234-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi at the harbor; Kōenji&#x27;s dominance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p275-1\">→ After: Day seven: rankings; Nanase&#x27;s strange air before the trap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p275-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka day seven  rankings  nanase s strange air before the trap on day seven morning  checks rankings with nanase   koenji nearly caught nagumo s first place group  8 point gap  a first year group  takahashi yagami utomiya tsubaki  unexpectedly in the top ten  which displeases him   he d rather see the other school years succeed   that said  you re also amazing  ayanokoji senpai   i m hoping for a miracle   from what i saw in the weather forecast  it should start raining    expects rain to cause retirements  he didn t buy rain gear  nanase slows on the mountain in the pre rain heat  he takes her backpack to help  and she warns the rain will make the mountain paths dangerous  senses nanase s  air of curiosity  since she first asked to accompany him  notes her breathing falter and her odd determination to reach the mountain area  the weather shift  clouds  wind  foreshadows the storm  her behavior grows increasingly strange  he carries her bag but stays alert","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p275-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Day seven: rankings; Nanase&#x27;s strange air before the trap<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.275–286<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On day seven morning, checks rankings with Nanase — Kōenji nearly caught Nagumo&#x27;s first-place group (8-point gap); a first-year group (Takahashi/Yagami/Utomiya/Tsubaki) unexpectedly in the top ten, which displeases him — he&#x27;d rather see the other school years succeed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;That said, you&#x27;re also amazing, Ayanokōji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m hoping for a miracle.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;From what I saw in the weather forecast, it should start raining&quot; — expects rain to cause retirements; he didn&#x27;t buy rain gear.<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Nanase slows on the mountain in the pre-rain heat; he takes her backpack to help, and she warns the rain will make the mountain paths dangerous.<span class=\"pg\">p.281<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Senses Nanase&#x27;s &quot;air of curiosity&quot; since she first asked to accompany him; notes her breathing falter and her odd determination to reach the mountain area; the weather shift (clouds, wind) foreshadows the storm.<span class=\"pg\">p.275–286<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Her behavior grows increasingly strange; he carries her bag but stays alert.<span class=\"pg\">p.275–286<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p260-1\">← Before: Day six: the cliff climb with Nanase<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p287-1\">→ After: Nanase&#x27;s confession: she is the White Room agent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p287-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa tsukishiro komiya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase s confession  she is the white room agent on the mountain path  northern d3  nanase asks him to stop  sets down her backpack at a tree  and reveals she lured him there   not to reach e2   the reason i wanted to head up the mountain was to lure you here  senpai   over the course of the last six days i ve been with you  i ve been able to witness all sorts of things   it s because you re from the white room   i enrolled here in this school under acting director tsukishiro s orders   i m going to knock you out here and injure you  setting off your emergency alert in the process   so  something similar to what happened to komiya and kinoshita  were you the one behind what happened to them as well   undoubtedly be the acting director himself   since it s come to this  there s really only one choice i can make  realizes the faculty responder would be tsukishiro himself  so any defense is useless  if he strikes a girl it warrants a penalty  and tsukishiro could expel both   if evenly matched  it s his loss  chooses to fight  refusing to abandon his bag and flee  which would make surviving the exam impossible  she reveals her mission and intent to frame him via injury   the first time he hears  white room  from another student  named as the one who sent her and who would cover it up  suspects she may also have caused the cliff incident","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p287-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase&#x27;s confession: she is the White Room agent<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.287–295<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the mountain path (northern D3), Nanase asks him to stop, sets down her backpack at a tree, and reveals she lured him there — not to reach E2.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#komiya\">Komiya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;The reason I wanted to head up the mountain was to lure you here, Senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Over the course of the last six days I&#x27;ve been with you, I&#x27;ve been able to witness all sorts of things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.288<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s because you&#x27;re from the White Room.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I enrolled here in this school under Acting Director Tsukishiro&#x27;s orders.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m going to knock you out here and injure you, setting off your Emergency Alert in the process.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, something similar to what happened to Komiya and Kinoshita. Were you the one behind what happened to them as well?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;undoubtedly be the Acting Director himself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Since it&#x27;s come to this, there&#x27;s really only one choice I can make.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes the faculty responder would be Tsukishiro himself, so any defense is useless; if he strikes a girl it warrants a penalty, and Tsukishiro could expel both — if evenly matched, it&#x27;s his loss; chooses to fight, refusing to abandon his bag and flee (which would make surviving the exam impossible).<span class=\"pg\">p.288–290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She reveals her mission and intent to frame him via injury — the first time he hears &quot;White Room&quot; from another student.<span class=\"pg\">p.287–295<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Named as the one who sent her and who would cover it up.<span class=\"pg\">p.289–290<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya<\/b> suspects she may also have caused the cliff incident.<span class=\"pg\">p.289<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p275-1\">← Before: Day seven: rankings; Nanase&#x27;s strange air before the trap<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p291-1\">→ After: The fight: Ayanokōji vs Nanase/&quot;Matsuo&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p291-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the fight  ayanokoji vs nanase matsuo  the two face off in the wind  he baits an opening  she attacks with an open palm  jiu jitsu  and he stops his fist centimeters from her face    that s the first    twice more  never actually hitting her   do you think you can beat me without even trying to fight back   nanase  are you tired  or was that hesitation   although you re free to make this show of dominance all you want  you don t stand a chance at winning if you don t actually fight back   i ll say this just in case you haven t noticed  but this makes three times now   it seems your strength is just as the rumors say  ayanokoji senpai   therefore i will  right here  right now   who are you   i came back from  that place  in order to put a stop to you   i m not nanase  the one standing here before you right now is  matsuo eiichiro   i ll make sure you suffer retribution  realizes her shift from  watashi  to  boku  and from jiu jitsu to karate  with doubled speed  is self deception   she has manufactured an aggressive alternate persona  possibly dissociative identity disorder  to do the fighting she is too nonviolent to do   matsuo eiichiro  is the son of a man killed by atsuomi  a real person she s impersonating  deliberately breaks her fighting spirit without hurting her   a bluff that she can never land a hit  reads her psychology precisely  you just took the liberty to dream up another personality inside of yourself  and notes her attacks grow wild and inefficient as desperation sets in  senses watchers tailing them  recording evidence  which is why he can t seriously strike back  he defeats her without hitting her  dismantling her  matsuo  persona and its self deception  she collapses in tears   matsuo eiichiro  is the boy from the year 1  vol  1 bus incident whose father was involved with atsuomi   the name tsukishiro mentioned   that man    atsuomi  ayanokoji senses an unseen presence tailing them all day   watchers recording evidence of the fight   which is why he cannot strike nanase for real without risking expulsion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p291-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The fight: Ayanokōji vs Nanase/&quot;Matsuo&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.291–304<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The two face off in the wind; he baits an opening, she attacks with an open palm (jiu-jitsu), and he stops his fist centimeters from her face — &quot;That&#x27;s the first&quot; — twice more, never actually hitting her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Do you think you can beat me without even trying to fight back…?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.293<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nanase, are you tired? Or was that hesitation?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.293<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Although you&#x27;re free to make this show of dominance all you want, you don&#x27;t stand a chance at winning if you don&#x27;t actually fight back.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.294<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll say this just in case you haven&#x27;t noticed, but this makes three times now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.294<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It seems your strength is just as the rumors say, Ayanokōji-senpai…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.295<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Therefore…『I』will. Right here, right now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who are you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;『I』came back from &#x27;that place&#x27; in order to put a stop to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.296<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;『I&#x27;m』not Nanase. The one standing here before you right now is… Matsuo Eiichiro.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;『I&#x27;ll』make sure you suffer retribution!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.300<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes her shift from &quot;Watashi&quot; to &quot;Boku&quot; and from jiu-jitsu to karate, with doubled speed, is self-deception — she has manufactured an aggressive alternate persona (possibly dissociative identity disorder) to do the fighting she is too nonviolent to do; &quot;Matsuo Eiichiro&quot; is the son of a man killed by Atsuomi, a real person she&#x27;s impersonating.<span class=\"pg\">p.296–302<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately breaks her fighting spirit without hurting her — a bluff that she can never land a hit; reads her psychology precisely (&quot;You just took the liberty to dream up another personality inside of yourself&quot;), and notes her attacks grow wild and inefficient as desperation sets in; senses watchers tailing them (recording evidence), which is why he can&#x27;t seriously strike back.<span class=\"pg\">p.291–304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> He defeats her without hitting her, dismantling her &quot;Matsuo&quot; persona and its self-deception; she collapses in tears.<span class=\"pg\">p.291–304<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> &quot;Matsuo Eiichiro&quot; is the boy from the Year 1, Vol. 1 bus incident whose father was involved with Atsuomi — the name Tsukishiro mentioned; &quot;that man&quot; = Atsuomi.<span class=\"pg\">p.299<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji senses an unseen presence tailing them all day — watchers recording evidence of the fight — which is why he cannot strike Nanase for real without risking expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.292<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p287-1\">← Before: Nanase&#x27;s confession: she is the White Room agent<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p346-1\">→ After: Nanase&#x27;s full confession; Ayanokōji offers her his hand<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p346-1","v":"y2v3","y":2,"o":18,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase s full confession  ayanokoji offers her his hand in the rain on the mountain  nanase admits defeat and  at his request  explains everything   her motive and tsukishiro s role   it s my loss  ayanokoji senpai    see note  can i take that to mean you re finally convinced   i enrolled in this school because i wanted to avenge my childhood friend   i knew that you weren t the one at fault  ayanokoji senpai  but  i wanted  no  needed someone to take it out on   you don t need to apologize  the anger you feel is perfectly justified   i ve failed to carry out the acting director s orders  there s no point in me staying here anymore   you have nothing to feel ashamed of  you simply tried your best to avenge your friend   i d rather not hear about you leaving the school  instead  i d like you to cooperate with me   can you lend me your hand   it s a promise  learns the full story  eiichiro  matsuo s son  was atsuomi s victim   expelled everywhere  father burned himself to death  eiichiro later took his own life on feb 14  tsukishiro told nanase ayanokoji was the cause  arranged her enrollment  and promised a meeting with his father if she expelled him  realizes tsukishiro s talk of a white room enforcer may have been a bluff   nanase  exceptional but too rough around the edges  may have been the actual agent all along  compassionate and strategic   recognizes his father s cruelty as  a projection of myself  but chooses to be the person who extends a hand to the ignorant  unlike atsuomi  asks nanase to cooperate rather than drop out  so her efforts to get here aren t wasted   privately intending to  make good use of her so that she could  even if i ended up only using her once and throwing her away  hears her confession  forgives her  and recruits her as an ally against tsukishiro  they shake hands on a promise  suspects he s still scheming to expel him as a  gift  to atsuomi   matsuo eiichiro  was nanase s childhood friend and the son of the butler who served atsuomi  his father burned himself to death after eiichiro s expulsion  and eiichiro later took his own life","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p346-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase&#x27;s full confession; Ayanokōji offers her his hand<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V3 · p.346–353<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the rain on the mountain, Nanase admits defeat and, at his request, explains everything — her motive and Tsukishiro&#x27;s role.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s my loss… Ayanokōji-senpai.&quot; — see note<span class=\"pg\">p.347<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Can I take that to mean you&#x27;re finally convinced?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.347<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;I enrolled in this school because I wanted to avenge my childhood friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.347<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I knew that you weren&#x27;t the one at fault, Ayanokōji-senpai, but… I wanted… no, needed someone to take it out on…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.350<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You don&#x27;t need to apologize. The anger you feel is perfectly justified.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ve failed to carry out the Acting Director&#x27;s orders. There&#x27;s no point in me staying here anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You have nothing to feel ashamed of. You simply tried your best to avenge your friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;d rather not hear about you leaving the school. Instead, I&#x27;d like you to cooperate with me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can you lend me your hand?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;─It&#x27;s a promise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Learns the full story: Eiichiro (Matsuo&#x27;s son) was Atsuomi&#x27;s victim — expelled everywhere, father burned himself to death, Eiichiro later took his own life on Feb 14; Tsukishiro told Nanase Ayanokōji was the cause, arranged her enrollment, and promised a meeting with his father if she expelled him; realizes Tsukishiro&#x27;s talk of a White Room enforcer may have been a bluff — Nanase (exceptional but too rough around the edges) may have been the actual agent all along.<span class=\"pg\">p.348–351<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Compassionate and strategic — recognizes his father&#x27;s cruelty as &quot;a projection of myself,&quot; but chooses to be the person who extends a hand to the ignorant (unlike Atsuomi); asks Nanase to cooperate rather than drop out, so her efforts to get here aren&#x27;t wasted — privately intending to &quot;make good use of her so that she could, even if I ended up only using her once and throwing her away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.346–353<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Hears her confession, forgives her, and recruits her as an ally against Tsukishiro; they shake hands on a promise.<span class=\"pg\">p.346–353<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Suspects he&#x27;s still scheming to expel him as a &quot;gift&quot; to Atsuomi.<span class=\"pg\">p.350–352<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> &quot;Matsuo Eiichiro&quot; was Nanase&#x27;s childhood friend and the son of the butler who served Atsuomi; his father burned himself to death after Eiichiro&#x27;s expulsion, and Eiichiro later took his own life.<span class=\"pg\">p.349<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v3-p291-1\">← Before: The fight: Ayanokōji vs Nanase/&quot;Matsuo&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p5-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p5-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.5-284<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p5-2\">→ After: Prologue note (Amasawa&#x27;s monologue — her own page)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p5-2","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka prologue note  amasawa s monologue   her own page  the prologue is amasawa ichika s own monologue  an ivf test tube  baby raised in the white room    recorded on her own page  not attributed here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p5-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Prologue note (Amasawa&#x27;s monologue — her own page)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.5–7<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The prologue is Amasawa Ichika&#x27;s own monologue (an IVF/&quot;test-tube&quot; baby raised in the White Room) — recorded on her own page, not attributed here.<span class=\"pg\">p.5<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p5-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p8-1\">→ After: Amasawa appears in the rain; reveals she is the White Room student<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p8-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka amasawa appears in the rain  reveals she is the white room student on the mountain in the storm after the fight with nanase  amasawa appears from behind with a wooden stick  no backpack tablet   having tracked them  same table  or gps walkie talkie relay   seems it s gonna really start coming down  huh sen pai   you  cannot be trusted   oh  nanase chan  shouldn t you be happy to see me   please don t listen to her  she s dangerous   back then  the one watching us from the shadows was you  wasn t it amasawa san   ahaha  so i was seen after all   there are certain things that only the fifth generation of students that came after you could learn   well there s no way i could do that  it has to do with the white room  after all   senpai  the curriculum you took back when you were 10 years old included systems  theory based on project 5  considers how she found them  tracked gps  and why she s armed  amasawa reveals white room only knowledge  his 10 year old systems  theory project 5  11 year old relativity project 7  the pure white facility  proving she s the real white room student   not something tsukishiro would tell an outsider  she reveals her identity  claims to admire him and not be his enemy  and warns him not to get himself crushed without her permission  now his ally  she fiercely guards him  accuses amasawa of pushing komiya kinoshita  and is called an  outsider loyal dog","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p8-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Amasawa appears in the rain; reveals she is the White Room student<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.8–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the mountain in the storm after the fight with Nanase, Amasawa appears from behind with a wooden stick, no backpack/tablet — having tracked them (same Table, or GPS/walkie-talkie relay).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;Seems it&#x27;s gonna really start coming down, huh Sen~pai?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.8<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;You─ cannot be trusted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;Oh? Nanase-chan, shouldn&#x27;t you be happy to see me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please don&#x27;t listen to her, she&#x27;s dangerous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Back then, the one watching us from the shadows was you, wasn&#x27;t it Amasawa-san?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ahaha, so I was seen after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;there are certain things that only the fifth generation of students that came after you could learn.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well there&#x27;s no way I could do that. It has to do with the White Room, after all~&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Senpai, the curriculum you took back when you were 10 years old included Systems&#x27; Theory based on Project 5.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Considers how she found them (tracked/GPS) and why she&#x27;s armed; Amasawa reveals White Room-only knowledge (his 10-year-old Systems&#x27; Theory/Project 5, 11-year-old Relativity/Project 7, the pure-white facility), proving she&#x27;s the real White Room student — not something Tsukishiro would tell an outsider.<span class=\"pg\">p.8–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> She reveals her identity, claims to admire him and not be his enemy, and warns him not to get himself crushed without her permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.8–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Now his ally, she fiercely guards him, accuses Amasawa of pushing Komiya/Kinoshita, and is called an &quot;outsider&quot;/&quot;loyal dog.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9–16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p5-2\">← Before: Prologue note (Amasawa&#x27;s monologue — her own page)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p18-1\">→ After: Amasawa&#x27;s motive: admiration; the mystery footprints<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p18-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka amasawa s motive  admiration  the mystery footprints amasawa explains why she revealed herself   later generations harbor immense jealousy toward him  the higher ups tried to exploit it  but chose the wrong person   it s cuz i wanted to tell you that i m not your enemy  senpai   they didn t predict that i was but a young maiden who secretly idolized you   you ve gotta talk with them and meet face to face before your admiration starts to feel justified   i too have thought about how nice it d be if i could just enjoy being a student like this up until graduation   still don t believe me   do you understand   so please  don t go and get yourself crushed without my permission  okay  judges her story partially credible  her white room knowledge proves origin  not motive  notes she s similar to him  poor at making friends  felt distance from others  though she claims better communication skills   a difference she attributes to the fifth generation s training in interpersonal communication  remains calm despite her being a white room student  admires him  claims not to be his enemy  and departs leaving a cryptic warning","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Amasawa&#x27;s motive: admiration; the mystery footprints<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.18–21<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Amasawa explains why she revealed herself — later generations harbor immense jealousy toward him; the higher-ups tried to exploit it, but chose the wrong person.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s cuz I wanted to tell you that I&#x27;m not your enemy, Senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;they didn&#x27;t predict that I was but a young maiden who secretly idolized you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;ve gotta talk with them and meet face-to-face before your admiration starts to feel justified.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I too have thought about how nice it&#x27;d be if I could just enjoy being a student like this up until graduation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Still don&#x27;t believe me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you understand?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So please, don&#x27;t go and get yourself crushed without my permission, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges her story partially credible (her White Room knowledge proves origin, not motive); notes she&#x27;s similar to him (poor at making friends, felt distance from others) though she claims better communication skills — a difference she attributes to the fifth generation&#x27;s training in interpersonal communication; remains calm despite her being a White Room student.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Admires him, claims not to be his enemy, and departs leaving a cryptic warning.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p8-1\">← Before: Amasawa appears in the rain; reveals she is the White Room student<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p21-1\">→ After: Investigating Amasawa&#x27;s footprints and the whittled stick<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p21-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka investigating amasawa s footprints and the whittled stick  the rain  we d better hurry   amasawa san s  footprints  is there something wrong with her footprints   i found some footprints nearby the scene of the crime  from what i can tell  i m fairly confident that they re the same size as amasawa s   it s been whittled down in certain places so it can be better used as a weapon   senpai  let s do a gps search right now  notes amasawa s footprints are clean steady but preceded by a larger mystery set that approached them then fled  the stick was deliberately whittled into a weapon   likely left by the mystery person  not amasawa  who had no intention of attacking  only wanted to be noticed  possibly to protect him  reasons the attacker did not break their watch  else gps reveal would be meaningless  so a gps search could identify the one missing signal as the culprit  discusses the footprints stick evidence  she pushes for a gps search","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Investigating Amasawa&#x27;s footprints and the whittled stick<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.21–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The rain. We&#x27;d better hurry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Amasawa-san&#x27;s… footprints? Is there something wrong with her footprints?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I found some footprints nearby the scene of the crime. From what I can tell, I&#x27;m fairly confident that they&#x27;re the same size as Amasawa&#x27;s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s been whittled down in certain places so it can be better used as a weapon.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Senpai, let&#x27;s do a GPS Search right now!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Notes Amasawa&#x27;s footprints are clean/steady but preceded by a larger mystery set that approached them then fled; the stick was deliberately whittled into a weapon — likely left by the mystery person, not Amasawa (who had no intention of attacking, only wanted to be noticed, possibly to protect him); reasons the attacker did NOT break their watch (else GPS reveal would be meaningless), so a GPS Search could identify the one missing signal as the culprit.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Discusses the footprints/stick evidence; she pushes for a GPS search.<span class=\"pg\">p.21–26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p18-1\">← Before: Amasawa&#x27;s motive: admiration; the mystery footprints<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p51-1\">→ After: Day eight: food shortage; parting with Nanase<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p51-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka day eight  food shortage  parting with nanase after the storm clears  reflects on running out of food   never having undergone starvation training  his immune system at risk  his only real food source is tasks   amasawa s most likely just going to head to the next designated area  right   may i continue to accompany you until we reach this first designated area   without putting too much thought into it  it s probably safe to assume that she approached us using a gps search on the morning of the seventh   our score didn t go down whatsoever yesterday   i m guessing she used a trick of some sort to find out my exact location   if i catch wind that something bad is going down  i ll come running   just don t overdo it  reasons amasawa didn t use gps search  group score unchanged  but traveled light to close the distance   likely had someone else disclose his location  concludes nanase is now a useful ally who can infiltrate first year circles  continues with him to the first area  then parts to rejoin amasawa hosen and spy on the first years for him  analyzes how she found them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Day eight: food shortage; parting with Nanase<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.51–54<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the storm clears, reflects on running out of food — never having undergone starvation training, his immune system at risk; his only real food source is Tasks.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Amasawa&#x27;s most likely just going to head to the next designated area, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;may I continue to accompany you until we reach this first designated area?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Without putting too much thought into it, it&#x27;s probably safe to assume that she approached us using a GPS Search on the morning of the seventh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;our score didn&#x27;t go down whatsoever yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m guessing she used a trick of some sort to find out my exact location.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If I catch wind that something bad is going down, I&#x27;ll come running&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just don&#x27;t overdo it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons Amasawa didn&#x27;t use GPS Search (group score unchanged) but traveled light to close the distance — likely had someone else disclose his location; concludes Nanase is now a useful ally who can infiltrate first-year circles.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Continues with him to the first area, then parts to rejoin Amasawa/Hōsen and spy on the first-years for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Analyzes how she found them.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p21-1\">← Before: Investigating Amasawa&#x27;s footprints and the whittled stick<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p55-1\">→ After: Reuniting with Horikita; coordinating the Shinohara rescue<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p55-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu shinohara ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka reuniting with horikita  coordinating the shinohara rescue on day eight  runs into horikita  first time since day one  near a task in f7  they head the same direction  his f8  her g8   it s been eight days  huh   yes  i am  it s troublesome in many ways  but being alone tends to make many things easier as well   no  not really  i think it could ve been both an incident or an accident   but if that s how things play out  then it ll be just you and shinohara scoring all the points   i m running low on food  so i think i d like to drop by this task  notes horikita is unexpectedly fresh and never in the bottom ten  she s taking first in contested tasks  learns from her that sakayanagi told her of his rescue plan and they re negotiating  keeps amasawa s role to himself  both head to a food task that becomes fiercely competitive  reunites with her  coordinates the shinohara rescue  she won 3 extra group slots in a task  and heads to the food task together  horikita is negotiating with her over the rescue plan  seventh from bottom   at risk of expulsion by day s end","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Reuniting with Horikita; coordinating the Shinohara rescue<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.55–59<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On day eight, runs into Horikita (first time since day one) near a Task in F7; they head the same direction (his F8, her G8).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara.html\">Shinohara<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s been eight days, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes, I am. It&#x27;s troublesome in many ways, but being alone tends to make many things easier as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No, not really. I think it could&#x27;ve been both an incident or an accident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But if that&#x27;s how things play out, then it&#x27;ll be just you and Shinohara scoring all the points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m running low on food, so I think I&#x27;d like to drop by this Task.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Horikita is unexpectedly fresh and never in the bottom ten (she&#x27;s taking first in contested Tasks); learns from her that Sakayanagi told her of his rescue plan and they&#x27;re negotiating; keeps Amasawa&#x27;s role to himself; both head to a food Task that becomes fiercely competitive.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reunites with her, coordinates the Shinohara rescue (she won 3 extra group slots in a Task), and heads to the food Task together.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Horikita is negotiating with her over the rescue plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> Seventh from bottom — at risk of expulsion by day&#x27;s end.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p51-1\">← Before: Day eight: food shortage; parting with Nanase<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p60-1\">→ After: Ranking analysis; the top-ten dynamics<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p60-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ranking analysis  the top ten dynamics reviews his standing   112 points  risen to 13th  11 behind kuronaga s 10th place group  123  notes the danger of showing up in the top ten  it draws attacks  and the effect of the  more people  card  reasons that top groups must actively impede rivals to protect their position  but doing so costs their own point earning capacity  expects nagumo to take countermeasures against koenji  but he seems to be simply pouring his energy into scoring points as koenji takes first or second  deliberately skipped a good task to protect his ranking  curious about nagumo s strategy and how many groups use walkie talkies","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p60-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ranking analysis; the top-ten dynamics<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.60–66<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reviews his standing — 112 points, risen to 13th, 11 behind Kuronaga&#x27;s 10th-place group (123); notes the danger of showing up in the top ten (it draws attacks) and the effect of the &quot;More People&quot; card.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons that top groups must actively impede rivals to protect their position, but doing so costs their own point-earning capacity; expects Nagumo to take countermeasures against Kōenji, but he seems to be simply pouring his energy into scoring points as Kōenji takes first or second.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately skipped a good Task to protect his ranking; curious about Nagumo&#x27;s strategy and how many groups use walkie-talkies.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p55-1\">← Before: Reuniting with Horikita; coordinating the Shinohara rescue<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p67-1\">→ After: Ibuki&#x27;s dehydration; the water-for-food trade<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p67-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ibuki s dehydration  the water for food trade encounters ibuki eating jerky  class 2 b s class wide jerky strategy    she s alone  exhausted  dark circles  and hasn t had a real conversation since day one  only horikita   just horikita  you heard me say i wouldn t lose to her  right   i don t think of my classmates as  friends   how many points you got right now   so you won t tell me   when you next see that bitch  do me a solid and tell her that i ll absolutely never lose to her   so  did horikita put you up to this  tryna get in my way   your pulse is racing   a full day  and then some    out of water  it did about an hour ago    first warning alert diagnoses her dehydration  racing pulse  dry mouth  cracked lips  empty water bottle for a full day  first warning alert already sounded  bluffs a gps search to catch her lying about resting  offers a  fair trade  of two 500ml bottles for half her remaining food  and uses horikita s name as the most effective lever   she accepts  advises her to rest tomorrow  but she refuses  her only goal is beating horikita  helps the exhausted  dehydrated ibuki via a water for food trade and warns her to recover   though she misreads his motives as manipulation on horikita s behalf  uses her name to motivate ibuki  notes horikita looks fresh and well supplied","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki&#x27;s dehydration; the water-for-food trade<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.67–78<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Encounters Ibuki eating jerky (Class 2-B&#x27;s class-wide jerky strategy) — she&#x27;s alone, exhausted, dark circles, and hasn&#x27;t had a real conversation since day one (only Horikita).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;Just Horikita. You heard me say I wouldn&#x27;t lose to her, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t think of my classmates as &#x27;friends&#x27;.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> &quot;How many points you got right now?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So you won&#x27;t tell me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When you next see that bitch, do me a solid and tell her that I&#x27;ll absolutely never lose to her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So? Did Horikita put you up to this? Tryna get in my way?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Your pulse is racing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…A full day… and then some.&quot; — out of water<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…It did about an hour ago.&quot; — first Warning Alert<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Diagnoses her dehydration (racing pulse, dry mouth, cracked lips, empty water bottle for a full day+, first Warning Alert already sounded); bluffs a GPS Search to catch her lying about resting; offers a &quot;fair trade&quot; of two 500ml bottles for half her remaining food, and uses Horikita&#x27;s name as the most effective lever — she accepts; advises her to rest tomorrow, but she refuses (her only goal is beating Horikita).<span class=\"pg\">p.67–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Helps the exhausted, dehydrated Ibuki via a water-for-food trade and warns her to recover — though she misreads his motives as manipulation on Horikita&#x27;s behalf.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Uses her name to motivate Ibuki; notes Horikita looks fresh and well-supplied.<span class=\"pg\">p.71–76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p60-1\">← Before: Ranking analysis; the top-ten dynamics<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p116-1\">→ After: Camping with Hiyori&#x27;s expanded group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p116-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka camping with hiyori s expanded group at j10 near sunset  encounters hiyori s class 2 b group merged with ishizaki s  six members  hiyori  isoyama  morofuji  ishizaki  nishino  tsutsube   you look better than i thought   everyone has worked very hard   i don t think there is anything to worry about  but you have to be careful   nothing happens  that is one of the good things about you  ishizaki kun  notices hiyori doesn t ask his score    convinced that they will not expel me  observes the group s warm  balanced atmosphere  hiyori the  brains  tsutsube well integrated  and that ryuen s class is  starting to change little by little  accepts their invitation to camp near i9  struck by how comfortable it feels  sits with her watching the sea  she trusts he won t be expelled and warns him to be careful  he happily invites ayanokoji to camp with them  the others readily agree  the class 2 c girl is hitomi tsutsube  tsutsube  she has integrated well into ishizaki s group","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Camping with Hiyori&#x27;s expanded group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.116–120<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At J10 near sunset, encounters Hiyori&#x27;s Class 2-B group merged with Ishizaki&#x27;s (six members: Hiyori, Isoyama, Morofuji, Ishizaki, Nishino, Tsutsube).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;You look better than I thought.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Everyone has worked very hard.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t think there is anything to worry about, but you have to be careful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing happens. That is one of the good things about you, Ishizaki-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notices Hiyori doesn&#x27;t ask his score — &quot;convinced that they will not expel me&quot;; observes the group&#x27;s warm, balanced atmosphere (Hiyori the &quot;brains,&quot; Tsutsube well-integrated) and that Ryūen&#x27;s class is &quot;starting to change little by little&quot;; accepts their invitation to camp near I9, struck by how comfortable it feels.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Sits with her watching the sea; she trusts he won&#x27;t be expelled and warns him to be careful.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> He happily invites Ayanokōji to camp with them; the others readily agree.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The Class 2-C girl is Hitomi Tsutsube (&quot;Tsutsube&quot;); she has integrated well into Ishizaki&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p67-1\">← Before: Ibuki&#x27;s dehydration; the water-for-food trade<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p120-1\">→ After: Nanase&#x27;s midnight warning: the first-years&#x27; day-12 play<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p120-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase s midnight warning  the first years  day 12 play at 2 30 a m  nanase slips to his tent  terrified   she was in i9 and avoided contact because she was with hosen s group   it s me  nanase   there is something i need to tell you as soon as possible   housen kun told me that on the twelfth day  the first years will make a great play on ayanokouji senpai   i don t know  but tsubaki was the main person i spoke to on the walkie talkie   that s enough for this uninhabited island exam  learns the first years plan to force his withdrawal at the exam s end  day 12  targeting solo seniors  hosen was contacted via walkie talkie by an errand boy and only pretending to cooperate  hasn t received details  suspects tsubaki as intermediary  with yagami takahashi possibly pulling strings  tells nanase to stop helping him so she won t be exposed  she risks coming at night to warn him about the day 12 plot  he sends her away for her own safety  only feigning cooperation with the first years  plot  received a walkie talkie","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase&#x27;s midnight warning: the first-years&#x27; day-12 play<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.120–122<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At 2:30 a.m., Nanase slips to his tent, terrified — she was in I9 and avoided contact because she was with Hōsen&#x27;s group.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s me, Nanase.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There is something I need to tell you as soon as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Housen-kun told me that on the twelfth day, the first years will make a great play on Ayanokouji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t know, but Tsubaki was the main person I spoke to on the walkie-talkie.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;that&#x27;s enough for this uninhabited island exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Learns the first-years plan to force his withdrawal at the exam&#x27;s end (day 12), targeting solo seniors; Hōsen was contacted via walkie-talkie by an errand boy and only pretending to cooperate, hasn&#x27;t received details; suspects Tsubaki as intermediary (with Yagami/Takahashi possibly pulling strings); tells Nanase to stop helping him so she won&#x27;t be exposed.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She risks coming at night to warn him about the day-12 plot; he sends her away for her own safety.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Only feigning cooperation with the first-years&#x27; plot; received a walkie-talkie.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p116-1\">← Before: Camping with Hiyori&#x27;s expanded group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p151-1\">→ After: Day 12: evading the first-year siege<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p151-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa tsubaki-sakurako ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka day 12  evading the first year siege on the twelfth day  uses gps searches to see the first years  utomiya  tsubaki  yagami  converging  recognizes from nanase s warning that today is the trap  with many class 1 d groups around d4 e6   how are you tsubaki san    narration of tsubaki s side  takuya yagami kun  riku utomiya kun  and sakurako tsubaki san  i wonder who    narration deliberately swerves to avoid head on collision  using gps to stay ahead  realizes the enemy is trying to herd him  but he has the advantage of knowing their plan  via nanase  arranges second year groups  ryuen s  to block the first year hunters  orchestrates a counter commander role that leaves tsubaki s groups baffled  calm and anticipatory   turns nanase s leaked warning into a prepared defense  staying one step ahead of tsubaki s gps trap and using the terrain and other students as pieces  her midnight warning let him prepare for the day 12 trap  the mastermind of the siege  he counters her plan  his counter uses ryuen to intercept hosen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Day 12: evading the first-year siege<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.151–164<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the twelfth day, uses GPS searches to see the first-years (Utomiya, Tsubaki, Yagami) converging; recognizes from Nanase&#x27;s warning that today is the trap, with many Class 1-D groups around D4/E6.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How are you Tsubaki-san?&quot; — narration of Tsubaki&#x27;s side<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Takuya Yagami-kun? Riku Utomiya-kun? and Sakurako Tsubaki-san? I wonder who&quot; — narration<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Deliberately swerves to avoid head-on collision, using GPS to stay ahead; realizes the enemy is trying to herd him, but he has the advantage of knowing their plan (via Nanase); arranges second-year groups (Ryūen&#x27;s) to block the first-year hunters; orchestrates a counter-commander role that leaves Tsubaki&#x27;s groups baffled.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and anticipatory — turns Nanase&#x27;s leaked warning into a prepared defense, staying one step ahead of Tsubaki&#x27;s GPS trap and using the terrain and other students as pieces.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Her midnight warning let him prepare for the day-12 trap.<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> The mastermind of the siege; he counters her plan.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His counter uses Ryūen to intercept Hōsen.<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p120-1\">← Before: Nanase&#x27;s midnight warning: the first-years&#x27; day-12 play<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p162-1\">→ After: Revealing Nanase&#x27;s role to Ryūen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p162-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka revealing nanase s role to ryuen explains to ryuen that nanase was one of the assassins tsukishiro sent  and why the lower risk plus new risk tipped the balance   enlisting his help to stop hosen  shares intel selectively with ryuen to neutralize the threat without expelling anyone  his intervention leads to ryuen stopping hosen  informs him about nanase tsukishiro  ryuen agrees to intercept hosen  nanase was one of his sent assassins","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p162-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Revealing Nanase&#x27;s role to Ryūen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.162–164<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Explains to Ryūen that Nanase was one of the assassins Tsukishiro sent, and why the lower risk plus new risk tipped the balance — enlisting his help to stop Hōsen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Shares intel selectively with Ryūen to neutralize the threat without expelling anyone; his intervention leads to Ryūen stopping Hōsen.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Informs him about Nanase/Tsukishiro; Ryūen agrees to intercept Hōsen.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Nanase was one of his sent assassins.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p151-1\">← Before: Day 12: evading the first-year siege<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p183-1\">→ After: Aftermath: Ryūen and Hōsen retire together<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p183-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru housen-kazuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka aftermath  ryuen and hosen retire together watches as ryuen  badly injured  decides to retire together with the unconscious hosen   the  only and most beautiful way  to stop him from returning to hunt ayanokoji   i m going to retire together with housen  understands ryuen s sacrifice  retiring to ensure hosen can t come after him again  tsubaki s plot collapses   hosen stopped  her first year groups neutralized   and she realizes her plan was doomed from early on  ryuen retires with hosen to protect ayanokoji s exam standing  neutralized   stops hunting ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Aftermath: Ryūen and Hōsen retire together<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.183–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Watches as Ryūen, badly injured, decides to retire together with the unconscious Hōsen — the &quot;only and most beautiful way&quot; to stop him from returning to hunt Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m going to retire together with Housen&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Understands Ryūen&#x27;s sacrifice (retiring to ensure Hōsen can&#x27;t come after him again); Tsubaki&#x27;s plot collapses — Hōsen stopped, her first-year groups neutralized — and she realizes her plan was doomed from early on.<span class=\"pg\">p.183–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen retires with Hōsen to protect Ayanokōji&#x27;s exam standing.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Neutralized — stops hunting Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p162-1\">← Before: Revealing Nanase&#x27;s role to Ryūen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p191-1\">→ After: Last day: Ichinose&#x27;s four-hour walk; her confession<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p191-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka last day  ichinose s four hour walk  her confession on the final day  reels from six consecutive missed areas  four penalties  sakayanagi warns via walkie talkie that ichinose has disappeared and was seen using gps near e3 d3   good morning  ayanokouji kun  you had a lot of problems yesterday   actually  i m in trouble  at dawn  ichinose san disappeared   i  i came here because i wanted to see you  ayanokouji kun   i have something i have to tell you  no matter what  ayanokouji kun   i  my watch broke  so i wanted to go back to the starting point to change it  and then  acting director tsukishiro  and shiba sensei  those two  they were there   if you re safe in the last day  ayanokouji kun  you ll be called to i2 and be buried   because i  because i like you  ayanokouji kun   thank you  ichinose   i think that there s still a few things that has to be addressed  and i don t think someone can answer yes or no in this state  deeply moved that ichinose walked 4  hours  exhausted and covered in mud  risking her classmates  expulsion to warn him of tsukishiro s i2 trap  accepts her confession graciously but can t reciprocate now  hides kei  deciding the exam climax isn t the place  realizes tsukishiro s move against him and resolves to go to i2  coming back from the dead  she confesses her love and warns him of the trap   a  watershed moment  for him  learned of his i2  burial  plot via ichinose  warns him about ichinose  he asks her to relay word if seen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Last day: Ichinose&#x27;s four-hour walk; her confession<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.191–201<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the final day, reels from six consecutive missed areas (four penalties); Sakayanagi warns via walkie-talkie that Ichinose has disappeared and was seen using GPS near E3/D3.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun. You had a lot of problems yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Actually, I&#x27;m in trouble. At dawn, Ichinose-san disappeared.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;I, I came here because I wanted to see you, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have something I have to tell you, no matter what, Ayanokouji-kun!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I, my watch broke, so I wanted to go back to the starting point to change it… And then, Acting Director Tsukishiro, and Shiba-sensei, those two, they were there…!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you&#x27;re safe in the last day, Ayanokouji-kun, you&#x27;ll be called to I2 and be buried.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Because I, because I like you, Ayanokouji-kun…!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;–Thank you, Ichinose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think that there&#x27;s still a few things that has to be addressed, and I don&#x27;t think someone can answer yes or no in this state.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deeply moved that Ichinose walked 4+ hours, exhausted and covered in mud, risking her classmates&#x27; expulsion to warn him of Tsukishiro&#x27;s I2 trap; accepts her confession graciously but can&#x27;t reciprocate now (hides Kei), deciding the exam climax isn&#x27;t the place; realizes Tsukishiro&#x27;s move against him and resolves to go to I2 (&quot;coming back from the dead&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.191–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She confesses her love and warns him of the trap — a &quot;watershed moment&quot; for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.191–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Learned of his I2 &quot;burial&quot; plot via Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Warns him about Ichinose; he asks her to relay word if seen.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p183-1\">← Before: Aftermath: Ryūen and Hōsen retire together<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p202-1\">→ After: Nagumo&#x27;s private talk; Kiryūin/Amasawa<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p202-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nagumo s private talk  kiryuin amasawa at i2 approach  meets nagumo alone  he claims to have been enjoying the beach at i4  they spar verbally about why he s there and ichinose   ayanokouji  what a coincidence   president nagumo  why are you here   i was having fun on the beach at i4   the more you try to stop me  the more i must go to i2  amasawa appears and  with nagumo  tries to discourage him from i2  he reads that they genuinely don t want him to go   confirming he must  nagumo s true role and amasawa s disobedience tie into tsukishiro s plot  he tries to dissuade him from i2   which only confirms ayanokoji s resolve  she joins the attempt to stop him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo&#x27;s private talk; Kiryūin/Amasawa<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.202–251<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At I2 approach, meets Nagumo alone (he claims to have been enjoying the beach at I4); they spar verbally about why he&#x27;s there and Ichinose.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji, what a coincidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;President Nagumo, why are you here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> &quot;I was having fun on the beach at I4.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The more you try to stop me, the more I must go to I2.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Amasawa appears and, with Nagumo, tries to discourage him from I2; he reads that they genuinely don&#x27;t want him to go — confirming he must. Nagumo&#x27;s true role and Amasawa&#x27;s disobedience tie into Tsukishiro&#x27;s plot.<span class=\"pg\">p.230–251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He tries to dissuade him from I2 — which only confirms Ayanokōji&#x27;s resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.202–230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> She joins the attempt to stop him.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p191-1\">← Before: Last day: Ichinose&#x27;s four-hour walk; her confession<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p252-1\">→ After: The showdown at I2: Ayanokōji vs Tsukishiro and Shiba<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p252-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"tsukishiro shiba-katsunori kiryuin-fuuka sakayanagi-arisu amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the showdown at i2  ayanokoji vs tsukishiro and shiba at i2 s tip  finds tsukishiro  in a sweater  and shiba waiting   tsukishiro s final trap to  bury  him  with no watch signal there   you have decided to take a very strong approach  acting director tsukishiro   you wouldn t call it unfair a two against one  right   i would have killed you now  but your reaction time is not normal    you are still a complicated person  acting director tsukishiro   it would have been easier if it was like a children s fight   let s solve this  acting director   you are an undeniable masterpiece   how did you know    tsukishiro  on the hidden stun gun  did you really try to expel me  fights the two adults  tsukishiro and shiba  both far stronger than their stated combat ratings   tsukishiro s  4  was disinformation  nearly overwhelmed in a 2 on 1 with kiryuin s help  she holds shiba  analyzes their timing  deduces tsukishiro s hidden stun gun from a glance at his feet  and beats him   targeting the nose to induce tears  then an uppercut  tsukishiro s last trump  a boat  is neutralized because ayanokoji had secretly called mashima and chabashira via sakayanagi s walkie talkie  reporting a class a and d student in danger  forcing their teachers to respond  defeats him in a one on one after seeing through his tricks  tsukishiro admits defeat but hints he hasn t shown everything  and delivers a message disqualifying amasawa from the white room  fights him alongside tsukishiro  held off by kiryuin  she appears  watch deliberately broken  and helps hold shiba    protect my kouhai  ayanokoji praises her  lent him the walkie talkie that saved him  tsukishiro s message disqualifies her for disobeying orders   free to stay or leave  ayanokoji doubts the white room matter is over","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The showdown at I2: Ayanokōji vs Tsukishiro and Shiba<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.252–272<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At I2&#x27;s tip, finds Tsukishiro (in a sweater) and Shiba waiting — Tsukishiro&#x27;s final trap to &quot;bury&quot; him, with no watch signal there.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a> · <a href=\"shiba-katsunori.html\">Shiba Katsunori<\/a> · <a href=\"kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You have decided to take a very strong approach, Acting Director Tsukishiro.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> &quot;You wouldn&#x27;t call it unfair a two against one, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> &quot;I would have killed you now, but your reaction time is not normal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;...... You are still a complicated person, Acting Director Tsukishiro.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.260<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It would have been easier if it was like a children&#x27;s fight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.261<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s solve this, Acting Director.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.265<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You are an undeniable masterpiece.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.267<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How did you know?&quot; — Tsukishiro, on the hidden stun gun<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did you really try to expel me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.271<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Fights the two adults (Tsukishiro and Shiba, both far stronger than their stated combat ratings — Tsukishiro&#x27;s &quot;4&quot; was disinformation), nearly overwhelmed in a 2-on-1 with Kiryūin&#x27;s help (she holds Shiba); analyzes their timing, deduces Tsukishiro&#x27;s hidden stun gun from a glance at his feet, and beats him — targeting the nose to induce tears, then an uppercut. Tsukishiro&#x27;s last trump (a boat) is neutralized because Ayanokōji had secretly called Mashima and Chabashira via Sakayanagi&#x27;s walkie-talkie (reporting a Class A and D student in danger, forcing their teachers to respond).<span class=\"pg\">p.252–272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Defeats him in a one-on-one after seeing through his tricks; Tsukishiro admits defeat but hints he hasn&#x27;t shown everything, and delivers a message disqualifying Amasawa from the White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiba Katsunori<\/b> Fights him alongside Tsukishiro; held off by Kiryūin.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–270<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> She appears (watch deliberately broken) and helps hold Shiba — &quot;protect my kouhai&quot;; Ayanokōji praises her.<span class=\"pg\">p.261–272<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Lent him the walkie-talkie that saved him.<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Tsukishiro&#x27;s message disqualifies her for disobeying orders — free to stay or leave; Ayanokōji doubts the White Room matter is over.<span class=\"pg\">p.272<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p202-1\">← Before: Nagumo&#x27;s private talk; Kiryūin/Amasawa<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p276-1\">→ After: After the exam: Sakayanagi&#x27;s promise with Ryūen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p276-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka after the exam  sakayanagi s promise with ryuen back on the ship after two weeks  learns the bottom five groups were notified in advance  so they can pay to avoid expulsion  on deck sees ryuen  face covered in scars from hosen  and sakayanagi talking   i m sorry to interrupt you  but don t forget the promise you made to me  okay  and some money   of course  ryuuen kun  please tell me when the time comes   promise  learns sakayanagi promised ryuen a favor if he asked   which is why he confronted hosen  the wish is  like strangling yourself in the near future   a dangerous promise  realizes this explains ryuen s cooperation  she explains the promise to ryuen and thanks ayanokoji for the gps timing help  looks forward to a future rematch  collected on his promise from sakayanagi  both he and hosen were removed for treatment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p276-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">After the exam: Sakayanagi&#x27;s promise with Ryūen<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.276–278<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back on the ship after two weeks; learns the bottom five groups were notified in advance (so they can pay to avoid expulsion); on deck sees Ryūen (face covered in scars from Hōsen) and Sakayanagi talking.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m sorry to interrupt you, but don&#x27;t forget the promise you made to me, okay? And some money.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;Of course, Ryuuen-kun. Please tell me when the time comes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Promise?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.276<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Learns Sakayanagi promised Ryūen a favor if he asked — which is why he confronted Hōsen; the wish is &quot;like strangling yourself in the near future&quot; (a dangerous promise); realizes this explains Ryūen&#x27;s cooperation.<span class=\"pg\">p.277<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She explains the promise to Ryūen and thanks Ayanokōji for the GPS-timing help; looks forward to a future rematch.<span class=\"pg\">p.277–278<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Collected on his promise from Sakayanagi; both he and Hōsen were removed for treatment.<span class=\"pg\">p.276–277<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p252-1\">← Before: The showdown at I2: Ayanokōji vs Tsukishiro and Shiba<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p278-1\">→ After: Results: 15 third-years expelled; Kōenji wins 1st<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p278-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke kouenji-rokusuke nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka results  15 third years expelled  koenji wins 1st class d gathers to eat  hirata notes with heartfelt relief that no second year class d group was absent and everyone is present   key to avoiding expulsion  at 8 p m  sasaki announces 13 students dropped out but no group was entirely absent  the five withdrawn groups are all third years  3 d mutou  3 d kawakami  3 c shinonome  3 c katsumata  3 b mikitani    15 students expelled  shocking everyone  nagumo failed to save them  tsukishiro  calm despite the fight  announces  3rd sakayanagi s seven member group  261 pts  2nd nagumo  325 pts  1st koenji alone  327 pts    a 2 point margin  koenji gains 300 class points  1 million private points and a protection point  and is granted immunity until graduation  notes koenji s feat of winning alone under the harshest conditions  wonders if nagumo s walkie talkie partner s voice  which he didn t answer  would have reversed 1st 2nd   but it can t be known  relieved all of class d survived  wins first place alone  ayanokoji acknowledges it  and horikita celebrates the 300 class points toward class a  takes 2nd  his failure to answer his partner s walkie talkie may have cost him 1st","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p278-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Results: 15 third-years expelled; Kōenji wins 1st<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.278–282<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D gathers to eat; Hirata notes with heartfelt relief that no second-year Class D group was absent and everyone is present — key to avoiding expulsion.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> At 8 p.m., Sasaki announces 13 students dropped out but no group was entirely absent; the five withdrawn groups are all third-years (3-D Mutou, 3-D Kawakami, 3-C Shinonome, 3-C Katsumata, 3-B Mikitani) — 15 students expelled, shocking everyone (Nagumo failed to save them).<span class=\"pg\">p.279<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Tsukishiro (calm despite the fight) announces: 3rd Sakayanagi&#x27;s seven-member group (261 pts), 2nd Nagumo (325 pts), 1st Kōenji alone (327 pts) — a 2-point margin; Kōenji gains 300 class points, 1 million private points and a Protection Point, and is granted immunity until graduation.<span class=\"pg\">p.280–281<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Kōenji&#x27;s feat of winning alone under the harshest conditions; wonders if Nagumo&#x27;s walkie-talkie partner&#x27;s voice (which he didn&#x27;t answer) would have reversed 1st/2nd — but it can&#x27;t be known.<span class=\"pg\">p.281–282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Relieved all of Class D survived.<span class=\"pg\">p.278<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Wins first place alone; Ayanokōji acknowledges it, and Horikita celebrates the 300 class points toward Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.281–282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Takes 2nd; his failure to answer his partner&#x27;s walkie-talkie may have cost him 1st.<span class=\"pg\">p.281–282<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p276-1\">← Before: After the exam: Sakayanagi&#x27;s promise with Ryūen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p282-1\">→ After: Closing: Amasawa&#x27;s side, lingering mysteries<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p282-1","v":"y2v4","y":2,"o":19,"k":"","w":"amasawa-ichika tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka closing  amasawa s side  lingering mysteries no second year was expelled   a  miraculous  summer survived  confirms amasawa ichika is a white room student who now seems to be on his side  not tsukishiro s  though whether coordinated or betrayal is unknown  notes unresolved mysteries and that the summer may not end quietly  revealed as a white room student  apparently now his ally  his opponent   the white room threat isn t over","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p282-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Closing: Amasawa&#x27;s side, lingering mysteries<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4 · p.282<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> No second-year was expelled — a &quot;miraculous&quot; summer survived; confirms Amasawa Ichika is a White Room student who now seems to be on his side (not Tsukishiro&#x27;s), though whether coordinated or betrayal is unknown; notes unresolved mysteries and that the summer may not end quietly.<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> Revealed as a White Room student, apparently now his ally.<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> His opponent — the White Room threat isn&#x27;t over.<span class=\"pg\">p.282<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4-p278-1\">← Before: Results: 15 third-years expelled; Kōenji wins 1st<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p10-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.10-290<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p10-2\">→ After: Prologue note; August class points; settling in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p10-2","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka prologue note  august class points  settling in the prologue is ayanokoji s monologue  phones returned  cruise rules stricter   no leaving rooms after 10 p m  some levels off limits  recorded as narration on his own page  august class points  a  sakayanagi  1206  b  ichinose  578  c  horikita   their class rose from d  571  d  ryuen  551   koenji s 300 points from his solo win lifted them just to class c  one step short of b  reflects koenji s  exempted from all cooperation  card would anger the class if public  judges ryuen s deal with sakayanagi makes class d  in name  the  scariest class right now  considers how to break dominant class a  remove sakayanagi s  limbs    kamuro  hashimoto  kito  receives 57 100 private points  571 class points   100  plans to reply to ichinose s confession in three days  notes the detailed exam results are displayed by the gym  no photos  tsukishiro s men watching    likely to avoid leaving evidence of his involvement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p10-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Prologue note; August class points; settling in<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.10–16<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The prologue is Ayanokōji&#x27;s monologue (phones returned, cruise rules stricter — no leaving rooms after 10 p.m., some levels off-limits); recorded as narration on his own page.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> August class points: A (Sakayanagi) 1206, B (Ichinose) 578, C (Horikita — their class rose from D) 571, D (Ryūen) 551 — Kōenji&#x27;s 300 points from his solo win lifted them just to Class C, one step short of B.<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reflects Kōenji&#x27;s &quot;exempted from all cooperation&quot; card would anger the class if public; judges Ryūen&#x27;s deal with Sakayanagi makes Class D (in name) the &quot;scariest class right now&quot;; considers how to break dominant Class A (remove Sakayanagi&#x27;s &quot;limbs&quot; — Kamuro, Hashimoto, Kitō).<span class=\"pg\">p.13–15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Receives 57,100 private points (571 class points × 100); plans to reply to Ichinose&#x27;s confession in three days; notes the detailed exam results are displayed by the gym (no photos, Tsukishiro&#x27;s men watching) — likely to avoid leaving evidence of his involvement.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p10-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p36-1\">→ After: Results check; third-years&#x27; stares; Kiryūin at the pool<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p36-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"kiryuin-fuuka ichinose-honami nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka results check  third years  stares  kiryuin at the pool checks the detailed results by the gym   koenji 1st  nagumo 2nd  sakayanagi 3rd  261  kiriyama 4th  255  just 6 points behind  all expulsions were third years  heads to the pool to confirm the stares are a coordinated plan  not paranoia   within seconds all third years at the pool begin watching him  estimates 80 90  chance nagumo ordered it  but the content is unknown  decides to pretend not to notice  finds the surveillance  unsettling    unlike the white room s ever present eyes  this is a new kind of stress he can t easily escape  notes ichinose hides behind her classmates when their eyes meet  awkward after her confession  she rests on a deck chair and teases him about the stares   calls nagumo s tactic  bizarre yet effective  against someone like him  and calls him  flawless limitless  hides from him at the pool  they have an appointment in two days for his reply  kiryuin explains he s now taking ayanokoji seriously after the island exam  prefers flashy one on ones but will use any strategy  mobilizing the whole third year  to win","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p36-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Results check; third-years&#x27; stares; Kiryūin at the pool<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.36–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Checks the detailed results by the gym — Kōenji 1st, Nagumo 2nd, Sakayanagi 3rd (261), Kiriyama 4th (255, just 6 points behind); all expulsions were third-years.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Heads to the pool to confirm the stares are a coordinated plan, not paranoia — within seconds all third-years at the pool begin watching him; estimates 80–90% chance Nagumo ordered it, but the content is unknown; decides to pretend not to notice.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finds the surveillance &quot;unsettling&quot; — unlike the White Room&#x27;s ever-present eyes, this is a new kind of stress he can&#x27;t easily escape; notes Ichinose hides behind her classmates when their eyes meet (awkward after her confession).<span class=\"pg\">p.37–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> She rests on a deck chair and teases him about the stares — calls Nagumo&#x27;s tactic &quot;bizarre yet effective&quot; against someone like him, and calls him &quot;flawless&quot;/&quot;limitless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Hides from him at the pool; they have an appointment in two days for his reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Kiryūin explains he&#x27;s now taking Ayanokōji seriously after the island exam; prefers flashy one-on-ones but will use any strategy (mobilizing the whole third year) to win.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p10-2\">← Before: Prologue note; August class points; settling in<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p45-1\">→ After: Kiriyama&#x27;s confrontation: why he stopped fighting Nagumo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p45-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"kiriyama horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kiriyama s confrontation  why he stopped fighting nagumo kiriyama brings him to a quiet upper deck  having paid off the third years there  and demands what he did to nagumo on the exam s last day   i won t beat around the bush  what did you do to nagumo on the last day of the uninhabited island exam   initially  it looked like you were working to take down nagumo  at what point did you stop fighting  did you give up   it s true that i wanted to take down nagumo   nagumo handed me a ticket to graduate from class a  so i decided to follow the rules that he made up  probes whether kiriyama gave up the fight or became nagumo s ally  deduces from his gaffe that he s conscious of being seen on the president s side  learns the third years shifted to individual competition early  nagumo ran off with a 900 point lead  and kiriyama accepted a class a graduation ticket   admitting defeat and changing sides are not the same  he admits he stopped fighting nagumo and took his class a ticket   a  regret resignation  he can t fully hide  ayanokoji invokes manabu s entrustment  kiriyama admits involving him was a mistake","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kiriyama&#x27;s confrontation: why he stopped fighting Nagumo<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.45–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kiriyama brings him to a quiet upper deck (having paid off the third-years there) and demands what he did to Nagumo on the exam&#x27;s last day.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> &quot;I won&#x27;t beat around the bush. What did you do to Nagumo on the last day of the uninhabited island exam?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Initially, it looked like you were working to take down Nagumo. At what point did you stop fighting…? Did you give up?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s true that I wanted to take down Nagumo.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nagumo handed me a ticket to graduate from Class A, so I decided to follow the rules that he made up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Probes whether Kiriyama gave up the fight or became Nagumo&#x27;s ally; deduces from his gaffe that he&#x27;s conscious of being seen on the president&#x27;s side; learns the third-years shifted to individual competition early, Nagumo ran off with a 900-point lead, and Kiriyama accepted a Class A graduation ticket — admitting defeat and changing sides are not the same.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> He admits he stopped fighting Nagumo and took his Class A ticket — a &quot;regret/resignation&quot; he can&#x27;t fully hide.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> Ayanokōji invokes Manabu&#x27;s entrustment; Kiriyama admits involving him was a mistake.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p36-1\">← Before: Results check; third-years&#x27; stares; Kiryūin at the pool<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p54-1\">→ After: Nanase and Kobashi; the girls&#x27; party invitation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p54-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"kobashi-yume nanase-tsubasa ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase and kobashi  the girls  party invitation in the corridor  nanase runs up and whispers something serious  but is interrupted by kobashi yume  ichinose s classmate   ayanokouji senpai   actually  the girls in my class are going to have a party tonight   we also wanted to thank you for helping chihiro chan   room 5034 you re doing it in someone s room  notes ichinose turned down the invitation to the party  to avoid him  decides to attend   a girls  party in room 5034   as it s not the right time to speak to ichinose face to face yet  she runs up eagerly to talk but flees when kobashi appears  invites him to the party and thanks him for helping chihiro  tells him not to tell ichinose she invited him  declined the party  likely because of him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase and Kobashi; the girls&#x27; party invitation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.54–58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the corridor, Nanase runs up and whispers something serious, but is interrupted by Kobashi Yume (Ichinose&#x27;s classmate).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kobashi-yume.html\">Kobashi Yume<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokouji-senpai!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kobashi Yume<\/b> &quot;Actually, the girls in my class are going to have a party tonight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kobashi Yume<\/b> &quot;We also wanted to thank you for helping Chihiro-chan.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Room 5034…You&#x27;re doing it in someone&#x27;s room?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Ichinose turned down the invitation to the party (to avoid him); decides to attend — a girls&#x27; party in room 5034 — as it&#x27;s not the right time to speak to Ichinose face to face yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She runs up eagerly to talk but flees when Kobashi appears.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kobashi Yume<\/b> Invites him to the party and thanks him for helping Chihiro; tells him not to tell Ichinose she invited him.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Declined the party, likely because of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p45-1\">← Before: Kiriyama&#x27;s confrontation: why he stopped fighting Nagumo<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p73-1\">→ After: Lunch alone; Nanase on the bow deck<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p73-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka lunch alone  nanase on the bow deck eats a cheap store rice ball and tea  250 pts  on the bow deck to save money  after a 7 a m  breakfast  8 9 slot full  notes the third years  stares continue   nanase   gulp um  i m sorry  but actually i was eating lunch   ah no  you seemed like you wanted to talk to me yesterday   i m sorry  but i ve already solved the problem myself  so could you just forget about it  uses nanase as an excuse to stop on the crowded deck  so he doesn t look like he s  running away  from the stares  feels bad when she panics at his sudden call  respects that she s solved her problem and leaves  she was about to tell him something yesterday  interrupted by kobashi  but says she s solved it herself and asks him to forget it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Lunch alone; Nanase on the bow deck<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.73–77<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Eats a cheap store rice ball and tea (250 pts) on the bow deck to save money, after a 7 a.m. breakfast (8–9 slot full); notes the third-years&#x27; stares continue.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nanase.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;Gulp…Um, I&#x27;m sorry, but actually…I was eating lunch.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ah no, you seemed like you wanted to talk to me yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m sorry, but I&#x27;ve already solved the problem myself, so could you just forget about it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Uses Nanase as an excuse to stop on the crowded deck (so he doesn&#x27;t look like he&#x27;s &quot;running away&quot; from the stares); feels bad when she panics at his sudden call; respects that she&#x27;s solved her problem and leaves.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She was about to tell him something yesterday (interrupted by Kobashi) but says she&#x27;s solved it herself and asks him to forget it.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p54-1\">← Before: Nanase and Kobashi; the girls&#x27; party invitation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p78-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi catches him: &quot;Beneath the Wheel&quot; and the sea<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p78-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sakayanagi catches him   beneath the wheel  and the sea eats on the quiet fifth floor stern  sakayanagi appears  having deduced his destination from his behavior  snacks  search for an ocean view   it was a coincidence  or so i would like to say  but i ve been chasing after you  ayanokoji kun   yes  that s right  i think so too  however  i did actually see the ocean once before entering this school   have you heard of  beneath the wheel   i don t think he was a genius  because a true genius would never fail   it s dangerous to wear it on the deck  you know    catching her hat in the wind  fufu  that s true isn t it  however  this is my trademark   i just wanted to talk to you  ayanokoji kun  discusses hesse s  beneath the wheel   protagonist hans  a  genius  who fails and dies   sakayanagi calls true genius something that never fails  and hans s death  the height of stupidity  reveals he first saw the ocean at 14  emotionless  catches her trademark hat in a gust  she chased him purely to talk  considerate of his dislike of being seen with her  she reads his patterns  joins him  and shares literary philosophical reflections   a quiet  mutual moment","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi catches him: &quot;Beneath the Wheel&quot; and the sea<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.78–81<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Eats on the quiet fifth-floor stern; Sakayanagi appears, having deduced his destination from his behavior (snacks, search for an ocean view).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;It was a coincidence. Or so I would like to say, but I&#x27;ve been chasing after you, Ayanokōji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes, that&#x27;s right, I think so too. However, I did actually see the ocean once before entering this school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;Have you heard of &#x27;Beneath the Wheel&#x27;?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t think he was a genius. Because a true genius would never fail.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s dangerous to wear it on the deck, you know.&quot; — catching her hat in the wind<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Fufu, that&#x27;s true isn&#x27;t it. However, this is my trademark.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I just wanted to talk to you, Ayanokōji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Discusses Hesse&#x27;s &quot;Beneath the Wheel&quot; (protagonist Hans, a &quot;genius&quot; who fails and dies — Sakayanagi calls true genius something that never fails, and Hans&#x27;s death &quot;the height of stupidity&quot;); reveals he first saw the ocean at 14, emotionless; catches her trademark hat in a gust; she chased him purely to talk, considerate of his dislike of being seen with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She reads his patterns, joins him, and shares literary/philosophical reflections — a quiet, mutual moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–81<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p73-1\">← Before: Lunch alone; Nanase on the bow deck<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p81-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi&#x27;s account of Ichinose&#x27;s apology<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p81-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sakayanagi s account of ichinose s apology as they talk  sakayanagi recounts how ichinose came to see her the previous day to apologize for her selfish last day actions   yesterday  ichinose came to see me   please raise your head  ichinose san  i m not angry about anything   you have a look on your face that says you feel you need to take responsibility somehow   go ahead  please order whatever you would like    her  punishment  30 minutes of afternoon tea  you re a hard person to describe  that s why you seem so scary to me at times  learns sakayanagi forgave ichinose  her contribution outweighed the few points lost   punished  her with tea  and observed that ichinose   conventionally  good    can still frighten people  ayanokoji reflects he s never met a  purely good  person  including ichinose  sakayanagi s account   ichinose s remorse and honesty  ayanokoji s view of her  she tells him about ichinose and shares her observations on goodness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p81-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi&#x27;s account of Ichinose&#x27;s apology<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.81–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As they talk, Sakayanagi recounts how Ichinose came to see her the previous day to apologize for her selfish last-day actions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;Yesterday, Ichinose came to see me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;Please raise your head, Ichinose-san. I&#x27;m not angry about anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;You have a look on your face that says you feel you need to take responsibility somehow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Go ahead; please order whatever you would like.&quot; — her &quot;punishment&quot;: 30 minutes of afternoon tea<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re a hard person to describe. That&#x27;s why you seem so scary to me at times.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Learns Sakayanagi forgave Ichinose (her contribution outweighed the few points lost), &quot;punished&quot; her with tea, and observed that Ichinose — conventionally &quot;good&quot; — can still frighten people; Ayanokōji reflects he&#x27;s never met a &quot;purely good&quot; person, including Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Sakayanagi&#x27;s account — Ichinose&#x27;s remorse and honesty; Ayanokōji&#x27;s view of her.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She tells him about Ichinose and shares her observations on goodness.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–85<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p78-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi catches him: &quot;Beneath the Wheel&quot; and the sea<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p97-1\">→ After: The private pool: Airi and Haruka&#x27;s bold swimsuits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p97-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"miyake-akito hasebe-haruka sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the private pool  airi and haruka s bold swimsuits with the ayanokoji group  akito  haruka  airi  keisei  at a rented private pool  akito asks his opinion of airi   hey  ayanokoji  what do you think of airi   i d be lying if i said i felt nothing like that whatsoever   but if it might destroy this group  i m not gonna push it   it means that she s desperately trying to change   i can t let her stumble during the first step of the airi remodelling project  it s called willpower   you re more like a saint than the other boys  kiyopon  politely averts his eyes from haruka and airi s daring swimsuits  i m trying to be careful not to look  learns haruka designed the  airi remodelling project  to encourage airi s self confidence  matching swimsuits so airi couldn t back out  haruka calls him a  saint  for his restrained gaze  notes the group has grown close  shared a lot of things from top to bottom  confides the  airi remodelling project  and her self consciousness about her body  he admits possible feelings for airi haruka but won t risk the group  her bold new swimsuit and attempt to jump into the pool","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The private pool: Airi and Haruka&#x27;s bold swimsuits<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.97–106<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With the Ayanokōji group (Akito, Haruka, Airi, Keisei) at a rented private pool; Akito asks his opinion of Airi.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;Hey, Ayanokōji. What do you think of Airi?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;d be lying if I said I felt nothing like that whatsoever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> &quot;But if it might destroy this group, I&#x27;m not gonna push it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It means that she&#x27;s desperately trying to change.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t let her stumble during the first step of the Airi remodelling project. It&#x27;s called willpower.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;you&#x27;re more like a saint than the other boys, Kiyopon.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Politely averts his eyes from Haruka and Airi&#x27;s daring swimsuits (&quot;I&#x27;m trying to be careful not to look&quot;); learns Haruka designed the &quot;Airi remodelling project&quot; to encourage Airi&#x27;s self-confidence, matching swimsuits so Airi couldn&#x27;t back out; Haruka calls him a &quot;saint&quot; for his restrained gaze; notes the group has grown close (&quot;shared a lot of things from top to bottom&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.97–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Confides the &quot;Airi remodelling project&quot; and her self-consciousness about her body.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> He admits possible feelings for Airi/Haruka but won&#x27;t risk the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her bold new swimsuit and attempt to jump into the pool.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p81-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi&#x27;s account of Ichinose&#x27;s apology<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p106-1\">→ After: Airi&#x27;s determination to change<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p106-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi hasebe-haruka ishigami-kyou miyake-akito ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka airi s determination to change sits beside airi after she s tired from water volleyball  she explains why she chose to be brave   you looked like you were having a great time   i thought maybe i can change now it might be the only time   i ve started to think that i should change  that i have to change   no  it s not too late     i m rooting for you   it means the original material was already top notch  encourages airi s resolution   she and haruka talked deeply during the island exam  childhood  middle school  and decided to change  airi removed her fake glasses and changed her hairstyle  the  image change  kept secret until second semester  keisei is flustered by her transformed appearance  ayanokoji genuinely praises her decision  she confides her wish to change  he roots for her  flustered by airi s appearance    totally attractive  also caught off guard by her transformation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Airi&#x27;s determination to change<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.106–113<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits beside Airi after she&#x27;s tired from water volleyball; she explains why she chose to be brave.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You looked like you were having a great time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I thought maybe I can change now…It might be the only time…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve started to think that I should change, that I have to change.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, it&#x27;s not too late.&quot; / &quot;I&#x27;m rooting for you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It means the original material was already top-notch.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Encourages Airi&#x27;s resolution — she and Haruka talked deeply during the island exam (childhood, middle school) and decided to change; Airi removed her fake glasses and changed her hairstyle (the &quot;image change&quot; kept secret until second semester); Keisei is flustered by her transformed appearance; Ayanokōji genuinely praises her decision.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> She confides her wish to change; he roots for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Flustered by Airi&#x27;s appearance — &quot;totally attractive.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Also caught off guard by her transformation.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p97-1\">← Before: The private pool: Airi and Haruka&#x27;s bold swimsuits<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p114-1\">→ After: Nanase and the Ike/Shinohara reveal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p114-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji hasebe-haruka ishigami-kyou nanase-tsubasa shinohara ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase and the ike shinohara reveal nanase appears near the pool  a  new record  of meeting him every day  she denies having any purpose beyond coincidence  then leaves   oh  next is ike huh   what a rare combination  shinohara and ike hanging out together   ike and shinohara are like oil and water  why would those two date each other  puzzled why nanase keeps appearing  suppressed a laugh at ike and shinohara arriving together holding hands   they re now dating  which shocks oblivious keisei  appears daily  claims coincidence   ayanokoji suspicious  arrives holding shinohara s hand  their relationship is revealed to the group  with ike  completely unaware ike and shinohara are dating","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p114-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase and the Ike/Shinohara reveal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.114–117<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nanase appears near the pool (a &quot;new record&quot; of meeting him every day); she denies having any purpose beyond coincidence, then leaves.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara.html\">Shinohara<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> &quot;Oh, next is Ike huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> &quot;What a rare combination, Shinohara and Ike hanging out together.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> &quot;Ike and Shinohara are like oil and water, why would those two date each other?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Puzzled why Nanase keeps appearing; suppressed a laugh at Ike and Shinohara arriving together holding hands — they&#x27;re now dating, which shocks oblivious Keisei.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Appears daily, claims coincidence — Ayanokōji suspicious.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Arrives holding Shinohara&#x27;s hand; their relationship is revealed to the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.115–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> With Ike.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Completely unaware Ike and Shinohara are dating.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p106-1\">← Before: Airi&#x27;s determination to change<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p118-1\">→ After: Katsuragi vs Tokitō; Hiyori&#x27;s serious invitation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p118-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"hiyori tokitou-hiroya katsuragi-kouhei shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka katsuragi vs tokito  hiyori s serious invitation hears of a dispute at the restroom between katsuragi and tokito hiroya  distant relative of tokito katsumi  goes to investigate  finding hiyori already there   have you seen katsuragi   katsuragi  are you really followin  ryuen   the current class has already set its course with ryuen as its leader   at that time  ayanokoji kun would you join our class   this invitation is different   i m not impressed  shiina  learns tokito hiroya  selfish  vindictive  and okabe resent katsuragi being ryuen s  dog  and want to use him to rebel  katsuragi defends following ryuen  the class s chosen leader  hiyori seriously invites ayanokoji to join class 2 b as an emergency leader if ryuen falls  and uses him to draw out katsuragi s honest concerns about the class s cohesion  she brings him to witness the dispute and makes a serious invitation for him to join the class  defends following ryuen  voices worry that dissatisfaction will destroy the class if it hits a downturn  criticizes hiyori s trust in ayanokoji  resents katsuragi  plots rebellion   a new  troublesome enemy  for ryuen  his dictatorship breeds hidden resentment  hiyori worries the class would collapse if he were expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p118-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Katsuragi vs Tokitō; Hiyori&#x27;s serious invitation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.118–128<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hears of a dispute at the restroom between Katsuragi and Tokitō Hiroya (distant relative of Tokitō Katsumi); goes to investigate, finding Hiyori already there.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tokitou-hiroya.html\">Tokitō Hiroya<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">hiyori<\/b> &quot;Have you seen Katsuragi?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tokitō Hiroya<\/b> &quot;Katsuragi, are you really followin&#x27; Ryūen?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> &quot;The current class has already set its course with Ryūen as its leader.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;At that time, Ayanokōji-kun…would you join our class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This invitation is different.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m not impressed, Shiina.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Learns Tokitō Hiroya (selfish, vindictive) and Okabe resent Katsuragi being Ryūen&#x27;s &quot;dog&quot; and want to use him to rebel; Katsuragi defends following Ryūen (the class&#x27;s chosen leader); Hiyori seriously invites Ayanokōji to join Class 2-B as an emergency leader if Ryūen falls, and uses him to draw out Katsuragi&#x27;s honest concerns about the class&#x27;s cohesion.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> She brings him to witness the dispute and makes a serious invitation for him to join the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Defends following Ryūen; voices worry that dissatisfaction will destroy the class if it hits a downturn; criticizes Hiyori&#x27;s trust in Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tokitō Hiroya<\/b> Resents Katsuragi, plots rebellion — a new &quot;troublesome enemy&quot; for Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His dictatorship breeds hidden resentment; Hiyori worries the class would collapse if he were expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p114-1\">← Before: Nanase and the Ike/Shinohara reveal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p159-1\">→ After: The surprise treasure hunt game announced<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p159-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the surprise treasure hunt game announced a bonus treasure hunt game is announced by email  free to enter  qr codes with cash rewards  rules explained by takato sensei in the theater  student council members  horikita  ichinose  etc  can t participate   they administer it  participants get a hint paper and pay 10 000 points to enter  100 qr codes around the ship with values from 5 000 to 1 000 000 points  notes ichinose sits with the student council  the tears she shed yesterday still on his mind  and the possibility that revealing his dating will erase her feelings  decides to participate  avoids pairing with kei  who paired with mori nene for appearances  her membership in the council prevents her joining  his planned public dating announcement may end her feelings  his girlfriend   deliberately doesn t pair with her so their secret stays hidden","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The surprise treasure hunt game announced<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.159–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A bonus treasure-hunt game is announced by email (free to enter, QR codes with cash rewards); rules explained by Takatō-sensei in the theater.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Student council members (Horikita, Ichinose, etc.) can&#x27;t participate — they administer it; participants get a hint paper and pay 10,000 points to enter; 100 QR codes around the ship with values from 5,000 to 1,000,000 points.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Ichinose sits with the student council (the tears she shed yesterday still on his mind, and the possibility that revealing his dating will erase her feelings); decides to participate, avoids pairing with Kei (who paired with Mori Nene for appearances).<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her membership in the council prevents her joining; his planned public dating announcement may end her feelings.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend — deliberately doesn&#x27;t pair with her so their secret stays hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p118-1\">← Before: Katsuragi vs Tokitō; Hiyori&#x27;s serious invitation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p167-1\">→ After: Teaming with Satō; QR-code deduction; Nagumo&#x27;s orders<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p167-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"satou-maya matsushita-chiaki nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka teaming with sato  qr code deduction  nagumo s orders bumps into sato  who asks him to pair up  she has  180 000 points   you know ayanokoji kun  have you partnered up with anyone yet   would you pair up with me   okay  i got it  if you re okay with me  sato  we can pair up   ehh  really  accepts  no reason to refuse  notes sato had been the first to confess to him last year  reasons the hint codes are modest  not the top 300 000  since it s a  luck  game  solves the riddle easily  and uses his phone s camera flash with sato s to find and photograph hidden qr codes   a two phone advantage  his partner   she trusts him to lead  her honest delight pleases him  she and third year tatara appear  tatara  under nagumo s order not to engage him  flees  confirms an order went out to all third years regarding him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p167-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Teaming with Satō; QR-code deduction; Nagumo&#x27;s orders<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.167–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Bumps into Satō, who asks him to pair up; she has ~180,000 points.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> &quot;You know…Ayanokōji-kun, have you partnered up with anyone yet?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> &quot;Would you…pair up with me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Okay, I got it. If you&#x27;re okay with me, Satō, we can pair up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ehh? Really?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Accepts (no reason to refuse); notes Satō had been the first to confess to him last year; reasons the hint codes are modest (not the top 300,000) since it&#x27;s a &quot;luck&quot; game, solves the riddle easily, and uses his phone&#x27;s camera/flash with Satō&#x27;s to find and photograph hidden QR codes — a two-phone advantage.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> His partner — she trusts him to lead; her honest delight pleases him.<span class=\"pg\">p.167–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> She and third-year Tatara appear; Tatara (under Nagumo&#x27;s order not to engage him) flees.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Confirms an order went out to all third-years regarding him.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p159-1\">← Before: The surprise treasure hunt game announced<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p176-1\">→ After: Nanase&#x27;s daily visits; Nakaizumi watching her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p176-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa satou-maya nakaizumi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase s daily visits  nakaizumi watching her nanase appears again  breaking his record of seeing her daily  sato teases her about becoming more mature   i m glad to see that you re doing well today  ayanokoji senpai   m mental  so not like drinking milk or getting a massage every day  realizes nanase has been checking on his condition daily  from when she was his ally  and that nakaizumi has been following her   likely investigating her  or marking her due to 20 million bounty suspicions  decides she s  completely innocent  of the cliff attack  checks on him daily  he notes her continued vigilance  following nanase   under whose orders is unclear","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p176-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase&#x27;s daily visits; Nakaizumi watching her<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.176–178<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nanase appears again (breaking his record of seeing her daily); Satō teases her about becoming more mature.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m glad to see that you&#x27;re doing well today, Ayanokōji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> &quot;M-mental? So not like drinking milk or getting a massage every day?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes Nanase has been checking on his condition daily (from when she was his ally), and that Nakaizumi has been following her — likely investigating her, or marking her due to 20-million-bounty suspicions; decides she&#x27;s &quot;completely innocent&quot; of the cliff attack.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Checks on him daily; he notes her continued vigilance.<span class=\"pg\">p.176–178<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">nakaizumi<\/b> Following Nanase — under whose orders is unclear.<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p167-1\">← Before: Teaming with Satō; QR-code deduction; Nagumo&#x27;s orders<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p192-1\">→ After: Satō&#x27;s self-doubt; asking to learn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p192-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"satou-maya horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sato s self doubt  asking to learn  i wonder what i should do  what do i need to work on so that i don t cause trouble for the class   this isn t just any high school  it s a hell of a place   if you want to work hard for your classmates  i suppose studying is essential   a ayanokoji kun  i don t suppose you could teach me how to study  listens to sato s doubts about being a burden  gently redirects   studying is essential  recommends horikita  who trained sudo  and agrees to be the bridge  avoiding the awkwardness of teaching her himself  karuizawa would be angry  she asks him to bridge her to horikita for tutoring  recommended as a tutor  ayanokoji brokers the request","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Satō&#x27;s self-doubt; asking to learn<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.192–193<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> &quot;I wonder what I should do. What do I need to work on so that I don&#x27;t cause trouble for the class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> &quot;this isn&#x27;t just any high school; it&#x27;s a hell of a place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you want to work hard for your classmates, I suppose studying is essential.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A-Ayanokōji-kun, I don&#x27;t suppose you could teach me how to study…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Listens to Satō&#x27;s doubts about being a burden; gently redirects — studying is essential, recommends Horikita (who trained Sudō) and agrees to be the bridge, avoiding the awkwardness of teaching her himself (Karuizawa would be angry).<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> She asks him to bridge her to Horikita for tutoring.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Recommended as a tutor; Ayanokōji brokers the request.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p176-1\">← Before: Nanase&#x27;s daily visits; Nakaizumi watching her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p194-1\">→ After: Student council shift; Kushida&#x27;s lunch invitation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p194-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"yagami-takuya kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka student council shift  kushida s lunch invitation  horikita senpai  it s time for your shift change    yagami  well then  i ll see you later  kushida senpai    yagami administering rewards with the council  judges yagami a reliable  skilled underclassman   a candidate for the next student council president  notes his  more than friends  less than lovers  closeness with kushida  accepts kushida s unusual lunch invitation as a chance to ask his lingering questions  reliable council worker  best next generation president candidate  her closeness with yagami  more than friends  less than lovers  accepts her lunch invitation  sensing an opportunity","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Student council shift; Kushida&#x27;s lunch invitation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.194–196<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Horikita-senpai, it&#x27;s time for your shift change.&quot; — Yagami<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Well then, I&#x27;ll see you later, Kushida-senpai.&quot; — Yagami<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Administering rewards with the council; judges Yagami a reliable, skilled underclassman — a candidate for the next Student Council President; notes his &quot;more than friends, less than lovers&quot; closeness with Kushida; accepts Kushida&#x27;s unusual lunch invitation as a chance to ask his lingering questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> Reliable council worker; best next-generation president candidate.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Her closeness with Yagami &quot;more than friends, less than lovers&quot;; accepts her lunch invitation, sensing an opportunity.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p192-1\">← Before: Satō&#x27;s self-doubt; asking to learn<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p217-1\">→ After: The &quot;I love you&quot; phone call with Kei<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p217-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei nanase-tsubasa nagumo-miyabi satou-maya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the  i love you  phone call with kei at  9 p m  receives a message from kei wanting to talk on the phone  no emoticons   serious  slips out to the deck and calls her   i heard some unpleasant rumours about you  you know   i can t think of anything   you ve been  like  messing around with an underclassman  that rumour   she s just an underclassman  nothing more   even though i actually wanted to pair up with you  kiyotaka   yeah  i love you   i ll never forgive you if you cheat on me   get it   i love you   yep  i knew it  you re the best  i m absolutely never giving you to anyone else   please say it     i love you  carefully feigns ignorance of the rumor  nanase  so as not to say the wrong thing  realizes the rumor likely came from nagumo  who saw him with ichinose  spread via third years  confirms going public about dating is necessary  checks the deck is empty before saying  i love you   kei laughs at his caution  finds the repeated  awkward exchanges a genuine expression of affection    the thing called love really was interesting  his girlfriend   jealous over the nanase rumor and the sato pairing  anxious about going public  demands repeated  i love you s  source of the rumor that he was involved with an underclassman   their many meetings were witnessed  suspects he spread the rumor after seeing his exchange with ichinose  kei knows he paired with her in the treasure hunt","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p217-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The &quot;I love you&quot; phone call with Kei<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.217–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At ~9 p.m., receives a message from Kei wanting to talk on the phone (no emoticons — serious); slips out to the deck and calls her.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;I heard some unpleasant rumours about you, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t think of anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> &quot;You&#x27;ve been, like, messing around with an underclassman! That rumour!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She&#x27;s just an underclassman, nothing more.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even though I actually wanted to pair up with you, Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, I love you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll never forgive you if you cheat on me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Get it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…I love you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yep, I knew it, you&#x27;re the best… I&#x27;m absolutely never giving you to anyone else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;…Please say it.&quot; / &quot;…I love you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Carefully feigns ignorance of the rumor (Nanase) so as not to say the wrong thing; realizes the rumor likely came from Nagumo (who saw him with Ichinose) spread via third-years; confirms going public about dating is necessary; checks the deck is empty before saying &quot;I love you&quot; (Kei laughs at his caution); finds the repeated, awkward exchanges a genuine expression of affection — &quot;the thing called love really was interesting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217–224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend — jealous over the Nanase rumor and the Satō pairing, anxious about going public, demands repeated &quot;I love you&quot;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Source of the rumor that he was involved with an underclassman — their many meetings were witnessed.<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Suspects he spread the rumor after seeing his exchange with Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Kei knows he paired with her in the treasure hunt.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p194-1\">← Before: Student council shift; Kushida&#x27;s lunch invitation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p268-1\">→ After: Epilogue: the last secret date; learning to kiss<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p268-1","v":"y2v4.5","y":2,"o":20,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  the last secret date  learning to kiss back at school after the cruise  reflects on a lazy remaining vacation but a vastly expanded circle of friends  ayanokoji group  sudo ike  ishizaki hiyori  even ichinose s class    unthinkable a year ago  spends the last day of summer vacation with kei in his room   ahh  today s the last day of summer vacation    kei  there s no need for you to force yourself to tell people  i won t be held responsible if your status drops   i ll absolutely tell them  even if something happens  you ll protect me so i ll be fine  right  kiyotaka  holds her hand and  after a first tentative kiss  repeats it   learning timing through practice  the only way to learn the timing was to repeat it over and over again  reflects that they ve finished  the first half of the curriculum of love  and will face an  arduous trial  when they graduate  a given  when kei will have to stand up on her own without her host  his girlfriend   they ll go public in second semester  they learn to kiss together","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p268-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: the last secret date; learning to kiss<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V4.5 · p.268–274<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back at school after the cruise, reflects on a lazy remaining vacation but a vastly expanded circle of friends (Ayanokōji group, Sudō/Ike, Ishizaki/Hiyori, even Ichinose&#x27;s class) — unthinkable a year ago; spends the last day of summer vacation with Kei in his room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ahh, today&#x27;s the last day of summer vacation…&quot; — Kei<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s no need for you to force yourself to tell people. I won&#x27;t be held responsible if your status drops.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.268<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll absolutely tell them. Even if something happens, you&#x27;ll protect me so I&#x27;ll be fine. Right, Kiyotaka?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.269<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Holds her hand and, after a first tentative kiss, repeats it — learning timing through practice (&quot;the only way to learn the timing was to repeat it over and over again&quot;); reflects that they&#x27;ve finished &quot;the first half of the curriculum of love&quot; and will face an &quot;arduous trial&quot; when they graduate (&quot;a given&quot;), when Kei will have to stand up on her own without her host.<span class=\"pg\">p.268–274<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend — they&#x27;ll go public in second semester; they learn to kiss together.<span class=\"pg\">p.268–274<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v4_5-p217-1\">← Before: The &quot;I love you&quot; phone call with Kei<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p7-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.7-243<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p9-1\">→ After: Second semester begins; the dating reveal to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p9-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka second semester begins  the dating reveal to sudo walks to school with sudo  yawning  up all night studying to raise his academics to b  asks whether ike has already kissed shinohara   suzune warned me about the possibility of a written exam early in the second semester  so i m staying up all night   i want to get higher scores so i can bring my oaa s academic performance up to b or something   i ve never asked  but have you ever had a girlfriend  ayanokoji   there s no use in lying to you  so i ll confess to you that i got my first girlfriend a little while ago   really  you re sure it s not suzune  aren t you   we re dating   wow  my bad  but  no  eh  hey  why is it karuizawa  amused by sudo s transformation  diligent  no longer late   both literary and military arts  honestly reveals he has a girlfriend rather than fake it  it would spread from kei anyway  tells sudo it s not horikita  and lets him be the first  icebreaker    sudo s whispered concern that kei s  flashy  past makes her a  hurdle  for a first girlfriend is left unchallenged  proud of his growth  becomes the first person told of the ayanokoji karuizawa relationship  his girlfriend  she arrives to walk with him and pouts about the timing of the public announcement  sudo assumed  hopefully worriedly  she might be the girlfriend  sudo references kei s past relationship with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Second semester begins; the dating reveal to Sudō<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.9–12<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks to school with Sudō (yawning, up all night studying to raise his Academics to B); asks whether Ike has already kissed Shinohara.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Suzune warned me about the possibility of a written exam early in the second semester, so I&#x27;m staying up all night.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;I want to get higher scores so I can bring my OAA&#x27;s academic performance up to B or something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.9<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve never asked, but have you ever had a girlfriend, Ayanokōji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no use in lying to you, so I&#x27;ll confess to you that I got my first girlfriend a little while ago.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Really? You&#x27;re sure it&#x27;s not Suzune, aren&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;re dating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wow, my bad. But, no, eh! Hey, why is it Karuizawa?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Amused by Sudō&#x27;s transformation (diligent, no longer late, &quot;both literary and military arts&quot;); honestly reveals he has a girlfriend rather than fake it (it would spread from Kei anyway), tells Sudō it&#x27;s not Horikita, and lets him be the first &quot;icebreaker&quot; — Sudō&#x27;s whispered concern that Kei&#x27;s &quot;flashy&quot; past makes her a &quot;hurdle&quot; for a first girlfriend is left unchallenged.<span class=\"pg\">p.9–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Proud of his growth; becomes the first person told of the Ayanokōji-Karuizawa relationship.<span class=\"pg\">p.9–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend; she arrives to walk with him and pouts about the timing of the public announcement.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sudō assumed (hopefully/worriedly) she might be the girlfriend.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Sudō references Kei&#x27;s past relationship with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p7-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p13-1\">→ After: Chabashira announces the second-semester events<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p13-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka chabashira announces the second semester events in homeroom  chabashira outlines a packed second semester  an october sports festival  a november cultural festival  the school s first  plus midterm final exams and a school trip  cultural festival  each 2nd year given 5 000 private points  1st years 5 500  3rd years 4 500  for preparation  100 class points to 1st 4th place  50 to 5th 8th  none below  extra funds for student council club contributions  unused funds confiscated  stall locations cost points  main gate 1   10 000  only one class per location  conflicts settled by bidding war to the school  stall details kept secret until the day  leaks penalized  outside items allowed with permission  analyzes the rules   the cultural festival is announced first because preparation must start early  suspects there s more to it than the straightforward rules  evidence that i ve become deeply ingrained in the structure of this school  delivers the briefing  he notes she looks the same as first semester","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira announces the second-semester events<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.13–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In homeroom, Chabashira outlines a packed second semester: an October sports festival, a November cultural festival (the school&#x27;s first), plus midterm/final exams and a school trip.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Cultural festival: each 2nd-year given 5,000 private points (1st-years 5,500, 3rd-years 4,500) for preparation; 100 class points to 1st–4th place, 50 to 5th–8th, none below; extra funds for student council/club contributions; unused funds confiscated.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Stall locations cost points (Main Gate 1 = 10,000); only one class per location, conflicts settled by bidding war to the school; stall details kept secret until the day (leaks penalized); outside items allowed with permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Analyzes the rules — the cultural festival is announced first because preparation must start early; suspects there&#x27;s more to it than the straightforward rules (&quot;evidence that I&#x27;ve become deeply ingrained in the structure of this school&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.13–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Delivers the briefing; he notes she looks the same as first semester.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p9-1\">← Before: Second semester begins; the dating reveal to Sudō<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p17-1\">→ After: The class&#x27;s festival discussion; Horikita&#x27;s proposal system<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p17-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune matsushita-chiaki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the class s festival discussion  horikita s proposal system  when it comes to cultural festivals  food  haunted houses  and the like are the orthodox ones  aren t they   maybe we should bring our ideas to the class and test them repeatedly  even if we have to use private points   i think some people will be reluctant to do anything if they have to pay for it themselves  listens as usual  learns horikita s system   test ideas with real money  reward planners from the class point windfall  100 class points   390 000 private points month split  and maintain total secrecy  judges it sensible  active students benefit  slackers benefit later  proposes the reward for ideas and confidentiality system  he approves privately  lists festival event options on the monitor  warns some students won t contribute if they must pay personally","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The class&#x27;s festival discussion; Horikita&#x27;s proposal system<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.17–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;When it comes to cultural festivals, food, haunted houses, and the like are the orthodox ones, aren&#x27;t they?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;maybe we should bring our ideas to the class and test them repeatedly, even if we have to use private points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> &quot;I think some people will be reluctant to do anything if they have to pay for it themselves.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Listens as usual; learns Horikita&#x27;s system — test ideas with real money, reward planners from the class-point windfall (100 class points = 390,000 private points/month split), and maintain total secrecy; judges it sensible (active students benefit, slackers benefit later).<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Proposes the reward-for-ideas and confidentiality system; he approves privately.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Lists festival event options on the monitor.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Warns some students won&#x27;t contribute if they must pay personally.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p13-1\">← Before: Chabashira announces the second-semester events<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p29-1\">→ After: The Unanimous Voting Exam briefing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p29-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the unanimous voting exam briefing in homeroom  chabashira announces a surprise special exam  before  the sports festival   held only for second years  tomorrow  the  unanimous voting exam  5 questions  up to 4 options each  all 39 classmates vote anonymously  60 seconds  not unanimous   10 minute discussion   revote  5 hour limit  90 seconds cumulative overtime penalty   expulsion  50 class points for clearing   300 for failing  protection points disabled  phones collected  binding agreements money exchanges forbidden  if a vote awards points to  one student  that student is chosen by majority nomination  their own vote removed  then the class votes for against  a unanimous  against  removes them and picks another  candidates may volunteer  analyzes the sample questions   5 class points are worth 9 000 private points over the remaining 18 months  so the 10 000 point instant gain is marginally better  but the  just in case  risk of losing class a matters more  deliberately votes  for  in the practice rounds to avoid unanimity and teach the class how the exam works  sudo does the same  watchful   notes horikita s growth as a  pillar of support   calmly reframes risk as benefit  winning class approval  sees chabashira s hidden sweetness  and realizes the exam s real difficulty is the anonymous vote  people can lie about how they voted  and the impossibility of enforced agreements  delivers the briefing  he notes she must be inwardly pleased with the class  her calming leadership earns the class s approval","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Unanimous Voting Exam briefing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.29–44<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In homeroom, Chabashira announces a surprise special exam *before* the sports festival — held only for second-years, tomorrow.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The &quot;Unanimous Voting Exam&quot;: 5 questions, up to 4 options each; all 39 classmates vote anonymously (60 seconds); not unanimous → 10-minute discussion → revote; 5-hour limit; 90 seconds cumulative overtime penalty = expulsion; 50 class points for clearing, −300 for failing; protection points disabled; phones collected; binding agreements/money exchanges forbidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> If a vote awards points to &quot;one student,&quot; that student is chosen by majority nomination (their own vote removed), then the class votes for/against; a unanimous &quot;against&quot; removes them and picks another; candidates may volunteer.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Analyzes the sample questions — 5 class points are worth 9,000 private points over the remaining 18 months, so the 10,000-point instant gain is marginally better, but the &quot;just in case&quot; risk of losing Class A matters more; deliberately votes &quot;for&quot; in the practice rounds to avoid unanimity and teach the class how the exam works (Sudō does the same).<span class=\"pg\">p.32–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watchful — notes Horikita&#x27;s growth as a &quot;pillar of support&quot; (calmly reframes risk as benefit, winning class approval), sees Chabashira&#x27;s hidden sweetness, and realizes the exam&#x27;s real difficulty is the anonymous vote (people can lie about how they voted) and the impossibility of enforced agreements.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Delivers the briefing; he notes she must be inwardly pleased with the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her calming leadership earns the class&#x27;s approval.<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p17-1\">← Before: The class&#x27;s festival discussion; Horikita&#x27;s proposal system<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p45-1\">→ After: Kushida proposes Horikita as emergency leader; Kei reveals the relationship<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p45-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kushida proposes horikita as emergency leader  kei reveals the relationship  then i think it s better to have a clear leader in case there s a contingency where the choices don t add up    kushida  yes  it s possible that other classes will have similar strategies  and you ll be able to use them if you have a difference of opinion    horikita  sorry guys  i m going to eat with kei today   sorry  but i m his girlfriend and i m his priority  you know    kei watches kushida s proposal to make horikita emergency leader pass easily  she s the unifying figure  then plays along as kei dramatically  kidnaps  him at lunch  calling her by her first name and confirming they re dating in front of the stunned class   the relationship goes public in one stroke  proposes horikita as leader   a move he notes with interest  accepts the emergency leader role  she publicly claims him as her boyfriend  he goes along  she s stunned by the reveal  first name basis   girlfriend","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kushida proposes Horikita as emergency leader; Kei reveals the relationship<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.45–46<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then I think it&#x27;s better to have a clear leader in case there&#x27;s a contingency where the choices don&#x27;t add up.&quot; — Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. It&#x27;s possible that other classes will have similar strategies, and you&#x27;ll be able to use them if you have a difference of opinion.&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sorry guys, I&#x27;m going to eat with Kei today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, but I&#x27;m his girlfriend and I&#x27;m his priority, you know?&quot; — Kei<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches Kushida&#x27;s proposal to make Horikita emergency leader pass easily (she&#x27;s the unifying figure); then plays along as Kei dramatically &quot;kidnaps&quot; him at lunch, Calling her by her first name and confirming they&#x27;re dating in front of the stunned class — the relationship goes public in one stroke.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Proposes Horikita as leader — a move he notes with interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Accepts the emergency-leader role.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She publicly claims him as her boyfriend; he goes along.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She&#x27;s stunned by the reveal (first-name basis, &quot;girlfriend&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p29-1\">← Before: The Unanimous Voting Exam briefing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p48-1\">→ After: Haruka walks home: Airi&#x27;s heartbreak; the maid-café request<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p48-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka sakura-airi karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka haruka walks home  airi s heartbreak  the maid cafe request  hey kiyopon  would you like to walk home with me    haruka  is it true that you started going out with karuizawasan  i still can t believe it  even now   i was in the same group as kei in the cruise ship special exam last year   we ve decided on one of the events for the cultural festival    the maid cafe  don t you think you re taking airi s feelings too lightly    haruka walks home with haruka  airi too heartbroken to speak to him  honestly confirms the relationship  explains how it developed from the cruise ship exam  and admits he confessed first  asks haruka and airi to be maid cafe waitresses  airi s second chance  haruka insists airi s feelings are too deep to change so easily  he misreads this and angers her  she becomes his confidante about the relationship  sharply rebukes him for underestimating airi  heartbroken   cried all through lunch  haruka shields her  ayanokoji sees a  gem  who could shine as a waitress  haruka is shocked it s her  her poor reputation  admits he confessed first  the maid cafe is a secret known only to him  horikita and the organizers","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Haruka walks home: Airi&#x27;s heartbreak; the maid-café request<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.48–55<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Hey Kiyopon, would you like to walk home with me?&quot; — Haruka<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;is it true that you started going out with Karuizawasan? I still can&#x27;t believe it, even now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was in the same group as Kei in the Cruise Ship special exam last year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;we&#x27;ve decided on one of the events for the cultural festival.&quot; — the maid café<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;don&#x27;t you think you&#x27;re taking Airi&#x27;s feelings too lightly?&quot; — Haruka<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Walks home with Haruka (Airi too heartbroken to speak to him); honestly confirms the relationship, explains how it developed from the cruise-ship exam, and admits he confessed first; asks Haruka and Airi to be maid-café waitresses (Airi&#x27;s second chance). Haruka insists Airi&#x27;s feelings are too deep to change so easily; he misreads this and angers her.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She becomes his confidante about the relationship; sharply rebukes him for underestimating Airi.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Heartbroken — cried all through lunch; Haruka shields her; Ayanokōji sees a &quot;gem&quot; who could shine as a waitress.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Haruka is shocked it&#x27;s her (her poor reputation); admits he confessed first.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The maid café is a secret known only to him, Horikita and the organizers.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p45-1\">← Before: Kushida proposes Horikita as emergency leader; Kei reveals the relationship<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p56-1\">→ After: Horikita&#x27;s late-night visit: consulting on the exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p56-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka horikita s late night visit  consulting on the exam in the dorm elevator and then his room  horikita catches him   a year ago their being alone together would have been unthinkable  kei good naturedly leaves them alone   how long have you been seeing her   i was prepared for you to refuse   if you want to make sure that you clear this special exam  i was thinking about making it semi compulsory before the exam   i have a proposal for a special exam tomorrow  i could ask someone else  but i want to ask someone who understands me  delights in how readily she accepts his help  she d expected refusal because of the maid cafe  amused that she s slightly angry about his dating  she guessed it began before spring break  agrees to advise her on the exam and notices her anger dissipate as she gets to the point  comes to his room for advice on the exam  their closeness has grown dramatically  gracefully yields the elevator to horikita  judging she s no romantic threat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p56-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Horikita&#x27;s late-night visit: consulting on the exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.56–59<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the dorm elevator and then his room, Horikita catches him — a year ago their being alone together would have been unthinkable; Kei good-naturedly leaves them alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How long have you been seeing her?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was prepared for you to refuse.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you want to make sure that you clear this special exam, I was thinking about making it semi-compulsory before the exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a proposal for a special exam tomorrow. I could ask someone else, but I want to ask someone who understands me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Delights in how readily she accepts his help (she&#x27;d expected refusal because of the maid café); amused that she&#x27;s slightly angry about his dating (she guessed it began before spring break); agrees to advise her on the exam and notices her anger dissipate as she gets to the point.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Comes to his room for advice on the exam; their closeness has grown dramatically.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Gracefully yields the elevator to Horikita, judging she&#x27;s no romantic threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p48-1\">← Before: Haruka walks home: Airi&#x27;s heartbreak; the maid-café request<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p78-1\">→ After: Exam day: pre-vote analysis; the &quot;spread the votes&quot; strategy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p78-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka exam day  pre vote analysis  the  spread the votes  strategy on the day of the unanimous voting exam  observes the class  chabashira notes a teacher who interferes with the exam s nature would be questioned  reaffirms the pact with horikita  he votes for the first option in round one to prevent accidental unanimity and gauge true class opinion  the exam allows one hour per question  and the greatest danger is a question that divides the class  realizes there s no room for cheating  anonymous votes  snooping impossible    unanimity is everything  calmly trusts horikita s leadership  they pre agreed their voting roles  notes airi is being pushed by haruka to reconcile over the dating news  she remains withdrawn  their pre exam pact   she votes second option  he votes first  to keep round one non unanimous  withdrawn and upset over the relationship reveal  haruka urges her to speak to ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Exam day: pre-vote analysis; the &quot;spread the votes&quot; strategy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.78–84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the day of the Unanimous Voting Exam, observes the class; Chabashira notes a teacher who interferes with the exam&#x27;s nature would be questioned.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reaffirms the pact with Horikita: he votes for the first option in round one to prevent accidental unanimity and gauge true class opinion; the exam allows one hour per question, and the greatest danger is a question that divides the class; realizes there&#x27;s no room for cheating (anonymous votes, snooping impossible) — unanimity is everything.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calmly trusts Horikita&#x27;s leadership (they pre-agreed their voting roles); notes Airi is being pushed by Haruka to reconcile over the dating news (she remains withdrawn).<span class=\"pg\">p.78–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Their pre-exam pact — she votes second option, he votes first, to keep round one non-unanimous.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Withdrawn and upset over the relationship reveal; Haruka urges her to speak to Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p56-1\">← Before: Horikita&#x27;s late-night visit: consulting on the exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p85-1\">→ After: Questions 1 and 2: opponent class and school trip<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p85-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ishigami-kyou sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka questions 1 and 2  opponent class and school trip q1  choose an opponent class for a special exam  extra class points for beating higher classes  first vote  a 5  b 21  d 13  horikita argues for class b  ichinose   fair fight  currently b  on a downward slope  unlikely to outsmart them  hirata and kei back her  second vote 39 for b  q2  school trip destination  hokkaido kyoto okinawa  split 17 3 19 then 18 4 17   i had agreed with horikita that i would always vote for the first choice  so without hesitation  i chose class a  the first choice    narration follows the pact  votes class a first round  then b  and observes horikita s skillful persuasion and the class s debate  q2 s deadlock between hokkaido and okinawa is settled when keisei volunteers for rock paper scissors and loses quickly  sudo s vote for okinawa  the ocean  is overridden  her arguments unify the class  he supports her from behind the scenes  keisei volunteers for rock paper scissors to break the q2 tie  loses  votes for okinawa because of the ocean  angry that his view was overridden","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Questions 1 and 2: opponent class and school trip<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.85–90<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I had agreed with Horikita that I would always vote for the first choice, so without hesitation, I chose Class A, the first choice.&quot; — narration<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Q1: choose an opponent class for a special exam (extra class points for beating higher classes). First vote: A 5, B 21, D 13; Horikita argues for Class B (Ichinose — fair fight, currently B, on a downward slope, unlikely to outsmart them); Hirata and Kei back her; second vote 39 for B. Q2: school trip destination (Hokkaido/Kyoto/Okinawa); split 17/3/19 then 18/4/17.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Follows the pact (votes Class A first round, then B), and observes Horikita&#x27;s skillful persuasion and the class&#x27;s debate; Q2&#x27;s deadlock between Hokkaido and Okinawa is settled when Keisei volunteers for rock-paper-scissors and loses quickly; Sudō&#x27;s vote for Okinawa (&quot;the ocean&quot;) is overridden.<span class=\"pg\">p.86–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her arguments unify the class; he supports her from behind the scenes.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Keisei volunteers for rock-paper-scissors to break the Q2 tie, loses.<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Votes for Okinawa because of the ocean; angry that his view was overridden.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p78-1\">← Before: Exam day: pre-vote analysis; the &quot;spread the votes&quot; strategy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p97-1\">→ After: Question 3: protection points; Keisei&#x27;s &quot;upfront investment&quot; argument<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p97-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ishigami-kyou horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka question 3  protection points  keisei s  upfront investment  argument q3  choose among  1  give up protection points   2  halve private points for 6 months to protect one student   3  similar   bottom five students lose private points for 6 months regardless  first vote  12 grant 3 random  5 grant 1 chosen  22 grant none  keisei argued that with class points set to rise over the next six months  the lost private points are an investment in the future   this option will result in losing half of our private points for six months   for the amount of protection points we give up  we can have the horikita girl work harder than anyone else  keisei reframes lost private points as an  upfront investment    with  300 class points by semester s end  transfers rise  50   20m  so a protection point is worth  7m private points  koenji unexpectedly supports it  ayanokoji agrees despite personally preferring options 1 3  since opposing without a good reason would be  for the good of the class  only in name  the class votes 39 to grant one protection point to horikita  keisei s strategic argument wins over the class  ayanokoji admires its logic  unanimously granted a protection point   a purchase that was not cheap but not too expensive unexpectedly backs keisei s plan   he wants horikita to  work harder","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Question 3: protection points; Keisei&#x27;s &quot;upfront investment&quot; argument<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.97–104<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This option will result in losing half of our private points for six months.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> &quot;For the amount of protection points we give up, we can have the Horikita girl work harder than anyone else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Q3: choose among (1) give up protection points, (2) halve private points for 6 months to protect one student, (3) similar — bottom-five students lose private points for 6 months regardless. First vote: 12 grant 3 random, 5 grant 1 chosen, 22 grant none.<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Keisei argued that with class points set to rise over the next six months, the lost private points are an investment in the future.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Keisei reframes lost private points as an &quot;upfront investment&quot; — with +300 class points by semester&#x27;s end, transfers rise ~50% (~20M), so a protection point is worth ~7M private points; Kōenji unexpectedly supports it; Ayanokōji agrees despite personally preferring options 1/3, since opposing without a good reason would be &quot;for the good of the class&quot; only in name; the class votes 39 to grant one protection point to Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Keisei&#x27;s strategic argument wins over the class; Ayanokōji admires its logic.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Unanimously granted a protection point — a purchase that was not cheap but not too expensive<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Unexpectedly backs Keisei&#x27;s plan — he wants Horikita to &quot;work harder.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p85-1\">← Before: Questions 1 and 2: opponent class and school trip<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p104-1\">→ After: Question 4: written-exam rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p104-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka question 4  written exam rules q4  choose one disadvantage for the end of semester written exam   increased difficulty  increased penalty  or decreased reward  first vote 6 18 15  second vote unanimous for  increase penalty  after horikita argues diligent study avoids penalties  notes these are  nasty choices  with no upside  the class reaches unanimity quickly on horikita s persuasion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p104-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Question 4: written-exam rules<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.104–105<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Q4: choose one disadvantage for the end-of-semester written exam — increased difficulty, increased penalty, or decreased reward. First vote 6/18/15; second vote unanimous for &quot;increase penalty&quot; after Horikita argues diligent study avoids penalties.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes these are &quot;nasty choices&quot; with no upside; the class reaches unanimity quickly on Horikita&#x27;s persuasion.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p97-1\">← Before: Question 3: protection points; Keisei&#x27;s &quot;upfront investment&quot; argument<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p106-1\">→ After: Question 5: expel a classmate for 100 class points; the deadlock<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p106-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kouenji-rokusuke karuizawa-kei sudou-ken hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka question 5  expel a classmate for 100 class points  the deadlock reaches the final question in about an hour  chabashira s complexion has visibly worsened as the exam progresses  q5   gain 100 class points in exchange for one classmate being expelled    if unanimously in favour  identify and vote on the student  ayanokoji reasons 100 points aren t worth a classmate now  unlike his third year scenario  so almost everyone should vote against   but the voting pact means round one must not be unanimous  he votes  against  anyway  deviating from the pact  to avoid needless conflict  leaving koenji as the only visible  for  vote   i voted against both the first vote and just now  in the second vote   but because of the content of the question  i took the liberty of deciding that it would be better to vote for the against option  realizes there s a  second  unseen  in favour  voter   someone clinging not to the 100 points but to  the right to expel someone  hides his own second vote against  lets horikita explain the pact away  and watches as koenji openly admits voting in favour  i ve never thought of any of you as my friends  then agrees to switch after horikita s deal  10 000 points month until graduation  deliberately stays sidelined  intervening only with a subtle cough to prompt kei to realize horikita suspects someone  understands horikita will never name the unseen voter  it would cost her future standing  and that the real battle is against the anonymous  in favour  vote  his pact partner  he shields her by taking the  for  vote on q1   q4 and quietly voting against on q5  notes her calm leadership and that she won t name the suspect  the visible  in favour  voter  ayanokoji knows he s bluffing for attention but watches horikita buy him off  his cough prompts kei to ask horikita if she knows who s voting in favour  suspects koenji and lashes out  ayanokoji notes the danger of mob justification  rationalizing expelling whoever is  holding back the class  makes the heartfelt appeal not to cut off classmates for points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Question 5: expel a classmate for 100 class points; the deadlock<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.106–115<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reaches the final question in about an hour; Chabashira&#x27;s complexion has visibly worsened as the exam progresses.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I voted against both the first vote and just now, in the second vote.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;But because of the content of the question, I took the liberty of deciding that it would be better to vote for the against option.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Q5: &quot;Gain 100 class points in exchange for one classmate being expelled&quot; — if unanimously in favour, identify and vote on the student. Ayanokōji reasons 100 points aren&#x27;t worth a classmate now (unlike his third-year scenario), so almost everyone should vote against — but the voting pact means round one must not be unanimous; he votes &quot;against&quot; anyway (deviating from the pact) to avoid needless conflict, leaving Kōenji as the only visible &quot;for&quot; vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes there&#x27;s a *second* unseen &quot;in favour&quot; voter — someone clinging not to the 100 points but to &quot;the right to expel someone&quot;; hides his own second vote against, lets Horikita explain the pact away, and watches as Kōenji openly admits voting in favour (&quot;I&#x27;ve never thought of any of you as my friends&quot;), then agrees to switch after Horikita&#x27;s deal (10,000 points/month until graduation).<span class=\"pg\">p.111–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately stays sidelined, intervening only with a subtle cough to prompt Kei to realize Horikita suspects someone; understands Horikita will never name the unseen voter (it would cost her future standing), and that the real battle is against the anonymous &quot;in favour&quot; vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.106–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> His pact partner; he shields her by taking the &quot;for&quot; vote on Q1 – Q4 and quietly voting against on Q5; notes her calm leadership and that she won&#x27;t name the suspect.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The visible &quot;in favour&quot; voter; Ayanokōji knows he&#x27;s bluffing for attention but watches Horikita buy him off.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His cough prompts Kei to ask Horikita if she knows who&#x27;s voting in favour.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Suspects Kōenji and lashes out; Ayanokōji notes the danger of mob justification (rationalizing expelling whoever is &quot;holding back the class&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.109–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Makes the heartfelt appeal not to cut off classmates for points.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p104-1\">← Before: Question 4: written-exam rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p171-1\">→ After: The final battle: pushing the vote to unanimity &quot;for&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p171-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the final battle  pushing the vote to unanimity  for  as the ninth round ends with the single unseen  for  vote unchanged  horikita goes down the row asking each classmate to raise a hand if they voted  against    all but koenji do  she personally visits everyone  even ayanokoji  but nobody confesses   horikita  i voted in favour on the 14th round just now    ayanokoji  a deliberate lie  he d actually voted  for  on the 12th   if we can t make this unanimous  we won t move up to class a   be prepared  horikita  your opponent is trying to defeat you  realizes the unseen voter is prepared to run out the clock to force an expulsion  with under two hours left  he decides to abandon opposition and deliberately push the class toward unanimous  for    calculating that the class will then have to choose someone to expel  and he can direct that choice  persuades hirata  who agrees to vote  for  to expel the persistent voter  and secures horikita s reluctant approval  ruthless pragmatism   knowingly lies about when he switched his vote  tells horikita her  opponent is trying to defeat you  and engineers the shift to  for  to avoid losing 300 class points  accepts that someone must be cut  he pushes her toward the  for  vote she can t bring herself to make  she resists to the end  persuades him to vote  for   to expel the culprit  hirata agrees","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The final battle: pushing the vote to unanimity &quot;for&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.171–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As the ninth round ends with the single unseen &quot;for&quot; vote unchanged, Horikita goes down the row asking each classmate to raise a hand if they voted &quot;against&quot; — all but Kōenji do; she personally visits everyone, even Ayanokōji, but nobody confesses.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Horikita, I voted in favour on the 14th round just now.&quot; — Ayanokōji (a deliberate lie; he&#x27;d actually voted &quot;for&quot; on the 12th)<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If we can&#x27;t make this unanimous, we won&#x27;t move up to Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Be prepared, Horikita. Your opponent is trying to defeat you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes the unseen voter is prepared to run out the clock to force an expulsion; with under two hours left, he decides to abandon opposition and deliberately push the class toward unanimous &quot;for&quot; — calculating that the class will then have to choose someone to expel, and he can direct that choice; persuades Hirata (who agrees to vote &quot;for&quot; to expel the persistent voter) and secures Horikita&#x27;s reluctant approval.<span class=\"pg\">p.173–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ruthless pragmatism — knowingly lies about when he switched his vote, tells Horikita her &quot;opponent is trying to defeat you,&quot; and engineers the shift to &quot;for&quot; to avoid losing 300 class points; accepts that someone must be cut.<span class=\"pg\">p.171–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He pushes her toward the &quot;for&quot; vote she can&#x27;t bring herself to make; she resists to the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.171–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Persuades him to vote &quot;for&quot; (to expel the culprit); Hirata agrees.<span class=\"pg\">p.179–181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p106-1\">← Before: Question 5: expel a classmate for 100 class points; the deadlock<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p181-1\">→ After: Unanimous &quot;for&quot;; Hirata volunteers; Kushida named<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p181-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka unanimous  for  hirata volunteers  kushida named the sixteenth round is 39 in favour   0 against  hirata volunteers as the specific student to be expelled  6 for   32 against  then horikita offers herself  16   22  ayanokoji offers to take the blame if his accusation is wrong  the class waits for him to name the persistent  for  voter   kushida  it s you   it wasn t long after i started school that i had the accidental opportunity to see kushida s true nature   kushida thought i was on her side  you didn t think i would expose your whole school life like this  did you  names kushida   the unseen voter who wanted him and horikita expelled  because they knew her middle school secret  he d known since the first vote  prepared for her counterattack by publicly offering to take the blame if wrong  exposes her as the anonymous  for  voter and reveals her secret  she is ultimately expelled  he volunteers to be expelled to force a resolution  ayanokoji later uses his vote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p181-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Unanimous &quot;for&quot;; Hirata volunteers; Kushida named<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.181–191<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The sixteenth round is 39 in favour / 0 against; Hirata volunteers as the specific student to be expelled (6 for / 32 against), then Horikita offers herself (16 / 22). Ayanokōji offers to take the blame if his accusation is wrong; the class waits for him to name the persistent &quot;for&quot; voter.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kushida. It&#x27;s you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It wasn&#x27;t long after I started school that I had the accidental opportunity to see Kushida&#x27;s true nature.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kushida thought I was on her side. You didn&#x27;t think I would expose your whole school life like this, did you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Names Kushida — the unseen voter who wanted him and Horikita expelled (because they knew her middle-school secret); he&#x27;d known since the first vote; prepared for her counterattack by publicly offering to take the blame if wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Exposes her as the anonymous &quot;for&quot; voter and reveals her secret; she is ultimately expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He volunteers to be expelled to force a resolution; Ayanokōji later uses his vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p171-1\">← Before: The final battle: pushing the vote to unanimity &quot;for&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p192-1\">→ After: Exposing Kushida: the secret, the deal, the collapse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p192-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka exposing kushida  the secret  the deal  the collapse reveals kushida and horikita attended the same middle school and that kushida destroyed her class there when her  true nature   jealous  needing to be first  was exposed  recounts her deal   half his monthly private points in exchange for not expelling him   and bluffs that he recorded the conversation  he does not actually have the recording  he recites it from memory  knowing she made her own   kushida threatened to expel me from school  and i made a deal with her which involved me giving her half of my monthly private points in exchange for her not expelling me   you may have enough to spend as pocket money  but you can never have too much in the case of an emergency   why are you betraying me  you promised not to be hostile  remember  his bluff works   kushida admits the deal  her counterattack  claiming he touched her breasts  with a supposed uniform bearing fingerprints  is dismantled  her carefully built mask crumbles and she admits she wanted horikita and ayanokoji expelled  she begins venting every classmate s secrets to ensure her expulsion  cold  precise and ruthless   methodically breaks kushida s defenses with bluff and psychology  we need to make the best of it  calculating that her self destruction  revealing everyone s secrets  will eliminate the last resistance to her expulsion  kei furiously defends him against kushida s expulsion proposal  kushida later attacks him via kei s jealousy  claiming he once pursued her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Exposing Kushida: the secret, the deal, the collapse<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.192–205<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reveals Kushida and Horikita attended the same middle school and that Kushida destroyed her class there when her &quot;true nature&quot; (jealous, needing to be first) was exposed; recounts her deal — half his monthly private points in exchange for not expelling him — and bluffs that he recorded the conversation (he does not actually have the recording; he recites it from memory, knowing she made her own).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kushida threatened to expel me from school, and I made a deal with her which involved me giving her half of my monthly private points in exchange for her not expelling me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You may have enough to spend as pocket money, but you can never have too much in the case of an emergency.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why are you betraying me?! You promised not to be hostile, remember?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> His bluff works — Kushida admits the deal; her counterattack (claiming he touched her breasts, with a supposed uniform bearing fingerprints) is dismantled; her carefully built mask crumbles and she admits she wanted Horikita and Ayanokōji expelled; she begins venting every classmate&#x27;s secrets to ensure her expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.198–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold, precise and ruthless — methodically breaks Kushida&#x27;s defenses with bluff and psychology (we need to make the best of it), calculating that her self-destruction (revealing everyone&#x27;s secrets) will eliminate the last resistance to her expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.192–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Kei furiously defends him against Kushida&#x27;s expulsion proposal; Kushida later attacks him via Kei&#x27;s jealousy (claiming he once pursued her).<span class=\"pg\">p.186, 202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p181-1\">← Before: Unanimous &quot;for&quot;; Hirata volunteers; Kushida named<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p205-1\">→ After: Horikita saves Kushida; Airi&#x27;s voluntary expulsion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p205-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi hasebe-haruka horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka horikita saves kushida  airi s voluntary expulsion horikita unexpectedly defends kushida   argues everyone has two sides  praises kushida s talent for kindness  faking kindness   think how difficult it is to be kind  and refuses to let her be expelled  vowing to  make the most of her  kushida breaks down in tears   i think i want to keep kushida san in this class   it wasn t dumb  it wasn t funny  it was just plain ugly  i saw nothing but a mere foolish idiot    horikita to kushida realizes horikita s plan to save kushida could throw away 350 class points  steps in to take the  cruel role  of choosing the expendable student himself   argues the lowest oaa student should go  identifies airi  lowest at 36  lets haruka volunteer to be expelled in airi s place  then turns airi herself against haruka s sacrifice  airi voluntarily offers herself and is expelled 38 0  he engineers airi s expulsion  lowest oaa  fewest friends  self sacrificing nature  to secure 100 class points  she accepts and leaves with a big smile  having revealed her new look  no glasses  styled hair    a  brave  farewell  haruka fights desperately to be expelled instead of airi  ayanokoji breaks her resolve by arguing self sacrifice only enables future exploitation  she collapses  sobbing  horikita chose to protect kushida  he takes on the  evil  role of cutting airi so she needn t  afterward she apologizes and calls him out on acting unreasonably cruel","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Horikita saves Kushida; Airi&#x27;s voluntary expulsion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.205–226<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita unexpectedly defends Kushida — argues everyone has two sides, praises Kushida&#x27;s talent for kindness (faking kindness — think how difficult it is to be kind), and refuses to let her be expelled, vowing to &quot;make the most of her&quot;; Kushida breaks down in tears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I think I want to keep Kushida-san in this class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It wasn&#x27;t dumb, it wasn&#x27;t funny, it was just plain ugly. I saw nothing but a mere foolish idiot.&quot; — Horikita to Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Realizes Horikita&#x27;s plan to save Kushida could throw away 350 class points; steps in to take the &quot;cruel role&quot; of choosing the expendable student himself — argues the lowest OAA student should go, identifies Airi (lowest at 36), lets Haruka volunteer to be expelled in Airi&#x27;s place, then turns Airi herself against Haruka&#x27;s sacrifice; Airi voluntarily offers herself and is expelled 38–0.<span class=\"pg\">p.205–226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> He engineers Airi&#x27;s expulsion (lowest OAA, fewest friends, self-sacrificing nature) to secure 100 class points; she accepts and leaves with a big smile, having revealed her new look (no glasses, styled hair) — a &quot;brave&quot; farewell.<span class=\"pg\">p.219–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Haruka fights desperately to be expelled instead of Airi; Ayanokōji breaks her resolve by arguing self-sacrifice only enables future exploitation; she collapses, sobbing.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita chose to protect Kushida; he takes on the &quot;evil&quot; role of cutting Airi so she needn&#x27;t; afterward she apologizes and calls him out on acting unreasonably cruel.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p192-1\">← Before: Exposing Kushida: the secret, the deal, the collapse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p227-1\">→ After: Aftermath: Keisei&#x27;s anger; Horikita&#x27;s apology; Airi&#x27;s goodbye<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p227-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"ishigami-kyou nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka aftermath  keisei s anger  horikita s apology  airi s goodbye  you re something else  aren t you  i m not going to tell you that you did anything wrong  it s just that i m still not sure if i can say you did the right thing    keisei accepts keisei s unspoken condemnation and horikita s apology  plays along with horikita s accusation of unreasonable cruelty to hide his own pain  he was probably trying to suppress his painful feelings  watches airi leave without looking back   the losers always look back on their inability and regret it when it is far too late  a fact he knows from the white room and this school  keisei walks away  unable to say he did right or wrong  warns her not to get desperate after her true nature is exposed  no one speaks to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p227-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Aftermath: Keisei&#x27;s anger; Horikita&#x27;s apology; Airi&#x27;s goodbye<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.227–230<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;re something else, aren&#x27;t you? I&#x27;m not going to tell you that you did anything wrong. It&#x27;s just that I&#x27;m still not sure if I can say you did the right thing.&quot; — Keisei<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Accepts Keisei&#x27;s unspoken condemnation and Horikita&#x27;s apology; plays along with Horikita&#x27;s accusation of unreasonable cruelty to hide his own pain (he was probably trying to suppress his painful feelings); watches Airi leave without looking back — the losers always look back on their inability and regret it when it is far too late, a fact he knows from the White Room and this school.<span class=\"pg\">p.227–230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Keisei walks away, unable to say he did right or wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Warns her not to get desperate after her true nature is exposed (no one speaks to her).<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p205-1\">← Before: Horikita saves Kushida; Airi&#x27;s voluntary expulsion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p232-1\">→ After: Rooftop with Chabashira: her confession, his cold logic<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p232-1","v":"y2v5","y":2,"o":21,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae sakura-airi horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka rooftop with chabashira  her confession  his cold logic meets chabashira on the rooftop stairs as promised  she leads the way to the roof  where she leans on the railing against the sunset and confesses the story of her own third year special exam  a confession   by the way  did it end the way you wanted it to  or was it the other way around   there is no real right answer in that test  i believe that   i mean  you can t choose to be leaderless   there is no need for persuasion   wasn t there a way to save sakura and blame the sacrifice on others   didn t it hurt your  heart   people may call me a monster  no one wants to be the one who made the  evil  choice  in the end  someone needs to make these decisions  it s the only way to succeed in this world  listens to her 11 year old trauma  she refused to let the leader  friend  and lover she once had be expelled  costing the class 300 points and their dream of class a  then analyzes her mistake with cold precision   her class could have cleared for 50 points rather than chase 100  but her lover s strategy was flawed  reveals he deliberately chose airi  lowest oaa  few friends  self sacrificing personality  and manipulated haruka and airi into accepting  admits he d act the same again  monster  but chabashira concludes she could never make such a decision  without hesitation  confides in him  they  make a deal with the past    she resolves to graduate her class from class a   unlike before  having grown through the exam  he notes her mind has finally caught up to her current age  discusses his choice of her for expulsion with chabashira   he knew she had  special feelings  for him and used her personality  says horikita  had the power to make change  but not enough time   she s the one who nearly saved kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p232-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Rooftop with Chabashira: her confession, his cold logic<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V5 · p.232–239<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Chabashira on the rooftop stairs as promised; she leads the way to the roof, where she leans on the railing against the sunset and confesses the story of her own third-year special exam (a confession).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;By the way, did it end the way you wanted it to? Or was it the other way around?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;there is no real right answer in that test. I believe that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I mean, you can&#x27;t choose to be leaderless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There is no need for persuasion.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wasn&#x27;t there a way to save Sakura and blame the sacrifice on others?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Didn&#x27;t it hurt your... heart?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;People may call me a monster. No one wants to be the one who made the &#x27;evil&#x27; choice. In the end, someone needs to make these decisions. It&#x27;s the only way to succeed in this world.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Listens to her 11-year-old trauma (she refused to let the leader, friend, and lover she once had be expelled, costing the class 300 points and their dream of Class A), then analyzes her mistake with cold precision — her class could have cleared for 50 points rather than chase 100, but her lover&#x27;s strategy was flawed; reveals he deliberately chose Airi (lowest OAA, few friends, self-sacrificing personality) and manipulated Haruka and Airi into accepting; admits he&#x27;d act the same again (&quot;monster&quot;), but Chabashira concludes she could never make such a decision &quot;without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232–239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Confides in him; they &quot;make a deal with the past&quot; — she resolves to graduate her class from Class A, &quot;unlike before,&quot; having grown through the exam; he notes her mind has finally caught up to her current age.<span class=\"pg\">p.232–239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Discusses his choice of her for expulsion with Chabashira — he knew she had &quot;special feelings&quot; for him and used her personality.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Says Horikita &quot;had the power to make change&quot; but not enough time — she&#x27;s the one who nearly saved Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v5-p227-1\">← Before: Aftermath: Keisei&#x27;s anger; Horikita&#x27;s apology; Airi&#x27;s goodbye<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p11-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.11-346<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p15-1\">→ After: Aftermath analysis: why he supported Horikita&#x27;s &quot;wrong&quot; choice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p15-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka aftermath analysis  why he supported horikita s  wrong  choice monday  september 20   reflects on the two causes of the class s fracture  kushida s explosive revelations and the broken promise to expel only the  traitor  logically  expelling kushida was the only correct choice  horikita s decision to keep her was  impossible  irrational and wrong  and he d never have made it before this school   yet he supported it because he wants to  watch  horikita s  growth  see  the chemical reaction  of leaving kushida in the class  and find out if it leads to class a  destruction  or something unexpected  regards the resulting pain as a  necessary and unavoidable cost  and chance to grow  he backed her  illogical mistake  to observe where it leads   a new kind of investment in her  the  ball of trust  he broke  her mask collapsed  making her a cracked but still potentially useful resource","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Aftermath analysis: why he supported Horikita&#x27;s &quot;wrong&quot; choice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.15–19<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Monday, September 20 — reflects on the two causes of the class&#x27;s fracture: Kushida&#x27;s explosive revelations and the broken promise to expel only the &quot;traitor.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Logically, expelling Kushida was the only correct choice; Horikita&#x27;s decision to keep her was &quot;impossible, irrational and wrong,&quot; and he&#x27;d never have made it before this school — yet he supported it because he wants to &quot;watch [Horikita&#x27;s] growth,&quot; see &quot;the chemical reaction&quot; of leaving Kushida in the class, and find out if it leads to Class A, destruction, or something unexpected; regards the resulting pain as a &quot;necessary and unavoidable cost&quot; and chance to grow.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He backed her &quot;illogical mistake&quot; to observe where it leads — a new kind of investment in her.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The &quot;ball of trust&quot; he broke; her mask collapsed, making her a cracked but still potentially useful resource.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p11-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p20-1\">→ After: Morning: Horikita waiting for Kushida; checking on the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p20-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou hasebe-haruka sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka morning  horikita waiting for kushida  checking on the group leaves his room  sees horikita waiting in the lobby   she s been waiting by kushida s door since dawn  dark circles under her eyes  but kushida won t leave her room   are you waiting for kushida   looks like you saw through me  yes  over the weekend  i went to her room many times  but   i had some contact with keisei and akito  but that s about it   you don t need to apologize again for the same thing  if you thought that was the right thing to do  i m fine with that  notes the group is fractured   haruka has blocked ignored his messages  keisei and akito talk but avoid the topic of airi  decides to watch from a distance rather than force contact  pities horikita s sleepless vigil but understands she must  follow up  on her choice  notes her lingering  what if   wishing the clock had run out rather than expel anyone    thoughts she suppresses as  cowardly  both apologizing and checking in  she regrets forcing him to take the blame for airi s expulsion  holed up in her room out of humiliation  refusing to see horikita  hasn t replied to any messages   he hasn t had the  courage  to contact her  her name is already gone from the oaa    as if such a student had never existed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Morning: Horikita waiting for Kushida; checking on the group<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.20–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves his room, sees Horikita waiting in the lobby — she&#x27;s been waiting by Kushida&#x27;s door since dawn (dark circles under her eyes) but Kushida won&#x27;t leave her room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Are you waiting for Kushida?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Looks like you saw through me. Yes. Over the weekend, I went to her room many times, but…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I had some contact with Keisei and Akito, but that&#x27;s about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You don&#x27;t need to apologize again for the same thing. If you thought that was the right thing to do, I&#x27;m fine with that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the group is fractured — Haruka has blocked/ignored his messages, Keisei and Akito talk but avoid the topic of Airi; decides to watch from a distance rather than force contact; pities Horikita&#x27;s sleepless vigil but understands she must &quot;follow up&quot; on her choice; notes her lingering &quot;what if&quot; (wishing the clock had run out rather than expel anyone) — thoughts she suppresses as &quot;cowardly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Both apologizing and checking in; she regrets forcing him to take the blame for Airi&#x27;s expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Holed up in her room out of humiliation, refusing to see Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.20–21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Hasn&#x27;t replied to any messages — he hasn&#x27;t had the &quot;courage&quot; to contact her.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her name is already gone from the OAA — &quot;as if such a student had never existed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p15-1\">← Before: Aftermath analysis: why he supported Horikita&#x27;s &quot;wrong&quot; choice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p35-1\">→ After: Sports festival rules; Horikita&#x27;s apology; Kōenji&#x27;s deal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p35-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune shinohara hirata-yousuke matsushita-chiaki kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sports festival rules  horikita s apology  koenji s deal chabashira explains the sports festival rules  ability  based  with class change tickets and 2 million points for first place  sudo and ike are excited  but part of the class is cold toward horikita s leadership  watches as horikita publicly apologizes for breaking her promise  keeping kushida  and as shinohara challenges her   horikita holds firm  arguing past contributions can t be erased and offering to  take responsibility  if kushida can t be brought back  sees koenji agree to compete  for the cash prizes  and confirm he won t change classes yet   but learns he never fully trusted horikita  i would never trust someone else with my life  neither would you  her public apology and iron will  koenji s deal with her  challenges horikita over keeping kushida   one of the people hurt by her revelations  requests the class keep kushida s secret internal  points out leaking the secret would only give a  temporary sense of victory  agrees to compete for money  calmly reveals he d have voted against his own expulsion   his  trust  in horikita was conditional  ayanokoji admits he can never fully analyze him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p35-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sports festival rules; Horikita&#x27;s apology; Kōenji&#x27;s deal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.35–47<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira explains the sports festival rules (&quot;Ability&quot; based, with Class Change Tickets and 2 million points for first place); Sudō and Ike are excited, but part of the class is cold toward Horikita&#x27;s leadership.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara.html\">Shinohara<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches as Horikita publicly apologizes for breaking her promise (keeping Kushida), and as Shinohara challenges her — Horikita holds firm, arguing past contributions can&#x27;t be erased and offering to &quot;take responsibility&quot; if Kushida can&#x27;t be brought back; sees Kōenji agree to compete (for the cash prizes) and confirm he won&#x27;t change classes yet — but learns he never fully trusted Horikita (&quot;I would never trust someone else with my life. Neither would you&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.35–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her public apology and iron will; Kōenji&#x27;s deal with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> Challenges Horikita over keeping Kushida — one of the people hurt by her revelations.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Requests the class keep Kushida&#x27;s secret internal.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Points out leaking the secret would only give a &quot;temporary sense of victory.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Agrees to compete for money; calmly reveals he&#x27;d have voted against his own expulsion — his &quot;trust&quot; in Horikita was conditional; Ayanokōji admits he can never fully analyze him.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p20-1\">← Before: Morning: Horikita waiting for Kushida; checking on the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p48-1\">→ After: Nagumo summons him; the lunch with Ichinose<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p48-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nagumo summons him  the lunch with ichinose horikita relays a student council summons from yagami  on nagumo s behalf  kei tries to intercept but relents  if it s the student council president   not much has changed  or so i would like to say  but well  i do have a few worries   if you beat me in even one head to head match during this sports festival  everything that s happened between us will be water under the bridge   you ll participate in all five competitions i specify   i also have to consider my class s plan  could you give me some time  plays humble with nagumo  knowing it won t satisfy him  accepts the challenge framework   one win in five specified events to end the harassment  with one week to decide  then endures a three way lunch with nagumo and ichinose  nagumo eating with her daily  silently eating as they talk  and reads nagumo s strategy  he wants a direct defeat and is using ichinose to humiliate him  speculates nagumo may cut ichinose off if she fails to become president  challenges him to five head to head events  one win   truce  he sees through ayanokoji s feigned distress  now has lunch with nagumo daily  downcast and avoiding his eyes  he wonders if her attachment to nagumo is real or a strategy  kei possessively blocks horikita s invitation  then quickly switches to satou when she hears it s the student council president  the messenger   ayanokoji notes she only has yagami s contact info  not nagumo s","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo summons him; the lunch with Ichinose<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.48–58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita relays a student-council summons from Yagami (on Nagumo&#x27;s behalf); Kei tries to intercept but relents (&quot;if it&#x27;s the student council president&quot;).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Not much has changed. Or so I would like to say, but well, I do have a few worries.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you beat me in even one head-to-head match during this sports festival, everything that&#x27;s happened between us will be water under the bridge.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;ll participate in all five competitions I specify.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I also have to consider my class&#x27;s plan. Could you give me some time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Plays humble with Nagumo (knowing it won&#x27;t satisfy him); accepts the challenge framework — one win in five specified events to end the harassment, with one week to decide; then endures a three-way lunch with Nagumo and Ichinose (Nagumo eating with her daily), silently eating as they talk, and reads Nagumo&#x27;s strategy: he wants a direct defeat and is using Ichinose to humiliate him; speculates Nagumo may cut Ichinose off if she fails to become president.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> Challenges him to five head-to-head events (one win = truce); he sees through Ayanokōji&#x27;s feigned distress.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Now has lunch with Nagumo daily; downcast and avoiding his eyes; he wonders if her attachment to Nagumo is real or a strategy.<span class=\"pg\">p.53–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Kei possessively blocks Horikita&#x27;s invitation, then quickly switches to Satou when she hears it&#x27;s the student council president.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The messenger — Ayanokōji notes she only has Yagami&#x27;s contact info, not Nagumo&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p35-1\">← Before: Sports festival rules; Horikita&#x27;s apology; Kōenji&#x27;s deal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p65-1\">→ After: Cooking for Kei; a quiet evening together<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p65-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei shinohara kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka cooking for kei  a quiet evening together invites kei to his room at 7 30 p m  she arrives grinning  and he cooks omurice  a dish she likes  while she clings to his back   oh  by the waaay  it s about shinohara san  but   do you know what kushida has that airi doesn t   a perspective that only kushida has  thoughts that only kushida has  statements that only kushida can make  tender and attentive   cooks for kei  something she s never done herself  endures her playful clinging  and kisses her repeatedly after the meal  explains to kei why keeping kushida  not airi  made sense  kushida offers a unique perspective  thoughts and statements that only kushida has that can support horikita in a way airi couldn t  kei remains unconvinced but accepts it  his girlfriend   they share an intimate evening  she calls him out on his  perfect answer  habit  kei is trying to repair her friendship with shinohara  hurt by kushida s leaked remarks  he argues her unique perspective justifies keeping her  kei feels she should have been expelled","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Cooking for Kei; a quiet evening together<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.65–80<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Invites Kei to his room at 7:30 p.m.; she arrives grinning, and he cooks omurice (a dish she likes) while she clings to his back.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"shinohara.html\">Shinohara<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Oh, by the waaay, it&#x27;s about Shinohara-san, but…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you know what Kushida has that Airi doesn&#x27;t?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;A perspective that only Kushida has. Thoughts that only Kushida has. Statements that only Kushida can make.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Tender and attentive — cooks for Kei (something she&#x27;s never done herself), endures her playful clinging, and kisses her repeatedly after the meal; explains to Kei why keeping Kushida (not Airi) made sense: Kushida offers a unique perspective, thoughts and statements that only Kushida has that can support Horikita in a way Airi couldn&#x27;t; Kei remains unconvinced but accepts it.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend — they share an intimate evening; she calls him out on his &quot;perfect answer&quot; habit.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara<\/b> Kei is trying to repair her friendship with Shinohara (hurt by Kushida&#x27;s leaked remarks).<span class=\"pg\">p.72–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> He argues her unique perspective justifies keeping her; Kei feels she should have been expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p48-1\">← Before: Nagumo summons him; the lunch with Ichinose<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p80-1\">→ After: Hirata&#x27;s visit: leader development; Mii-chan; his guilt<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p80-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune asahina-nazuna ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hirata s visit  leader development  mii chan  his guilt hirata arrives at the room  still in uniform from club activities  kei treats the place as her own  making hirata smile   then  moving forward i want you to take these conversations not to me  but to horikita  the leader of the class   it will be a burden on her  i m not sure if she ll come up with a solution  so i can t rely on her  won t rely on her  if you do that  do you think horikita will ever become a true leader   you should meet mii chan and accept her feelings  yousuke   i wonder  would it have been better to choose to let the time run out    hirata deliberately pushes hirata and kei to take their problems to horikita first  so she gains experience as a leader  promising to back them up on anything she can t fix  suggests the  crude  solution for mii chan  hirata accepting her feelings  as he did with kei s fake relationship  realizes hirata is suffering just as much from airi s expulsion  and reassures him  comes for advice  he pushes him toward horikita and helps him work through his guilt   hirata says he wants to believe in ayanokoji  not just does  she also relies on ayanokoji  he redirects her to horikita  he wants her to be relied on so she can grow into a true leader  mii chan is absent from school after confessing to hirata  he proposes hirata accept her  crude but effective","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p80-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hirata&#x27;s visit: leader development; Mii-chan; his guilt<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.80–89<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hirata arrives at the room (still in uniform from club activities); Kei treats the place as her own, making Hirata smile.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then, moving forward I want you to take these conversations not to me, but to Horikita, the leader of the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It will be a burden on her. I&#x27;m not sure if she&#x27;ll come up with a solution. So I can&#x27;t rely on her, won&#x27;t rely on her. If you do that, do you think Horikita will ever become a true leader?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;you should meet Mii-chan and accept her feelings, Yousuke.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.85<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wonder… would it have been better to choose to let the time run out…&quot; — Hirata<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately pushes Hirata and Kei to take their problems to Horikita first (so she gains experience as a leader), promising to back them up on anything she can&#x27;t fix; suggests the &quot;crude&quot; solution for Mii-chan (Hirata accepting her feelings, as he did with Kei&#x27;s fake relationship); realizes Hirata is suffering just as much from Airi&#x27;s expulsion, and reassures him.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Comes for advice; he pushes him toward Horikita and helps him work through his guilt — Hirata says he wants to believe in Ayanokōji, not just does.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She also relies on Ayanokōji; he redirects her to Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He wants her to be relied on so she can grow into a true leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Mii-chan is absent from school after confessing to Hirata; he proposes Hirata accept her (crude but effective).<span class=\"pg\">p.85–86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p65-1\">← Before: Cooking for Kei; a quiet evening together<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p90-1\">→ After: Sudō&#x27;s toilet talk; Onodera&#x27;s doubles proposal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p90-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken onodera-kayano ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudo s toilet talk  onodera s doubles proposal sudo invites him to the toilet as an excuse to talk  onodera intercepts  wanting to speak to sudo about the sports festival   the individual rewards for this year s sports festival are separated by gender  right   if you and i worked together  sudou kun  there d be nothing to be worried about   it ain t that  as if i could complain about your abilities  onodera    sudo facilitates without giving direct answers   lets onodera propose pairing with sudo for doubles events  both aiming for first in their gender  observes sudo s reluctance  wanting to pair with horikita  and notes pairing with onodera is better  no distracting feelings  advises sudo on the shinohara ike issue  they need to  lay their feelings bare  with a mediator present  leading him to realize hirata is the right person  confides in him about shinohara ike and accepts his advice to ask hirata to mediate  proposes a doubles pairing with sudo   she distrusts ayanokoji  from the expulsion  but trusts sudo s ability  his relationship with shinohara is awkward after kushida s leaks","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p90-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sudō&#x27;s toilet talk; Onodera&#x27;s doubles proposal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.90–97<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sudō invites him to the toilet as an excuse to talk; Onodera intercepts, wanting to speak to Sudō about the sports festival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"onodera-kayano.html\">Onodera Kayano<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The individual rewards for this year&#x27;s sports festival are separated by gender, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you and I worked together, Sudou-kun, there&#x27;d be nothing to be worried about.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It ain&#x27;t that. As if I could complain about your abilities, Onodera.&quot; — Sudō<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Facilitates without giving direct answers — lets Onodera propose pairing with Sudō for doubles events (both aiming for first in their gender); observes Sudō&#x27;s reluctance (wanting to pair with Horikita) and notes pairing with Onodera is better (no distracting feelings); advises Sudō on the Shinohara/Ike issue (they need to &quot;lay their feelings bare&quot; with a mediator present), leading him to realize Hirata is the right person.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Confides in him about Shinohara/Ike and accepts his advice to ask Hirata to mediate.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Onodera Kayano<\/b> Proposes a doubles pairing with Sudō — she distrusts Ayanokōji (from the expulsion) but trusts Sudō&#x27;s ability.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> His relationship with Shinohara is awkward after Kushida&#x27;s leaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p80-1\">← Before: Hirata&#x27;s visit: leader development; Mii-chan; his guilt<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p98-1\">→ After: Gym scouting: Class A&#x27;s serious practice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p98-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka gym scouting  class a s serious practice scouts the gym with hirata  class a is practicing intensely  volleyball table tennis  aware they re at a disadvantage in a pure sports contest and following sakayanagi s instructions to raise their baseline  notes his own class hasn t shown up at all  still reeling from the exam  and that class a is  serious  because a sports based contest isn t their forte  observes sakayanagi s strategy forming  class a s practice is almost certainly following her instructions  her class and ryuen s are still  fumbling about  in comparison  scouts the competition with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Gym scouting: Class A&#x27;s serious practice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.98–100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Scouts the gym with Hirata; Class A is practicing intensely (volleyball/table tennis), aware they&#x27;re at a disadvantage in a pure sports contest and following Sakayanagi&#x27;s instructions to raise their baseline.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes his own class hasn&#x27;t shown up at all (still reeling from the exam), and that Class A is &quot;serious&quot; because a sports-based contest isn&#x27;t their forte; observes Sakayanagi&#x27;s strategy forming.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Class A&#x27;s practice is almost certainly following her instructions.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Her class and Ryūen&#x27;s are still &quot;fumbling about&quot; in comparison.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Scouts the competition with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p90-1\">← Before: Sudō&#x27;s toilet talk; Onodera&#x27;s doubles proposal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p101-1\">→ After: Horikita&#x27;s resolve; Chabashira&#x27;s counsel (from Horikita&#x27;s POV)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p101-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka horikita s resolve  chabashira s counsel  from horikita s pov  this opening section is horikita s pov   recorded on her own page  on friday  five days of absences  she asks chabashira about the three missing students  learns their good records earn them a reprieve  but if they remain absent next week the 100 class points will vanish  confides her doubt about whether expelling airi was right  chabashira  changed since the exam  gently advises her  she did well to reach an answer at all  breaking a promise is sometimes necessary for adults  and she must  protect that choice you made  notes ayanokoji is likely observing to see how she handles it and considers him  more outstanding than the oaa can evaluate   still calling him  defective","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Horikita&#x27;s resolve; Chabashira&#x27;s counsel (from Horikita&#x27;s POV)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.101–111<\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> This opening section is Horikita&#x27;s POV — recorded on her own page. On Friday (five days of absences), she asks Chabashira about the three missing students; learns their good records earn them a reprieve, but if they remain absent next week the 100 class points will vanish; confides her doubt about whether expelling Airi was right.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Chabashira (changed since the exam) gently advises her: she did well to reach an answer at all, breaking a promise is sometimes necessary for adults, and she must &quot;protect that choice you made&quot;; notes Ayanokōji is likely observing to see how she handles it and considers him &quot;more outstanding than the OAA can evaluate&quot; (still calling him &quot;defective&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.101–111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p98-1\">← Before: Gym scouting: Class A&#x27;s serious practice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p112-1\">→ After: Ibuki confronts Ayanokōji; the plan to get Kushida out<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p112-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ibuki confronts ayanokoji  the plan to get kushida out ibuki corner him at the dorm elevator  shoving her phone in his face   a message he sent her  if you get expelled because of something that has nothing to do with me  naturally  it will count as a loss against me  you wouldn t be such an idiot  right  which she spent a week trying to understand   if you get expelled because of something that has nothing to do with me  naturally  it will count as a loss against me  you wouldn t be such an idiot  right    ibuki reading  i m about to go meet kushida san    horikita  arriving amused by ibuki s slowness  her message was straightforward advice not to be manipulated into expulsion  when horikita arrives  realizes she s chosen ibuki to help force kushida out   someone outside the group who knows her secret and has no qualms  he sent her a message warning her not to let herself be used expelled  she couldn t parse it  she s about to meet kushida   he suspects why she brought ibuki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ibuki confronts Ayanokōji; the plan to get Kushida out<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.112–117<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ibuki corner him at the dorm elevator, shoving her phone in his face — a message he sent her (&quot;If you get expelled because of something that has nothing to do with me, naturally, it will count as a loss against me. You wouldn&#x27;t be such an idiot, right?&quot;) which she spent a week trying to understand.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;&#x27;If you get expelled because of something that has nothing to do with me, naturally, it will count as a loss against me. You wouldn&#x27;t be such an idiot, right?&#x27;&quot; — Ibuki reading<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m about to go meet Kushida-san.&quot; — Horikita, arriving<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Amused by Ibuki&#x27;s slowness (her message was straightforward advice not to be manipulated into expulsion); when Horikita arrives, realizes she&#x27;s chosen Ibuki to help force Kushida out — someone outside the group who knows her secret and has no qualms.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> He sent her a message warning her not to let herself be used/expelled; she couldn&#x27;t parse it.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She&#x27;s about to meet Kushida — he suspects why she brought Ibuki.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p101-1\">← Before: Horikita&#x27;s resolve; Chabashira&#x27;s counsel (from Horikita&#x27;s POV)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p118-1\">→ After: The Kushida intervention: Ibuki breaks the door; the left-handed &quot;alliance&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p118-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the kushida intervention  ibuki breaks the door  the left handed  alliance  at kushida s room  ibuki mashes the doorbell for ten seconds  then forces the door open  slipping her foot in  and berates kushida   venting her own pent up stress at horikita  not actually trying to save her  kushida emerges in casual clothes   i m gonna force kushida out of her room  this will be all or nothing    ibuki  i ve never thought positively of you even once    ibuki to kushida watches horikita negotiate   she argues kushida s continued absence only hurts herself  her  revenge  would fail if she s the one expelled  explains her plan to use kushida as a  weapon   capable in academics sports  gather intel from other classes while keeping up her facade  and promises to commit to her until graduation  kushida finally agrees to fight for the class and contribute to it for the next year and a half   solely for her own sake  deliberately stays in the background  letting horikita handle it  and notes the  left handed handshake signifies animosity   they both remember their previous handshake  watches the two women get into a ridiculous cheek pinching contest until ibuki leaves in disgust    she sure has the talent to annoy people  but he admits ibuki made the meeting possible  forcefully opens kushida s door  curses her out  her  talent to annoy  breaks the stalemate  she negotiates kushida s return alone  growing into her role  agrees to return for her own sake  not the class  seals an  animosity  alliance with a left handed handshake","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p118-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Kushida intervention: Ibuki breaks the door; the left-handed &quot;alliance&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.118–145<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Kushida&#x27;s room, Ibuki mashes the doorbell for ten seconds, then forces the door open (slipping her foot in) and berates Kushida — venting her own pent-up stress at Horikita, not actually trying to save her; Kushida emerges in casual clothes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m gonna force Kushida out of her room. This will be all or nothing.&quot; — Ibuki<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve never thought positively of you even once.&quot; — Ibuki to Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Watches Horikita negotiate — she argues Kushida&#x27;s continued absence only hurts herself (her &quot;revenge&quot; would fail if she&#x27;s the one expelled), explains her plan to use Kushida as a &quot;weapon&quot; (capable in academics/sports, gather intel from other classes while keeping up her facade), and promises to commit to her until graduation; Kushida finally agrees to fight for the class and contribute to it for the next year and a half — solely for her own sake.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately stays in the background, letting Horikita handle it, and notes the &quot;left-handed handshake signifies animosity&quot; (they both remember their previous handshake); watches the two women get into a ridiculous cheek-pinching contest until Ibuki leaves in disgust — &quot;She sure has the talent to annoy people,&quot; but he admits Ibuki made the meeting possible.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Forcefully opens Kushida&#x27;s door, curses her out; her &quot;talent to annoy&quot; breaks the stalemate.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She negotiates Kushida&#x27;s return alone, growing into her role.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Agrees to return for her own sake (not the class); seals an &quot;animosity&quot; alliance with a left-handed handshake.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p112-1\">← Before: Ibuki confronts Ayanokōji; the plan to get Kushida out<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p155-1\">→ After: Visiting Mii-chan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p155-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"asahina-nazuna ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka visiting mii chan visits mii chan  wang san  who s been absent   a genuinely hardworking girl trying to get back on her feet  unlike kushida haruka  someone s been delivering food to her  hirata   not skipping is because i feel like it would be uncool to do so   you can just come to school  a nonchalant look on your face   i i will definitely go to school properly on monday  gently reasons with mii chan   she can t hide forever  especially with kushida and haruka also absent  if she returns and they don t  she ll actually be fine  cites ike s worry  mii chan resolves to return monday  he persuades her to return to school  she s been secretly supported by hirata","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p155-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Visiting Mii-chan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.155–161<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Visits Mii-chan (Wang-san), who&#x27;s been absent — a genuinely hardworking girl trying to get back on her feet, unlike Kushida/Haruka; someone&#x27;s been delivering food to her (Hirata).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;not skipping is because I feel like it would be uncool to do so.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You can just come to school, a nonchalant look on your face.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I—I will definitely go to school properly on Monday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Gently reasons with Mii-chan — she can&#x27;t hide forever, especially with Kushida and Haruka also absent; if she returns and they don&#x27;t, she&#x27;ll actually be fine; cites Ike&#x27;s worry. Mii-chan resolves to return Monday.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–161<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> He persuades her to return to school; she&#x27;s been secretly supported by Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p118-1\">← Before: The Kushida intervention: Ibuki breaks the door; the left-handed &quot;alliance&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p162-1\">→ After: Haruka&#x27;s return; the group permanently fractures<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p162-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka miyake-akito ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka haruka s return  the group permanently fractures notes increased security at school  phones collected  receives word via akito that haruka will return monday    a temporary return  since she still won t talk to ayanokoji   haruka will be coming to school from monday next week    akito s message  could you quietly watch over haruka for a while    akito agrees to  quietly watch over  haruka from a distance rather than force contact  receives messages indirectly  from mii chan  from haruka via akito    the group hasn t met once since the exam  will return but refuses to speak to him  he watches over her from afar  relays haruka s messages and asks him to watch over her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p162-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Haruka&#x27;s return; the group permanently fractures<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.162–170<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Notes increased security at school (phones collected); receives word via Akito that Haruka will return Monday — &quot;a temporary return,&quot; since she still won&#x27;t talk to Ayanokōji.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Haruka will be coming to school from Monday next week.&quot; — Akito&#x27;s message<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Could you quietly watch over Haruka for a while?&quot; — Akito<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Agrees to &quot;quietly watch over&quot; Haruka from a distance rather than force contact; receives messages indirectly (from Mii-chan, from Haruka via Akito) — the group hasn&#x27;t met once since the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.162–170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Will return but refuses to speak to him; he watches over her from afar.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Relays Haruka&#x27;s messages and asks him to watch over her.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p155-1\">← Before: Visiting Mii-chan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p171-1\">→ After: The three return; Kushida&#x27;s new aggressive facade<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p171-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou chabashira-sae horikita-suzune hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the three return  kushida s new aggressive facade monday  mii chan and haruka return first  with friends supporting them  haruka glances at ayanokoji then turns away  horikita enters alone  stiff    her attempt to bring kushida failed   but kushida arrives just before the bell   i heard from horikita san that you ve been absent because of me    kushida to mii chan  i don t intend to get along with you    kushida  who knows  at the very least  this is who i really am    kushida  if anybody comes at me with hostility  i won t show any mercy     i m not doing it for the class  i m doing it for myself  watches kushida drop the  kushida the angel  facade   she bluntly tells mii chan she doesn t intend to get along  apologizes to shinohara matsushita  mostly out of obligation  and openly threatens the class with her arsenal of secrets if crossed  while promising to contribute for her own sake  to graduate class a  the class regards her  as if she was a tumor  chabashira covers for them  i m keeping watch  returns changed   the mask gone  openly aggressive and self serving  no longer  kushida the angel  messages him  i m keeping watch    quietly protecting the class s internal affairs  enters alone stiff   her attempt to bring kushida failed  kushida beat her to it  returns but still won t speak to him  the group hasn t met at all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p171-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The three return; Kushida&#x27;s new aggressive facade<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.171–176<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Monday: Mii-chan and Haruka return first (with friends supporting them); Haruka glances at Ayanokōji then turns away. Horikita enters alone (stiff) — her attempt to bring Kushida failed — but Kushida arrives just before the bell.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I heard from Horikita-san that you&#x27;ve been absent because of me.&quot; — Kushida to Mii-chan<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t intend to get along with you.&quot; — Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Who knows? At the very least, this is who I really am.&quot; — Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;if anybody comes at me with hostility, I won&#x27;t show any mercy&quot; / &quot;I&#x27;m not doing it for the class, I&#x27;m doing it for myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches Kushida drop the &quot;Kushida the Angel&quot; facade — she bluntly tells Mii-chan she doesn&#x27;t intend to get along, apologizes to Shinohara/Matsushita (mostly out of obligation), and openly threatens the class with her arsenal of secrets if crossed, while promising to contribute for her own sake (to graduate Class A); the class regards her &quot;as if she was a tumor&quot;; Chabashira covers for them (&quot;I&#x27;m keeping watch&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.171–176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Returns changed — the mask gone, openly aggressive and self-serving; no longer &quot;Kushida the Angel.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173–175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Messages him &quot;I&#x27;m keeping watch&quot; — quietly protecting the class&#x27;s internal affairs.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Enters alone/stiff — her attempt to bring Kushida failed; Kushida beat her to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Returns but still won&#x27;t speak to him; the group hasn&#x27;t met at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.171, 176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p162-1\">← Before: Haruka&#x27;s return; the group permanently fractures<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p194-1\">→ After: The karaoke negotiation: Horikita–Ryūen alliance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p194-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the karaoke negotiation  horikita ryuen alliance waits with horikita in a karaoke parlor  their  weird back and forth  of studying while waiting  ryuen and katsuragi arrive 25 minutes late  deliberately stays in the background  leave it to horikita to drive it through the end  watches her negotiate with ryuen and katsuragi   she proposes a cooperative alliance to take down sakayanagi s class a  refuses concessions  calls ryuen the most untrustworthy person yet chooses his class by  process of elimination  and bluffs  sees she s grown  finding out about him even as she uses him  she insisted he just  be present  he witnesses her growth into a shrewd negotiator  tests him by seemingly throwing orange juice at him  he dodges  ryuen   ayanokouji is suzune s lethal weapon  ryuen demands he leave  horikita refuses","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The karaoke negotiation: Horikita–Ryūen alliance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.194–212<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits with Horikita in a karaoke parlor (their &quot;weird back and forth&quot; of studying while waiting); Ryūen and Katsuragi arrive 25 minutes late.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately stays in the background (&quot;leave it to Horikita to drive it through the end&quot;); watches her negotiate with Ryūen and Katsuragi — she proposes a cooperative alliance to take down Sakayanagi&#x27;s Class A, refuses concessions, calls Ryūen the most untrustworthy person yet chooses his class by &quot;process of elimination,&quot; and bluffs; sees she&#x27;s grown (finding out about him even as she uses him).<span class=\"pg\">p.194–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She insisted he just &quot;be present&quot;; he witnesses her growth into a shrewd negotiator.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Tests him by seemingly throwing orange juice at him; he dodges (Ryūen: &quot;Ayanokouji is Suzune&#x27;s Lethal Weapon&quot;); Ryūen demands he leave, Horikita refuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.206–211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p171-1\">← Before: The three return; Kushida&#x27;s new aggressive facade<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p215-1\">→ After: His offer: neutralize Sakayanagi; a &quot;siege on Class A&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p215-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka his offer  neutralize sakayanagi  a  siege on class a   if whether or not sakayanagi participates is threatening our cooperation  then i may be able to be of help   if you leave everything to me  i ll make sure sakayanagi doesn t participate   in exchange for making sakayanagi not participate  i don t want you to expect even a single point from me at the sports festival   after i crush sakayanagi  you re next    ryuen offers to keep sakayanagi out of the festival in exchange for scoring no points himself   a strategy only he can execute  also proposes a  different matter   a siege on class a with ryuen s class members  which ryuen initially rejects out of personal spite but katsuragi and horikita accept  he has a strategy to seal her non participation that none of the others can execute  he accepts his siege proposal after katsuragi s urging    after i crush sakayanagi  you re next","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p215-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">His offer: neutralize Sakayanagi; a &quot;siege on Class A&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.215–218<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If whether or not Sakayanagi participates is threatening our cooperation, then I may be able to be of help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you leave everything to me, I&#x27;ll make sure Sakayanagi doesn&#x27;t participate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;in exchange for making Sakayanagi not participate, I don&#x27;t want you to expect even a single point from me at the Sports Festival.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;After I crush Sakayanagi, you&#x27;re next.&quot; — Ryūen<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Offers to keep Sakayanagi out of the festival in exchange for scoring no points himself — a strategy only he can execute; also proposes a &quot;different matter&quot; (a siege on Class A with Ryūen&#x27;s class members), which Ryūen initially rejects out of personal spite but Katsuragi and Horikita accept.<span class=\"pg\">p.215–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> He has a strategy to seal her non-participation that none of the others can execute.<span class=\"pg\">p.215–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He accepts his siege proposal after Katsuragi&#x27;s urging — &quot;after I crush Sakayanagi, you&#x27;re next.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p194-1\">← Before: The karaoke negotiation: Horikita–Ryūen alliance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p223-1\">→ After: Kei&#x27;s birthday shopping; Ishizaki&#x27;s apology; the double-birthday proposal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p223-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kei s birthday shopping  ishizaki s apology  the double birthday proposal on a date at keyaki mall with kei  shopping for his birthday  oct 20    he carefully picks something that won t burden her wallet  she sees through him   kiyotaka  you hiding anything from me is a no no too  you got that   you guys were beaten to a pulp by kiyotaka  and since you lost you have no choice but to apologize    kei  i won t forgive you but i will stop blaming you    kei to ishizaki notes he s told kei nothing true about himself  family  white room  his goals  runs into ishizaki albert buying ryuen a birthday gift  also oct 20  accepts kei s grudging forgiveness of ishizaki and her idea to hold a joint birthday party  moved that she wants him to have friends  his group is in pieces    though he takes ishizaki s  double birthday party  proposal  with a grain of salt  his girlfriend   shopping for his birthday  she accepts ishizaki s apology partly to give him friends  he and albert apologize for the rooftop bullying  they discover ayanokoji and ryuen share a birthday   ishizaki proposes a double party  conditional on ryuen apologizing  shares his october 20 birthday  ryuen s evolution  using good as well as evil  noted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p223-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kei&#x27;s birthday shopping; Ishizaki&#x27;s apology; the double-birthday proposal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.223–233<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On a date at Keyaki Mall with Kei, shopping for his birthday (Oct 20) — he carefully picks something that won&#x27;t burden her wallet (she sees through him).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kiyotaka, you hiding anything from me is a no-no too, you got that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You guys were beaten to a pulp by Kiyotaka, and since you lost you have no choice but to apologize.&quot; — Kei<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I won&#x27;t forgive you but I will stop blaming you.&quot; — Kei to Ishizaki<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes he&#x27;s told Kei nothing true about himself (family, White Room, his goals); runs into Ishizaki/Albert buying Ryūen a birthday gift (also Oct 20); accepts Kei&#x27;s grudging forgiveness of Ishizaki and her idea to hold a joint birthday party, moved that she wants him to have friends (his group is in pieces) — though he takes Ishizaki&#x27;s &quot;double birthday party&quot; proposal &quot;with a grain of salt.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223–233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend — shopping for his birthday; she accepts Ishizaki&#x27;s apology partly to give him friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.223–233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> He and Albert apologize for the rooftop bullying; they discover Ayanokōji and Ryūen share a birthday — Ishizaki proposes a double party (conditional on Ryūen apologizing).<span class=\"pg\">p.226–233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Shares his October 20 birthday; Ryūen&#x27;s evolution (using good as well as evil) noted.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p215-1\">← Before: His offer: neutralize Sakayanagi; a &quot;siege on Class A&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p234-1\">→ After: Satou is approached; Ayanokōji&#x27;s &quot;sitting out&quot; plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p234-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune satou-maya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka satou is approached  ayanokoji s  sitting out  plan the day before the festival  calls horikita   says he plans to sit out the festival  essential to his  attack on sakayanagi   sakayanagi san is set on participating in the sports festival tomorrow  you know    horikita  i m thinking of sitting out the sports festival tomorrow   this is my strategy  it s essential  keeps his  attack on sakayanagi  vague  knows his sitting out is connected to sealing her participation   but sakayanagi has already decided to participate  so his plan must adapt  she s thrown by his announcement  dropping the hair dryer  he won t explain yet  off page   a first year approaches her  in satou s pov  saying  if karuizawa senpai were expelled  don t you think you d have a chance    a plot against kei  ayanokoji doesn t yet know","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p234-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Satou is approached; Ayanokōji&#x27;s &quot;sitting out&quot; plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.234–240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The day before the festival, calls Horikita — says he plans to sit out the festival, essential to his &quot;attack on Sakayanagi.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sakayanagi-san is set on participating in the Sports Festival tomorrow, you know?&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m thinking of sitting out the Sports Festival tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;this is my strategy, it&#x27;s essential.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Keeps his &quot;attack on Sakayanagi&quot; vague; knows his sitting out is connected to sealing her participation — but Sakayanagi has already decided to participate, so his plan must adapt.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She&#x27;s thrown by his announcement (dropping the hair dryer); he won&#x27;t explain yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Off-page — a first-year approaches her (in Satou&#x27;s POV), saying &quot;if Karuizawa-senpai were expelled, don&#x27;t you think you&#x27;d have a chance&quot; — a plot against Kei; Ayanokōji doesn&#x27;t yet know.<span class=\"pg\">p.234–237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p223-1\">← Before: Kei&#x27;s birthday shopping; Ishizaki&#x27;s apology; the double-birthday proposal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p302-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi visits; the &quot;special lesson&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p302-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sakayanagi visits  the  special lesson  sitting out the festival in his room  he predicted sakayanagi would come  having had director sakayanagi tell her he was  sick  to draw her in  and she arrives with mont blancs   you really are a terrible person  ayanokouji kun  this was part of your strategy  wasn t it   observation  i decided that it was a good opportunity for me to determine how well the other students would be able to fight when i don t directly participate in the sports festival   a secret for a secret  and a threat for a threat   let s begin a special lesson  shall we  calmly explains his true aim   he wanted to  observe  how the class fights without him  sakayanagi s non participation a  side effect  reveals he wanted to prove  the white room is by no means perfect  by building the strongest class with his own hands  then corners sakayanagi  physically overpowering her  taking a photo  to bind her to secrecy about his plan   registering her with a  special lesson  she sees through his trap  accepts the  lesson  with complicated feelings  and vows to use him in return  they share a secret    see note director sakayanagi  the school director  sakayanagi arisu s father  arranged his sick leave at his request   part of the trap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p302-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi visits; the &quot;special lesson&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.302–317<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sitting out the festival in his room; he predicted Sakayanagi would come (having had Director Sakayanagi tell her he was &quot;sick&quot; to draw her in), and she arrives with mont blancs.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You really are a terrible person, Ayanokouji-kun. This was part of your strategy, wasn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.304<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Observation.&#x27; I decided that it was a good opportunity for me to determine how well the other students would be able to fight when I don&#x27;t directly participate in the Sports Festival.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.313<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;A secret for a secret, and a threat for a threat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.316<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s begin a special lesson, shall we?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calmly explains his true aim — he wanted to *observe* how the class fights without him (Sakayanagi&#x27;s non-participation a &quot;side effect&quot;); reveals he wanted to prove &quot;the White Room is by no means perfect&quot; by building the strongest class with his own hands; then corners Sakayanagi (physically overpowering her, taking a photo) to bind her to secrecy about his plan — registering her with a &quot;special lesson.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.302–317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She sees through his trap, accepts the &quot;lesson&quot; with complicated feelings, and vows to use him in return; they share a secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.302–317<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> — see note<\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Director Sakayanagi (the school director, Sakayanagi Arisu&#x27;s father) arranged his sick leave at his request — part of the trap.<span class=\"pg\">p.302<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p234-1\">← Before: Satou is approached; Ayanokōji&#x27;s &quot;sitting out&quot; plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p320-1\">→ After: The mysterious voice at the door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p320-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the mysterious voice at the door at  12 30  a boy s voice speaks through the door   someone he recognizes by voice but can t place  he heard it once after his father visited the school  the visitor warns him not to labor under the  misapprehension  that eliminating the white room student will bring peace after tsukishiro is gone   remain as you are and listen to me   after eliminating tsukishiro  peace will return if you eliminate the white room student   your existence is a bad influence  i want to prevent anything more from happening  that s it  doesn t open the door  listens  sakayanagi notes she recognizes the voice from  five  maybe ten years ago    meaning he s likely not a white room student  ayanokoji decides not to pursue it since no harm has been done  she s with him and recognizes the voice too  the visitor is unnamed   a neutral figure  neither enemy nor ally  no roster id assigned  7","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p320-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The mysterious voice at the door<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.320–322<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At ~12:30, a boy&#x27;s voice speaks through the door — someone he recognizes by voice but can&#x27;t place (he heard it once after his father visited the school); the visitor warns him not to labor under the &quot;misapprehension&quot; that eliminating the White Room student will bring peace after Tsukishiro is gone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Remain as you are and listen to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.320<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;After eliminating Tsukishiro, peace will return if you eliminate the White Room student.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Your existence is a bad influence. I want to prevent anything more from happening, that&#x27;s it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Doesn&#x27;t open the door, listens; Sakayanagi notes she recognizes the voice from &quot;five, maybe ten years ago&quot; — meaning he&#x27;s likely not a White Room student; Ayanokōji decides not to pursue it since no harm has been done.<span class=\"pg\">p.320–322<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She&#x27;s with him and recognizes the voice too.<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The visitor is unnamed — a neutral figure, neither enemy nor ally; no roster id assigned (§7).<span class=\"pg\">p.321<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p302-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi visits; the &quot;special lesson&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p323-1\">→ After: Results; Horikita&#x27;s resolve; his hidden plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p323-1","v":"y2v6","y":2,"o":22,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka results  horikita s resolve  his hidden plan days later  rankings   horikita 1st  ryuen 2nd  ichinose 3rd  sakayanagi 4th  sudo onodera first in individual rankings  both chose private points over class change tickets  koenji won 10 events but placed 2nd overall  walks back with horikita after she calls him  listens as she reaffirms her choice to keep kushida  a a good shortcut  but a risky promise  and declares she ll move forward with the class s support  calling him  absolutely essential  privately reflects he s like  training wheels    he intends to leave her class once she s grown  and secretly hopes for a future where his victory isn t certain  i hope i am wrong  she s grown  reaffirmed her choice  and grown dependent on him  he plans to leave once she no longer needs him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p323-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Results; Horikita&#x27;s resolve; his hidden plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V6 · p.323–326<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Days later: rankings — Horikita 1st, Ryūen 2nd, Ichinose 3rd, Sakayanagi 4th; Sudō/Onodera first in individual rankings (both chose private points over class-change tickets); Kōenji won 10 events but placed 2nd overall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Walks back with Horikita after she calls him; listens as she reaffirms her choice to keep Kushida (a a good shortcut, but a risky promise) and declares she&#x27;ll move forward with the class&#x27;s support, calling him &quot;absolutely essential&quot;; privately reflects he&#x27;s like &quot;training wheels&quot; — he intends to leave her class once she&#x27;s grown, and secretly hopes for a future where his victory isn&#x27;t certain (&quot;I hope I am wrong&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.324–326<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She&#x27;s grown, reaffirmed her choice, and grown dependent on him; he plans to leave once she no longer needs him.<span class=\"pg\">p.324–326<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v6-p320-1\">← Before: The mysterious voice at the door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p7-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p7-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.7-207<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p7-2\">→ After: Cultural festival rules; OAA results; maid café prep<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p7-2","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune hasebe-haruka sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka cultural festival rules  oaa results  maid cafe prep chabashira reviews the cultural festival rules and additional funds   horikita s class has the most  39 400 pts  10 000 each for horikita sudo onodera  ahead of ichinose  26 600  and sakayanagi ryuen  283 adults  10 000 pts each    202 minors  5 000    3 840 000 points across 485 guests  stall locations cost 1 000 50 000 pts  first floor   50 000  equal sales   equal rank  collusion theoretically possible  oaa results  keisei 1st  horikita 2nd  3 points behind  sudo jumps to 11th  c  367 total    a  center of attention  surprise from his studying  bottom 20 within  15 pts  during maid cafe prep  with horikita and the four originators  learns haruka may  do something  at the festival  she s still bitter over airi  proposes photo tickets  800 pts photo  1 200 with a maid  as a tie in  and insists they need a  feel  for the maid cafe business  co organizing the maid cafe  she s wary of haruka going  out of control  she s still hostile  ayanokoji tells horikita she has  no intention of working as a maid    a general role was assigned instead  his 11th place oaa jump    the center of attention today","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p7-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Cultural festival rules; OAA results; maid café prep<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.7–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira reviews the cultural festival rules and additional funds — Horikita&#x27;s class has the most (39,400 pts: 10,000 each for Horikita/Sudō/Onodera), ahead of Ichinose (26,600) and Sakayanagi/Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> 283 adults (10,000 pts each) + 202 minors (5,000) = 3,840,000 points across 485 guests; stall locations cost 1,000–50,000 pts (first floor = 50,000); equal sales = equal rank (collusion theoretically possible).<span class=\"pg\">p.9–10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> OAA results: Keisei 1st, Horikita 2nd (3 points behind); Sudō jumps to 11th (C+, 367 total) — a &quot;center of attention&quot; surprise from his studying; bottom 20 within ~15 pts.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> During maid café prep (with Horikita and the four originators), learns Haruka may &quot;do something&quot; at the festival (she&#x27;s still bitter over Airi); proposes photo tickets (800 pts/photo, 1,200 with a maid) as a tie-in, and insists they need a &quot;feel&quot; for the maid café business.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Co-organizing the maid café; she&#x27;s wary of Haruka going &quot;out of control.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She&#x27;s still hostile; Ayanokōji tells Horikita she has &quot;no intention of working as a maid&quot; — a general role was assigned instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His 11th-place OAA jump — &quot;the center of attention today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11–12, 23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p7-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p17-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi scouts; the Ryūen &quot;leak&quot;; maid café planning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p17-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu hashimoto-masayoshi horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sakayanagi scouts  the ryuen  leak  maid cafe planning sakayanagi  kamuro and hashimoto tour the special building  hashimoto needles horikita about teaming with ryuen  do you think you can trust him forever   since i m in charge of running the maid cafe  of course i can t cut corners  reveals to the four originators that they ll cooperate with ryuen again  only they plus katsuragi know  outlines maid cafe details  main customers are men  photo tickets  low cost high quality food  horikita is surprised by his knowledge  she watches them with a wry smile   the the leader of class a he asks whether she can trust ryuen   horikita replies on the same level  he informs her of the plan  she knew only the four originators   katsuragi in ryuen s class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi scouts; the Ryūen &quot;leak&quot;; maid café planning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.17–22<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sakayanagi, Kamuro and Hashimoto tour the special building; Hashimoto needles Horikita about teaming with Ryūen (&quot;do you think you can trust him forever?&quot;).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Since I&#x27;m in charge of running the maid café, of course I can&#x27;t cut corners.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reveals to the four originators that they&#x27;ll cooperate with Ryūen again (only they plus Katsuragi know); outlines maid café details (main customers are men, photo tickets, low-cost high-quality food); Horikita is surprised by his knowledge.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She watches them with a wry smile — the the leader of Class A<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He asks whether she can trust Ryūen — Horikita replies on the same level.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He informs her of the plan (she knew only the four originators + Katsuragi in Ryūen&#x27;s class).<span class=\"pg\">p.19–22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p7-2\">← Before: Cultural festival rules; OAA results; maid café prep<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p23-1\">→ After: Sudō&#x27;s growth; Kei&#x27;s night; Satō&#x27;s reaction<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p23-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken karuizawa-kei satou-maya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudo s growth  kei s night  sato s reaction  you were the center of attention today  sudo     huh  well    sudo  if you have any trouble  you can always tell me  well  i m sure you don t need my help  ayanokoji    sudo at keyaki mall  talks with sudo   now a  well balanced  student  c  academics  a  physical  no longer a  one trick pony  thinking about his future beyond high school  he saw akito haruka and asks for help  later  kei  who stayed the night  takes his hand without hesitation   a step up the staircase of adulthood  he s grown through studying for horikita  admits he might need ayanokoji s help with haruka akito  she stayed the night    i m very happy    growing more confident  she spots kei arriving and gives ayanokoji  a gaze    she s still hurt jealous","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p23-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sudō&#x27;s growth; Kei&#x27;s night; Satō&#x27;s reaction<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.23–26<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You were the center of attention today, Sudō.&quot; / &quot;Huh? Well...&quot; — Sudō<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you have any trouble, you can always tell me. Well, I&#x27;m sure you don&#x27;t need my help, Ayanokōji.&quot; — Sudō<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> At Keyaki Mall, talks with Sudō — now a &quot;well-balanced&quot; student (C+ academics, A+ physical), no longer a &quot;one-trick pony,&quot; thinking about his future beyond high school; he saw Akito/Haruka and asks for help; later, Kei (who stayed the night) takes his hand without hesitation — a step up the staircase of adulthood.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He&#x27;s grown through studying for Horikita; admits he might need Ayanokōji&#x27;s help with Haruka/Akito.<span class=\"pg\">p.23–25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She stayed the night — &quot;I&#x27;m very happy&quot; — growing more confident.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> She spots Kei arriving and gives Ayanokōji &quot;a gaze&quot; — she&#x27;s still hurt/jealous.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p17-1\">← Before: Sakayanagi scouts; the Ryūen &quot;leak&quot;; maid café planning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p27-1\">→ After: Ryūen&#x27;s betrayal: leaking the maid café &amp; copying it<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p27-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru horikita-suzune maezono ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ryuen s betrayal  leaking the maid cafe   copying it  we were on equal terms  the same goes for the cultural festival proposal    ryuen  we ll have the same concept as you guys     does that mean a maid cafe   the one who earns as many points as possible will receive 5 million points  watches as ryuen arrives with ishizaki albert kaneda and publicly announces the alliance and that his class will also run a maid cafe   a  declaration of war  leaking their secret so the whole grade knows  ryuen pressures nagumo to bet tens of millions  offering students as collateral  which nagumo refuses  ayanokoji suspects ryuen wants a direct contest  whoever earns more gets 5 million points  he leaks the maid cafe plan and copies the concept   a calculated  gamble  for the 5 million point side bet  she confronts maezono ike over the leak and greets ryuen in the hallway  she angrily asks horikita whether ryuen betrayed them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ryūen&#x27;s betrayal: leaking the maid café &amp; copying it<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.27–31<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"maezono.html\">Maezono<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We were on equal terms. The same goes for the cultural festival proposal.&quot; — Ryūen<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;ll have the same concept as you guys.&quot; / &quot;Does that mean a maid café?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The one who earns as many points as possible will receive 5 million points&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches as Ryūen arrives with Ishizaki/Albert/Kaneda and publicly announces the alliance AND that his class will also run a maid café — a &quot;declaration of war,&quot; leaking their secret so the whole grade knows; Ryūen pressures Nagumo to bet tens of millions (offering students as collateral), which Nagumo refuses; Ayanokōji suspects Ryūen wants a direct contest (whoever earns more gets 5 million points).<span class=\"pg\">p.27–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He leaks the maid café plan and copies the concept — a calculated &quot;gamble&quot; for the 5-million-point side bet.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She confronts Maezono/Ike over the leak and greets Ryūen in the hallway.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Maezono<\/b> She angrily asks Horikita whether Ryūen betrayed them.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p23-1\">← Before: Sudō&#x27;s growth; Kei&#x27;s night; Satō&#x27;s reaction<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p32-1\">→ After: Ichinose, Kanzaki, Asahina: Nagumo&#x27;s plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p32-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"asahina-nazuna ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ichinose  kanzaki  asahina  nagumo s plan encounters ichinose and kanzaki in line  ichinose bows and averts her eyes  awkward  later meets asahina  mii chan  who warns him nagumo may start targeting people close to him   nagumo is saying that he s going to let the non a s compete and pick one student from the class that takes first place  nagumo had never experienced losing  only winning streak after winning streak  i m starting to get a little interested in student council president nagumo  analyzes nagumo  he s never truly lost  only beat weaker opponents like manabu avoided him  so his  warped  desire to compete festers  mii chan warns nagumo could target ichinose kei  realizes nagumo is a man who has never lost and decides he s now  interested  in challenging him   the  calm before the storm  mii chan meets him secretly  warns him about nagumo targeting his close ones  kei ichinose    she knows nagumo well after three years  she s awkward around him  her class is falling in points but not disastrous   nagumo s plan concentrates points on her  he waits for ichinose  later explains nagumo s plan  concentrate private points on one student to win class a    impossible to get consensus in ichinose s class without her  mii chan warns nagumo may target kei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ichinose, Kanzaki, Asahina: Nagumo&#x27;s plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.32–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Encounters Ichinose and Kanzaki in line; Ichinose bows and averts her eyes (awkward); later meets Asahina (Mii-chan), who warns him Nagumo may start targeting people close to him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nagumo is saying that he&#x27;s going to let the non-A&#x27;s compete and pick one student from the class that takes first place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Nagumo had never experienced losing, only winning streak after winning streak<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m starting to get a little interested in Student Council President Nagumo.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Analyzes Nagumo: he&#x27;s never truly lost (only beat weaker opponents like Manabu avoided him), so his &quot;warped&quot; desire to compete festers; Mii-chan warns Nagumo could target Ichinose/Kei; realizes Nagumo is a man who has never lost and decides he&#x27;s now &quot;interested&quot; in challenging him — the &quot;calm before the storm.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> Mii-chan meets him secretly, warns him about Nagumo targeting his close ones (Kei/Ichinose) — she knows Nagumo well after three years.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She&#x27;s awkward around him; her class is falling in points but not disastrous — Nagumo&#x27;s plan concentrates points on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.32, 38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> He waits for Ichinose; later explains Nagumo&#x27;s plan (concentrate private points on one student to win Class A) — impossible to get consensus in Ichinose&#x27;s class without her.<span class=\"pg\">p.32, 42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Mii-chan warns Nagumo may target Kei.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p27-1\">← Before: Ryūen&#x27;s betrayal: leaking the maid café &amp; copying it<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p44-1\">→ After: The Nagumo negotiation: a match and a favor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p44-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi karuizawa-kei ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the nagumo negotiation  a match and a favor visits nagumo in the student council room   a direct  one on one negotiation   i wasn t interested    he admits he never needed to involve nagumo  i have a proposal for president nagumo  can i make a challenge to the student council president this time   if you refuse  that s the end of it  i will never fight the student council president again   it doesn t matter who it is    when nagumo threatens kei  if she disappears  she s gone  and that s all there is to it    his bluff about kei proposes a match  to settle their score  in exchange for a favor   that nagumo stop targeting kei ichinose horikita  when nagumo threatens kei  he declares  it doesn t matter who it is  and that he won t retaliate no matter who s expelled   pure sincerity that shocks nagumo into accepting  afterward he reveals he knew nagumo would target his classmates anyway  you knew  and delivers a cold bluff that if kei vanished  she s gone  and that s all there is to it    nagumo calls him  crazy   loose screws  but he believes suppressing emotion with the  solution  is sanity  he secures a future match with him by agreeing not to interfere with nagumo s harassment   a calculated trade  nagumo accepts   playing  with him  he publicly bluffs indifference to her expulsion to make the deal credible   his  solution  nagumo s plan also targets her  his deal covers her too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Nagumo negotiation: a match and a favor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.44–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Visits Nagumo in the student council room — a direct, one-on-one negotiation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I wasn&#x27;t interested.&quot; — he admits he never needed to involve Nagumo<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have a proposal for President Nagumo. Can I make a challenge to the student council president this time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you refuse, that&#x27;s the end of it. I will never fight the Student Council President again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It doesn&#x27;t matter who it is.&quot; — when Nagumo threatens Kei<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If she disappears, she&#x27;s gone, and that&#x27;s all there is to it.&quot; — his bluff about Kei<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Proposes a match (to settle their score) in exchange for a favor — that Nagumo stop targeting Kei/Ichinose/Horikita; when Nagumo threatens Kei, he declares &quot;it doesn&#x27;t matter who it is&quot; and that he won&#x27;t retaliate no matter who&#x27;s expelled — pure sincerity that shocks Nagumo into accepting; afterward he reveals he knew Nagumo would target his classmates anyway (&quot;you knew?&quot;), and delivers a cold bluff that if Kei vanished &quot;she&#x27;s gone, and that&#x27;s all there is to it&quot; — Nagumo calls him &quot;crazy&quot; (&quot;loose screws&quot;), but he believes suppressing emotion with the &quot;solution&quot; is sanity.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He secures a future match with him by agreeing not to interfere with Nagumo&#x27;s harassment — a calculated trade; Nagumo accepts, &quot;playing&quot; with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> He publicly bluffs indifference to her expulsion to make the deal credible — his &quot;solution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Nagumo&#x27;s plan also targets her; his deal covers her too.<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p32-1\">← Before: Ichinose, Kanzaki, Asahina: Nagumo&#x27;s plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p54-1\">→ After: Kei&#x27;s maturity; asking Mashima about unstated rules<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p54-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"karuizawa-kei mashima-tomonari chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kei s maturity  asking mashima about unstated rules after school  messages kanzaki to meet  off campus  in the special wing  kei asks to go home with him but gracefully switches to sato when he declines   she s grown more mature  even inviting shinohara  formerly her enemy   ayanokoji  what are you doing here in the special building    mashima sensei overhears teachers discussing how chabashira has  changed   laughs more  since the exam  takes the opportunity to ask mashima about  unstated rules  of the festival  e g  purchasing a teacher s time with private points    confirms it s possible  mashima asks about chabashira s change  but ayanokoji deflects  she handles his rejection gracefully  going home with sato and even shinohara   grown more mature than before  he confirms unstated rules  buying a teacher s help  are allowed   the  hidden gem  he ll use later  teachers gossip about her change   mashima notices  ayanokoji doesn t explain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kei&#x27;s maturity; asking Mashima about unstated rules<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.54–57<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After school, messages Kanzaki to meet (off-campus, in the special wing); Kei asks to go home with him but gracefully switches to Satō when he declines — she&#x27;s grown more mature, even inviting Shinohara (formerly her enemy).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"mashima-tomonari.html\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokōji, what are you doing here in the special building?&quot; — Mashima-sensei<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Overhears teachers discussing how Chabashira has &quot;changed&quot; (laughs more) since the exam; takes the opportunity to ask Mashima about &quot;unstated rules&quot; of the festival (e.g. purchasing a teacher&#x27;s time with private points) — confirms it&#x27;s possible; Mashima asks about Chabashira&#x27;s change, but Ayanokōji deflects.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She handles his rejection gracefully, going home with Satō and even Shinohara — grown more mature than before.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> He confirms unstated rules (buying a teacher&#x27;s help) are allowed — the &quot;hidden gem&quot; he&#x27;ll use later.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Teachers gossip about her change — Mashima notices; Ayanokōji doesn&#x27;t explain.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p44-1\">← Before: The Nagumo negotiation: a match and a favor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p57-1\">→ After: The Kanzaki–Himeno plan: changing Ichinose&#x27;s class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p57-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji himeno ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the kanzaki himeno plan  changing ichinose s class meets kanzaki in the special wing  kanzaki confesses he s been struggling alone   ichinose s class cannot reach class a under her  protect everyone  policy  and she never listens to dissent   i need your advice on  ichinose   how about now  we kept following ichinose s policy and lost class points   i don t know  i don t know  but i think there is someone more qualified    on who can move ichinose  what needs to change is the class consciousness  by changing the consciousness of the class  you can bring about change in ichinose  deliberately lets kanzaki unload first  learning the class s inner workings  then reveals he also called himeno   another quiet dissenter  he argues the class  not ichinose  must change  if even 2 3 students  all but ichinose  opposed her policy in the unanimous exam  she might have broken and even volunteered for expulsion  kanzaki and himeno are  the first ones  to change the class  orchestrates the conversation so kanzaki reveals his true intention  he may transfer classes  to motivate himeno    a gamble  he comes for advice  ayanokoji manipulates him into revealing his doubts and transfer threat to himeno  she s summoned  reveals she privately thinks white is white even when the class says black  but stays silent due to peer pressure  kanzaki s threat shakes her  they discuss how to change her without ayanokoji s direct intervention   she won t listen to others but would change if the class did","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p57-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Kanzaki–Himeno plan: changing Ichinose&#x27;s class<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.57–67<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Kanzaki in the special wing; Kanzaki confesses he&#x27;s been struggling alone — Ichinose&#x27;s class cannot reach Class A under her &quot;protect everyone&quot; policy, and she never listens to dissent.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#himeno\">Himeno<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I need your advice on... Ichinose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How about now? We kept following Ichinose&#x27;s policy and lost class points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t know. I don&#x27;t know, but I think there is someone more qualified.&quot; — on who can move Ichinose<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What needs to change is the class consciousness. By changing the consciousness of the class, you can bring about change in Ichinose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately lets Kanzaki unload first (learning the class&#x27;s inner workings), then reveals he also called Himeno — another quiet dissenter. He argues the class (not Ichinose) must change: if even 2–3 students (all but Ichinose) opposed her policy in the Unanimous exam, she might have broken and even volunteered for expulsion; Kanzaki and Himeno are &quot;the first ones&quot; to change the class; orchestrates the conversation so Kanzaki reveals his true intention (he may transfer classes) to motivate Himeno — &quot;a gamble.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> He comes for advice; Ayanokōji manipulates him into revealing his doubts and transfer threat to Himeno.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Himeno<\/b> She&#x27;s summoned; reveals she privately thinks white is white even when the class says black, but stays silent due to peer pressure; Kanzaki&#x27;s threat shakes her.<span class=\"pg\">p.62–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> They discuss how to change her without Ayanokōji&#x27;s direct intervention — she won&#x27;t listen to others but would change if the class did.<span class=\"pg\">p.59–64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p54-1\">← Before: Kei&#x27;s maturity; asking Mashima about unstated rules<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p71-1\">→ After: Kanzaki&#x27;s resolve<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p71-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kanzaki s resolve  it s not too late  be strong  and defeat the class led by horikita in the final exam    ichinose  to kanzaki  recounted   ayanokoji  i ll pay you back for this debt in the final exam  kanzaki leaves with renewed resolve   he and himeno may now work to change ichinose s class before the end of year exam  he vows to repay the  debt  by changing his class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p71-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kanzaki&#x27;s resolve<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.71<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not too late. Be strong. And defeat the class led by Horikita in the final exam.&quot; — Ichinose (to Kanzaki, recounted)<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ayanokōji, I&#x27;ll pay you back for this debt in the final exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kanzaki leaves with renewed resolve — he and Himeno may now work to change Ichinose&#x27;s class before the end-of-year exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> He vows to repay the &quot;debt&quot; by changing his class.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p57-1\">← Before: The Kanzaki–Himeno plan: changing Ichinose&#x27;s class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p72-1\">→ After: Preliminary festival; the &quot;love letter&quot; anagram<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p72-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi yagami-takuya kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka preliminary festival  the  love letter  anagram hears from horikita that the third years held a  preliminary festival  the day before to test stalls and get third party evaluations   this was nagumo s  strange revenge   a separate budget collected from students  sees horikita is concerned about losing   defeat doesn t only mean losing class points  but it s just as bad to fail to earn class points   you re no longer paying contributions to kushida san  right  notices horikita broadening her horizons  confirms she s stopped paying kushida  whose personality has profoundly changed  when ichihashi asks horikita to deliver an anonymous  love letter  to nagumo  he realizes it s a trap and uses the situation   horikita unwillingly becomes the messenger  at the student council meeting nagumo acts oddly  late  not happy  mentioning  secret notes  and offering meeting records  and ayanokoji watches yagami s reactions   the letter is an anagram  a message only certain people can decode  she s growth minded  he lets her deliver the letter  she s reluctant  to draw out yagami nagumo  he acts strangely  late  mentions  secret notes  offers to show meeting records    part of the anagram trap  he s the intended  reader  of the anagram letter  ayanokoji watches for his reaction  horikita has stopped paying her   kushida has changed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Preliminary festival; the &quot;love letter&quot; anagram<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.72–83<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hears from Horikita that the third-years held a &quot;preliminary festival&quot; the day before to test stalls and get third-party evaluations — this was Nagumo&#x27;s &quot;strange revenge&quot; (a separate budget collected from students); sees Horikita is concerned about losing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Defeat doesn&#x27;t only mean losing class points. But it&#x27;s just as bad to fail to earn class points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;re no longer paying contributions to Kushida-san, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notices Horikita broadening her horizons; confirms she&#x27;s stopped paying Kushida (whose personality has profoundly changed); when Ichihashi asks Horikita to deliver an anonymous &quot;love letter&quot; to Nagumo, he realizes it&#x27;s a trap and uses the situation — Horikita unwillingly becomes the messenger; at the student council meeting Nagumo acts oddly (late, not happy, mentioning &quot;secret notes&quot; and offering meeting records), and Ayanokōji watches Yagami&#x27;s reactions — the letter is an anagram, a message only certain people can decode.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She&#x27;s growth-minded; he lets her deliver the letter (she&#x27;s reluctant) to draw out Yagami/Nagumo.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He acts strangely (late, mentions &quot;secret notes,&quot; offers to show meeting records) — part of the anagram trap.<span class=\"pg\">p.78–81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> He&#x27;s the intended &quot;reader&quot; of the anagram letter; Ayanokōji watches for his reaction.<span class=\"pg\">p.75, 81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Horikita has stopped paying her — Kushida has changed.<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p71-1\">← Before: Kanzaki&#x27;s resolve<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p84-1\">→ After: Pre-festival prep; Kushida&#x27;s non-practice; Ryūen&#x27;s café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p84-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka pre festival prep  kushida s non practice  ryuen s cafe the day before the festival  horikita s class has four booths  maid cafe   food stalls  haruka and akito left early   suspicion they may sabotage or skip the festival   i know what you mean  but i don t intend to remove her    horikita  on kushida  don t worry  she s thinking about the festival and the maid cafe in her own way  just believe in kushida san   i heard that she had a match with ryuen kun for complete exemption from helping at the festival  notes kushida hasn t practiced as a maid at all yet horikita defends her  she has her own way  watches ryuen s class set up a traditional japanese cafe  they spent heavily on japanese attire  chabashira and sakayanagi s classes are also preparing  confirms ryuen can t use his usual tactics with so many guests watching  there is no need to worry  she refuses to remove kushida despite others  complaints    believe in kushida san  she s aloof  doesn t practice with the other maids   but ayanokoji trusts she has a plan  she visits horikita late at night  his class runs a competing traditional japanese cafe  he went to check class a  he had a match with someone  ichinose  for exemption from helping  she and akito left early   potentially planning revenge sabotage","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p84-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Pre-festival prep; Kushida&#x27;s non-practice; Ryūen&#x27;s café<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.84–92<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The day before the festival; Horikita&#x27;s class has four booths (maid café + food stalls); Haruka and Akito left early — suspicion they may sabotage or skip the festival.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I know what you mean. But I don&#x27;t intend to remove her.&quot; — Horikita, on Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Don&#x27;t worry. She&#x27;s thinking about the festival and the maid cafe in her own way. Just believe in Kushida-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I heard that she had a match with Ryūen-kun for complete exemption from helping at the festival.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Kushida hasn&#x27;t practiced as a maid at all yet Horikita defends her (she has her own way); watches Ryūen&#x27;s class set up a Traditional Japanese café (they spent heavily on Japanese attire); Chabashira and Sakayanagi&#x27;s classes are also preparing; confirms Ryūen can&#x27;t use his usual tactics with so many guests watching (&quot;there is no need to worry&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.84–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She refuses to remove Kushida despite others&#x27; complaints — &quot;believe in Kushida-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.85–86, 91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She&#x27;s aloof, doesn&#x27;t practice with the other maids — but Ayanokōji trusts she has a plan (she visits Horikita late at night).<span class=\"pg\">p.85–86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His class runs a competing Traditional Japanese café; he went to check Class A; he had a match with someone (Ichinose?) for exemption from helping.<span class=\"pg\">p.88–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She and Akito left early — potentially planning revenge/sabotage.<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p72-1\">← Before: Preliminary festival; the &quot;love letter&quot; anagram<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p93-1\">→ After: Festival simulation: Ishizaki&#x27;s protein; Onodera&#x27;s uniform; Sudō&#x27;s feelings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p93-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"ishizaki-daichi karuizawa-kei onodera-kayano sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka festival simulation  ishizaki s protein  onodera s uniform  sudo s feelings  wow  how did an enforcer like you get permission from ryuen to do this    kei to ishizaki  i m going to surprise my customers tomorrow   you have for horikita  onodera has for you    ayanokoji to sudo during the two hour simulation  runs into ishizaki selling protein drinks  ryuen let him  do whatever you want with your points  kei refuses to drink it  onodera wants a maid uniform but her legs are  too thick    sudo crouches to measure  ayanokoji hints to sudo that onodera likes  him  the way he likes horikita   leaving him to decide between them  he runs a protein drink stand at the festival  500 pts cup    kei distrusts him but he s grown  she refuses ishizaki s drink and glares at him   still not fully trusting  she wants to be a maid but is self conscious about her legs  ayanokoji notes her feelings for sudo  he s conflicted between horikita and onodera   ayanokoji nudges him to decide","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p93-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Festival simulation: Ishizaki&#x27;s protein; Onodera&#x27;s uniform; Sudō&#x27;s feelings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.93–100<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"onodera-kayano.html\">Onodera Kayano<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Wow, how did an enforcer like you get permission from Ryūen to do this?&quot; — Kei to Ishizaki<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m going to surprise my customers tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;you have for Horikita, Onodera has for you.&quot; — Ayanokōji to Sudō<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> During the two-hour simulation, runs into Ishizaki selling protein drinks (Ryūen let him &quot;do whatever you want with your points&quot;); Kei refuses to drink it; Onodera wants a maid uniform but her legs are &quot;too thick&quot; — Sudō crouches to measure; Ayanokōji hints to Sudō that Onodera likes *him* the way he likes Horikita — leaving him to decide between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.93–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> He runs a protein drink stand at the festival (500 pts/cup) — Kei distrusts him but he&#x27;s grown.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She refuses Ishizaki&#x27;s drink and glares at him — still not fully trusting.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Onodera Kayano<\/b> She wants to be a maid but is self-conscious about her legs; Ayanokōji notes her feelings for Sudō.<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He&#x27;s conflicted between Horikita and Onodera — Ayanokōji nudges him to decide.<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p84-1\">← Before: Pre-festival prep; Kushida&#x27;s non-practice; Ryūen&#x27;s café<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p101-1\">→ After: Yagami contacts Kushida; the anagram setup<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p101-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"yagami-takuya kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka yagami contacts kushida  the anagram setup ayanokoji and horikita discuss mandatory breaks  yagami contacts kushida and pushes her to a location   the  love letter  anagram trap is being sprung  in a unanimous special exam  yagami expected kushida to expel horikita and ayanokoji  sets up the trap  yagami  believing kushida failed to expel them  is lured by the anagram  love letter  he decoded   ayanokoji anticipates he ll come to the student council room seeking confirmation  where nagumo  ryuen and others will be waiting  he s the target of the anagram trap   he decoded the letter and will come to the student council room  she s contacted by yagami   used as a pawn in the trap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p101-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Yagami contacts Kushida; the anagram setup<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.101–106<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji and Horikita discuss mandatory breaks; Yagami contacts Kushida and pushes her to a location — the &quot;love letter&quot; anagram trap is being sprung.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">In a unanimous special exam, Yagami expected Kushida to expel Horikita and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sets up the trap: Yagami, believing Kushida failed to expel them, is lured by the anagram &quot;love letter&quot; he decoded — Ayanokōji anticipates he&#x27;ll come to the student council room seeking confirmation, where Nagumo, Ryūen and others will be waiting.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> He&#x27;s the target of the anagram trap — he decoded the letter and will come to the student council room.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She&#x27;s contacted by Yagami — used as a pawn in the trap.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p93-1\">← Before: Festival simulation: Ishizaki&#x27;s protein; Onodera&#x27;s uniform; Sudō&#x27;s feelings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p107-1\">→ After: Festival day: the maid café&#x27;s success; a former guest<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p107-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hasebe-haruka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka festival day  the maid cafe s success  a former guest the festival begins at 9 a m  rumors swirl that haruka akito may be the ones who leaked the maid cafe info  kei says not to jump to conclusions  overall oaa ranking shown   horikita s class is strong   rumors are rumors  haruka and akito didn t actually leak the information   new customers  please show them around    horikita  in an  inorganic voice  at outdoor advertising observes the maid cafe running smoothly  horikita awkward at  customer service  but effective at advertising  photos sell for 800 pts  recognizes a guest who visited during the sports festival   connected to the political figures backing the school  tsukishiro forced the festival through  he s prepared for the if the festival were stuck in a bad situation scenario  she s in charge of the cafe  awkward as a  maid  but managing  she and akito are missing   suspected of leaking the info  unfairly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p107-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Festival day: the maid café&#x27;s success; a former guest<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.107–116<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The festival begins at 9 a.m.; rumors swirl that Haruka/Akito may be the ones who leaked the maid café info (Kei says not to jump to conclusions); overall OAA ranking shown — Horikita&#x27;s class is strong.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Rumors are rumors. Haruka and Akito didn&#x27;t actually leak the information.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;New customers, please show them around.&quot; — Horikita, in an &quot;inorganic voice&quot; at outdoor advertising<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Observes the maid café running smoothly (Horikita awkward at &quot;customer service&quot; but effective at advertising); photos sell for 800 pts; recognizes a guest who visited during the sports festival — connected to the political figures backing the school (Tsukishiro forced the festival through); he&#x27;s prepared for the if the festival were stuck in a bad situation scenario.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She&#x27;s in charge of the café, awkward as a &quot;maid&quot; but managing.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She and Akito are missing — suspected of leaking the info (unfairly).<span class=\"pg\">p.107–108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p101-1\">← Before: Yagami contacts Kushida; the anagram setup<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p117-1\">→ After: Amasawa restrains Kushida; Ayanokōji intervenes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p117-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"amasawa-ichika kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka amasawa restrains kushida  ayanokoji intervenes kushida asks to leave her post briefly  she slips away to an indoor pool area to meet amasawa  ayanokoji tracks her via phone  a  hidden gem  location  and follows   what  why is  ayanokoji kun here    kushida  kushida senpai will pay you back later  so can you give me a little time   you know  kushida senpai  if you say anything bad  i ll have you expelled    amasawa  let s see if you break kushida s arm first  or if i can  stop you  finds amasawa holding kushida in a painful wrist lock  threatening to break her arm if she reveals something  he calmly challenges her    let s see if you break kushida s arm first  or if i can stop you    then  in under 10 seconds  dives in  frees kushida and twists amasawa into a restraint on the ground  amasawa s fighting skills  learned in the white room  are real  he understands  why  amasawa contacted kushida  to silence her about something important  lets amasawa go  and returns with kushida   whose  thank you  surprises him  she grabbed kushida to silence her  ayanokoji overpowers her   she realizes he understood her motive  she met amasawa secretly  he saves her from a broken arm   she s shocked and grateful","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Amasawa restrains Kushida; Ayanokōji intervenes<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.117–130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida asks to leave her post briefly; she slips away to an indoor pool area to meet Amasawa; Ayanokōji tracks her via phone (a &quot;hidden gem&quot; location) and follows.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What? Why is... Ayanokōji-kun here..?&quot; — Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kushida-senpai will pay you back later, so can you give me a little time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You know, Kushida-senpai, if you say anything bad, I&#x27;ll have you expelled&quot; — Amasawa<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s see if you break Kushida&#x27;s arm first, or if I can [stop you].&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finds Amasawa holding Kushida in a painful wrist lock (threatening to break her arm if she reveals something); he calmly challenges her — &quot;let&#x27;s see if you break Kushida&#x27;s arm first, or if I can stop you&quot; — then, in under 10 seconds, dives in, frees Kushida and twists Amasawa into a restraint on the ground (Amasawa&#x27;s fighting skills, learned in the White Room, are real); he understands *why* Amasawa contacted Kushida (to silence her about something important), lets Amasawa go, and returns with Kushida — whose &quot;thank you&quot; surprises him.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> She grabbed Kushida to silence her; Ayanokōji overpowers her — she realizes he understood her motive.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She met Amasawa secretly; he saves her from a broken arm — she&#x27;s shocked and grateful.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p107-1\">← Before: Festival day: the maid café&#x27;s success; a former guest<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p131-1\">→ After: Haruka&#x27;s revenge; Airi&#x27;s maid uniform and SNS<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p131-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka miyake-akito kushida-kikyou sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka haruka s revenge  airi s maid uniform and sns with the cafe overcrowded  kushida suggests using the spare maid uniforms  ayanokoji realizes haruka and akito plan to  withdraw  after the festival as revenge  costing  600 class points  and that haruka plans to visit airi afterward   i estimate 600 class points for the two of them combined    ayanokoji  this is the festival that airi was looking forward to   you re filthy and disgusting    haruka  before lunging at him  a ai    haruka  recognizing the maid uniform in the box confronts haruka  akito restrains her  and gives her airi s maid uniform  airi had left it  hoping haruka would wear it  kushida arrives and reveals airi s sns account   she s now an idol  spreading her wings in the outside world  haruka breaks down  tears up the withdrawal letter  and decides to wear the uniform  the reason for withdrawal is gone  she was going to withdraw out of revenge  the uniform   airi s sns changes her mind   she returns to the cafe  he was going to withdraw with her  he stays when she does  she reveals airi s sns  she gathered information on everyone    the key to stopping haruka  her maid uniform and her new life as an idol  sns    the  gift  that saves haruka","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Haruka&#x27;s revenge; Airi&#x27;s maid uniform and SNS<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.131–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With the café overcrowded, Kushida suggests using the spare maid uniforms; Ayanokōji realizes Haruka and Akito plan to *withdraw* after the festival as revenge (costing ~600 class points), and that Haruka plans to visit Airi afterward.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I estimate 600 class points for the two of them combined.&quot; — Ayanokōji<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This is the festival that Airi was looking forward to.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;re filthy and disgusting.&quot; — Haruka, before lunging at him<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A-ai...&quot; — Haruka, recognizing the maid uniform in the box<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Confronts Haruka (Akito restrains her) and gives her Airi&#x27;s maid uniform (Airi had left it, hoping Haruka would wear it); Kushida arrives and reveals Airi&#x27;s SNS account — she&#x27;s now an idol, spreading her wings in the outside world; Haruka breaks down, tears up the withdrawal letter, and decides to wear the uniform; the reason for withdrawal is gone.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She was going to withdraw out of revenge; the uniform + Airi&#x27;s SNS changes her mind — she returns to the café.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> He was going to withdraw with her; he stays when she does.<span class=\"pg\">p.135–142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She reveals Airi&#x27;s SNS (she gathered information on everyone) — the key to stopping Haruka.<span class=\"pg\">p.142–144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Her maid uniform and her new life as an idol (SNS) — the &quot;gift&quot; that saves Haruka.<span class=\"pg\">p.139–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p117-1\">← Before: Amasawa restrains Kushida; Ayanokōji intervenes<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p153-1\">→ After: Chabashira as a maid: the 100,000-point hire<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p153-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka chabashira as a maid  the 100 000 point hire with sales close  ayanokoji invokes the unstated rule  confirmed by mashima  100 000 private points buys one hour of a teacher s help   he pays to make chabashira a maid for the final hour   why should i be the maid  i m the homeroom teacher   there is nothing in this school that cannot be bought with private points   that s not fair  ayanokoji  using the school rules   standing room only  i ve never heard of that idea in a maid cafe  pays 100 000 points  over mashima s objections  to rent chabashira  changes the cafe policy to standing room only  1 000 pts entry   2 000 pts photo with chabashira    the novelty draws huge crowds  chabashira  red faced  takes 63 photos   surpassing kushida    chabashira s cosplay wins the festival  he blackmails her into being a maid for an hour via the rules   she becomes the cafe s biggest draw  63 photos  she s stunned by the  standing room only  crowd and chabashira s photo count   she tells him he s a nuisance to have around","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Chabashira as a maid: the 100,000-point hire<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.153–160<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With sales close, Ayanokōji invokes the unstated rule (confirmed by Mashima): 100,000 private points buys one hour of a teacher&#x27;s help — he pays to make Chabashira a maid for the final hour.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why should I be the maid!? I&#x27;m the homeroom teacher.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There is nothing in this school that cannot be bought with private points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s not fair, Ayanokōji, using the school rules.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Standing room only, I&#x27;ve never heard of that idea in a maid cafe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pays 100,000 points (over Mashima&#x27;s objections) to rent Chabashira; changes the café policy to standing room only (1,000 pts entry / 2,000 pts photo with Chabashira) — the novelty draws huge crowds; Chabashira, red-faced, takes 63 photos, &quot;surpassing Kushida&quot; — Chabashira&#x27;s cosplay wins the festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> He blackmails her into being a maid for an hour via the rules — she becomes the café&#x27;s biggest draw (63 photos).<span class=\"pg\">p.153–160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She&#x27;s stunned by the &quot;standing-room-only&quot; crowd and Chabashira&#x27;s photo count — she tells him he&#x27;s a nuisance to have around.<span class=\"pg\">p.158–160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p131-1\">← Before: Haruka&#x27;s revenge; Airi&#x27;s maid uniform and SNS<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p184-1\">→ After: Epilogue: Haruka&#x27;s apology; the results<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p184-1","v":"y2v7","y":2,"o":23,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue  haruka s apology  the results after the festival  haruka addresses the class   she hasn t forgiven them  but the person she can t forgive most is herself  she and akito were going to withdraw as revenge  costing 600 class points  but airi s sns  idol  showed her airi had  spread her wings  so she wants to stay and graduate class a to see her without embarrassment   i have not forgiven everyone here   after this festival ended  i was going to leave school   airi will grow a lot  probably more than i thought she would  so i want to be able to graduate in class a and go see her   from now on  you can think of me as your regular hasebe san  okay    haruka notes haruka s speech  horikita s grace  if you are going to be punished  it will only be by remaining classmates with me  and that keisei  akito and haruka reconcile    the group of five was now three  but the bond stronger  he deliberately doesn t approach them  a  farewell  sensing they don t need him anymore  the results  horikita s class 1st  ryuen s 2nd  sakayanagi s 4th  nagumo s 3rd year class a 11th  she apologizes and stays  he doesn t rejoin the group    that place doesn t need me  she handles haruka s return with grace    you made a good decision  the final ranking  1st 2nd year b  horikita  2nd 2nd year c  ryuen  3rd 3rd year b  4th 2nd year a  sakayanagi  11th 3rd year a  nagumo     everything is going according to plan","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p184-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue: Haruka&#x27;s apology; the results<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V7 · p.184–187<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the festival, Haruka addresses the class — she hasn&#x27;t forgiven them, but the person she can&#x27;t forgive most is herself; she and Akito were going to withdraw as revenge (costing 600 class points), but Airi&#x27;s SNS (idol) showed her Airi had &quot;spread her wings,&quot; so she wants to stay and graduate Class A to see her without embarrassment.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have not forgiven everyone here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;After this festival ended, I was going to leave school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Airi will grow a lot. Probably more than I thought she would. So I want to be able to graduate in Class A and go see her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;From now on, you can think of me as your regular Hasebe-san, okay?&quot; — Haruka<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Haruka&#x27;s speech, Horikita&#x27;s grace (&quot;if you are going to be punished, it will only be by remaining classmates with me&quot;), and that Keisei, Akito and Haruka reconcile — &quot;the group of five was now three,&quot; but the bond stronger; he deliberately doesn&#x27;t approach them (a &quot;farewell&quot;), sensing they don&#x27;t need him anymore; the results: Horikita&#x27;s class 1st, Ryūen&#x27;s 2nd, Sakayanagi&#x27;s 4th, Nagumo&#x27;s 3rd-year Class A 11th.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> She apologizes and stays; he doesn&#x27;t rejoin the group — &quot;that place doesn&#x27;t need me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She handles Haruka&#x27;s return with grace — &quot;you made a good decision.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The final ranking: 1st 2nd-year B (Horikita), 2nd 2nd-year C (Ryūen), 3rd 3rd-year B, 4th 2nd-year A (Sakayanagi), 11th 3rd-year A (Nagumo) — &quot;everything is going according to plan.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v7-p153-1\">← Before: Chabashira as a maid: the 100,000-point hire<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p11-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11-208<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p11-2\">→ After: Final exam results; the anonymous evaluation task; school trip to Hokkaido<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p11-2","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka final exam results  the anonymous evaluation task  school trip to hokkaido late november  school trip to hokkaido approaches  former ayanokoji group  haruka akito keisei  walks ahead   he notes the  group of three  remains separate  final exams  horikita and keisei tie 1st  93 5 avg  sudo 10th  solid  kei 56 avg  class a 1st  class b 2nd  25 pts  lowest ranked students get extra  guidance  but no expulsion  new task  each student anonymously assigns each classmate a different number 0 37  based on daily interactions    the evaluations are secret from teachers and students  he ranks koenji no  1  hidden potential  concrete contributions  horikita keisei mii chan high  the data will form the school trip groups  class votes for trip destination  hokkaido wins  he  horikita and keisei voted kyoto  chabashira promises  no special exam to compete for class points  notes sudo s growth is due to horikita  her talent as an educator  kei wants to study more  just like sudo kun    he knows forced studying won t work for her like it did for sudo  suspects the evaluation numbers might be used for a later special exam  his girlfriend   she wants to study with him  her minimum score is rising  his academic growth is  unmistakably attributed  to horikita   a model ayanokoji can t simply replicate with kei  he ranked koenji no  1   his hidden potential and concrete benefits  extremely significant   undeniably responsible for the current status of class b","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p11-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Final exam results; the anonymous evaluation task; school trip to Hokkaido<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.11–18<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Late November; school trip to Hokkaido approaches; former Ayanokōji group (Haruka/Akito/Keisei) walks ahead — he notes the &quot;group of three&quot; remains separate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Final exams: Horikita and Keisei tie 1st (93.5 avg), Sudō 10th (solid); Kei 56 avg; Class A 1st, Class B 2nd (+25 pts); lowest-ranked students get extra &quot;guidance&quot; but no expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> New task: each student anonymously assigns each classmate a different number 0–37 (based on daily interactions) — the evaluations are secret from teachers and students; he ranks Kōenji No. 1 (hidden potential, concrete contributions), Horikita/Keisei/Mii-chan high; the data will form the school-trip groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Class votes for trip destination: Hokkaido wins (he, Horikita and Keisei voted Kyoto); Chabashira promises &quot;no special exam to compete for class points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Sudō&#x27;s growth is due to Horikita (her talent as an educator); Kei wants to study more &quot;just like Sudō-kun&quot; — he knows forced studying won&#x27;t work for her like it did for Sudō; suspects the evaluation numbers might be used for a later special exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> His girlfriend — she wants to study with him; her minimum score is rising.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His academic growth is &quot;unmistakably attributed&quot; to Horikita — a model Ayanokōji can&#x27;t simply replicate with Kei.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He ranked Kōenji No. 1 — his hidden potential and concrete benefits (&quot;extremely significant&quot;), &quot;undeniably responsible for the current status of Class B.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p11-1\">← Before: Full volume<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p19-1\">→ After: School trip rules: fixed mixed groups; Chabashira&#x27;s warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p19-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae kouenji-rokusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka school trip rules  fixed mixed groups  chabashira s warning chabashira explains the trip s purpose   since the school has only 160 students per year  this is a chance to know students from other classes  as a person  before being a student in another class  groups  4 students   one male and one female from each of the four second year classes  groups are fixed from departure to the final bus ride  only the ryokan is exempt  group behavior is mandatory  deprivation of freedom  otherwise  phones allowed  cash exchange up to 10 000 yen  analyzes the fixed group pressure  the pressure of a fixed group  students must make it work even with people they dislike  notes all eyes turn to koenji when discipline is mentioned  he s not listening  realizes the trip s  theme  is cross class relationships  she explains the rules and warns against confusing the trip with a regular school trip  he s not paying attention   the obvious target of the group behavior rule","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">School trip rules: fixed mixed groups; Chabashira&#x27;s warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.19–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira explains the trip&#x27;s purpose — since the school has only 160 students per year, this is a chance to know students from other classes &quot;as a person, before being a student in another class.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Groups: 4 students — one male and one female from each of the four second-year classes; groups are fixed from departure to the final bus ride (only the ryokan is exempt); group behavior is mandatory (&quot;deprivation of freedom&quot; otherwise); phones allowed (cash exchange up to 10,000 yen).<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Analyzes the fixed-group pressure (the pressure of a fixed group: students must make it work even with people they dislike); notes all eyes turn to Kōenji when discipline is mentioned (he&#x27;s not listening); realizes the trip&#x27;s &quot;theme&quot; is cross-class relationships.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She explains the rules and warns against confusing the trip with a regular school trip.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> He&#x27;s not paying attention — the obvious target of the group-behavior rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p11-2\">← Before: Final exam results; the anonymous evaluation task; school trip to Hokkaido<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p28-1\">→ After: Nanase&#x27;s warnings; Amasawa; the outside world<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p28-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"nanase-tsubasa amasawa-ichika yagami-takuya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nanase s warnings  amasawa  the outside world  i want ayanokoji senpai to remain at this school and graduate   the outside world is full of danger  meets nanase  who reports a first year s approach to him  she reveals yagami was  scared  of fighting him  and warns about dangers on the school trip  the outside world  white room involvement via family registers  he probes gently about what she knows  noting her vigilance   she s become an advocate for him staying at school  she warns him about the school trip s dangers and yagami s fear    i can t believe i m the one worried about ayanokoji senpai  he considers what she might do on the trip   she s not a normal student  nanase says he was  afraid of fighting ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p28-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nanase&#x27;s warnings; Amasawa; the outside world<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.28–38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a> · <a href=\"yagami-takuya.html\">Yagami Takuya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I want Ayanokōji-senpai to remain at this school and graduate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;the outside world is full of danger.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Meets Nanase (who reports a first-year&#x27;s approach to him); she reveals Yagami was &quot;scared&quot; of fighting him, and warns about dangers on the school trip (the outside world, white-room involvement via family registers); he probes gently about what she knows, noting her vigilance — she&#x27;s become an advocate for him staying at school.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She warns him about the school trip&#x27;s dangers and Yagami&#x27;s fear — &quot;I can&#x27;t believe I&#x27;m the one worried about Ayanokōji-senpai.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> He considers what she might do on the trip — she&#x27;s not a normal student.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yagami Takuya<\/b> Nanase says he was &quot;afraid of fighting Ayanokōji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p19-1\">← Before: School trip rules: fixed mixed groups; Chabashira&#x27;s warning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p39-1\">→ After: Sudō&#x27;s confession plan; Kei&#x27;s bet; information gathering<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p39-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sudo s confession plan  kei s bet  information gathering  i m going to officially confess to suzune on the school trip  i m serious  i   how did you know     your acting was perfect  i just knew you would be listening    kei eavesdropping  we re getting to the point where we need information on each class in order to move up to class a  sudo visits to say he ll confess to horikita on the trip  he encourages him  kei overhears  he catches her at the cushion  and he explains he wants them in separate groups to gather intel on other classes  kei s  remarkable ability    he motivates her by betting on sudo s confession  success   christmas present  failure   kei does whatever he says  he visits and declares he ll confess to horikita on the trip    i m serious  she eavesdrops  he wants her to gather class information  her  remarkable ability  and makes a bet on sudo s confession  sudo s confession target   ayanokoji thinks it has a  chance   betting on success","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p39-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sudō&#x27;s confession plan; Kei&#x27;s bet; information gathering<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.39–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m going to officially confess to Suzune on the school trip. I&#x27;m serious, I&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;How did you know?&quot; / &quot;Your acting was perfect. I just knew you would be listening.&quot; — Kei eavesdropping<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re getting to the point where we need information on each class in order to move up to Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sudō visits to say he&#x27;ll confess to Horikita on the trip; he encourages him; Kei overhears (he catches her at the cushion), and he explains he wants them in separate groups to gather intel on other classes (kei&#x27;s &quot;remarkable ability&quot;) — he motivates her by betting on Sudō&#x27;s confession (success = Christmas present; failure = Kei does whatever he says).<span class=\"pg\">p.39–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He visits and declares he&#x27;ll confess to Horikita on the trip — &quot;I&#x27;m serious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.39–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> She eavesdrops; he wants her to gather class information (her &quot;remarkable ability&quot;) and makes a bet on Sudō&#x27;s confession.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sudō&#x27;s confession target — Ayanokōji thinks it has a &quot;chance&quot; (betting on success).<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p28-1\">← Before: Nanase&#x27;s warnings; Amasawa; the outside world<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p46-1\">→ After: School trip begins: group 6; bus seating<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p46-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka school trip begins  group 6  bus seating four buses depart for hokkaido  ayanokoji is in group 6   himself  kushida  class b  ryuen and nishino  class d  plus class a members  watanabe amikura etc  surprised to be grouped with ryuen  he reveals his private evaluation numbers  kushida 6  ryuen high  etc    the highest went to kushida and ryuen  kei is in a different group  with akito  as are yosuke  sato   is it okay if i have yosuke sit next to me  kei  notes the groupings seem designed to mix classes  observes kushida deftly take charge of the group  calling out to the class a students  while ryuen doesn t lead  recognizes ryuen and kushida were once  working together  but now seem cordial   deliberately lets kushida lead to avoid conflict  his group mate   she takes charge  and he notes she s resolved not to repeat her past mistakes  his group mate   he doesn t lead  and ayanokoji has  no complaints  about the pairing  different groups   kei sits with sato  he notes it s easier to know who sits next to whom now that they re dating","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">School trip begins: group 6; bus seating<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.46–53<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Four buses depart for Hokkaido; Ayanokōji is in group 6 — himself, Kushida (Class B), Ryūen and Nishino (Class D), plus Class A members (Watanabe/Amikura/etc.); surprised to be grouped with Ryūen.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is it okay if I have Yōsuke sit next to me, Kei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He reveals his private evaluation numbers (Kushida 6, Ryūen high, etc.) — the highest went to Kushida and Ryūen; Kei is in a different group (with Akito), as are Yōsuke, Satō.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the groupings seem designed to mix classes; observes Kushida deftly take charge of the group (calling out to the Class A students), while Ryūen doesn&#x27;t lead; recognizes Ryūen and Kushida were once &quot;working together&quot; but now seem cordial — deliberately lets Kushida lead to avoid conflict.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> His group-mate — she takes charge, and he notes she&#x27;s resolved not to repeat her past mistakes.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> His group-mate — he doesn&#x27;t lead, and Ayanokōji has &quot;no complaints&quot; about the pairing.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Different groups — Kei sits with Satō; he notes it&#x27;s easier to know who sits next to whom now that they&#x27;re dating.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p39-1\">← Before: Sudō&#x27;s confession plan; Kei&#x27;s bet; information gathering<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p55-1\">→ After: Skiing; Kushida probes Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p55-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou yamamura ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka skiing  kushida probes ayanokoji at the ski resort  beginners intermediate advanced groups  he joins beginners with kushida yamamura  ryuen  kito  nishino  kushida were absent  on advanced   i still can t read you  ayanokoji kun   as soon as horikita decided to keep you  the line of me expelling you from  the school disappeared  rides the lift with kushida  who probes what he thinks of her and why horikita kept her  he tells her horikita would have told her off if she d cornered him   an  indisputable  fact she dislikes  observes yamamura  quiet  closed minded  and kushida s strong interpersonal skills  catches her knit hat in a gust  their hands meet    a small  charged moment  she can t read him  tries to figure out what she would think and how she would act if she were him   he lets her struggle  seeing it as a way for her to understand  catches her hat  he notes the quiet first year in their beginner group   she s slow to open up","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Skiing; Kushida probes Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.55–64<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the ski resort: beginners/intermediate/advanced groups; he joins beginners with Kushida/Yamamura; Ryūen, Kitō, Nishino, Kushida were absent (on advanced).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I still can&#x27;t read you, Ayanokōji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;As soon as Horikita decided to keep you, the line of me expelling you from [the school disappeared].&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rides the lift with Kushida, who probes what he thinks of her and why Horikita kept her; he tells her Horikita would have told her off if she&#x27;d cornered him — an &quot;indisputable&quot; fact she dislikes; observes Yamamura (quiet, closed-minded?) and Kushida&#x27;s strong interpersonal skills; catches her knit hat in a gust (their hands meet) — a small, charged moment.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She can&#x27;t read him, tries to figure out what she would think and how she would act if she were him — he lets her struggle, seeing it as a way for her to understand; catches her hat.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">yamamura<\/b> He notes the quiet first-year in their beginner group — she&#x27;s slow to open up.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p46-1\">← Before: School trip begins: group 6; bus seating<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p65-1\">→ After: The ryokan: rooms; the bathhouse (Horikita/Kushida/Ibuki)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p65-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the ryokan  rooms  the bathhouse  horikita kushida ibuki  arrive at the ryokan  group 6 gets rooms  boys girls separate  ryuen dumps his luggage and heads to the baths  kito resents it   you know what  i think we should talk about our group activities  notes kushida proposing the girls visit the boys  room at night  group bonding  the tension between ryuen and kito  and the baths  from horikita s pov  p 70 75  she goes to the outdoor bath  kushida follows and needles her  by the way  you were lucky  weren t you horikita san    horikita admits if not for him she d have been expelled by kushida  ibuki crashes the bath and challenges horikita to a swimming race  ichinose arrives  she leads the group and  in the bath  tells horikita she was  lucky    horikita acknowledges ayanokoji saved her  she s in the bath  admits ayanokoji s role in her survival  ibuki challenges her  he dumps his luggage on watanabe and heads to the baths    clumsy kindness  noted later","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p65-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The ryokan: rooms; the bathhouse (Horikita/Kushida/Ibuki)<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.65–75<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrive at the ryokan; group 6 gets rooms (boys/girls separate); Ryūen dumps his luggage and heads to the baths; Kitō resents it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You know what? I think we should talk about our group activities&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes Kushida proposing the girls visit the boys&#x27; room at night (group bonding), the tension between Ryūen and Kitō, and the baths; from Horikita&#x27;s POV (p.70–75): she goes to the outdoor bath, Kushida follows and needles her (&quot;By the way, you were lucky, weren&#x27;t you Horikita-san?&quot;) — Horikita admits if not for him she&#x27;d have been expelled by Kushida; Ibuki crashes the bath and challenges Horikita to a swimming race; Ichinose arrives.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She leads the group and, in the bath, tells Horikita she was &quot;lucky&quot; — Horikita acknowledges Ayanokōji saved her.<span class=\"pg\">p.66, 73–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She&#x27;s in the bath; admits Ayanokōji&#x27;s role in her survival; Ibuki challenges her.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He dumps his luggage on Watanabe and heads to the baths — &quot;clumsy kindness&quot; noted later.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p55-1\">← Before: Skiing; Kushida probes Ayanokōji<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p90-1\">→ After: Skiing day 2; Yamamura&#x27;s cold; Ryūen&#x27;s &quot;clumsy kindness&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p90-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"yamamura ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka skiing day 2  yamamura s cold  ryuen s  clumsy kindness  morning at the ryokan  ryuen proposes a contest  magazines about kittens  the group goes skiing  notices yamamura shivering without gloves  ryuen  of all people  points it out and orders ayanokoji to lend his gloves    clumsy kindness  typical of ryuen  ayanokoji gives his gloves to yamamura  costing him some comfort  not points  later skiing with kushida ryuen kito  he notes ryuen kito are experts  true role models  and hides that this is only his second time skiing  he lends her his gloves when she s cold   the start of their bond  she s a quiet beginner  he notices yamamura s cold and orders ayanokoji to help    clumsy kindness  he and kito ski like experts  they ski together  she s impressed by his  second time  skill  unknowingly a white room feat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p90-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Skiing day 2; Yamamura&#x27;s cold; Ryūen&#x27;s &quot;clumsy kindness&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.90–108<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning at the ryokan; Ryūen proposes a contest (magazines about kittens); the group goes skiing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notices Yamamura shivering without gloves; Ryūen (of all people) points it out and orders Ayanokōji to lend his gloves — &quot;clumsy kindness, typical of Ryūen&quot;; Ayanokōji gives his gloves to Yamamura (costing him some comfort, not points); later skiing with Kushida/Ryūen/Kitō, he notes Ryūen/Kitō are experts (&quot;true role models&quot;) and hides that this is only his second time skiing.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">yamamura<\/b> He lends her his gloves when she&#x27;s cold — the start of their bond; she&#x27;s a quiet beginner.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He notices Yamamura&#x27;s cold and orders Ayanokōji to help — &quot;clumsy kindness&quot;; he and Kitō ski like experts.<span class=\"pg\">p.98–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> They ski together; she&#x27;s impressed by his &quot;second time&quot; skill (unknowingly a White Room feat).<span class=\"pg\">p.103–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p65-1\">← Before: The ryokan: rooms; the bathhouse (Horikita/Kushida/Ibuki)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p108-1\">→ After: Ryūen&#x27;s 800-million-point plan; the end-of-year exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p108-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru sakayanagi-arisu kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ryuen s 800 million point plan  the end of year exam at lunch  ryuen pulls ayanokoji aside  kushida sends a worried message  to talk   this school trip isn t for cultivating friendship   i hope you remember what i said a year ago about my 800 million points  plan   i ve been very cordial with your class up to this point  ryuen reveals he s still aiming for 800 million private points  to buy class a transfers    he s been  cordial  because he needs horikita s class to help crush sakayanagi in the end of year exam  he s confident   defeated and then resurrected  ayanokoji realizes ryuen has grown and now respects him as a threat  not just an obstacle  warns him not to set him up  he talks strategy  800m points  sakayanagi    a  battle between sakayanagi and ryuen  ayanokoji notes his absolute confidence  they discuss how to defeat her   ryuen wants to  crush her by any means necessary  in the end of year exam  she texted him  worried about being summoned by ryuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ryūen&#x27;s 800-million-point plan; the end-of-year exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.108–114<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At lunch, Ryūen pulls Ayanokōji aside (Kushida sends a worried message) to talk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This school trip isn&#x27;t for cultivating friendship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I hope you remember what I said a year ago about my 800 million points [plan].&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve been very cordial with your class up to this point.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ryūen reveals he&#x27;s still aiming for 800 million private points (to buy Class A transfers) — he&#x27;s been &quot;cordial&quot; because he needs Horikita&#x27;s class to help crush Sakayanagi in the end-of-year exam; he&#x27;s confident, &quot;defeated and then resurrected&quot;; Ayanokōji realizes Ryūen has grown and now respects him as a threat, not just an obstacle; warns him not to set him up.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He talks strategy (800M points, Sakayanagi) — a &quot;battle between Sakayanagi and Ryūen&quot;; Ayanokōji notes his absolute confidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> They discuss how to defeat her — Ryūen wants to &quot;crush her by any means necessary&quot; in the end-of-year exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She texted him, worried about being summoned by Ryūen.<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p90-1\">← Before: Skiing day 2; Yamamura&#x27;s cold; Ryūen&#x27;s &quot;clumsy kindness&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p130-1\">→ After: Sapporo sightseeing: the group&#x27;s 20-point challenge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p130-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kushida-kikyou kitou-hayato ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sapporo sightseeing  the group s 20 point challenge day 3  sapporo sightseeing  groups must visit 6 of 15 spots  score by location  20  points   30 000 private points  with a photo at each  the sixth group debates sightseeing vs points  ryuen  bound to his 800m goal  and kito  rebellious  refuse the majority s choice to tour  ayanokoji deliberately steers kito  giving him  the ball  so ryuen backs down   convincing the group to enjoy sightseeing while keeping the option open  they d get private points another way     a meaningful and satisfying  outcome  notes proximity to kushida drew attention  ryuen noticed  he wants the 30 000 points but ayanokoji outmaneuvers him via kito    you ve gone the extra mile  ayanokoji  they have a  strategy meeting   private conversation    kushida covers for it when ryuen notices  of course  i just talked with ayanokoji kun  he opposes ryuen   ayanokoji uses his rebelliousness to break the deadlock","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p130-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sapporo sightseeing: the group&#x27;s 20-point challenge<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.130–139<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Day 3: Sapporo sightseeing; groups must visit 6 of 15 spots (score by location, 20+ points = 30,000 private points), with a photo at each.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The sixth group debates sightseeing vs points; Ryūen (bound to his 800M goal) and Kitō (rebellious) refuse the majority&#x27;s choice to tour; Ayanokōji deliberately steers Kitō (giving him &quot;the ball&quot;) so Ryūen backs down — convincing the group to enjoy sightseeing while keeping the option open (they&#x27;d get private points another way) — &quot;a meaningful and satisfying&quot; outcome; notes proximity to Kushida drew attention (Ryūen noticed).<span class=\"pg\">p.131–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He wants the 30,000 points but Ayanokōji outmaneuvers him via Kitō — &quot;You&#x27;ve gone the extra mile, Ayanokōji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> They have a &quot;strategy meeting&quot; (private conversation) — Kushida covers for it when Ryūen notices (&quot;Of course, I just talked with Ayanokōji-kun&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.135–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> He opposes Ryūen — Ayanokōji uses his rebelliousness to break the deadlock.<span class=\"pg\">p.133–138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p108-1\">← Before: Ryūen&#x27;s 800-million-point plan; the end-of-year exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p140-1\">→ After: The dining hall: Kushida asks Ryūen to back off; Ayanokōji intervenes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p140-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ryuuen-kakeru katsuragi-kouhei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the dining hall  kushida asks ryuen to back off  ayanokoji intervenes  it s about my relationship with ryuen kun   i m sorry  ryuen  but i m going to have to ask you to back off on this one   that s right  kushida is now taking a new step forward  at breakfast  observes ishizaki yamamura katsuragi  kushida waits to ask ryuen to stop threatening her  lighting a fuse under kushida twice  when ryuen won t back down  ayanokoji steps in   warns that if ryuen s antagonism pushes kushida to reveal class b s secrets in the final exam  it would hurt his own class  ryuen s smile fades  as when he once fearlessly abducted kei  and he relents  she asks him to stop ryuen s threats  he protects her as horikita s ally   she s  taking a new step forward  he threatens kushida  ayanokoji forces him to back off by invoking the final exam  he s eating with class a   ryuen and ayanokoji note his situation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The dining hall: Kushida asks Ryūen to back off; Ayanokōji intervenes<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.140–149<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"katsuragi-kouhei.html\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s about my relationship with Ryūen-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m sorry, Ryūen, but I&#x27;m going to have to ask you to back off on this one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s right. Kushida is now taking a new step forward&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> At breakfast, observes Ishizaki/Yamamura/Katsuragi; Kushida waits to ask Ryūen to stop threatening her (lighting a fuse under Kushida twice); when Ryūen won&#x27;t back down, Ayanokōji steps in — warns that if Ryūen&#x27;s antagonism pushes Kushida to reveal Class B&#x27;s secrets in the final exam, it would hurt his own class; Ryūen&#x27;s smile fades (as when he once fearlessly abducted Kei) and he relents.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She asks him to stop Ryūen&#x27;s threats; he protects her as Horikita&#x27;s ally — she&#x27;s &quot;taking a new step forward.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146–148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He threatens Kushida; Ayanokōji forces him to back off by invoking the final exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.145–149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> He&#x27;s eating with Class A — Ryūen and Ayanokōji note his situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.144–146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p130-1\">← Before: Sapporo sightseeing: the group&#x27;s 20-point challenge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p162-1\">→ After: Final day: the snowball fight; Yamamura&#x27;s thanks<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p162-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"yamamura horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka final day  the snowball fight  yamamura s thanks day 4  an informal snowball fight  1 000 pt entry  winner takes the pot  42 students  6 teams  he  ibuki and yamamura team with horikita s group against sudo s boys  team   let s do our best together  yamamura   if you lose  i ll make up the points  so don t worry  protects the timid yamamura in the fight  pulls her away from snowballs  draws fire himself  sudo s team wins  his  frustration at being rejected by horikita  channeled into snowballs  the final match is horikita vs ibuki   ibuki wins  horikita s snowball disperses  fragments hit ibuki but horikita concedes  yamamura thanks ayanokoji   she felt she formed a bit of a bond as a group  the first trip she enjoyed  he notes her joyful look suddenly faded when he mentioned something  a hidden concern  he protects her in the snowball fight and promises to cover her losses   she thanks him  transformed by the trip  little by little  i think kito kun s curses for ryuen kun are decreasing  she fights ibuki in the final   concedes when her snowball fragments hit   tried to act calm  she wins the final match  demands 1 000 pts from horikita    you re responsible for getting the souvenir money  his team wins the first match    quintessential top class athlete","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p162-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Final day: the snowball fight; Yamamura&#x27;s thanks<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.162–174<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Day 4: an informal snowball fight (1,000-pt entry, winner takes the pot); 42 students, 6 teams; he, Ibuki and Yamamura team with Horikita&#x27;s group against Sudō&#x27;s boys&#x27; team.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Let&#x27;s do our best together, Yamamura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you lose, I&#x27;ll make up the points, so don&#x27;t worry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Protects the timid Yamamura in the fight (pulls her away from snowballs, draws fire himself); Sudō&#x27;s team wins (his &quot;frustration at being rejected by Horikita&quot; channeled into snowballs); the final match is Horikita vs Ibuki — Ibuki wins (Horikita&#x27;s snowball disperses; fragments hit Ibuki but Horikita concedes); Yamamura thanks Ayanokōji — she felt she formed a bit of a bond as a group, the first trip she enjoyed; he notes her joyful look suddenly faded when he mentioned something (a hidden concern).<span class=\"pg\">p.162–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">yamamura<\/b> He protects her in the snowball fight and promises to cover her losses — she thanks him, transformed by the trip (&quot;Little by little, I think Kitō-kun&#x27;s curses for Ryūen-kun are decreasing&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.165–172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She fights Ibuki in the final — concedes when her snowball fragments hit; &quot;tried to act calm.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> She wins the final match, demands 1,000 pts from Horikita — &quot;You&#x27;re responsible for getting the souvenir money.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His team wins the first match — &quot;quintessential top-class athlete.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p140-1\">← Before: The dining hall: Kushida asks Ryūen to back off; Ayanokōji intervenes<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p175-1\">→ After: The final night: Sakayanagi, Kanzaki, the &quot;Ishigami&quot; revelation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p175-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu kanzaki-ryuuji ishigami-kyo-1a nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the final night  sakayanagi  kanzaki  the  ishigami  revelation  it was short  but did you enjoy the school trip   do you think i would lose in a direct confrontation with ryuen kun   i don t think ayanokoji kun will be defeated by someone who isn t me  talks with sakayanagi  she analyzed the grouping bias   high low middle evaluations   and the end of year exam  they agree neither can easily  draw  kanzaki reveals he knows ayanokoji is  ayanokoji sensei s child   his father adores ayanokoji senior  and that first year  ishigami kyo   class a    recommended by ayanokoji senior   is  testing ayanokoji s ability  sakayanagi  on the phone  also knows and vows not to eliminate him unless her father orders it  he resolves to deal with ishigami with kanzaki sakayanagi  she discusses the final exam and grouping  she knows he s ayanokoji senior s son and says  i don t think ayanokoji kun will be defeated by someone who isn t me  he reveals he knows ayanokoji s parentage and the truth about ishigami    i can t believe you re his child  first year class a student  recommended by ayanokoji senior  testing ayanokoji s ability   a new threat  she discussed the mysterious caller  called my father  ayanokoji sensei    not white room  with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p175-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The final night: Sakayanagi, Kanzaki, the &quot;Ishigami&quot; revelation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.175–184<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ishigami-kyo-1a\">Ishigami Kyō (Class 1-A)<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It was short, but did you enjoy the school trip?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you think I would lose in a direct confrontation with Ryūen-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t think Ayanokōji-kun will be defeated by someone who isn&#x27;t me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Talks with Sakayanagi (she analyzed the grouping bias — high/low/middle evaluations — and the end-of-year exam; they agree neither can easily &quot;draw&quot;); Kanzaki reveals he knows Ayanokōji is &quot;Ayanokōji-sensei&#x27;s child&quot; (his father adores Ayanokōji Senior) and that first-year **Ishigami Kyō** (Class A) — recommended by Ayanokōji Senior — is &quot;testing Ayanokōji&#x27;s ability&quot;; Sakayanagi (on the phone) also knows and vows not to eliminate him unless her father orders it; he resolves to deal with Ishigami with Kanzaki/Sakayanagi.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She discusses the final exam and grouping; she knows he&#x27;s Ayanokōji Senior&#x27;s son and says &quot;I don&#x27;t think Ayanokōji-kun will be defeated by someone who isn&#x27;t me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> He reveals he knows Ayanokōji&#x27;s parentage and the truth about Ishigami — &quot;I can&#x27;t believe you&#x27;re his child.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180–183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō (Class 1-A)<\/b> First-year Class A student, recommended by Ayanokōji Senior, testing Ayanokōji&#x27;s ability — a new threat.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She discussed the mysterious caller (&quot;called my father &#x27;Ayanokōji-sensei&#x27;&quot; — not White Room) with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p162-1\">← Before: Final day: the snowball fight; Yamamura&#x27;s thanks<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p187-1\">→ After: After the trip: Ichinose&#x27;s resolve; Ayanokōji&#x27;s refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p187-1","v":"y2v8","y":2,"o":24,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka after the trip  ichinose s resolve  ayanokoji s refusal back from the trip  meets ichinose  she needed a way to contact him    we re in the same group for the school trip  she avoids the topic of kei   if only i could command my classmates like sakayanagi san  if only i could lead as strongly as ryuen kun   our class is definitely moving farther  away   i won t let you stop until the final exam  ichinose admits she s struggling  results don t follow  her class falling further behind  and wishes she could lead like sakayanagi ryuen horikita  ayanokoji refuses to let her give up before the final exam  telling her to keep fighting  until the end    a firm  uncharacteristically harsh push  she opens up about her failings  he refuses to let her stop    w what  ayanokoji kun   surprised by his intensity  ichinose steers clear of the subject of kei  it wasn t that something happened on the school trip","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p187-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">After the trip: Ichinose&#x27;s resolve; Ayanokōji&#x27;s refusal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V8 · p.187–195<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back from the trip; meets Ichinose (she needed a way to contact him — &quot;we&#x27;re in the same group for the school trip&quot;); she avoids the topic of Kei.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If only I could command my classmates like Sakayanagi-san. If only I could lead as strongly as Ryūen-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Our class is definitely moving farther [away].&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I won&#x27;t let you stop until the final exam&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ichinose admits she&#x27;s struggling (&quot;results don&#x27;t follow,&quot; her class falling further behind) and wishes she could lead like Sakayanagi/Ryūen/Horikita; Ayanokōji refuses to let her give up before the final exam, telling her to keep fighting &quot;until the end&quot; — a firm, uncharacteristically harsh push.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She opens up about her failings; he refuses to let her stop — &quot;W-what? Ayanokōji-kun!?&quot; (surprised by his intensity).<span class=\"pg\">p.187–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Ichinose steers clear of the subject of Kei (&quot;it wasn&#x27;t that something happened on the school trip&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v8-p175-1\">← Before: The final night: Sakayanagi, Kanzaki, the &quot;Ishigami&quot; revelation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p8-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the end of semester special exam  a cooperative written test summoned by nagumo to the student council room after school  chabashira announces the final special exam of the second semester   class a  sakayanagi  1250 pts  vs class b  horikita  985 pts  winner takes 50 class points from the loser  special rules  a cooperative written test done by one student at a time in a separate room  no rules to memorize  time bonus  10 pts hour remaining  and per question points  inversely  tied to oaa rating  a 1 pt   e 5 pts    so lower rated students score more per correct answer  a fixed number of questions are randomly  unanswerable   based on absences    zero points  dec 22 exam  dec 23 results  sees this as a  good chance of winning    class b s many lower oaa students  kei  sato  ike  shinohara  can now score 4 5 pts each  horikita grasps the possibility  notes class a still formidable in pure written exams and that 4 absent students would create 4 unanswerable questions  she leads the analysis    we have a good chance of winning  he summoned him    nagumo s message was so compelling that i had no choice but to accept it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p8-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The end-of-semester special exam: a cooperative written test<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.8–17<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summoned by Nagumo to the student council room after school; Chabashira announces the final special exam of the second semester — Class A (Sakayanagi, 1250 pts) vs Class B (Horikita, 985 pts), winner takes 50 class points from the loser.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Special rules: a cooperative written test done by one student at a time in a separate room; no rules to memorize; time bonus (10 pts/hour remaining), and per-question points *inversely* tied to OAA rating (A=1 pt ... E=5 pts) — so lower-rated students score more per correct answer; a fixed number of questions are randomly &quot;unanswerable&quot; (based on absences) — zero points; Dec 22 exam, Dec 23 results.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sees this as a &quot;good chance of winning&quot; — Class B&#x27;s many lower-OAA students (Kei, Satō, Ike, Shinohara) can now score 4–5 pts each; Horikita grasps the possibility; notes Class A still formidable in pure written exams and that 4 absent students would create 4 unanswerable questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She leads the analysis — &quot;we have a good chance of winning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He summoned him — &quot;Nagumo&#x27;s message was so compelling that I had no choice but to accept it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.8, 18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p18-1\">→ After: Nagumo&#x27;s election bet: 20 million points<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p18-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"nagumo-miyabi kiriyama ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka nagumo s election bet  20 million points in the student council room  nagumo and kiriyama reveal they ve called horikita and ichinose   nagumo will step down and hold an election for the next student council president   if i win  i want to get some private points from you   if you re fine with paying ayanokouji  nagumo proposes they pick the next president together and bet   if ayanokoji wins  he gets enough private points to  buy a ticket to move to the next class   20 million  the third year votes are at nagumo s discretion  1 3 already his  ayanokoji recognizes nagumo s  conscience  and refuses to be outdone   accepts the high stakes match  he wants a  battle  to decide the president  they bet 20 million points on the outcome   the  match  ayanokoji wanted  the vice president   watches silently  urges nagumo to be pragmatic","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p18-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Nagumo&#x27;s election bet: 20 million points<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.18–25<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the student council room, Nagumo and Kiriyama reveal they&#x27;ve called Horikita and Ichinose — Nagumo will step down and hold an election for the next student council president.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I win, I want to get some private points from you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you&#x27;re fine with paying Ayanokouji&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Nagumo proposes they pick the next president together and bet — if Ayanokōji wins, he gets enough private points to &quot;buy a ticket to move to the next class&quot; (20 million); the third-year votes are at Nagumo&#x27;s discretion (1/3 already his); Ayanokōji recognizes Nagumo&#x27;s &quot;conscience&quot; and refuses to be outdone — accepts the high-stakes match.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He wants a &quot;battle&quot; to decide the president; they bet 20 million points on the outcome — the &quot;match&quot; Ayanokōji wanted.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> The vice president — watches silently, urges Nagumo to be pragmatic.<span class=\"pg\">p.18–25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p8-1\">← Before: The end-of-semester special exam: a cooperative written test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p26-1\">→ After: Ichinose withdraws; Horikita becomes president unopposed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p26-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune kiryuin-fuuka nagumo-miyabi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ichinose withdraws  horikita becomes president unopposed horikita and ichinose arrive  kiryuin bursts in  revealing nagumo ordered first year yamanaka to shoplift as a  mission   a way to be expelled gain class a tickets    yamanaka s lie would only punish herself  no evidence against nagumo   i m not going to run for the student council this time   a person like me can t be the student council president  a criminal  that s why   before the election  i would like to resign from the student council today   i m sure you ll be a wonderful student council president  horikita san  watches as ichinose   shaken by kiryuin s  criminal  remark  her shoplifting past    withdraws from the election and resigns from the student council entirely  believing her own  conceitedness  caused her class s fall  horikita  unopposed  becomes president and is ordered to recruit new members  one second year  one first year to replace yagami  ayanokoji is roped into helping  he gives nagumo hokkaido souvenirs   nagumo calls him  disciplined in a strange way  she withdraws and resigns  calling herself a  criminal    ayanokoji can t explain the shoplifting context  she departs smiling  rooting for horikita  she becomes student council president unopposed  tasked with recruiting   ayanokoji agrees to help  she bursts in and exposes nagumo s shoplifting order    i m sorry for interrupting  but i want to talk about what you said earlier  he loses his  match   ichinose s withdrawal ends it  tells ayanokoji to help recruit  and accepts souvenirs","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p26-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ichinose withdraws; Horikita becomes president unopposed<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.26–37<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita and Ichinose arrive; Kiryūin bursts in, revealing Nagumo ordered first-year Yamanaka to shoplift as a &quot;mission&quot; (a way to be expelled/gain Class A tickets) — Yamanaka&#x27;s lie would only punish herself (no evidence against Nagumo).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m—not going to run for the student council this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;a person like me can&#x27;t be the student council president. A criminal, that&#x27;s why…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Before the election, I would like to resign from the student council today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m sure you&#x27;ll be a wonderful student council president, Horikita-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches as Ichinose — shaken by Kiryūin&#x27;s &quot;criminal&quot; remark (her shoplifting past) — withdraws from the election and resigns from the student council entirely, believing her own &quot;conceitedness&quot; caused her class&#x27;s fall; Horikita, unopposed, becomes president and is ordered to recruit new members (one second-year, one first-year to replace Yagami); Ayanokōji is roped into helping; he gives Nagumo Hokkaido souvenirs — Nagumo calls him &quot;disciplined in a strange way.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She withdraws and resigns, calling herself a &quot;criminal&quot; — Ayanokōji can&#x27;t explain the shoplifting context; she departs smiling, rooting for Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.33–35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She becomes student council president unopposed; tasked with recruiting — Ayanokōji agrees to help.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> She bursts in and exposes Nagumo&#x27;s shoplifting order — &quot;I&#x27;m sorry for interrupting, but I want to talk about what you said earlier.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He loses his &quot;match&quot; (Ichinose&#x27;s withdrawal ends it), tells Ayanokōji to help recruit, and accepts souvenirs.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p18-1\">← Before: Nagumo&#x27;s election bet: 20 million points<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p44-1\">→ After: Recruiting Kushida: Horikita&#x27;s prostration gambit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p44-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka recruiting kushida  horikita s prostration gambit as new student council president  horikita sets out to fill the vacancies  one second year  one first year  she approaches kushida   a  skilled  high reputation candidate   though they are  oil and water   yes  if you show me a  please  kushida san  attitude  i will consider it  no  i will definitely join the student council   so  just prostrate myself and ask you to join the student council    horikita watches as horikita corners kushida  in front of witnesses  so she can t drop the  good girl  facade  then takes the negotiation private  special wing  when kushida demands horikita prostrate herself  horikita actually starts to kneel   ayanokoji notes the vice president has more real power than the student council president  appealing to kushida s ambition  to make the president her  plaything  kushida finally agrees   but only because it benefits her  and she still wants to see horikita prostrate herself  she uses ayanokoji s tactics    i m sure i won t get any compliments from nagumo  but i m so happy to    and nearly humiliates herself to recruit kushida  she resists joining  hates working under horikita  demands prostration  and accepts for her own benefit    three times more annoying  than horikita  she appeared eavesdropping on the kushida negotiation  claiming she came to see kushida  teased kushida  i m the only one who can tease kushida senpai so blatantly    ayanokoji suspects she wanted to see him horikita interact","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Recruiting Kushida: Horikita&#x27;s prostration gambit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.44–59<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As new student council president, Horikita sets out to fill the vacancies (one second-year, one first-year); she approaches Kushida — a &quot;skilled,&quot; high-reputation candidate — though they are &quot;oil and water.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yes. If you show me a &#x27;please, Kushida-san&#x27; attitude, I will consider it… No, I will definitely join the student council!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So… just prostrate myself and ask you to join the student council?&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches as Horikita corners Kushida (in front of witnesses, so she can&#x27;t drop the &quot;good girl&quot; facade), then takes the negotiation private (special wing); when Kushida demands Horikita prostrate herself, Horikita actually starts to kneel — Ayanokōji notes the vice president has more real power than the student council president, appealing to Kushida&#x27;s ambition (to make the president her &quot;plaything&quot;); Kushida finally agrees — but only because it benefits her, and she still wants to see Horikita prostrate herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She uses Ayanokōji&#x27;s tactics — &quot;I&#x27;m sure I won&#x27;t get any compliments from Nagumo, but I&#x27;m so happy to...&quot; — and nearly humiliates herself to recruit Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She resists joining (hates working under Horikita), demands prostration, and accepts for her own benefit — &quot;three times more annoying [than Horikita].&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44–59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> She appeared eavesdropping on the Kushida negotiation (claiming she came to see Kushida), teased Kushida (&quot;I&#x27;m the only one who can tease Kushida-senpai so blatantly&quot;) — Ayanokōji suspects she wanted to see him/Horikita interact.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p26-1\">← Before: Ichinose withdraws; Horikita becomes president unopposed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p61-1\">→ After: Recruiting Nanase; Ishigami declines<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p61-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"","w":"ishigami-kyo-1a nanase-tsubasa amasawa-ichika ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka recruiting nanase  ishigami declines horikita targets first year ishigami  class a  for the council   ayanokoji feigns ignorance  ishigami  polished honor student  declines   i have no interest in club activities nor in joining the student council  turns to class 1 d  where nanase volunteers  ayanokoji recommends her  good academic rating  serious  and horikita accepts pending nagumo s approval   nanase joins the student council  a  most welcome addition  given her hidden agenda to keep him at school  horikita asks him to join  he refuses outright   ayanokoji notes he s the one kanzaki warned about  she volunteers for the student council   ayanokoji has doubts about her true motive but sees the benefit  she s acquainted with ishigami  kushida senpai s  knows of him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p61-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Recruiting Nanase; Ishigami declines<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.61–67<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita targets first-year Ishigami (Class A) for the council — Ayanokōji feigns ignorance; Ishigami (polished honor student) declines: &quot;I have no interest in club activities nor in joining the student council.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#ishigami-kyo-1a\">Ishigami Kyō (Class 1-A)<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a> · <a href=\"amasawa-ichika.html\">Amasawa Ichika<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Turns to Class 1-D, where Nanase volunteers; Ayanokōji recommends her (good academic rating, serious), and Horikita accepts pending Nagumo&#x27;s approval — Nanase joins the student council (a &quot;most welcome addition&quot; given her hidden agenda to keep him at school).<span class=\"pg\">p.61–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō (Class 1-A)<\/b> Horikita asks him to join; he refuses outright — Ayanokōji notes he&#x27;s the one Kanzaki warned about.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She volunteers for the student council — Ayanokōji has doubts about her true motive but sees the benefit.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amasawa Ichika<\/b> She&#x27;s acquainted with Ishigami (&quot;Kushida-senpai&#x27;s...&quot;), knows of him.<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p44-1\">← Before: Recruiting Kushida: Horikita&#x27;s prostration gambit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p118-1\">→ After: The gym date with Ichinose; her changed feelings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p118-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami amikura-mako ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the gym date with ichinose  her changed feelings meets ichinose at the dorm lobby  she comes  prepared  unlike the trip  and goes to the gym with her   a  date  of sorts to learn why she resigned from the student council and about the  ideal man  she mentioned   i was surprised that you resigned from the student council  i thought there was a good chance you would win the student council election against horikita   i don t feel the need to support horikita just because we are classmates  if nagumo said he would support horikita  i still would have supported you  spends  2 hours training with ichinose  treadmill  weights  observes amikura teasing her about  a guy   ayanokoji  learns ichinose s class is studying hard  she reveals she quit the council to focus on the fight for class a  and that her feelings for him remain but she won t  take that final step that would go against her morals    he realizes ichinose has changed  eyes seemed to have more sparkle  and that her love had undeniably given her great strength  gym  date  she confides her reasons for quitting  resists confessing fully  she didn t take that final step    her love  still strong  but self restrained  she notices ichinose ayanokoji together  teases ichinose about  a guy     you have at least an idea that she has a special interest in you  don t you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p118-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The gym date with Ichinose; her changed feelings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.118–139<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Ichinose at the dorm lobby (she comes &quot;prepared,&quot; unlike the trip) and goes to the gym with her — a &quot;date&quot; of sorts to learn why she resigned from the student council and about the &quot;ideal man&quot; she mentioned.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"amikura-mako.html\">Amikura Mako<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was surprised that you resigned from the student council. I thought there was a good chance you would win the student council election against Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t feel the need to support Horikita just because we are classmates. If Nagumo said he would support Horikita, I still would have supported you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Spends ~2 hours training with Ichinose (treadmill, weights), observes Amikura teasing her about &quot;a guy&quot; (Ayanokōji), learns Ichinose&#x27;s class is studying hard; she reveals she quit the council to focus on the fight for Class A, and that her feelings for him remain but she won&#x27;t &quot;take that final step that would go against her morals&quot; — he realizes Ichinose has changed (&quot;eyes seemed to have more sparkle&quot;), and that her love had undeniably given her great strength.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Gym &quot;date&quot;; she confides her reasons for quitting, resists confessing fully (&quot;she didn&#x27;t take that final step&quot;) — her love &quot;still strong&quot; but self-restrained.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amikura Mako<\/b> She notices Ichinose/Ayanokōji together, teases Ichinose about &quot;a guy&quot; — &quot;You have at least an idea that she has a special interest in you, don&#x27;t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125–131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p61-1\">← Before: Recruiting Nanase; Ishigami declines<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p153-1\">→ After: The shoplifting case: Kiriyama exposed as the mastermind<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p153-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"","w":"kiriyama nagumo-miyabi kiryuin-fuuka asahina-nazuna ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the shoplifting case  kiriyama exposed as the mastermind investigating kiryuin s complaint that nagumo ordered a first year  yamanaka  to shoplift  he gathers intel from third years   learns of nagumo s  contract  with lower classes  75  of private points to nagumo in exchange for class a tickets  and the anti nagumo faction  pieces together that kiriyama  nagumo s vp  was the real instigator   he ordered yamanaka tachibana to shoplift  blaming nagumo  to force kiryuin to complain to the student council  stop the election  and nagumo s 20m point bet  and make ichinose recall her  shoplifting  trauma and withdraw  his motive  prevent nagumo s  selfish  outflow of third year points and vote buying  he exposes him as the mastermind    kiriyama senpai s objective was to destroy the student council  election  he learns the details of nagumo s contract  75  of points  class a tickets    nagumo is  indirectly  the cause of much unrest  he warns her he can prove kiriyama s role    i m sure you could ve collected private points and redistributed them  she tells him about sachi  yamanaka s withdrawal and nagumo s contract    i d say it s more like a loophole","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p153-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The shoplifting case: Kiriyama exposed as the mastermind<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.153–169<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Investigating Kiryūin&#x27;s complaint that Nagumo ordered a first-year (Yamanaka) to shoplift, he gathers intel from third-years — learns of Nagumo&#x27;s &quot;contract&quot; with lower classes (75% of private points to Nagumo in exchange for Class A tickets) and the anti-Nagumo faction.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a> · <a href=\"nagumo-miyabi.html\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/a> · <a href=\"kiryuin-fuuka.html\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/a> · <a href=\"asahina-nazuna.html\">Asahina Nazuna<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pieces together that Kiriyama (Nagumo&#x27;s VP) was the real instigator — he ordered Yamanaka/Tachibana to shoplift (blaming Nagumo) to force Kiryūin to complain to the student council, stop the election (and Nagumo&#x27;s 20M-point bet), and make Ichinose recall her &quot;shoplifting&quot; trauma and withdraw; his motive: prevent Nagumo&#x27;s &quot;selfish&quot; outflow of third-year points and vote-buying.<span class=\"pg\">p.153–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> He exposes him as the mastermind — &quot;Kiriyama-senpai&#x27;s objective was to destroy the student council [election].&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nagumo Miyabi<\/b> He learns the details of Nagumo&#x27;s contract (75% of points, Class A tickets) — Nagumo is &quot;indirectly&quot; the cause of much unrest.<span class=\"pg\">p.160–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiryuin Fuuka<\/b> He warns her he can prove Kiriyama&#x27;s role — &quot;I&#x27;m sure you could&#x27;ve collected private points and redistributed them...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Asahina Nazuna<\/b> She tells him about Sachi (Yamanaka)&#x27;s withdrawal and Nagumo&#x27;s contract — &quot;I&#x27;d say it&#x27;s more like a loophole.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157–163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p118-1\">← Before: The gym date with Ichinose; her changed feelings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p170-1\">→ After: Ichinose visits his room: a &quot;selfish&quot; farewell to her feelings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p170-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ichinose visits his room  a  selfish  farewell to her feelings ichinose waits outside after school  asks to come to his room for  a little chat    a  selfish  request  she enters  notices kei s things  photo frame  drinks  and smiles   selfishness  did you mind   i m always leading a life of self indulgence  she asks him to sit beside her  her selfish wish  drinks cocoa  and   determined  not looking away   effectively gives voice to her feelings without confessing fully  he realizes she  didn t beg  and restrained herself from the act that would violate her morals    the core of ichinose honami    and that her change  bright  strong  will drive her class  he decides to support her from the side  she makes a  selfish  visit  sits close  and reveals her resolved feelings without crossing her moral line    she was able to restrain herself  kei s belongings photo are in the room   ichinose is aware of their relationship","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ichinose visits his room: a &quot;selfish&quot; farewell to her feelings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.170–176<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ichinose waits outside after school, asks to come to his room for &quot;a little chat&quot; — a &quot;selfish&quot; request; she enters, notices Kei&#x27;s things (photo frame, drinks) and smiles.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;selfishness. Did you mind?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m always leading a life of self-indulgence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She asks him to sit beside her (her selfish wish), drinks cocoa, and — determined, not looking away — effectively gives voice to her feelings without confessing fully; he realizes she &quot;didn&#x27;t beg&quot; and restrained herself from the act that would violate her morals — &quot;the core of Ichinose Honami&quot; — and that her change (bright, strong) will drive her class; he decides to support her from the side.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She makes a &quot;selfish&quot; visit, sits close, and reveals her resolved feelings without crossing her moral line — &quot;she was able to restrain herself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170–176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Kei&#x27;s belongings/photo are in the room — Ichinose is aware of their relationship.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p153-1\">← Before: The shoplifting case: Kiriyama exposed as the mastermind<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p177-1\">→ After: The special exam; Horikita beats Sakayanagi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p177-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune sakayanagi-arisu karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the special exam  horikita beats sakayanagi day of the collaborative written test vs class a  horikita submits the answering order   keisei leadoff  solves 2 quickly  reads the rest  then alternating high low students  students pass in the hallway and use hand signs to indicate which problem to solve  not against the rules    a clever exploitation of a loophole  notes the strategy  hand signals for problem numbers  lower ranked students solve easy problems  and koenji s unpredictability  if he refuses  only 4 pts lost  after the exam  class b wins   but their correct answer rate is 72  vs sakayanagi s 86   under identical conditions  horikita would have lost  sakayanagi accepts the loss with composure  her elaborate strategy wins    you used an interesting strategy for this special exam  she s frustrated only by the lower accuracy rate  not pessimistic  her class lost despite 86  accuracy    she would not be happy  she did what she had to do  and lost  their  cold war  continues   kei s morale  can easily affect the rest of our class  worries horikita  ayanokoji plans to  make up with her as soon as possible","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p177-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The special exam; Horikita beats Sakayanagi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.177–198<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Day of the collaborative written test vs Class A; Horikita submits the answering order — Keisei leadoff (solves 2 quickly, reads the rest), then alternating high/low students; students pass in the hallway and use hand signs to indicate which problem to solve (not against the rules) — a clever exploitation of a loophole.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the strategy (hand signals for problem numbers; lower-ranked students solve easy problems) and Kōenji&#x27;s unpredictability (if he refuses, only 4 pts lost); after the exam, Class B wins — but their correct-answer rate is 72% vs Sakayanagi&#x27;s 86% (under identical conditions, Horikita would have lost); Sakayanagi accepts the loss with composure.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her elaborate strategy wins — &quot;You used an interesting strategy for this special exam&quot;; she&#x27;s frustrated only by the lower accuracy rate, not pessimistic.<span class=\"pg\">p.177–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Her class lost despite 86% accuracy — &quot;She would not be happy. She did what she had to do, and lost.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Their &quot;cold war&quot; continues — Kei&#x27;s morale (can easily affect the rest of our class) worries Horikita; Ayanokōji plans to &quot;make up with her as soon as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195–198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p170-1\">← Before: Ichinose visits his room: a &quot;selfish&quot; farewell to her feelings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p183-1\">→ After: The student council hearing; Horikita judges Kiriyama<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p183-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kiriyama kushida-kikyou nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the student council hearing  horikita judges kiriyama after the exam  the new student council  horikita president  kushida vp  nanase agasaka first years  convenes with kiryuin  nagumo  kiriyama   horikita presides   the real person behind this case is not nagumo senpai  but kiriyamasenpai  the vice president    horikita watches as horikita  prompted by his report  unravels the case  kiriyama framed yamanaka tachibana to blame nagumo and stop the election  kiriyama admits it  his  betrayal  of nagumo to prevent  unnecessary  point outflows  horikita s judgment   kiriyama sincerely apologizes to kiryuin and voluntarily suspends himself for a week  nagumo must not revoke his class a ticket  and third year collected points may only be used for third years   is accepted by all  even nagumo  you have the power to undermine me  he notes kiriyama s  meaningful expression  at the end    i don t know if this is really the end  her first case as president   she judges fairly and firmly   a much more capable student council president than i thought  he s exposed  admits it    it is an action based on a contract  do whatever you want  now student council vice president    i guess you chose kushida as the vice president after all  she takes the meeting notes as a new first year council member","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p183-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The student council hearing; Horikita judges Kiriyama<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.183–194<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the exam, the new student council (Horikita president, Kushida VP, Nanase/Agasaka first-years) convenes with Kiryūin, Nagumo, Kiriyama — Horikita presides.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"kiriyama.html\">Kiriyama<\/a> · <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The real person behind this case is not Nagumo-senpai, but Kiriyamasenpai, the vice president.&quot; — Horikita<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches as Horikita (prompted by his report) unravels the case: Kiriyama framed Yamanaka/Tachibana to blame Nagumo and stop the election; Kiriyama admits it (his &quot;betrayal&quot; of Nagumo to prevent &quot;unnecessary&quot; point outflows); Horikita&#x27;s judgment — Kiriyama sincerely apologizes to Kiryūin and voluntarily suspends himself for a week, Nagumo must not revoke his Class A ticket, and third-year-collected points may only be used for third-years — is accepted by all, even Nagumo (&quot;You have the power to undermine me&quot;); he notes Kiriyama&#x27;s &quot;meaningful expression&quot; at the end — &quot;I don&#x27;t know if this is really the end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her first case as president — she judges fairly and firmly, &quot;a much more capable student council president than I thought.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kiriyama<\/b> He&#x27;s exposed, admits it — &quot;It is an action based on a contract. Do whatever you want.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Now student council vice president — &quot;I guess you chose Kushida as the vice president after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> She takes the meeting notes as a new first-year council member.<span class=\"pg\">p.181–190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p177-1\">← Before: The special exam; Horikita beats Sakayanagi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p199-1\">→ After: Sakayanagi&#x27;s ultimatum to Ichinose; a quiet warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p199-1","v":"y2v9","y":2,"o":25,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sakayanagi s ultimatum to ichinose  a quiet warning after the results  meets sakayanagi  who summoned him  and ichinose  who also messaged  outside  sakayanagi congratulates them and reveals her  ultimatum  for ichinose   distance herself from ayanokoji  you are being controlled by him   i have called you both here today to tell you that i am here to give an ultimatum to ichinose san  who has a faint crush on ayanokouji kun   you should distance yourself from ayanokouji kun now  watches as ichinose   changed   cold look in her eyes    rejects the ultimatum  accusing sakayanagi of wanting to control her and being conscious of ayanokoji as a special person  sakayanagi is briefly caught off guard  a rare upset  and concedes  afterward she tells ayanokoji she never thought she would be re evaluating ichinose  and reveals she has no intention of stopping ichinose   the only difference is who destroys her   planning to visit his room again  she gives ichinose an ultimatum and shows her hand  i will visit your room again in the near future  she sees ichinose as a  consumable  pawn  she rejects sakayanagi s ultimatum   her good directed outward  completely transformed into evil  ayanokoji realizes love can influence our reason and nature   an unpredictable force","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sakayanagi&#x27;s ultimatum to Ichinose; a quiet warning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9 · p.199–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the results, meets Sakayanagi (who summoned him) and Ichinose (who also messaged) outside; Sakayanagi congratulates them and reveals her &quot;ultimatum&quot; for Ichinose — distance herself from Ayanokōji (&quot;you are being controlled by him&quot;).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I have called you both here today to tell you that I am here to give an ultimatum to Ichinose-san, who has a faint crush on Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You should distance yourself from Ayanokouji-kun now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Watches as Ichinose — changed, &quot;cold look in her eyes&quot; — rejects the ultimatum, accusing Sakayanagi of wanting to control her and being conscious of Ayanokōji as a special person; Sakayanagi is briefly caught off guard (a rare upset) and concedes; afterward she tells Ayanokōji she never thought she would be re-evaluating Ichinose, and reveals she has no intention of stopping Ichinose — the only difference is who destroys her — planning to visit his room again.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> She gives Ichinose an ultimatum and shows her hand (&quot;I will visit your room again in the near future&quot;); she sees Ichinose as a &quot;consumable&quot; pawn.<span class=\"pg\">p.199–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She rejects Sakayanagi&#x27;s ultimatum — her good directed outward, completely transformed into evil; Ayanokōji realizes love can influence our reason and nature — an unpredictable force.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9-p183-1\">← Before: The student council hearing; Horikita judges Kiriyama<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9_75-p4-1","v":"y2v9.75","y":2,"o":27,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v9_75-p4-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V9.75 · p.4-8<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v10-p9-1","v":"y2v10","y":2,"o":28,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v10-p9-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10 · p.9-235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v10_25-p1-1","v":"y2v10.25","y":2,"o":29,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v10_25-p1-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V10.25 · p.1-10<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v11-p11-1","v":"y2v11","y":2,"o":30,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka full volume appears in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v11-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V11 · p.11-223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears in this volume.<\/p><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v12_5-p11-1","v":"y2v12.5","y":2,"o":32,"k":"","w":"sakayanagi-arisu ryuuen-kakeru karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ichinose-honami tsukishiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1 epilogue  full volume horikita explains the end of year special exam to the class  reveals maezono leaked his role as general  meets sakayanagi and ryuen  sakayanagi reveals ayanokoji s message  meets morishita and yamamura  learns class a s state  meets matsushita  mii chan  onodera at keyaki mall  meets hoshinomiya at a cafe  she proposes he concede victory  breaks up with karuizawa kei  date at cinema with kei  ibuki appears  meets sakayanagi at her farewell  she makes two requests  three way meeting with atsuomi  atsuomi meets koenji s father and kijima  reflects on breakup  horikita visits  meets ishizaki and hiyori  ishizaki recruits him to ryuen s class  meets ichinose at night  proposes kaishaku  she reveals her plan  victory celebration  horikita asks about his goal  transfers to class 2 a  meets her farewell  meets him  breaks up with her  discusses exam and goals  meets her at night  meets atsuomi","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y2v12_5-p11-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1–Epilogue: Full volume<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y2V12.5 · p.11–216<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita explains the end-of-year special exam to the class. Reveals Maezono leaked his role as general. Meets Sakayanagi and Ryūen; Sakayanagi reveals Ayanokōji&#x27;s message. Meets Morishita and Yamamura; learns Class A&#x27;s state. Meets Matsushita, Mii-chan, Onodera at Keyaki Mall. Meets Hoshinomiya at a café; she proposes he concede victory. Breaks up with Karuizawa Kei. Date at cinema with Kei; Ibuki appears. Meets Sakayanagi at her farewell; she makes two requests. Three-way meeting with Atsuomi; Atsuomi meets Kōenji&#x27;s father and Kijima. Reflects on breakup; Horikita visits. Meets Ishizaki and Hiyori; Ishizaki recruits him to Ryūen&#x27;s class. Meets Ichinose at night; proposes kaishaku; she reveals her plan. Victory celebration; Horikita asks about his goal. Transfers to Class 2-A.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"tsukishiro.html\">Tsukishiro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Meets her farewell.<span class=\"pg\">p.33, 93–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Meets him.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Breaks up with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.77–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Discusses exam and goals.<span class=\"pg\">p.11–20, 139–147, 192–199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Meets her at night.<span class=\"pg\">p.148–176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsukishiro<\/b> Meets Atsuomi.<span class=\"pg\">p.107–118, 137–138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p29-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune matsushita-chiaki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2   depth read  refusing to explain is at the keyaki mall cafe with hashimoto  morishita and ichinose when horikita and matsushita arrive   i won t deny it  with sakayanagi around  that chance was nonexistent anyway    on becoming a leader candidate  what matsushita just mentioned about being an accompaniment must be a pretext   that s not the case  there have been several instances where you ve skillfully arranged things from behind the scenes when i needed help  even when maezono was expelled  it was because you lent a hand   there s no point in exploring the reasons for the transfer  i haven t told anyone about this  not horikita  not matsushita not anyone in the class   sorry  but i don t feel like answering  the only thing i can make clear is that the fact i moved from class a to class c is real it isn t a dream or an illusion   isn t that more or less the case already    on being called a traitor calm and detached  casually exposes matsushita s secret cooperation and refuses to give horikita any explanation  turns away her demand for a reason  accepts being seen as a traitor and enemy  publicly reveals their behind the scenes cooperation  shaking her composure  states that hashimoto  morishita and ichinose were not surprised by his transfer   implying he told them in advance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 — depth read: refusing to explain<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.29–39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is at the Keyaki Mall café with Hashimoto, Morishita and Ichinose when Horikita and Matsushita arrive.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I won&#x27;t deny it. With Sakayanagi around, that chance was nonexistent anyway.&quot; — on becoming a leader candidate<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What Matsushita just mentioned about being an accompaniment must be a pretext.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s not the case. There have been several instances where you&#x27;ve skillfully arranged things from behind the scenes when I needed help. Even when Maezono was expelled, it was because you lent a hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no point in exploring the reasons for the transfer. I haven&#x27;t told anyone about this, not Horikita, not Matsushita—not anyone in the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, but I don&#x27;t feel like answering. The only thing I can make clear is that the fact I moved from Class A to Class C is real—it isn&#x27;t a dream or an illusion.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn&#x27;t that more or less the case already?&quot; — on being called a traitor<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and detached; casually exposes Matsushita&#x27;s secret cooperation and refuses to give Horikita any explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Turns away her demand for a reason; accepts being seen as a traitor and enemy.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Publicly reveals their behind-the-scenes cooperation, shaking her composure.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> States that Hashimoto, Morishita and Ichinose were not surprised by his transfer — implying he told them in advance.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1\">→ After: Ayanokōji at the café: coldly cutting ties with Class A<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune matsushita-chiaki hashimoto-masayoshi ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ayanokoji at the cafe  coldly cutting ties with class a sits in the keyaki mall cafe with hashimoto  morishita and ichinose  conversing indifferently an hour after the transfer   i won t deny it  with sakayanagi around  that chance was nonexistent anyway   what matsushita just mentioned about being an accompaniment must be a pretext   but in reality  she s quite a schemer   there have been several instances where you ve skillfully arranged things from behind the scenes when i needed help   there s no point in exploring the reasons for the transfer  i haven t told anyone about this  not horikita  not matsushita not anyone in the class   it s scary when a student leaves the class  huh  horikita  deliberately cold   refuses to explain  reveals he told no one in class a  and casually exposes his secret cooperation with matsushita  including maezono s expulsion  making it clear he is no longer their ally and shifting the ground to class c s advantage  blocks her questions  exposes matsushita to rattle her  and tells her there s no point exploring the transfer s reasons  reveals their behind the scenes cooperation  praising her as  one of the sharpest minds in horikita s class  lets him act as gatekeeper  chuckles at his  leader candidate  claim  present at the cafe  she listens with keen interest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ayanokōji at the café: coldly cutting ties with Class A<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.34–38<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits in the Keyaki Mall café with Hashimoto, Morishita and Ichinose, conversing indifferently an hour after the transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"matsushita-chiaki.html\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I won&#x27;t deny it. With Sakayanagi around, that chance was nonexistent anyway.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What Matsushita just mentioned about being an accompaniment must be a pretext.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;But in reality, she&#x27;s quite a schemer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There have been several instances where you&#x27;ve skillfully arranged things from behind the scenes when I needed help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no point in exploring the reasons for the transfer. I haven&#x27;t told anyone about this, not Horikita, not Matsushita—not anyone in the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s scary when a student leaves the class, huh, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately cold — refuses to explain, reveals he told no one in Class A, and casually exposes his secret cooperation with Matsushita (including Maezono&#x27;s expulsion), making it clear he is no longer their ally and shifting the ground to Class C&#x27;s advantage.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Blocks her questions, exposes Matsushita to rattle her, and tells her there&#x27;s no point exploring the transfer&#x27;s reasons.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matsushita Chiaki<\/b> Reveals their behind-the-scenes cooperation, praising her as &quot;one of the sharpest minds in Horikita&#x27;s class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Lets him act as gatekeeper; chuckles at his &quot;leader candidate&quot; claim.<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Present at the café; she listens with keen interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p29-1\">← Before: Ch.2 — depth read: refusing to explain<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 — depth read (half 1): entering Class C<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3   depth read  half 1  entering class c flashback  after the opening ceremony  submits his transfer notice and introduces himself to class 3 c   the opening ceremony just ended  but i  ayanokouji kiyotaka  have transferred to this class using twenty million private points  i can t replace sakayanagi  who voluntarily withdrew  but if there s still a will to fight among everyone here  i m confident that i can help overcome the class s greatly deteriorated situation   glad to have ya  ayanokouji  takes the seat in front of morishita  notes the class s general quality is high but cold toward him  expects cold  skeptical gazes   it would speak poorly of the class if they accepted a  helper  too easily  hashimoto  the biggest investor in his transfer  publicly welcomes him  is seated in front of her at her proposal  she questions his pop culture ignorance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 — depth read (half 1): entering Class C<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.40–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Flashback: after the opening ceremony, submits his transfer notice and introduces himself to Class 3-C. Takes the seat in front of Morishita; notes the class&#x27;s general quality is high but cold toward him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The opening ceremony just ended, but I, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka, have transferred to this class using twenty million Private Points. I can&#x27;t replace Sakayanagi, who voluntarily withdrew, but if there&#x27;s still a will to fight among…<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Glad to have ya, Ayanokouji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The opening ceremony just ended, but I, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka, have transferred to this class using twenty million Private Points. I can&#x27;t replace Sakayanagi, who voluntarily withdrew, but if there&#x27;s still a will to fight among everyone here, I&#x27;m confident that I can help overcome the class&#x27;s greatly deteriorated situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Expects cold, skeptical gazes — it would speak poorly of the class if they accepted a &quot;helper&quot; too easily.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Hashimoto, the biggest investor in his transfer, publicly welcomes him.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Is seated in front of her at her proposal; she questions his pop-culture ignorance.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p34-1\">← Before: Ayanokōji at the café: coldly cutting ties with Class A<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-2\">→ After: Ch.3 — depth read (half 2): the confrontation behind the dorm<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-2","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken yukimura-teruhiko miyake-akito ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3   depth read  half 2  the confrontation behind the dorm  yeah  sorry    to sudo  confirming the transfer was his own free will  worry and confusion  huh  well  that s right  i transferred classes without telling anyone to get that reaction   just take it at face value  i didn t say anything because i wanted to trouble the class  and my reason that you wanted to hear is simple  class c was in trouble without sakayanagi  so  i chose to help by transferring in exchange for private points   you can rest assured  it s purely  100  a transfer solely for my own benefit   nothing    to hirata s question of whether he has anything to tell the class coldly indifferent on the surface  deliberately gives a self serving explanation to avoid troubling them  keeping the true motive hidden  is questioned by him  who ultimately accepts the choice  notes hirata s new distrust and his odd use of  kiyotaka  faces his anger  sudo insists he is important to the class and offers to pool money to bring him back  keisei says ayanokoji saved him and asks whether there were hidden circumstances  akito relays hasebe s guilt and says they remain friends  hashimoto notes ayanokoji deliberately timed the transfer just after the ceremony to maximise the shock to class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 — depth read (half 2): the confrontation behind the dorm<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.40–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"yukimura-teruhiko.html\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. Sorry.&quot; — to Sudō, confirming the transfer was his own free will<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Worry and confusion, huh? Well, that&#x27;s right. I transferred classes without telling anyone to get that reaction.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just take it at face value. I didn&#x27;t say anything because I wanted to trouble the class. And my reason that you wanted to hear is simple. Class C was in trouble without Sakayanagi. So, I chose to help by transferring in exchange…<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just take it at face value. I didn&#x27;t say anything because I wanted to trouble the class. And my reason that you wanted to hear is simple. Class C was in trouble without Sakayanagi. So, I chose to help by transferring in exchange for Private Points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can rest assured. It&#x27;s purely, 100%, a transfer solely for my own benefit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing.&quot; — to Hirata&#x27;s question of whether he has anything to tell the class<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly indifferent on the surface; deliberately gives a self-serving explanation to avoid troubling them, keeping the true motive hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Is questioned by him, who ultimately accepts the choice; notes Hirata&#x27;s new distrust and his odd use of &quot;Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Faces his anger; Sudō insists he is important to the class and offers to pool money to bring him back.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Keisei says Ayanokōji saved him and asks whether there were hidden circumstances.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Akito relays Hasebe&#x27;s guilt and says they remain friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Hashimoto notes Ayanokōji deliberately timed the transfer just after the ceremony to maximise the shock to Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 — depth read (half 1): entering Class C<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-3\">→ After: Arriving in Class C; Morishita seats him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-3","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"morishita-ai hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka arriving in class c  morishita seats him after submitting his transfer notice to the chairman  stands before class c and introduces himself   the opening ceremony just ended  but i  ayanokouji kiyotaka  have transferred to this class using twenty million private points   i can t replace sakayanagi  who voluntarily withdrew  but if there s still a will to fight among everyone here  i m confident that i can help overcome the class s greatly deteriorated situation  hashimoto   the biggest investor in his transfer   applauds first   glad to have ya  ayanokouji  most others watch with cold  skeptical gazes  which he judges is a sign of the class s quality  morishita proposes he sit in front of her  center ish  easily surveilled  not the coveted back window seat  sugio eagerly gives it up   about what s to come  carefully chooses his words  reflecting on his failed first year self introduction  reads the class as high quality but cautious and easy to navigate  she arranges his seat in front of her and peppers him with jokes  making 100 friends  eating onigiri with 100 people    classic references he doesn t know  the transfer s biggest investor  publicly welcomes him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-3\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Arriving in Class C; Morishita seats him<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.40–44<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After submitting his transfer notice to the chairman, stands before Class C and introduces himself.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The opening ceremony just ended, but I, Ayanokouji Kiyotaka, have transferred to this class using twenty million Private Points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t replace Sakayanagi, who voluntarily withdrew, but if there&#x27;s still a will to fight among everyone here, I&#x27;m confident that I can help overcome the class&#x27;s greatly deteriorated situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;About what&#x27;s to come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hashimoto — the biggest investor in his transfer — applauds first: &quot;Glad to have ya, Ayanokouji&quot;; most others watch with cold, skeptical gazes, which he judges is a sign of the class&#x27;s quality.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Morishita proposes he sit in front of her (center-ish, easily surveilled, not the coveted back window seat); Sugio eagerly gives it up.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Carefully chooses his words, reflecting on his failed first-year self-introduction; reads the class as high-quality but cautious and easy to navigate.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> She arranges his seat in front of her and peppers him with jokes (making 100 friends, eating onigiri with 100 people) — classic references he doesn&#x27;t know.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> The transfer&#x27;s biggest investor; publicly welcomes him.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-2\">← Before: Ch.3 — depth read (half 2): the confrontation behind the dorm<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1\">→ After: The rejected welcome party<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the rejected welcome party hashimoto proposes a flashy welcome party at keyaki mall  the room goes tense   it s natural that they can t welcome me wholeheartedly   well  maybe  sits as a bystander  unable to ask for or refuse the party  notes the awkwardness is about him  and accepts morishita s blunt observation that he is  spectacularly unpopular  tries to throw him a welcome party  yoshida  machida and others refuse  saying he must prove his worth first  tells him he is  leftover merchandise  unpopular  and that if ichinose or kushida had transferred they d be surrounded by smiles","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The rejected welcome party<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.45–48<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hashimoto proposes a flashy welcome party at Keyaki Mall; the room goes tense.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s natural that they can&#x27;t welcome me wholeheartedly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;…Well… maybe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sits as a bystander, unable to ask for or refuse the party; notes the awkwardness is about him, and accepts Morishita&#x27;s blunt observation that he is &quot;spectacularly unpopular.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45–48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Tries to throw him a welcome party; Yoshida, Machida and others refuse, saying he must prove his worth first.<span class=\"pg\">p.45–48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Tells him he is &quot;leftover merchandise,&quot; unpopular, and that if Ichinose or Kushida had transferred they&#x27;d be surrounded by smiles.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p40-3\">← Before: Arriving in Class C; Morishita seats him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1\">→ After: The contract with Hashimoto; reason for transferring via Class A money<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the contract with hashimoto  reason for transferring via class a money  it s only a matter of time   i told you when we talked about the transfer  i won t guarantee anything when making decisions   i m worried about being betrayed like sakayanagi   for this transfer  class c s unanimous consent was a must  there were things i couldn t entrust to you and your problematic issues  he gave hashimoto a choice  give up his fortune and accept him  or forgo accepting him entirely   knowing hashimoto s sunk cost investment and risky position made accepting the only rational choice  coldly strategic   keeps hashimoto slightly tense  withholds strategy  and brought morishita in because her doubts forced him to share information hashimoto couldn t be trusted with  discusses the transfer  the money  and his risks  hashimoto insists he s  all in  penniless  she followed them  calls him the  embodiment of unpopularity  and attacks on  presence popularity  wordplay  she joins to verify the alliance with ichinose","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The contract with Hashimoto; reason for transferring via Class A money<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.49–54<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s only a matter of time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I told you when we talked about the transfer. I won&#x27;t guarantee anything when making decisions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m worried about being betrayed like Sakayanagi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For this transfer, Class C&#x27;s unanimous consent was a must. There were things I couldn&#x27;t entrust to you and your problematic issues.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He gave Hashimoto a choice: give up his fortune and accept him, or forgo accepting him entirely — knowing Hashimoto&#x27;s sunk-cost investment and risky position made accepting the only rational choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly strategic — keeps Hashimoto slightly tense, withholds strategy, and brought Morishita in because her doubts forced him to share information Hashimoto couldn&#x27;t be trusted with.<span class=\"pg\">p.49–54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Discusses the transfer, the money, and his risks; Hashimoto insists he&#x27;s &quot;all in... penniless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> She followed them, calls him the &quot;embodiment of unpopularity&quot; and attacks on &quot;presence&quot;/&quot;popularity&quot; wordplay; she joins to verify the alliance with Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p45-1\">← Before: The rejected welcome party<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1\">→ After: The café: explaining the alliance; the delayed reveal to Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafe  explaining the alliance  the delayed reveal to horikita  it s because for the next year  as class c aims for class a  ichinose and her class s cooperation is essential   indeed  i m serious  in fact  ichinose and i have formed a complete alliance   forming an alliance isn t just about yielding to each other and not fighting   a tightly bound contract can sometimes be a fatal blow   it s more effective when we make it known   for them to learn about it once the wound of the transfer has healed a bit  that will hurt them more deeply  explains the alliance s logic  doubled information  coordinated private points  no binding contract  allowing flexibility  and mutual concession only while the classes are unequal  deliberately delays telling horikita to maximize the psychological damage  ruthless toward horikita   his true goal is not her downfall but her growth  trusting her classmates will help her recover  uses lip service for hashimoto s benefit  reveals their complete alliance  she explains the arrangement of conceding victory to whichever class has fewer points  based on equality and trust  no contract  answers his skeptical questions  hashimoto calls ichinose a  burden  and probes what return she wants  skeptical of the alliance  argues conceding victories throws away opportunities  and that hashimoto would oppose the plan if he weren t invested","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The café: explaining the alliance; the delayed reveal to Horikita<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.55–65<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s because for the next year, as Class C aims for Class A, Ichinose and her class&#x27;s cooperation is essential.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Indeed, I&#x27;m serious. In fact, Ichinose and I have formed a complete alliance.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Forming an alliance isn&#x27;t just about yielding to each other and not fighting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A tightly bound contract can sometimes be a fatal blow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s more effective when we make it known.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;for them to learn about it once the wound of the transfer has healed a bit. That will hurt them more deeply.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Explains the alliance&#x27;s logic: doubled information, coordinated Private Points, no binding contract (allowing flexibility), and mutual concession only while the classes are unequal; deliberately delays telling Horikita to maximize the psychological damage.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ruthless toward Horikita — his true goal is not her downfall but her growth, trusting her classmates will help her recover; uses lip service for Hashimoto&#x27;s benefit.<span class=\"pg\">p.64–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Reveals their complete alliance; she explains the arrangement of conceding victory to whichever class has fewer points, based on equality and trust, no contract.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Answers his skeptical questions; Hashimoto calls Ichinose a &quot;burden&quot; and probes what return she wants.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Skeptical of the alliance; argues conceding victories throws away opportunities, and that Hashimoto would oppose the plan if he weren&#x27;t invested.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p49-1\">← Before: The contract with Hashimoto; reason for transferring via Class A money<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1\">→ After: Aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke sudou-ken ike-kanji miyake-akito ishigami-kyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates  i m aware of that  sooner or later  there will be students who voice their opinions against me   i didn t say anything because i wanted to trouble the class   class c was in trouble without sakayanagi  so  i chose to help by transferring in exchange for private points   nothing  times the transfer for immediately after the opening ceremony to maximize class a s shock  tells his former friends the transfer was selfish and for private points   a contrived half truth  since he wanted that reaction  cold and indifferent to their pleas   gives them no real reason  calls his departure voluntary  and accepts hirata s respectful withdrawal  notes he and hirata had been intentionally distancing by first last name  he approaches privately  later respectfully accepts that kiyotaka left on his own free will and departs  having grown to distrust him somewhat  he demands to know why  ayanokoji says there s no meaning in answering  sudo is left frustrated  blames the karuizawa breakup  confused why class c would pay 20 million for him  asks the real reason and notes hasebe was heartbroken  blaming herself  keisei says ayanokoji saved him  he might not have stayed at the school  and asks for the full story","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.66–74<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"miyake-akito.html\">Miyake Akito<\/a> · <a href=\"ishigami-kyou.html\">Ishigami Kyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m aware of that. Sooner or later, there will be students who voice their opinions against me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I didn&#x27;t say anything because I wanted to trouble the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Class C was in trouble without Sakayanagi. So, I chose to help by transferring in exchange for Private Points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Times the transfer for immediately after the opening ceremony to maximize Class A&#x27;s shock; tells his former friends the transfer was selfish and for Private Points — a contrived half-truth, since he wanted that reaction.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cold and indifferent to their pleas — gives them no real reason, calls his departure voluntary, and accepts Hirata&#x27;s respectful withdrawal; notes he and Hirata had been intentionally distancing by first/last name.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He approaches privately; later respectfully accepts that Kiyotaka left on his own free will and departs, having grown to distrust him somewhat.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> He demands to know why; Ayanokōji says there&#x27;s no meaning in answering; Sudō is left frustrated.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Blames the Karuizawa breakup; confused why Class C would pay 20 million for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Miyake Akito<\/b> Asks the real reason and notes Hasebe was heartbroken, blaming herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishigami Kyō<\/b> Keisei says Ayanokōji saved him (he might not have stayed at the school) and asks for the full story.<span class=\"pg\">p.70–72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p55-1\">← Before: The café: explaining the alliance; the delayed reveal to Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1\">→ After: Ch.4 — depth read: observing Class C and the Shiraishi talk<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka yoshida-kenta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4   depth read  observing class c and the shiraishi talk arrives at class 3 c thirty minutes early to observe the students directly  not just through oaa  finds shiraishi already there   i didn t expect someone to be here already  you re rather early   since i ve switched classes  it s like i m a transfer student from a different school  rather than being welcomed  i thought it d be better to be the one doing the welcoming   that might be true under normal circumstances   hashimoto and the others should ve explained it to you  i came to this class as reinforcement   it s too late to start now  couldn t you have opposed and refused my transfer   i ll take you up on that offer    accepting shiraishi s offer to introduce friends deliberately mixes truths while probing shiraishi  notes he finds starting conversations harder than expected and compares himself unfavourably with hirata  has his first real conversation with her  she presses on his motive and offers to introduce him to friends  yoshida offers to help him fit in after shiraishi s needling  shiraishi s oaa  academics b   76  physical d  34  adaptability c   57  social contribution c   44  overall c  54","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 — depth read: observing Class C and the Shiraishi talk<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.75–97<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives at Class 3-C thirty minutes early to observe the students directly, not just through OAA; finds Shiraishi already there.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I didn&#x27;t expect someone to be here already. You&#x27;re rather early.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Since I&#x27;ve switched classes, it&#x27;s like I&#x27;m a transfer student from a different school. Rather than being welcomed, I thought it&#x27;d be better to be the one doing the welcoming.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That might be true under normal circumstances.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hashimoto and the others should&#x27;ve explained it to you. I came to this class as reinforcement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s too late to start now. Couldn&#x27;t you have opposed and refused my transfer?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll take you up on that offer.&quot; — accepting Shiraishi&#x27;s offer to introduce friends<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately mixes truths while probing Shiraishi; notes he finds starting conversations harder than expected and compares himself unfavourably with Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Has his first real conversation with her; she presses on his motive and offers to introduce him to friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Yoshida offers to help him fit in after Shiraishi&#x27;s needling.<span class=\"pg\">p.82–83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Shiraishi&#x27;s OAA: Academics B+ (76), Physical D (34), Adaptability C+ (57), Social Contribution C– (44), Overall C (54).<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p66-1\">← Before: Aftermath and the confrontation with former classmates<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-2\">→ After: Getting to know Shiraishi; the morning conversation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-2","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka yoshida-kenta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka getting to know shiraishi  the morning conversation arrives 30  minutes early to observe class c  finds shiraishi already at the desk beside his  shiraishi s oaa  academic b   76  physical d  34  adaptability c   57  social c   44  overall c  54  noted beauty mark under her left eye  long blonde hair  headband  calm aura   i didn t expect someone to be here already  you re rather early   since i ve switched classes  it s like i m a transfer student from a different school  rather than being welcomed  i thought it d be better to be the one doing the welcoming   that s only natural   it s too late to start now  couldn t you have opposed and refused my transfer  deliberately mixes truths to probe her  finds it harder to talk than expected  unlike hirata  and learns she holds him in high regard with high expectations  accepts her offer to introduce friends  his new desk neighbor  has a long morning conversation  learns her views  and accepts her offer to meet her friends  yoshida arrives  is needled by shiraishi into retracting his  acknowledge him  demand and helping ayanokoji fit in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Getting to know Shiraishi; the morning conversation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.75–84<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives 30+ minutes early to observe Class C; finds Shiraishi already at the desk beside his.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I didn&#x27;t expect someone to be here already. You&#x27;re rather early.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Since I&#x27;ve switched classes, it&#x27;s like I&#x27;m a transfer student from a different school. Rather than being welcomed, I thought it&#x27;d be better to be the one doing the welcoming.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s only natural.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Shiraishi&#x27;s OAA: Academic B+ (76), Physical D (34), Adaptability C+ (57), Social C− (44), Overall C (54); noted beauty mark under her left eye, long blonde hair, headband, calm aura.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s too late to start now. Couldn&#x27;t you have opposed and refused my transfer?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately mixes truths to probe her, finds it harder to talk than expected (unlike Hirata), and learns she holds him in high regard with high expectations; accepts her offer to introduce friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> His new desk neighbor; has a long morning conversation, learns her views, and accepts her offer to meet her friends.<span class=\"pg\">p.75–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Yoshida arrives, is needled by Shiraishi into retracting his &quot;acknowledge him&quot; demand and helping Ayanokōji fit in.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-1\">← Before: Ch.4 — depth read: observing Class C and the Shiraishi talk<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1\">→ After: Hōsen&#x27;s challenge; Chabashira&#x27;s tailing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"housen-kazuomi chabashira-sae nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hosen s challenge  chabashira s tailing  sorry  but i m not interested in fighting   if that s what you re looking for  you should ask ryuuen   nanase seems more capable of being a solid leader than you  housen   i thought you might think that way  chabashira sensei   this transfer is entirely for my own sake  declines hosen s challenge  a  punching bag  search  notes he delegated class leadership to nanase  and repeatedly deflects chabashira s probing about the transfer s true reason  tells her it wasn t because of hoshinomiya and won t disclose his task  second year class d  approaches aggressively  calls him  paisen  wants a fight  and threatens to return for a  sparring partner  his former homeroom teacher has been tailing him in the cold mornings  confronts him  suspects he sacrificed himself over hoshinomiya   he denies it  hosen says he s delegated class matters to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hōsen&#x27;s challenge; Chabashira&#x27;s tailing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.85–89<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"housen-kazuomi.html\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sorry, but I&#x27;m not interested in fighting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If that&#x27;s what you&#x27;re looking for, you should ask Ryuuen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Nanase seems more capable of being a solid leader than you, Housen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.87<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I thought you might think that way, Chabashira-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This transfer is entirely for my own sake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Declines Hōsen&#x27;s challenge (a &quot;punching bag&quot; search), notes he delegated class leadership to Nanase, and repeatedly deflects Chabashira&#x27;s probing about the transfer&#x27;s true reason; tells her it wasn&#x27;t because of Hoshinomiya and won&#x27;t disclose his task.<span class=\"pg\">p.85–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hōsen Kazuomi<\/b> Second-year Class D; approaches aggressively, calls him &quot;Paisen,&quot; wants a fight, and threatens to return for a &quot;sparring partner.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.85–87<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> His former homeroom teacher has been tailing him in the cold mornings; confronts him, suspects he sacrificed himself over Hoshinomiya — he denies it.<span class=\"pg\">p.87–89<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Hōsen says he&#x27;s delegated class matters to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p75-2\">← Before: Getting to know Shiraishi; the morning conversation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p98-1\">→ After: Ch.5 — depth read: taking charge and planning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p98-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi shimazaki-ikkei ryuuen-kakeru morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5   depth read  taking charge and planning in class c  is asked to take charge of the special exam  plays down his chances deliberately to sound safe   i can t guarantee our victory or defeat  but if you entrust me with it  i intend to give it my all   whether it s the dorm  karaoke  or behind the school building  i ll join you    proposing a meeting place  i can t talk about that at this point yet  saying anything careless here and having them taken at face value would be troublesome   there s no particular reason  sakayanagi left  and class c came to help me transfer  plans to win by accurately predicting which opponents receive penalty points  judges that hitting two of the five small group participants would prove his read and win the class over  told yamamura to keep her distance so the transfer s attention would not stress her  wants to nurture her as an asset at her own pace  entrusted with the exam  strategizes with him at the cafe  shimazaki resists entrusting him but agrees to the compromise  is told ryuen welcomes the chance to defeat him now that he leads class c directly  strategizes with her  she questions his plans and yamamura s involvement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p98-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 — depth read: taking charge and planning<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.98–145<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In Class C, is asked to take charge of the special exam; plays down his chances deliberately to sound safe.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t guarantee our victory or defeat, but if you entrust me with it, I intend to give it my all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Whether it&#x27;s the dorm, karaoke, or behind the school building, I&#x27;ll join you.&quot; — proposing a meeting place<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t talk about that at this point yet. Saying anything careless here and having them taken at face value would be troublesome.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no particular reason. Sakayanagi left, and Class C came to help me transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Plans to win by accurately predicting which opponents receive penalty points; judges that hitting two of the five small-group participants would prove his read and win the class over.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Told Yamamura to keep her distance so the transfer&#x27;s attention would not stress her; wants to nurture her as an asset at her own pace.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Entrusted with the exam; strategizes with him at the café.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Shimazaki resists entrusting him but agrees to the compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Is told Ryūen welcomes the chance to defeat him now that he leads Class C directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Strategizes with her; she questions his plans and Yamamura&#x27;s involvement.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p85-1\">← Before: Hōsen&#x27;s challenge; Chabashira&#x27;s tailing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1\">→ After: Class C entrusts the exam to Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi shimazaki-ikkei sanada-kousei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka class c entrusts the exam to ayanokoji  i can t guarantee our victory or defeat  but if you entrust me with it  i intend to give it my all   if you entrust it to me  i ll do my best  hashimoto pushes to leave the exam to him  shimazaki objects  wanting class discussion  sanada proposes a compromise   test him by seeing whether he can predict the opponent s small group participants and penalty distribution  deliberately plays it safe with his words  unlike his confident opening ceremony speech  to avoid a unanimous delegation  accepting the  test  framing  pushes fiercely for ayanokoji to lead  agitated about being excluded from the transfer talks  skeptical  doesn t want to entrust the exam to him  proposes judging him by his prediction accuracy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Class C entrusts the exam to Ayanokōji<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.108–110<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"sanada-kousei.html\">Sanada Kōsei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t guarantee our victory or defeat, but if you entrust me with it, I intend to give it my all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you entrust it to me, I&#x27;ll do my best.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hashimoto pushes to leave the exam to him; Shimazaki objects, wanting class discussion; Sanada proposes a compromise — test him by seeing whether he can predict the opponent&#x27;s small-group participants and penalty distribution.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately plays it safe with his words (unlike his confident opening-ceremony speech) to avoid a unanimous delegation, accepting the &quot;test&quot; framing.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Pushes fiercely for Ayanokōji to lead; agitated about being excluded from the transfer talks.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Skeptical; doesn&#x27;t want to entrust the exam to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sanada Kōsei<\/b> Proposes judging him by his prediction accuracy.<span class=\"pg\">p.109<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p98-1\">← Before: Ch.5 — depth read: taking charge and planning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1\">→ After: The café strategy: penalty points, spies, and withheld info<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"morishita-ai yamamura-miki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafe strategy  penalty points  spies  and withheld info  i ve already given yamamura a heads up  it s better for her to keep her distance from me for a while   i can t talk about that at this point yet  saying anything careless here and having them taken at face value would be troublesome   i don t know a thing about it   there s still time until the exam  all i have to do is come up with a winning strategy by then   i have no intention of participating in the small group battles in this special exam   there s an eighty to ninety percent chance ryuuen will impose multiple penalty points on me  identifies komiya yamawaki and two first years  including takikura  as ryuen s surveillance   the first years  phones placed face down toward them  never checked  deduces ryuen has been recruiting first years within a week  withholds real analysis  only shares  safe  information  reasons that ryuen will target him so he needn t participate  and reads the enemy s spy network sharply  discusses yamamura  has told her to keep her distance  morishita joins as a listener and needles him  has told her to keep her distance so she isn t stressed by the attention around him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The café strategy: penalty points, spies, and withheld info<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.112–121<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a> · <a href=\"yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve already given Yamamura a heads-up. It&#x27;s better for her to keep her distance from me for a while.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t talk about that at this point yet. Saying anything careless here and having them taken at face value would be troublesome.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t know a thing about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s still time until the exam. All I have to do is come up with a winning strategy by then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have no intention of participating in the small-group battles in this special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s an eighty to ninety percent chance Ryuuen will impose multiple penalty points on me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Identifies Komiya/Yamawaki and two first-years (including Takikura) as Ryūen&#x27;s surveillance — the first-years&#x27; phones placed face-down toward them, never checked; deduces Ryūen has been recruiting first-years within a week.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Withholds real analysis (only shares &quot;safe&quot; information), reasons that Ryūen will target him so he needn&#x27;t participate, and reads the enemy&#x27;s spy network sharply.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Discusses Yamamura (has told her to keep her distance); Morishita joins as a listener and needles him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Has told her to keep her distance so she isn&#x27;t stressed by the attention around him.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p108-1\">← Before: Class C entrusts the exam to Ayanokōji<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1\">→ After: Ryūen and Ishizaki confront him at the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ryuen and ishizaki confront him at the cafe  there s no particular reason  sakayanagi left  and class c came to help me transfer   does my transferring to class c cause any inconvenience to you   my class expects results in the upcoming special exam  please go easy on us   i intend to    on seeing shiina faces ryuen calmly  gives the same  no reason  line  and privately notes ryuen welcomed the transfer as a better stage to defeat him  has deliberately avoided the library and decides to see hiyori after the exam  he comes to the cafe with ishizaki and albert  welcomes the transfer because now ayanokoji leads class c directly  and vows to play every card  explodes demanding why he transferred  leaves frustrated  tells him to meet shiina  who s been down  ishizaki s message about shiina being down is what ayanokoji uses to decide to visit the library after the exam","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ryūen and Ishizaki confront him at the café<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.122–125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ishizaki-daichi.html\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s no particular reason. Sakayanagi left, and Class C came to help me transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Does my transferring to Class C cause any inconvenience to you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My class expects results in the upcoming special exam. Please go easy on us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I intend to.&quot; — on seeing Shiina<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Faces Ryūen calmly, gives the same &quot;no reason&quot; line, and privately notes Ryūen welcomed the transfer as a better stage to defeat him; has deliberately avoided the library and decides to see Hiyori after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> He comes to the café with Ishizaki and Albert; welcomes the transfer because now Ayanokōji leads Class C directly, and vows to play every card.<span class=\"pg\">p.122–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Explodes demanding why he transferred; leaves frustrated, tells him to meet Shiina (who&#x27;s been down).<span class=\"pg\">p.122–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ishizaki&#x27;s message about Shiina being down is what Ayanokōji uses to decide to visit the library after the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p112-1\">← Before: The café strategy: penalty points, spies, and withheld info<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.6 — depth read: new friendships and the eraser prank<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"yoshida-kenta shiraishi-asuka nishikawa-ryouko morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6   depth read  new friendships and the eraser prank  so are you  yoshida   do you like shiraishi   unfortunately  i don t have those types of feelings for her   there are things i can t ask hashimoto about   sorry  but if that s true  i d refuse   sorry  but let go of my hand  yoshida might see and misinterpret our relationship  reads social situations better than before  credits his time with karuizawa  politely declines nishikawa s bait and shiraishi s advances to protect his position  confronts his feelings for shiraishi  asks him for the class s evaluation of hashimoto  at karaoke  keeps his distance despite her closeness  sees her curiosity  not affection  refuses her whispered offer  earns her hostility  catches her throwing eraser crumbs at him after shiraishi tips him off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 — depth read: new friendships and the eraser prank<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.146–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"nishikawa-ryouko.html\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So are you, Yoshida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Do you like Shiraishi?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Unfortunately, I don&#x27;t have those types of feelings for her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There are things I can&#x27;t ask Hashimoto about.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, but if that&#x27;s true, I&#x27;d refuse.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, but let go of my hand. Yoshida might see and misinterpret our relationship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads social situations better than before (credits his time with Karuizawa); politely declines Nishikawa&#x27;s bait and Shiraishi&#x27;s advances to protect his position.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Confronts his feelings for Shiraishi; asks him for the class&#x27;s evaluation of Hashimoto.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> At karaoke, keeps his distance despite her closeness; sees her curiosity, not affection.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/b> Refuses her whispered offer; earns her hostility.<span class=\"pg\">p.148–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Catches her throwing eraser crumbs at him after Shiraishi tips him off.<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p122-1\">← Before: Ryūen and Ishizaki confront him at the café<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-2\">→ After: The Sunday karaoke outing; Nishikawa&#x27;s warnings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-2","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"yoshida-kenta nishikawa-ryouko shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the sunday karaoke outing  nishikawa s warnings meets yoshida outside the dorm for the outing  yoshida has been waiting since 9 30 for a 10 30 meeting   that rumor s real    yoshida nishikawa joins in place of shiraishi initially  warns that shiraishi is the  hundred man slayer   romantically involved with a hundred guys    advice  for ayanokouji kun too   i ve come to respect her  it s honestly amazing for someone my age to be involved with a hundred people  reads yoshida s infatuation calmly  learning about romance through karuizawa  probes the class s view of hashimoto  and refuses nishikawa s bait to become shiraishi s 101st   because word could reach yoshida and hinder his class c battles  confirms he likes shiraishi  asks about the class and hashimoto s reputation  she teases him about shiraishi and makes a suggestive offer he refuses  she ends up reconsidering her impression of him with something like hostility  sits beside her in the karaoke l seating  she touches his hand  examines his long fingers nails  and treats him as an interesting experimental subject  like a guinea pig in a small box","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Sunday karaoke outing; Nishikawa&#x27;s warnings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.146–154<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Yoshida outside the dorm for the outing; Yoshida has been waiting since 9:30 for a 10:30 meeting.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a> · <a href=\"nishikawa-ryouko.html\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That rumor&#x27;s real…?&quot; — Yoshida<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ve come to respect her. It&#x27;s honestly amazing for someone my age to be involved with a hundred people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Nishikawa joins in place of Shiraishi initially; warns that Shiraishi is the &quot;Hundred-Man Slayer&quot; (romantically involved with a hundred guys) — advice &quot;for Ayanokouji-kun too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Yoshida&#x27;s infatuation calmly (learning about romance through Karuizawa), probes the class&#x27;s view of Hashimoto, and refuses Nishikawa&#x27;s bait to become Shiraishi&#x27;s 101st — because word could reach Yoshida and hinder his Class C battles.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Confirms he likes Shiraishi; asks about the class and Hashimoto&#x27;s reputation.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/b> She teases him about Shiraishi and makes a suggestive offer he refuses; she ends up reconsidering her impression of him with something like hostility.<span class=\"pg\">p.148–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Sits beside her in the karaoke L-seating; she touches his hand, examines his long fingers/nails, and treats him as an interesting experimental subject, like a guinea pig in a small box.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.6 — depth read: new friendships and the eraser prank<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1\">→ After: The eraser-crumb prank; Shiraishi signals the timing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the eraser crumb prank  shiraishi signals the timing during self study  feels an uncomfortable sensation in his hair   morishita behind him is rubbing an eraser on the desk and throwing crumbs at his head   you saved me  shiraishi  thanks to you telling me the timing  i caught her red handed  shiraishi silently signals the timing of the eraser taps by pointing at the floor and tapping her desk  he grabs morishita s clenched fist and finds the worn eraser  sharp sensing and composed   uses shiraishi s silent cues to catch morishita  declines to call it  bullying  and learns sugio had given up his seat because of the same trouble  she silently signals the prank s timing to help him  he thanks her and calls her  impressive  catches her throwing eraser crumbs  she plays ignorant and justifies it as  jeanne d arc  defeating evil","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The eraser-crumb prank; Shiraishi signals the timing<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.156–162<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">During self-study, feels an uncomfortable sensation in his hair — Morishita behind him is rubbing an eraser on the desk and throwing crumbs at his head.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You saved me, Shiraishi. Thanks to you telling me the timing, I caught her red-handed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Shiraishi silently signals the timing of the eraser-taps by pointing at the floor and tapping her desk; he grabs Morishita&#x27;s clenched fist and finds the worn eraser.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sharp-sensing and composed — uses Shiraishi&#x27;s silent cues to catch Morishita, declines to call it &quot;bullying,&quot; and learns Sugio had given up his seat because of the same trouble.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> She silently signals the prank&#x27;s timing to help him; he thanks her and calls her &quot;impressive.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157–162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Catches her throwing eraser crumbs; she plays ignorant and justifies it as &quot;Jeanne d&#x27;Arc&quot; defeating evil.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p146-2\">← Before: The Sunday karaoke outing; Nishikawa&#x27;s warnings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.7 — depth read: zero predictions, still acknowledged<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p163-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"shimazaki-ikkei ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7   depth read  zero predictions  still acknowledged  give me a break  ryuuen  i m busy today   according to shimazaki  the outcome doesn t matter  what mattered was my precision in selecting the right students to assign the penalty points to in the small group battles  unfortunately  i couldn t identify any of the students you nominated   ryuuen  considering that s your take on it  aren t your senses a bit too numb   the key to victory lies in the small group battles  scored a perfect 100 on the exam but received 100 penalty points  losing his small group bout to ishizaki   class c still won 6 1  explains that predicting participants is meaningless when the opponent does not take the exam seriously  ryuen fielded predictable names  confronted over missing all five predictions  shimazaki ultimately acknowledges him as leader regardless  ryuen barges in and taunts him  he fires back that ryuen s senses are  numb  credits her courage in trusting his advice for class d s win","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 — depth read: zero predictions, still acknowledged<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.163–202<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Give me a break, Ryuuen. I&#x27;m busy today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;According to Shimazaki, the outcome doesn&#x27;t matter; what mattered was my precision in selecting the right students to assign the penalty points to in the small-group battles. Unfortunately, I couldn&#x27;t identify any of the…<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ryuuen, considering that&#x27;s your take on it, aren&#x27;t your senses a bit too numb?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;According to Shimazaki, the outcome doesn&#x27;t matter; what mattered was my precision in selecting the right students to assign the penalty points to in the small-group battles. Unfortunately, I couldn&#x27;t identify any of the students you nominated.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The key to victory lies in the small-group battles.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Scored a perfect 100 on the exam but received 100 penalty points, losing his small-group bout to Ishizaki — Class C still won 6–1.<span class=\"pg\">p.185–186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Explains that predicting participants is meaningless when the opponent does not take the exam seriously (Ryūen fielded predictable names).<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Confronted over missing all five predictions; Shimazaki ultimately acknowledges him as leader regardless.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen barges in and taunts him; he fires back that Ryūen&#x27;s senses are &quot;numb.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189–193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Credits her courage in trusting his advice for Class D&#x27;s win.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p156-1\">← Before: The eraser-crumb prank; Shiraishi signals the timing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1\">→ After: The aftermath: Shimazaki&#x27;s challenge and Ayanokōji&#x27;s true plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru shimazaki-ikkei hashimoto-masayoshi ichinose-honami morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the aftermath  shimazaki s challenge and ayanokoji s true plan  calm down  shimazaki  we won the exam  so it s all the same in the end   give me a break  ryuuen  i m busy today   the key to victory lies in the small group battles   what i really had to see through wasn t your irrational selection after you chose to abandon thinking  but the essence of the opponent your very aim   ryuuen  did this turn out the way you wanted it to   an alliance brings various benefits  his true aim wasn t penalty point accuracy but a demonstrative loss   taking all 100 penalty points and a perfect 100 score to show class c his ability and that ryuen feared him  predicted ryuen would abandon the academic fight and delay his leadership  and deliberately fed that via leaked  tasks  to the first year spies  coldly calculating   enters the small group battle assuming defeat because he  had to see through  ryuen s aim  not his lineup  turns the enemy s surveillance into a channel for his own message  ryuen barges in for a  winner s interview  ayanokoji reveals he read his intent and turned it against him  ryuen leaves  outmaneuvered  shimazaki confronts him over 0 5 penalty accuracy but ultimately acknowledges him  welcome to class c  they shake hands  he mediates  ayanokoji later explains the plan to him and morishita  reveals he had ichinose quietly gather intel on the first years  her cross class trust made her ideal  enabling the alliance s win  explains the plan  she had been skeptical about the first years being ryuen s spies","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The aftermath: Shimazaki&#x27;s challenge and Ayanokōji&#x27;s true plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.189–198<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Calm down, Shimazaki. We won the exam, so it&#x27;s all the same in the end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Give me a break, Ryuuen. I&#x27;m busy today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The key to victory lies in the small-group battles.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What I really had to see through wasn&#x27;t your irrational selection after you chose to abandon thinking, but the essence of the opponent—your very aim.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ryuuen, did this turn out the way you wanted it to?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;An alliance brings various benefits.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> His true aim wasn&#x27;t penalty-point accuracy but a demonstrative loss — taking all 100 penalty points and a perfect 100 score to show Class C his ability and that Ryūen feared him; predicted Ryūen would abandon the academic fight and delay his leadership, and deliberately fed that via leaked &quot;tasks&quot; to the first-year spies.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly calculating — enters the small-group battle assuming defeat because he &quot;had to see through&quot; Ryūen&#x27;s aim, not his lineup; turns the enemy&#x27;s surveillance into a channel for his own message.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Ryūen barges in for a &quot;winner&#x27;s interview&quot;; Ayanokōji reveals he read his intent and turned it against him; Ryūen leaves, outmaneuvered.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Shimazaki confronts him over 0/5 penalty accuracy but ultimately acknowledges him (&quot;welcome to Class C&quot;); they shake hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He mediates; Ayanokōji later explains the plan to him and Morishita.<span class=\"pg\">p.189–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Reveals he had Ichinose quietly gather intel on the first-years (her cross-class trust made her ideal), enabling the alliance&#x27;s win.<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Explains the plan; she had been skeptical about the first-years being Ryūen&#x27;s spies.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.7 — depth read: zero predictions, still acknowledged<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p203-1\">→ After: Ch.8 — depth read: recruiting an insider<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p203-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ichinose-honami horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 8   depth read  recruiting an insider  to close the gap we have with class a  it would be easier to have an insider from now on   that s exactly it  if you deliver results  i ll pay you in private points   you re free not to cooperate  but in that case  i can t guarantee i ll keep your secrets   it won t be that easy  horikita will definitely recover soon   unfortunately  i want more than just one thing   of course  i ll tell you the amount before you do anything  tries to recruit kushida as an insider in class a using payment and the leverage of her exposed secret  leaves the offer open  reminiscing  recalls a white room girl he has almost entirely forgotten  hinting at his suppressed past  proposes the betrayal deal and promises private points  explains how they coordinated to target the right students   her intel plus his advice  expects her to recover soon and become an obstacle","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.8 — depth read: recruiting an insider<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.203–224<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;To close the gap we have with Class A, it would be easier to have an insider from now on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s exactly it. If you deliver results, I&#x27;ll pay you in private points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You&#x27;re free not to cooperate, but in that case, I can&#x27;t guarantee I&#x27;ll keep your secrets.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It won&#x27;t be that easy. Horikita will definitely recover soon.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Unfortunately, I want more than just one thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. I&#x27;ll tell you the amount before you do anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Tries to recruit Kushida as an insider in Class A using payment and the leverage of her exposed secret; leaves the offer open.<span class=\"pg\">p.221–224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reminiscing, recalls a White Room girl he has almost entirely forgotten, hinting at his suppressed past.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Proposes the betrayal deal and promises Private Points.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Explains how they coordinated to target the right students — her intel plus his advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Expects her to recover soon and become an obstacle.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p189-1\">← Before: The aftermath: Shimazaki&#x27;s challenge and Ayanokōji&#x27;s true plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1\">→ After: After the welcome party; the dusk meeting with Kushida<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka after the welcome party  the dusk meeting with kushida returns from a small class c welcome party at keyaki mall  takes a detour from the dorm route  and meets kushida   whom he called out   waiting at the railing at dusk   why did you choose this place to meet   that did happen   it was something like an accident  but i was really anxious when you threatened me    kushida reflects that for third years there is no time to rest   it is  already april  and preparation for career choices and the next exam is like stocking emergency supplies before a catastrophe  deliberately chose an isolated spot  echoing where kushida once offered her body to keep him silent  notes her true nature was revealed to class a but not widely known elsewhere  called her out to a secluded dusk meeting  she evades his question about the place  guarded after their first year transaction","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">After the welcome party; the dusk meeting with Kushida<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.216–220<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns from a small Class C welcome party at Keyaki Mall, takes a detour from the dorm route, and meets Kushida — whom he called out — waiting at the railing at dusk.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why did you choose this place to meet?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That did happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It was something like an accident, but I was really anxious when you threatened me.&quot; — Kushida<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Reflects that for third-years there is no time to rest — it is &quot;already April,&quot; and preparation for career choices and the next exam is like stocking emergency supplies before a catastrophe.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately chose an isolated spot (echoing where Kushida once offered her body to keep him silent); notes her true nature was revealed to Class A but not widely known elsewhere.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Called her out to a secluded dusk meeting; she evades his question about the place, guarded after their first-year transaction.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p203-1\">← Before: Ch.8 — depth read: recruiting an insider<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1\">→ After: Recruiting Kushida as an insider; subtle threats<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune ichinose-honami shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka recruiting kushida as an insider  subtle threats  i was just wondering how the class is doing  i m a bit worried   to close the gap we have with class a  it would be easier to have an insider from now on   that s exactly it  if you deliver results  i ll pay you in private points   you re free not to cooperate  but in that case  i can t guarantee i ll keep your secrets   it won t be that easy  horikita will definitely recover soon   besides  if we need to forcibly expel some people in the future  that would change things   then you ll have to save up enough private points to transfer in the remaining year   i m not asking for an immediate answer  you re free to tell horikita or anyone else about this invitation to betrayal   unfortunately  i want more than just one thing  uses her exposed secret as leverage  her nature known to class a but not other classes  ryuen s rumors would lack credibility  hints at future expulsions from class a  giving her an incentive to save transfer money  and lets her record the whole thing to strengthen class a s unity if she wishes   a calculated  multi layered gambit  calm and manipulative   makes an open offer of betrayal backed by veiled blackmail  refuses to over explain  and deliberately leaves her room to maneuver  notes she is masking her true intentions as much as he is  offers to pay her for class a intel  implicitly threatens to expose her secret and hints at expelling her classmates  expects her to recover soon and become a significant obstacle  has no intention of recruiting her while she leads  discusses how he advised her class   yukimura  hirata and wan mei yui s roles  and koenji as the exploitable opportunity  credits ichinose s own intel gathering as the reason she could accept his advice  reminisces about a white room dropout girl he met once before enrolling   a memory he has almost entirely forgotten  99  of it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Recruiting Kushida as an insider; subtle threats<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.220–223<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I was just wondering how the class is doing. I&#x27;m a bit worried.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;To close the gap we have with Class A, it would be easier to have an insider from now on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s exactly it. If you deliver results, I&#x27;ll pay you in private points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re free not to cooperate, but in that case, I can&#x27;t guarantee I&#x27;ll keep your secrets.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It won&#x27;t be that easy. Horikita will definitely recover soon.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Besides, if we need to forcibly expel some people in the future, that would change things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then you&#x27;ll have to save up enough Private Points to transfer in the remaining year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m not asking for an immediate answer. You&#x27;re free to tell Horikita or anyone else about this invitation to betrayal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Unfortunately, I want more than just one thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Uses her exposed secret as leverage (her nature known to Class A but not other classes; Ryūen&#x27;s rumors would lack credibility); hints at future expulsions from Class A, giving her an incentive to save transfer money, and lets her record the whole thing to strengthen Class A&#x27;s unity if she wishes — a calculated, multi-layered gambit.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and manipulative — makes an open offer of betrayal backed by veiled blackmail, refuses to over-explain, and deliberately leaves her room to maneuver; notes she is masking her true intentions as much as he is.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Offers to pay her for Class A intel; implicitly threatens to expose her secret and hints at expelling her classmates.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Expects her to recover soon and become a significant obstacle; has no intention of recruiting her while she leads.<span class=\"pg\">p.222–223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Discusses how he advised her class — Yukimura, Hirata and Wan Mei-Yui&#x27;s roles, and Kōenji as the exploitable opportunity; credits Ichinose&#x27;s own intel gathering as the reason she could accept his advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Reminisces about a White Room dropout girl he met once before enrolling — a memory he has almost entirely forgotten (&quot;99% of it&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p216-1\">← Before: After the welcome party; the dusk meeting with Kushida<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1\">→ After: Epilogue — depth read: Tsubaki, Kitou and the White Room memory<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"tsubaki-sakurako kitou-hayato ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue   depth read  tsubaki  kitou and the white room memory  tsubaki sakurako  huh   recently  i suddenly thought of someone other than my family that i d like to meet   i m not actually going to meet them  it s just that i suddenly felt nostalgic   indeed  i also intend to do as i please   you not recognizing me as the class leader is too childish a reason   i ll look forward to that  fights kitou behind the dorm   dodges his punches and lands a palm strike  ear slap and kick   then wins his conditional loyalty  remembers a forgotten white room girl named  yuki  triggered by tsubaki and the snow wordplay  but decides not to seek her out  encounters her and utomiya  her words trigger a memory of the white room  is challenged by him  defeats him in a fight and secures his conditional loyalty","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue — depth read: Tsubaki, Kitou and the White Room memory<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.225–287<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Tsubaki Sakurako… huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Recently, I suddenly thought of someone other than my family that I&#x27;d like to meet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m not actually going to meet them. It&#x27;s just that I suddenly felt nostalgic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Indeed, I also intend to do as I please.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You not recognizing me as the class leader is too childish a reason.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll look forward to that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Fights Kitou behind the dorm — dodges his punches and lands a palm strike, ear-slap and kick — then wins his conditional loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.231–234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Remembers a forgotten White Room girl named &quot;Yuki,&quot; triggered by Tsubaki and the snow wordplay, but decides not to seek her out.<span class=\"pg\">p.226–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> Encounters her and Utomiya; her words trigger a memory of the White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Is challenged by him; defeats him in a fight and secures his conditional loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–234<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p220-1\">← Before: Recruiting Kushida as an insider; subtle threats<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-2\">→ After: Meeting Tsubaki and Utomiya; remembering Yuki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-2","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"tsubaki-sakurako utomiya-riku yuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka meeting tsubaki and utomiya  remembering yuki leaves school after class and runs into utomiya and tsubaki on the way to the dorm  they mention the rumor about his transfer   it feels like it s been a while since i ve seen the two of you together   we re not together all the time    tsubaki  tsubaki sakurako  huh   what is it  it s creepy when you suddenly call me by my full name   recently  i suddenly thought of someone other than my family that i d like to meet   how should i put this  if i had to put it in familiar terms  they would probably be a childhood friend  i guess  tsubaki s name and her training camp question  do you like snow   snow   yuki  trigger a faint memory of a white room girl named yuki  the snow camellia  yuki tsubaki  connection makes him wonder whether it was really coincidence  finds himself recalling  unnecessary memories  of the white room  concludes it would be better not to actually meet yuki again  since the past and present would likely be unchanged  meets her and utomiya  calling her by her full name startles her  she presses him about the person he d like to meet  he greets him reluctantly  utomiya sharply interjects when tsubaki s conversation turns personal  remembered as a white room classmate   the only girl he studied with there","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Meeting Tsubaki and Utomiya; remembering Yuki<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.225–228<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves school after class and runs into Utomiya and Tsubaki on the way to the dorm; they mention the rumor about his transfer.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"tsubaki-sakurako.html\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/a> · <a href=\"utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a> · <a href=\"yuki.html\">Yuki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It feels like it&#x27;s been a while since I&#x27;ve seen the two of you together.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re not together all the time.&quot; — Tsubaki<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Tsubaki Sakurako… huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What is it? It&#x27;s creepy when you suddenly call me by my full name.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Recently, I suddenly thought of someone other than my family that I&#x27;d like to meet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;How should I put this? If I had to put it in familiar terms, they would probably be a childhood friend… I guess.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Tsubaki&#x27;s name and her training-camp question &quot;do you like snow?&quot; (snow = yuki) trigger a faint memory of a White Room girl named Yuki; the snow camellia (yuki-tsubaki) connection makes him wonder whether it was really coincidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.226–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finds himself recalling &quot;unnecessary memories&quot; of the White Room; concludes it would be better not to actually meet Yuki again, since the past and present would likely be unchanged.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Tsubaki Sakurako<\/b> Meets her and Utomiya; calling her by her full name startles her; she presses him about the person he&#x27;d like to meet.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> He greets him reluctantly; Utomiya sharply interjects when Tsubaki&#x27;s conversation turns personal.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> Remembered as a White Room classmate — the only girl he studied with there.<span class=\"pg\">p.227–228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-1\">← Before: Epilogue — depth read: Tsubaki, Kitou and the White Room memory<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1\">→ After: Kitou&#x27;s challenge: a show of strength behind the dorm<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"spoken","w":"kitou-hayato ryuuen-kakeru sawada sakayanagi-arisu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka kitou s challenge  a show of strength behind the dorm meets kitou hayato  who called him to a spot near the garbage disposal area behind the dorm  kitou refuses to recognize him as leader   good  you didn t run away    kitou  i don t recognize you as a leader    kitou  you can t bring yourself to recognize anyone other than sakayanagi  can you   as long as i m not the person leading the class  someone needs to step forward    kitou  you re the same as sakayanagi  you don t really care about graduating from class a    kitou  i don t trust you    kitou  show me that you can suppress my dissatisfaction with your strength    kitou  if you had acted fast enough  you could ve prevented sawada from getting into danger   ugh    kitou  you re strong  is there this much of a difference    kitou  i ll look forward to that  accepts kitou s physical challenge on his terms   dodges punches and kicks  lands one left fist blow to the abdomen and slaps both ears to break his guard  then offers respect and a promise to raise class c  winning him over  tests him  refuses to follow until bested  then takes his hand and pledges loyalty  compares kitou s fighting style to ryuen s   kitou s upper body more refined  legs less so  rebukes kitou for not acting when she was endangered during ryuen s classroom intrusion  kitou had followed her believing she had the higher chance of winning","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Kitou&#x27;s challenge: a show of strength behind the dorm<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.229–234<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Kitou Hayato, who called him to a spot near the garbage disposal area behind the dorm; Kitou refuses to recognize him as leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good, you didn&#x27;t run away.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t recognize you as a leader.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You can&#x27;t bring yourself to recognize anyone other than Sakayanagi, can you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As long as I&#x27;m not the person leading the class, someone needs to step forward.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re the same as Sakayanagi. You don&#x27;t really care about graduating from Class A.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t trust you.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Show me that you can suppress my dissatisfaction with your strength.&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;if you had acted fast enough, you could&#x27;ve prevented Sawada from getting into danger.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ugh…!&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re strong… Is there this much of a difference…?&quot; — Kitou<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll look forward to that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Accepts Kitou&#x27;s physical challenge on his terms — dodges punches and kicks, lands one left-fist blow to the abdomen and slaps both ears to break his guard; then offers respect and a promise to raise Class C, winning him over.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Tests him; refuses to follow until bested, then takes his hand and pledges loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Compares Kitou&#x27;s fighting style to Ryūen&#x27;s — Kitou&#x27;s upper body more refined, legs less so.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">sawada<\/b> Rebukes Kitou for not acting when she was endangered during Ryūen&#x27;s classroom intrusion.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Kitou had followed her believing she had the higher chance of winning.<span class=\"pg\">p.229–230<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p225-2\">← Before: Meeting Tsubaki and Utomiya; remembering Yuki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p236-1\">→ After: Closing the distance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p236-1","v":"y3v1","y":3,"o":33,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka closing the distance reflects that he must close the distance with each student in the way most suitable to them   a conversation for those who seek it  a show of strength for those who seek it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Closing the distance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V1 · p.236<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Reflects that he must close the distance with each student in the way most suitable to them — a conversation for those who seek it, a show of strength for those who seek it.<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v1-p229-1\">← Before: Kitou&#x27;s challenge: a show of strength behind the dorm<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p13-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shimazaki-ikkei yoshida-kenta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1   depth read  study secrets and romance he can t feel meets yoshida and shimazaki in the rainy dorm lobby  joins them to keyaki mall   if this was a problem i could solve  i would ve been more than willing to cooperate   to be honest  i hardly ever use these kinds of study guides anymore   you said you envy me  but i m the one who envies you  yoshida   you can honestly say that you re in love with shiraishi   it s not sarcasm  i still don t understand romantic feelings  realizes he cannot share his real study method  white room training is inapplicable  gives partial truths about internet videos and browsing guides  still does not understand romantic feelings despite dating karuizawa  envious of yoshida s ability to feel them  is pressed for his study secrets  gives partial answers and helps him choose study guides  advises him over shiraishi and the romance rumors  discusses his own inability to feel love","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1 — depth read: study secrets and romance he can&#x27;t feel<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.13–42<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Yoshida and Shimazaki in the rainy dorm lobby; joins them to Keyaki Mall.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If this was a problem I could solve, I would&#x27;ve been more than willing to cooperate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;To be honest, I hardly ever use these kinds of study guides anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You said you envy me, but I&#x27;m the one who envies you, Yoshida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can honestly say that you&#x27;re in love with Shiraishi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not sarcasm. I still don&#x27;t understand romantic feelings.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes he cannot share his real study method (White Room training is inapplicable); gives partial truths about internet videos and browsing guides.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Still does not understand romantic feelings despite dating Karuizawa; envious of Yoshida&#x27;s ability to feel them.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Is pressed for his study secrets; gives partial answers and helps him choose study guides.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Advises him over Shiraishi and the romance rumors; discusses his own inability to feel love.<span class=\"pg\">p.34–42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p13-2\">→ After: The rainy day out; Shimazaki&#x27;s real reason<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p13-2","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shimazaki-ikkei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the rainy day out  shimazaki s real reason leaves his room before 10 a m  on a rainy sunday with an umbrella  in the elevator notes the wet floor from early risers  shimazaki  a former class a student  removed a white wireless earbud from his right ear and put it in a small case   he was listening to english listening practice for entrance exams  he studies about five hours a day outside of class   that depends on the topic of discussion  what exactly did you want to talk about  shimazaki arranged the meeting through yoshida because he and ayanokoji were not close enough to go out and talk directly  he asked ayanokoji to bring an umbrella   odd for a mere talk that could have happened in a room   today  i m going to make you confess all of your secrets  ayanokoji realizes the study method conversation is the real purpose  follows shimazaki  who walks briskly toward keyaki mall","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p13-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The rainy day out; Shimazaki&#x27;s real reason<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.13–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leaves his room before 10 a.m. on a rainy Sunday with an umbrella; in the elevator notes the wet floor from early risers.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That depends on the topic of discussion. What exactly did you want to talk about?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;Today, I&#x27;m going to make you confess all of your secrets.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Shimazaki, a former Class A student, removed a white wireless earbud from his right ear and put it in a small case — he was listening to English listening practice for entrance exams; he studies about five hours a day outside of class.<span class=\"pg\">p.13–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Shimazaki arranged the meeting through Yoshida because he and Ayanokōji were not close enough to go out and talk directly; he asked Ayanokōji to bring an umbrella — odd for a mere talk that could have happened in a room.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Ayanokōji realizes the study-method conversation is the real purpose; follows Shimazaki, who walks briskly toward Keyaki Mall.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.1 — depth read: study secrets and romance he can&#x27;t feel<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p17-1\">→ After: The bookstore: deflecting about study methods<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p17-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"inner spoken","w":"shimazaki-ikkei yoshida-kenta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the bookstore  deflecting about study methods at keyaki mall s bookstore  shimazaki leads them to the study guide section   his destination   tell me what kind of study guides you usually use  and how you study   after seeing the results of the last special exam  i know you re ranked higher than me  ayanokoji cannot give the real answer  his current  studying  is complete review of material mastered in childhood  not learning  so he has no method to teach   if this was a problem i could solve  i would ve been more than willing to cooperate   it s not that i want to show off being number one  nor do i want to be  he wants others to be able to surpass him in academics   there are students better than him in various fields  and he wants it that way   to be honest  i hardly ever use these kinds of study guides anymore   to be honest  a lot of it is just coincidence  i usually pick up my knowledge from the internet  he gives partial truths   internet videos  browsing guides   rather than the white room based method  which he could not realistically teach  he still recommends a suitable study guide from memory  recognizes his sincere determination and rivalry  gives partial answers and offers advice he can  yoshida joins in asking to be taught too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The bookstore: deflecting about study methods<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.17–20<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Keyaki Mall&#x27;s bookstore, Shimazaki leads them to the study-guide section — his destination.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;Tell me what kind of study guides you usually use, and how you study.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;After seeing the results of the last special exam, I know you&#x27;re ranked higher than me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If this was a problem I could solve, I would&#x27;ve been more than willing to cooperate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji cannot give the real answer: his current &quot;studying&quot; is complete review of material mastered in childhood, not learning, so he has no method to teach.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not that I want to show off being number one, nor do I want to be.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He wants others to be able to surpass him in academics — there are students better than him in various fields, and he wants it that way.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;To be honest, I hardly ever use these kinds of study guides anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;To be honest, a lot of it is just coincidence. I usually pick up my knowledge from the internet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He gives partial truths — internet videos, browsing guides — rather than the White Room-based method, which he could not realistically teach; he still recommends a suitable study guide from memory.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Recognizes his sincere determination and rivalry; gives partial answers and offers advice he can.<span class=\"pg\">p.17–20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Yoshida joins in asking to be taught too.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p13-2\">← Before: The rainy day out; Shimazaki&#x27;s real reason<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p43-1\">→ After: Ch.2 — depth read: the vague exam and the OAA reveal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p43-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"nishikawa-ryouko kitou-hayato yoshida-kenta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2   depth read  the vague exam and the oaa reveal notes third years busily preparing for entrance exams employment  morishita teases him about fitting in during homeroom   if possible  i d like to hear my classmates  opinions first   my opinion is mostly the same as the ones already brought up  the fact that the school deliberately didn t explain the rules this time means it must be something that can be understood and established without explanation   a lot of different opinions have been thrown around  but one that i feel is a strong possibility is that our  attitude in daily life  will be observed for the next week  starting tomorrow   i don t like to stand out  at first  i wasn t even interested in graduating from class a   a major factor was that hashimoto asked me for help  wanting me to do something about the situation where we could no longer win after sakayanagi left  judges the exam s intent is to see how long students can maintain tension toward a vague  undefined goal  at lunch  fielding her skepticism and her  assassin sent by horikita  theory  is questioned by him about why he hid his ability and why he got serious  he leaves the meal early  yoshida defends him and cheers his high oaa as a comrade  ayanokoji s new oaa  academic a   96  physical a  81  adaptability b  66  social contribution b   77  overall b   80  a year earlier it was all c level  academic c 51  physical c  60  adaptability d  37  social c  60  overall c 51","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 — depth read: the vague exam and the OAA reveal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.43–65<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Notes third-years busily preparing for entrance exams/employment; Morishita teases him about fitting in during homeroom.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nishikawa-ryouko.html\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If possible, I&#x27;d like to hear my classmates&#x27; opinions first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My opinion is mostly the same as the ones already brought up. The fact that the school deliberately didn&#x27;t explain the rules this time means it must be something that can be understood and established without explanation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;A lot of different opinions have been thrown around, but one that I feel is a strong possibility is that our &#x27;attitude in daily life&#x27; will be observed for the next week, starting tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t like to stand out. At first, I wasn&#x27;t even interested in graduating from Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A major factor was that Hashimoto asked me for help, wanting me to do something about the situation where we could no longer win after Sakayanagi left.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Judges the exam&#x27;s intent is to see how long students can maintain tension toward a vague, undefined goal.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/b> At lunch, fielding her skepticism and her &quot;assassin sent by Horikita&quot; theory.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Is questioned by him about why he hid his ability and why he got serious; he leaves the meal early.<span class=\"pg\">p.58–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Yoshida defends him and cheers his high OAA as a comrade.<span class=\"pg\">p.57–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji&#x27;s new OAA: Academic A+ (96), Physical A (81), Adaptability B (66), Social Contribution B+ (77), Overall B+ (80); a year earlier it was all C-level (Academic C 51, Physical C+ 60, Adaptability D+ 37, Social C+ 60, Overall C 51).<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p17-1\">← Before: The bookstore: deflecting about study methods<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p44-1\">→ After: The vague exam; steering the class discussion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p44-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi shimazaki-ikkei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the vague exam  steering the class discussion in homeroom  morishita whispers from behind  asking if he has gotten used to the class   if possible  i d like to hear my classmates  opinions first  mashima sensei announces a new exam starting  tomorrow  rewards only  50 20 0 25 class points  details in one week  no questions   phrasing that catches ayanokoji s attention   my opinion is mostly the same as the ones already brought up  the fact that the school deliberately didn t explain the rules this time means it must be something that can be understood and established without explanation   a lot of different opinions have been thrown around  but one that i feel is a strong possibility is that our  attitude in daily life  will be observed for the next week  starting tomorrow  judges the exam s intent is to see how long students can maintain tension toward a vague goal  proposes  attitude in daily life   echoing the first year conduct exam  as a provisional guidepost   even picking up a piece of trash could decide it  he notices mashima said  exam  not  special exam  but holds back  judging it could be a slip of the tongue  he tries to start the discussion  ayanokoji defers to the class  pushes for a decision  later accepts the daily attitude possibility","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The vague exam; steering the class discussion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.44–51<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In homeroom, Morishita whispers from behind, asking if he has gotten used to the class.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If possible, I&#x27;d like to hear my classmates&#x27; opinions first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My opinion is mostly the same as the ones already brought up. The fact that the school deliberately didn&#x27;t explain the rules this time means it must be something that can be understood and established without explanation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;A lot of different opinions have been thrown around, but one that I feel is a strong possibility is that our &#x27;attitude in daily life&#x27; will be observed for the next week, starting tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Mashima-sensei announces a new exam starting &quot;tomorrow,&quot; rewards only (+50/+20/0/−25 Class Points), details in one week, no questions — phrasing that catches Ayanokōji&#x27;s attention.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Judges the exam&#x27;s intent is to see how long students can maintain tension toward a vague goal; proposes &quot;attitude in daily life&quot; (echoing the first-year conduct exam) as a provisional guidepost — even picking up a piece of trash could decide it.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He notices Mashima said &quot;exam,&quot; not &quot;special exam,&quot; but holds back, judging it could be a slip of the tongue.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He tries to start the discussion; Ayanokōji defers to the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Pushes for a decision; later accepts the daily-attitude possibility.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p43-1\">← Before: Ch.2 — depth read: the vague exam and the OAA reveal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p52-1\">→ After: The lunch invitation; inviting Kitou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p52-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka yoshida-kenta kitou-hayato ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the lunch invitation  inviting kitou at lunch break  shiraishi invites him to eat  yoshida transparently tries to muscle in   i don t mind  what s up   what a coincidence to get two invitations at once  is it alright if yoshida joins us   wait a minute  there s someone else i want to invite  is that alright   dead serious  invites kitou specifically to observe him   noting the others  surprise and yoshida s worry that  things could get ugly  accepts her invitation  she good naturedly approves inviting kitou  allows him to join  notes his transparent  easily read antics  deliberately invites him to lunch to gauge him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The lunch invitation; inviting Kitou<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.52–54<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At lunch break, Shiraishi invites him to eat; Yoshida transparently tries to muscle in.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t mind. What&#x27;s up?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What a coincidence to get two invitations at once. Is it alright if Yoshida joins us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Wait a minute. There&#x27;s someone else I want to invite, is that alright?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Dead serious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Invites Kitou specifically to observe him — noting the others&#x27; surprise and Yoshida&#x27;s worry that &quot;things could get ugly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53–54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Accepts her invitation; she good-naturedly approves inviting Kitou.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Allows him to join; notes his transparent, easily-read antics.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Deliberately invites him to lunch to gauge him.<span class=\"pg\">p.53–54<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p44-1\">← Before: The vague exam; steering the class discussion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p55-1\">→ After: The cafeteria: OAA and Ike&#x27;s avoidance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p55-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"inner spoken","w":"nishikawa-ryouko yoshida-kenta kitou-hayato ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafeteria  oaa and ike s avoidance in the cafeteria  arranges seating with yoshida right  kitou left  shiraishi across  notes ike and hondou deliberately avoid them  he wanted ike and friends to sit nearby as harassment and to prevent careless remarks   but they showed no such inclination   something like that  probably  yoshida reveals ayanokoji s oaa  academic a   96  physical a  81  adaptability b  66  social contribution b   77  overall b   80    top class among third years  his scores rose after transferring to class c and not holding back  the transfer itself  being legal  likely did not hurt social contribution  quietly strategic   uses the lunch to gather reactions  welcomes suspicion as healthy  and reads the class s shifting attitudes  she calls him  quite hated    a  traitor  from ike s view and voices suspicion he s an assassin sent by horikita  he root for ayanokoji s high oaa as a  comrade  sits on his left  reacts to nothing  including the oaa","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p55-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The cafeteria: OAA and Ike&#x27;s avoidance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.55–58<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the cafeteria, arranges seating with Yoshida right, Kitou left, Shiraishi across; notes Ike and Hondou deliberately avoid them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"nishikawa-ryouko.html\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\">He wanted Ike and friends to sit nearby as harassment and to prevent careless remarks — but they showed no such inclination.<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Something like that, probably.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Yoshida reveals Ayanokōji&#x27;s OAA: Academic A+ (96), Physical A (81), Adaptability B (66), Social Contribution B+ (77), Overall B+ (80) — top-class among third-years.<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> His scores rose after transferring to Class C and not holding back; the transfer itself, being legal, likely did not hurt Social Contribution.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Quietly strategic — uses the lunch to gather reactions, welcomes suspicion as healthy, and reads the class&#x27;s shifting attitudes.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nishikawa Ryōko<\/b> She calls him &quot;quite hated&quot; / a &quot;traitor&quot; from Ike&#x27;s view and voices suspicion he&#x27;s an assassin sent by Horikita.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> He root for Ayanokōji&#x27;s high OAA as a &quot;comrade.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Sits on his left; reacts to nothing, including the OAA.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p52-1\">← Before: The lunch invitation; inviting Kitou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.4 — depth read: 90% certain it&#x27;s conduct<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori shiraishi-asuka hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4   depth read  90  certain it s conduct tries to leave early for school but is blocked from the elevator by cold eyed class a girls  ends up walking with hiyori   to be precise  it may be more accurate to say that it s not that i don t care about winning or losing  but rather that i can t   over 90  at least  that s my assessment   you can avoid obvious demerits  but you can t earn merits  the only thing we can do is wait for the other classes to make a mistake   if it was only mashima sensei s comment  the probability wouldn t even have reached 50   by the way  how i procured information from the two classes is a trade secret   who can say  it might be twenty million  it might be thirty million  deduces conduct is the exam by comparing the parting words of all four classes  homeroom teachers  deliberately stays cold under ike s accusations so class a will unite against him as a common enemy  painting class c as peaceful  walks with her briefly but struggles to find words  plans to visit the library to apologize properly  walks back with him  is puzzled by her reintroducing herself and her deliberate mystery  discusses the exam and intel with him at the cafe  notes that a high stakes exam with expulsion may come next  morishita cites  15 expulsions the previous year","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 — depth read: 90% certain it&#x27;s conduct<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.126–151<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tries to leave early for school but is blocked from the elevator by cold-eyed Class A girls; ends up walking with Hiyori.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;To be precise, it may be more accurate to say that it&#x27;s not that I don&#x27;t care about winning or losing, but rather that I can&#x27;t.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Over 90%. At least, that&#x27;s my assessment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You can avoid obvious demerits, but you can&#x27;t earn merits. The only thing we can do is wait for the other classes to make a mistake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If it was only Mashima-sensei&#x27;s comment, the probability wouldn&#x27;t even have reached 50%.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;By the way, how I procured information from the two classes is a trade secret.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who can say. It might be twenty million, it might be thirty million.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Deduces conduct is the exam by comparing the parting words of all four classes&#x27; homeroom teachers.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately stays cold under Ike&#x27;s accusations so Class A will unite against him as a common enemy, painting Class C as peaceful.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Walks with her briefly but struggles to find words; plans to visit the library to apologize properly.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Walks back with him; is puzzled by her reintroducing herself and her deliberate mystery.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–151<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Discusses the exam and intel with him at the café.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Notes that a high-stakes exam with expulsion may come next; Morishita cites ~15 expulsions the previous year.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p55-1\">← Before: The cafeteria: OAA and Ike&#x27;s avoidance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-2\">→ After: The elevator with Hiyori; a failed conversation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-2","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the elevator with hiyori  a failed conversation takes the elevator early  three class a girls  shinohara  matsushita  inogashira  stare coldly so he waits for the next one  then steps in beside hiyori   good morning   same as always  he struggles to keep the conversation going   unthinkable for him   and realizes being alone with hiyori was something he should have anticipated in the small community  the encounter leaves him unable to find words  atypically flustered around hiyori  he had envisioned going to the library to apologize for the transfer and talk about books but keeps procrastinating  walks with her briefly  they have never had a proper conversation since his transfer","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The elevator with Hiyori; a failed conversation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.126–128<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Takes the elevator early; three Class A girls (Shinohara, Matsushita, Inogashira) stare coldly so he waits for the next one, then steps in beside Hiyori.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Good morning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Same as always.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He struggles to keep the conversation going — unthinkable for him — and realizes being alone with Hiyori was something he should have anticipated in the small community; the encounter leaves him unable to find words.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Atypically flustered around Hiyori; he had envisioned going to the library to apologize for the transfer and talk about books but keeps procrastinating.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Walks with her briefly; they have never had a proper conversation since his transfer.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.4 — depth read: 90% certain it&#x27;s conduct<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p127-1\">→ After: Hashimoto, Morishita, Shiraishi interrogate him; Kondou intrudes<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p127-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai shiraishi-asuka kondou-reo ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hashimoto  morishita  shiraishi interrogate him  kondou intrudes outside the dorms  hashimoto  morishita and shiraishi intercept them  hiyori takes the cue and leaves for school alone   it s fine   why would you think that   of course  as allies  we need to share information   the moment you let your guard down is when the rug gets pulled out from under you   by the way  how i procured information from the two classes is a trade secret  he posted in the group chat that daily conduct was likely the exam focus  advising students not confident in their actions not to leave the dorms even on weekends  deliberately drives hiyori away so the questioning can happen  then uses it to gather intel  hides his sources  ichinose  horikita  as a trade secret  he and the others question him about the exam plan  hashimoto investigated the other classes with no real find  calls him  traitorous hashimoto the righteous  defends sakayanagi s legacy  defends sakayanagi s two years of class a stability  deduces the conduct exam  he and komiya from ryuen s class apply pressure  fishing for hints","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hashimoto, Morishita, Shiraishi interrogate him; Kondou intrudes<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.127–130<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Outside the dorms, Hashimoto, Morishita and Shiraishi intercept them; Hiyori takes the cue and leaves for school alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"kondou-reo.html\">Kondō Reo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Why would you think that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Of course. As allies, we need to share information.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The moment you let your guard down is when the rug gets pulled out from under you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;By the way, how I procured information from the two classes is a trade secret.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He posted in the group chat that daily conduct was likely the exam focus, advising students not confident in their actions not to leave the dorms even on weekends.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Deliberately drives Hiyori away so the questioning can happen, then uses it to gather intel; hides his sources (Ichinose, Horikita) as a trade secret.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He and the others question him about the exam plan; Hashimoto investigated the other classes with no real find.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Calls him &quot;traitorous Hashimoto THE Righteous&quot;; defends Sakayanagi&#x27;s legacy.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Defends Sakayanagi&#x27;s two years of Class A stability; deduces the conduct exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kondō Reo<\/b> He and Komiya from Ryūen&#x27;s class apply pressure, fishing for hints.<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p126-2\">← Before: The elevator with Hiyori; a failed conversation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p136-1\">→ After: The café: revealing the 90% conduct deduction<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p136-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the cafe  revealing the 90  conduct deduction in the keyaki mall cafe with hashimoto  morishita and shiraishi  begins the  serious discussion   alright  time for a serious discussion   you seem fired up  but to be honest  i don t intend to be particularly concerned with winning or losing this exam   to be precise  it may be more accurate to say that it s not that i don t care about winning or losing  but rather that i can t   you can avoid obvious demerits  but you can t earn merits  the only thing we can do is wait for the other classes to make a mistake   over 90  at least  that s my assessment   if it was only mashima sensei s comment  the probability wouldn t even have reached 50   hoshinomiya sensei apparently said   you ll be fine as your usual selves  chabashira sensei supposedly said   i want you to show me that you re different from when you enrolled   i wouldn t be surprised if that was included in the rules with a fairly high probability  deduces the conduct exam with  90  confidence by comparing the teachers  parting words across all four classes   mashima s remark about behaving befitting a student  hoshinomiya s about being one s usual self  chabashira s about being different from when they enrolled   each matched to that class s situation  specifies he is unconcerned because conduct can t decide the outcome   only others  mistakes can   and shifts focus to the next likely high stakes exam  she challenges his 90  figure  he explains his cross class reasoning  and she is convinced","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p136-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The café: revealing the 90% conduct deduction<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.136–140<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the Keyaki Mall café with Hashimoto, Morishita and Shiraishi, begins the &quot;serious discussion.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Alright, time for a serious discussion.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You seem fired up, but to be honest, I don&#x27;t intend to be particularly concerned with winning or losing this exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;To be precise, it may be more accurate to say that it&#x27;s not that I don&#x27;t care about winning or losing, but rather that I can&#x27;t.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can avoid obvious demerits, but you can&#x27;t earn merits. The only thing we can do is wait for the other classes to make a mistake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Over 90%. At least, that&#x27;s my assessment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If it was only Mashima-sensei&#x27;s comment, the probability wouldn&#x27;t even have reached 50%.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hoshinomiya-sensei apparently said, &#x27;You&#x27;ll be fine as your usual selves.&#x27; Chabashira-sensei supposedly said, &#x27;I want you to show me that you&#x27;re different from when you enrolled.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wouldn&#x27;t be surprised if that was included in the rules with a fairly high probability.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Deduces the conduct exam with &gt;90% confidence by comparing the teachers&#x27; parting words across all four classes — Mashima&#x27;s remark about behaving befitting a student, Hoshinomiya&#x27;s about being one&#x27;s usual self, Chabashira&#x27;s about being different from when they enrolled — each matched to that class&#x27;s situation.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Specifies he is unconcerned because conduct can&#x27;t decide the outcome — only others&#x27; mistakes can — and shifts focus to the next likely high-stakes exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.136–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> She challenges his 90% figure; he explains his cross-class reasoning, and she is convinced.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p127-1\">← Before: Hashimoto, Morishita, Shiraishi interrogate him; Kondou intrudes<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p141-1\">→ After: Ike&#x27;s accusation in the café<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p141-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ike s accusation in the cafe ike and hondou arrive at the next table  ike calls him a  traitor   we re fated to meet   yeah  we re class a  but ayanokouji hid how smart he was   i m hearing all sorts of nasty rumors  y know  that you intentionally set up both sakura and maezono to get expelled from the very beginning  stays cold under ike s hatred  letting him direct it at him to unite class a  privately notes ike may be acting to drag down class c  but doubts it  he vents his anger and blames him for sakura  maezono and yamauchi s expulsions  hashimoto tries to defuse ike s rage by flattering class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p141-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ike&#x27;s accusation in the café<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.141–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike and Hondou arrive at the next table; Ike calls him a &quot;traitor.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re fated to meet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah, we&#x27;re Class A, but Ayanokouji hid how smart he was.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m hearing all sorts of nasty rumors, y&#x27;know. That you intentionally set up both Sakura and Maezono to get expelled from the very beginning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Stays cold under Ike&#x27;s hatred, letting him direct it at him to unite Class A; privately notes Ike may be acting to drag down Class C, but doubts it.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> He vents his anger and blames him for Sakura, Maezono and Yamauchi&#x27;s expulsions.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Hashimoto tries to defuse Ike&#x27;s rage by flattering Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.141–142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p136-1\">← Before: The café: revealing the 90% conduct deduction<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 — depth read: Yamamura, Hasebe and his own avoidance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p152-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"yamamura-miki hasebe-haruka shiina-hiyori hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5   depth read  yamamura  hasebe and his own avoidance is pulled out of his thoughts by morishita tugging his hair  saying yamamura wants to see him   is that so   i want you to find out about shiraishi asuka   i m currently struggling to raise my understanding of the class   then you ll have to be prepared for people to keep secrets from you or avoid you to some extent   it s completely unrelated  so you can rest easy    to hasebe about her fear she caused his transfer  that s not true  i d like to hear it  admits he has been avoiding the library because he doesn t want to see the sadness on hiyori s face after rejecting her invitation  tasks yamamura with investigating her own classmate shiraishi to understand her  meets her  gives her the task of investigating shiraishi  hears her out about the expelled sakura s tv appearances  reflects on avoiding her out of guilt  notes his full commitment to class c","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 — depth read: Yamamura, Hasebe and his own avoidance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.152–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Is pulled out of his thoughts by Morishita tugging his hair, saying Yamamura wants to see him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a> · <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is that so?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I want you to find out about Shiraishi Asuka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m currently struggling to raise my understanding of the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then you&#x27;ll have to be prepared for people to keep secrets from you or avoid you to some extent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s completely unrelated, so you can rest easy.&quot; — to Hasebe about her fear she caused his transfer<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s not true. I&#x27;d like to hear it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Admits he has been avoiding the library because he doesn&#x27;t want to see the sadness on Hiyori&#x27;s face after rejecting her invitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Tasks Yamamura with investigating her own classmate Shiraishi to understand her.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Meets her; gives her the task of investigating Shiraishi.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Hears her out about the expelled Sakura&#x27;s TV appearances.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Reflects on avoiding her out of guilt.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Notes his full commitment to Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p141-1\">← Before: Ike&#x27;s accusation in the café<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p164-1\">→ After: Hashimoto&#x27;s declaration of loyalty<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p164-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hashimoto s declaration of loyalty  then you ll have to be prepared for people to keep secrets from you or avoid you to some extent   it d be a lie to say i wasn t wondering about it  hashimoto reveals he abandoned his escape route  threw away his private points  and now believes class c can win  ayanokoji sees this as proof of his resolve  listens to his declaration  hashimoto says he ll keep  pestering  him and steps aside for the library visit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p164-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hashimoto&#x27;s declaration of loyalty<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.164–167<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then you&#x27;ll have to be prepared for people to keep secrets from you or avoid you to some extent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;d be a lie to say I wasn&#x27;t wondering about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Hashimoto reveals he abandoned his escape route (threw away his Private Points) and now believes Class C can win; Ayanokōji sees this as proof of his resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Listens to his declaration; Hashimoto says he&#x27;ll keep &quot;pestering&quot; him and steps aside for the library visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.164–167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 — depth read: Yamamura, Hasebe and his own avoidance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p168-1\">→ After: Avoiding the library; Hasebe and Sakura&#x27;s TV success<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p168-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hasebe-haruka sakura-airi shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka avoiding the library  hasebe and sakura s tv success walks toward the library after 5 p m  admitting to himself he has been avoiding it because he doesn t want to see sadness on hiyori s face  realizes he unconsciously avoided hiyori   he betrayed the girl who invited him with all her heart  and though he knows he should apologize and repair it  he keeps finding excuses  wrestles with an unfamiliar reluctance  notes hiyori wasn t the only one saddened by his transfer  horikita s class above all  yet he is concerned only about her   yeah  i couldn t hear you out when you came to talk to me before   it was just the other day   it s completely unrelated  so you can rest easy   that s not true  i d like to hear it   yeah  i didn t have the courage to look into it myself  but to be honest  i ve been wondering about her all this time   it s fine  i enjoyed talking with you  hasebe  it s been a while  hasebe reveals the expelled sakura airi has begun appearing on late night tv   having passed an audition in under a year since her expulsion  ayanokoji sees it as a way to test winning over class a students  hears her out about sakura  she unconsciously calls him  kiyopon  learns of her tv appearances  still avoiding her  arrives at the library after six but she left ten minutes earlier    i ll try again another day","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p168-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Avoiding the library; Hasebe and Sakura&#x27;s TV success<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.168–174<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks toward the library after 5 p.m., admitting to himself he has been avoiding it because he doesn&#x27;t want to see sadness on Hiyori&#x27;s face.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hasebe-haruka.html\">Hasebe Haruka<\/a> · <a href=\"sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. I couldn&#x27;t hear you out when you came to talk to me before.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It was just the other day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s completely unrelated, so you can rest easy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes he unconsciously avoided Hiyori — he betrayed the girl who invited him with all her heart, and though he knows he should apologize and repair it, he keeps finding excuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Wrestles with an unfamiliar reluctance; notes Hiyori wasn&#x27;t the only one saddened by his transfer (Horikita&#x27;s class above all) yet he is concerned only about her.<span class=\"pg\">p.168–169<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s not true. I&#x27;d like to hear it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. I didn&#x27;t have the courage to look into it myself, but to be honest, I&#x27;ve been wondering about her all this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s fine. I enjoyed talking with you, Hasebe, it&#x27;s been a while.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hasebe reveals the expelled Sakura Airi has begun appearing on late-night TV — having passed an audition in under a year since her expulsion; Ayanokōji sees it as a way to test winning over Class A students.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hasebe Haruka<\/b> Hears her out about Sakura; she unconsciously calls him &quot;Kiyopon.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169–174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Learns of her TV appearances.<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Still avoiding her; arrives at the library after six but she left ten minutes earlier — &quot;I&#x27;ll try again another day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.168, 174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p164-1\">← Before: Hashimoto&#x27;s declaration of loyalty<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-1\">→ After: Ch.6 — depth read: Hoshinomiya&#x27;s test and Hiyori<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie shiina-hiyori kaneda-satoru morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6   depth read  hoshinomiya s test and hiyori  you leave no openings  do you  hoshinomiya sensei   what the school will judge over the course of one week is our  attitude in our daily school life   isn t it also necessary to believe in your own class   remember to watch over them  that s something even chabashira sensei is capable of   no  i came to see you today  hiyori   if you don t mind  hiyori  why don t we talk about this past month we ve been apart   envy me  i m a traitor who abandoned class a  uses hoshinomiya s deliberate physical advance to confirm the exam judges daily conduct via security camera recordings  admits hiyori is  a little different from the frameworks  he used   simply reading and sharing space with her gives him a sense of  happiness  meets her  stops her interference by invoking the alliance and chabashira  finally visits her  apologizes  talks for hours  and realizes his feelings for her may be more than friendship  talks with him in the library  is praised and envied  and questioned about hiyori  is shot repeatedly with her rubber band gun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 — depth read: Hoshinomiya&#x27;s test and Hiyori<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.182–210<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;You leave no openings, do you, Hoshinomiya-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What the school will judge over the course of one week is our &#x27;attitude in our daily school life.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Isn&#x27;t it also necessary to believe in your own class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Remember to watch over them. That&#x27;s something even Chabashira-sensei is capable of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, I came to see you today, Hiyori.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you don&#x27;t mind, Hiyori, why don&#x27;t we talk about this past month we&#x27;ve been apart?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Envy me? I&#x27;m a traitor who abandoned Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Uses Hoshinomiya&#x27;s deliberate physical advance to confirm the exam judges daily conduct via security-camera recordings.<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Admits Hiyori is &quot;a little different from the frameworks&quot; he used — simply reading and sharing space with her gives him a sense of &quot;happiness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Meets her; stops her interference by invoking the alliance and Chabashira.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Finally visits her, apologizes, talks for hours, and realizes his feelings for her may be more than friendship.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Talks with him in the library; is praised and envied, and questioned about Hiyori.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Is shot repeatedly with her rubber-band gun.<span class=\"pg\">p.182–184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p168-1\">← Before: Avoiding the library; Hasebe and Sakura&#x27;s TV success<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-2\">→ After: The rubber-band gun; Hoshinomiya&#x27;s &quot;service&quot; confirms the exam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-2","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ichinose-honami satonaka-satoru morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the rubber band gun  hoshinomiya s  service  confirms the exam as school ends on day five  notes all four classes have maintained perfect conduct  morishita shoots him with a rubber band gun made from chopsticks   ow  ow  that hurts  what the   it is a gun  a gun   that s because i m shooting you with the intent to cause pain  satonaka invites him to hang out sunday with yanagibashi  tsukasaki and hoashi  morishita bluntly refuses  goes to the special building after ichinose s message that hoshinomiya wants to see him  hoshinomiya presses against him and entwines her arm with his   you leave no openings  do you  hoshinomiya sensei   what the school will judge over the course of one week is our  attitude in our daily school life   please  rest assured  even if you were to intentionally act in a way that lowers my evaluation  hoshinomiya sensei  it won t affect our alliance   isn t it also necessary to believe in your own class   remember to watch over them  that s something even chabashira sensei is capable of   please consider our alliance from a long term perspective  not a short term one  uses hoshinomiya s deliberate physical advance to confirm the conduct exam  cameras would record it  affecting assessment  invokes chabashira  her rival  to make her withdraw  and refuses to manipulate the exam s outcome for her class  she tests entices him  he stops her with words  invokes her desire to beat chabashira  and tells her to trust the alliance long term  sent his message  the alliance is why he restrains hoshinomiya  invited him to a sunday outing  shoots him repeatedly with her rubber band gun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The rubber-band gun; Hoshinomiya&#x27;s &quot;service&quot; confirms the exam<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.182–189<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As school ends on day five, notes all four classes have maintained perfect conduct; Morishita shoots him with a rubber-band gun made from chopsticks. Goes to the special building after Ichinose&#x27;s message that Hoshinomiya wants to see him; Hoshinomiya presses against him and entwines her arm with his.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"satonaka-satoru.html\">Satonaka Satoru<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ow, ow, that hurts. What the...?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It is a gun. A gun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s because I&#x27;m shooting you with the intent to cause pain.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Satonaka invites him to hang out Sunday with Yanagibashi, Tsukasaki and Hoashi; Morishita bluntly refuses.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You leave no openings, do you, Hoshinomiya-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What the school will judge over the course of one week is our &#x27;attitude in our daily school life.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please, rest assured. Even if you were to intentionally act in a way that lowers my evaluation, Hoshinomiya-sensei, it won&#x27;t affect our alliance.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn&#x27;t it also necessary to believe in your own class?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Remember to watch over them. That&#x27;s something even Chabashira-sensei is capable of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please consider our alliance from a long-term perspective, not a short-term one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Uses Hoshinomiya&#x27;s deliberate physical advance to confirm the conduct exam (cameras would record it, affecting assessment); invokes Chabashira (her rival) to make her withdraw, and refuses to manipulate the exam&#x27;s outcome for her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.185–189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> She tests/entices him; he stops her with words, invokes her desire to beat Chabashira, and tells her to trust the alliance long-term.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–189<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Sent his message; the alliance is why he restrains Hoshinomiya.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satonaka Satoru<\/b> Invited him to a Sunday outing.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Shoots him repeatedly with her rubber-band gun.<span class=\"pg\">p.182–184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-1\">← Before: Ch.6 — depth read: Hoshinomiya&#x27;s test and Hiyori<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p190-1\">→ After: The library reunion: apologizing to Hiyori<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p190-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the library reunion  apologizing to hiyori arrives at the library  the librarian points him to the mystery novel section where hiyori is hiding behind shelves  avoiding his eyes   was i bothering you   did you come here to look for a book to read   no  i came to see you today  hiyori   i thought i was prepared   we re in different classes now  ayanokouji kun  i thought that our relationship  where we could chat so familiarly  had to come to an end   if you don t mind  hiyori  why don t we talk about this past month we ve been apart  we have plenty of time today   of course  i came here today because i wanted to see you and talk with you  hiyori  realizes hiyori had been trying to sever their friendly relationship and see him as an enemy  feels relief he made it in time  her face shows its first smile of the day  reconciles with her after a month of avoidance  she had been apologizing when he had the greater reason to","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The library reunion: apologizing to Hiyori<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.190–194<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives at the library; the librarian points him to the mystery-novel section where Hiyori is hiding behind shelves, avoiding his eyes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Was I bothering you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Did you come here to look for a book to read...?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No, I came to see you today, Hiyori.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I thought I was prepared...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;re in different classes now, Ayanokouji-kun. I thought that our relationship, where we could chat so familiarly, had to come to an end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you don&#x27;t mind, Hiyori, why don&#x27;t we talk about this past month we&#x27;ve been apart? We have plenty of time today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. I came here today because I wanted to see you and talk with you, Hiyori.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Realizes Hiyori had been trying to sever their friendly relationship and see him as an enemy; feels relief he made it in time; her face shows its first smile of the day.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Reconciles with her after a month of avoidance; she had been apologizing when he had the greater reason to.<span class=\"pg\">p.190–194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p182-2\">← Before: The rubber-band gun; Hoshinomiya&#x27;s &quot;service&quot; confirms the exam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p195-1\">→ After: Talking with Hiyori; the corn poppy; mutual feelings<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p195-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori kaneda-satoru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka talking with hiyori  the corn poppy  mutual feelings sits with hiyori in the empty library seats  filling the month s blank with conversation  kaneda joins   so  even after becoming a third year student  the bookworm remains unchanged   it seems like we ve been swapping places   envy me  i m a traitor who abandoned class a   that s not it  i would say the same thing in the same way to anyone   it was different from willfully moving a category from right to left   it s fine  i want to give this to you   it s an apology for making you wait a month   why are you crying   it s much the same for me  this was supposed to end as just another ordinary day  realizes hiyori has been making friends  kaneda  and that  just reading books and sharing the same space  fills him with a sense of fulfillment he can only call  happiness    she is  a little different from the frameworks  he used  buys her a single corn poppy  400 points  as an impulsive   selfish  apology  her tears and his identical state of mind confirm mutual feelings  burning the image of her into memory  their feelings are shown to be mutual beneath the sunset  he joins them  praises ayanokoji while disparaging himself  the very picture of a hero  envies him  and asks  what if that person were shiina shi  before leaving abruptly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p195-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Talking with Hiyori; the corn poppy; mutual feelings<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.195–205<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sits with Hiyori in the empty library seats, filling the month&#x27;s blank with conversation; Kaneda joins.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;So, even after becoming a third-year student, the bookworm remains unchanged.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It seems like we&#x27;ve been swapping places.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Envy me? I&#x27;m a traitor who abandoned Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s not it. I would say the same thing in the same way to anyone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It was different from willfully moving a category from right to left.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.201<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s fine. I want to give this to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s an apology for making you wait a month.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Why are you crying?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s much the same for me. This was supposed to end as just another ordinary day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Realizes Hiyori has been making friends (Kaneda) and that &quot;just reading books and sharing the same space&quot; fills him with a sense of fulfillment he can only call &quot;happiness&quot; — she is &quot;a little different from the frameworks&quot; he used.<span class=\"pg\">p.200–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Buys her a single corn poppy (&lt;400 points) as an impulsive, &quot;selfish&quot; apology; her tears and his identical state of mind confirm mutual feelings; burning the image of her into memory.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Their feelings are shown to be mutual beneath the sunset.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> He joins them; praises Ayanokōji while disparaging himself (&quot;the very picture of a hero&quot;), envies him, and asks &quot;what if that person were Shiina-shi?&quot; before leaving abruptly.<span class=\"pg\">p.195–200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p190-1\">← Before: The library reunion: apologizing to Hiyori<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p206-1\">→ After: Hashimoto&#x27;s questioning; &quot;Perhaps I&#x27;m in love with Hiyori&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p206-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ichinose-honami karuizawa-kei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka hashimoto s questioning   perhaps i m in love with hiyori  back at the dorm lobby  hashimoto pulls him aside to ask about hiyori and the flower   it s not just me  ichinose probably isn t too happy about it either  is she   we re not dating   ichinose and i have an alliance  nothing more  nothing less   perhaps i m in love with hiyori   i can t say for sure what this feeling is just yet  but i might at least be harboring  or starting to harbor  feelings for hiyori that i don t have for anyone else  pressed by hashimoto s insistence that he treats hiyori differently  admits for the first time that he may be in love with her   an emotion outside his empirical rules  decides to observe it as a fascinating subject for experimentation rather than deduce it hastily  he presses him about hiyori  ichinose and romance  ayanokoji realizes hashimoto s  view on love  drives the questioning  rumored to like him and a  girlfriend candidate  he insists they are only allies  hashimoto notes he recently broke up with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p206-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Hashimoto&#x27;s questioning; &quot;Perhaps I&#x27;m in love with Hiyori&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.206–209<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back at the dorm lobby, Hashimoto pulls him aside to ask about Hiyori and the flower.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not just me. Ichinose probably isn&#x27;t too happy about it either, is she?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re not dating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ichinose and I have an alliance. Nothing more, nothing less.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps I&#x27;m in love with Hiyori.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t say for sure what this feeling is just yet. But I might at least be harboring, or starting to harbor, feelings for Hiyori that I don&#x27;t have for anyone else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Pressed by Hashimoto&#x27;s insistence that he treats Hiyori differently, admits for the first time that he may be in love with her — an emotion outside his empirical rules; decides to observe it as a fascinating subject for experimentation rather than deduce it hastily.<span class=\"pg\">p.206–209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He presses him about Hiyori, Ichinose and romance; Ayanokōji realizes Hashimoto&#x27;s &quot;view on love&quot; drives the questioning.<span class=\"pg\">p.206–209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Rumored to like him and a &quot;girlfriend candidate&quot;; he insists they are only allies.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Hashimoto notes he recently broke up with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p195-1\">← Before: Talking with Hiyori; the corn poppy; mutual feelings<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-1\">→ After: Ch.7 — depth read: results, the gym plan and a new emotion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami shiina-hiyori watanabe-norihito nanase-tsubasa ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7   depth read  results  the gym plan and a new emotion  i don t think it s a concern with this class  but make sure to tell everyone not to slander the two who are absent under any circumstances   letting her know you like her is also a valid strategy  you know   kanzaki and himeno  then hamaguchi  should be okay with these three  right   i intended to use kanzaki and the others to bring about a change in ichinose   it s not a problem in the grand scheme of things  it s a gap we can close if we aim to win the next special exam   the three i m thinking of asking are watanabe  kanzaki  and himeno  class c places last  25  due to two absentees  no ranking change overall  questions whether the emotion he felt during the library scene with hiyori is romance   a new  blissful feeling he clearly desires to repeat  coaches watanabe s romance tactically  plans to use the gym to elevate ichinose s class  kanzaki  himeno  watanabe  amikura  walk home  asks her to invite students to the gym  their hands touch and she apologizes for wanting to touch him  recalls the library moment and flower as his  blissful  memory  advises him on approaching amikura  not on friendly terms  she appears at the gym","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 — depth read: results, the gym plan and a new emotion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.211–230<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"watanabe-norihito.html\">Watanabe Norihito<\/a> · <a href=\"nanase-tsubasa.html\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s a concern with this class, but make sure to tell everyone not to slander the two who are absent under any circumstances.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Letting her know you like her is also a valid strategy, you know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kanzaki and Himeno. Then Hamaguchi. Should be okay with these three, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I intended to use Kanzaki and the others to bring about a change in Ichinose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not a problem in the grand scheme of things. It&#x27;s a gap we can close if we aim to win the next special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The three I&#x27;m thinking of asking are Watanabe, Kanzaki, and Himeno.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Class C places last (−25) due to two absentees; no ranking change overall.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Questions whether the emotion he felt during the library scene with Hiyori is romance — a new, blissful feeling he clearly desires to repeat.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coaches Watanabe&#x27;s romance tactically; plans to use the gym to elevate Ichinose&#x27;s class (Kanzaki, Himeno, Watanabe, Amikura).<span class=\"pg\">p.213–216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Walk home; asks her to invite students to the gym; their hands touch and she apologizes for wanting to touch him.<span class=\"pg\">p.220–225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Recalls the library moment and flower as his &quot;blissful&quot; memory.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Watanabe Norihito<\/b> Advises him on approaching Amikura.<span class=\"pg\">p.213–216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Nanase Tsubasa<\/b> Not on friendly terms; she appears at the gym.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p206-1\">← Before: Hashimoto&#x27;s questioning; &quot;Perhaps I&#x27;m in love with Hiyori&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-2\">→ After: The exam reveal: two absences, no ranking change<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-2","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the exam reveal  two absences  no ranking change on reveal thursday  hashimoto reports rokkaku and yano are absent  sick after a mall employee sneezed on them   i don t think it s a concern with this class  but make sure to tell everyone not to slander the two who are absent under any circumstances   probably  the exam s scope extends to that morning s attendance  the absences could be fatal in a neck and neck race  but he ensures the class doesn t blame them  calm and protective of class unity  notes ryuen s class also had an exemplary week   the outcome will hinge on a trivial difference  he reports the absences and sends out the notice not to slander them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The exam reveal: two absences, no ranking change<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.211–212<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On reveal Thursday, Hashimoto reports Rokkaku and Yano are absent (sick after a mall employee sneezed on them).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s a concern with this class, but make sure to tell everyone not to slander the two who are absent under any circumstances.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Probably.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The exam&#x27;s scope extends to that morning&#x27;s attendance; the absences could be fatal in a neck-and-neck race, but he ensures the class doesn&#x27;t blame them.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and protective of class unity; notes Ryūen&#x27;s class also had an exemplary week — the outcome will hinge on a trivial difference.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He reports the absences and sends out the notice not to slander them.<span class=\"pg\">p.211–212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-1\">← Before: Ch.7 — depth read: results, the gym plan and a new emotion<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p213-1\">→ After: Watanabe&#x27;s gym plan; camouflaging his romance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p213-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"watanabe-norihito ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka watanabe s gym plan  camouflaging his romance meets watanabe pacing outside the gym at keyaki mall  wanting to join to be near amikura   letting her know you like her is also a valid strategy  you know   kanzaki and himeno  then hamaguchi  should be okay with these three  right   for now  hold off on joining today and give me a little time  tactically coaches watanabe s romance   suggests camouflage by having several classmates join at once  deliberately picking people from class d  and plans  to use kanzaki and the others to bring about a change in ichinose  advises him on approaching amikura  he calls ayanokoji  a good guy  intends to use the gym recruitment to elevate her and her class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Watanabe&#x27;s gym plan; camouflaging his romance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.213–216<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Meets Watanabe pacing outside the gym at Keyaki Mall, wanting to join to be near Amikura.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"watanabe-norihito.html\">Watanabe Norihito<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Letting her know you like her is also a valid strategy, you know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Kanzaki and Himeno. Then Hamaguchi. Should be okay with these three, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;For now, hold off on joining today and give me a little time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Tactically coaches Watanabe&#x27;s romance — suggests camouflage by having several classmates join at once, deliberately picking people from Class D, and plans &quot;to use Kanzaki and the others to bring about a change in Ichinose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213–216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Watanabe Norihito<\/b> Advises him on approaching Amikura; he calls Ayanokōji &quot;a good guy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213–216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Intends to use the gym recruitment to elevate her and her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p211-2\">← Before: The exam reveal: two absences, no ranking change<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p216-1\">→ After: Utomiya at the gym; Akiyama&#x27;s gossip<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p216-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"spoken","w":"utomiya-riku akiyama-san ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka utomiya at the gym  akiyama s gossip  they offer a free trial  so if you re interested  you should give it a try   while i cannot definitively deny the possibility that he possesses such a side  i do believe he s a reliable teacher  utomiya from class 2 c has been coming to the gym for two days  akiyama says a first year girl he brought joined two days ago and can run at a 20 km h treadmill pace for several minutes   akiyama jokes  perhaps a storm of love is brewing  ayanokoji notes even some white room dropouts couldn t reach that level   the girl is remarkably talented  he appears at the gym with a cold attitude  they are not on friendly terms  chats with him at the gym  asks if mashima is  a player","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Utomiya at the gym; Akiyama&#x27;s gossip<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.216–219<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"utomiya-riku.html\">Utomiya Riku<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;They offer a free trial, so if you&#x27;re interested, you should give it a try.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;While I cannot definitively deny the possibility that he possesses such a side, I do believe he&#x27;s a reliable teacher.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Utomiya from Class 2-C has been coming to the gym for two days; Akiyama says a first-year girl he brought joined two days ago and can run at a 20 km/h treadmill pace for several minutes — Akiyama jokes &quot;perhaps a storm of love is brewing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Ayanokōji notes even some White Room dropouts couldn&#x27;t reach that level — the girl is remarkably talented.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Utomiya Riku<\/b> He appears at the gym with a cold attitude; they are not on friendly terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">akiyama-san<\/b> Chats with him at the gym; asks if Mashima is &quot;a player.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217–219<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p213-1\">← Before: Watanabe&#x27;s gym plan; camouflaging his romance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p221-1\">→ After: Results and the walk home with Ichinose; her hand, his new emotion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p221-1","v":"y3v2","y":3,"o":34,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ichinose-honami shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka results and the walk home with ichinose  her hand  his new emotion results  horikita 1240  ryuen 1081  ayanokoji 867  ichinose 864   no ranking change  class c last  25  from the two absences   it s not a problem in the grand scheme of things  it s a gap we can close if we aim to win the next special exam   the three i m thinking of asking are watanabe  kanzaki  and himeno  recalls the blissful library moment with hiyori holding the flower    a space enveloped in a sense of bliss  he desires to repeat   an emotion i had no memory of experiencing   because you looked so happy  i suppose  denies his heart was swayed by romance toward ichinose even as she touched his hand  dwells on the  joy of learning a new emotion  and whether it brings prosperity or ruin   a  very fulfilling  contented moment  walks home with her  she sees through his trio choices  their hands touch and she apologizes  her perception having sharpened since  that night  his thoughts turn to her holding the flower   the blissful memory","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p221-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Results and the walk home with Ichinose; her hand, his new emotion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V2 · p.221–225<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Results: Horikita 1240, Ryūen 1081, Ayanokōji 867, Ichinose 864 — no ranking change, Class C last (−25) from the two absences.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not a problem in the grand scheme of things. It&#x27;s a gap we can close if we aim to win the next special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The three I&#x27;m thinking of asking are Watanabe, Kanzaki, and Himeno.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Because you looked so happy, I suppose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Recalls the blissful library moment with Hiyori holding the flower — &quot;a space enveloped in a sense of bliss&quot; he desires to repeat, &quot;an emotion I had no memory of experiencing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Denies his heart was swayed by romance toward Ichinose even as she touched his hand; dwells on the &quot;joy of learning a new emotion&quot; and whether it brings prosperity or ruin — a &quot;very fulfilling, contented moment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224–225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Walks home with her; she sees through his trio choices, their hands touch and she apologizes, her perception having sharpened since &quot;that night.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221–225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> His thoughts turn to her holding the flower — the blissful memory.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v2-p216-1\">← Before: Utomiya at the gym; Akiyama&#x27;s gossip<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"shiina-hiyori ryuuen-kakeru ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka depth review  survival game mastermind leads class c onto the uninhabited island for the third straight year  under the survival game exam rules   i surrender   there s nothing in the rules against it   i ll make it official here  runs out of ammunition against ryuuen and ibuki  eliminates ibuki with a paintball to the thigh  then defeats ryuuen by throwing a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on impact  allowed class b s surprise attack on his own class so that cornered class c would be forced to accept an alliance with ichinose s class d   then declares that alliance after class a is eliminated  identified class a s three vips by attacking at night and watching the guards rush to protect wang mei yu  sato maya and yukimura teruhiko  passed the names to class b  class c places second  the alliance with class d is now open  is the object of hiyori s unspoken confession  she resolves to defeat him in this exam  fights him on the beach  ryuuen concedes and vows no mercy from here on  declares the c d alliance with her class  commands him in class c  hashimoto loses a duel to hirata  uses her as recon commander over the radio","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Depth review: survival game mastermind<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.14–251<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leads Class C onto the uninhabited island for the third straight year, under the Survival Game exam rules.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I surrender.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There&#x27;s nothing in the rules against it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll make it official here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Runs out of ammunition against Ryuuen and Ibuki, eliminates Ibuki with a paintball to the thigh, then defeats Ryuuen by throwing a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on impact.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Allowed Class B&#x27;s surprise attack on his own class so that cornered Class C would be forced to accept an alliance with Ichinose&#x27;s Class D — then declares that alliance after Class A is eliminated.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Identified Class A&#x27;s three VIPs by attacking at night and watching the guards rush to protect Wang Mei-Yu, Satō Maya and Yukimura Teruhiko; passed the names to Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C places second; the alliance with Class D is now open.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Is the object of Hiyori&#x27;s unspoken confession; she resolves to defeat him in this exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Fights him on the beach; Ryuuen concedes and vows no mercy from here on.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Declares the C–D alliance with her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Commands him in Class C; Hashimoto loses a duel to Hirata.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Uses her as recon commander over the radio.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2\">→ After: Ch.1 — depth read: the survival game opens<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi sanada-kousei shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 1   depth read  the survival game opens arrives on the same uninhabited island for his third straight year  notes the grid is now a o   1 15  larger than last year s a j   1 10   maybe  but speculating now won t tell us anything   looks like we re finally arriving   an expulsion from the class whose three vip s get taken out first  huh  well  i figured they d pull something like that  concludes the expulsion can be minimized  victims with protection points  but that fear of expulsion will force combat eventually   a draw decided by luck is worse  class c starts at area e12  ryuen c12  horikita g12  ichinose i12  talks through the rules and strategy with him on the ship and beach  has him draw the starting position lot  hears her point about the food shortage forcing event participation  exam rules  3 nights 4 days  roles commander vip guard analyst scout  global gps shutdown  1  individual  3  identity check  5  first wiped out class selects one for expulsion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.1 — depth read: the survival game opens<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.14–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arrives on the same uninhabited island for his third straight year; notes the grid is now A–O × 1–15 (larger than last year&#x27;s A–J × 1–10).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"sanada-kousei.html\">Sanada Kōsei<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Maybe. But speculating now won&#x27;t tell us anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Looks like we&#x27;re finally arriving.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;An expulsion from the class whose three VIP&#x27;s get taken out first, huh? Well, I figured they&#x27;d pull something like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Concludes the expulsion can be minimized (victims with Protection Points) but that fear of expulsion will force combat eventually — a draw decided by luck is worse.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C starts at area E12 (Ryūen C12, Horikita G12, Ichinose I12).<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Talks through the rules and strategy with him on the ship and beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.14–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sanada Kōsei<\/b> Has him draw the starting-position lot.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Hears her point about the food shortage forcing event participation.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Exam rules: 3 nights/4 days; roles Commander/VIP/Guard/Analyst/Scout; Global GPS Shutdown ×1, Individual ×3, Identity Check ×5; first wiped-out class selects one for expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-1\">← Before: Depth review: survival game mastermind<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-3\">→ After: Arrival: the ship, Hashimoto&#x27;s complaints and the landing order<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-3","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"narration spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka arrival  the ship  hashimoto s complaints and the landing order cruise ship crossing to the same uninhabited island at just past 8 a m  ayanokoji and hashimoto wait in the ship s cafe to disembark  the third years are on their third straight uninhabited island exam  and the stage is the exact same island as last year   the schedule moved up about a month from prior years   looks like we re finally arriving   ah  i m sleepy  i should ve gone to bed a little earlier yesterday   well then  i wonder what kind of troublesome  no  pain in the ass exam is waiting for us this year  new gym clothes were distributed to all third years on boarding   jersey tops and bottoms plus shirts  nearly identical to the usual ones but with slightly thicker fabric   but isn t this unbearable for students preparing for entrance exams  being pulled away from their desks at this time of year  have the third years up until now never complained about this   who knows  but i did see shimazaki bringing a set of study materials onto the ship   so he s stuck studying even on the ship  huh   they wouldn t cut into our precious summer vacation  would they  if that s how they  make up for it  then spare me  an onboard announcement orders third years to leave all personal belongings  including phones  in their rooms and change into the designated gym clothes   the fact that the first and second years haven t been called yet  does that mean  by any chance  that they won t be landing on the uninhabited island right away   maybe  but speculating now won t tell us anything   true","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-3\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Arrival: the ship, Hashimoto&#x27;s complaints and the landing order<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.14–16<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Cruise ship crossing to the same uninhabited island at just past 8 a.m.; Ayanokōji and Hashimoto wait in the ship&#x27;s café to disembark.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Looks like we&#x27;re finally arriving.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Ah~, I&#x27;m sleepy. I should&#x27;ve gone to bed a little earlier yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Well then... I wonder what kind of troublesome, no, pain-in-the-ass exam is waiting for us this year.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> The third-years are on their third straight uninhabited-island exam, and the stage is the exact same island as last year — the schedule moved up about a month from prior years.<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> New gym clothes were distributed to all third-years on boarding — jersey tops and bottoms plus shirts, nearly identical to the usual ones but with slightly thicker fabric.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But isn&#x27;t this unbearable for students preparing for entrance exams? Being pulled away from their desks at this time of year. Have the third-years up until now never complained about this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who knows. But I did see Shimazaki bringing a set of study materials onto the ship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So he&#x27;s stuck studying even on the ship, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;They wouldn&#x27;t cut into our precious summer vacation, would they? If that&#x27;s how they &#x27;make up for it&#x27;, then spare me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> An onboard announcement orders third-years to leave all personal belongings, including phones, in their rooms and change into the designated gym clothes.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The fact that the first and second-years haven&#x27;t been called yet... does that mean, by any chance, that they won&#x27;t be landing on the uninhabited island right away?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Maybe. But speculating now won&#x27;t tell us anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;True...&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-2\">← Before: Ch.1 — depth read: the survival game opens<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p17-1\">→ After: Disembarkation: the grid, Nakanishi&#x27;s absence and the rules begin<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p17-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner narration spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka disembarkation  the grid  nakanishi s absence and the rules begin disembarks onto the beach  the island is more developed than last year and cardboard boxes are stacked up  a school official directs the third years to line up by class at their homeroom teachers  no first  or second years are landing yet   i remember quite a bit  talk about nostalgia  mashima sensei announces that nakanishi of class d is absent due to a fever  so his class begins with one less person  nakanishi s absence was touched on lightly with no heavy penalty  since it is ichinose s class and he is not a standout  the damage is likely minimal   the downside is real but small  the island grid has been subdivided  last year a j   1 10  this year a o   1 15  exam duration is a maximum of three nights and four days  ending early on a decisive result  daily hours 9 00 a m 6 00 p m   4 00 p m  on the final day  five mandatory roles  commander  1  gps tablet  tactics  cannot be eliminated  confined to hq f14  vip  3  plus guards  analysts  2 and scout  1  the exam is won by eliminating other classes  vips and guards with paint guns","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Disembarkation: the grid, Nakanishi&#x27;s absence and the rules begin<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.17–20<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Disembarks onto the beach; the island is more developed than last year and cardboard boxes are stacked up.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">A school official directs the third-years to line up by class at their homeroom teachers; no first- or second-years are landing yet.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I remember quite a bit. Talk about nostalgia.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">Mashima-sensei announces that Nakanishi of Class D is absent due to a fever, so his class begins with one less person.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Nakanishi&#x27;s absence was touched on lightly with no heavy penalty; since it is Ichinose&#x27;s class and he is not a standout, the damage is likely minimal — the downside is real but small.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> The island grid has been subdivided: last year A–J × 1–10, this year A–O × 1–15.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Exam duration is a maximum of three nights and four days, ending early on a decisive result; daily hours 9:00 a.m.–6:00 p.m. (4:00 p.m. on the final day).<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Five mandatory roles: Commander ×1 (GPS tablet, tactics, cannot be eliminated, confined to HQ F14), VIP ×3, plus Guards, Analysts ×2 and Scout ×1; the exam is won by eliminating other classes&#x27; VIPs and guards with paint guns.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p14-3\">← Before: Arrival: the ship, Hashimoto&#x27;s complaints and the landing order<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p21-1\">→ After: Tactics, watches, events and the expulsion penalty<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p21-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner narration spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka tactics  watches  events and the expulsion penalty on the beach  mashima sensei explains that handling assigned roles and the commander s limited use tactics will be critical   anyone here ever played a survival game  or know anything about it  no one in class c admits to knowing survival games  while class a s onizuka and ijuuin chat excitedly  suggesting prior experience  commander tactics  global gps shutdown  30 min   1  individual gps shutdown  30 min   3  identity check  reveals name and role at a location   5  the using commander can still see positions every five minutes  the global gps shutdown in particular could be a trump card for surprise attacks or escaping pursuers  but poor timing would waste it  wristwatches are distributed and must be worn 24 hours a day  removal risks disqualification  the watch shows vitals  area and direction  and issues an  out  when a paintball bursts on the sensor clothes   an expulsion from the class whose three vip s get taken out first  huh  well  i figured they d pull something like that   is this what you expected   well  pretty much  the expulsion can be minimized   a class can nominate a student with protection points   but fear of it could produce a draw  and since a draw is decided by luck  no class can keep running  combat is forced","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p21-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tactics, watches, events and the expulsion penalty<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.21–24<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the beach, Mashima-sensei explains that handling assigned roles and the commander&#x27;s limited-use tactics will be critical.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Anyone here ever played a survival game? Or know anything about it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;An expulsion from the class whose three VIP&#x27;s get taken out first, huh? Well, I figured they&#x27;d pull something like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Is this what you expected?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> No one in Class C admits to knowing survival games, while Class A&#x27;s Onizuka and Ijuuin chat excitedly, suggesting prior experience.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Commander tactics: Global GPS Shutdown (30 min, ×1), Individual GPS Shutdown (30 min, ×3), Identity Check (reveals name and role at a location, ×5); the using commander can still see positions every five minutes.<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The global GPS shutdown in particular could be a trump card for surprise attacks or escaping pursuers, but poor timing would waste it.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Wristwatches are distributed and must be worn 24 hours a day; removal risks disqualification. The watch shows vitals, area and direction, and issues an &quot;Out&quot; when a paintball bursts on the sensor clothes.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, pretty much—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The expulsion can be minimized — a class can nominate a student with Protection Points — but fear of it could produce a draw, and since a draw is decided by luck, no class can keep running; combat is forced.<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p17-1\">← Before: Disembarkation: the grid, Nakanishi&#x27;s absence and the rules begin<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p25-1\">→ After: Weapons: the prototype paintball guns<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p25-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka weapons  the prototype paintball guns mashima sensei unveils the guards  weapons   assault rifles  shotguns  submachine guns and handguns   and kishinami of kanto shooter co  explains the prototype system  the gym clothes incorporate proprietary temperature sensitive  color reacting and impact sensor technology  a strong hit to the abdomen or back links to the watch and declares an out  while a tiny edge hit may not activate  self reporting a malfunction induced out avoids penalty  but continuing while knowing one is out is a serious violation that can cost the whole class the exam  the lunchtime announcement and rules suggest the school is still going easy on them   an escape route far more lenient than expected","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p25-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Weapons: the prototype paintball guns<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.25–28<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mashima-sensei unveils the guards&#x27; weapons — assault rifles, shotguns, submachine guns and handguns — and Kishinami of Kanto Shooter Co. explains the prototype system.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">The gym clothes incorporate proprietary temperature-sensitive, color-reacting and impact-sensor technology; a strong hit to the abdomen or back links to the watch and declares an out, while a tiny edge hit may not activate.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">Self-reporting a malfunction-induced out avoids penalty, but continuing while knowing one is out is a serious violation that can cost the whole class the exam.<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">The lunchtime announcement and rules suggest the school is still going easy on them — an escape route far more lenient than expected.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p21-1\">← Before: Tactics, watches, events and the expulsion penalty<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p29-1\">→ After: The starting-position lottery and meager supplies<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p29-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner narration spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the starting position lottery and meager supplies mashima sensei has one representative per class draw lots for the four starting areas   c12  e12  g12  i12   about a 15 minute walk apart  the western c12  not sandwiched  and eastern i12  easy to escape  look advantageous  but the result is the same whoever draws  so he has sanada draw   there were a lot of messy explanations  but basically  it means we just have to win a class vs class survival game  right   pretty much   for now  we keep our distance from the other classes and wait things out  yeah  let s just have them crush each other  that would be the most graceful outcome  but the rules are built so that anyone would want to reap the benefits of the chaos  class c starts at e12  ryuen s b at c12  horikita s a at g12  ichinose s d at i12  sanada apologizes for not drawing a corner area  ayanokoji tells him not to worry  initial supplies are identical for every class and must be chosen now   leftovers are collected once the exam starts  the food is only two nutritional supplement blocks and mineral water per person  barely one lunch  securing food from event supplies becomes essential  which forces event participation and raises the risk of contact with other classes   clearly designed to induce combat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p29-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The starting-position lottery and meager supplies<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.29–30<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mashima-sensei has one representative per class draw lots for the four starting areas — C12, E12, G12, I12 — about a 15-minute walk apart.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;There were a lot of messy explanations, but basically, it means we just have to win a class vs class survival game, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Pretty much.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;For now, we keep our distance from the other classes and wait things out, yeah? Let&#x27;s just have them crush each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The western C12 (not sandwiched) and eastern I12 (easy to escape) look advantageous, but the result is the same whoever draws, so he has Sanada draw.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> That would be the most graceful outcome, but the rules are built so that anyone would want to reap the benefits of the chaos.<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Class C starts at E12; Ryūen&#x27;s B at C12, Horikita&#x27;s A at G12, Ichinose&#x27;s D at I12. Sanada apologizes for not drawing a corner area; Ayanokōji tells him not to worry.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Initial supplies are identical for every class and must be chosen now — leftovers are collected once the exam starts. The food is only two nutritional supplement blocks and mineral water per person, barely one lunch.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Securing food from event supplies becomes essential, which forces event participation and raises the risk of contact with other classes — clearly designed to induce combat.<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p25-1\">← Before: Weapons: the prototype paintball guns<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p31-1\">→ After: The food debate: Shiraishi, Sugio and Shimazaki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p31-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka sugio-hiroshi shimazaki-ikkei hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the food debate  shiraishi  sugio and shimazaki the class debates strategy over the meager food supply before the first event   looking at the rules  if we can keep running away  we won t lose for the time being  paintballs won t be consumed unless we fight  but the food problem is unavoidable   i definitely think aiming for nearby events is dangerous  if we re going to shoulder the risk of fighting poorly and getting out  why don t we just avoid class a from the start and cross the mountain  that way  it ll be easier for us to monopolize the events in the northeast area  other classes wouldn t bother traveling that far to fight us  right   i m against it  other classes might be thinking something similar  besides  even if we force ourselves to cross the mountain  there s no guarantee that events will necessarily occur in the northeast  is there   in that case  i think it s better not to go too far from the starting point until the first event begins  deriving the correct opening move is impossible at this stage  the shortest safe route north runs through the narrow riverside g8  where class a might arrive first   not moving  huh  i don t intend to deny that  but if we do that  it means we re resolving ourselves to a shootout right from the start  doesn t it  if  by some chance  three vips get taken out because of   okay  okay  i get what you want to say  sugio  but for now  let s look at the other supplies before we argue about that  our leader will squeeze out a good idea for us in the meantime  neither sugio nor shimazaki had the resolve to push their opinion and shoulder the responsibility  so they left the judgment to the leader","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p31-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The food debate: Shiraishi, Sugio and Shimazaki<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.31–32<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The class debates strategy over the meager food supply before the first event.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"sugio-hiroshi.html\">Sugio Hiroshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> &quot;Looking at the rules, if we can keep running away, we won&#x27;t lose for the time being. Paintballs won&#x27;t be consumed unless we fight, but the food problem is unavoidable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sugio Hiroshi<\/b> &quot;I definitely think aiming for nearby events is dangerous. If we&#x27;re going to shoulder the risk of fighting poorly and getting out, why don&#x27;t we just avoid Class A from the start and cross the mountain? That way, it&#x27;ll be easier…<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;m against it. Other classes might be thinking something similar. Besides, even if we force ourselves to cross the mountain, there&#x27;s no guarantee that events will necessarily occur in the northeast, is there?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I definitely think aiming for nearby events is dangerous. If we&#x27;re going to shoulder the risk of fighting poorly and getting out, why don&#x27;t we just avoid Class A from the start and cross the mountain? That way, it&#x27;ll be easier for us to monopolize the events in the northeast area. Other classes wouldn&#x27;t bother traveling that far to fight us, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In that case, I think it&#x27;s better not to go too far from the starting point until the first event begins.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Deriving the correct opening move is impossible at this stage; the shortest safe route north runs through the narrow riverside G8, where Class A might arrive first.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Not moving, huh? I don&#x27;t intend to deny that, but if we do that, it means we&#x27;re resolving ourselves to a shootout right from the start, doesn&#x27;t it? If, by some chance, three VIPs get taken out because of—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Okay, okay. I get what you want to say, Sugio, but for now, let&#x27;s look at the other supplies before we argue about that. Our leader will squeeze out a good idea for us in the meantime.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Neither Sugio nor Shimazaki had the resolve to push their opinion and shoulder the responsibility, so they left the judgment to the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p29-1\">← Before: The starting-position lottery and meager supplies<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p33-1\">→ After: Tents and weapons: supplying the class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p33-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner narration spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka tents and weapons  supplying the class the class sorts through the remaining boxes   small items  tents and weapons   and ayanokoji sets a supply guideline   tents  huh  we need to think about what to take and how much right away  the question is how much of the thinking we should burden ayanokouji with    i will provide a guideline for what supplies are necessary and how much to carry  if there are objections  voice them then with your reasoning  he sets a framework first and folds in classmates  views later   the optimal way to avoid wasting time  favors two  and multi person tents for shared carrying  since small tents become convenient as the class shrinks  forty main weapons are prepared   twenty assault rifles  ten submachine guns  ten shotguns   plus two handguns  each guard can carry one main weapon   they look real up close  this is my first time touching something like this   man  the shotguns look hard to use  though  and they re heavy  the assault rifle looks the most user friendly and well balanced  submachine guns and shotguns would only fill out the guard ranks   if we start with zero analysts  it looks like we can take two extra guns  what will you do   getting slightly more paintballs is certainly an advantage  but we will need analysts immediately  considering the trouble of carrying and managing the guns at that time  it s hard to say if it s worth it   we ll go with a policy of not increasing our luggage   so you don t intend to take any surplus  at times like this  human psychology makes us want to prepare at least a little insurance  one tends to get greedy   if we need something  we can just obtain it through an event  that s what the rules are for","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Tents and weapons: supplying the class<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.33–35<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The class sorts through the remaining boxes — small items, tents and weapons — and Ayanokōji sets a supply guideline.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Tents, huh? We need to think about what to take and how much right away. The question is how much of the thinking we should burden Ayanokouji with —&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I will provide a guideline for what supplies are necessary and how much to carry. If there are objections, voice them then with your reasoning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;They look real up close. This is my first time touching something like this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He sets a framework first and folds in classmates&#x27; views later — the optimal way to avoid wasting time; favors two- and multi-person tents for shared carrying, since small tents become convenient as the class shrinks.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Forty main weapons are prepared — twenty assault rifles, ten submachine guns, ten shotguns — plus two handguns; each Guard can carry one main weapon.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Man, the shotguns look hard to use, though. And they&#x27;re heavy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The assault rifle looks the most user-friendly and well-balanced; submachine guns and shotguns would only fill out the Guard ranks.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If we start with zero analysts, it looks like we can take two extra guns; what will you do?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Getting slightly more paintballs is certainly an advantage, but we will need analysts immediately. Considering the trouble of carrying and managing the guns at that time, it&#x27;s hard to say if it&#x27;s worth it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;ll go with a policy of not increasing our luggage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So you don&#x27;t intend to take any surplus. At times like this, human psychology makes us want to prepare at least a little insurance; one tends to get greedy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If we need something, we can just obtain it through an event. That&#x27;s what the rules are for.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p31-1\">← Before: The food debate: Shiraishi, Sugio and Shimazaki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p36-1\">→ After: Taking responsibility: I will be the one expelled<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p36-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi morishita-ai ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka taking responsibility  i will be the one expelled the class reacts with horror to the idea of naming an expulsion sacrifice before the exam  ayanokoji lets morishita float hashimoto s name  then intervenes   if hashimoto is willing to volunteer  that s fine  but unfortunately  i have already decided who will be expelled  and i won t change it even if there are objections   if we end up receiving the penalty  i ll take on that role   taking responsibility for defeat precisely because i am the leader  it sounds cool if i say it like that  but the reason is different  for better or worse  i m an outsider  not many days have gone by since i entered this class  if i  who joined to lead the class to victory  instead lead us to defeat  then bearing that responsibility is only logical   either way  you wouldn t be able to trust a leader who lost miserably without being able to do anything  right   as i just said  in the event that an expulsion occurs in the class  i want to confirm it s me  this is to prevent something like retracting it later  announcing and determining it in advance is unrelated to the rules of the exam  right   of course  these aren t words that should be spoken merely to ease the anxiety of my classmates  without a firm public commitment he could resist at the last moment and shift the blame onto someone else   announcing it in advance removes that escape  the declaration is a calculated move to galvanize the class  it buys their trust and unites them behind him  while costing him nothing he intends to pay  calm and strategically ruthless   deliberately lets the class squirm over the sacrifice before naming himself  knowing a leader who owns defeat is one they will follow  lets morishita name him as sacrifice  hashimoto is trapped into relying on ayanokoji s ability since he has no other route to class a  plays along with her proposal that hashimoto be the victim","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p36-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Taking responsibility: I will be the one expelled<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.36–39<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The class reacts with horror to the idea of naming an expulsion sacrifice before the exam; Ayanokōji lets Morishita float Hashimoto&#x27;s name, then intervenes.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"morishita-ai.html\">Morishita Ai<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If Hashimoto is willing to volunteer, that&#x27;s fine, but unfortunately, I have already decided who will be expelled, and I won&#x27;t change it even if there are objections.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If we end up receiving the penalty, I&#x27;ll take on that role.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Taking responsibility for defeat precisely because I am the leader. It sounds cool if I say it like that, but the reason is different. For better or worse, I&#x27;m an outsider. Not many days have gone by since I entered this class.…<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Taking responsibility for defeat precisely because I am the leader. It sounds cool if I say it like that, but the reason is different. For better or worse, I&#x27;m an outsider. Not many days have gone by since I entered this class. If I, who joined to lead the class to victory, instead lead us to defeat, then bearing that responsibility is only logical.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Either way, you wouldn&#x27;t be able to trust a leader who lost miserably without being able to do anything, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As I just said, in the event that an expulsion occurs in the class, I want to confirm it&#x27;s me. This is to prevent something like retracting it later. Announcing and determining it in advance is unrelated to the rules of the exam, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. These aren&#x27;t words that should be spoken merely to ease the anxiety of my classmates.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Without a firm public commitment he could resist at the last moment and shift the blame onto someone else — announcing it in advance removes that escape.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The declaration is a calculated move to galvanize the class: it buys their trust and unites them behind him, while costing him nothing he intends to pay.<span class=\"pg\">p.37–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and strategically ruthless — deliberately lets the class squirm over the sacrifice before naming himself, knowing a leader who owns defeat is one they will follow.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Lets Morishita name him as sacrifice; Hashimoto is trapped into relying on Ayanokōji&#x27;s ability since he has no other route to Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Morishita Ai<\/b> Plays along with her proposal that Hashimoto be the victim.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p33-1\">← Before: Tents and weapons: supplying the class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p40-1\">→ After: Assigning roles: guard, not commander<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p40-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi shimazaki-ikkei ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka assigning roles  guard  not commander mashima sensei leaves the class thirty minutes to assign the five roles or the school picks randomly   isn t the reason obvious  it s because i view ayanokouji as a special combat asset   my hope is to be a guard  two untagged lines follow his  guard  statement in the text   one approving the choice  one adding that it depends on finding a trustworthy commander  the translation leaves both speakers unmarked  so no  says  row is claimed for them  he had already ruled out vip  analyst and scout for himself  the choice was commander or guard  commander s gps overview is attractive  but as a guard he can demonstrate his ability without relying on others   and class c lacks physically gifted students to execute orders  appoints shimazaki as commander  takemoto shiraishi nishikawa as vips  sanada nakajima as analysts  tsukaji as scout  the rest as guards  chooses him as commander by elimination despite doubts about his flexibility  takes full responsibility for the outcome to ease his burden  rebuts the suggestion he be commander  relies on his case for him as guard","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Assigning roles: guard, not commander<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.40–43<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Mashima-sensei leaves the class thirty minutes to assign the five roles or the school picks randomly.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> &quot;Isn&#x27;t the reason obvious? It&#x27;s because I view Ayanokouji as a special combat asset.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My hope is to be a guard.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">He had already ruled out VIP, analyst and scout for himself; the choice was commander or guard. Commander&#x27;s GPS overview is attractive, but as a guard he can demonstrate his ability without relying on others — and Class C lacks…<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two untagged lines follow his &quot;guard&quot; statement in the text — one approving the choice, one adding that it depends on finding a trustworthy commander. The translation leaves both speakers unmarked, so no `[says]` row is claimed for them.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He had already ruled out VIP, analyst and scout for himself; the choice was commander or guard. Commander&#x27;s GPS overview is attractive, but as a guard he can demonstrate his ability without relying on others — and Class C lacks physically gifted students to execute orders.<span class=\"pg\">p.41–42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Appoints Shimazaki as commander, Takemoto/Shiraishi/Nishikawa as VIPs, Sanada/Nakajima as analysts, Tsukaji as scout, the rest as guards.<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Chooses him as commander by elimination despite doubts about his flexibility; takes full responsibility for the outcome to ease his burden.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Rebuts the suggestion he be commander; relies on his Case for him as guard.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p36-1\">← Before: Taking responsibility: I will be the one expelled<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p44-1\">→ After: Briefing Shimazaki: report everything to Shiraishi<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p44-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"shimazaki-ikkei shiraishi-asuka yoshida-kenta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka briefing shimazaki  report everything to shiraishi pulls shimazaki aside before parting   they cannot speak directly until the exam ends   no matter how trivial  i want you to report anything you find strange or unusual without hesitation   that s not it  the more you feel the weight of the commander position  the more likely you are to miss what s right under your nose  a commander from another class laughed  or got angry  changes in the gps that feels slightly off but doesn t seem worth mentioning  please report anything that concerns you personally  shimazaki   that s true  which is why it can t just be anyone  let s narrow it down to one person   it doesn t matter who  but let s see  let s go with shiraishi for now  that should make things easier for you as well   there s no need to favor only yoshida  to me  both of you are important friends   in other words  you can tell shiraishi anything and everything  no matter what it is  routes shimazaki s reports through shiraishi deliberately   knowing he likes her  this raises their contact  and she is the vip he reads most clearly  quietly matchmaking while optimizing command  uses the briefing to increase shimazaki s contact with shiraishi under the guise of avoiding  telephone game  confusion  briefs him on reporting  knows of his feelings for shiraishi  names her as the single reporting conduit  trusts her judgment most  cites him as another important friend to defuse shimazaki s objection  safety goggles recommended at all times  sensors are on the gym uniform only  though hits register through a tracksuit","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Briefing Shimazaki: report everything to Shiraishi<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.44–45<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pulls Shimazaki aside before parting — they cannot speak directly until the exam ends.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shimazaki-ikkei.html\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"yoshida-kenta.html\">Yoshida Kenta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;No matter how trivial, I want you to report anything you find strange or unusual without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s not it. The more you feel the weight of the commander position, the more likely you are to miss what&#x27;s right under your nose. A commander from another class laughed, or got angry. Changes in the GPS that feels slightly…<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s true, which is why it can&#x27;t just be anyone. Let&#x27;s narrow it down to one person.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s not it. The more you feel the weight of the commander position, the more likely you are to miss what&#x27;s right under your nose. A commander from another class laughed, or got angry. Changes in the GPS that feels slightly off but doesn&#x27;t seem worth mentioning. Please report anything that concerns you personally, Shimazaki.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It doesn&#x27;t matter who, but let&#x27;s see. Let&#x27;s go with Shiraishi for now. That should make things easier for you as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no need to favor only Yoshida. To me, both of you are important friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In other words, you can tell Shiraishi anything and everything, no matter what it is.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Routes Shimazaki&#x27;s reports through Shiraishi deliberately — knowing he likes her, this raises their contact, and she is the VIP he reads most clearly.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Quietly matchmaking while optimizing command: uses the briefing to increase Shimazaki&#x27;s contact with Shiraishi under the guise of avoiding &quot;telephone game&quot; confusion.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shimazaki Ikkei<\/b> Briefs him on reporting; knows of his feelings for Shiraishi.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Names her as the single reporting conduit; trusts her judgment most.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yoshida Kenta<\/b> Cites him as another important friend to defuse Shimazaki&#x27;s objection.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Safety goggles recommended at all times; sensors are on the gym uniform only, though hits register through a tracksuit.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p40-1\">← Before: Assigning roles: guard, not commander<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-1\">→ After: Ch.2 — depth read: the ambush and the alliance reveal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kitou-hayato hashimoto-masayoshi shiina-hiyori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2   depth read  the ambush and the alliance reveal  even if we were to pick up the pace  the enemy would find out within five minutes  if they knew we d quickened our movement  class a would do the same   yeah  if i determine the supplies are necessary  i ll go for them without hesitation   i believe this class s ultimate goal  the rank we should be aiming for  is second place   the reason is simple and clear  i m thinking we can give first place to ichinose s class   you could say a provisional agreement has been made  the other side is keen on it   everyone  run  now   the answer is quite simple  ryuuen s class deliberately kept its distance after the start to make it seem like they were avoiding engagement  rotates a magazine removed weapon to each vip as misdirection so enemies cannot identify vips by their lack of a gun  deduced ryuen s fake retreat   global gps shutdown ambush from the frozen position updates  is asked by him to confirm he aims to win  relies on his counterattack during the ambush  relays instructions and reports  both react to the ambush  vip in the front row  struggles to keep up during the retreat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 — depth read: the ambush and the alliance reveal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.46–85<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Even if we were to pick up the pace, the enemy would find out within five minutes. If they knew we&#x27;d quickened our movement, Class A would do the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. If I determine the supplies are necessary, I&#x27;ll go for them without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I believe this class&#x27;s ultimate goal, the rank we should be aiming for, is second place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The reason is simple and clear. I&#x27;m thinking we can give first place to Ichinose&#x27;s class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You could say a provisional agreement has been made. The other side is keen on it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Everyone, run! Now!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The answer is quite simple. Ryuuen&#x27;s class deliberately kept its distance after the start to make it seem like they were avoiding engagement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Rotates a magazine-removed weapon to each VIP as misdirection so enemies cannot identify VIPs by their lack of a gun.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Deduced Ryūen&#x27;s fake-retreat + Global GPS Shutdown ambush from the frozen position updates.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Is asked by him to confirm he aims to win; relies on his counterattack during the ambush.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Relays instructions and reports; both react to the ambush.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> VIP in the front row; struggles to keep up during the retreat.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p44-1\">← Before: Briefing Shimazaki: report everything to Shiraishi<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-2\">→ After: The first reports: other classes&#x27; commanders and movements<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner narration spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the first reports  other classes  commanders and movements leads class c north in scattered formation from e12 toward g8  head of the group  the self sacrifice declaration had a greater effect than expected  the first strategy is to head north and be first across g8  avoiding the pincer between ryuuen west and horikita east  commanders revealed  matsushita  a  kaneda  b  ichinose  d    only ichinose commands her own class  matsushita is a solid  fitting choice for class a s honor student makeup  kaneda is safe and unremarkable   unlikely to shine or blunder  first gps update  class b heading north into c11  class a in g11 also north  class d east toward j12   all avoiding early conflict   even if we were to pick up the pace  the enemy would find out within five minutes  if they knew we d quickened our movement  class a would do the same  that would be nothing more than an act that increases risk   that s the situation  i don t want to do anything that would give another class the chance to profit from our conflict   yeah  if i determine the supplies are necessary  i ll go for them without hesitation  cautious and controlling   refuses to quicken pace because the five minute gps update exposes it  commits to fighting for supplies if needed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The first reports: other classes&#x27; commanders and movements<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.46–50<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Leads Class C north in scattered formation from E12 toward G8, head of the group.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Even if we were to pick up the pace, the enemy would find out within five minutes. If they knew we&#x27;d quickened our movement, Class A would do the same. That would be nothing more than an act that increases risk.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s the situation. I don&#x27;t want to do anything that would give another class the chance to profit from our conflict.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. If I determine the supplies are necessary, I&#x27;ll go for them without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> The self-sacrifice declaration had a greater effect than expected; the first strategy is to head north and be first across G8, avoiding the pincer between Ryuuen west and Horikita east.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Commanders revealed: Matsushita (A), Kaneda (B), Ichinose (D) — only Ichinose commands her own class.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Matsushita is a solid, fitting choice for Class A&#x27;s honor-student makeup; Kaneda is safe and unremarkable — unlikely to shine or blunder.<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> First GPS update: Class B heading north into C11, Class A in G11 also north, Class D east toward J12 — all avoiding early conflict.<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cautious and controlling — refuses to quicken pace because the five-minute GPS update exposes it; commits to fighting for supplies if needed.<span class=\"pg\">p.46–50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-1\">← Before: Ch.2 — depth read: the ambush and the alliance reveal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p51-1\">→ After: Halting for weapons practice; the Kōenji question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p51-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka halting for weapons practice  the koenji question class stops to learn weapon handling as yoshida and morishita urge caution about fighting before they know the guns   it s not like i decided this because yoshida told me to  i was also thinking we should wait and see for a bit   ten minutes have passed and we ve gotten a small glimpse of each class s intentions  our primary objective was to pass through g8 first  but allow me to revise that  first  we ll learn how to properly handle our weapons here and once we re ready to fight  we ll check the gps positions again   i can t say for sure  but if anything  the usual koenji has no motivation  in almost every exam  he does as he pleases  last year s island was an exception to koenji s apathy because of his  complete freedom until graduation  bet with horikita  which she lost   he is now a free agent  but he could still be bought with points   have the commander identify the gps of the student who started acting alone   i don t mind  it s worth a try  let s use one as a test  has nishikawa test whether a second vip can contact the commander while she is speaking   confirms the line is one to one and busy when occupied   tell them i want to know the movements of the three classes every five minutes until the event starts   let s decide on our positions and formation for when the whole class moves together from now on   i considered that at one point  but i figured it s important to place someone who can react instantly in the rear precisely because she can  besides  shiraishi isn t good at raising her voice and it won t carry far  but nishikawa  on the other hand  has a loud voice  disperses the three vips across front middle rear rows and places fast responders to the rear so enemies can t wipe the class out at once  probing and efficient   uses the lull to gather intel  commander loopholes  radio line limits  koenji s identity  and locks down formation and communications","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Halting for weapons practice; the Kōenji question<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.51–56<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class stops to learn weapon handling as Yoshida and Morishita urge caution about fighting before they know the guns.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not like I decided this because Yoshida told me to. I was also thinking we should wait and see for a bit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Ten minutes have passed and we&#x27;ve gotten a small glimpse of each class&#x27;s intentions. Our primary objective was to pass through G8 first, but allow me to revise that. First, we&#x27;ll learn how to properly handle our weapons here and…<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t say for sure, but if anything, the usual Koenji has no motivation. In almost every exam, he does as he pleases.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ten minutes have passed and we&#x27;ve gotten a small glimpse of each class&#x27;s intentions. Our primary objective was to pass through G8 first, but allow me to revise that. First, we&#x27;ll learn how to properly handle our weapons here and once we&#x27;re ready to fight, we&#x27;ll check the GPS positions again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Last year&#x27;s island was an exception to Kōenji&#x27;s apathy because of his &quot;complete freedom until graduation&quot; bet with Horikita, which she lost — he is now a free agent, but he could still be bought with points.<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Have the commander identify the GPS of the student who started acting alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t mind. It&#x27;s worth a try. Let&#x27;s use one as a test.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Has Nishikawa test whether a second VIP can contact the commander while she is speaking — confirms the line is one-to-one and busy when occupied.<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Tell them I want to know the movements of the three classes every five minutes until the event starts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s decide on our positions and formation for when the whole class moves together from now on.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I considered that at one point, but I figured it&#x27;s important to place someone who can react instantly in the rear precisely because she can. Besides, Shiraishi isn&#x27;t good at raising her voice and it won&#x27;t carry far. But Nishikawa, on the other hand, has a loud voice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Disperses the three VIPs across front/middle/rear rows and places fast responders to the rear so enemies can&#x27;t wipe the class out at once.<span class=\"pg\">p.55–56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Probing and efficient — uses the lull to gather intel (commander loopholes, radio line limits, Kōenji&#x27;s identity) and locks down formation and communications.<span class=\"pg\">p.51–56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p46-2\">← Before: The first reports: other classes&#x27; commanders and movements<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p58-1\">→ After: The weapon lecture and the misdirection plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p58-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"toba-shigeru kitou-hayato ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the weapon lecture and the misdirection plan has shimazaki check what commanders can and cannot do   direct contact and messages are banned  screenshots are blacked out  but gps markers can be annotated   i had him look into it because i thought there might be things he could do outside of his official authority as commander  but it seems they re being monitored more strictly than i anticipated   that s why i m going to take the time now to properly lecture you all on how to use these weapons   then  after the lecture  i want one of the guards who isn t confident in their fighting ability to temporarily give their weapon to one of the three vips  one after another   one method for identifying another class s vip is to see if they can use a weapon  if we get into an unexpected fight  it s entirely conceivable that they ll prioritize targeting any student without one   the firing chamber basically  there might be cases where a round remains inside even after you remove the magazine   regarding this type of firearm  ijuuin from horikita s class is very knowledgeable and he taught me a few things in the past  his firearms knowledge actually comes from the white room  the ijuuin story is a cover toba cannot verify  rotates a magazine removed  chamber checked weapon among the vips as misdirection so enemies cannot identify them by their lack of a gun  teaches him to check the chamber  notes he is athletic and a capable fighter  is pressed by him for a commitment to win","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p58-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The weapon lecture and the misdirection plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.58–63<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Has Shimazaki check what commanders can and cannot do — direct contact and messages are banned, screenshots are blacked out, but GPS markers can be annotated.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"toba-shigeru.html\">Toba Shigeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I had him look into it because I thought there might be things he could do outside of his official authority as commander, but it seems they&#x27;re being monitored more strictly than I anticipated.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s why I&#x27;m going to take the time now to properly lecture you all on how to use these weapons.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then, after the lecture, I want one of the guards who isn&#x27;t confident in their fighting ability to temporarily give their weapon to one of the three VIPs, one after another.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;One method for identifying another class&#x27;s VIP is to see if they can use a weapon. If we get into an unexpected fight, it&#x27;s entirely conceivable that they&#x27;ll prioritize targeting any student without one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The firing chamber—basically, there might be cases where a round remains inside even after you remove the magazine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Regarding this type of firearm, Ijuuin from Horikita&#x27;s class is very knowledgeable and he taught me a few things in the past.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> His firearms knowledge actually comes from the White Room; the Ijuuin story is a cover Toba cannot verify.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Rotates a magazine-removed, chamber-checked weapon among the VIPs as misdirection so enemies cannot identify them by their lack of a gun.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Toba Shigeru<\/b> Teaches him to check the chamber; notes he is athletic and a capable fighter.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Is pressed by him for a commitment to win.<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p51-1\">← Before: Halting for weapons practice; the Kōenji question<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p64-1\">→ After: Announcing the alliance; postponing the vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p64-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi matoba-shinji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka announcing the alliance  postponing the vote addresses the whole class after kitou s question and reveals the true aim   i believe this class s ultimate goal  the rank we should be aiming for  is second place   the reason is simple and clear  i m thinking we can give first place to ichinose s class   i transferred to raise this class to class a  but given that the hurdle is actually very high  we must use a strategy to win efficiently   that strategy  i believe  lies in an alliance with ichinose s class   in this survival exam  we re supposed to be fighting three other classes  that means we re facing nearly 120 enemies  but an alliance can change that premise   you can refuse or rather  reject the idea but it s not something we can pick up and drop as we please   look  we re not going to form an alliance just from this one discussion  there s no way  that said  i m not going to reject the idea out of hand  either   my bad for bringing this up so suddenly  like matoba and the others said  let s talk about the alliance again after this special exam is over  for now  just forget we had this conversation  introduces the c d alliance deliberately when the class is desperate  then withdraws the immediate vote   a big step toward making them accept it later  the backlash is expected and welcomed  a single change in perspective can overturn it  and postponing is not the same as abandoning  he tries to interrupt and whisper that now is the wrong time  ayanokoji ignores him and says it anyway  faces his criticism of the  selfish proposition  and lets him think he has won the postponement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p64-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Announcing the alliance; postponing the vote<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.64–68<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Addresses the whole class after Kitou&#x27;s question and reveals the true aim.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"matoba-shinji.html\">Matoba Shinji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I believe this class&#x27;s ultimate goal, the rank we should be aiming for, is second place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The reason is simple and clear. I&#x27;m thinking we can give first place to Ichinose&#x27;s class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I transferred to raise this class to Class A. But given that the hurdle is actually very high, we must use a strategy to win efficiently.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That strategy, I believe, lies in an alliance with Ichinose&#x27;s class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In this survival exam, we&#x27;re supposed to be fighting three other classes. That means we&#x27;re facing nearly 120 enemies, but an alliance can change that premise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You can refuse—or rather, reject the idea—but it&#x27;s not something we can pick up and drop as we please.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Look, we&#x27;re not going to form an alliance just from this one discussion. There&#x27;s no way. That said, I&#x27;m not going to reject the idea out of hand, either.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;My bad for bringing this up so suddenly. Like Matoba and the others said, let&#x27;s talk about the alliance again after this special exam is over. For now, just forget we had this conversation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Introduces the C–D alliance deliberately when the class is desperate, then withdraws the immediate vote — a big step toward making them accept it later.<span class=\"pg\">p.65–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The backlash is expected and welcomed; a single change in perspective can overturn it, and postponing is not the same as abandoning.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> He tries to interrupt and whisper that now is the wrong time; Ayanokōji ignores him and says it anyway.<span class=\"pg\">p.65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matoba Shinji<\/b> Faces his criticism of the &quot;selfish proposition&quot; and lets him think he has won the postponement.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p58-1\">← Before: The weapon lecture and the misdirection plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p68-1\">→ After: The surprise attack and the retreat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p68-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kitou-hayato ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the surprise attack and the retreat senses the rustle of trees before anyone else as the class stands at ease after the alliance debate   everyone  run  now   we ll leave this place to kitou and the others and retreat   the answer is quite simple  ryuuen s class deliberately kept its distance after the start to make it seem like they were avoiding engagement   judging by the speed of their decision  they must have been planning to use it from the moment they understood the rules of the special exam   no  this is about our limit  if we force ourselves to keep going  we ll only increase the risk of our allies dropping out  deduced ryuen s fake retreat   global gps shutdown ambush from the frozen position updates  stops the retreat when laggards start falling behind  calm under sudden violence   issues one word of warning  abandons the rear to kitou  and manages the retreat pace to prevent further dropouts  leaves him and several boys to hold off the ambush while the front line withdraws","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The surprise attack and the retreat<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.68–73<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Senses the rustle of trees before anyone else as the class stands at ease after the alliance debate.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kitou-hayato.html\">Kitō Hayato<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;—Everyone, run! Now!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;ll leave this place to Kitou and the others and retreat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The answer is quite simple. Ryuuen&#x27;s class deliberately kept its distance after the start to make it seem like they were avoiding engagement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Judging by the speed of their decision, they must have been planning to use it from the moment they understood the rules of the special exam.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, this is about our limit. If we force ourselves to keep going, we&#x27;ll only increase the risk of our allies dropping out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Deduced Ryūen&#x27;s fake-retreat + Global GPS Shutdown ambush from the frozen position updates; stops the retreat when laggards start falling behind.<span class=\"pg\">p.72–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm under sudden violence — issues one word of warning, abandons the rear to Kitou, and manages the retreat pace to prevent further dropouts.<span class=\"pg\">p.69–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kitō Hayato<\/b> Leaves him and several boys to hold off the ambush while the front line withdraws.<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p64-1\">← Before: Announcing the alliance; postponing the vote<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.3 — depth read: pressure, provisioning and camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p86-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"yamamura-miki hashimoto-masayoshi matoba-shinji ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3   depth read  pressure  provisioning and camp  if you  yamamura  can just stay in for even one second longer without getting out  that alone is useful   head north and class a s there to greet you  head east and it s class d  there s no escaping a scenario where we get pincered by class b coming up from behind   if i were ryuuen no  if i were any other class  i d be grateful to see class c moving in one big clump   this is my decision as the one temporarily in charge of class c   i ll go to i10 alone   basically  if we don t attack  we won t be attacked  operate under that assumption   i can t say something baseless   i suppose it s because i don t dislike the deserted island exam itself  goes alone to i10 and secures food supplies while the d12 group draws class b away  divides provisions equally and explains small portion eating  rejects grouping up   it would let other classes ignore them and gather supplies freely   and splits the team to cover both food drops  reassures her that simply surviving is a contribution  discusses strategy and the gloomy mood  listens to his story in the tent  rebuts his group up and escape plans  reasons about how ryuen would exploit class c s mistakes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 — depth read: pressure, provisioning and camp<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.86–118<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"matoba-shinji.html\">Matoba Shinji<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you, Yamamura, can just stay in for even one second longer without getting out, that alone is useful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Head north and Class A&#x27;s there to greet you; head east and it&#x27;s Class D. There&#x27;s no escaping a scenario where we get pincered by Class B coming up from behind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I were Ryuuen—no, if I were any other class, I&#x27;d be grateful to see Class C moving in one big clump.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is my decision as the one temporarily in charge of Class C.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll go to I10 alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Basically, if we don&#x27;t attack, we won&#x27;t be attacked. Operate under that assumption.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can&#x27;t say something baseless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I suppose it&#x27;s because I don&#x27;t dislike the deserted island exam itself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Goes alone to I10 and secures food supplies while the D12 group draws Class B away; divides provisions equally and explains small-portion eating.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Rejects grouping up — it would let other classes ignore them and gather supplies freely — and splits the team to cover both food drops.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Reassures her that simply surviving is a contribution.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Discusses strategy and the gloomy mood; listens to his story in the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matoba Shinji<\/b> Rebuts his group-up and escape plans.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Reasons about how Ryūen would exploit Class C&#x27;s mistakes.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p68-1\">← Before: The surprise attack and the retreat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p91-1\">→ After: Event one: splitting for supplies<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p91-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka event one  splitting for supplies the first event begins  he directs the class from the f12 base as sanada reads the ten locations   the main unit will move to g13 and we ll form a separate detachment with four people to escort our vip  takemoto   just getting there wouldn t be a problem  but no matter how safe d14 is  i want to avoid a situation where we can t find the event location  or the supplies are too much to carry back all at once   yeah  the base is an easy landmark  so f13 is fine  sends the main unit to g13 and a four person escort with takemoto to d14  keeps watch from f12 g12 for class b","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p91-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Event one: splitting for supplies<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.91–94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The first event begins; he directs the class from the F12 base as Sanada reads the ten locations.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The main unit will move to G13 and we&#x27;ll form a separate detachment with four people to escort our VIP, Takemoto.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Just getting there wouldn&#x27;t be a problem, but no matter how safe D14 is, I want to avoid a situation where we can&#x27;t find the event location, or the supplies are too much to carry back all at once.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yeah. The base is an easy landmark, so F13 is fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Sends the main unit to G13 and a four-person escort with Takemoto to D14; keeps watch from F12/G12 for Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.91–94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.3 — depth read: pressure, provisioning and camp<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1\">→ After: Reassuring Yamamura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"yamamura-miki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka reassuring yamamura notices yamamura s anxious look as the class prepares to depart   what is it  if you have a problem  i ll hear you out   that s not true  our class was half decimated due to my poor judgment  but at least we still have half of us left  as long as half of us are still here  it means there s still a chance to win   if you  yamamura  can just stay in for even one second longer without getting out  that alone is useful   even if you can t shoot  as long as you don t get shot  that alone is a huge plus for the class  you should remember that the value is the same  reframes survival itself as contribution   calmly turns yamamura s fear into a concrete  achievable role  reassures her that simply staying in the exam is useful","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Reassuring Yamamura<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.94<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Notices Yamamura&#x27;s anxious look as the class prepares to depart.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yamamura-miki.html\">Yamamura Miki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What is it? If you have a problem, I&#x27;ll hear you out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s not true. Our class was half-decimated due to my poor judgment, but at least we still have half of us left. As long as half of us are still here, it means there&#x27;s still a chance to win.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you, Yamamura, can just stay in for even one second longer without getting out, that alone is useful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even if you can&#x27;t shoot, as long as you don&#x27;t get shot, that alone is a huge plus for the class. You should remember that the value is the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reframes survival itself as contribution — calmly turns Yamamura&#x27;s fear into a concrete, achievable role.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamamura Miki<\/b> Reassures her that simply staying in the exam is useful.<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p91-1\">← Before: Event one: splitting for supplies<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p100-1\">→ After: The stalemate with Class B&#x27;s &quot;stalkers&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p100-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"narration spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the stalemate with class b s  stalkers  by 5 p m  the class has secured five supply sets  class b s main camp between g9 and g10 pins them in  five sets  200 rounds  1 5 kg rice  eight cans  nuts  chicken  a few provisions  15 liters of water   a minimal harvest from 39 crates   i can t exactly pull off something like the protagonist of an american action movie  at best  i d get taken down after defeating two or three of them   that d be rough  attacking them from our position is a complete suicide mission   head north and class a s there to greet you  head east and it s class d  there s no escaping a scenario where we get pincered by class b coming up from behind   i m sure they don t want to fight  but we d be crashing an event they re trying to claim in safety  right  clear eyed about the hopeless position   rejects both a heroic charge and a breakout  reading the other classes  incentives precisely","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The stalemate with Class B&#x27;s &quot;stalkers&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.100–103<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">By 5 p.m. the class has secured five supply sets; Class B&#x27;s main camp between G9 and G10 pins them in.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I can&#x27;t exactly pull off something like the protagonist of an American action movie. At best, I&#x27;d get taken down after defeating two or three of them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;d be rough. Attacking them from our position is a complete suicide mission.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Head north and Class A&#x27;s there to greet you; head east and it&#x27;s Class D. There&#x27;s no escaping a scenario where we get pincered by Class B coming up from behind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> Five sets: 200 rounds, 1.5 kg rice, eight cans, nuts, chicken, a few provisions, 15 liters of water — a minimal harvest from 39 crates.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m sure they don&#x27;t want to fight. But we&#x27;d be crashing an event they&#x27;re trying to claim in safety, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Clear-eyed about the hopeless position — rejects both a heroic charge and a breakout, reading the other classes&#x27; incentives precisely.<span class=\"pg\">p.101–103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p94-1\">← Before: Reassuring Yamamura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p104-1\">→ After: Going alone to I10<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p104-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"matoba-shinji hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka going alone to i10 the final 5 p m  event offers only d12 and i10  he decides to go after both   we re staying based in the southern area and securing the supplies   if we were only thinking about today  avoiding them would be fine  but tomorrow s event isn t until 11 00 am at the earliest   the other classes are the ones who desperately need supplies right now  if we group up  we d just be helping them out  huh   sorry  but we don t have time to debate this any further  this is my decision as the one temporarily in charge of class c   if i were ryuuen no  if i were any other class  i d be grateful to see class c moving in one big clump   i ll go to i10 alone   even so  i have no intention of changing my decision   after that  we ll regroup in one to one and a half hours  the primary rendezvous is f12  rejects matoba s group up plan because a large  slow moving clump would let other classes ignore them and gather supplies freely  starving class c by morning  splits the team   goes alone to i10 while takemoto hashimoto take d12   and sets f12 primary   h12 secondary rendezvous points  decisive and unyielding under dissent   makes the call alone and makes clear that objections carry the risk of expulsion  overrules his group up and eastward escape proposals  sends him with takemoto to d12  brushes off his alarm at going alone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p104-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Going alone to I10<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.104–107<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The final 5 p.m. event offers only D12 and I10; he decides to go after both.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"matoba-shinji.html\">Matoba Shinji<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re staying based in the southern area and securing the supplies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If we were only thinking about today, avoiding them would be fine. But tomorrow&#x27;s event isn&#x27;t until 11:00 AM at the earliest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The other classes are the ones who desperately need supplies right now. If we group up, we&#x27;d just be helping them out, huh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, but we don&#x27;t have time to debate this any further. This is my decision as the one temporarily in charge of Class C.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If I were Ryuuen—no, if I were any other class, I&#x27;d be grateful to see Class C moving in one big clump.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll go to I10 alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even so. I have no intention of changing my decision.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;After that, we&#x27;ll regroup in one to one and a half hours. The primary rendezvous is F12.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Rejects Matoba&#x27;s group-up plan because a large, slow-moving clump would let other classes ignore them and gather supplies freely, starving Class C by morning.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Splits the team — goes alone to I10 while Takemoto/Hashimoto take D12 — and sets F12 primary / H12 secondary rendezvous points.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Decisive and unyielding under dissent — makes the call alone and makes clear that objections carry the risk of expulsion.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matoba Shinji<\/b> Overrules his group-up and eastward-escape proposals.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Sends him with Takemoto to D12; brushes off his alarm at going alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p100-1\">← Before: The stalemate with Class B&#x27;s &quot;stalkers&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p119-1\">→ After: Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji and the G11 offensive<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p119-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke ryuuen-kakeru hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4   depth read  koenji and the g11 offensive  that s our common understanding  but there s just a certain  creepiness to it  it s because i don t understand the reason why he s still here instead of retiring   right now  everyone s focused on moving around the island  gathering supplies and staying healthy  but that s nothing more than a prelude   we re leaving now  we re going to secure the supplies and food at g11   enough idle talk  it s precisely because the enemy is closer that we must get there first   we ll wait here for five minutes   we re not using any tactics  if we save them  the enemy will have to remain constantly on guard  chooses to go on the offensive for g11 and deliberately delays twice by five minutes  saving tactics and exploiting the enemy s need to stay vigilant    i already knew the result  deduces the exam s true endgame is a chaotic firefight in a shrinking area  where stray rounds could eliminate vips  puzzled that he hasn t retired  keeps monitoring him as a wild card  anticipates his moves at g11 and positions the class for the confrontation  relies on him to steady the anxious class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p119-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji and the G11 offensive<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.119–150<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s our common understanding, but there&#x27;s just a certain... creepiness to it. It&#x27;s because I don&#x27;t understand the reason why he&#x27;s still here instead of retiring.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Right now, everyone&#x27;s focused on moving around the island, gathering supplies and staying healthy, but that&#x27;s nothing more than a prelude.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re leaving now. We&#x27;re going to secure the supplies and food at G11.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Enough idle talk. It&#x27;s precisely because the enemy is closer that we must get there first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;ll wait here for five minutes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;re not using any tactics. If we save them, the enemy will have to remain constantly on guard.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Chooses to go on the offensive for G11 and deliberately delays twice by five minutes, saving tactics and exploiting the enemy&#x27;s need to stay vigilant — &quot;I already knew the result.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Deduces the exam&#x27;s true endgame is a chaotic firefight in a shrinking area, where stray rounds could eliminate VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Puzzled that he hasn&#x27;t retired; keeps monitoring him as a wild card.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Anticipates his moves at G11 and positions the class for the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Relies on him to steady the anxious class.<span class=\"pg\">p.137–139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p104-1\">← Before: Going alone to I10<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p123-1\">→ After: Day two: Kōenji still alive; waiting strategy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p123-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka day two  koenji still alive  waiting strategy hears the first report of day two   no one is missing and koenji is still alive alone in d6   that s our common understanding  but there s just a certain  creepiness to it  it s because i don t understand the reason why he s still here instead of retiring   it s more accurate to say that s how i saw him  that s why i expected him to have already retired by this morning   this place is the same as last year  there shouldn t be anything new about it for koenji   unless the other classes make any suspicious moves  our basic strategy is to wait until an event occurs  finds koenji s continued presence  creepy  and unreadable   expected him to retire   and keeps monitoring his gps rather than dismissing him  discusses koenji s survival with him  she suggests leaving koenji alone  he agrees it is the common understanding but remains uneasy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p123-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Day two: Kōenji still alive; waiting strategy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.123–125<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hears the first report of day two — no one is missing and Kōenji is still alive alone in D6.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s our common understanding, but there&#x27;s just a certain... creepiness to it. It&#x27;s because I don&#x27;t understand the reason why he&#x27;s still here instead of retiring.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s more accurate to say that&#x27;s how I saw him. That&#x27;s why I expected him to have already retired by this morning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;This place is the same as last year. There shouldn&#x27;t be anything new about it for Koenji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Unless the other classes make any suspicious moves, our basic strategy is to wait until an event occurs.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Finds Kōenji&#x27;s continued presence &quot;creepy&quot; and unreadable — expected him to retire — and keeps monitoring his GPS rather than dismissing him.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Discusses Kōenji&#x27;s survival with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.123–124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> She suggests leaving Kōenji alone; he agrees it is the common understanding but remains uneasy.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p119-1\">← Before: Ch.4 — depth read: Kōenji and the G11 offensive<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p135-1\">→ After: Reading the shrinking map; deciding on G11<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p135-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"matoba-shinji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka reading the shrinking map  deciding on g11 after the perimeter is restricted  weighs how the four classes will move as the map shrinks   right now  everyone s focused on moving around the island  gathering supplies and staying healthy  but that s nothing more than a prelude   it s become more likely that the class that can secure the best position for the final firefight or the one that can seize even the slightest momentum  will be the victor   we re leaving now  we re going to secure the supplies and food at g11   enough idle talk  it s precisely because the enemy is closer that we must get there first  deduces the exam s endgame is a chaotic final firefight in the shrinking area  decides to strike rather than wait   he already knew the result  overrides his objection to the risky offensive","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p135-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Reading the shrinking map; deciding on G11<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.135–137<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the perimeter is restricted, weighs how the four classes will move as the map shrinks.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"matoba-shinji.html\">Matoba Shinji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Right now, everyone&#x27;s focused on moving around the island, gathering supplies and staying healthy, but that&#x27;s nothing more than a prelude.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s become more likely that the class that can secure the best position for the final firefight or the one that can seize even the slightest momentum, will be the victor.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re leaving now. We&#x27;re going to secure the supplies and food at G11.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Enough idle talk. It&#x27;s precisely because the enemy is closer that we must get there first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Deduces the exam&#x27;s endgame is a chaotic final firefight in the shrinking area; decides to strike rather than wait — he already knew the result.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matoba Shinji<\/b> Overrides his objection to the risky offensive.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p123-1\">← Before: Day two: Kōenji still alive; waiting strategy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p139-1\">→ After: The G11 standoff: waiting five minutes twice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p139-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"matoba-shinji hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the g11 standoff  waiting five minutes twice halts the class two or three minutes from the hidden class b positions   we ll wait here for five minutes   they don t have that luxury   we re not using any tactics  if we save them  the enemy will have to remain constantly on guard   we ll wait another five minutes   let s advance  once you find the enemy  you have my permission to attack without hesitation   also  matoba  you ll take command during the battle  delays twice by five minutes   saving tactics and forcing the enemy to stay constantly vigilant   then hands battlefield command to matoba  knowing the outcome already  patient and coldly calculating   times the engagement for the ideal moment and stays behind to protect the vips rather than take command  appoints him battlefield commander to coordinate the front line  manages the weapon alongside him  asks ayanokoji to stay back and protect the vips","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p139-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The G11 standoff: waiting five minutes twice<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.139–143<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Halts the class two or three minutes from the hidden Class B positions.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"matoba-shinji.html\">Matoba Shinji<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;ll wait here for five minutes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;They don&#x27;t have that luxury.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;re not using any tactics. If we save them, the enemy will have to remain constantly on guard.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We&#x27;ll wait another five minutes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s advance. Once you find the enemy, you have my permission to attack without hesitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Also, Matoba, you&#x27;ll take command during the battle.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Delays twice by five minutes — saving tactics and forcing the enemy to stay constantly vigilant — then hands battlefield command to Matoba, knowing the outcome already.<span class=\"pg\">p.139–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Patient and coldly calculating — times the engagement for the ideal moment and stays behind to protect the VIPs rather than take command.<span class=\"pg\">p.139–140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Matoba Shinji<\/b> Appoints him battlefield commander to coordinate the front line.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Manages the weapon alongside him; asks Ayanokōji to stay back and protect the VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.138, 140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p135-1\">← Before: Reading the shrinking map; deciding on G11<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-1\">→ After: Ch.5 — depth read: sealing the alliance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hashimoto-masayoshi kanzaki-ryuuji shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5   depth read  sealing the alliance  if you ve seen the kind of student ichinose is  you should understand that she can be trusted   it s not like taking first place one time will get them to class a   what s wrong  are you worried about the alliance after all   i suppose i ll gratefully accept your sentiment    to hashimoto offering to be his shield  let s join forces  that way  class c and class d can form a group of fifty   you should try to better understand just how incredible it is to be trusted  goes unarmed with hashimoto to negotiate the alliance with kanzaki s class d  securing their acceptance  trusts her to honor the alliance  she had pre briefed class d to accept them  persuades the class  hashimoto offers to shield him and voices private doubts  negotiates with him  defuses his armed welcome  and later urges him to trust in class d and know ichinose  discusses class d s trust with her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.5 — depth read: sealing the alliance<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.151–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you&#x27;ve seen the kind of student Ichinose is, you should understand that she can be trusted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not like taking first place one time will get them to Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What&#x27;s wrong? Are you worried about the alliance after all?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I suppose I&#x27;ll gratefully accept your sentiment.&quot; — to Hashimoto offering to be his shield<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s join forces. That way, Class C and Class D can form a group of fifty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should try to better understand just how incredible it is to be trusted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Goes unarmed with Hashimoto to negotiate the alliance with Kanzaki&#x27;s Class D, securing their acceptance.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Trusts her to honor the alliance; she had pre-briefed Class D to accept them.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Persuades the class; Hashimoto offers to shield him and voices private doubts.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Negotiates with him, defuses his armed welcome, and later urges him to trust in Class D and know Ichinose.<span class=\"pg\">p.156–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Discusses Class D&#x27;s trust with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p139-1\">← Before: The G11 standoff: waiting five minutes twice<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-2\">→ After: Moving to contact Class D; the class accepts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka moving to contact class d  the class accepts after the retreat  moves east toward class d at m10 as the map shrinks toward the center   if you ve seen the kind of student ichinose is  you should understand that she can be trusted   it s not like taking first place one time will get them to class a  if they were to carelessly throw away our alliance  the backlash would be greater than you can imagine  the collapse of a class that s been built on trust would be inevitable   what s wrong  are you worried about the alliance after all   i don t mind  in fact  actively speaking your mind is a benefit to me  not a detriment  argues ichinose can be trusted because betrayal would destroy the trust based class she built  encourages hashimoto s doubts as useful  persuades the class  fields hashimoto s private doubts","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Moving to contact Class D; the class accepts<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.151–154<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After the retreat, moves east toward Class D at M10 as the map shrinks toward the center.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If you&#x27;ve seen the kind of student Ichinose is, you should understand that she can be trusted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s not like taking first place one time will get them to Class A. If they were to carelessly throw away our alliance, the backlash would be greater than you can imagine. The collapse of a class that&#x27;s been built on trust would…<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What&#x27;s wrong? Are you worried about the alliance after all?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not like taking first place one time will get them to Class A. If they were to carelessly throw away our alliance, the backlash would be greater than you can imagine. The collapse of a class that&#x27;s been built on trust would be inevitable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don&#x27;t mind. In fact, actively speaking your mind is a benefit to me, not a detriment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Argues Ichinose can be trusted because betrayal would destroy the trust-based class she built; encourages Hashimoto&#x27;s doubts as useful.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Persuades the class; fields Hashimoto&#x27;s private doubts.<span class=\"pg\">p.151–154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-1\">← Before: Ch.5 — depth read: sealing the alliance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p154-1\">→ After: Going unarmed to negotiate<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p154-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"action spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka going unarmed to negotiate hands his weapon to matoba and walks unarmed toward class d s standby point with hashimoto   we ll wait here for now  i ll go talk to them by myself first   i suppose i ll gratefully accept your sentiment   it would be the same even if we had our weapons  standing up to them would be futile against their overwhelming numbers   we have no intention of attacking   but in reality  we have no desire to fight class d  first  let us talk   let s join forces  that way  class c and class d can form a group of fifty   right now  we need class d s help  and we believe we can be the strength that class d needs  walks unarmed into kanzaki s gun wall  argues that beating class c doesn t win the exam  and secures class d s acceptance of the alliance  negotiates with him at gunpoint  his calm win or lose logic and ichinose s prior briefing win him over  lets him come as a shield  grateful for his resolve","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p154-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Going unarmed to negotiate<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.154–157<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Hands his weapon to Matoba and walks unarmed toward Class D&#x27;s standby point with Hashimoto.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We&#x27;ll wait here for now. I&#x27;ll go talk to them by myself first.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I suppose I&#x27;ll gratefully accept your sentiment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It would be the same even if we had our weapons. Standing up to them would be futile against their overwhelming numbers.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We have no intention of attacking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But in reality, we have no desire to fight Class D. First, let us talk.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let&#x27;s join forces. That way, Class C and Class D can form a group of fifty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Right now, we need Class D&#x27;s help. And we believe we can be the strength that Class D needs.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Walks unarmed into Kanzaki&#x27;s gun wall, argues that beating Class C doesn&#x27;t win the exam, and secures Class D&#x27;s acceptance of the alliance.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Negotiates with him at gunpoint; his calm win-or-lose logic and Ichinose&#x27;s prior briefing win him over.<span class=\"pg\">p.155–157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Lets him come as a shield, grateful for his resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p151-2\">← Before: Moving to contact Class D; the class accepts<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p160-1\">→ After: The merged campsite and the talk with Kanzaki<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p160-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ichinose-honami shiraishi-asuka ayanokouji-atsuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the merged campsite and the talk with kanzaki the combined c d camp  class d treats the wary class c students as equals  lowering their guard   i m surprised  too  it s a strength that can t be seen from class rankings or test scores alone   to maintain an alliance  both sides must be equal  it would never work if the powerful party tried to dominate from above   if i m just stating my wishful thinking  i d want them to crush each other somewhere that doesn t involve us   i see  i appreciate that  but are you ok with that   such impressive loyalty   there s no  why  to it  we were hit with a surprise attack from ryuuen s class and lost half our classmates in an instant   you re overestimating me   can t you think of the alliance as insurance  just in case   you should try to better understand just how incredible it is to be trusted  frames the alliance as insurance that divides horikita s and ryuen s attention   it makes class c easier to operate  not a gift  humble about his own losses yet quietly pushing kanzaki to believe in class d s potential and trust  explains his motives  presses him to share ichinose s confidence and resolve  she entrusted command of class d to him  they discuss class d s trust building together  kanzaki s admiration of his father colors his high opinion of ayanokoji","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p160-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The merged campsite and the talk with Kanzaki<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.160–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The combined C–D camp; Class D treats the wary Class C students as equals, lowering their guard.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;m surprised, too. It&#x27;s a strength that can&#x27;t be seen from class rankings or test scores alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;To maintain an alliance, both sides must be equal. It would never work if the powerful party tried to dominate from above.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If I&#x27;m just stating my wishful thinking, I&#x27;d want them to crush each other somewhere that doesn&#x27;t involve us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.161<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. I appreciate that, but are you ok with that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Such impressive loyalty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s no &#x27;why&#x27; to it. We were hit with a surprise attack from Ryuuen&#x27;s class and lost half our classmates in an instant.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You&#x27;re overestimating me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can&#x27;t you think of the alliance as insurance, just in case?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should try to better understand just how incredible it is to be trusted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Frames the alliance as insurance that divides Horikita&#x27;s and Ryūen&#x27;s attention — it makes Class C easier to operate, not a gift.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Humble about his own losses yet quietly pushing Kanzaki to believe in Class D&#x27;s potential and trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Explains his motives; presses him to share Ichinose&#x27;s confidence and resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.163–166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She entrusted command of Class D to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> They discuss Class D&#x27;s trust-building together.<span class=\"pg\">p.160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> Kanzaki&#x27;s admiration of his father colors his high opinion of Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p154-1\">← Before: Going unarmed to negotiate<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p167-1\">→ After: Ch.6 — depth read: the solo plan<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p167-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru kanzaki-ryuuji takemoto ninomiya-yui ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6   depth read  the solo plan  my bad  i had some business to take care of   the damage will only be greater if they lie to themselves and force it   there are broadly two methods for determining our plan  one is to envision the objective you wish to achieve and map out a path to it  the other is to gauge the enemy s aim and thwart their intentions   no  avoiding engagement is best for now  we ll stick to a defensive strategy   moving a little closer now would be the better option  h10 isn t a bad choice   class a is moving as planned  contact the commander now and tell them to disable my personal gps the moment the next gps update occurs   yeah  i m not coming back today  chooses a defensive strategy  letting the shrinking area force a general firefight   the development he s been waiting for  goes to retrieve g9 supplies then has his gps disabled  disappearing from the exam to execute a solo plan  i m not coming back today  reasons ryuen attacked class c specifically because ayanokoji is his arch rival  not class a  analyzes his motives and anticipates his final day move  explains his strategic reasoning to him  instructs him to disable his gps and handle the plan if he s  taken out  directs that she retire immediately due to fever","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p167-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.6 — depth read: the solo plan<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.167–196<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"ninomiya-yui.html\">Ninomiya Yui<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My bad, I had some business to take care of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The damage will only be greater if they lie to themselves and force it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There are broadly two methods for determining our plan. One is to envision the objective you wish to achieve and map out a path to it. The other is to gauge the enemy&#x27;s aim and thwart their intentions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, avoiding engagement is best for now. We&#x27;ll stick to a defensive strategy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Moving a little closer now would be the better option. H10 isn&#x27;t a bad choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Class A is moving as planned. Contact the commander now and tell them to disable my personal GPS the moment the next GPS update occurs.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, I&#x27;m not coming back today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Chooses a defensive strategy, letting the shrinking area force a general firefight — the development he&#x27;s been waiting for.<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Goes to retrieve G9 supplies then has his GPS disabled, disappearing from the exam to execute a solo plan (&quot;I&#x27;m not coming back today&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.183–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reasons Ryūen attacked Class C specifically because Ayanokōji is his arch-rival, not Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Analyzes his motives and anticipates his final-day move.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Explains his strategic reasoning to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">takemoto<\/b> Instructs him to disable his GPS and handle the plan if he&#x27;s &quot;taken out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ninomiya Yui<\/b> Directs that she retire immediately due to fever.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p160-1\">← Before: The merged campsite and the talk with Kanzaki<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1\">→ After: The alliance base: supply report and defensive strategy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji hashimoto-masayoshi moriyama ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the alliance base  supply report and defensive strategy returns to the k13 alliance base after  business  the previous night  hashimoto notices his dirty right hand   my bad  i had some business to take care of   it s nothing serious  don t worry about it   if one is the vip  it would be a bit of a hassle  but if they re guards  having them retire now may be an option   the damage will only be greater if they lie to themselves and force it   there s a troublesome presence in class a from the start  needless to say  it s koenji   he ll wait until the last possible moment without launching a hasty attack   no  avoiding engagement is best for now  we ll stick to a defensive strategy  predicts ryuen will not attack until the shrinking area forces a confrontation  chooses to wait for the general firefight they have been hoping for  calm and strategic   hides the late night infiltration  manages the ill students  and reasons precisely about ryuen s motives  receives supply and illness reports  debates ryuen s likely moves  concerns about dwindling supplies  sends him to relay his words to the unwell students","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The alliance base: supply report and defensive strategy<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.174–177<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns to the K13 alliance base after &quot;business&quot; the previous night; Hashimoto notices his dirty right hand.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a> · <a href=\"moriyama.html\">Moriyama<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;My bad, I had some business to take care of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s nothing serious, don&#x27;t worry about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;If one is the VIP, it would be a bit of a hassle, but if they&#x27;re guards, having them retire now may be an option.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The damage will only be greater if they lie to themselves and force it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s a troublesome presence in Class A from the start. Needless to say, it&#x27;s Koenji.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He&#x27;ll wait until the last possible moment without launching a hasty attack.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, avoiding engagement is best for now. We&#x27;ll stick to a defensive strategy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Predicts Ryūen will not attack until the shrinking area forces a confrontation; chooses to wait for the general firefight they have been hoping for.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calm and strategic — hides the late-night infiltration, manages the ill students, and reasons precisely about Ryūen&#x27;s motives.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Receives supply and illness reports; debates Ryūen&#x27;s likely moves.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Concerns about dwindling supplies.<span class=\"pg\">p.174–175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Moriyama<\/b> Sends him to relay his words to the unwell students.<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p167-1\">← Before: Ch.6 — depth read: the solo plan<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p178-1\">→ After: Moving toward the center<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p178-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka moving toward the center the 11 a m  event shrinks the area to a 9 9 grid  d4 l12   that s right  i want to avoid the risk of pushing ourselves unnecessarily  losing stamina  or getting injured   however  i want to send a few people ahead to secure the food at h10   it s simply a matter of the priority of fighting changing depending on what you prioritize   moving a little closer now would be the better option  h10 isn t a bad choice   form a retrieval squad and send a small group to j12  ignores treacherous supply routes  sends a light group for h10 food  and moves the alliance to h10 for flexibility as the area shifts southwest  agrees on the h10 move and the retrieval squads","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p178-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Moving toward the center<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.178–181<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The 11 a.m. event shrinks the area to a 9×9 grid (D4–L12).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s right. I want to avoid the risk of pushing ourselves unnecessarily, losing stamina, or getting injured.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;However, I want to send a few people ahead to secure the food at H10.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;It&#x27;s simply a matter of the priority of fighting changing depending on what you prioritize.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Moving a little closer now would be the better option. H10 isn&#x27;t a bad choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Form a retrieval squad and send a small group to J12.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Ignores treacherous supply routes, sends a light group for H10 food, and moves the alliance to H10 for flexibility as the area shifts southwest.<span class=\"pg\">p.178–181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Agrees on the H10 move and the retrieval squads.<span class=\"pg\">p.178–181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p174-1\">← Before: The alliance base: supply report and defensive strategy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p182-1\">→ After: Ninomiya&#x27;s fever; the G9 run and the GPS shutdown<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p182-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ninomiya-yui takemoto-shigeru moriyama amikura-mako ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ninomiya s fever  the g9 run and the gps shutdown finds ninomiya ill with a fever in the shade of a tree  amikura is anxiously by her side   she should retire immediately and have the school come pick her up   a few students have been coughing since this morning  it s possible we might have a few more students retire between tonight and tomorrow   i ll go to g9  takemoto  and about six others  lend me a hand   class a is moving as planned  contact the commander now and tell them to disable my personal gps the moment the next gps update occurs   yeah  i m not coming back today  suspects a cold is spreading through the alliance  worsened by shared food and close proximity over three days  goes to retrieve g9 supplies then has his gps disabled   disappearing from the exam to execute a solo plan  with a contingency already shared with shimazaki via takemoto  orders her immediate retirement  instructs him to disable his gps and handle the  taken out  contingency  relays his words to the ill students  accompanies the g9 run  is with the ill ninomiya","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p182-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ninomiya&#x27;s fever; the G9 run and the GPS shutdown<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.182–184<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Finds Ninomiya ill with a fever in the shade of a tree; Amikura is anxiously by her side.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ninomiya-yui.html\">Ninomiya Yui<\/a> · <a href=\"takemoto-shigeru.html\">Takemoto Shigeru<\/a> · <a href=\"moriyama.html\">Moriyama<\/a> · <a href=\"amikura-mako.html\">Amikura Mako<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;She should retire immediately and have the school come pick her up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;A few students have been coughing since this morning. It&#x27;s possible we might have a few more students retire between tonight and tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I&#x27;ll go to G9. Takemoto... and about six others, lend me a hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Class A is moving as planned. Contact the commander now and tell them to disable my personal GPS the moment the next GPS update occurs.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, I&#x27;m not coming back today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Suspects a cold is spreading through the alliance, worsened by shared food and close proximity over three days.<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Goes to retrieve G9 supplies then has his GPS disabled — disappearing from the exam to execute a solo plan, with a contingency already shared with Shimazaki via Takemoto.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ninomiya Yui<\/b> Orders her immediate retirement.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Takemoto Shigeru<\/b> Instructs him to disable his GPS and handle the &quot;taken out&quot; contingency.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Moriyama<\/b> Relays his words to the ill students; accompanies the G9 run.<span class=\"pg\">p.182–184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Amikura Mako<\/b> Is with the ill Ninomiya.<span class=\"pg\">p.182<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p178-1\">← Before: Moving toward the center<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p197-1\">→ After: Ch.7 — depth read: the mastermind&#x27;s final-day moves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p197-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune shiraishi-asuka satou-maya ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7   depth read  the mastermind s final day moves  the right call  headquarters is undoubtedly tracking every student s gps in real time  24 7   what am i planning  nothing  if there s a path  i ll walk it   we kept losing points in the beginning  i m glad i could make up for it  even just a little   there was something i came to understand from infiltrating class a  it was that class a was slightly lacking the tension it should ve had   appoint a commander  gather supplies  keep your distance  read the enemy s movements and avoid engagement   the objective wasn t to eliminate as many people as possible  but to find out who the vips were   if they could have predicted the attack beforehand  it could ve been a feint   now  all that s left is to take out the remaining class b students and this special exam will be over   adjustments  identified class a s three vips via the previous night s attack and passed the names to class b to catalyze an assault  aims to throw the battlefield into chaos so students panic and eliminate each other  then escape the vips  walks the path she leaves open  reads that she expects him to flee  has her report the battlefield state  leaves her with yamamura  identified her as a class a vip  her elimination narrows class a to one vip","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p197-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.7 — depth read: the mastermind&#x27;s final-day moves<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.197–232<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"satou-maya.html\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The right call. Headquarters is undoubtedly tracking every student&#x27;s GPS in real-time, 24/7.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;What am I planning? Nothing. If there&#x27;s a path, I&#x27;ll walk it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We kept losing points in the beginning. I&#x27;m glad I could make up for it, even just a little.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There was something I came to understand from infiltrating Class A. It was that Class A was slightly lacking the tension it should&#x27;ve had.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Appoint a commander, gather supplies, keep your distance, read the enemy&#x27;s movements and avoid engagement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The objective wasn&#x27;t to eliminate as many people as possible, but to find out who the VIPs were.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If they could have predicted the attack beforehand, it could’ve been a feint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Now, all that&#x27;s left is to take out the remaining Class B students and this special exam will be over.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Adjustments.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Identified Class A&#x27;s three VIPs via the previous night&#x27;s attack and passed the names to Class B to catalyze an assault.<span class=\"pg\">p.231–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Aims to throw the battlefield into chaos so students panic and eliminate each other, then escape the VIPs.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Walks the path she leaves open; reads that she expects him to flee.<span class=\"pg\">p.201–203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Has her report the battlefield state; leaves her with Yamamura.<span class=\"pg\">p.230–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> Identified her as a Class A VIP; her elimination narrows Class A to one VIP.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p182-1\">← Before: Ninomiya&#x27;s fever; the G9 run and the GPS shutdown<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p204-1\">→ After: Shaking Class A; the &quot;adjustment&quot;<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p204-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"hashimoto-masayoshi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka shaking class a  the  adjustment  returns to h10 a little after 10 a m  having shaken off class a s guards overnight   yo  i got the report yesterday that you were out right at the very end and i   we kept losing points in the beginning  i m glad i could make up for it  even just a little   there was something i came to understand from infiltrating class a  it was that class a was slightly lacking the tension it should ve had  released after the rule violation elimination  calmly rejoins the alliance and notes class a s lack of tension  is greeted by him and takemoto at h10","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p204-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Shaking Class A; the &quot;adjustment&quot;<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.204–206<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Returns to H10 a little after 10 a.m., having shaken off Class A&#x27;s guards overnight.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"hashimoto-masayoshi.html\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Yo! I got the report yesterday that you were out right at the very end and I—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;We kept losing points in the beginning. I&#x27;m glad I could make up for it, even just a little.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;There was something I came to understand from infiltrating Class A. It was that Class A was slightly lacking the tension it should&#x27;ve had.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Released after the rule-violation elimination, calmly rejoins the alliance and notes Class A&#x27;s lack of tension.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hashimoto Masayoshi<\/b> Is greeted by him and Takemoto at H10.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p197-1\">← Before: Ch.7 — depth read: the mastermind&#x27;s final-day moves<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p230-1\">→ After: Sowing chaos; how he found Class A&#x27;s VIPs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p230-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"shiraishi-asuka ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka sowing chaos  how he found class a s vips  appoint a commander  gather supplies  keep your distance  read the enemy s movements and avoid engagement   they can carry things out reasonably well up to this point  but once the firefight actually starts  anyone would lose their ability to think calmly   the objective wasn t to eliminate as many people as possible  but to find out who the vips were   if they could have predicted the attack beforehand  it could ve been a feint   i think class a s movements weren t bad  considering they knew they were a target   adjustments  sows chaos so students panic and eliminate each other  identified class a s three vips  wang  sato  yukimura  by attacking at night and watching who the guards protected  then fed the names to class b  uses the individual gps shutdown on the class d vips  not his own class  to hide them   no rule against targeting any class  has her report the battlefield state  leaves her with yamamura before heading to f11  walked home with her earlier","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p230-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Sowing chaos; how he found Class A&#x27;s VIPs<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.230–232<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"shiraishi-asuka.html\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/a> · <a href=\"ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Appoint a commander, gather supplies, keep your distance, read the enemy&#x27;s movements and avoid engagement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;They can carry things out reasonably well up to this point, but once the firefight actually starts, anyone would lose their ability to think calmly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;The objective wasn&#x27;t to eliminate as many people as possible, but to find out who the VIPs were.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If they could have predicted the attack beforehand, it could&#x27;ve been a feint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think Class A&#x27;s movements weren&#x27;t bad, considering they knew they were a target.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Adjustments.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Sows chaos so students panic and eliminate each other; identified Class A&#x27;s three VIPs (Wang, Satō, Yukimura) by attacking at night and watching who the guards protected, then fed the names to Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.230–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Uses the individual GPS shutdown on the Class D VIPs (not his own class) to hide them — no rule against targeting any class.<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiraishi Asuka<\/b> Has her report the battlefield state; leaves her with Yamamura before heading to F11.<span class=\"pg\">p.230–232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Walked home with her earlier.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p204-1\">← Before: Shaking Class A; the &quot;adjustment&quot;<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1\">→ After: Epilogue — depth read: the bluff and the true goal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio shiina-hiyori beppu-ryouta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka epilogue   depth read  the bluff and the true goal stands over the battlefield as the three minute mark seals class a s elimination  kanzaki  the two class d vips  shiraishi and yamamura gather before him   were the remaining guards taken out   tell me the details   then there are three left  i just took down yoshimoto there a moment ago   it s not robbery or anything  it s just a transfer   i have 22 rounds left  that should be enough   i surrender   impossible  there s no way i can dodge them all   i already told you it s impossible  the muzzle velocity of these paint guns is about 90 m s   it s a matter of perspective   there s nothing in the rules against it   i ll make it official here  i  class d and ichinose have joined forces   that s right  unfortunately for you  winning a shootout wasn t my first priority   it was a matter of sooner or later  burns his ammunition against ibuki and ryuen  eliminates ibuki with a paintball to the thigh  then   out of ammo and apparently surrendered   throws a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on ryuen s abdomen  eliminating both  led ryuen onto the coverless beach and bluffed that yamamura was behind him  exploiting ryuen s need for a certain victory  the damaged paintball was prepared over three days of repeated trials  reveals the exam s true goal  he allowed class b s surprise attack so that cornered class c would have no choice but to request an alliance with class d  class c places second behind class d  the alliance is now open  and a new exam built on trust and betrayal is announced  fights him on the beach  ryuen concedes and vows no mercy from here on  outmaneuvers her in the forest and eliminates her with a paintball to the thigh  looks for her on the disembarkation beach and finds her talking with kaneda  in good spirits  takes the class d vip with him to the center of e11 to bait the confrontation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Epilogue — depth read: the bluff and the true goal<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.233–252<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands over the battlefield as the three-minute mark seals Class A&#x27;s elimination; Kanzaki, the two Class D VIPs, Shiraishi and Yamamura gather before him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"shiina-hiyori.html\">Shiina Hiyori<\/a> · <a href=\"beppu-ryouta.html\">Beppu Ryōta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Were the remaining guards taken out?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Tell me the details.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then there are three left. I just took down Yoshimoto there a moment ago.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not robbery or anything. It&#x27;s just a transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have 22 rounds left. That should be enough.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I surrender.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Impossible. There&#x27;s no way I can dodge them all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I already told you it&#x27;s impossible. The muzzle velocity of these paint guns is about 90 m/s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s a matter of perspective.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s nothing in the rules against it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll make it official here. I, Class D and Ichinose have joined forces.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s right. Unfortunately for you, winning a shootout wasn&#x27;t my first priority.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It was a matter of sooner or later.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Burns his ammunition against Ibuki and Ryūen, eliminates Ibuki with a paintball to the thigh, then — out of ammo and apparently surrendered — throws a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on Ryūen&#x27;s abdomen, eliminating both.<span class=\"pg\">p.240–248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Led Ryūen onto the coverless beach and bluffed that Yamamura was behind him, exploiting Ryūen&#x27;s need for a certain victory; the damaged paintball was prepared over three days of repeated trials.<span class=\"pg\">p.245–249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Reveals the exam&#x27;s true goal: he allowed Class B&#x27;s surprise attack so that cornered Class C would have no choice but to request an alliance with Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class C places second behind Class D; the alliance is now open, and a new exam built on trust and betrayal is announced.<span class=\"pg\">p.251–252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Fights him on the beach; Ryūen concedes and vows no mercy from here on.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Outmaneuvers her in the forest and eliminates her with a paintball to the thigh.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiina Hiyori<\/b> Looks for her on the disembarkation beach and finds her talking with Kaneda, in good spirits.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> Takes the Class D VIP with him to the center of E11 to bait the confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.235–236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p230-1\">← Before: Sowing chaos; how he found Class A&#x27;s VIPs<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-2\">→ After: Class A eliminated; handing over ammo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-2","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji beppu-ryouta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka class a eliminated  handing over ammo at 3 p m  class a is eliminated  yamamura  shiraishi  kanzaki and the two class d vips gather before him   were the remaining guards taken out   tell me the details   then there are three left  i just took down yoshimoto there a moment ago   i cleaned up the area within my line of sight to a certain extent  but it seems the two troublesome ones are still left   i figured  there s no merit whatsoever in making ibuki the vip   then take this   it s not robbery or anything  it s just a transfer   i have 22 rounds left  that should be enough   ryuuen won t be satisfied with the exam ending like this   sorry  but beppu  could you come with me for a bit  class a last is set  no expulsion risk  but third place and above are undecided   one surviving guard could decide it  gives his two spare magazines to kanzaki so the guards can protect the vips  keeping only 22 rounds   an intentionally small amount to enjoy the uncertain fight  transfers spare ammo to him  takes the class d vip with him toward e11 to bait a confrontation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-2\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Class A eliminated; handing over ammo<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.233–235<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At 3 p.m. Class A is eliminated; Yamamura, Shiraishi, Kanzaki and the two Class D VIPs gather before him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a> · <a href=\"beppu-ryouta.html\">Beppu Ryōta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Were the remaining guards taken out?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Tell me the details.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Then there are three left. I just took down Yoshimoto there a moment ago.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I cleaned up the area within my line of sight to a certain extent. But it seems the two troublesome ones are still left.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I figured. There&#x27;s no merit whatsoever in making Ibuki the VIP.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then take this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s not robbery or anything. It&#x27;s just a transfer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have 22 rounds left. That should be enough.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ryuuen won&#x27;t be satisfied with the exam ending like this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, but Beppu, could you come with me for a bit?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Class A last is set (no expulsion risk), but third place and above are undecided — one surviving guard could decide it.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Gives his two spare magazines to Kanzaki so the guards can protect the VIPs, keeping only 22 rounds — an intentionally small amount to enjoy the uncertain fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Transfers spare ammo to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> Takes the Class D VIP with him toward E11 to bait a confrontation.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-1\">← Before: Epilogue — depth read: the bluff and the true goal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p236-1\">→ After: Eliminating Ibuki; out of ammo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p236-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio beppu-ryouta ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka eliminating ibuki  out of ammo walks into the center of e11 with beppu  ryuen and ibuki emerge from the trees  yamashita behind them   that s unlikely  yamashita isn t very athletic and she s probably nearing her limit   she s fast  as expected   sounds like you were pretty successful  how many people did you take out   it would be a problem for the other three classes if class a didn t lose  right   die  ayanokouji  reads ibuki s predictable movement and  with the muzzle alone aimed at her new position  hits her right thigh   then finds his rifle empty  calculation under pressure   with  20 rounds he processes distance  cover angles  ibuki s habits and ryuen s line of fire  refusing to waste shots  outmaneuvers and eliminates her with a thigh shot  has him check the enemy s position  then sends him away  i m outta here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Eliminating Ibuki; out of ammo<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.236–240<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walks into the center of E11 with Beppu; Ryūen and Ibuki emerge from the trees, Yamashita behind them.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"beppu-ryouta.html\">Beppu Ryōta<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;That&#x27;s unlikely. Yamashita isn&#x27;t very athletic and she&#x27;s probably nearing her limit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;She&#x27;s fast, as expected.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Sounds like you were pretty successful. How many people did you take out?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It would be a problem for the other three classes if Class A didn&#x27;t lose. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Die, Ayanokouji!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads Ibuki&#x27;s predictable movement and, with the muzzle alone aimed at her new position, hits her right thigh — then finds his rifle empty.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Calculation under pressure — with ~20 rounds he processes distance, cover angles, Ibuki&#x27;s habits and Ryūen&#x27;s line of fire, refusing to waste shots.<span class=\"pg\">p.237–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Outmaneuvers and eliminates her with a thigh shot.<span class=\"pg\">p.238–240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Beppu Ryōta<\/b> Has him check the enemy&#x27;s position, then sends him away (&quot;I&#x27;m outta here&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p233-2\">← Before: Class A eliminated; handing over ammo<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p241-1\">→ After: The beach surrender and the damaged paintball<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p241-1","v":"y3v3","y":3,"o":35,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the beach surrender and the damaged paintball throws down the empty weapon on the coverless beach and surrenders to ryuen at gunpoint   i surrender   impossible  there s no way i can dodge them all   correct  while we re standing here like this  yamashita might be getting targeted by one of our guards   i already told you it s impossible  the muzzle velocity of these paint guns is about 90 m s   it s a matter of perspective   she s skilled at erasing her presence  she s lightweight and nimble   there s nothing in the rules against it  throws a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on ryuen s abdomen  eliminating both   prepared over three days of trial and error on how much damage makes it rupture on impact  lures ryuen onto the coverless beach  bluffs that yamamura is behind him to force a glance  then strikes with the concealed paintball   winning the psychological duel by making ryuen need  all the answers  coldly theatrical   surrenders in appearance while manipulating every variable   fine with losing here  because the true goal is already achieved  duels him on the beach  ryuen concedes defeat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The beach surrender and the damaged paintball<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y3V3 · p.241–248<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Throws down the empty weapon on the coverless beach and surrenders to Ryūen at gunpoint.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I surrender.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Impossible. There&#x27;s no way I can dodge them all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;Correct. While we&#x27;re standing here like this, Yamashita might be getting targeted by one of our guards.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I already told you it&#x27;s impossible. The muzzle velocity of these paint guns is about 90 m/s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s a matter of perspective.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She&#x27;s skilled at erasing her presence, she&#x27;s lightweight and nimble.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There&#x27;s nothing in the rules against it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Throws a deliberately damaged paintball that bursts on Ryūen&#x27;s abdomen, eliminating both — prepared over three days of trial and error on how much damage makes it rupture on impact.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Lures Ryūen onto the coverless beach, bluffs that Yamamura is behind him to force a glance, then strikes with the concealed paintball — winning the psychological duel by making Ryūen need &quot;all the answers.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245–248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Coldly theatrical — surrenders in appearance while manipulating every variable, &quot;fine with losing here&quot; because the true goal is already achieved.<span class=\"pg\">p.241–248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Duels him on the beach; Ryūen concedes defeat.<span class=\"pg\">p.236–250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y3v3-p236-1\">← Before: Eliminating Ibuki; out of ammo<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p131-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka first memory  the pure white ceiling recalls his very first memory in the white room   staring at a pure white ceiling   the first memory everyone shared was of  white  spreading across the entirety of the surface   as the name  white room  implied  this facility was based on the color white   the ceiling was no exception   in my first memory  i was staring at that pure white ceiling   before showing interest in my own fingertips  i just wondered what this white ceiling was   day after day  i just stared at the ceiling   at first  i cried  crying out of loneliness  eventually  i learned that no one would come to help  a newborn  unable to speak  accepted the environment as  the first lesson  later he became aware of his fingers  sucking and licking them to pass empty time   inhuman adults  brought only the nutrition necessary to live  even when sick  treatment was unemotional and life returned to normal   no one panicked  worried or rejoiced  learned at an early stage that joy  anger  sorrow and pleasure were  practically useless  in the facility","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">First memory: the pure white ceiling<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.131<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls his very first memory in the White Room — staring at a pure white ceiling.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;The first memory everyone shared was of &#x27;white&#x27; spreading across the entirety of the surface.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;As the name &#x27;White Room&#x27; implied, this facility was based on the color white.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;The ceiling was no exception.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;In my first memory, I was staring at that pure white ceiling.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Before showing interest in my own fingertips, I just wondered what this white ceiling was.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Day after day, I just stared at the ceiling.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;At first, I cried, crying out of loneliness. Eventually, I learned that no one would come to help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> A newborn, unable to speak, accepted the environment as &quot;the first lesson&quot;; later he became aware of his fingers, sucking and licking them to pass empty time.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> &quot;Inhuman adults&quot; brought only the nutrition necessary to live; even when sick, treatment was unemotional and life returned to normal — no one panicked, worried or rejoiced.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Learned at an early stage that joy, anger, sorrow and pleasure were &quot;practically useless&quot; in the facility.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p132-1\">→ After: The gummy hand-game at age two; the third option<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p132-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the gummy hand game at age two  the third option recalls a one on one test at around age two   an instructor holds a tiny gummy in one hand   if you can guess where the gummy is  you can eat it   i ll keep giving you a chance to answer until you miss three times  a tiny gummy   a rare snack in the facility  with a sweetness he craved  the instructor s face was stern  almost expressionless  and so was the two year old kiyotaka s  naturally  the first four rounds the gummy is in the right hand  the fifth the instructor crosses both arms behind his back  grip and position identical  gaze unchanged   a fifty fifty choice  he touches the right  which is empty  other children had a slightly higher right hand bias with  no clear reason  all instructors actually held the gummies in their left hands that round  he observes the other children s choices   an overwhelming number point left  but the answer is right   and infers the instructor s gummy is in the right  he points right and a green gummy appears  the hands won t open until everyone has answered  you re the last one  everyone guesses wrong  and most children hit three misses and lose their chance   why point behind   gummy  it s not there  on his last chance he points behind  neither hand  reasoning the gummy might be hidden elsewhere  the instructor opens both hands   the gummy was in the right  the instructor eats it himself   behind  with a special extra chance  he again points behind  the gummy was in the left    too bad again  are you frustrated  he nods  frustrated not by wanting the gummy but by his thinking being off  the adults whisper that he   unlike the other children   observed others  choices  conceived a third option  and didn t discard it even after it was disproved  they remark it is not the thought process of a two year old  and argue over whether he understands them  even at two  reasons by observation and inference rather than instinct   tracks others  behavior  considers hidden alternatives  and is driven by accuracy rather than reward  when the buzzer ends the test  the adults leave and not a single child cries   being left alone with no help was deeply ingrained by age two","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The gummy hand-game at age two; the third option<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.132–137<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls a one-on-one test at around age two — an instructor holds a tiny gummy in one hand.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;If you can guess where the gummy is, you can eat it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I&#x27;ll keep giving you a chance to answer until you miss three times.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Why point behind?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> A tiny gummy — a rare snack in the facility, with a sweetness he craved; the instructor&#x27;s face was stern, almost expressionless, and so was the two-year-old Kiyotaka&#x27;s, naturally.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The first four rounds the gummy is in the right hand; the fifth the instructor crosses both arms behind his back, grip and position identical, gaze unchanged — a fifty-fifty choice; he touches the right, which is empty.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Other children had a slightly higher right-hand bias with &quot;no clear reason&quot;; all instructors actually held the gummies in their left hands that round.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He observes the other children&#x27;s choices — an overwhelming number point left, but the answer is right — and infers the instructor&#x27;s gummy is in the right; he points right and a green gummy appears.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The hands won&#x27;t open until everyone has answered (&quot;You&#x27;re the last one&quot;); everyone guesses wrong, and most children hit three misses and lose their chance.<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Gummy, it&#x27;s not there.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> On his last chance he points behind (neither hand), reasoning the gummy might be hidden elsewhere; the instructor opens both hands — the gummy was in the right; the instructor eats it himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Behind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> With a special extra chance, he again points behind; the gummy was in the left — &quot;Too bad again. Are you frustrated?&quot; He nods, frustrated not by wanting the gummy but by his thinking being off.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> The adults whisper that he — unlike the other children — observed others&#x27; choices, conceived a third option, and didn&#x27;t discard it even after it was disproved; they remark it is not the thought process of a two-year-old, and argue over whether he understands them.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Even at two, reasons by observation and inference rather than instinct — tracks others&#x27; behavior, considers hidden alternatives, and is driven by accuracy rather than reward.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> When the buzzer ends the test, the adults leave and not a single child cries — being left alone with no help was deeply ingrained by age two.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p131-1\">← Before: First memory: the pure white ceiling<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p138-1\">→ After: Names, no surnames; the written exam at four<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p138-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka names  no surnames  the written exam at four recalls being told to state his name    kiyotaka    a symbol  an identifying sequence of letters   kiyotaka  white room children were taught names to identify people  but not surnames when young   instructors used first names  a rule set to prevent future identification  by age four  new curriculums were implemented one after another  the written exam used hiragana  katakana  the alphabet  numbers and simple kanji  with pen gripping fingers moving without hesitation  a certain score within a time limit was required or there was a penalty  elegant handwriting was mandatory   no extra points for good handwriting  but hurried or poor handwriting meant deductions   no one in this facility asked whether the problems could be solved or not  the only answer was that everyone could do it  those who couldn t were eliminated at age three  the fourth generation initially numbered seventy four  those judged incapable at three had already dropped out  the written exam lasted thirty minutes but strong students finished in half to two thirds the time","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p138-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Names, no surnames; the written exam at four<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.138–139<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls being told to state his name — &quot;Kiyotaka&quot; — a symbol, an identifying sequence of letters.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> White Room children were taught names to identify people, but not surnames when young — instructors used first names, a rule set to prevent future identification.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> By age four, new curriculums were implemented one after another; the written exam used hiragana, katakana, the alphabet, numbers and simple kanji, with pen-gripping fingers moving without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> A certain score within a time limit was required or there was a penalty; elegant handwriting was mandatory — no extra points for good handwriting, but hurried or poor handwriting meant deductions.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> &quot;No one in this facility asked whether the problems could be solved or not. The only answer was that everyone could do it&quot;; those who couldn&#x27;t were eliminated at age three.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> The fourth generation initially numbered seventy-four; those judged incapable at three had already dropped out. The written exam lasted thirty minutes but strong students finished in half to two-thirds the time.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p132-1\">← Before: The gummy hand-game at age two; the third option<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p140-1\">→ After: Judo, randori, and Mikuru&#x27;s collapse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p140-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"","w":"mikuru shiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka judo  randori  and mikuru s collapse recalls the judo curriculum added in their fourth year   being slammed to the floor by instructors  breathing knocked out  forced to stand  the instructor shouts for them to get up  that he doesn t spare even children  and that no one will cry for them   the translation leaves these lines untagged  so no  says  row is claimed for them  judo had been learned for four months  progressing to randori  one on one sparring  the children were always made to taste bitter defeat against instructors  mikuru  pleading  i can t  stand anymore  clung to the instructor s leg  was shaken off  kicked away  spinning across the floor while scattering vomit around her  and lost consciousness  the instructor called her a  weakling  and had her removed  the instructors were  the kind who wouldn t hesitate to push women and children to the brink of death  being thrown  breathing difficulty and sobbing pain were normal  and even thinking about them a waste of energy  after harsh lessons  they did randori with three other children at day s end  weak prey was hunted by the strong   a lesson learned  his record  144 fights  127 wins  17 losses  currently a four win streak  witnesses her brutal breakdown and removal  faces him in randori   shiro s record 135 wins  9 losses  best at judo  waited and aimed for a counter this third fight","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p140-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Judo, randori, and Mikuru&#x27;s collapse<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.140–142<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls the judo curriculum added in their fourth year — being slammed to the floor by instructors, breathing knocked out, forced to stand.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#mikuru\">Mikuru<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#shiro\">Shiro<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The instructor shouts for them to get up, that he doesn&#x27;t spare even children, and that no one will cry for them — the translation leaves these lines untagged, so no `[says]` row is claimed for them.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Judo had been learned for four months, progressing to randori (one-on-one sparring); the children were always made to taste bitter defeat against instructors.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Mikuru, pleading &quot;I can&#x27;t… stand anymore…!&quot;, clung to the instructor&#x27;s leg, was shaken off, kicked away &quot;spinning across the floor while scattering vomit around her,&quot; and lost consciousness; the instructor called her a &quot;weakling&quot; and had her removed.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The instructors were &quot;the kind who wouldn&#x27;t hesitate to push women and children to the brink of death&quot;; being thrown, breathing difficulty and sobbing pain were normal, and even thinking about them a waste of energy.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> After harsh lessons, they did randori with three other children at day&#x27;s end; weak prey was hunted by the strong — a lesson learned. His record: 144 fights, 127 wins, 17 losses, currently a four-win streak.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mikuru<\/b> Witnesses her brutal breakdown and removal.<span class=\"pg\">p.140–141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiro<\/b> Faces him in randori — Shiro&#x27;s record 135 wins, 9 losses, best at judo; waited and aimed for a counter this third fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p138-1\">← Before: Names, no surnames; the written exam at four<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p144-1\">→ After: Yuki, carrots, and the first smile<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p144-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"yuki shiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka yuki  carrots  and the first smile recalls dinner at age five  when the children had never directly spoken to one another  the number of children had dropped to about fifty by age five  no one paid attention    there was no room to care  the children never talked  no favoritism in food  no sense of comradeship  their presence was  no different from the surrounding scenery   i don t like it   kiyotaka  do you like it   i don t like them either  he analyzed carrots   beta carotene   vitamin a  cell aging  skin and mucous membranes  immunity   but had never considered liking or disliking them  concluded he didn t dislike them  checked the surveillance camera  the instructors monitored meals and audio  and since there was no scolding  such conversation was apparently allowed  though never encouraged  yuki walked three laps around the small room  then tripped before him  he caught her and noted  it s strange to trip over nothing  then considered accumulated fatigue and dismissed it  she made an expression he had never seen   the orbicularis oculi around the eyes and corrugator supercilii near the eyebrows   which she realized was a  smile  something humans have from birth as instinct  never taught in the white room  the girl who always sat in front of him  her carrot question and unlearned smile are his first encounters with spontaneous emotion  sits on his left and answers yuki s question for him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Yuki, carrots, and the first smile<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.144–148<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls dinner at age five, when the children had never directly spoken to one another.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yuki.html\">Yuki<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#shiro\">Shiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t like it…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> &quot;Kiyotaka, do you like it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiro<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t like them either.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The number of children had dropped to about fifty by age five; no one paid attention — &quot;there was no room to care.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The children never talked: no favoritism in food, no sense of comradeship; their presence was &quot;no different from the surrounding scenery.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He analyzed carrots — beta-carotene → Vitamin A, cell aging, skin and mucous membranes, immunity — but had never considered liking or disliking them; concluded he didn&#x27;t dislike them.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Checked the surveillance camera; the instructors monitored meals and audio, and since there was no scolding, such conversation was apparently allowed, though never encouraged.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Yuki walked three laps around the small room, then tripped before him; he caught her and noted &quot;It&#x27;s strange to trip over nothing,&quot; then considered accumulated fatigue and dismissed it.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> She made an expression he had never seen — the orbicularis oculi around the eyes and corrugator supercilii near the eyebrows — which she realized was a &quot;smile,&quot; something humans have from birth as instinct, never taught in the White Room.<span class=\"pg\">p.146–148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> The girl who always sat in front of him; her carrot question and unlearned smile are his first encounters with spontaneous emotion.<span class=\"pg\">p.144–148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiro<\/b> Sits on his left and answers Yuki&#x27;s question for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p140-1\">← Before: Judo, randori, and Mikuru&#x27;s collapse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p149-1\">→ After: The daily schedule at age five<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p149-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the daily schedule at age five recalls the strict daily routine in the latter half of their fifth year  7 00 am   an inorganic mechanical voice announces  time to wake up  alarm exact to the second  staff remove the electrodes attached to them  immediate health check   height and weight changes  then bathroom  urine tests once a month and a small blood draw  staff leave without greetings  hydrate  thirty minutes of basic warmup training  record daily physical data such as grip strength  then training room with set quotas separated by gender   those who can t comply are barred from the room the next day  by 8 00 am   breakfast  nutrition focused  evolved into supplements and nutrition blocks  taste and preference irrelevant  eaten in the order served  subjects  language arts  mathematics  economics  political science  with brief breaks until noon  similar lunch  studies at desks until 5 00 pm  then physical education  everything ends at 7 00 pm  after dinner  bath and physical exam at 9 00 pm   a thirty minute  meeting  for children only  no educators  to reflect on the day  topics not freely chosen  adults intervene only for  unnecessary chatter  silence permitted  conversations overheard   part of the curriculum with no assigned quota  never spoke voluntarily in all this time  always just listened during the  meeting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p149-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The daily schedule at age five<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.149–150<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls the strict daily routine in the latter half of their fifth year.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> 7:00 AM — an inorganic mechanical voice announces &quot;Time to wake up,&quot; alarm exact to the second; staff remove the electrodes attached to them.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Immediate health check — height and weight changes; then bathroom; urine tests once a month and a small blood draw; staff leave without greetings.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Hydrate, thirty minutes of basic warmup training, record daily physical data such as grip strength, then training room with set quotas separated by gender — those who can&#x27;t comply are barred from the room the next day.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> By 8:00 AM — breakfast, nutrition-focused, evolved into supplements and nutrition blocks; taste and preference irrelevant, eaten in the order served.<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Subjects: language arts, mathematics, economics, political science, with brief breaks until noon; similar lunch; studies at desks until 5:00 PM, then physical education; everything ends at 7:00 PM.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> After dinner, bath and physical exam at 9:00 PM — a thirty-minute &quot;meeting&quot; for children only, no educators, to reflect on the day; topics not freely chosen, adults intervene only for &quot;unnecessary chatter,&quot; silence permitted, conversations overheard — part of the curriculum with no assigned quota.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Never spoke voluntarily in all this time; always just listened during the &quot;meeting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149–150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p144-1\">← Before: Yuki, carrots, and the first smile<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p152-1\">→ After: Deliberately scoring 80 to keep the ceiling low<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p152-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"suzukake-tanji ishida-yuusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka deliberately scoring 80 to keep the ceiling low recalls the  thinning out    as studies grew harder by two or three levels  children fell behind and were gradually removed  the special high difficulty exam s difficulty was set to the top score   a perfect score raised the ceiling and forced low scorers to struggle more next time  a sub perfect top score lowered it  trivial calculation errors  careless oversights and excuses were unacceptable  children repeatedly checked papers even after finishing  he had already filled every answer and stared ahead  the questions and answers  etched word for word  in his mind  he intentionally held back to score eighty points  an adult representative summoned him to a small private room after glancing at his paper   no   i wasn t instructed not to   in the first place  i ve never once recognized the other children around me as comrades   it was more time efficient to leave it blank   i won t make a mistake   if i hadn t held back  the percentage of children dropping out would have been much higher than it is now   no  losing experience that s how i thought of it   i want to know what the weak can see and feel  the instructor s lines   calling his name   it is foolish not to use the power you have   leave the room   why did you hold back  the accusation of camaraderie  and the warning that knowledge fades   are untagged in the corpus  no  says  row is claimed for them  he held back not from camaraderie  which he denies  but to gain data on weaker children and because writing answers he already knew was inefficient   a reason the instructors had never considered  begins to dislike the instructor who lectures him  understands yuki s aversion to carrots as a comparable irrational feeling  suzukake argues for observing him    if he does something we hadn t even considered  that s exactly what we hoped for  ishida is among the researchers who question his deliberate underperformance  another boy  sobbing  keeps writing after the buzzer and is dragged out screaming that he doesn t want to drop out  scattering gastric fluid over his paper  neck and clothes   though no one could drop out on that exam  most children just stare ahead","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Deliberately scoring 80 to keep the ceiling low<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.152–157<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls the &quot;thinning out&quot; — as studies grew harder by two or three levels, children fell behind and were gradually removed.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"suzukake-tanji.html\">Suzukake Tanji<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ishida-yuusuke\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;No.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I wasn&#x27;t instructed not to.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;In the first place, I&#x27;ve never once recognized the other children around me as comrades.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The special high-difficulty exam&#x27;s difficulty was set to the top score — a perfect score raised the ceiling and forced low scorers to struggle more next time; a sub-perfect top score lowered it.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Trivial calculation errors, careless oversights and excuses were unacceptable; children repeatedly checked papers even after finishing. He had already filled every answer and stared ahead, the questions and answers &quot;etched word for word&quot; in his mind.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He intentionally held back to score eighty points; an adult representative summoned him to a small private room after glancing at his paper.<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;It was more time-efficient to leave it blank.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I won&#x27;t make a mistake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;If I hadn&#x27;t held back, the percentage of children dropping out would have been much higher than it is now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.155<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;No. Losing experience—that&#x27;s how I thought of it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I want to know what the weak can see and feel.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The instructor&#x27;s lines — calling his name, &quot;it is foolish not to use the power you have,&quot; &quot;leave the room,&quot; &quot;why did you hold back,&quot; the accusation of camaraderie, and the warning that knowledge fades — are untagged in the corpus; no `[says]` row is claimed for them.<span class=\"pg\">p.154–156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He held back not from camaraderie (which he denies) but to gain data on weaker children and because writing answers he already knew was inefficient — a reason the instructors had never considered.<span class=\"pg\">p.152–156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Begins to dislike the instructor who lectures him; understands Yuki&#x27;s aversion to carrots as a comparable irrational feeling.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Suzukake Tanji<\/b> Suzukake argues for observing him — &quot;if he does something we hadn&#x27;t even considered, that&#x27;s exactly what we hoped for.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/b> Ishida is among the researchers who question his deliberate underperformance.<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Another boy, sobbing, keeps writing after the buzzer and is dragged out screaming that he doesn&#x27;t want to drop out, scattering gastric fluid over his paper, neck and clothes — though no one could drop out on that exam. Most children just stare ahead.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p149-1\">← Before: The daily schedule at age five<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p158-1\">→ After: The &quot;Travel&quot; virtual class and the odd instructor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p158-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the  travel  virtual class and the odd instructor recalls the  travel  class  introduced the year they turned six  run once or twice a month for half a day using a virtual console  the class taught about places like new york and hawaii  previously known only from materials  used goggles and a virtual console  and doubled as observation insight training  the instructor announces an  equipment malfunction  ending the virtual session  then a new instructor appears for one on one sessions with  ten seconds per turn  and a demonstration to observe   the translation leaves these lines untagged  no  says  row is claimed  notes the session s abrupt end and the unfamiliar one on one format as curriculum detail","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p158-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The &quot;Travel&quot; virtual class and the odd instructor<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.158–166<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Recalls the &quot;Travel&quot; class, introduced the year they turned six, run once or twice a month for half a day using a virtual console.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The class taught about places like New York and Hawaii, previously known only from materials; used goggles and a virtual console, and doubled as observation/insight training.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The instructor announces an &quot;equipment malfunction&quot; ending the virtual session, then a new instructor appears for one-on-one sessions with &quot;ten seconds per turn&quot; and a demonstration to observe — the translation leaves these lines untagged; no `[says]` row is claimed.<span class=\"pg\">p.159–160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Notes the session&#x27;s abrupt end and the unfamiliar one-on-one format as curriculum detail.<span class=\"pg\">p.158–166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p152-1\">← Before: Deliberately scoring 80 to keep the ceiling low<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p167-1\">→ After: The conversation with Yuki about smiling<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p167-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"yuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the conversation with yuki about smiling  i don t know  but i feel like i can laugh again if i m near you  kiyotaka   i can t understand that  yuki says she can t laugh now  though she laughed before  kiyotaka notes he himself doesn t know how to smile    i hadn t learned the basics of emotions  he speculates that laughter may require being near a specific person  noting instructors show anger and smiles toward others  concludes emotions are probably unnecessary since he wasn t taught them","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p167-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The conversation with Yuki about smiling<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.167–168<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yuki.html\">Yuki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t know, but I feel like I can laugh again if I&#x27;m near you, Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I can&#x27;t understand that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Yuki says she can&#x27;t laugh now, though she laughed before; Kiyotaka notes he himself doesn&#x27;t know how to smile — &quot;I hadn&#x27;t learned the basics of emotions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> He speculates that laughter may require being near a specific person, noting instructors show anger and smiles toward others; concludes emotions are probably unnecessary since he wasn&#x27;t taught them.<span class=\"pg\">p.167–168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p158-1\">← Before: The &quot;Travel&quot; virtual class and the odd instructor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p172-1\">→ After: Arisu Sakayanagi observes the White Room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p172-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"sakayanagi-arisu sakayanagi-narimori ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka arisu sakayanagi observes the white room arisu  held by her father  watches the white room students through a one way mirror in the observation room  sakayanagi tells his daughter  these children might someday be responsible for japan s future  she presses her hands to the glass  staring for five then ten minutes without tiring   an experiment to artificially create geniuses  how could i not be interested   from a humanitarian perspective  people are likely to criticize it from all sides   ultimately  i think the children who stand out just have excellent dna   that child  he s been handling all the tasks calmly and effortlessly since earlier   he s spent his entire life in this facility since he was born  the first thing he saw wasn t his mother or father  but the facility s white ceiling   do you dislike this facility  father   i m not sure  i can t honestly support it   rest assured  i will shatter it  i will prove that a genius is not determined by their education  but by the moment they re born   by the way  father  i think i ll try to learn chess  arisu notices kiyotaka s unusual aura  narimori pities him as the ideal subject  and arisu concludes the survivors and dropouts exist for future children   a fight decided fifty or even a hundred years from now  a young girl with an adult like perspective who resolves to  shatter  the white room and takes up chess   the origin of her rivalry with kiyotaka  watches with his daughter  atsuomi monitors their conversation via camera audio but concludes it was  an unnecessary concern","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p172-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Arisu Sakayanagi observes the White Room<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.172–176<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Arisu, held by her father, watches the White Room students through a one-way mirror in the observation room.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"sakayanagi-arisu.html\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"sakayanagi-narimori.html\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;An experiment to artificially create geniuses. How could I not be interested?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;From a humanitarian perspective, people are likely to criticize it from all sides.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> &quot;Ultimately, I think the children who stand out just have excellent DNA.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Sakayanagi tells his daughter &quot;these children might someday be responsible for Japan&#x27;s future&quot;; she presses her hands to the glass, staring for five then ten minutes without tiring.<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;That child, he&#x27;s been handling all the tasks calmly and effortlessly since earlier.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.175<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;He&#x27;s spent his entire life in this facility since he was born. The first thing he saw wasn&#x27;t his mother or father, but the facility&#x27;s white ceiling.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Do you dislike this facility, Father?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m not sure… I can&#x27;t honestly support it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Rest assured. I will shatter it. I will prove that a genius is not determined by their education, but by the moment they&#x27;re born.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;By the way, Father. I think I&#x27;ll try to learn chess…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Arisu notices Kiyotaka&#x27;s unusual aura; Narimori pities him as the ideal subject, and Arisu concludes the survivors and dropouts exist for future children — a fight decided fifty or even a hundred years from now.<span class=\"pg\">p.175–176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> A young girl with an adult-like perspective who resolves to &quot;shatter&quot; the White Room and takes up chess — the origin of her rivalry with Kiyotaka.<span class=\"pg\">p.172–176<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Narimori<\/b> Watches with his daughter; Atsuomi monitors their conversation via camera audio but concludes it was &quot;an unnecessary concern.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172–176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p167-1\">← Before: The conversation with Yuki about smiling<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p178-1\">→ After: Yuki fails and leaves<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p178-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"yuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka yuki fails and leaves waits as papers are graded  yuki s small back trembles in the front row   please wait   yuki seemed unwell since before noon  she was restless during the test  and perhaps she couldn t demonstrate her abilities due to reasons other than her capabilities  he speaks without permission and is kicked by the instructor  the adults notice bleeding   the onset of menstruation  unusual this early  normally age nine at the earliest  likely from stress  she also has a fever  the instructor orders her to the infirmary  as she leaves crying  she looks at kiyotaka but he doesn t meet her gaze  from that day on  yuki never returned  he provokes a rookie instructor into a wild swing that he dodges  another instructor stops the  rookie    he wanted to test and either properly educate or dispose of the new instructor  detects yuki s irregular condition through observation and challenges the instructor s authority deliberately   testing those who would use him  tries to argue for her  she leaves crying and never returns","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p178-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Yuki fails and leaves<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.178–185<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Waits as papers are graded; Yuki&#x27;s small back trembles in the front row.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yuki.html\">Yuki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Please wait.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Yuki seemed unwell since before noon. She was restless during the test, and perhaps she couldn&#x27;t demonstrate her abilities due to reasons other than her capabilities—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He speaks without permission and is kicked by the instructor; the adults notice bleeding — the onset of menstruation, unusual this early (normally age nine at the earliest), likely from stress; she also has a fever.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The instructor orders her to the infirmary; as she leaves crying, she looks at Kiyotaka but he doesn&#x27;t meet her gaze; from that day on, Yuki never returned.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> He provokes a rookie instructor into a wild swing that he dodges; another instructor stops the &quot;rookie&quot; — he wanted to test and either properly educate or dispose of the new instructor.<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Detects Yuki&#x27;s irregular condition through observation and challenges the instructor&#x27;s authority deliberately — testing those who would use him.<span class=\"pg\">p.184–185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> Tries to argue for her; she leaves crying and never returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.178–185<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p172-1\">← Before: Arisu Sakayanagi observes the White Room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p186-1\">→ After: Shiro&#x27;s farewell: wanting freedom<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p186-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"shiro ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka shiro s farewell  wanting freedom with only him and shiro left  they begin a judo randori while the referee steps out   can i say something   it s been years since i last won against you in judo  hasn t it   i ve decided to leave this facility   that s why i m going to drop out voluntarily   i want to be free  i want friends   i ll go ahead  let s meet again someday  kiyotaka   in the end  i lost again  huh   goodbye  shiro   goodbye  kiyotaka  shiro  hurt in boxing  karate and jeet kune do too  wants the real world rather than a virtual one  kiyotaka cannot understand wanting freedom or friends  in the final match kiyotaka resolves to out exert him  if the opponent exerted 140  effort  i would exert 150  and slams him onto the tatami  they are watched from the second floor beyond the glass  cannot comprehend shiro s desire for freedom or the outside world   he is not dissatisfied  and intellectual curiosity drives him to stay and keep learning  his last real rival  their final randori and farewell   shiro drops out soon after","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p186-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Shiro&#x27;s farewell: wanting freedom<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.186–191<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With only him and Shiro left, they begin a judo randori while the referee steps out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"index.html#shiro\">Shiro<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiro<\/b> &quot;Can I say something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiro<\/b> &quot;It&#x27;s been years since I last won against you in judo, hasn&#x27;t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.186<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Shiro<\/b> &quot;I&#x27;ve decided to leave this facility.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;That&#x27;s why I&#x27;m going to drop out voluntarily.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I want to be free. I want friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ll go ahead. Let&#x27;s meet again someday, Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;In the end… I lost again, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Goodbye, Shiro.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Goodbye, Kiyotaka.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Shiro, hurt in boxing, karate and Jeet Kune Do too, wants the real world rather than a virtual one; Kiyotaka cannot understand wanting freedom or friends. In the final match Kiyotaka resolves to out-exert him (&quot;if the opponent exerted 140% effort, I would exert 150%&quot;) and slams him onto the tatami; they are watched from the second floor beyond the glass.<span class=\"pg\">p.186–190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Cannot comprehend Shiro&#x27;s desire for freedom or the outside world — he is not dissatisfied, and intellectual curiosity drives him to stay and keep learning.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shiro<\/b> His last real rival; their final randori and farewell — Shiro drops out soon after.<span class=\"pg\">p.186–191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p178-1\">← Before: Yuki fails and leaves<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p192-1\">→ After: The baton fight against grown men; father revealed<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p192-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-atsuomi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the baton fight against grown men  father revealed at age nine  after defeating all the martial arts instructors  he is ordered to fight multiple grown men in  actual combat   kiyotaka  from now on  you will fight multiple people in actual combat format   and you don t need to hold back at all  you can go as far as killing   i was ordered to kill   you probably understand by now  but i am the head of the white room  and i m also your biological father   i know   when i was four  i remember hearing it while the instructors were talking   you are special to me  chooses a collapsing baton  30 cm  extends to  60 cm  for reach  shatters the last man s leg and aims a head blow to knock him out  stopped by  stop  the men are carried out on stretchers  atsuomi tells him alone that he is his biological father  kiyotaka had known since age four    a father to me  that was nothing special  his biological father reveals himself  kiyotaka is unmoved  follows the kill order literally and without emotion  treats the father reveal as  just a fact","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The baton fight against grown men; father revealed<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.192–196<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At age nine, after defeating all the martial-arts instructors, he is ordered to fight multiple grown men in &quot;actual combat.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Kiyotaka, from now on, you will fight multiple people in actual combat format.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;And you don&#x27;t need to hold back at all. You can go as far as killing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;I was ordered to kill.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;You probably understand by now, but I am the head of the White Room, and I&#x27;m also your biological father.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;When I was four. I remember hearing it while the instructors were talking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;You are special to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Chooses a collapsing baton (~30 cm, extends to ~60 cm) for reach; shatters the last man&#x27;s leg and aims a head blow to knock him out, stopped by &quot;STOP!&quot;; the men are carried out on stretchers.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Atsuomi tells him alone that he is his biological father; Kiyotaka had known since age four — &quot;a father—to me, that was nothing special.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> His biological father reveals himself; Kiyotaka is unmoved.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Follows the kill order literally and without emotion; treats the father reveal as &quot;just a fact.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192–196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p186-1\">← Before: Shiro&#x27;s farewell: wanting freedom<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p197-1\">→ After: The researchers on his lack of emotion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p197-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the researchers on his lack of emotion  that is both kiyotaka s strength and a permanent weakness   it s too late to instill emotions in the white room now  if so  we have no choice but to significantly change his environment   kiyotaka is clearly an anomaly  this isn t just favoritism because he s your son  ishida and atsuomi discuss him in front of him   his pulse barely changes even in conversation or combat  he has  almost nothing  in the way of emotion  but can skillfully lie and disguise himself  atsuomi orders them to investigate why he has no limits  paying them enough to pursue it  he listens without reaction   praise or criticism doesn t matter   everything comes down to whether you drop out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p197-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The researchers on his lack of emotion<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.197–198<\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;That is both Kiyotaka&#x27;s strength and a permanent weakness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;It&#x27;s too late to instill emotions in the White Room now. If so, we have no choice but to significantly change his environment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Kiyotaka is clearly an anomaly. This isn&#x27;t just favoritism because he&#x27;s your son.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Ishida and Atsuomi discuss him in front of him — his pulse barely changes even in conversation or combat; he has &quot;almost nothing&quot; in the way of emotion, but can skillfully lie and disguise himself. Atsuomi orders them to investigate why he has no limits, paying them enough to pursue it.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He listens without reaction — praise or criticism doesn&#x27;t matter; &quot;everything comes down to whether you drop out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p192-1\">← Before: The baton fight against grown men; father revealed<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p251-1\">→ After: The Yuki reunion; first day outside<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p251-1","v":"y0","y":0,"o":36,"k":"narration","w":"yuki ayanokouji-atsuomi kamogawa ishida-yuusuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka the yuki reunion  first day outside at a counseling clinic  meets a man in his early forties holding a vase of sakura flowers   kiyotaka s first time outside the white room after fourteen years   who are you   is that  sakura   yuki  i m yuki   why are you here   i ve been there for fourteen years  today is the first time i ve come outside   i have nothing to say   it s better if you stop  talking with me is impossible for you   then i refuse   nothing has changed since the time you ve disappeared   goodbye  it s better if we never meet again   nothing   understood  the man is yuki s father  she has grown weak  shut herself in  and could only be calmed by meeting a fellow fourth generation student   sakura is her favorite flower  her smile is  a bit awkward  but her emotions are rich  yuki trembles and hyperventilates recalling the white room  clings to his sleeve  her father blocks the exit and admits neither he  his wife nor his younger daughter can reach her  circumspect and cold   sees the meeting as  a meeting with the dead  declines to talk about the white room  refuses the father s personal request  it isn t  right  the white room representative didn t give me any specific instructions  and judges continued contact would only make yuki suffer  tells his father  nothing  about the outside scenery  deliberately letting him believe he feels no emotion    it was just easier to let him think everything was under control  in truth he is  constantly sharpening my fangs  his former white room classmate  refuses her desperate plea to talk  and leaves saying they should never meet again  his father  hides his true sharpening resolve from him  meets him in the car after leaving the clinic  doesn t respond to his greeting  ishida warns kamogawa that kiyotaka is a  monster","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p251-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">The Yuki reunion; first day outside<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Side stories · p.251–258<\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At a counseling clinic, meets a man in his early forties holding a vase of sakura flowers — Kiyotaka&#x27;s first time outside the White Room after fourteen years.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"yuki.html\">Yuki<\/a> · <a href=\"ayanokouji-atsuomi.html\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/a> · <a href=\"kamogawa.html\">Kamogawa<\/a> · <a href=\"index.html#ishida-yuusuke\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Who are you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Is that… sakura?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q narration\">&quot;Yuki, I&#x27;m Yuki!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Why are you here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;ve been there for fourteen years. Today is the first time I&#x27;ve come outside.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;I have nothing to say.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;It&#x27;s better if you stop. Talking with me is impossible for you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Then I refuse.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Nothing has changed since the time you&#x27;ve disappeared.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Goodbye. It&#x27;s better if we never meet again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> &quot;Understood.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The man is Yuki&#x27;s father; she has grown weak, shut herself in, and could only be calmed by meeting a fellow fourth-generation student — sakura is her favorite flower. Her smile is &quot;a bit awkward&quot; but her emotions are rich.<span class=\"pg\">p.251–252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> Yuki trembles and hyperventilates recalling the White Room; clings to his sleeve; her father blocks the exit and admits neither he, his wife nor his younger daughter can reach her.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Circumspect and cold — sees the meeting as &quot;a meeting with the dead,&quot; declines to talk about the White Room, refuses the father&#x27;s personal request (&quot;It isn&#x27;t, right? The White Room representative didn&#x27;t give me any specific instructions&quot;), and judges continued contact would only make Yuki suffer.<span class=\"pg\">p.251–258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Tells his father &quot;Nothing&quot; about the outside scenery, deliberately letting him believe he feels no emotion — &quot;it was just easier to let him think everything was under control&quot;; in truth he is &quot;constantly sharpening my fangs.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yuki<\/b> His former White Room classmate; refuses her desperate plea to talk, and leaves saying they should never meet again.<span class=\"pg\">p.251–256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Atsuomi<\/b> His father; hides his true sharpening resolve from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.256–258<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kamogawa<\/b> Meets him in the car after leaving the clinic; doesn&#x27;t respond to his greeting.<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishida Yūsuke<\/b> Ishida warns Kamogawa that Kiyotaka is a &quot;monster.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y0-p197-1\">← Before: The researchers on his lack of emotion<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
